[
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0000",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 0,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 0,
    "char_end": 1327,
    "char_count": 1327,
    "text": "No.:318/17/2024-GridConnectedRooftop\nMinistry of New and RenewableEnergy\nGovernmentof India\nAtalAkshayUrjaBhawan\nLodhiRoad,NewDelhi-110003\nDated 07.06.2024\nOfficeMemorandum\nSubject: Operational Guidelines for Implementation of PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nfor the component “CFA to Residential Consumers\"\nThis refers Ministry's order No. 318/17/2024-GCRT Division dated 16th March 2024 vide\nwhich sanction was issued for the PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana, aimed at installing rooftop\nsolar plants in one crore households, with a total financial outlay of Rs. 75,021 crore.\n2.\nThe operational Guidelines for the implementation of PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nfor the component “CFA to Residential Consumers\" are enclosed.\nThis issues with the approval of competent authority.\n(DivyanshuJha)\nDeputy Secretary\nd.jha1989@ias.nic.in\nTo\n1. ACS/Principal Secretaries/Secretaries (Renewable Energy/Energy/Power) of all States/\nUTs\n2.\nCMDs/MDs of Discoms/State Nodal Agencies of all States/UTs\n3.\nChairperson, All State/Joint Electricity Regulatory Commission\nCopy for information to:\n1. PS to Hon'ble Minister of New & Renewable Energy\n2. PS to Hon'ble Minister of State of New and Renewable Energy\n3. PPS to SecretarylAS/JS/JS&FA, MNRE\n4. All Advisers & Group Heads\n5. Director (NIC) for uploading on Ministry's website\n***",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0001",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 1,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 1329,
    "char_end": 1548,
    "char_count": 219,
    "text": "2\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\n1) Background",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0002",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 2,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 1550,
    "char_end": 2483,
    "char_count": 933,
    "text": "a) The Government of India has approved the PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana on 29th February,\n2024 to increase the share of solar rooftop capacity and empower residential households to\ngenerate their own electricity. The scheme has an outlay of Rs 75,021 crore and is to be\nimplemented till FY 2026-27. The administrative approval was granted to the scheme vide\nOrder No. 318/17/2024-Grid Connected Rooftop dated 16th March, 2024.\nb) The Financial Outlay for the scheme includes the following components:-\nS. No.\nScheme Component\nOutlay\n1.\nCFA to Residential Consumers\n₹ 65,700 crore\n2.\nIncentives for Discoms\n₹ 4,950 crore\n3.\nModel Solar Villages in each district\n₹ 800 crore\n4.\nIncentives for Local Bodies\n₹ 1000 crore\n5.\nPayment Security Mechanism\n₹ 100 crore\n6.\nInnovative Projects\n₹ 500 crore\n7.\nCapacity Building (1% of CFA)\n₹ 657 crore\n8.\nAwareness & Outreach (1% of CFA)\n₹ 657 crore\n9.\nService Charge (1% of CFA)\n₹ 657 crore",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0003",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 3,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 2485,
    "char_end": 2793,
    "char_count": 308,
    "text": "Total\n₹ 75,021 crore\n\n2) Scope\na) These guidelines pertain to the implementation of Component 1 “Central Financial\nAssistance (CFA) to residential consumers” under the capex mode for eligible consumer\ncategories only.\nb) The guidelines pertaining to other components of the scheme shall be issued separately.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0004",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 4,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 2795,
    "char_end": 3135,
    "char_count": 340,
    "text": "3\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nc) These guidelines shall be applicable for all applications received on the National Portal\nfrom the date of the launch of the scheme, i.e. 13th February, 2024.\nd) The implementation period of the scheme shall be till 31st March, 2027.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0005",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 5,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 3137,
    "char_end": 4798,
    "char_count": 1661,
    "text": "3) Aim and Objectives of PM – Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nThe key objectives of the scheme are:\na) To achieve 1 crore rooftop solar system (RTS) installation in residential sector.\nb) To help provide free/low-cost electricity to 1 crore households up to 300 units of\nelectricity per month by installation of rooftop solar.\nc) To produce renewable electricity of 1,000 billion units through the capacity installed\nunder the scheme, which will result in reduction of 720 million ton of CO2eq emission\nduring the 25 years of lifetime for rooftop solar projects.\nd) To develop the required enabling ecosystem for rooftop solar projects, including\nregulatory support, manufacturing facilities, supply chain, vendor network, operation &\nmaintenance facilities, etc., in the country.\ne) To boost local economy and employment generation along with enhanced energy\nsecurity\nf) To aid in achievement of India’s commitment for green climate through its NDCs\n(Nationally Determined Contributions) at UNFCCC by installation of 30 GW of solar\ncapacity through rooftop solar by 2026-27\n4) Transition From Existing Scheme\na) The Ministry of New and Renewable Energy has been implementing the Grid Connected\nRooftop Solar Phase II Programme since 2019, which was proposed to be implemented\ntill 2025-26 with a budgetary outlay of Rs 11,814 crores. This scheme stands subsumed\nwithin the PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana.\nb) The CFA and other releases for the PM – Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana shall be made from\nthe budgetary outlays of Rooftop Solar Phase II Programme till the dedicated budget\nallocation for the scheme is operational and disbursements can be made from it.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0006",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 6,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 4800,
    "char_end": 5714,
    "char_count": 914,
    "text": "4\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nc) Once the new scheme budget is operational, the budget of Phase II programme will get\nsubsumed into the new scheme, and the new scheme funds shall be utilized for meeting\nthe ongoing liabilities of the Phase II programme also.\nd) The CFA releases for ongoing projects against allocations made by MNRE to\nimplementation agencies under Phase II shall be governed by the guidelines issued under\nthe Phase II programme and shall not be covered under the PM – Surya Ghar Scheme\nCFA structure. However, the budgetary releases for phase II programme shall be met\nthrough the new scheme outlay.\ne) The Phase II programme was implemented in Tender Mode as well as through National\nPortal. The applicability of CFA rates for claims submitted under Phase II programme has\nbeen defined in Annexure 1 for greater clarity.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0007",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 7,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 5716,
    "char_end": 7173,
    "char_count": 1457,
    "text": "5) Central Financial Assistance\na) The scheme will support the installation of grid-connected rooftop solar projects in the\nresidential sector through Central Financial Support (CFA) support from the Central\nGovernment.\nb) Eligibility: For the purpose of CFA, residential RTS plant would be the grid connected\nsolar power system tagged to a particular residential power connection of the local\nDISCOM and will only include installations on a roof/terrace/balcony or on top of\nelevated structures. Special RTS installations such as Building Integrated PV (BiPV)\nsystems shall also be considered eligible for CFA support. To clarify, installations under\nmetering mechanisms such as Group Net Metering and Virtual Net Metering shall be\neligible for CFA if the installations are on any roof/terrace/balcony or on top of elevated\nstructures or as BiPV and the metering arrangement is approved by the DISCOM.\nc) Capex Mode: The Capex mode is considered to be one wherein the consumer herself,\neither through her own capital or through borrowings from financial institutions or\notherwise, funds the initial investment into the rooftop solar system. To clarify, these\nguidelines do not cover RESCO models (where a third party entity other than the\nconsumer makes the initial investment) or Utility Led/State Led Aggregation Models\n(where a state entity invests on behalf of consumers on an aggregate basis). These modes\nwill be dealt separately in other guidelines.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0008",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 8,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 7175,
    "char_end": 8699,
    "char_count": 1524,
    "text": "5\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nd) No CFA will be provided to non-residential segments of consumers (including\ngovernment segment, commercial and industrial segment etc.).\ne) CFA Structure: The Central Financial Assistance for the residential sector shall be as per\nthe following table:\nS. No. Type of Residential Segment\nCFA\n1.\nResidential Sector (first 2 kWp of RTS capacity\nor part thereof)\n60% of benchmark cost of 2 kWp\n2.\nResidential Sector (with additional RTS\ncapacity of 1 kWp or part thereof)\n40% of benchmark cost of\nadditional kWp\n3.\nResidential Sector (additional RTS capacity\nbeyond 3 kWp)\nNo additional CFA\n4.\nGroup Housing Societies/ Residential Welfare\nAssociations (GHS/RWA) etc, for common\nfacilities including EV charging up to 500 kWp\n(@3 kWp per house)\nAs per CFA of S. No. (2) above\nFor GHS/RWAs, the upper limit of CFA supported RTS capacity is inclusive of individual rooftop plants\ninstalled by individual residents in the GHS/RWA.\nf) The GHS/RWA connection eligible under the scheme shall be dedicated only for common\nfacilities and should not be utilized for providing electricity supply to residential\nconsumers within the GHS/RWA.\ni) The CFA support will generally be provided to entities created by residents for overall\nmaintenance and that are responsible for upkeep of common facilities and these may\nbe known by alternative terminologies such as Apartment Owner Associations\n(AOAs), Cooperative Housing Societies etc.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0009",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 9,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 6,
    "char_start": 8701,
    "char_end": 9933,
    "char_count": 1232,
    "text": "6\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\ng) Benchmark Cost: The benchmark cost for 1 kW system is fixed at ₹ 50,000/kW for the\nfirst 2 kW of RTS capacity and ₹ 45,000 for the additional kW with effect from 13th\nFebruary, 2024. The benchmark for special category States (States/UTs of Uttarakhand,\nHimachal Pradesh, J&K, Ladakh, States in the North East including Sikkim, UTs of A&N\nand Lakshadweep) will be Rs 55,000 for first 2 kW of RTS capacity and Rs 49,500 for the\nadditional kW of RTS capacity.\nh) Effective CFA: The CFA for the scheme with effect from date of initiation, i.e., 13th\nFebruary, 2024 is as follows:-\nS.\nNo.\nType of Residential Segment\nCFA\nCFA\n(Special\nCategory States)\n1.\nResidential Sector (first 2 kWp of RTS capacity\nor part thereof)\nRs 30,000/kWp\nRs 33,000/kWp\n2.\nResidential Sector (with additional RTS\ncapacity of 1 kWp or part thereof)\nRs 18,000/kWp\nRs 19,800/kWp\n3.\nResidential Sector (additional RTS capacity\nbeyond 3 kWp)\nNo additional CFA\nNo additional CFA\n4.\nGroup Housing Societies/ Residential Welfare\nAssociations (GHS/RWA) etc, for common\nfacilities including EV charging up to 500 kWp\n(@3 kWp per house)\nRs 18,000/kWp\nRs 19,800/kWp",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0010",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 10,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 6,
    "char_start": 9935,
    "char_end": 10163,
    "char_count": 228,
    "text": "To illustrate\ni.\nIf a consumer installs a system of 1.5 kW, she is eligible for a CFA of ₹ 30,000x 1.5 = ₹\n45,000\nii.\nIf a consumer installs a capacity of 2.5 kW, she is eligible for a CFA of ₹ 30,000x2 + ₹\n18,000x0.5 = ₹ 69,000",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0011",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 11,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 10165,
    "char_end": 11957,
    "char_count": 1792,
    "text": "7\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\niii.\nIf a consumer installs a capacity of 6 kW, she is eligible for a CFA of ₹ 30,000x2  +\nRs18,000x1 = ₹ 78,000\niv.\nIf an RWA installs a capacity of 100 kW, with 20 households, it will be eligible for a CFA\nof ₹ 18,000x60 kW (Lower of (20x3 kW), 100 kW) = ₹ 10,80,000\nv.\nIf an RWA installs a capacity of 100 kW, with 50 households, it will be eligible for a CFA\nof ₹ 18,000x100 kW (Lower of (50x3 kW), 100 kW)= ₹ 18,00,000\ni) Additional State Subsidy: The State/UT governments may supplement the CFA provided\nby the central government for the residential sector with an additional subsidy for RTS;\nhowever, this shall be subject to adherence to all scheme guidelines by the State. The\nframework of such support by the State/UT governments shall be in alignment with the\nsupport provided under the scheme. The process for disbursement of state subsidy\ncomponent shall be integrated with the National Portal.\nj) Revision of Benchmark Cost: The benchmark cost will be revised at the time of midterm\nreview of the scheme to reflect changed market trends, if any, or earlier in case of\nsubstantial upward revision in module prices for unforeseen reasons. The benchmark will\nreflect changes in solar module supply prices, inverter costs and other systems costs as\nper the methodology defined by the Ministry of New and Renewable Energy. In case of\nupward revision of benchmark rates and consequent increase in requirement of\nbudgetary support, necessary approvals in consultation with Department of Expenditure\nshall be taken separately by the Ministry to revise the scheme targets appropriately.\nk) Sizing of Inverter: The CFA shall be irrespective of the size of the inverter installed. If a",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0012",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 12,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 11958,
    "char_end": 12615,
    "char_count": 657,
    "text": "consumer installs a rooftop solar plant with a higher/lower rated inverter capacity than\nthe number of modules, the CFA provided will be as per the rated DC capacity of the\nmodule system (according to the CFA structure) and not as per the inverter capacity. The\ninverter should, however, meet the technical specification defined in the scheme.\nl) Additional Components: The rooftop solar installation may include additional\ntechnology components such as small wind hybrids, battery storage, solar tracker\nsystems etc. However, the CFA calculation shall be based on the CFA structure under the\nscheme as per capacity of solar modules installed in the system.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0013",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 13,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 12617,
    "char_end": 14414,
    "char_count": 1797,
    "text": "8\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nm) Domestic Content Requirement: Solar modules used in the installation must satisfy the\nDomestic Content Requirement condition i.e., domestically manufactured modules\nmanufactured from domestically manufactured cells. This is an essential condition for\nthe installation to be eligible for the CFA. Use of non-DCR modules in any form in the\ninstallation shall render the installation ineligible for CFA.\nn) Pre-existing RTS: A rooftop solar installation by residential consumers/RWAs that has\navailed CFA under a prior/current scheme for rooftop solar by Ministry of New and\nRenewable Energy and has subsequently increased the RTS installation size shall be\neligible for additional CFA under the current scheme only for the balance capacity up to\n3 kW of overall RTS plant size.\n(1)\nFor example, if a household had installed a RTS of 1 kW under Phase 2 Grid Connected\nRooftop Solar Scheme and availed a subsidy of Rs 14,588, and if such a household\nenhances the total capacity to 4 kW overall, in such a case, the household shall be\neligible to claim an additional subsidy under the current scheme only for the\nadditional 2 kW capacity, i.e. Rs 48,000.\n(2)\nAlternatively, if a household installs a RTS of 1 kW under PM – Surya Ghar scheme\nand avails a subsidy of Rs 30,000, and if such a household later enhances the total\ncapacity to 4 kW overall, in such a case, the household shall be eligible to claim an\nadditional subsidy under the current scheme only for the additional 2 kW capacity,\ni.e. Rs 48,000.\no) A rooftop solar installation shall be eligible for CFA only once after installation. If an\nalready installed rooftop solar is shifted/relocated to a new location, such a system shall",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0014",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 14,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 14415,
    "char_end": 14970,
    "char_count": 555,
    "text": "not be eligible for CFA under the scheme.\np) Give It Up: Consumers will have the option to forgo the CFA under the scheme so that\nthe scheme benefits can reach a wider cross-section of consumers. This will be enabled\nby a “Give It Up” option on the National Portal. Consumers who opt for installing RTS\nwithout availing CFA under this scheme, including those who may wish to forgo the RTS\nCFA (under the “Give It Up” campaign or otherwise) shall be free to do so without using\ndomestically manufactured cells/modules (Domestic Content Requirement or DCR).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0015",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 15,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 14971,
    "char_end": 14998,
    "char_count": 27,
    "text": "6) Method of Implementation",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0016",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 16,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 15000,
    "char_end": 16769,
    "char_count": 1769,
    "text": "9\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\na) National Portal: Any eligible consumer shall avail the benefits of the scheme only\nthrough the PM Surya Ghar National Portal (hereinafter referred to as “Portal” or “NP”).\nb) Eligible Consumer: Any interested consumer with a valid Consumer Account Number (or\nits equivalent consumer ID) for a Distribution Utility (Distribution Companies, or in some\ncases Power/Energy Department of the state wherever applicable) shall apply on the\nNational Portal. The Portal shall generate an application ID for the application. The\nconsumer shall be assisted on the National Portal with informational aids, audio visual\nmaterial and other decision-making tools to decide on rooftop solar installation and its\npossible configurations.\nc) Choice of Vendor: The consumer shall then choose a vendor who is registered on the\nNational Portal. The consumer shall be free to enter into arrangements with any such\nRTS vendor at mutually decided rates. There shall be no tendering or rate discovery by\nthe state DISCOMs/agencies under the scheme to empanel RTS vendors as was being\ncarried out in the Phase II program. The portal shall include a mechanism of vendor\ncomparison so that consumer can make a better decision in finalizing the vendor of\nchoice.\nd) Finalization of Terms: The consumer shall mutually decide with the vendor on the system\ndesign, system components, system quality, additional functionalities, localized design\nrequirements etc. Based on the mutually decided system design, the consumer shall also\nmutually agree with the vendor on the financial terms and conditions. The vendor and\nthe consumer may sign an agreement covering these aspects. A suggested sample",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0017",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 17,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 16770,
    "char_end": 17513,
    "char_count": 743,
    "text": "vendor-consumer agreement is attached at Annexure 2, however, the actual agreement\nmay vary on a case-to-case basis.\ne) In order to protect the interests of the consumers, the National Portal will provide\ncomprehensive informational material, decision making tools, system and vendor\ncomparison tools etc. so that the consumers can make an informed choice.\nf) Minimum Technical Specifications: The Ministry shall identify the minimum technical\nspecifications to be adhered to by all vendors for RTS systems installed under the\nscheme. It will be the responsibility of the vendors to ensure that the system meets the\nminimum technical specifications as detailed in Annexure 3. This will also be checked by\nthe DISCOMs at the time of inspection.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0018",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 18,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 17515,
    "char_end": 19260,
    "char_count": 1745,
    "text": "10\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\ng) Indicative Costs of Components: The Ministry will publish indicative costs of system\ncomponents (modules, inverters and other important equipment) for the benefit of\nconsumers in order to ensure that consumers are not overcharged.\nh) Feasibility Approval: As per the provisions of the Electricity (Rights of Consumers) Rules,\n2020 and subsequent amendments, applications for rooftop solar systems up to 10 kW\ncapacity shall be deemed to have been accepted without requiring approval of technical\nfeasibility by the DISCOMs. Till the operationalization of this provision by respective\nRegulatory Commissions/DISCOMs, the consumer shall upload the necessary documents\nfor seeking feasibility approval, wherever required as per extant state regulations.\ni) Vendor Installation: The vendor shall install the system, conduct necessary safety and\nother checks and also educate the consumer on various aspects of RTS maintenance and\nsafety and provide informational material to the consumer as appropriate.\nj) Portal Updation: After the vendor has completed the installations, the consumer shall\nupdate the system details on the portal and upload all the relevant documents including\ngeo-tagged photographs as required on the portal. The vendor may assist the consumers\nin filling up the necessary details through the consumer login. Subsequently, the\napplication will move to the DISCOM.\nk) DISCOM Inspection: The concerned DISCOM shall conduct a physical inspection of the\nsystem, sign the appropriate agreements with the consumer (net meter agreement or\notherwise), conduct a checklist-based inspection as per the National Portal and approve",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0019",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 19,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 19261,
    "char_end": 19565,
    "char_count": 304,
    "text": "the application on the National Portal for release of CFA. Alternatively, the DISCOMs may\nsend back the application for corrections or reject the claim with adequate justification.\nThe CFA will be processed only after the DISCOM has physically verified the system and\ncompleted the process on the Portal.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0020",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 20,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 19567,
    "char_end": 21321,
    "char_count": 1754,
    "text": "11\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nl) Meter Installation and Agreement: The meter shall be installed by DISCOM after rooftop\ninstallation is complete and the DISCOM and the consumer will sign the appropriate\nmetering agreement as per state regulations. The net meter will be provided by the\nDISCOM or the consumer may procure the net meters from enlisted meter vendors. A\nmodel net metering agreement is shown at Annexure 4. However, the actual agreement\nmay vary. All metering arrangements (net metering, gross metering, net billing, virtual\nnet metering, group net metering etc.) approved by the respective Electricity Regulatory\nCommissions of States/UTs shall be covered under the scheme.\nm) Metering in AMISP Areas: For the purpose of net metering, in the areas where the Smart\nMetering works have already been awarded under Revamped Distribution Sector\nScheme (RDSS), DISCOMs/PDs (Power Departments) should mandatorily get the Smart\nMeters installed through the AMISP (Advance Metering Infrastructure Service Provider).\nn) Metering in Non-AMISP Areas: In case the Smart Metering works are yet to be awarded\nunder RDSS, the net meters should be installed (preferably Smart Meters with 4G Cellular\nNIC card) as per manufacturers empaneled list and technical specifications published by\nCentral Electricity Authority in its website.\no) Non Metered Grid Connected Systems: Systems that are not feeding into the grid but\nare connected to the grid (behind-the-meter systems, battery hybrid systems etc.) shall\nbe eligible for CFA under the scheme subject to approval by the respective Electricity\nRegulatory Commissions. In such cases, the DISCOM will inspect the installation, ensure",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0021",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 21,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 21322,
    "char_end": 22096,
    "char_count": 774,
    "text": "the functioning of the reverse power relay protection and incorporate suitable remarks\nin the report. However, Off-grid connected installations will not be eligible for CFA under\nthe scheme.\np) E-Token: The release of the CFA shall be operationalized through an e-token. The e-token\nwill be generated after submission of application on the National Portal and will be visible\non the consumer profile in the Portal. After the necessary documents have been\nuploaded and inspection by the DISCOM has been completed, the e-token shall be\nactivated with the amount of eligible CFA as per the actual installed capacity. The e-token\nshall then be redeemed by the consumer by logging into her profile on the Portal and the\nCFA shall subsequently be released to the consumer account.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0022",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 22,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 22098,
    "char_end": 23834,
    "char_count": 1736,
    "text": "12\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nq) Financing: The consumer may also opt for financing through the National Portal. The loan\nproducts of various banks and financial institutions will be available on the NP and the\nconsumer may opt for any of them through integration provided by Jan Samarth Portal\nor through other Financial Institutions directly.\nr) Loan Products: It is envisaged that standardized low interest loan products in the range\nof benchmark rates (Repo + 50 bps) for installation of residential RTS systems that are up\nto 3 kW in size will be made available to the consumers by Banks.\ni) These financing options shall be supplemented by standardized products of similar\nnature for non-subsidized segments also, including residential sector RTS of sizes\nmore than 3 kW. The standard loan products from Banks/FIs will be published on the\nportal.\ns) Consumer Account Details: All consumer details including bank account information and\na cancelled cheque image/bank e-statement file/passbook scan or any other electronic\ndocument certifying that the bank account number is held by the concerned consumer\nmust be submitted on the National Portal by the consumer.\ni) In case the consumer has opted for a loan product to finance the rooftop solar\ninstallation, the consumer profile shall also include the loan account details (entered\nby the Consumer or through integration with banking portals). On redemption of the\ne-token in such cases, the CFA will be transferred to the loan account of the\nconsumer. If the CFA exceeds the outstanding loan amount of the consumer, the CFA\nwill be disbursed to the consumer's loan account in the bank up to the amount of",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0023",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 23,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 23835,
    "char_end": 24018,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "loan outstanding, with the remainder disbursed into the consumer's bank account.\nt) Processing of Claims: The CFA will be processed within 15 days of approval by the\nconcerned DISCOM.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0024",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 24,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 24019,
    "char_end": 24261,
    "char_count": 242,
    "text": "7) Vendor Registration and Performance\na) Registration of Vendors: The scheme shall be implemented only through the vendors\nregistered on the National Portal i.e. a consumer has to choose a registered vendor for\navailing CFA under the scheme.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0025",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 25,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 24263,
    "char_end": 26032,
    "char_count": 1769,
    "text": "13\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nb) Registration Levels: The vendors shall have the option to register with the state\nDISCOMs/state agencies for state level registration and with the National Programme\nImplementation Agency (NPIA) for national/multi-state/state level registration as per\nprocedure prescribed by MNRE. In case of multiple DISCOMs within a state, the state\ngovernment shall identify a nodal DISCOM/agency which shall undertake vendor\nregistrations on behalf of all DISCOMs of that state.\nc) Vendor Profiles: The registered vendors will be able to create their profiles on National\nPortal, including RTS system specifications offered, prices offered and key contacts for\nconsumers to reach out to. The consumers will be able to raise requests for enquiries\nthrough the portal and it is also expected that the vendors will respond to interest\nexpressed by consumers in a timely and reasonable manner. The vendor profile will also\ninclude vendor rating, details about consumer feedback and other data relating to the\nperformance of the vendor on completed/ongoing projects for which they are the\ndesignated vendors.\nd) Services: Registered vendors shall provide the services to the consumers for\nrepairs/maintenance of the RTS plant free of cost for 5 years of the Comprehensive\nMaintenance Contract (CMC) period from the date of commissioning of the plan. Non-\nperforming/ under-performing system component will be replaced/repaired free of cost\nin the CMC period. The consumer shall be provided with the warranties given by the\nrespective OEMs on the system components for any future replacement of\nmalfunctioning components. Any deficiency of the RTS system leading to non-disbursal",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0026",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 26,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 26033,
    "char_end": 26779,
    "char_count": 746,
    "text": "of CFA/non-commissioning of the RTS by the DISCOM on account of system\nquality/component issues shall be rectified by the vendor. In all cases, the vendors shall\nadhere to the minimum technical specifications provided in the scheme in their\ninstallations.\ne) Penalties: The Implementing agency (State DISCOM or agency) or MNRE officials or any\nother designated agency may inspect the ongoing installation or installed plants. In case\nthe systems are not as per standards, nonfunctional on account of poor quality of\ninstallation, or in non-compliance of scheme guidelines, the respective registering\nauthority will reserve the right to de-register the vendor and/or levy such penalties as\nmay be prescribed, after giving due notice to the vendor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0027",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 27,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 26781,
    "char_end": 26885,
    "char_count": 104,
    "text": "14\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0028",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 28,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 26887,
    "char_end": 28653,
    "char_count": 1766,
    "text": "8) Functionalities in the National Portal\na) The National Portal is currently live and functional, however over the period of the\nimplementation of the scheme, various value additions and feature enhancements will\nbe undertaken for up gradation of the portal. These enhancements inter alia may include\nthe following:-\ni) Integration with State Portals: The National Portal will provide a seamless and fully\nintegrated experience to prosumers in the residential sector. The portal will be fully\nintegrated with State DISCOM portals for a harmonized experience for consumers in\nall stages of rooftop installations, including requests for net metering, load sanctions,\ninspections etc.\nii) Platform Services: The portal will create a public platform on which other\napplications, websites, financing intermediaries and e-commerce sites can plug into,\nthrough Application Programming Interfaces (APIs) and provide additional services\nfor citizens.\niii) GIS based Services: The portal will be augmented with GIS based services to enable\nbetter decision making and visualization of RTS systems for vendors and consumers.\nThe GIS based system planning will also be integrated with PM-Gati Shakti Portal to\nleverage additional functionalities and optimize power systems planning.\niv) Marketplace for Vendors: The National Portal will create a transparent and open\nmarketplace for vendors by adding vendor feedback and vendor performance on the\nportal.\nv) Multimode Messaging: The National Portal will be accessible through apps, chatbots\nand WhatsApp also, enabling wider outreach to all segments. The Portal will also\ngenerate multi-level triggers for delays in DISCOM inspection and net meter\ninstallations and the DISCOMs shall be encouraged to ensure timely commissioning",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0029",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 29,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 28654,
    "char_end": 28931,
    "char_count": 277,
    "text": "of RTS plants, once the vendors have installed the systems.\nvi) Other Value Added Services: There shall be other value-added activities such as\nproviding basic financial modelling of the proposed system and consumer’s return\nperiod, entry of technical parameters of the system.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0030",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 30,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 28933,
    "char_end": 30663,
    "char_count": 1730,
    "text": "15\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nvii) Integration with Banks: The portal will provide integration with banking products\noffered by various financial institutions and will promote digital-only products for\nease of use by the consumers. Integration with Jan Samarth portal shall be done to\nensure bidirectional flow of information to and from the National Portal to the\nrespective financial institutions and to ensure tagging of loan account of consumer\nto the application on National Portal.\nviii) Give It Up: The facility for forgoing CFA under the scheme as a part of the “Give It\nUp” campaign shall be created on the National Portal. Such consumers would still be\nable to access all facilities of the National Portal as well as linkages with banks for\nnecessary financial products as per availability. This segment will benefit from non-\nfinancial easement of processes and standardized financing products created by\nbanks through the National Portal.\nix) Generation and Benefits Tracking: The National Portal will receive generation data\nfrom connected inverters/smart meters for providing better analytical services to the\nconsumer as well as to assist DISCOMs in collecting data. In case the RTS generation\ndata (intermittent or real-time or near real-time) of an RTS is being received by the\nvendor through SIM/dongle/Wi-Fi etc., access to that data shall be provided by the\nvendor to the National Portal. This will enable tracking of the RTS generation data on\nthe National Portal.\nb) Active Applications: MNRE may specify a time period for which an application shall be\nkept active on the National Portal from the date of application, after which the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0031",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 31,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 30664,
    "char_end": 31326,
    "char_count": 662,
    "text": "application shall be deemed to be dormant. In case such period is specified, the applicant\nwould be able to reactivate the dormant application at any time through the consumer\nprofile on the National Portal subject to the overall limit of 1 crore active applications.\nc) Limit on Active Applications: As the scheme is fund limited, the receiving of applications\non the National Portal shall be limited to 1 crore active applications and only these\napplications shall be considered for release of CFA. Once this limit is reached, MNRE may\nspecify a time period for completion of installations so as to ensure achievement of\nscheme target of 1 crore installations.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0032",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 32,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 31328,
    "char_end": 31881,
    "char_count": 553,
    "text": "16\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nd) Applicant Login: Applicant login will be provided on the national portal to undertake\nrelevant activities pertaining to each installation including updating of status of\ninstallation, technical specifications of the system installed, grievance redressal,\nuploading of relevant pictures (pre and post installation) and other items. The consumer\nhas the user rights to undertake all activities on the National Portal without relying on\nthe vendor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0033",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 33,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 31883,
    "char_end": 32714,
    "char_count": 831,
    "text": "9) System Components and Minimum Technical Specifications\nSystem Components: A Roof Top Solar (RTS) Photo Voltaic (PV) system shall generally\nconsist of equipment/components like Solar Photo Voltaic (SPV) modules, Inverter/micro\ninverters, Module Mounting structures, Energy Meter, Array Junction Boxes, DC\nDistribution Box, AC Distribution Box, Protections – Earthing, Lightning, Surge, Cables,\nDrawing & Manuals and any other necessary component based upon the site\nrequirement. The installations under the scheme that shall be commissioned shall\nadhere to the minimum technical specifications and quality standards as published by\nMNRE (Detailed in Annexure 3, as may be amended from time to time). Consumers may\ninstall specifications that are higher than these standards and will still be considered\neligible under the scheme.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0034",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 34,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 32716,
    "char_end": 33143,
    "char_count": 427,
    "text": "10) Ensuring Quality of Installations\na) Inspections and Evaluations: The Scheme Implementation Agencies (National\nProgramme Implementation Agency (NPIA) nationally and State Implementation\nAgencies (SIA) at State level) as well as other designated agencies by State/UT\ngovernments shall conduct regular inspections/evaluation of RTS systems installed\nunder the scheme, both at the time of commissioning and post commissioning.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0035",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 35,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 33145,
    "char_end": 33339,
    "char_count": 194,
    "text": "b) Third Party Assessment: The NPIA shall establish adequate mechanism to ensure\nindependent third party assessment of RTS installations of at least 1% of installed\nsystems on a pan-India basis.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0036",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 36,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 33341,
    "char_end": 33667,
    "char_count": 326,
    "text": "17\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nc) SIA Monitoring: The SIA may establish adequate mechanism to ensure post-\ncommissioning inspection of installed systems on a sampling basis. The SIA may conduct\nadditional independent third party assessments of systems.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0037",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 37,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 33669,
    "char_end": 34058,
    "char_count": 389,
    "text": "d) Vendor Rating: All the vendors registered on the National Portal will be given a vendor\nrating depending on the size and scale of installations done, quality of equipment,\nquality of workmanship, quality of service and other criteria. This vendor rating will be\nvisible to the consumers on the National Portal. Detailed methodology regarding\nvendor rating will be as prescribed by MNRE.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0038",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 38,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 34060,
    "char_end": 34677,
    "char_count": 617,
    "text": "11) Grievance Redressal\na) The consumers and vendors can raise grievances through the National Portal that will be\nchanneled for resolution to the SIA/ NPIA. The grievances will be resolved within a period\nof 30 days.\nb) The consumers and vendors will get regular updates regarding status of grievances\nthrough SMS, emails and other channels of communication.\nc) The grievances may be raised through the National Call Centre, National Portal or the\nPortal app. In each case, a unique tracking ID will be created by the NPIA for the\nconsumer to track the status of resolution of the grievance through an online system.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0039",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 39,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 34679,
    "char_end": 35379,
    "char_count": 700,
    "text": "12) Memorandum of Understanding\na) A Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) will be signed under the scheme between\nMinistry of New and Renewable Energy and the State/UT Energy Department within 3\nmonths of notification of these guidelines. The Draft MoU between MNRE and the\nState/UTs is as per Annexure 5.\nb) Release of funds under other scheme components (Incentives to DISCOMs, Model Solar\nVillage, Incentives to PRIs/ULBs, Payment Security Mechanism etc.) to State/UTs or\nentities under the State/UTs will be conditional to signing of the MoU with the concerned\nState/UT.\nc) The MoU will also be mandatory for allowing the release of additional state/UT subsidy\nfor RTS to consumers under the scheme.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0040",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 40,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 35381,
    "char_end": 35485,
    "char_count": 104,
    "text": "18\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0041",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 41,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 35487,
    "char_end": 35919,
    "char_count": 432,
    "text": "13) Implementation Agency\na) REC Limited shall initially be the Implementation Agency at the national level (National\nProgramme Implementation Agency (NPIA)) and will undertake activities relating to\noperation of the National Portal and registration of vendors at the national level as well\nas all other scheme related activities. However, MNRE will have the discretion to\ndesignate any other agency as the NPIA as per any exigency.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0042",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 42,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 35921,
    "char_end": 36413,
    "char_count": 492,
    "text": "b) The Distribution Utility (DISCOMs or Power/Energy Departments, as the case may be)\nshall be the State Implementation Agencies (SIA) at the State/UT level and shall ensure\nadherence to timelines specified for provisioning of services for prosumers and shall\ncoordinate with NPIA on matters pertaining to performance of vendors registered on the\nNational Portal, grievance redressal, programme monitoring at State/UT level and other\nresponsibilities ascribed to it by MNRE from time to time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0043",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 43,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 36415,
    "char_end": 37358,
    "char_count": 943,
    "text": "14) Fund Release Mechanism\na) The NPIA will assess the expected liabilities for each quarter for release of CFA to\nconsumers under the scheme (consumers under PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana and\nconsumers under Phase II Simplified Procedure) and status of expenditure against\npreviously sanctioned releases and make necessary requisitions for release of funds to\nMNRE.\nb) MNRE will process such requisitions and release funds from time to time in accordance\nwith norms of Government of India in order to ensure that the CFA is disbursed to\nconsumers without delay.\nc) For liabilities under the RTS Phase II programme (Tender mode), MNRE will process the\nclaims in accordance with Phase II scheme guidelines and issue necessary sanctions for\nrelease of funds.\nd) The Implementing agencies will remit the accrued interested and other charges to\nConsolidated Fund of India as per Rule 230 (8) of General Financial Rules, 2017 and its\namendments.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0044",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 44,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 37360,
    "char_end": 38659,
    "char_count": 1299,
    "text": "19\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\n15) Scheme Monitoring\na) A Group of Ministers will be constituted for overall guidance and coordination with\nstates.\nb) A Steering Committee under the chairmanship of Cabinet Secretary and including\nSecretaries of Ministry of New and Renewable Energy, Department of Financial Services,\nMinistry of Power, Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs and Ministry of Rural\nDevelopment will monitor the implementation of the scheme.\nc) The Mission Directorate in the Ministry of New and Renewable Energy will be responsible\nfor the implementation of the scheme. The Directorate will be headed by a Mission\nDirector not below the rank of  Joint Secretary to Government of India. The NPIA will\nfunction under the directions of the Mission Directorate.\nd) There will be a State Level Coordination Committee headed by the Chief\nSecretary/Advisor to Lieutenant Governor/Administrator and comprising of Secretaries\nof key departments to coordinate and monitor the implementation of the scheme in the\nState/UT.\ne) There will be a District Level Committee headed by the District Magistrate/District\nCollector and comprising of other members for monitoring the implementation of the\nscheme at the district level.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0045",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 45,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 38661,
    "char_end": 38982,
    "char_count": 321,
    "text": "16) Amendment of Scheme Guidelines\na) MNRE may make necessary amendments in the scheme guidelines within the overall\nspirit of the Cabinet approval or issue any clarification to remove difficulties in the\nimplementation of the scheme, as and when required, with the approval of Hon’ble\nMinister, New and Renewable Energy.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0046",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 46,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 38984,
    "char_end": 39088,
    "char_count": 104,
    "text": "20\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0047",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 47,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 39090,
    "char_end": 40392,
    "char_count": 1302,
    "text": "Annexure 1\nCoverage of applications under PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\n\nApplication received under Phase II rooftop solar programme (before 13th Feb 2024)\nSr. No\nParameter\nApplicable Subsidy\n1\nFirst instance of claims submission\nbefore 5th Jan\nRs. 14,588/kW for upto 3 kW capacity and\nthereafter Rs. 7,294/kW till 10kW capacity\n(Subsidy prevailing before revision on\n05.01.2024)\n2\nFirst instance of claims submission on\nand after 5th Jan\nRs. 18,000/kw for upto 3kW capacity and\nthereafter Rs. 9,000/kw till 10kW capacity\n(revised subsidy as per notification dated\n05.01.2024)\nNote: all applications received prior to launch of PM - Surya Ghar : Muft Bijli Yojana (before 13th\nFeb 2024 will be covered under the Phase II rooftop solar programme) and will be eligible for the\nCFA as indicate above. All applications submitted under the Phase II of rooftop solar programme\nwill be admissible for CFA if the claim is received till October 2024. The claims received after\nOctober 2024 will not be entertained.\nApplication received under PM - Surya Ghar : Muft Bijli Yojana (on and after 13th Feb 2024)\n1\nAll applications made on and after 13th\nFeb\n60% of benchmark cost upto 2 kW capacity\nand 40% for 1 kW additional capacity. No\nsubsidy beyond 3 kW.\n(as approved under PM-Surya Ghar: Muft\nBijli Yojana)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0048",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 48,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 40394,
    "char_end": 40967,
    "char_count": 573,
    "text": "21\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nThe CFA claims from installations undertaken in tender mode by respective\nDISCOMs/implementation agencies under previous programmes for Rooftop Solar will be\nconsidered under the guidelines of the respective programmes and not PM Suryaghar. The CFA\ncalculation will also be as per the respective programme guidelines. No new/additional\ncapacity allocation by issuing any sanction under tender mode of GCRT phase II will be allowed\non or after 12.2.2024 to the DISCOMs.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0049",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 49,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 40969,
    "char_end": 42006,
    "char_count": 1037,
    "text": "22\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nAnnexure 2\nModel Draft Agreement between Consumer & Vendor for installation of grid connected\nrooftop solar (RTS) project under PM – Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nThis agreement is executed on -------(Day)------(Month)-------(Year) for design, supply,\ninstallation, commissioning and 5-year comprehensive maintenance of RTS project/system\nalong with warranty under PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nBetween\n…………………………………………….\n(Name\nof\nConsumer)\nhaving\naddress\nat\n…………………………………………………………………. (hereinafter referred to as first Party i.e.\n/consumer/consumer/purchaser /owner of system).\nAnd\n………………………………………………………..(Name\nof\nVendor)\nhaving\nregistered\noffice\nat\n……………………………………………….(hereinafter referred to as second Party i.e. Vendor/ contractor/\nSystem Integrator).\nWhereas\nFirst Party wishes to install a Grid Connected Rooftop Solar Plant on the rooftop of the residential\nbuilding of the Consumer under PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0050",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 50,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 42008,
    "char_end": 42315,
    "char_count": 307,
    "text": "And whereas\n\nSecond Party has verified availability of appropriate roof and found it feasible to install a Grid\nConnected Roof Top Solar plant and that the second party is willing to design, supply, install,\ntest, commission and carry out Operation & Maintenance of the Rooftop Solar plant for 5 year\nperiod",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0051",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 51,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 42317,
    "char_end": 42458,
    "char_count": 141,
    "text": "On this day, the First Party and Second Party agree to the following:\n\nThe First Party hereby undertakes to perform the following activities:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0052",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 52,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 42460,
    "char_end": 43485,
    "char_count": 1025,
    "text": "23\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\n1. Submission of online application at National Portal for installation of RTS project/system,\nSubmission of application for net-metering and system inspection and upload of the\nrelevant documents on the National Portal of the scheme\n2. Provide secure storage of the material of the RTS plant delivered at the premises till\nhandover of the system.\n3. Provide access to the Roof Top during installation of the plant, operation &\nmaintenance, testing of the plant and equipment and for meter reading from solar\nmeter, inverter etc.\n4. Provide electricity during plant installation and water for cleaning of the panels.\n5. Report any malfunctioning of the plant to the Vendor during the warranty period.\n6. Pay the amount as per the payment schedule as mutually agreed with the vendor,\nincluding any additional amount to the second party for any additional work\n/customization required depending upon the building condition",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0053",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 53,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 43487,
    "char_end": 44786,
    "char_count": 1299,
    "text": "The Second Party hereby undertakes to perform the following activities:\n1. The Vendor must follow all the standards and safety guidelines prescribed under state\nregulations and technical standards prescribed by MNRE for RTS projects, failing which\nthe vendor is liable for blacklisting from participation in the govt. project/ scheme and\nother penal actions in accordance with the law. The responsibility of supply, installation\nand commissioning of the rooftop solar project/system in complete compliance with\nMNRE scheme guidelines lies with the Vendor.\n2. Site Survey: Site visit, survey and development of detailed project report for installation\nof RTS system. This also includes, feasibility study of roof, strength of roof and shadow\nfree area.  If any additional work or customization is involved for the plant installation as\nper site condition and requirement of the consumer building, the Vendor shall prepare\nan estimate and can raise separate invoice including GST in addition to the amount\ntowards standard plant cost. The consumer shall pay the amount for such additional\nwork directly to the Vendor.\n3. Design & Engineering: Design of plant along with drawings and selection of components\nas per standard provided by the DISCOM/SERC/MNRE for best performance and safety\nof the plant.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0054",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 54,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 44788,
    "char_end": 44892,
    "char_count": 104,
    "text": "24\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0055",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 55,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 44893,
    "char_end": 45262,
    "char_count": 369,
    "text": "4. Module and Inverter: The solar modules, including the solar cells, should be\nmanufactured in India. Both the solar modules and inverters shall conform to the\nrelevant standards and specifications prescribed by MNRE. Any other requirement, viz.\nstar labelling (solar modules), quality control orders and standards & labelling (inverters)\netc., shall also be complied.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0056",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 56,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 45263,
    "char_end": 45514,
    "char_count": 251,
    "text": "5. Procurement & Supply: Procurement of complete system as per BIS/IS/IEC standard\n(whatever applicable) & safety guidelines for installation of rooftop solar plants. The\nsupplied materials should comply with all MNRE standards for release of subsidy.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0057",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 57,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 45515,
    "char_end": 45674,
    "char_count": 159,
    "text": "6. Installation & Civil work: Complete civil work, structure work and electrical work\n(including drawings) following all the safety and relevant BIS standards.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0058",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 58,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 45675,
    "char_end": 46052,
    "char_count": 377,
    "text": "7. Documentation (Technical Catalogues/Warranty Certificates/BIS certificates/other\ntest reports etc): All such documents shall be provided to the consumer for online\nuploading and submission of technical specifications, IEC/BIS report, Sr. Nos, Warranty\ncard of Solar Panel & Inverter, Layout & Electrical SLD, Structure Design and Drawing,\nCable and other detailed documents.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0059",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 59,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 46053,
    "char_end": 46200,
    "char_count": 147,
    "text": "8. Project completion report (PCR): Assisting the consumer in filling and uploading of\nsigned documents (Consumer & Vendor) on the national portal.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0060",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 60,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 46201,
    "char_end": 46587,
    "char_count": 386,
    "text": "9. Warranty: System warranty certificates should be provided to the consumer. The\ncomplete system should be warranted for 5 years from the date of commissioning by\nDISCOM. Individual component warranty documents provided by the manufacturer shall\nbe provided to the consumer and all possible assistance should be extended to the\nconsumer for claiming the warranty from the manufacturer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0061",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 61,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 46588,
    "char_end": 46773,
    "char_count": 185,
    "text": "10. NET meter & Grid Connectivity: Net meter supply/procurement, testing and approvals\nshall be in the scope of vendor. Grid connection of the plant shall be in the scope of the\nvendor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0062",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 62,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 46774,
    "char_end": 46888,
    "char_count": 114,
    "text": "11. Testing and Commissioning: The vendor shall be present at the time of testing and\ncommissioning by the DISCOM.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0063",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 63,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 46889,
    "char_end": 47220,
    "char_count": 331,
    "text": "12. Operation & Maintenance: Five (5) years Comprehensive Operation and Maintenance\nincluding overhauling, wear and tear and regular checking of healthiness of system at\nproper interval shall be in the scope of vendor. The vendor shall also educate the\nconsumer on best practices for cleaning of the modules and system maintenance.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0064",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 64,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 47222,
    "char_end": 48979,
    "char_count": 1757,
    "text": "25\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\n13. Insurance: Any insurance cost pertaining to material transfer/storage before\ncommissioning of the system shall be in the scope of the vendor.\n14. Applicable Standard: The system must meet the technical standards and specifications\nnotified by MNRE. The vendor is solely responsible to supply component and service\nwhich meets the technical standards and specification prescribed by MNRE and State\nDISCOMs.\n15. Project/system cost & payment terms:  The cost of the plant and payment schedule\nshould be mutually discussed and decided between the vendor and consumer. The\nconsumer may opt for milestone-based payment to the vendor and the same shall be\nincluded in the agreement.\n16. Dispute:\nIn-case\nof\nany\ndispute\nbetween\nconsumer\nand\nvendor\n(in\nsupply/installation/maintenance of system or payment terms), both parties must settle\nthe same mutually or as per law. MNRE/DISCOM shall not be liable for, and would not\nbe a party to any dispute arising between vendor and consumer.\n17. Subsidy / Project Related Documents: Vendor must provide all the documents to\nconsumer and help in uploading the same to National Portal for smooth release of\nsubsidy.\n18. Performance of Plant: The Performance Ratio (PR) of Plant must be 75% at the time of\ncommissioning of the project by DISCOM or its authorised agency. Vendor must provide\n(returnable basis) radiation sensor with valid calibration certificate of any NABL /\nInternational laboratory at the time of commissioning / testing of the plant. Vendor must\nmaintain the PR of the plant till warranty of project i.e. 5 years from the date of\ncommissioning.\n19. Mutually Agreed Terms of Payment …\nFirst Party",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0065",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 65,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 48981,
    "char_end": 49037,
    "char_count": 56,
    "text": "Second Party\nName\n\nName\nAddress\n\nAddress\nSign\n\nSign\nDate",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0066",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 66,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 49039,
    "char_end": 49043,
    "char_count": 4,
    "text": "Date",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0067",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 67,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 49045,
    "char_end": 49320,
    "char_count": 275,
    "text": "26\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nDisclaimer: This agreement is between vendor and consumer and any dispute related to the same\nshall not involve any third party including MNRE and Distribution Utilities.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0068",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 68,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 49322,
    "char_end": 49587,
    "char_count": 265,
    "text": "27\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nAnnexure 3\nTECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS FOR ROOFTOP SOLAR PLANTS INSTALLED\nUNDER THE COMPONENT OF “CFA TO RESIDENTIAL CONSUMERS” OF\nPM-SURYA GHAR: MUFT BIJLI YOJANA",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0069",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 69,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 49589,
    "char_end": 50639,
    "char_count": 1050,
    "text": "The projects under PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana shall be commissioned as per the\ntechnical specifications given below. The vendor will be solely responsible for any\nshortcomings or negligence/malpractice, which may lead to the delisting/blacklisting of the\nfirm/vendor from participation in any programme of the Ministry.\nA Roof Top Solar (RTS) Photo Voltaic (PV) system shall be installed on\nrooftops/terraces/balcony/Building Integrated Photovoltaic (BIPV) or on elevated\nstructures. In case of installation on an elevated structure, the structure must have a\nminimum ground clearance of 8 feet at the lowest point, in order to be considered eligible\nfor the CFA under the scheme. The RTS system shall consist of the following:\n1. Solar Photo Voltaic (SPV) modules consisting of required number of SPV modules\n2. Inverter/PCU\n3. Module Mounting structures\n4. Net Meter/Smart Meter\n5. Array Junction Boxes\n6. DC Distribution Box\n7. AC Distribution Box\n8. Protections – Earthing, Lightning, Surge\n9. Cables\n10. Drawing & Manuals\n11. Miscellaneous",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0070",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 70,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 50641,
    "char_end": 51448,
    "char_count": 807,
    "text": "28\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nComponents/Package of Grid Connected Rooftop Solar PV System: The components of a Grid\nConnected Rooftop Solar PV System shall essentially comprise but not be limited to solar PV\nPanels/modules of required number, Inverters/PCU, module mounting structures of minimum\n600mm ground clearance at the lowest point from the roof surface, total Cable/wiring of\nsuitable length, cable conduits, required array junction boxes, DC distribution box, AC\ndistribution box, various connectors, nut- bolts, civil and mechanical works, Protection-\nEarthing, lightning, surges, drawling & manual, 05 years of comprehensive operation &\nmaintenance of grid-connected rooftop solar PV plant and other miscellaneous works.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0071",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 71,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 51450,
    "char_end": 52792,
    "char_count": 1342,
    "text": "1. Solar PV modules\n1.1.\nDomestic Manufactured Solar PV modules using domestically manufactured Solar\ncells shall be used in the Scheme.\n1.2.\nThe PV modules used must qualify to the latest edition of IEC standards or\nequivalent BIS standards, i.e. IEC 61215/IS 14286, IEC 61853-Part I or IS 16170-Part\nI, IS/IEC 61730 Part-1 & Part 2 and IS 17210(part 1) or IEC 62804-1 (PID). For the PV\nmodules to be used in a highly corrosive atmosphere throughout their lifetime,\nthey must qualify to IEC   61701/IS 61701. Thin - Film terrestrial photovoltaic (PV)\nmodules must qualify to IS 16077: 2013 / IEC 61646: 2008\n1.3.\nThe rated power of solar PV module shall have maximum tolerance up to +3%.\n1.4.\nThe peak-power point current of any supplied module string (series connected\nmodules) shall not vary by +1% from the respective arithmetic means for all\nmodules and/or for all module strings (connected to the same MPPT), as the case\nmay be.\n1.5.\nThe peak-power point voltage of any supplied module string (series connected\nmodules) shall not vary by + 2% from the respective arithmetic means for all\nmodules and/or for all module strings (connected to the same MPPT), as the case\nmay be.\n1.6.\nThe temperature co-efficient power of the PV module shall be equal to or better\nthan -0.4%/°C for crystalline modules and -0.3 %/°C for thin films modules.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0072",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 72,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 52794,
    "char_end": 53549,
    "char_count": 755,
    "text": "29\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\n1.7.\nSolar PV modules capacity to be used should adhere to the Approved List of Models\nand Manufacturers (ALMM)   of Solar Photovoltaic Modules (Requirement for\nCompulsory Registration) Order 2019 - Implementation issued vide OM NO.\n283/54/2018-GRID SOLAR -Part (I) Dated 10th March 2021 and subsequent\namendments.\n1.8.\nSolar PV modules of minimum fill factor 75%, to be used.\n1.9.\nAll PV modules should have a nominal power output of >90% at STC during the first\n10 years, and >80% during the next 15 years. Further, module shall have nominal\npower output of >97% during the first year of installation—degradation of the\nmodule below 0.5 % per annum",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0073",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 73,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 53550,
    "char_end": 54225,
    "char_count": 675,
    "text": "1.10. The manufacturer should warrant the Solar Module(s) to be free from the defects\nand/or failures specified below for a period not less than five (5) years from the\ndate of commissioning.\ni.\nDefects and/or failures due to manufacturing.\nii. Defects and/or failures due to quality of materials.\niii. Nonconformity to specifications due to faulty manufacturing and/or\ninspection processes. If the solar Module(s) fails to conform to this warranty,\nthe manufacturer will repair or replace the solar module(s), at the Owners sole\noption. The PV modules shall be replaced by manufacturers, without charging\nany cost to the end consumer during the specified period of warranty.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0074",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 74,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 54226,
    "char_end": 54853,
    "char_count": 627,
    "text": "1.11. Modules deployed must use a RF identification tag laminated inside the glass. The\nfollowing information must be mentioned in the RFID used on each module:\ni.\nName of the manufacturer of the PV module\nii.\nName of the manufacturer of Solar Cells.\niii.\nMonth & year of the manufacture (separate for solar cells and modules)\niv.\nCountry of origin (separately for solar cells and module)\nv.\nI-V curve for the module Wattage, Im, Vm and FF for the module\nvi.\nUnique Serial No and Model No of the module\nvii.\nDate and year of obtaining IEC PV module qualification certificate.\nviii.\nName of the test lab issuing IEC certificate.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0075",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 75,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 54855,
    "char_end": 55112,
    "char_count": 257,
    "text": "30\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nix.\nOther relevant information on traceability of solar cells and module as per\nISO 9001 and ISO 14001.\nx.\nNominal wattage +3%.\nxi.\nName, if applicable.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0076",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 76,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 55114,
    "char_end": 55629,
    "char_count": 515,
    "text": "1.12. Other details as per IS/IEC 61730-1 clause 11 should be provided at appropriate\nplace. In addition to the above, the following information should also be provided:\ni.\nThe actual Power Output Pmax shall be mentioned on the label pasted on\nthe back side of PV Module.\nii.\nThe Maximum system voltage for which the module is suitable to be\nprovided on the back sheet of the module.\niii.\nPolarity of terminals or leads (colour coding is permissible) on junction Box\nhousing near cable entry or cable and connector.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0077",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 77,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 55631,
    "char_end": 55800,
    "char_count": 169,
    "text": "1.13. Unique Serial No, Model No, Name of Manufacturer, Manufacturing year, Make in\nIndia logo and module wattage details should be displayed inside the laminated\nglass.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0078",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 78,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 55802,
    "char_end": 56604,
    "char_count": 802,
    "text": "2. Inverter/PCU\n2.1 The Solar Photovoltaic Inverters must comply with the Quality Control Order dated\n30.08.2017  for Solar Photovoltaic Inverters and its amendments thereof.\n2.2 Inverters/PCU should comply with applicable IEC/equivalent BIS standard for efficiency\nmeasurements and environmental tests as per standard codes IEC 61683/IS 61683, IS\n16221 (Part 2), IS 16169 and IEC 60068-2(1,2,14,30)\n2.3 /Equivalent BIS Std.\n2.4 Maximum Power Point Tracker (MPPT) shall be integrated in the inverter/PCU to\nmaximize energy drawn from the array. Charge controller (if any) / MPPT units\nenvironmental testing should qualify IEC 60068-2(1, 2, 14, 30)/Equivalent BIS standard.\nThe junction boxes/enclosures should be IP 65 or better (for outdoor)/ IP 54or better\n(indoor) and as per IEC 529 Specifications.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0079",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 79,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 56606,
    "char_end": 57981,
    "char_count": 1375,
    "text": "31\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\n2.5 All inverters/PCUs shall be IEC 61000 compliant for electromagnetic compatibility,\nharmonics, Surge, etc.\n2.6 The PCU/ inverter shall have overloading capacity of minimum 20%.\n2.7 Typical technical features of the inverter shall be as follows-\ni.\nNominal AC output voltage and frequency: as per CEA/State regulations\nii.\nOutput frequency: 50 Hz\niii.\nGrid Frequency Synchronization range: as per CEA/State Regulations\niv.\nAmbient temperature considered: -20°C to 60°C\nv.\nProtection of Enclosure: IP-54 (Minimum) for indoor and IP-65(Minimum) for\noutdoor.\nvi.\nGrid Frequency Tolerance range: as per CEA/State regulations\nvii.\nGrid Voltage tolerance: as per CEA/State Regulations\nviii.\nNo-load losses: Less than 1% of rated power\nix.\nInverter efficiency (Min.): >90% (In case of 10 kW or below with in-built galvanic\nisolation)\nx.\nThe Minimum Overall Efficiency (ηt) as per IS 17980 for Solar Inverters should\nadhere to the following:\nxi.\nTHD: < 3%\nxii.\nPF: > 0.9 (lag or lead)\nxiii.\nShould not inject DC power more than 0.5% of full rated output at the\ninterconnection point and comply to IEEE 519.\nxiv.\nThe inverter should have the inbuilt facility to communicate system related\ndata through SIM/dongle. The inverter may also be enabled for Wi-Fi based\ncommunication.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0080",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 80,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 57983,
    "char_end": 58305,
    "char_count": 322,
    "text": "2.8 All the Inverters should contain the following clear and indelible Marking Label &\nWarning Label as per IS16221 Part II, clause 5. The equipment shall, as a minimum, be\npermanently marked with:\ni.\nThe name or trademark of the manufacturer or supplier;\nii.\nA model number, name or other means to identify the equipment,",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0081",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 81,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 58307,
    "char_end": 58724,
    "char_count": 417,
    "text": "32\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\niii.\nA serial number, code or other marking allowing identification of\nmanufacturing location and the manufacturing batch or date within a twelve-\nmonth time period.\niv.\nInput voltage, type of voltage (a.c. or d.c.), frequency, and maximum\ncontinuous current for each input.\nv.\nThe Ingress Protection (IP) rating",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0082",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 82,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 58726,
    "char_end": 59736,
    "char_count": 1010,
    "text": "2.9 In case the consumer is having a 3-ϕ connection, 1-ϕ/3-ϕ inverter shall be provided by\nthe vendor as per the consumer’s requirement and regulations of the State.\n2.10 Inverter/PCU shall be capable of complete automatic operation including wake-up,\nsynchronization & shutdown.\n2.11 Integration of PV Power with Grid & Grid Islanding:\ni.\nIn the event of a power failure on the electric grid, it is required that any\nindependent power-producing inverters attached to the grid turn off in a short\nperiod of time. This prevents the DC-to-AC inverters from continuing to feed power\ninto small sections of the grid, known as “islands.” Powered islands present a risk to\nworkers who may expect the area to be unpowered, and they may also damage\ngrid-tied equipment. The Rooftop PV system shall be equipped with islanding\nprotection. In addition to disconnection from the grid (due to islanding protection)\ndisconnection due to under and over voltage conditions shall also be provided, if\nnot available in inverter.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0083",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 83,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 59738,
    "char_end": 60162,
    "char_count": 424,
    "text": "3. Module Mounting Structure (MMS):\n3.1 Supply, installation, erection and acceptance of module mounting structure (MMS) with\nall necessary accessories, auxiliaries and spare part shall be in the scope of the work.\n3.2 Module mounting structures can be made from three types of materials. They are Hot Dip\nGalvanized Iron, Aluminium and Hot Dip Galvanized Mild Steel (MS). However, MS will be\npreferred for raised structure.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0084",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 84,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 60164,
    "char_end": 61951,
    "char_count": 1787,
    "text": "33\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\n3.3 MMS Steel shall be as per latest IS 2062:2011 and galvanization of the mounting structure\nshall be in compliance of latest IS 4759. MMS Aluminium shall be as per AA6063 T6. For\nAluminium structures, necessary protection towards rusting need to be provided either\nby coating or anodization.\n3.4 All bolts, nuts, fasteners shall be of stainless steel of grade SS 304 or hot dip galvanized,\npanel mounting clamps shall be of aluminium and must sustain the adverse climatic\nconditions. Structural material shall be corrosion resistant and electrolytically compatible\nwith the materials used in the module frame, its fasteners, nuts and bolts.\n3.5 The module mounting structures should have angle of inclination as per the site\nconditions to take maximum insolation and complete shadow-free operation during\ngeneration hours. However, to accommodate more capacity the angle of inclination may\nbe reduced until the plant meets the specified performance ratio requirements.\n3.6 The Mounting structure shall be so designed to withstand the speed for the wind zone of\nthe location where a PV system is proposed to be installed. The PV array structure design\nshall be appropriate with a factor of safety of minimum 1.5.\n3.7 The upper edge of the module must be covered with wind shield so as to avoid build air\ningress below the module. Slight clearance must be provided on both edges (upper &\nlower) to allow air for cooling.\n3.8 Suitable fastening arrangement such as grouting and calming should be provided to\nsecure the installation against the specific wind speed. The Empanelled Agency shall be\nfully responsible for any damages to SPV System caused due to high wind velocity within",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0085",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 85,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 61952,
    "char_end": 62616,
    "char_count": 664,
    "text": "guarantee period as per technical specification.\n3.9 The structures shall be designed to allow easy replacement, repairing and cleaning of any\nmodule. The array structure shall be so designed that it will occupy minimum space\nwithout sacrificing the output from the SPV panels. Necessary testing provision for MMS\nto be made available at site.\n3.10 Adequate spacing shall be provided between two panel frames and rows of panels to\nfacilitate personnel protection, ease of installation, replacement, cleaning of panels and\nelectrical maintenance.\n3.11 The structure shall be designed to withstand operating environmental conditions for a\nperiod of minimum 25 years.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0086",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 86,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 62618,
    "char_end": 63277,
    "char_count": 659,
    "text": "34\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\n3.12 The Rooftop Structures maybe classified in three broad categories as follows:\ni.\nBallast structure\na. The mounting structure must be Non-invasive ballast type and any sort of penetration of\nroof to be avoided.\nb. The minimum clearance of the structure from the roof level should be in between 70-\n150 mm to allow ventilation for cooling, also ease of cleaning and maintenance of panels\nas well as cleaning of terrace.\nc. The structures should be suitably loaded with reinforced concrete blocks of appropriate\nweight made out of M25 concrete mixture.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0087",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 87,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 63279,
    "char_end": 63869,
    "char_count": 590,
    "text": "ii.\nTin shed\na. The structure design should be as per the slope of the tin shed.\nb. The inclination angle of structure can be done in two ways-\nc. Parallel to the tin shed (flat keeping zero-degree tiling angle), if the slope of shed in\nProper south direction\nd. With same tilt angle based on the slope of tin shed to get the maximum output.\ne. The minimum clearance of the lowest point from the tin shade should be more then\n100mm.\nf. The base of structure should be connected on the Purlin of tin shed with the proper\nriveting.\ng. All structure member should be of minimum 2 mm thickness.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0088",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 88,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 63871,
    "char_end": 64180,
    "char_count": 309,
    "text": "iii.\nRCC Elevated structure: It can be divided into further three categories:\nA\nMinimum clearance from roof (upto 1000 MM) (for reference only)\na. The structure shall be designed to allow easy replacement of any module and shall be in\nline with site requirement. The gap between module should be minimum 30MM.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0089",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 89,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 64182,
    "char_end": 65368,
    "char_count": 1186,
    "text": "35\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nb. Base Plate – Base plate thickness of the Structure should be 5MM for this segment.\nc. Column – Structure Column should be minimum 2MM in Lip section / 3MM in C-Channel\nsection. The minimum section should be 70MM in Web side and 40 MM in flange side in\nLip section.\nd. Rafter - Structure rafter should be minimum 2MM in Lip section / 3MM in C-Channel\nsection. The minimum section should be 70MM in Web side (y- axis) and 40 MM in flange\nside (x-axis).\ne. Purlin - Structure purlin should be minimum 2MM in Lip section. The minimum section\nshould be 60MM in Web side and 40MM in flange side in Lip section.\nf. Front/back bracing – The section for bracing part should be minimum 2MM  thickness.\ng. Connection – The structure connection should be bolted completely. Leg to rafter should\nbe connected with minimum 12 diameter bolt. Rafter and purlin should be connected\nwith minimum 10 diameter bolt. Module mounting fasteners should be SS-304 only and\nremaining fasteners either SS-304 or HDG 8.8 Grade.\nh. For single portrait structure the minimum ground clearance should be 500MM.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0090",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 90,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 65370,
    "char_end": 66049,
    "char_count": 679,
    "text": "B\nMedium clearance from roof (1000MM – 2000 MM) ( for reference only)\na. Base Plate – Base plate thickness of the Structure should be Minimum 6MM for this\nsegment.\nb. Column – Structure Column should be minimum 2MM in Lip section / 3MM in C-Channel\nsection. The minimum section should be 80MM in Web side and 50MM in flange side in\nLip section.\nc. Rafter - Structure rafter should be minimum 2MM in Lip section / 3MM in C-Channel\nsection. The minimum section should be 70MM in Web side and 40MM in flange side in\nLip section.\nd. Purlin - Structure purlin should be minimum 2MM in Lip section. The minimum section\nshould be 70MM in Web side and 40MM in flange side in Lip section.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0091",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 91,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 66051,
    "char_end": 66550,
    "char_count": 499,
    "text": "36\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\ne. Front/back bracing – The section for bracing part should be minimum 2MM thickness.\nf. Connection – The structure connection should be bolted completely. Leg to rafter\nshould be connected with minimum 12 diameter bolt. Rafter and purlin should be\nconnected with minimum 10 diameter bolt. Module mounting fasteners should be SS-\n304 only and remaining fasteners either SS-304 or HDG 8.8 Grade.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0092",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 92,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 66552,
    "char_end": 67624,
    "char_count": 1072,
    "text": "C\nMaximum clearance from roof (2000MM – 3000 MM) (for reference only)\na. Base Plate – Base plate thickness of the Structure should be minimum 8 MM for this\nsegment.\nb. Column – Structure Column thickness should be minimum 2.6MM in square hollow\nsection (minimum 50x50) or rectangular hollow section (minimum 60x40) or 3MM in C-\nChannel section.\nc. Rafter - Structure rafter should be minimum 2MM in Lip section / 3MM in Channel\nsection. The minimum section should be 80MM in Web side and 50MM in flange side in\nLip section.\nd. Purlin - Structure purlin should be minimum 2MM in Lip section. The minimum section\nshould be 80MM in Web side and 50MM in flange side in Lip section.\ne. Front/back bracing – The section for bracing part should be minimum 3MM thickness.\nf. Connection – The structure connection should be bolted completely. Leg to rafter\nshould be connected with minimum 12 diameter bolt. Rafter and purlin should be\nconnected with minimum 10 diameter bolt. Module mounting fasteners should be SS-\n304 only and remaining fasteners either SS-304 or HDG 8.8 Grade.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0093",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 93,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 67626,
    "char_end": 67818,
    "char_count": 192,
    "text": "D\nSuper elevated structure (More than 3000 MM clearance from roof) (for reference only)\nA.\nBase structure\na. Base Plate – Base plate thickness of the Structure should be 10MM for this segment.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0094",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 94,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 67820,
    "char_end": 69544,
    "char_count": 1724,
    "text": "37\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nb. Column – Structure Column minimum thickness should be minimum 2.9MM in square\nhollow section (minimum 60x60) or rectangular hollow section (minimum 80x40).\nc. Rafter - Structure Rafter minimum thickness should be minimum 2.9MM in square\nhollow section (minimum 60x60) or rectangular hollow section (minimum 80x40).\nd. Cross bracing – Bracing for the connection of rafter and column should be of minimum\nthickness of 4mm L-angle with the help of minimum bolt diameter of 10mm.\nB.\nUpper structure of super elevated structure –\na. Base Plate – Base plate thickness of the Structure should be minimum 5MM for this\nsegment.\nb. Column – Structure Column should be minimum 2MM in Lip section / 3MM in Channel\nsection. The minimum section should be 70MM in Web side and 40MM in flange side in\nLip section.\nc. Rafter - Structure rafter should be minimum 2MM in Lip section / 3MM in Channel\nsection. The minimum section should be 70MM in Web side and 40MM in flange side in\nLip section.\nd. Purlin - Structure purlin should be minimum 2MM in Lip section. The minimum section\nshould be 60MM in Web side and 40MM in flange side in Lip section.\ne. Front/back bracing – The section for bracing part should be minimum 2MM thickness.\nf. Connection – The structure connection should be bolted completely. Leg to rafter\nshould be connected with minimum 12 diameter bolt. Rafter and\ng. purlin should be connected with minimum 10 diameter bolt. Module mounting\nfasteners should be SS-304 only and remaining fasteners either SS-304 or HDG 8.8 Grade.\nC.\nIf distance between two legs in X-Direction is more than 3M than sag angle/Bar should",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0095",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 95,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 69545,
    "char_end": 69845,
    "char_count": 300,
    "text": "be provide for purlin to avoid deflection failure. The sag angle should be minimum\n2MM thick, and bar should be minimum 12Dia.\nD.\nDegree - The Module alignment and tilt angle shell be calculated to provide the\nmaximum annual energy output. This shall be decided on the location of array\ninstallation.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0096",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 96,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 69847,
    "char_end": 70724,
    "char_count": 877,
    "text": "38\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nE.\nFoundation – Foundation should be as per the roof condition; two types of the\nfoundation can be done- either penetrating the roof or without penetrating the roof.\na. If penetration on the roof is allowed (based on the client requirement) then minimum\n12MM diameter anchor fasteners with minimum length 100MM can be used with\nproper chipping. The minimum RCC size should be 400x400x300 cubic mm. Material\ngrade of foundation should be minimum M20.\nb. If penetration on roof is not allowed, then foundation can be done with the help of ‘J\nBolt’ (refer IS 5624 for foundation hardware). Proper Neto bond solution should be used\nto adhere the Foundation block with the RCC roof. Foundation J - bolt length should be\nminimum 12MM diameter and length should be minimum 300MM.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0097",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 97,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 70726,
    "char_end": 71734,
    "char_count": 1008,
    "text": "F.\nMaterial standards:\na. Design of foundation for mounting the structure should be as per defined standards\nwhich clearly states the Load Bearing Capacity & other relevant parameters for\nfoundation design (As per IS 6403 / 456 / 4091 / 875).\nb. Grade of raw material to be used for mounting the structures so that it complies the\ndefined wind loading conditions (As per IS 875 - III) should be referred as follows (IS\n2062 – for angles and channels, IS 1079 – for sheet, IS 1161 & 1239 for round pipes, IS\n4923 for rectangular and square hollow section)\nc. Test reports for the raw material should be as per IS 1852 / 808 / 2062 / 1079 / 811.\nd. In process inspection report as per approved drawing & tolerance should be as per IS\n7215.\ne. For ascertaining proper welding of structure part following should be referred:\nf. D.P. Test (Pin Hole / Crack) (IS 822)\ng. Weld wire grade should be of grade (ER 70 S - 6)\nh. For ascertaining hot dip galvanizing of fabricated structure following should be\nreferred:-",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0098",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 98,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 71736,
    "char_end": 72256,
    "char_count": 520,
    "text": "39\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\ni. Min coating required should be as per IS 4759 & EN 1461.\nj. Testing of galvanized material\na) Pierce Test (IS 2633)\nb) Mass of Zinc (IS 6745)\nc) Adhesion Test (IS 2629)\nd) CuSO4 Test (IS 2633)\ne) Superior High-Grade Zinc Ingot should be of 99.999% purity (IS 209) (Preferably\nHindustan Zinc Limited or Equivalent).\nk. Foundation Hardware – If using foundation bolt in foundation then it should be as per\nIS 5624.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0099",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 99,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 72258,
    "char_end": 72919,
    "char_count": 661,
    "text": "4. Metering\n4.1 The specifications net meter/smart meter shall be as per the latest technical specifications\nissued by the Central Electricity Authority (CEA) and its amendment thereof.\n4.2 A Roof Top Solar (RTS) Photo Voltaic (PV) system shall consist of following energy meters:\na) Net meter/ smart meter: To record import and export units.\nb) Generation meter (if required as per the state regulations: To keep record for total\ngeneration of the plant.\n4.3 The installation of meters including CTs & PTs, wherever applicable, shall be carried out\nby the respective DisComs as per the terms, conditions and procedures laid down by the\nconcerned SERCs/DISCOMs.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0100",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 100,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 72921,
    "char_end": 73499,
    "char_count": 578,
    "text": "5. Array Junction Boxes\n5.1 The junction boxes are to be provided in the PV array for termination of connecting cables.\nThe Junction Boxes (JBs) shall be made of GRP/FRP/Powder Coated aluminum /cast aluminum\nalloy with full dust, water & vermin proof arrangement. All wires/cables must be terminated\nthrough cable lugs. The JBs shall be such that input & output termination can be made through\nsuitable cable glands. Suitable markings shall be provided on the bus-bars for easy\nidentification and cable ferrules will be fitted at the cable termination points for identification.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0101",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 101,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 73501,
    "char_end": 74361,
    "char_count": 860,
    "text": "40\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\n5.2 Copper bus bars/terminal blocks housed in the junction box with suitable termination threads\nConforming to IP 65 or better standard and IEC 62208 Hinged door with EPDM rubber gasket\nto prevent water entry, Single /double compression cable glands should be provided.\n5.3 Polyamide glands and MC4 Connectors may also be provided. The rating of the junction box\nshall be suitable with adequate safety factor to interconnect the Solar PV array.\n5.4 Suitable markings shall be provided on the bus bar for easy identification and the cable\nferrules must be fitted at the cable termination points for identification.\n5.5 Junction boxes shall be mounted on the MMS such that they are easily accessible and are\nprotected from direct sunlight and harsh weather.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0102",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 102,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 74363,
    "char_end": 74996,
    "char_count": 633,
    "text": "6. DC Distribution Box (DCDB)\n6.1 May not be required for small plants, if suitable arrangement is available in the inverter.\n6.2 DC Distribution Box are to be provided to receive the DC output from the PV array field.\n6.3 DCDBs shall be dust & vermin proof conform having IP 65 or better protection, as per site\nconditions.\n6.4 The bus bars are made of EC grade copper of required size. Suitable capacity MCBs/MCCB shall\nbe provided for controlling the DC power output to the inverter along with necessary surge\narrestors. MCB shall be used for currents up to 63 Amperes, and MCCB shall be used for\ncurrents greater than 63 Amperes.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0103",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 103,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 74998,
    "char_end": 75679,
    "char_count": 681,
    "text": "7. AC Distribution Box (ACDB)\n7.1 AC Distribution Panel Board (DPB) shall control the AC power from inverter, and should have\nnecessary surge arrestors, if required. There is interconnection from ACDB to mains at LT Bus\nbar while in grid tied mode.\n7.2 All switches and the circuit breakers, connectors should conform to IEC 60947:2019, part I, II\nand III/ IS 60947 part I, II and III.\n7.3 The isolators, cabling work should be undertaken as part of the project.\n7.4 All the Panel’s shall be metal clad, totally enclosed, rigid, floor mounted, air -insulated, cubical\ntype suitable for operation on 1-ϕ/3-ϕ, 415 or 230 volts, 50 Hz (or voltage levels as per\nCEA/State regulations).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0104",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 104,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 75681,
    "char_end": 76878,
    "char_count": 1197,
    "text": "41\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\n7.5 The panels shall be designed for minimum expected ambient temperature of 45 degree\nCelsius, 80 percent humidity and dusty weather.\n7.6 All indoor panels will have protection of IP 54 or better, as per site conditions. All outdoor\npanels will have protection of IP 65 or better, as per site conditions.\n7.7 Should conform to Indian Electricity Act and CEA safety regulations (till last amendment).\n7.8 All the 415 or 230 volts (or voltage levels as per CEA/State regulations) AC devices / equipment\nlike bus support insulators, circuit breakers, SPDs, Voltage Transformers (VTs) etc., mounted\ninside the switchgear shall be suitable for continuous operation and satisfactory performance\nunder the following supply conditions.\na. Variation in supply voltage: as per CEA/State regulations\nb. Variation in supply frequency: as per CEA/State regulations\n7.9 The inverter output shall have the necessary rated AC surge arrestors, if required and MCB/\nMCCB. RCCB shall be used for successful operation of the PV system, if inverter does not have\nrequired earth fault/residual current protection.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0105",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 105,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 76880,
    "char_end": 77816,
    "char_count": 936,
    "text": "8. Protections\nThe system should be provided with all necessary protections like earthing, Lightning, and\nSurge Protection, as described below:\n8.1 Earthing Protection\n8.1.1 The earthing shall be done in accordance with latest Standards.\n8.1.2 Each array structure of the PV yard, Low Tension (LT) power system, earthing grid for\nswitchyard, all electrical equipment, inverter, all junction boxes, etc. shall be grounded\nproperly as per IS 3043-2018.\n8.1.3 All metal casing/ shielding of the plant shall be thoroughly grounded in accordance\nwith CEA Safety Regulation 2010. In addition, the lightning arrester/masts should also\nbe earthed inside the array field.\n8.1.4 Earth resistance should be as low as possible and shall never be higher than 5 ohms.\n8.1.5 For 10 KW and above systems, separate three earth pits shall be provided for individual\nthree earthing viz.: DC side earthing, AC side earthing and lightning arrestor earthing.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0106",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 106,
    "page_start": 42,
    "page_end": 42,
    "char_start": 77818,
    "char_end": 79135,
    "char_count": 1317,
    "text": "42\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\n8.2 Lightning Protection\n8.2.1 The SPV power plants shall be provided with lightning & over voltage protection, if\nrequired. The main aim in this protection shall be to reduce the overvoltage to a\ntolerable value before it reaches the PV or other sub system components. The source\nof over voltage can be lightning, atmosphere disturbances etc. Lightning arrestor shall\nnot be installed on the mounting structure.\n8.2.2 The entire space occupying the SPV array shall be suitably protected against\nLightning by deploying required number of Lightning Arrestors (LAs). Lightning\nprotection should be provided as per NFC17-102:2011/IEC 62305 standard.\n8.2.3 The protection against induced high-voltages shall be provided by the use of Metal\nOxide Varistors (MOVs)/Franklin Rod type LA/Early streamer type LA.\n8.2.4 The current carrying cable from lightning arrestor to the earth pit should have\nsufficient current carrying capacity according to IEC 62305. According to standard,\nthe minimum requirement for a lightning protection system designed for class of\nLPS III is a 6 mm2 copper/ 16 mm2 aluminum or GI strip bearing size 25*3 mm thick).\nSeparate pipe for running earth wires of Lightning Arrestor shall be used.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0107",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 107,
    "page_start": 42,
    "page_end": 42,
    "char_start": 79137,
    "char_end": 79337,
    "char_count": 200,
    "text": "8.3 Surge Protection\n8.3.1 Internal surge protection, wherever required, shall be provided. It will consist of three\nSPD type-II/MOV type surge arrestors connected from +ve and –ve terminals to earth.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0108",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 108,
    "page_start": 42,
    "page_end": 42,
    "char_start": 79339,
    "char_end": 79730,
    "char_count": 391,
    "text": "9. Cables\n9.1 All cables should conform to latest edition of IEC/equivalent BIS Standards along with\nIEC 60227/IS 694, IEC 60502/IS 1554 standards.\n9.2 Cables should be flexible and should have good resistance to heat, cold, water, oil,\nabrasion etc.\n9.3 Armored cable should be used and overall PVC type ‘A’ pressure extruded insulation or\nXLPE insulation should be there for UV protection.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0109",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 109,
    "page_start": 43,
    "page_end": 43,
    "char_start": 79732,
    "char_end": 81131,
    "char_count": 1399,
    "text": "43\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\n9.4 Cables should have Multi Strand, annealed high conductivity copper conductor on DC\nside and copper/FRLS type Aluminum conductor on AC side. For DC cabling, multi- core\ncables shall not be used.\n9.5 Cables should have operating temperature range of -10°C to +80°C and voltage rating\nof 660/1000 V.\n9.6 Sizes of cables between array interconnections, array to junction boxes, junction boxes\nto Inverter etc. shall be so selected to keep the voltage drop less than 2% (DC Cable\nlosses).\n9.7 The size of each type of AC cable selected shall be based on minimum voltage drop.\nHowever; the maximum drop shall be limited to 2%.\n9.8 The electric cables for DC systems for rated voltage of 1500 V shall conform to IS\n17293:2020.\n9.9 All cable/wires are to be routed in a RPVC pipe/ GI cable tray and suitably tagged and\nmarked with proper manner by good quality ferule or by other means so that the cable\nis easily identified.\n9.10 All cable trays including covers to be provided.\n9.11 Thermo-plastic clamps to be used to clamp the cables and conduits, at intervals not\nexceeding 50 cm.\n9.12 Size of neutral wire shall be equal to the size of phase wires, in a three phase system.\n9.13 The Cable should be so selected that it should be compatible up to the life of the solar\nPV panels i.e. 25 years.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0110",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 110,
    "page_start": 43,
    "page_end": 43,
    "char_start": 81133,
    "char_end": 81622,
    "char_count": 489,
    "text": "10. Drawings & Manuals:\n\n10.1 Operation & Maintenance manual/user manual, Engineering and Electrical Drawings\nshall be supplied along with the power plant.\n10.2 The manual shall include complete system details such as array lay out, schematic of\nthe system, inverter details, working principle etc.\n10.3 The Manual should also include all the Dos & Don’ts of Power Plant along with Graphical\nRepresentation with indication of proper methodology for cleaning, Operation and\nMaintenance etc.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0111",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 111,
    "page_start": 44,
    "page_end": 44,
    "char_start": 81624,
    "char_end": 81897,
    "char_count": 273,
    "text": "44\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\n10.4 Step by step maintenance and troubleshooting procedures shall also be given in the\nmanuals.\n10.5 Vendors should also educate the consumers during their AMC period.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0112",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 112,
    "page_start": 44,
    "page_end": 44,
    "char_start": 81899,
    "char_end": 82753,
    "char_count": 854,
    "text": "11. Miscellaneous:\n11.1\nConnectivity: The maximum capacity for interconnection with the grid at a specific\nvoltage level shall be as specified in the SERC regulation for Grid connectivity and\nnorms of DISCOM and amended from time to time.\n11.2 Safety measures: Electrical safety of the installation(s) including connectivity with the\ngrid must be taken into account and all the safety rules & regulations applicable as per\nElectricity Act, 2003 and CEA Safety Regulation 2010 etc. must be followed.\n11.3 Shadow analysis: The shadow analysis report with the instrument such as Solar\nPathfinder or professional shadow analysis software of each site should be provided\nand the consumer should be educated to install the system only in shadow free space.\nLower performance of the system due to shadow effect shall be liable for penalty for\nlower performance.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0113",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 113,
    "page_start": 45,
    "page_end": 45,
    "char_start": 82755,
    "char_end": 84543,
    "char_count": 1788,
    "text": "45\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nQuality Certification, Standards and Testing for Grid-Connected Rooftop Solar PV Systems/Power Plants\nSolar PV Modules/Panels\nIEC 61215/\nIS 14286\nDesign Qualification and Type Approval for Crystalline Silicon Terrestrial\nPhotovoltaic (PV) Modules\nIS/IEC 61701\nSalt Mist Corrosion Testing of Photovoltaic (PV) Modules\nIEC 61853- 1 /\nIS 16170-1\nPhotovoltaic (PV) module performance testing and energy rating\n–:Irradiance and temperature performance measurements, and power\nRating.\nIEC 62716/ IS 16664\nPhotovoltaic (PV) Modules – Ammonia (NH3) Corrosion Testing (as per the\nsite condition like dairies, toilets etc)\nIS 16077 : 2013 / IEC\n61646 : 2008\nThin - Film terrestrial photovoltaic (PV) modules - Design qualification and\ntype approval\nIS/IEC 61730-1,2\nPhotovoltaic (PV) Module Safety Qualification – Part 1:\nRequirements for Construction, Part 2: Requirements for Testing\nIS 17210 (part 1) or\nIEC TS  62804-1\nPhotovoltaic (PV) modules – Test method for detection of potential-\ninduced degradation. IEC 62804-1: Part 1: Crystalline Silicon\nSolar PV Inverters\nIEC 62109 or\nIS : 16221\nSafety of power converters for use in photovoltaic power systems – Part 1:\nGeneral requirements, and Safety of power converters for use in\nphotovoltaic power systems\nPart 2: Particular requirements for inverters. Safety compliance (Protection\ndegree IP 65 or better for outdoor mounting, IP 54 or better for indoor\nmounting)\nIS/IEC 61683 latest\nPhotovoltaic Systems – Power conditioners: Procedure for\nMeasuring Efficiency (10%, 25%, 50%, 75% & 90-100% Loading Conditions)\n(as applicable)\nIEC 60068-2 /IEC 62093\n(as applicable)\nEnvironmental Testing of PV System – Power Conditioners and Inverters",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0114",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 114,
    "page_start": 46,
    "page_end": 46,
    "char_start": 84545,
    "char_end": 85885,
    "char_count": 1340,
    "text": "46\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nIEC 62116:2014/\nIS16169\nUtility-interconnected photovoltaic inverters - Test procedure of\nislanding prevention measures\nFuses\nIS/IEC 60947 (Part 1, 2\n& 3), EN 50521\nGeneral safety requirements for connectors, switches, circuit breakers\n(AC/DC):\n1)Low-voltage Switchgear and Control-gear, Part 1: General rules 2)Low-\nVoltage Switchgear and Control-gear, Part 2: Circuit Breakers\n3) Low-voltage\nswitchgear and\nControl-gear,\nPart\n3:\nSwitches,\ndisconnectors switch-disconnectors and fuse-combination units\n4) EN\n50521:\nConnectors\nfor\nphotovoltaic system-Safety\nrequirements and tests\nIS/IEC 60269-6\nLow-voltage fuses - Part 6: Supplementary requirements for fuse-\nLinks for the protection of solar photovoltaic energy systems\nSolar PV Roof Mounting Structure\nIS 2062/IS 4759/\nAA6063 T6\nMaterial for the structure mounting\nSurge Arrestors\nBFC 17-102:2011/\nNFC 102:2011/ IEC\n62305\nLightening Protection Standard\nIEC 60364-5-53/ IS\n15086-5 (SPD)\nIEC 61643- 11:2011\nElectrical installations of buildings - Part 5-53: Selection and erection of\nelectrical equipment - Isolation, switching and control Low-voltage surge\nprotective devices - Part 11: Surge protective\ndevices connected to low-voltage power systems - Requirements\nand test methods",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0115",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 115,
    "page_start": 47,
    "page_end": 47,
    "char_start": 85887,
    "char_end": 86072,
    "char_count": 185,
    "text": "47\nGuidelines for PM-Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana\nCentral Financial Assistance to Residential Consumers\nCables\nIEC 60227/IS 694, IEC\n60502/IS 1554 (Part\n1& 2)/ IEC69947 (as\napplicable)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0116",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 116,
    "page_start": 47,
    "page_end": 47,
    "char_start": 86074,
    "char_end": 86948,
    "char_count": 874,
    "text": "General test and measuring method for PVC (Polyvinyl chloride) insulated\ncables (for working voltages up to and including 1100 V, and resistant for\noutdoor installation)\nIS 17293:2020\nElectric Cables for Photovoltaic Systems for Rated Voltage 1500 V DC\nEarthing /Lightning\nIEC 62561/IEC 60634\nSeries (Chemical\nearthing) (as\napplicable)\nIEC 62561-1: Lightning protection system components (LPSC) - Part:\nRequirements for connection components\nIEC 62561-2: Lightning protection system components (LPSC) – Part\n2:Requirements for conductors and earth electrodes\nIEC 62561-7: Lightning protection system components (LPSC) - Part\n7:Requirements for earthing enhancing compounds\nJunction Boxes\nIEC 60529\nJunction boxes and solar panel terminal boxes shall be of the thermo-plastic\ntype with IP 65 or better protection for outdoor use, and IP 54 or better\nprotection for indoor use",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0117",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 117,
    "page_start": 48,
    "page_end": 48,
    "char_start": 86950,
    "char_end": 86952,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "48",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0118",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 118,
    "page_start": 48,
    "page_end": 48,
    "char_start": 86954,
    "char_end": 87239,
    "char_count": 285,
    "text": "Annexure 4\nModel Net Metering Agreement\n\nThis Agreement is made and entered into at (location) …………….. on this (date) …………….. day\nof (month) …………………. (year) …………… between the Eligible Consumer (Name) ……………\nhaving premises at (address) ……………… and Consumer No. ……………… as the first Party,",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0119",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 119,
    "page_start": 48,
    "page_end": 48,
    "char_start": 87241,
    "char_end": 87244,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "AND",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0120",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 120,
    "page_start": 48,
    "page_end": 48,
    "char_start": 87246,
    "char_end": 87425,
    "char_count": 179,
    "text": "The Distribution Licensee ………………………………. (hereinafter referred to as 'the Licensee') and\nhaving its Registered Office at (address) …………………………………. as second Party of this\nAgreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0121",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 121,
    "page_start": 48,
    "page_end": 48,
    "char_start": 87427,
    "char_end": 87706,
    "char_count": 279,
    "text": "Whereas, the Eligible Consumer has applied to the Licensee for approval of a Net Metering\nArrangement under the provisions of the (State Guidelines reference name)\n……………………………………………………. and subsequent amendments and sought its connectivity\nto the Licensee's Distribution Network.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0122",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 122,
    "page_start": 48,
    "page_end": 48,
    "char_start": 87708,
    "char_end": 87957,
    "char_count": 249,
    "text": "And whereas, the Licensee has agreed to provide Network connectivity to the Eligible\nConsumer for injection of electricity generated from its Roof-top Renewable Energy\nGenerating System of …………….. kilowatt (kW)\nBoth Parties hereby agree as follows:-",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0123",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 123,
    "page_start": 48,
    "page_end": 48,
    "char_start": 87959,
    "char_end": 87974,
    "char_count": 15,
    "text": "1.\nEligibility:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0124",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 124,
    "page_start": 49,
    "page_end": 49,
    "char_start": 87976,
    "char_end": 87978,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "49",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0125",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 125,
    "page_start": 49,
    "page_end": 49,
    "char_start": 87980,
    "char_end": 88211,
    "char_count": 231,
    "text": "The Roof-top Renewable Energy Generating System meets the applicable norms for being\nintegrated into the Distribution Network, and that the Eligible Consumer shall maintain the\nSystem accordingly for the duration of this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0126",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 126,
    "page_start": 49,
    "page_end": 49,
    "char_start": 88213,
    "char_end": 88651,
    "char_count": 438,
    "text": "2.\nTechnical and Inter-connection Requirements:\n\n2.1.\nThe metering arrangement and the inter-connection of the Roof-top Renewable Energy\nGenerating System with the Network of the Licensee shall be as per the provisions of the Net\nMetering Regulations and the technical standards and norms specified by the Central\nElectricity Authority for connectivity of distributed generation resources and for the\ninstallation and operation of meters.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0127",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 127,
    "page_start": 49,
    "page_end": 49,
    "char_start": 88653,
    "char_end": 89019,
    "char_count": 366,
    "text": "2.2.\nThe Eligible Consumer agrees that he shall install, prior to connection of the Roof-top\nRenewable Energy Generating System to the Network of the Licensee, an isolation device\n(both automatic and in built within inverter and external manual relays); and the Licensee\nshall have access to it if required for the repair and maintenance of the Distribution Network.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0128",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 128,
    "page_start": 49,
    "page_end": 49,
    "char_start": 89021,
    "char_end": 89109,
    "char_count": 88,
    "text": "2.3.\nThe Licensee shall specify the interface/inter-connection point and metering point.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0129",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 129,
    "page_start": 49,
    "page_end": 49,
    "char_start": 89111,
    "char_end": 89286,
    "char_count": 175,
    "text": "2.4.\nThe Eligible Consumer shall furnish all relevant data, such as voltage, frequency, circuit\nbreaker, isolator position in his System, as and when required by the Licensee.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0130",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 130,
    "page_start": 49,
    "page_end": 49,
    "char_start": 89288,
    "char_end": 89469,
    "char_count": 181,
    "text": "2.5. All the equipment connected to Network of the Licensee at the time of installation shall be\ncompliant with the Technical Specifications for rooftop system as Published by MNRE.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0131",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 131,
    "page_start": 49,
    "page_end": 49,
    "char_start": 89471,
    "char_end": 89622,
    "char_count": 151,
    "text": "3.\nSafety:\n\n3.1.\nThe consumer shall comply with the Central Electricity Authority (Measures Relating to Safety\nand Electricity Supply) Regulations 2010",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0132",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 132,
    "page_start": 50,
    "page_end": 50,
    "char_start": 89624,
    "char_end": 89626,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "50",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0133",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 133,
    "page_start": 50,
    "page_end": 50,
    "char_start": 89628,
    "char_end": 89967,
    "char_count": 339,
    "text": "3.2.\nThe equipment connected to the Licensee's Distribution System shall be compliant with\nrelevant International (IEEE/IEC) or Indian Standards (BIS), as the case may be, and the\ninstallation of electrical equipment shall comply with the requirements specified by the\nCentral Electricity Authority regarding safety and electricity supply.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0134",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 134,
    "page_start": 50,
    "page_end": 50,
    "char_start": 89969,
    "char_end": 90218,
    "char_count": 249,
    "text": "3.3.\nThe design, installation, maintenance and operation of the Roof-top Renewable Energy\nGenerating System shall be undertaken in a manner conducive to the safety of the Roof-top\nRenewable Energy Generating System as well as the Licensee's Network.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0135",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 135,
    "page_start": 50,
    "page_end": 50,
    "char_start": 90220,
    "char_end": 90670,
    "char_count": 450,
    "text": "3.4.\nIf, at any time, the Licensee determines that the Eligible Consumer's Roof-top  Renewable\nEnergy Generating System is causing or may cause damage to and/or results in the Licensee's\nother consumers or its assets, the Eligible Consumer shall disconnect the Roof-top Renewable\nEnergy Generating System from the distribution Network upon direction from the Licensee\nand shall undertake corrective measures at his own expense prior to re-connection.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0136",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 136,
    "page_start": 50,
    "page_end": 50,
    "char_start": 90672,
    "char_end": 91033,
    "char_count": 361,
    "text": "3.5.\nThe Licensee shall not be responsible for any accident resulting in injury to human beings or\nanimals or damage to property that may occur due to back- feeding from the Roof-top\nRenewable Energy Generating System when the grid supply is off. The Licensee may\ndisconnect the installation at any time in the event of such exigencies to prevent such\naccident.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0137",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 137,
    "page_start": 50,
    "page_end": 50,
    "char_start": 91035,
    "char_end": 91338,
    "char_count": 303,
    "text": "4.\nOther Clearances and Approvals:\n\nThe Eligible Consumer shall obtain any statutory approvals and clearances that may be\nrequired, such as from the Electrical Inspector or the municipal or other authorities, before\nconnecting the Roof-top Renewable Energy Generating System to the distribution Network.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0138",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 138,
    "page_start": 50,
    "page_end": 50,
    "char_start": 91340,
    "char_end": 91380,
    "char_count": 40,
    "text": "5.\nPeriod of Agreement, and Termination:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0139",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 139,
    "page_start": 51,
    "page_end": 51,
    "char_start": 91382,
    "char_end": 91384,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "51",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0140",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 140,
    "page_start": 51,
    "page_end": 51,
    "char_start": 91386,
    "char_end": 91937,
    "char_count": 551,
    "text": "This Agreement shall be for a period for 25 years, but may be terminated prematurely.\n(a) By mutual consent; or\n(b) By the Eligible Consumer, by giving 30 days' notice to the Licensee.\n(c) By the Licensee, by giving 30 days' notice, if the Eligible Consumer breaches any terms of this\nAgreement or the provisions of the Net Metering Regulations and does not remedy such\nbreach within 30 days, or such other reasonable period as may be provided, of receiving\nnotice of such breach, or for any other valid reason communicated by the Licensee in writing.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0141",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 141,
    "page_start": 51,
    "page_end": 51,
    "char_start": 91939,
    "char_end": 92185,
    "char_count": 246,
    "text": "6.\nAccess and Disconnection:\n\n6.1.\nThe Eligible Consumer shall provide access to the Licensee to the metering equipment and\ndisconnecting devices of Roof-top Renewable Energy Generating System, both automatic and\nmanual, by the Eligible Consumer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0142",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 142,
    "page_start": 51,
    "page_end": 51,
    "char_start": 92187,
    "char_end": 92411,
    "char_count": 224,
    "text": "6.2.\nIf, in an emergent or outage situation, the Licensee cannot access the disconnecting devices\nof the Roof-top Renewable Energy Generating System, both automatic and manual, it may\ndisconnect power supply to the premises.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0143",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 143,
    "page_start": 51,
    "page_end": 51,
    "char_start": 92413,
    "char_end": 92599,
    "char_count": 186,
    "text": "6.3.\nUpon termination of this Agreement under Clause 5, the Eligible Consumer shall disconnect\nthe Roof-top Renewable Energy Generating System forthwith from the Network of the\nLicensee.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0144",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 144,
    "page_start": 51,
    "page_end": 51,
    "char_start": 92601,
    "char_end": 92883,
    "char_count": 282,
    "text": "7.\nLiabilities:\n\n7.1.\nThe Parties shall indemnify each other for damages or adverse effects of either Party's\nnegligence or misconduct during the installation of the Roof-top Renewable Energy\nGenerating System, connectivity with the distribution Network and operation of the System.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0145",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 145,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 92885,
    "char_end": 92887,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "52",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0146",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 146,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 92889,
    "char_end": 93245,
    "char_count": 356,
    "text": "7.2.\nThe Parties shall not be liable to each other for any loss of profits or revenues, business\ninterruption losses, loss of contract or goodwill, or for indirect, consequential, incidental or\nspecial damages including, but not limited to, punitive or exemplary damages, whether any\nof these liabilities, losses or damages arise in contract, or otherwise.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0147",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 147,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 93247,
    "char_end": 93384,
    "char_count": 137,
    "text": "8.\nCommercial Settlement:\n\n8.1.\nThe commercial settlements under this Agreement shall be in accordance with the Net\nMetering Regulations.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0148",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 148,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 93386,
    "char_end": 93640,
    "char_count": 254,
    "text": "8.2.\nThe Licensee shall not be liable to compensate the Eligible Consumer if his Rooftop\nRenewable Energy Generating System is unable to inject surplus power generated into the\nLicensee's Network on account of failure of power supply in the grid/Network.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0149",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 149,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 93642,
    "char_end": 94155,
    "char_count": 513,
    "text": "8.3.\nThe existing metering System, if not in accordance with the Net Metering Regulations, shall\nbe replaced by a bi-directional meter (whole current/CT operated) or a pair of meters (as per\nthe definition of 'Net Meter' in the Regulations), and a separate generation meter may be\nprovided to measure Solar power generation. The bi-directional meter (whole current/CT\noperated) or pair of meters shall be installed at the inter-connection point to the Licensee's\nNetwork for recording export and import of energy.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0150",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 150,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 94157,
    "char_end": 94280,
    "char_count": 123,
    "text": "8.4.\nThe uni-directional and bi-directional or pair of meters shall be fixed in separate meter boxes\nin the same proximity.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0151",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 151,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 94282,
    "char_end": 94451,
    "char_count": 169,
    "text": "9.\nConnection Costs:\n\nThe Eligible Consumer shall bear all costs related to the setting up of the Roof-top Renewable\nEnergy Generating System and the cost of Net Meters.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0152",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 152,
    "page_start": 53,
    "page_end": 53,
    "char_start": 94453,
    "char_end": 94455,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "53",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0153",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 153,
    "page_start": 53,
    "page_end": 53,
    "char_start": 94457,
    "char_end": 94618,
    "char_count": 161,
    "text": "10.\nDispute Resolution:\n\n10.1.\nAny dispute arising under this Agreement shall be resolved promptly, in good faith and in an\nequitable manner by both the Parties.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0154",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 154,
    "page_start": 53,
    "page_end": 53,
    "char_start": 94620,
    "char_end": 94854,
    "char_count": 234,
    "text": "10.2.\nThe Eligible Consumer shall have recourse to the concerned Consumer Grievance Redressal\nForum constituted under the relevant Regulations in respect of any grievance regarding\nbilling which has not been redressed by the Licensee.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0155",
    "doc_id": "DOC-001",
    "paragraph_index": 155,
    "page_start": 53,
    "page_end": 53,
    "char_start": 94856,
    "char_end": 95012,
    "char_count": 156,
    "text": "In the witness where of …………… (name) for and on behalf of Eligible Consumer and\nShri. ……………….. (name) for and on behalf of Licensee agree to this agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": true
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC001-0156",
