  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC016-0009",
    "doc_id": "DOC-016",
    "paragraph_index": 9,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 3205,
    "char_end": 4050,
    "char_count": 845,
    "text": " 4. That interest at the rate of 18% per annum or as may be prescribed under section 40(b) (iv)\nof the Income-tax Act, 1961 or any other applicable provisions as may be in force in the income-\ntax assessment of the partnership firm for the relevant accounting period or at a lower rate as\nmay be agreed to by and between the parties from time to time shall be paid to the partners or\ncredited to the partners on the amount standing to the credit of the account of the partners.\nSuch interest shall be considered as an expenditure of the firm and shall be debited to the\nProfit & Loss Account of the firm before arriving at the divisible profit or loss. The interest to\npersons other than partners shall be paid or credited to their accounts at the rate or rates as\nmay be agreed to by and between the partners and such persons from time to time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC016-0010",
    "doc_id": "DOC-016",
    "paragraph_index": 10,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 4051,
    "char_end": 5423,
    "char_count": 1372,
    "text": "5. That Shri................................ Shri ..................... and Shri ............................ the parties of\nthe.......................parts have agreed to keep themselves actively engaged in conducting the\naffairs of the business of the partnership firm. The said partners shall be working partners. It is\nhereby agreed to that in consideration of the said parties keeping themselves actively engaged\nin the business of the partnership firm and working as working partners, shall be entitled to\nremuneration on monthly basis/yearly basis. The remuneration payable to the said working\npartners shall be computed in the manner laid down or deduction under section 40(b)(v), read\nwith Explanation 3 of the Income-tax Act, 1961 or any other applicable provision as may be in\nforce in the income-tax assessment of the partnership firm for the relevant accounting year.\nSuch amount of remuneration shall be distributed between the said working partners in the\nfollowing proportion:\na) Shri................................ .......per cent of such amount\nb) Shri................................ .......per cent of such amount\nc) Shri................................ .......per cent of such amount\nThe partners shall be entitled to increase or reduce the above remuneration and may agree to\npay remuneration to other working partner or partners as the case may be.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC016-0011",
    "doc_id": "DOC-016",
    "paragraph_index": 11,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 5424,
    "char_end": 5591,
    "char_count": 167,
    "text": "6. That the parties hereto shall be true and faithful to each other and shall not do or cause to be\ndone anything which may be detrimental to the interest of the firm.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
