    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC016-0014",
    "doc_id": "DOC-016",
    "paragraph_index": 14,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 6041,
    "char_end": 6184,
    "char_count": 143,
    "text": " 8. That the partnership has been and shall be a partnership at will and can be dissolved as and\nwhen decided by the partners here to mutually.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC016-0015",
    "doc_id": "DOC-016",
    "paragraph_index": 15,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 6185,
    "char_end": 6755,
    "char_count": 570,
    "text": " 9. That the net profit of the partnership firm after deduction of all expenses including rent,\nsalaries, other establishment expenses, interest and remuneration payable to the partners in\naccordance with this deed of partnership or any supplementary deed as may be executed by\nthe partners from time, to time, shall be divided and distributed amongst the partners in the\nfollowing proportion:\nSr. No. Name of Party Share in profits\n1.\n 2.\n 3.\n 4.\nThe losses, if any, including loss of capital suffered in any year shall also be apportioned in the\nabove said proportion.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC016-0016",
    "doc_id": "DOC-016",
    "paragraph_index": 16,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 6756,
    "char_end": 6908,
    "char_count": 152,
    "text": "10. That the bank account or accounts have been and shall be maintained in the name of the\nfirm and shall be operated singly or jointly by the partners.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC016-0017",
    "doc_id": "DOC-016",
    "paragraph_index": 17,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 6909,
    "char_end": 7712,
    "char_count": 803,
    "text": "11. That the books of account shall be closed on 31st day of March each year. The net profit or\nloss after deducting all expenses, interest, remuneration, outgoings shall be divided between\nthe parties in proportion to the sharing ratio referred to hereinabove.\n12.That notwithstanding anything contained in the Indian Partnership Act it is hereby mutually\nagreed to by and between the parties that in case of death/retirement of any one or more\npartners, the firm shall not be dissolved but shall continue to be carried on by and between the\nsurviving partners and legal heirs and/or representatives of the deceased partner, as a\ncontinuing concern, on the same terms and conditions as incorporated in this Deed or on such\nterms and conditions as may be agreed to by and between them from time to time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
