    "text": "Date: 02 June 2026\nTo,\nThe Listing Compliance Department\nNational Stock Exchange of India Limited – Emerge Platform (SME Segment)\nExchange Plaza, C-1, Block G, Bandra-Kurla Complex, Bandra (E), Mumbai – 400 051\nSymbol: TECHD    |    Series: SME\nSubject: Intimation under Regulation 30 of the SEBI (LODR) Regulations, 2015 – Receipt of three (3)\nPurchase Orders aggregating INR 1,40,54,756.98/- (inclusive of GST) in the ordinary course of\nbusiness.\nReference: SEBI Master Circular No. SEBI/HO/CFD/PoD2/CIR/P/0155 dated 11 November 2024 read\nwith Para B of Part A of Schedule III to the SEBI (LODR) Regulations, 2015 and the Company’s Policy\nfor Determination of Materiality of Events / Information.\nDear Sir / Madam,\nPursuant to Regulation 30 read with Para B of Part A of Schedule III of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and\nDisclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015, we wish to intimate that TechD Cybersecurity Limited\n(“the Company”) has received three (3) separate Purchase Orders from a Listed Cybersecurity System\nIntegrator / Distribution Partner of the Company, in the ordinary course of business, for the supply of\nOEM Support / Managed Services. Aggregate Order Value is  INR 1,19,10,811/-  (excl. GST)   |   INR\n1,40,54,756.98/-  (incl. GST)\nThe end-managed services beneficiaries are situated in the (i) automobile manufacturing, (ii)\nfinancial-sector technology services and (iii) public-sector general insurance verticals. Detailed\nparticulars in the SEBI-prescribed format are set out in Annexure A, Annexure B and Annexure C\nenclosed herewith.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
