    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 1926,
    "char_end": 1974,
    "char_count": 48,
    "text": "For Knowledge Marine & Engineering Works Limited",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC042-0012",
    "doc_id": "DOC-042",
    "paragraph_index": 12,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 1976,
    "char_end": 2405,
    "char_count": 429,
    "text": "Avdhoot Kotwal\nCompany Secretary & Compliance Officer\n\nAVDHOOT\nAJAY\nKOTWAL\nDigitally signed by AVDHOOT AJAY KOTWAL\nDN: c=IN, o=PERSONAL,\npseudonym=7c50645041024a7da40265c22d8b\ndfae,\n2.5.4.20=9488868bd8ff13348c05c250e489fda4fe\nab02badcec5b4128f676e0a60fd26a,\npostalCode=421002, st=MAHARASHTRA,\nserialNumber=31021b09408671aa91158760ef77\n9c694b3964247dafc253c754ed8d95c2d9e6,\ncn=AVDHOOT AJAY KOTWAL\nDate: 2025.12.19 10:58:12 +05'30'",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC042-0013",
    "doc_id": "DOC-042",
    "paragraph_index": 13,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 2407,
    "char_end": 2609,
    "char_count": 202,
    "text": "Unit No. 706-707, The Epicentre, W. T. Pa8l Marg, Oﬀ Eastern Freeway, BEST Colony, Near Shivaji Chowk\nChembur (East), Mumbai – 400 071\nKnowledge Marine & Engineering Works Ltd.\n(BSE: 543273) (NSE: KMEW)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC042-0014",
    "doc_id": "DOC-042",
    "paragraph_index": 14,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 2611,
    "char_end": 4386,
    "char_count": 1775,
    "text": "KMEW to execute Complex Rock Dredging  Work at Jawaharlal Nehru Port for DCIL\nMumbai, India, December 19, 2025: - Knowledge Marine & Engineering Works Limited (“KMEW”)\n(BSE: 543273) (NSE: KMEW) is proud to announce that we have been awarded a Work order from\nDredging Corporation of India Limited (DCIL) for Rock Dredging (removal of pinnacles/ high spots)\nat Coastal Berth at JNPA and discharge of dredged material at DS-3 Dumping Ground. The said\nwork order is valued at ₹ 58.39 Crores (Rupees Fifty-Eight Crores and Thirty-Nine Lakhs) including\ntaxes and is to be completed within 90 days from the commencement of work.\nThe scope of the work order encompasses the removal of rock pinnacles and high spots at the\nCoastal Berth of Jawaharlal Nehru Port, followed by the disposal of the dredged material at the\ndesignated dumping ground, DS-3. This technically critical rock dredging assignment\nnecessitates extensive pre-treatment and the execution of underwater controlled blasting,\nsubsequent to high-precision drilling operations in rock formations exhibiting compressive\nstrengths in excess of 170 megapascals. The operations will be carried out through an integrated\ndeployment of advanced marine assets, including a dedicated drilling and blasting barge, trailing\nsuction hopper dredgers (TSHDs), a backhoe dredger, self-propelled hopper barges, and secured\nexplosives storage facilities. KMEW has 60 days to mobilise the equipment and get all the requisite\npermissions before commencing the works.\nThrough meticulous planning and seamless mobilization, KMEW will execute the dredging of\napproximately 10,500 cubic meters of exceptionally hard rock material from water depths\nof up to 16 meters (at high-tide conditions) within a tightly compressed execution timeframe",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC042-0015",
    "doc_id": "DOC-042",
    "paragraph_index": 15,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 4387,
    "char_end": 6061,
    "char_count": 1674,
    "text": "of 90 days. This undertaking further underscores the Company’s proven capability to deliver\ncomplex subsea engineering projects under stringent schedule constraints.\nThe Company possesses a demonstrated track record of successfully executing and completing\nrock dredging works at Mangrol Fishing Harbour, reinforcing its technical credibility and\noperational competence in similarly challenging environments.\nThis work order stands as a testament to the confidence placed in KMEW’s capabilities. The\nCompany is comprehensively equipped to deliver the project within the stipulated timelines and\nwill deploy vessels from its existing fleet, in addition to acquiring an additional vessel specifically\nfor the execution of this assignment.\nThis contract award further consolidates KMEW’s standing as a preferred partner in India’s\ndredging and marine engineering sector and exemplifies its continued ability to deliver mission-\ncritical infrastructure solutions at one of the nation’s busiest and most strategically significant\nports.\nCommenting on the Work Order, Mr. Sujay Kewalramani, CEO of Knowledge Marine &\nEngineering Works Ltd said that,\n“We are positioning ourselves as a comprehensive solution provider capable of executing the\nmost technically demanding works within the port sector. This assignment has been\nattempted by several dredging contractors; however, it has largely remained unsuccessful\ndue to its extraordinary complexity. The rock formation targeted for dredging is estimated\nto exhibit compressive strengths exceeding 170 megapascals, rendering it the most\nformidable geological stratum ever undertaken by the KMEW team. To address these\nPress Release",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC042-0016",
    "doc_id": "DOC-042",
    "paragraph_index": 16,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 6063,
    "char_end": 7832,
    "char_count": 1769,
    "text": "Unit No. 706-707, The Epicentre, W. T. Pa8l Marg, Oﬀ Eastern Freeway, BEST Colony, Near Shivaji Chowk\nChembur (East), Mumbai – 400 071\nKnowledge Marine & Engineering Works Ltd.\n(BSE: 543273) (NSE: KMEW)\nchallenges, we will engage the expertise of India’s most eminent rock drilling and blasting\nspecialists.\nThe scope of work necessitates the development of an exceptionally intricate underwater\ncontrolled blasting methodology, given its immediate proximity to critical port\ninfrastructure. Upon successful execution, KMEW will have established unparalleled\nexpertise in rock dredging across both shallow and deep-water environments, employing\nmethodologies with or without pre-treatment, utilizing entirely in-house equipment. Our\nestablished credentials—underscored by the successful dredging of over 137,000 cubic\nmeters of rock at Mangrol Fishing Harbour—instill strong confidence in our ability to deliver\nthis project with the highest levels of precision, safety, and operational efficiency.\nAt KMEW, we remain steadfast in our commitment to operational excellence, disciplined\nproject execution, and continuous innovation in marine engineering. This award further\nconsolidates our standing as a trusted partner within India’s dredging industry and\nreinforces our contribution to the advancement of the nation’s maritime infrastructure.”\nAbout Knowledge Marine & Engineering Works Ltd:\nIncorporated in 2015, KMEW is in the business of owning and operating Marine Crafts, dredging,\nrepair and maintenance/refits of Marine Crafts and Marine Infrastructure. The Company provides\nmultiple solutions of marine engineering including dredging at various ports, carrying out repair\nand refit services of naval and merchant ships, conducting hydrographic and magnetometer",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC042-0017",
    "doc_id": "DOC-042",
    "paragraph_index": 17,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 7833,
    "char_end": 9244,
    "char_count": 1411,
    "text": "surveys and technical solutions for maintenance and operations of vessels. Over the years, it has\nbecome an established player in the small marine craft business segment and dredging services in\nIndia and have evolved from a small ship-repair unit to a ship-owning Company. The company has\na multi-million order book from esteemed clients such as Ministry of External Affairs, Kolkata Port\nTrust, Visakhapatnam Port Trust, Deendayal Port Trust, Paradip Port Trust, Dredging Corporation\nof India and various other ports.\nSafe Harbour\nAny forward-looking statements about expected future events, financial and operating results of\nthe Company are based on certain assumptions which the Company does not guarantee the\nfulfilment of. These statements are subject to risks and uncertainties. Actual results might differ\nsubstantially or materially from those expressed or implied. Important developments that could\naffect the Company’s operations include a downtrend in the industry, global or domestic or both,\nsignificant changes in political and economic environment in India or key markets abroad, tax\nlaws, litigation, labour relations, exchange rate fluctuations, technological changes, investment\nand business income, cash flow projections, interest, and other costs. The Company does not\nundertake any obligation to update forward-looking statements to reflect events or circumstances\nafter the date thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
