    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 324,
    "char_end": 526,
    "char_count": 202,
    "text": "1.\n[___] hereinafter referred to as the “Company” (which expression shall, unless repugnant to the context or\nmeaning thereof, be deemed to mean and include its successors and assigns) of the First Part",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0004",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 4,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 528,
    "char_end": 531,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "and",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0005",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 5,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 533,
    "char_end": 730,
    "char_count": 197,
    "text": "2.\n[___] hereinafter referred to as “Employee”, (which expression shall, unless repugnant to the meaning or\ncontext hereof mean and include its successors and permitted assigns) of the Second Part.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0006",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 6,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 732,
    "char_end": 848,
    "char_count": 116,
    "text": "The Company and the Employee are each hereinafter collectively referred to as \"Parties\" and individually as “Party”.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0007",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 7,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 850,
    "char_end": 858,
    "char_count": 8,
    "text": "WHEREAS:",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0008",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 8,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 860,
    "char_end": 1512,
    "char_count": 652,
    "text": "A. The Employee is an employee of the Company and by virtue of being an employee, is provided access to\nconfidential and proprietary information of the Company;\nB. The Employee may conceive and contribute to the development of intellectual property of the Company\nduring the course of his/her employment with the Company and for the discharge of the Employee’s\nobligations set forth in the employment agreement executed by the Employee with the Company;\nC. The Parties wish to enter into this Agreement to set forth the terms relating to confidentiality obligations\nand ownership of intellectual property rights in information shared with the Employee.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0009",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 9,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 1514,
    "char_end": 1729,
    "char_count": 215,
    "text": "In consideration of the employment provided by the Company and other mutual promises and agreements contained\nherein below, the receipt and sufficiency of which are hereby acknowledged, the Parties agree as follows:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0010",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 10,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 1731,
    "char_end": 1968,
    "char_count": 237,
    "text": "1.\nDEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION\n\n1.1.\nIn this Agreement (including in the recitals herein above or schedules hereto), the following words and\nexpressions shall have, where the context so permits, the following meaning ascribed to them:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0011",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 11,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 1970,
    "char_end": 2747,
    "char_count": 777,
    "text": "1.1.1.\n\"Affiliate\", with respect to either Party means any Person who directly or indirectly, Controls, is controlled\nby, or is under the common Control of such Parties. The term “Control” is used in the sense of the\npossession by a Person or a group of Persons acting in concert, directly or indirectly, of the right to direct\nor cause the direction of the management and policies of another Person, whether through the board of\ndirectors or ownership of voting rights by such other Person, by the Articles of Association, contract or\notherwise. A Person or a group of Persons acting in concert shall be deemed to be in control of a body\ncorporate if such Person or group of Persons is in a position to appoint or appoints the majority of the\ndirectors of such body corporate.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0012",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 12,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 2749,
    "char_end": 3653,
    "char_count": 904,
    "text": "1.1.2.\n“Confidential Information” shall mean and includes information which is confidential including\nProprietary Information and other information related to the business of the Company, its affiliates or any\nthird parties with which the Company associates, whether or not such information is expressly marked or\ndesignated as confidential information and includes but is not limited to:\n'\na)\ninformation of value or significance to the Company or its competitors (including potential competitors)\nsuch as:\ni.\ndata of or about the Company or its vendors, customers, employees, advisors, mentors, service\nproviders or consultants, in particular, contact information and sales information;\nii.\ndata about Company’s compliance with applicable law including data about licenses, permissions,\napprovals, permissions or consents applied for, requested by, granted to or denied to the Company\nor its promoters;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0013",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 13,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 3655,
    "char_end": 3760,
    "char_count": 105,
    "text": "Confidentiality and Intellectual Property Assignment Agreement Template (India) | OS v. 1 | November\n2016",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0014",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 14,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 3762,
    "char_end": 5561,
    "char_count": 1799,
    "text": "iii.\ndata about all filings and official submissions made by the Company to governmental authorities\nand the content of the discussion and communication by the Company with such authorities;\niv.\ndata related to the Company’s business, its existing and upcoming products, services, business\nstrategy, terms of engagement with its vendors or customers, pricing data, business plans;\nv.\nany data, documents, sketches, designs, plans, drawings, photographs, reports, communication,\ntechnical information, information about Intellectual Property Rights, user information,\ncompilation, subscription details, asset information, know-how, research and development, internal\npolicies;\nvi.\nany information related to the Company’s technology, software, hardware, code, design, business\nstrategy, business plan, internal systems, business architecture;\nvii.\nfinancial data, in particular, concerning budgets, fees and revenue calculations, sales figures,\nfinancial statements, profit expectations and inventories of the Company;\nviii.\ntraining data, particularly documents, videos, processes, multimedia files, presentations and any\nsuch training resources that the Employee gains access to during his association with the Company;\nix.\nsecurity information (including passwords, login credentials) used to access any resource owned or\noperated by the Company, its affiliates, clients or third party agents;\nx.\nclient or user data, user credits, user analytics, user preferences, feedback information;\nb) any information which may be reasonably understood by its nature, or by the context of its disclosure,\nto be confidential; and\nc)\nany information derived from any of the above-mentioned information; and\nd) original information supplied by the Company or information provided to the Company by third parties",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0015",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 15,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 5562,
    "char_end": 5991,
    "char_count": 429,
    "text": "which the Company is obligated to keep confidential.\n1.1.3.\n“Intellectual Property Rights” means and includes, without limitation, any patents, copyrights, trademarks,\ntrade secrets, service marks, database right, design right, moral right or any other property rights (in each\ncase, whether registered or not and including applications for registration, if any) that grant similar rights as\nthe foregoing, anywhere in the world.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0016",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 16,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 5993,
    "char_end": 6177,
    "char_count": 184,
    "text": "1.1.4.\n“Company Intellectual Property” means any Proprietary Information created, conceived, developed,\nimproved upon or contributed to by the Employee during the course of Employment.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0017",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 17,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 6179,
    "char_end": 7066,
    "char_count": 887,
    "text": "1.1.5.\n“Proprietary Information” means and includes, but is not limited to, Company Intellectual Property\ninformation about software programs, designs, source code, object code, algorithms, trade secrets, formulae,\ndesigns, know-how, domain names, processes, applications, data, ideas, techniques, documents, notes,\npresentations, works of authorship, business plans, customer lists, user information, vendor data, customer\ndata, operational data, terms of compensation and performance levels of employees, and other information\nconcerning the actual or anticipated business, research or development, prices and pricing structures,\nmarketing and sales information, competitive analysis, and any information and materials relating thereto, or\nwhich is received in confidence by or for the Company or its Affiliates from any other person, whether or\nnot it is in written or permanent form.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0018",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 18,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 7068,
    "char_end": 7394,
    "char_count": 326,
    "text": "2.\nCONFIDENTIALITY OBLIGATIONS\n\n2.1.\nThe Employee agrees and acknowledges that during the term of his employment with the Company\n(“Employment”), the Employee shall have access to Confidential Information through oral, visual,\nelectronic or written means, solely by virtue of the Employment and for the purpose of enabling the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0019",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 19,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 7396,
    "char_end": 7501,
    "char_count": 105,
    "text": "Confidentiality and Intellectual Property Assignment Agreement Template (India) | OS v. 1 | November\n2016",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0020",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 20,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 7503,
    "char_end": 7687,
    "char_count": 184,
    "text": "Employee to discharge his obligations towards the Company as an employee. The provision of access\nto Confidential Information to the Employee shall be at the discretion of the Company.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0021",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 21,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 7689,
    "char_end": 8295,
    "char_count": 606,
    "text": "2.2.\nThe Employee understands and acknowledges that the Confidential Information is of immense value\nto the Company and its Affiliates and/or its present, past or prospective clients. The Employee\nunderstands that any use or disclosure of such Confidential Information including any inadvertent\ndisclosure can cause immense and irreparable harm, loss, damage and injury to the Company and its\nAffiliates and its reputation and hence undertakes to keep such Confidential Information confidential\nand use it solely in the manner expressly authorized by the Company and only during the term of his\nEmployment.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0022",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 22,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 8297,
    "char_end": 8816,
    "char_count": 519,
    "text": "2.3.\nThe Employee agrees and undertakes that at all times during the term of his Employment and thereafter\non termination of his Employment for whatever reason to hold in the strictest confidence, and not to\nuse, except for the benefit of the Company and its Affiliates, and absolutely refrain from in any manner\ndivulging, discussing, disclosing the Confidential Information to any third party or in any manner\ndirectly or indirectly using the Confidential Information without the written authorisation of the\nCompany.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0023",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 23,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 8818,
    "char_end": 9356,
    "char_count": 538,
    "text": "2.4.\nThe Employee recognises that the Company and its Affiliates have received and in the future will receive\nfrom third parties, information that would be confidential and proprietary in nature to such third parties,\nduring the course of his Employment. The Employee agrees to hold all such third party information in\nthe strictest confidence and not to disclose it to any person, firm or corporation or to use it except as\nnecessary in carrying out his work for the Company consistent with the Company’s agreement with such\nthird party.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0024",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 24,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 9358,
    "char_end": 9782,
    "char_count": 424,
    "text": "2.5.\nThe Employee further undertakes not to make copies of such Confidential Information except as\nauthorised by the Company. Nothing contained in this Agreement shall be construed as granting or\nconferring any rights either as a license or otherwise in the Confidential Information. The Employee\nshall not claim or represent to hold any interest by way of ownership, assignment or otherwise in the\nConfidential Information.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0025",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 25,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 9784,
    "char_end": 10003,
    "char_count": 219,
    "text": "2.6.\nThe Employee shall, upon termination of the Employment, promptly return to the Company all\nConfidential Information including all materials and documents obtained from or through the Company\n(in hard or soft copy).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0026",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 26,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 10005,
    "char_end": 10522,
    "char_count": 517,
    "text": "2.7.\nNothing in this Clause 2 shall apply to information: (i) that was previously known by the Employee, as\nestablished by written records of the Employee prior to receipt of such information from the Company;\n(ii) that was lawfully obtained by the Employee from a third party without any obligations of\nconfidentiality to Company; (iii) that was developed by the Employee independent of the Confidential\nInformation; and (iv) information disclosed to the Employee by the Company without confidentiality\nrestrictions.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0027",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 27,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 10524,
    "char_end": 10636,
    "char_count": 112,
    "text": "2.8.\nThis Clause shall survive the expiration or termination of this Agreement.\n\n3.\nINTELLECTUAL PROPERTY RIGHTS",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0028",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 28,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 10638,
    "char_end": 11205,
    "char_count": 567,
    "text": "3.1.\nThe Company shall retain all rights, title and interest and Intellectual Property Rights in any Company\nIntellectual Property created, conceived, developed, contributed to or improved upon by the Employee\nduring the course of his Employment, shall vest with the Company upon such creation, conception,\ndevelopment, contribution or improvement. Notwithstanding anything to the contrary, no license with\nrespect to Intellectual Property Rights shall be deemed or implied to be granted by the Company to the\nEmployee in respect of the Company Intellectual Property.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0029",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 29,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 11207,
    "char_end": 11699,
    "char_count": 492,
    "text": "3.2.\nThe Employee shall not reverse- engineer, decompile, or disassemble, modify or copy (except for\nmaking a single back-up copy) any methodologies, software or whitepaper article, themes, headlines, or\nConfidential Information disclosed under this Agreement and shall not remove, overprint, deface or\nchange any notice of confidentiality, copyright, trademark, logo, legend or other notices of ownership\nfrom any originals or copies of Confidential Information it receives from the Company.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0030",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 30,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 11701,
    "char_end": 11806,
    "char_count": 105,
    "text": "Confidentiality and Intellectual Property Assignment Agreement Template (India) | OS v. 1 | November\n2016",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0031",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 31,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 11808,
    "char_end": 12575,
    "char_count": 767,
    "text": "3.3.\nTo the extent that any rights referred to under Clause 3.1 do not vest with the Company automatically\nas per the terms above or through operation of law, the Employee hereby irrevocably and in perpetuity\nassigns to the Company all of right, title and interest (including without limitation any and all Intellectual\nProperty Rights),  that is now or may be available, in: (a) any and all Company Intellectual Property; and\n(b) any and all Proprietary Information that the Employee may  have conceived, created, improved\nupon, developed or contributed to prior to the Effective Date, as part of his association with,\ncontribution to the Company or its incorporation (including as part of work undertaken for the business\nof the Company prior to its incorporation).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0032",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 32,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 12577,
    "char_end": 13388,
    "char_count": 811,
    "text": "3.4.\nThe Employee agrees and understands that any and all copyrightable works that are prepared by the\nEmployee, within his scope of service, is “work for hire” under applicable law and the Company will be\nconsidered the first owner of such copyrightable works. To the extent that the Company is not\nconsidered the first owner of the Intellectual Property Rights created by the Employee, the copyright\nand all related rights, title and interest in all such Company Intellectual Property is irrevocably assigned\nby the Employee to the Company in consideration of the Employment which constitutes valid and\nadequate consideration. The Employee hereby waives any right to and agrees that he shall not raise any\nobjection or claims under applicable law in respect of ownership of such Company Intellectual Property.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0033",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 33,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 13390,
    "char_end": 13905,
    "char_count": 515,
    "text": "3.5.\nDuring the Employment, whatever gets created, developed, modified in the form of any hardware or\nsoftware design, engineering, hardware code, software code, hardware and software library , schematic,\narchitectural, layout, protocol, model or any Intellectual Property or document in any format by the\nEmployee with or without the assistance or involvement of any other Person during the Term using\nown tools or the Company’s or its partners/Affiliates’ tools and systems will always be property of the\nCompany.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0034",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 34,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 13907,
    "char_end": 14194,
    "char_count": 287,
    "text": "3.6.\nThe Employee shall do all acts, deeds and things including execution of necessary documents without\ncharge or compensation but at the cost of the Company for fully and effectively vesting in the Company\nthe rights in any Intellectual Property Rights as referred to in this Clause 3.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0035",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 35,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 14196,
    "char_end": 14415,
    "char_count": 219,
    "text": "3.7.\nThe Employee hereby irrevocably appoints the Company as his attorney for the purpose of executing\nin the name and on behalf of the Employee all such deeds and documents as may be required pursuant\nto this Clause 3.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0036",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 36,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 14417,
    "char_end": 14673,
    "char_count": 256,
    "text": "3.8.\nThe Employee represents and warrants that the Employee has not violated and will not violate the\nIntellectual Property Rights of any third party and agrees not to violate the Intellectual Property Rights\nof any third party in the course of Employment.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0037",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 37,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 14675,
    "char_end": 14889,
    "char_count": 214,
    "text": "3.9.\nThe Employee acknowledges that the Employment and the remuneration paid by the Company to the\nEmployee is a good, valuable and adequate consideration, to be bound by the terms and conditions of\nthis Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0038",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 38,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 14891,
    "char_end": 15422,
    "char_count": 531,
    "text": "4.\nNON COMPETE AND NON SOLICITATION AGREEMENT\n\n4.1.\nThe Employee hereby agrees that pursuant to the termination of their employment in the Company as\nper this Agreement or for any reason whatsoever, they shall not directly or indirectly compete with the\nBusiness of the Company or its Affiliates for a period of 1 (one) year from the Termination Date. The\nnon-compete period referred to in this Clause 4 shall be extended by the length of time during which\nthe Employee shall have been in breach of the provisions of this Clause 4.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC048-0039",
    "doc_id": "DOC-048",
    "paragraph_index": 39,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 15424,
    "char_end": 15856,
    "char_count": 432,
    "text": "4.2.\nThe Employee hereby agrees and undertakes that during the term of the Employment with the\nCompany and for a period of 1 (one) year following the Termination Date, the Employee shall not,\ndirectly or indirectly, either as an individual on his own account or as a partner, employee, consultant,\nadvisor, agent, contractor, director, trustee, committee member, office bearer, or shareholder (or in a\nsimilar capacity or function):",
