    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 3082,
    "char_end": 3145,
    "char_count": 63,
    "text": "Consultancy Agreement Template (India) | OS v.1 | November 2016",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC051-0010",
    "doc_id": "DOC-051",
    "paragraph_index": 10,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 3147,
    "char_end": 3425,
    "char_count": 278,
    "text": "Page 2\n\nthe Intellectual Property Rights, in such Deliverables. Each Consultant shall provide such further assurances, take\nsuch action, and execute such further documents and instruments as the Company may reasonably request in order\nto carry out the purposes of this Clause 4.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC051-0011",
    "doc_id": "DOC-051",
    "paragraph_index": 11,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 3427,
    "char_end": 4061,
    "char_count": 634,
    "text": "To the extent that any Deliverable is based on or uses or embodies any material of a Consultant that was created\noutside or prior to this Agreement (“Pre-existing Material”) then, in consideration for the fees payable under\nthis Agreement, such Consultant hereby grants the Company, a limited, worldwide right to use the Pre-existing\nMaterial as long as such use is required for the use of the Deliverables by the Company.  The Parties agree and\nacknowledge that all rights in and to the Pre-existing Material shall continue to be with the Consultant except for\nthe limited rights expressly granted to the Company under this Clause 4.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC051-0012",
    "doc_id": "DOC-051",
    "paragraph_index": 12,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 4063,
    "char_end": 4431,
    "char_count": 368,
    "text": "“Deliverable” for the purposes of this Agreement shall mean any report, document, paper, drawing, design,\npresentation, photo, graphic, logo, typographical arrangement, software or any other material not including the\nPre-existing Material that is provided by the Consultants and represented to be the final deliverable in performing\nthe Services under this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC051-0013",
    "doc_id": "DOC-051",
    "paragraph_index": 13,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 4433,
    "char_end": 5114,
    "char_count": 681,
    "text": "“Intellectual Property Rights” for the purposes of this Agreement shall mean patents, rights to inventions,\ncopyright and related rights, trademarks, trade names and domain names, rights in goodwill or to sue for passing\noff, rights in designs, rights in computer software, database rights, rights in confidential information (including\nknow-how and trade secrets) and any other intellectual property rights, in each case whether registered or\nunregistered and including all applications (or rights to apply) for, and renewals or extensions of, such rights and\nall similar or equivalent rights or forms of protection which may now or in the future subsist in any part of the\nworld.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC051-0014",
    "doc_id": "DOC-051",
    "paragraph_index": 14,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 5116,
    "char_end": 5826,
    "char_count": 710,
    "text": "5. Confidentiality\n\nEach Party understands and acknowledges that it may receive Confidential Information (“Receiving Party”) of\nthe other Party (“Disclosing Party”) during the term of this Agreement. The Receiving Party shall not disclose\nthe Disclosing Party’s Confidential Information to a third party without the Disclosing Party’s prior written\nconsent.  Further, the Receiving Party shall only share Confidential Information with such of its employees and\nrepresentatives who have a need to know the Confidential Information in relation to the Receiving Party’s\nobligations under this Agreement and who are subject to confidentiality obligations which are no less onerous\nthan contained in this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC051-0015",
    "doc_id": "DOC-051",
    "paragraph_index": 15,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 5828,
    "char_end": 6329,
    "char_count": 501,
    "text": "“Confidential Information” shall mean any confidential or proprietary information, of a Party, in any form,\nincluding but not limited to the information relating to the such Party’s past, present or future products, services,\nresearch and development or business activities (and the terms of this Agreement), that is not in public domain\nwhich when disclosed is (a) marked as confidential (b) is identified as confidential at the time of disclosure; or (c)\nthat is manifestly of a confidential nature.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC051-0016",
    "doc_id": "DOC-051",
    "paragraph_index": 16,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 6331,
    "char_end": 6801,
    "char_count": 470,
    "text": "Confidential Information shall not include information that is:\n\na. publicly available prior to this Agreement or is made publicly available by the Disclosing Party without\nrestriction;\nb. rightfully received by the Receiving Party from third parties without accompanying confidentiality obligations;\nc. already in the Receiving Party’s possession and was lawfully received from sources other than the Disclosing\nParty;\nd. independently developed by the Receiving Party.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC051-0017",
    "doc_id": "DOC-051",
    "paragraph_index": 17,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 6803,
    "char_end": 6992,
    "char_count": 189,
    "text": "The confidentiality obligations under this Agreement shall continue for a period of three (3) years following\ndisclosure thereof irrespective of whether this Agreement is terminated or not.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC051-0018",
    "doc_id": "DOC-051",
    "paragraph_index": 18,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 6994,
    "char_end": 7534,
    "char_count": 540,
    "text": "Each Party acknowledges that any breach of its obligations under this Clause 5 shall be construed to be a material\nbreach of this Agreement. Each Party further acknowledges and agrees that, in the event of a breach or threatened\nbreach of any provision of this section, the Disclosing Party may have no adequate remedy in damages and,\naccordingly, is entitled, without waiving any other rights or remedies, to seek such injunctive or equitable relief\nagainst the Receiving Party as may be deemed proper by a court of competent jurisdiction.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
