    "char_start": 7601,
    "char_end": 7904,
    "char_count": 303,
    "text": "Page 3\n\n6. Warranty and Disclaimers\n\n(a)\nThe Consultant warrants to the Company that he: (i) has all necessary rights and authority to enter into and\nperform this Agreement; (ii) has no conflict of interest in respect of any third party obligations that he is\nbound by, in performance of this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC051-0021",
    "doc_id": "DOC-051",
    "paragraph_index": 21,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 7906,
    "char_end": 8361,
    "char_count": 455,
    "text": "(b) The Consultant hereby disclaims, and the Company expressly waives all other conditions, representations\nand guarantees, whether express or implied, arising by law, custom, oral or written statements of the\nConsultant or third parties including, but not limited to, any warranty of merchantability or fitness for\nparticular purpose or of error-free and uninterrupted use or of non-infringement except to the extent\nexpressly provided in this agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC051-0022",
    "doc_id": "DOC-051",
    "paragraph_index": 22,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 8363,
    "char_end": 8843,
    "char_count": 480,
    "text": "7. Termination\n\nEither Party may terminate this Agreement by issuing a written notice of termination to the other Party [___] days\nin advance of such intended termination. The Consultant shall not be liable to refund any amount in respect of\nthe Advisory Equity or part thereof, or transfer any part of the Advisory Equity to the Company upon earlier\ntermination of this Agreement, provided that such termination was not for reasons of breach or default on part\nof the Consultant.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC051-0023",
    "doc_id": "DOC-051",
    "paragraph_index": 23,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 8845,
    "char_end": 9256,
    "char_count": 411,
    "text": "8. Nature of Relationship\n\nThe Consultant is engaged by the Company in the capacity of an independent contractor to render the Services in\naccordance with the terms of this Agreement. Nothing in this Agreement shall be construed to mean that the\nConsultant is an employee, worker, agent or partner of the Company. Nothing in this Agreement shall be\nconstrued to have created a joint venture between the Parties.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC051-0024",
    "doc_id": "DOC-051",
    "paragraph_index": 24,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 9258,
    "char_end": 9746,
    "char_count": 488,
    "text": "9. Limitation of Liability\n\nIn no event shall the Consultant be liable to the Company, its employees or any person acting on its behalf, whether\nin contract, tort (including negligence) or otherwise for any loss of goodwill, any loss of business, profits or\nrevenue, loss of operation time, increased costs or wasted expenditure, damages of any kind including special,\nindirect, incidental, consequential, punitive, exemplary, or tort damages arising out of or relating to this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC051-0025",
    "doc_id": "DOC-051",
    "paragraph_index": 25,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 9748,
    "char_end": 10107,
    "char_count": 359,
    "text": "The maximum aggregate amount that the Company or any Party claiming through it can recover from the\nConsultant for all claims arising from, under or relating to this Agreement (whether in contract, tort including\nnegligence or otherwise) will in no event exceed the value of the services performed under this Agreement till the\ndate on which such claim arose.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC051-0026",
    "doc_id": "DOC-051",
    "paragraph_index": 26,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 10109,
    "char_end": 10632,
    "char_count": 523,
    "text": "10. Force Majeure\n\nNeither Party shall be responsible for delays or failures in performance resulting from acts of god, acts of civil or\nmilitary authority, fire, flood, strikes, war, epidemics, shortage of power, or other acts or causes reasonably beyond\nthe control of such Party. The Party experiencing the force majeure event agrees to give the other Party notice\npromptly following the occurrence of a force majeure event, and to use diligent efforts to re-commence\nperformance as promptly as commercially practicable.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC051-0027",
    "doc_id": "DOC-051",
    "paragraph_index": 27,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 10634,
    "char_end": 11209,
    "char_count": 575,
    "text": "11. Non-exclusivity\n\nThe Services provided by the Consultant under this Agreement is not exclusive to the Company and the Consultant\nshall have the right to enter into similar arrangements with any third party without the knowledge or consent of\nthe Company. Nothing in this Agreement shall prevent the Consultant from being engaged, concerned or having\nany financial or other interest in any capacity in any other business or entity during the term of this Agreement as\nlong as such activity does not cause a breach of the obligations of the Consultant under this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
