    "char_start": 45876,
    "char_end": 46348,
    "char_count": 472,
    "text": "21 | P a g e\n\n9. Integrity Pact:\nAll the Users in GeM i.e. Seller as well as Buyer agree not to indulge in any corrupt\npractices including without limitation any activity or action to influence the\ntransaction on any aspect of contract and commit to take all measures necessary to\nprevent corruption maintaining complete transparency and fairness in all activities\nrelated to GeM. Users agree to follow and adhere with the Integrity Pact guidelines\nprovided on GeM Portal.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0045",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 45,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 46349,
    "char_end": 48138,
    "char_count": 1789,
    "text": "10. Guarantee And Warrantee:\ni.\nThe Goods/Services supplied under the Contract(s) shall be in accordance with\nthe contract specifications & quality and the Goods shall be brand new and have\nstandard Guarantee/Warrantee for one year period from the date of final\nacceptance by the consignee unless otherwise specified in category\nspecifications, specific Bid/RA . Seller, at the time of listing their product on\nGeM portal or offering their products against any Bid / RA, may accordingly\nprovide longer Guarantee/Warrantee period (i.e. more than 1 year) and in such\ncase, Guarantee/Warrantee period stipulation made in category specifications /\nBid / RA document, shall prevail over standard Guarantee / Warrantee period of\n1 year stipulated in these General Terms and Conditions.\nii.\nNotwithstanding the fact that the Buyer or its Quality Assurance Officer may\nhave inspected and/or approved / accepted the said Goods, it is further\nguaranteed that if during the said guarantee / warrantee period, the Goods be\ndiscovered not to conform to the requisite description and quality and/or not\ngiving satisfactory performance or have deteriorated, and the decision of the\nBuyer in that behalf shall be final and binding on the Seller and the Buyer shall\nbe entitled to call upon the Seller to rectify and/or replace the Goods or such\nportion thereof as is found to be defective by the Buyer within 7 days.\nOtherwise, the Seller shall pay to the Buyer such compensations that may arise\nby reasons of the warranty therein contained. In cases requiring Spares, the\nSeller guarantees that they will supply Spare Parts, if and when required on\nagreed basis for an agreed price for a minimum period of three years from the\ndate of expiry of warrantee period (unless otherwise specified in STC / ATC).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0046",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 46,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 48139,
    "char_end": 48444,
    "char_count": 305,
    "text": "The agreed basis could be, including but without any limitation, an agreed\ndiscount on the published catalogue or an agreed percentage of profit on the\nlanded cost. The aforesaid provisions made specifically for Goods, shall also be\napplicable for Services to the extent the same are practically possible.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0047",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
