    "char_end": 50709,
    "char_count": 514,
    "text": "the rejection / part rejection by the Buyer/ Consignee, the Seller shall be liable\nto remove / lift back such rejected Goods within 10 days without any extra\ncharge/cost to the Buyer / Consignee failing which suitable ground rent /\nwarehousing charges would be payable by the Seller to the Buyer /Consignee.\nIf the Seller fails to remove / lift back such rejected Goods within reasonable\ntime period, the Buyer / Consignee shall have the right to dispose off such\nrejected goods at the risk and cost of the seller.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0049",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 49,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 50710,
    "char_end": 50823,
    "char_count": 113,
    "text": "12. Payment Authority and Payment Terms:\nPayments shall be made to the Seller in the manner below:\ni.\nFor Goods :",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0050",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 50,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 50825,
    "char_end": 51328,
    "char_count": 503,
    "text": "23 | P a g e\n\nIn case of goods, 100% payment will be released within ten (10) days of issue\nof consignee receipt-cum-acceptance certificate (CRAC) and on-line submission\nof bills unless otherwise specified in STC / ATC.\nii.\nFor Services:\nIn case of services, 100% payments on the basis of monthly (unless otherwise\nspecified) bills will be paid within ten (10) days of issue of consignee receipt-\ncum-acceptance certificate (CRAC) and on-line submission of bills unless\notherwise specified in STC / ATC.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0051",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 51,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 51329,
    "char_end": 51702,
    "char_count": 373,
    "text": "13. Terms of Delivery:\nAll the Goods or Services in the GeM shall be offered on Free Delivery at Site basis\nincluding\nloading/unloading.\nIn\nrespect\nof\nitems\nrequiring\ninstallation,\ncommissioning and other services in the scope of supply (as indicated in respective\nproduct category specification / STC / ATC), the cost of the same shall also be\nincluded in the offer price.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0052",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 52,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 51703,
    "char_end": 52204,
    "char_count": 501,
    "text": "14. Delivery Period\nSeller shall indicate the quantity which can be supplied over the specified time\nperiod(s). The Seller would offer these details, which would constitute the part of\nthe awarded Contract(s) in the GeM and would make a binding Contract between\nthe Seller & the Buyer. Any modification thereto shall be mutually agreed and\nincorporated in the Contract. This Delivery Period/Time shall be deemed to be\nessence of the Contract and delivery must be completed not later than such date(s).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0053",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 53,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 52205,
    "char_end": 53093,
    "char_count": 888,
    "text": "15. Extension of Delivery Period and Liquidated Damages:\nBuyer may, on the request of the Seller or otherwise, extend the delivery date\nsuitably subject to the following conditions:\ni.\nThe original Delivery Period may be re-fixed by the Buyer without any\nLiquidated damages subject to Force Majeure conditions mentioned below and\nalso on the ground/reasons of delay attributable to the Buyer / Consignee.\nii.\nFor other cases, provided the price trend is not lower, the Delivery Period may\nbe suitably extended for which an amount equal to the Liquidated Damages for\nthe extended period(s) for delay in the supply of the Goods/Services after the\nexpiry of contract delivery period /re-fixed delivery period, shall be recovered\nfrom the Seller as mentioned hereinafter for the extended period. No increase in\nprice on any ground after the original/re-fixed delivery date shall be admissible",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0054",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 54,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 53095,
    "char_end": 54872,
    "char_count": 1777,
    "text": "24 | P a g e\n\nduring such extended period(s). Nevertheless the Buyer shall be entitled to the\nbenefit of any decrease in price on account of reduction in GST taking place\nduring extended delivery period.\niii.\nLiquidated Damages: If the Seller fails to deliver any or all of the\nGoods/Services within the original/re-fixed delivery period(s) specified in the\ncontract, the Buyer will be entitled to deduct/recover the Liquidated Damages\nfor the delay, unless covered under Force Majeure conditions aforesaid, @\n0.5% per week or part of the week of delayed period as pre-estimated damages\nnot exceeding 10% of the contract value without any controversy/dispute of any\nsort whatsoever.\niv.\nForce Majeure Conditions :\nIf at any time during the continuance of the Contract, the performance in\nwhole or in part by either party of any obligation under this Contract shall be\nprevented or delayed by the reasons of any war, hostility, acts of the public\nenemy, epidemics, civil commotion, sabotage, fires, floods, explosion,\nquarantine restrictions, strikes, lockouts or act of God provided notice of\nhappening of such event duly evidenced with documents is given by one party\nto the other within 10 days from the date of occurrence thereof, neither party\nshall be by reasons of such event, be entitled to terminate the Contract nor\nshall either party have any claim for damages against the other in respect of\nsuch non-performance or the delay in performance, and deliveries under the\ncontract shall be resumed as soon as practicable after such event has come to\nan end or ceased to exist, and the decision of the Buyer as to whether the\ndeliveries have been so resumed or not, shall be final and conclusive,\nProvided further that if the performance in whole or part of any obligation",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0055",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 55,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 54873,
    "char_end": 55506,
    "char_count": 633,
    "text": "under this contract is prevented or delayed by reason of any such event for a\nperiod exceeding 10 days, either party may at its option terminate the contract\nprovided also that the Buyer shall be at liberty to take over from the Seller at a\nprice to be fixed by Buyer, which shall be final, all unused, undamaged and\naccepted material, bought out components and Goods in course of\nmanufacture in the possession of the Seller at the time of such termination or\nsuch portion thereof as the Buyer may deem fit excepting such materials,\nbought out components and Goods as the Seller may with the concurrence of\nthe Buyer elect to retain.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0056",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 56,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 55507,
    "char_end": 55576,
    "char_count": 69,
    "text": "16. Dispute Resolution Between Buyer and Seller:\nAMICABLE SETTLEMENT:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0057",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 57,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 55578,
    "char_end": 57377,
    "char_count": 1799,
    "text": "25 | P a g e\n\nIn the event of any question, dispute or difference arising connection with the\nContract, the Parties shall use their respective reasonable endeavour to settle any\ndispute amicably. If a Dispute is not resolved within 30 days after written notice of\nany dispute by one Party to the other, the same shall be resolved through the\nmechanism of a co-ordination committee to be formed by the Buyer and\nSeller/Service Provider and to be chaired by the Primary User of Buyer\nOrganization/Department along with representatives from Buyer Department and\nSeller.\nARBITRATION:\nIn the event of any question, dispute or difference arising under the terms and\nconditions of the contract placed through GeM, the same shall be referred to\nthe sole arbitration by an officer nominated as Arbitrator by the Primary Buyer of\nthe concerned Buyer Organization. It will be no objection that the arbitrator is a\nGovernment Servant and that he had to deal with the matters to which the\ncontract relates or that in the course of his duties as a Government servant he has\nexpressed views on all or any of the matters in dispute or difference. The award\nof the arbitrator shall be final and binding on the parties to the contract. The\narbitration shall be governed as per Indian Arbitration and Conciliation Act 1996\nas amended up to date. The place for arbitration shall be at the place from where\ncontract has been placed by the Buyer or at the place of Primary Buyer as decided\nby the Primary Buyer.\nIn the event of the Arbitrator dying, neglecting or refusing to act or resigning or\nbeing unable to act for any reason, or his award being set aside by the court for\nany reason, it shall be lawful for the Primary Buyer to appoint another arbitrator in\nplace of the outgoing arbitrator in the manner aforesaid.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0058",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 58,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 57379,
    "char_end": 57954,
    "char_count": 575,
    "text": "In respect of all contract placed through GeM, the dispute would not be referred or\nentertained by Micro and Small Enterprise Facilitation Council, Consumer Forum\nor any other adjudication forum.\nAll disputes in connection with the Contract, shall be subject to the\nexclusive jurisdiction of the Court within the local limits of whose jurisdiction, the\nplace from where Contract was issued is situated\nGeM SPV would not be a party to any such dispute/matter.\n17. Laws Governing the Contract:\ni.\nThe contract shall be governed by the laws of India for the time being in force.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0059",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 59,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 57956,
    "char_end": 58437,
    "char_count": 481,
    "text": "26 | P a g e\n\nii.\nIrrespective of the place of delivery, the place of performance or the place of\npayment under the contract, the contract shall be deemed to have been made at the\nregistered address of the Buyer and / or Primary Buyer.\niii.\nJurisdiction of Courts: The courts of the place from where the contract has been\nmade shall alone have jurisdiction to decide any dispute arising out of or in respect\nof the contract.\niv.\nGeM SPV would not be a party to any such litigation.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0060",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 60,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 58438,
    "char_end": 59363,
    "char_count": 925,
    "text": "18. Limitation of Liability:\nNotwithstanding anything contained in this agreement, no party will be liable for\nany special, incidental or consequential damages arising out of or in connection\nwith this agreement or any breach hereof (including for loss of data or profits, or\ncost of cover), whether or not such party has been advised of the possibility of such\ndamages, and whether under a theory of contract, tort (including negligence) or\notherwise; except for liabilities arising out of any violation, misappropriation or\ninfringement of a party’s intellectual property rights, or from a breach by either\nparty of its obligation. In no event will either party’s aggregate liability arising out\nof or in connection with this agreement or any breach hereof (whether under a\ntheory of contract, tort (including negligence), warranty or otherwise) exceed the\nContract Price entered into the Contract between Buyer and Seller.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0061",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 61,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 59364,
    "char_end": 60020,
    "char_count": 656,
    "text": "19. Termination for Default:\nIf the Seller does not perform its obligations within the Delivery Period/Date\nmentioned in the Contract, the same would constitute the breach of the Contract and\nthe Buyer shall have the right to Cancel or withdraw the Contract for the unsupplied\nportion after the expiry of the original or re-fixed delivery date or period stipulated\nin the Contract. Such cancellation of contract on account of non -performance by\nthe Seller would entitle the Buyer to forfeit the performance security besides other\nactions such as   downgrading the Seller’s rating or debarment from the GeM for\nspecified period as decided by GeM on merits.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0062",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 62,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 60021,
    "char_end": 60214,
    "char_count": 193,
    "text": "20. Closure of Transaction:\nAfter satisfactory completion of all the obligations under the Contract and release of\npayments for the goods / services, the transaction shall be treated as closed.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0063",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 63,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 60215,
    "char_end": 60288,
    "char_count": 73,
    "text": "21. Grounds for Administrative Action Against Seller’s Misconduct in GeM:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0064",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 64,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 60290,
    "char_end": 61976,
    "char_count": 1686,
    "text": "27 | P a g e\n\nThe Seller would be liable for administrative actions such as suspension / debarment\n/ removal from GeM, if they fail to abide by any of the terms & conditions\nstipulated in this document and/or on the following grounds, if the Seller:-\ni.\nListing the products/services not in the relevant categories and/or listing the\nsame with vague/conflicting product specifications/details and irrelevant\nproduct photographs.\nii.\nOffering Goods / Services without having proper authorization\niii.\nSupplies goods of inferior/ substandard quality\niv.\nSupplies refurbished or counterfeit products\nv.\nWithdraws or modify or impairs or derogates from the bid in any respect\nwithin the period of validity of its bid; or\nvi.\nIf it comes to notice that the information / documents furnished in its bid is\ninaccurate ,false, misleading or forged; or\nvii.\nFails to furnish requisite performance security / PBG within stipulated time\nrequired as per e-bid / RA conditions.\nviii.\nFails to update GeM about any change in information furnished within the\nprescribed time limits.\nix.\nExecutes services without conforming to requirement given in Service Level\nAgreement (SLA)\nx.\nFails to execute an order/ contract or fail to execute it satisfactorily\nxi.\nIs declared bankrupt or insolvent\nxii.\nFails to produce the requisite documents/ information during the course of\ninspection / assessment at any stage; and\nxiii.\nOn any other ground for which, in the opinion of GeM, the retention of the\nseller or any of its offered product in GeM is not in Public Interest\nThe grounds mentioned above are illustrative only. Users are advised to read the list\nof prohibited activities published on the website.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0065",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 65,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 61977,
    "char_end": 62224,
    "char_count": 247,
    "text": "22. Role of Government E- Marketplace - Gem SPV\nGovernment e-Marketplace – GeM SPV is the owner of the GeM portal which\nmonitors and supervises all the business transactions on the portal. The role and\nresponsibilities of the company are as under:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0066",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 66,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 62226,
    "char_end": 63699,
    "char_count": 1473,
    "text": "28 | P a g e\n\na. To develop, operate and maintain technology driven e-marketplace, through a\nManaged Service Provider (MSP), to be used by government agencies for\nprocurement of various goods and services in a transparent and efficient\nmanner.\nb. Overall supervision and monitoring of GeM portal operations, policy\nmanagement, finalization and implementation of various business processes\nand work flows in adherence with the applicable law and executive orders\nissued from time to time . To provide tools for on-line Bidding, on-line Reverse\nAuction and Business Analytics Tools on GeM.\nc. To work continuously for improvements in the Business Processes and Work\nFlows for various activities / functions on GeM based on feedback from various\nstakeholders to enhance transparency, efficiency, competitiveness, equality,\neconomy in procurement of goods and services by government agencies.\nd. To finalize General Terms and Conditions for sale and purchase of Goods and\nServices on GeM, Product / Service Specific Special Terms and Conditions,\nSpecial Terms and Conditions for Bunching of Goods / Services, Bid Specific\nSpecial Conditions, Project Specific Special Conditions etc.\ne. To finalize, upload and approve Technical Specification Frameworks for\nvarious item / service categories on GeM and to monitor conformity of offered\nproducts to the larger framework so finalized and uploaded.\nf. To decide addition / deletion of any of the offered product(s)/Product category",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0067",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 67,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 63700,
    "char_end": 64544,
    "char_count": 844,
    "text": "(ies) and their framework of technical parameters on GeM.\ng. To work and co-ordinate with different Organizations/Departments / Agencies\nfor integration of their Databases with the GeM portal on real time basis for the\npurpose of verification/authentication of data entries made by stakeholders.\nh. To offer and manage Demand Aggregation services for identified categories\nacross buyers with assured reasonability of price, recommending for placement\nof orders by individual buyers\ni. To co-ordinate with MSP for conducting workshops for the various\nStakeholders in capacity building and in change management associated with\nthe implementation of technology enabled procurement process.\nj. To monitor MSP that the Buyers, Sellers and Service Providers are being\nassisted properly by them to onboard their goods and services on the GeM\nplatform.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0068",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 68,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 64546,
    "char_end": 66305,
    "char_count": 1759,
    "text": "29 | P a g e\n\nk. To identify and offer services of 3rd parties for Vendor Assessment relating to\ntechnical, financial capacity, past experience of sellers including manufacturing\n/ testing facilities / quality control arrangement(s) of manufacturing premises\nand/or any of the premises related to manufacturing process of products /\nservices offered by the seller / service provider on GeM.\nl. To identify and offer services of 3rd parties for testing and certifying the quality\nof the product offered/ supplied, through documents, test reports/ certificates,\ntesting at any independent lab or through inspection/testing by its authorized\nrepresentative/s at firm’s premises or at user’s premises, that buyer choose to\nuse.\nm. Overall monitoring and management of Call Centre/Help desk operations being\nprovided by the MSP.\nn. Removal / debarring the Sellers/Buyers and Goods / services in GeM.\no. Management of complaints and their redressal mechanism in GeM (not\ndisputes related to concluded contracts).\np. To identify, integrate and manage MoUs with verifying, certifying and\nvalidating entities across government(s) and also professional agencies to\nreinforce the online paperless, contactless and cashless system on GeM.\nq. To issue Notices, Circulars, News, Flashes, Updates etc in GeM\nr. Reporting and MIS mechanism in GeM\ns. Any other related activities in the GeM\nt. In exceptional circumstances, for ensuring propriety of procurement processes\nor to obviate possible misuse of GeM functionalities, GeM SPV as GeM Admin\nmay keep any Bidding / RA process on hold for some time as considered\nappropriate.\nu. To take approved User Charges from Buyers and Sellers for the various\ntransactions on the GeM portal as decided and notified on the GeM portal.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0069",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 69,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 66306,
    "char_end": 66741,
    "char_count": 435,
    "text": "23. Miscellaneous Provisions\na. Assignment: Users understand and agree that the GTC, STC and ATC\nprovisions, rights and obligations granted by GeM are non- transferrable or\nassignable by the User to any third party, without the prior written consent of\nGeM. If same is permitted by GeM, all the conditions, rights and obligations of\nthe GTC or any on–going STC/ATC shall also be binding upon such third party\nassignee besides the User.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
