    "char_end": 72486,
    "char_count": 276,
    "text": "(i) threatens the unity, integrity, defence, security or sovereignty of\nIndia, friendly relations with foreign states, or public order or causes\nincitement to the commission of any cognizable offence or prevents\ninvestigation of any offence or is insulting any other nation. \"",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0080",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 80,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 72487,
    "char_end": 73328,
    "char_count": 841,
    "text": "24. Incident management Policy on GeM: GeM is a trust based system and self-declaration\nis the key, along with a strong automated process to penalize any deviant behaviour on\npart of Sellers / Buyers. For this purpose, deviations from the terms and conditions of\nprocurement on GeM, including general terms and conditions, special and additional\nterms and conditions and any other relevant Government rules and guidelines, are termed\nas “deviation”. A deviation can occur while listing the products on GeM, at pre-contract\nstage, during bidding or at post contract stage on GeM. The mechanism for reporting and\ninitiating action on such deviation has been detailed in the Incident Management Policy\navailable on GeM portal under Resources. All stake holders of GeM shall be bound by the\nactions as detailed in the Incident Management Policy.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0081",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 81,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 73330,
    "char_end": 73844,
    "char_count": 514,
    "text": "33 | P a g e\n\nAll administrative actions under this Incident management Policy, taken by GeM against\nany of the stakeholders shall not cause any limitation on the legal and/or contractual\nremedies including any financial recoveries, available to Buyers/Sellers under the Terms\nand Conditions of contract and/or GeM policies. In case the Buyer / Seller choose to\npursue any of these remedies, GeM shall not be made party to such proceedings /\nremedial actions taken by Buyer/Seller under the contractual provisions.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC052-0082",
    "doc_id": "DOC-052",
    "paragraph_index": 82,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 73846,
    "char_end": 74968,
    "char_count": 1122,
    "text": "25. e-Sign authorization:\nI hereby authorize NSDL e-Gov on behalf of my organisation to:\n1. Use my Aadhaar details for all transactions on Government e-Marketplace and\nauthenticate my identity through the Aadhaar Authentication system (Aadhaar\nbased e-KYC services of UIDAI) in accordance with the provisions of the Aadhar\n(Targeted Delivery of Financial and other Subsidies, Benefits and Services) Act,\n2016 and the allied rules and regulations notified there under and for no other\npurpose.\n2. Authenticate my Aadhaar through OTP or Biometric for authenticating my identity\nthrough the Aadhaar Authentication system for obtaining my e-KYC through\nAadhaar based e-KYC services of UIDAI and use my Photo and Demographic\ndetails (Name, Gender, Date of Birth and Address) for signing all documents\nrelated to transactions on Government e-Marketplace.\n3. I understand that Security and confidentiality of personal identity data provided,\nfor the purpose of Aadhaar based authentication is ensured by NSDL e-Gov and\nthe data will be stored by NSDL e-Govt till such time as mentioned in guidelines\nfrom UIDAI from time to time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
