    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0031",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 31,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 7148,
    "char_end": 8079,
    "char_count": 931,
    "text": "GOVERNMENT OF PUDUCHERRY\nPUBLIC WORKS DEPARTMENT\n\nGeneral Rules &\nDirections\n1.\nAll work proposed for execution by contract will be notified in a form of invitation\nto tender pasted by publication in News papers or posted on website as the\ncase may be. This form will state the work to be carried out, as well as the date\nfor submitting and opening tenders and the time allowed for carrying out the\nwork, also the amount of earnest money to be deposited with the tender, and\nthe amount of the security deposit and Performance guarantee to be deposited\nby the successful tenderer and the percentage, if any, to be deducted from bills.\nCopies of the specifications, designs and drawings and any other documents\nrequired in connection with the work signed for the purpose of identification by\nthe officer inviting tender shall also be open for inspection by the contractor at\nthe office of officer inviting tender during office hours.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0032",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 32,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 8081,
    "char_end": 8479,
    "char_count": 398,
    "text": "2.\nIn the event of tender being submitted by a firm, it must be signed separately by\neach partner thereof or in the event of the absence of any partner, it must be\nsigned on his behalf by a person holding a power of attorney authorizing him to\ndo so, such power of attorney to be produced with the tender, and it must\ndisclose that the firm is duly registered under the Indian Partnership Act 1952.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0033",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 33,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 8481,
    "char_end": 10129,
    "char_count": 1648,
    "text": "3.\nReceipts for payment made on account of work, when executed by a firm, must\nalso be signed by all the partners, except where contractors are described in\ntheir tender as a firm, in which case the receipts must be signed in the name of\nthe firm by one of the partners, or by some other person having due authority to\ngive effectual receipts for the firm.\nApplicable for Item\nRate Tender only\n(PWD - 8)\n4.\nThe rate(s) must be quoted in decimal coinage. Amounts must be quoted in full\nrupees by ignoring fifty paisa and considering more than fifty paisa as rupee\none.\nIn case the lowest tendered amount (worked out on the basis of quoted rate of\nIndividual items) of two or more contractors is same, then such lowest\ncontractors may be asked to submit sealed revised offer quoting rate of each\nitem of the schedule of quantity for all sub sections/sub heads as the case may\nbe, but the revised quoted rate of each item of schedule of quantity for all sub\nsections/sub heads should not be higher than their respective original rate\nquoted already at the time of submission of tender. The lowest tender shall be\ndecided on the basis of revised offer.\nIf the revised tendered amount (worked out on the basis of quoted rate of\nindividual items) of two or more contractors received in revised offer is again\nfound to be equal, then the lowest tender, among such contractors, shall be\ndecided by draw of lots in the presence of SE of the circle, or CE of the zone\nEE(s) in-charge of major & minor component(s) (also DDH in case Horticulture\nwork is also included in the tender), and the lowest contractors those have\nquoted equal amount of their tenders.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0034",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 34,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 10131,
    "char_end": 10161,
    "char_count": 30,
    "text": "GENERAL RULES & DIRECTIONS\nPWD",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0035",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 35,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 10163,
    "char_end": 10164,
    "char_count": 1,
    "text": "7",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0036",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 36,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 10166,
    "char_end": 11952,
    "char_count": 1786,
    "text": "In case of any such lowest contractor in his revised offer quotes rate of any item\nmore than their respective original rate quoted already at the time of submission\nof tender, then such revised offer shall be treated invalid. Such case of revised\noffer of the lowest contractor or case of refusal to submit revised offer by the\nlowest contractor shall be treated as withdrawal of his tender before acceptance\nand 50% of his earnest money shall be forfeited. In case all the lowest\ncontractors those have same tendered amount (as a result of their quoted rate\nof individual items), refuse to submit revised offers, then tenders are to be\nrecalled after forfeiting 50% of EMD of each lowest contractors. Contractor,\nwhose earnest money is forfeited because of non-submission of revised offer, or\nquoting higher revised rate(s) of any item(s) than their respective original rate\nquoted already at the time of submission of his bid shall not be allowed to\nparticipate in the retendering process of the work.\nApplicable for\nPercentage Rate\nTender only [PWD- 7]\n4A. In case of Percentage Rate Tenders, contractor shall fill up the usual printed\nform, stating at what percentage below/above (in figures as well as in words)\nthe total estimated cost given in Schedule of Quantities at Schedule-A, he will\nbe willing to execute the work. The tender submitted shall be treated as invalid if\n:-\nI.\nThe contractor does not quote percentage above/below on the total\namount of tender or any section/sub head of the tender.\nII.\nThe percentage above/below is not quoted in figures & words both on the\ntotal amount of tender or any section/sub head of the tender.\nIII.\nThe percentage quoted above/below is different in figures & words on the\ntotal amount of tender or any section/sub head of the tender.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0037",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 37,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 11953,
    "char_end": 12213,
    "char_count": 260,
    "text": "Tenders, which propose any alteration in the work specified in the said form of\ninvitation to tender, or in the time allowed for carrying out the work, or which\ncontain any other conditions of any sort including conditional rebates, will be\nsummarily rejected.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0038",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 38,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 12215,
    "char_end": 12820,
    "char_count": 605,
    "text": "4B. In case the lowest tendered amount (estimated cost + amount worked on the\nbasis of percentage above/below) of two or more contractors is same, such\nlowest contractors will be asked to submit sealed revised offer in the form of\nletter mentioning percentage above/ below on estimated cost of tender including\nall sub sections/sub heads as the case may be, but the revised percentage\nquoted above/below on tendered cost or on each sub section/ sub head should\nnot be higher than the percentage quoted at the time of submission of tender.\nThe lowest tender shall be decided on the basis of revised offers.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0039",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 39,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 12822,
    "char_end": 13001,
    "char_count": 179,
    "text": "In case any of such contractor refuses to submit revised offer, then it shall be\ntreated as withdrawal of his tender before acceptance and 50% of earnest\nmoney shall be forfeited.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0040",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 40,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 13003,
    "char_end": 13431,
    "char_count": 428,
    "text": "If the revised tendered amount of two more contractors received in revised offer\nis again found to be equal, the lowest tender, among such contractors, shall be\ndecided by draw of lots in the presence of SE of the circle, or CE of the zone\nEE(s) in-charge of major & minor component(s) (also DDH in case Horticulture\nwork is also included in the tender), & the lowest contractors those have quoted\nequal amount of their tenders.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0041",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 41,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 13433,
    "char_end": 13789,
    "char_count": 356,
    "text": "In case all the lowest contractors those have quoted same tendered amount,\nrefuse to submit revised offers, then tenders are to be recalled after forfeiting\n50% of EMD of each contractor. Contractor(s), whose earnest money is\nforfeited because of non-submission of revised offer, shall not be allowed to\nparticipate in the re-tendering process of the work.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0042",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 42,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 13791,
    "char_end": 13821,
    "char_count": 30,
    "text": "GENERAL RULES & DIRECTIONS\nPWD",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0043",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 43,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 13823,
    "char_end": 13824,
    "char_count": 1,
    "text": "8",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0044",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 44,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 13826,
    "char_end": 14141,
    "char_count": 315,
    "text": "5.\nThe officer inviting tender or his duly authorized assistant, will open tenders in\nthe presence of any intending contractors who may be present at the time.\n6.\nThe officer inviting tenders shall have the right of rejecting all or any of the\ntenders and will not be bound to accept the lowest or any other tender.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0045",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 45,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 14143,
    "char_end": 15753,
    "char_count": 1610,
    "text": "7.\nThe receipt of an accountant or clerk for any money paid by the contractor will\nnot be considered as any acknowledgment or payment to the officer inviting\ntender and the contractor shall be responsible for seeing that he procures a\nreceipt signed by the officer inviting tender or a duly authorized Cashier.\nApplicable for Item\nRate Tender only\n(PWD - 8)\n8.\nIn the case of Item Rate Tenders, only rates quoted shall be considered. Any\ntender containing percentage below/above the rates quoted is liable to be\nrejected. Rates quoted by the contractor in item rate tender in figures and words\nshall be accurately filled in so that there is no discrepancy in the rates written in\nfigures and words. However, if a discrepancy is found, the rates which\ncorrespond with the amount worked out by the contractor shall unless otherwise\nproved be taken as correct. If the amount of an item is not worked out by the\ncontractor or it does not correspond with the rates written either in figures or in\nwords, then the rates quoted by the contractor in words shall be taken as\ncorrect. Where the rates quoted by the contractor in figures and in words tally,\nbut the amount is not worked out correctly, the rates quoted by the contractor\nwill unless otherwise proved be taken as correct and not the amount. In event\nno rate has been quoted for any item(s), leaving space both in figure(s),\nword(s), and amount blank, it will be presumed that the contractor has included\nthe cost of this/these item(s) in other items and rate for such item(s) will be\nconsidered as zero and work will be required to be executed accordingly.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0046",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 46,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 15755,
    "char_end": 17301,
    "char_count": 1546,
    "text": "However, if a tenderer quotes nil rates against each item in item rate tender, the\ntender shall be treated as invalid and will not be considered as lowest tenderer\nand earnest money deposited shall be forfeited\nApplicable for\npercentage Rate\nTender only (PWD - 7)\n9.\nIn case of Percentage Rate Tenders only percentage quoted shall be\nconsidered. Any tender containing item rates is liable to be rejected. Percentage\nquoted by the contractor in percentage rate tender shall be accurately filled in\nfigures and words, so that there is no discrepancy.\nApplicable for\nPercentage Rate\nTender only (PWD - 7)\n10. In Percentage Rate Tender, the tenderer shall quote percentage below/above\n(in figures as well as in words) at which he will be willing to execute the work.\nHe shall also work out the total amount of his offer and the same should be\nwritten in figures as well as in words in such a way that no interpolation is\npossible. In case of figures, the word ‘Rs.’ should be written before the figure of\nrupees and word ‘P’ after the decimal figures, e.g. ‘Rs. 2.15P and in case of\nwords, the word ‘Rupees’ should precede and the word ‘Paisa’ should be written\nat the end.\n11. (i) The Contractor whose tender is accepted, will be required to furnish\nperformance guarantee at specified percentage of the tendered amount as\nmentioned in Schedule 'E' and within the period specified in Schedule F. This\nguarantee shall be in the form of Insurance Surety Bonds, Account Payee\nDemand Draft, Fixed Deposit Receipt or Bank Guarantee of any Commercial\nBank.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0047",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 47,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 17303,
    "char_end": 17333,
    "char_count": 30,
    "text": "GENERAL RULES & DIRECTIONS\nPWD",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0048",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 48,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 17335,
    "char_end": 17336,
    "char_count": 1,
    "text": "9",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0049",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 49,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 17338,
    "char_end": 19042,
    "char_count": 1704,
    "text": "(ii) The contractor whose tender is accepted will also be required to furnish by\nway of Security Deposit for the fulfillment of his contract, an amount equal to\n2.5% of the tendered amount of the work. The Security deposit will be collected\nby deductions from the running bills as well as final bill of the contractor at the\nrates mentioned above. The Security amount will also be accepted in the shape\nof Insurance Surety Bonds, Account Payee Demand Draft, Fixed Deposit\nReceipt or Bank Guarantee from any of the Commercial Banks will be accepted\nfor this purpose provided confirmatory advice is enclosed.\n12. On acceptance of the tender, the name of the accredited representative(s) of\nthe contractor who would be responsible for taking instructions from the\nEngineer-in-Charge shall be communicated in writing to the Engineer-in-\nCharge.\n13. GST or any other tax applicable in respect of inputs procured by the contractor\nfor this contract shall be payable by the Contractor and Government will not\nentertain any claim whatsoever in respect of the same. However, component of\nGST at time of supply of service (as provided in CGST Act 2017) provided by\nthe contract shall be varied if different from that applicable on the last date of\nreceipt of tender including extension if any.\n14. The contractor shall give a list of both gazetted and non-gazetted P.W.D.\nemployees related to him.\n15. The tender for composite work includes, in addition to building work, all other\nworks such as sanitary and water supply installations drainage installation,\nelectrical work, horticulture work, roads and paths etc.\n16. The contractor shall submit list of works which are in hand (progress) in the\nfollowing form:-",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0050",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 50,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 19044,
    "char_end": 19172,
    "char_count": 128,
    "text": "Name of\nwork\nName and particulars of Divn\nwhere work is being executed\nValue of\nwork\nPosition of\nworks in\nRemarks\n1.\n2.\n3.\n4.\n5.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
