    "char_start": 19199,
    "char_end": 19201,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "10",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0053",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 53,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 19203,
    "char_end": 20211,
    "char_count": 1008,
    "text": "CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\n\nDefinitions\n1.\nThe Contract means the documents forming the tender and acceptance thereof\nand the formal agreement executed between the competent authority on behalf\nof the President of India and the Contractor, together with the documents\nreferred to therein including these conditions, the specifications, designs,\ndrawings and instructions issued from time to time by the Engineer-in- Charge\nand all these documents taken together, shall be deemed to form one contract\nand shall be complementary to one another.\n2.\nIn the contract, the following expressions shall, unless the context otherwise\nrequires, have the meanings, hereby respectively assigned to them:-\n(i)\nThe expression works or work shall, unless there be something either in\nthe subject or context repugnant to such construction, be construed and\ntaken to mean the works by or by virtue of the contract contracted to be\nexecuted whether temporary or permanent, and whether original, altered,\nsubstituted or additional.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0054",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 54,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 20212,
    "char_end": 20528,
    "char_count": 316,
    "text": "(ii) The Site shall mean the land, places on, into or or where work is to be\nexecuted under the contract or any adjacent land, path or street or where\nwork is to be executed under the contract or any adjacent land, path or\nstreet which may be temporally allotted or used for the purpose of carrying\nout the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0055",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 55,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 20529,
    "char_end": 20869,
    "char_count": 340,
    "text": "(iii) The Contractor shall mean the individual, firm or company, whether\nincorporated or not, undertaking the works and shall include the legal\npersonal representative of such individual or the persons composing such\nfirm or company, or the successors of such firm or company and the\npermitted assignees of such individual, firm or company.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0056",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 56,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 20870,
    "char_end": 21015,
    "char_count": 145,
    "text": "(iv) The President means the President of India and his successors.\n(v) Government or Government of Puducherry shall mean the President of\nIndia.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0057",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 57,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 21016,
    "char_end": 21227,
    "char_count": 211,
    "text": "(vi) The Engineer-in-charge means the Engineer Officer who shall supervise\nand be in charge of the work and who shall sign the contract on behalf of\nthe President of India as mentioned in Schedule 'F' hereunder.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0058",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 58,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 21228,
    "char_end": 21337,
    "char_count": 109,
    "text": "(vii) The term Director General includes Special Director General/Additional\nDirector General/Chief Engineer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0059",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 59,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 21338,
    "char_end": 22096,
    "char_count": 758,
    "text": "(viii) Accepting Authority shall mean the authority mentioned in Schedule 'F'.\n(ix) Excepted Risk are risks due to riots (other than those on account of\ncontractor's employees), war (whether declared or not) invasion, act of\nforeign enemies, hostilities, civil war, rebellion revolution, insurrection,\nmilitary or usurped power, any acts of Government, damages from aircraft,\nacts of God, such as earthquake, lightening and unprecedented floods, and\nother causes over which the contractor has no control and accepted as\nsuch by the Accepting Authority or causes solely due to use or occupation\nby Government of the part of the works in respect of which a certificate of\ncompletion has been issued or a cause solely due to Government's faulty\ndesign of works.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0060",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 60,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 22097,
    "char_end": 22348,
    "char_count": 251,
    "text": "(x) (a) Market Rate shall be the rate as decided by the Engineer-in-Charge on\nthe basis of the cost of materials and labour at the site where the work is to\nbe executed plus the percentage mentioned in Schedule 'F' to cover, all\noverheads and profits.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
