    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 86463,
    "char_end": 86994,
    "char_count": 531,
    "text": "Then, M = C+F+I-J\n\nCost of work for which escalation is applicable (W) = 0.85M\n\nComponents for materials, labour, etc. shall be pre-determined for every work\nand incorporated in the conditions of contract attached to the tender documents\nincluded in Schedule 'F'. The decision of the Engineer-in-Charge in working out\nsuch percentage shall be binding on the contractors.\n(iii)  The following principles shall be followed while working out the payment/recovery\non account of variation of prices of materials and/ or wages of labour.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0192",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 192,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 86996,
    "char_end": 87716,
    "char_count": 720,
    "text": "(a) The compensation for escalation shall be worked out at quarterly intervals\nand shall be with respect to the cost of work done as per bills paid during the\nthree calendar months of the said quarter. The date of submission of bill by\nthe contractor to the department shall be the guiding factor to decide the bills\nrelevant to the quarterly interval. The first such payment shall be made at the\nend of three months after the month (excluding the month in which the letter\nof commencement of work is issued by the Engineer-in-Charge) and\nthereafter at three months' interval. At the time of completion of the work, the\nlast period for payment might become less than 3 months, depending on the\nactual date of completion.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0193",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 193,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 87718,
    "char_end": 88154,
    "char_count": 436,
    "text": "(b) The indices as defined below (excluding LI) relevant to any quarter/period for\nwhich such compensation is to be paid shall be the arithmetical average of\nthe indices relevant to the three calendar months. If the period up to the date\nof completion after the quarter covered by the last such installment of\npayment, is less than three months, the indices shall be the average of the\nindices for the months falling within that period.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0194",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 194,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 88156,
    "char_end": 88394,
    "char_count": 238,
    "text": "(c) The minimum wage of an unskilled Mazdoor shall be the higher of the wage\nnotified by Government of India, Ministry of Labour and that notified by the\nlocal administration both relevant to the place of work and the period of\nreckoning.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0195",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 195,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 88396,
    "char_end": 88744,
    "char_count": 348,
    "text": "(d) The escalation for labour also shall be paid at the same quarterly intervals\nwhen escalation due to increase in cost of materials is paid under this\nclause. If such revision of minimum wages takes place during any such\nquarterly intervals, the escalation compensation shall be payable at revised\nrates only for work done in subsequent quarters;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC053-0196",
    "doc_id": "DOC-053",
    "paragraph_index": 196,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 88746,
    "char_end": 89640,
    "char_count": 894,
    "text": "(e) Irrespective of variations in minimum wages of any category of labour, for\nthe purpose of this clause, the variation in the rate for an unskilled Mazdoor\nalone shall form the basis for working out the escalation compensation\npayable on the labour component.\n(iv) In the event the price of materials and/or wages of labour required for execution\nof the work decreases, there shall be a downward adjustment of the cost of work\nso that such price of materials and/or wages of labour shall be deductible from the\ncost of work under this contract and in this regard the formula herein stated below\nunder this Clause 10CC shall mutatis mutandis apply.\n(v)\nThe contract price shall be adjusted for increase or decrease in rates and prices\nof labour, cement, steel reinforcement bar, fuel and lubricants and other input\nmaterials as per percentage of materials/labour specified in schedule F and in",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC054-0000",
    "doc_id": "DOC-054",
    "paragraph_index": 0,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 0,
    "char_end": 1791,
    "char_count": 1791,
    "text": "Agreement\nThis agreement is made on _th day of\nat New Delhi by and between:\nMis Telecommunications\nConsultants\nIndia Limited, a Company registered under\nthe Indian Companies Act 1956, with its registered and corporate office at TCll\nShawan, Greater Kailash-1, New Delhi - 110048, hereinafter referred to as \"TCll\",\nwhich expression shall include its successors and its permitted assigns, of one part.\nAND\nMis\n----'\nregistered under the Indian Companies Act 1956, with\nits registered office at\n, hereinafter referred to as \"CSP\n(Cloud\nservice\nprovider)\",\nwhich expression\nshall include its successors\nand\npermitted assigns, of the other part.\n\"TCll\" and \"CSP\" are individually referred to as \"Party\" and collectively as \"Parties\".\nThe Government of India has decided to implement \"Digital\nMSME\" Scheme for the\npromotion of Information and Communication Technology\nin MSME Sector. The\nScheme envisages promotion of Information and Communication Technology (ICT)\napplications to make MSMEs \"Digital\" by adopting new approach of cloud computing.\n(Notification wide letter no. 81(12)/NMCP/ICT/Misc.l2016-17\ndated 31.05.2017 and\nScheme Guidelines). Initially the Scheme will be implemented for the period of 3\nYears which may be extended, if required, with the approval of Competent Authority.\nInitially, following four applications will be made available to MSMEs through CSP:\na.\nERP\nb. Accounting\nc.\nManufacturing I Design\nd.\nRegulatory Compliances including GST.\nMore applications may be added need based in due course of time.\nWHEREAS TCll\nhas been nominated as\n\"Implementing Agency\" by Ministry of\nMSME,\nNirman\nShawan,\nNew\nDelhi and will\nbe responsible\nfor\nfacilitating\n,\nimplementation and monitoring of Cloud Computing Services by empanelling various\nCloud Service Providers (CSPs).\nWHEREAS",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC054-0001",
    "doc_id": "DOC-054",
    "paragraph_index": 1,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 1792,
    "char_end": 2565,
    "char_count": 773,
    "text": "CSP is in the business of providing Cloud services in the form of\nSoftware\nas\na\nService\n(SaaS)\nand\nhas\n.......................................................................................................\n(packa\nge name) to offer under the scheme.\nNow, therefore, TCll appoint/nominate\n.\nas one the Cloud Service Provider on the following terms & Conditions:\n1.\nCSP will work in close coordination with TCll\nand Ministry of MSME to fulfill the\nobjectives of the scheme.\n~\\~\n~\n3JG<'rolT I VINAY AOLAKHA\n\\31J ~\nI Deputy Director\n\"*f'1'Vn ~\n, Govl. of India\n~\n~lffi\"\n..,..\n~~(~.,..\nTf·-U)\nOfflc. of the Dovelopment Commi•• ion\", CMSME,\n~_.\n<'fq ~\n~\n~\"\"f'f\n-.r-st'.,p:j\nMln'a\"y .t Mlcr.p Sma\" & MediumEnterprise.\n~\n........\n~\n~~108/Ninne.B)law.n.\".wO.lhl.,08\nPage 1 0/5\nDRAFT",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC054-0002",
    "doc_id": "DOC-054",
    "paragraph_index": 2,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 2567,
    "char_end": 4308,
    "char_count": 1741,
    "text": "2.\nAwareness Programs and Workshops will organized by field units of MSME to\ncreate awareness amongst MSMEs. CSP shall essentially involve in Awareness\nprograms and workshops as and when required along with TCIL. Apart from\ntechnical deliberations, there will be live demonstration of ICT through Cloud\nComputing Services by CSP.\n3.\nFor another type of business promotions like Regular media campaign through\nelectronic, print media and radio, making of Documentary/Short films on benefits\nof adopting ICT technology and Preparation and printing of book of knowledge on\nICT, study material on cloud computing and success stories of MSME sector\nimplemented ICT etc will also be done and CSP shall provide the necessary\nsupport as and when require for successful business promotions.\n4.\nCSP shall not be paid any cost or TAIDA for promotional activities. CSP shall\nbring its own material (Brochures, Banners and posters etc.) for promotional\nactivities.\n5.\nTCll\nwill provide a portal which will display the list of CSP's along with their\nservice,\ncharges,\nservice\nlevel\nagreement,\ncomparative\ncost\nof\nsimilar\napplications, features and specifications of their services, workflow to avail the\nservices.\n6.\nCSP shall make available the services on portal as per requirements within the\nstipulated timeline so that the portal gets suitably hyperlinked with the portal of\nCSP.\n7.\nDigital MSME Web Portal will have the Payment gateway for MSMEs monthly\npayments to CSPs.\nor\nThe portal of CSP shall be further linked to payment gateways.\n8.\nCSP shall provide usage details like duration (time) and volume (data) or any\nother parameter so desired on monthly basis to TCll.\n9.\nCSP will provide offered cloud service to MSME as per the agreed terms and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC054-0003",
    "doc_id": "DOC-054",
    "paragraph_index": 3,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 4309,
    "char_end": 5114,
    "char_count": 805,
    "text": "conditions of the SLA (Annexure-II) with the MSEM. Broad Service Criteria of the\nSLA is attached at Annexure -III. Both Annexure-I and Annexure-II will form part\nof this agreement. CSP as per policy will issue monthly bill to MSME. MSME will\nmake full payment to CSP. MSMEs will make full payment to CSP.\n10.\nCSP will provide the billing and payment details to TCll to enable TCll to release\nsubsidy to MSME.\n11.\nTCll will transfer subsidy, wherever applicable, in the account of MSMEs through\nDBT route.\n12.\nIn case MSME decides to quite from the service or vise-versa, all the data will be\nprovided to MSME in electronic form.\n13.\nIn case CSP decides to discontinue its service, then they will give 6 months\nnotice in advance and will provide complete data to all the MSME in electronic\nform.\nPage 2 0/5",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC054-0004",
    "doc_id": "DOC-054",
    "paragraph_index": 4,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 5116,
    "char_end": 6859,
    "char_count": 1743,
    "text": "14.\nIn case any dispute with MSME with respect to service provided by CSP, TCll\nshall not be liable in any circumstance any. Any dispute or claim in respect of the\nservices utilized by MSME shall be between MSME and CSP and TCll\nshall not\nbe liable for any claim of any nature what so ever. In case any dispute between\nCSP and MSME is not resolved amicably, TCll\nmay intervene and decision of\nTCll\nin this regard may be binding to both the parties.\n15.\nCSP will not share or disclose the data of any MSME to any other CSP or MSME\nwithout written consent of the party\n16.\nThe term of this Agreement shall be for 36 months (\"Term\") from the date of\nsigning of this Agreement (\"Effective Date\"). All obligations hereunder shall only\napply\nduring\nthe\nTerm\nof\nthis\nAgreement\nand\nto\nsuch\nobligations\nand\ncommitments in relation to the Scheme, as may have been undertaken by the\nParties during the Term with validity exceeding the Term. The Term of this\nAgreement\ncan\nbe\nextended\nby\nmutual\nagreement\nbetween\nthe\nParties,\ndepending upon the requirement.\n17.\nNothing in this Agreement shall constitute, create or give effect or recognize a JV,\npartnership or business entity of any kind\n18.\nThis Agreement shall be construed and governed by the laws of India and the\nparties hereby submit to the exclusive jurisdiction of the Delhi Courts of law.\n19.\nAny matter, which is not stipulated in the Agreement, shall be settled in good faith\nby discussion among the parties in the spirit of understanding and cooperation.\n20.\nAll disputes or differences whatsoever arising among the parties under and/or in\nconnection with and/or in respect of this Agreement shall be referred to and\ndecided by a sole arbitrator, who shall be appointed by the CMD, TCll.\nThe",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC054-0005",
    "doc_id": "DOC-054",
    "paragraph_index": 5,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 6860,
    "char_end": 8317,
    "char_count": 1457,
    "text": "arbitration shall be conducted in accordance with Arbitration and Conciliation Act\nof 1996 and the venue of the arbitration shall be in New Delhi.\n21.\nDuring its Term, this Agreement will be terminated in the event of\na.\nCSP withdrawing the offer provided it does not create any financial\nobligation on TCIL. In case of financial obligation, the same shall be\nrecovered from CSP.\nb.\nDuring regular performance checks, if complaints resolution is very\npoor.\nc.\nBankruptcy proceedings being initiated against either of the Parties\nd.\nMutual agreement between the \"Parties\"\nIn any case, the CSP will provide complete data to all MSMEs in electronic form.\n22.\nNotices and other communications under this Agreement shall be in writing and\ncommunicated through post, courier, fax, email or any other recognized mode of\nsuch communication. All such notices and communications shall be directed to\nthe address as mentioned in the Agreement.\n23.\nCSP shall deposit Rs. 1 lakh towards non refundable registration fees for two\nyears to TCIL.\n24.\nBy signing this Agreement, the \"Parties\" acknowledge that it correctly records the\nunderstanding they have reached with regard to the Project.\n~\"\n~\n~I\nVINAY ADLAKHA\n~\n~\nI Deputy Director\n~\n~\n~\nI\nGov •. o' Ind ••\n3IT!l~\n\"itiT\n... , .. f......(~\nCOl. \"f. \",.)\nOft'c.\naf 1~. Dev.l~pm.ntComml•• 'on.r\n(MSME,\n'fl.-. \"'\"l ~ ~\n~\n~~\n~ni.1'Y\nof Micro. Smelt & M.d'um Enterprlaos\n.....\".\n~\n~-108/\"1f\"\"It'haw\"'.JI\"D.lhl\n108\nPage 3 0/5",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC054-0006",
    "doc_id": "DOC-054",
    "paragraph_index": 6,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 8319,
    "char_end": 8762,
    "char_count": 443,
    "text": "IN WITNESS WHEREOF,\neach party hereto has caused this Agreement to be\nexecuted in duplicate to be effective as of the Effective Date, by its duly authorized\nrepresentative.\n(For Telecommunications\n(For\n_\nIndia Ltd.)\nPrivate Limited)\nConsultants\nSignature:\nSignature:\nName:\nName:\nDesignation:\nDesignation:\nDate:\nDate:\nWitness:\nWitness:\nEncl:\n1. Guidelines- Digital MSME Scheme Annexure -I\n2.\nSLA Annexure-II\n3.\nBroad SLA Annexure-III\nPage 4 0/5",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC054-0007",
    "doc_id": "DOC-054",
    "paragraph_index": 7,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 8764,
    "char_end": 9656,
    "char_count": 892,
    "text": "Annx\nCloud\nService\nProvider\nName -\nS.No\nBroad\nService\nCriteria\nof Service\nLevel\nAgreement\n(SLA)\n1\nAvailability\n(e.g. 99.99% during work days, 99.9% for\nnights/weekends)\n2\nPerformance\n(e.g. maximum response times)\n3\nSecurity / privacy of the data\n(e.g. encrypting all stored and transmitted\ndata)\n4\nDisaster Recovery expectations\n(e.g. worse case recovery commitment)\n5\nLocation of the data\n(e.g. consistent with local legislation)\n6\nAccess to the data\n(e.g. data retrievable from provider in\nreadable format)\n7\nPortability of the data\n(e.g. ability to move data to a different\nprovider)\n8\nProcess to identify problems and\nresolution expectations\n(e.g. call centre)\n9\nChange Management process\n(e.g. changes - updates or new services)\n10\nDispute mediation process\n(e.g. escalation process, consequences)\n11\nExit Strategy with expectations on the\nprovider to ensure smooth transition\nPage 5 of5",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
