    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 10968,
    "char_end": 11052,
    "char_count": 84,
    "text": "FURNITURE INVENTORY (If the furniture is provided by Lessor)\n\nItem\n\nNos.\n\nItem\n\nNos.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0000",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 0,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 0,
    "char_end": 123,
    "char_count": 123,
    "text": "Section IV: General Conditions of Contract (GCC)\n\nPart I: General Conditions of Contract applicable to all types of Tenders",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0001",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 1,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 125,
    "char_end": 230,
    "char_count": 105,
    "text": "1.\nInterpretation; Definitions and Abbreviations: In the contract, unless the\ncontext otherwise requires:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0002",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 2,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 232,
    "char_end": 364,
    "char_count": 132,
    "text": "1.1 Interpretation and Definitions:\n\n1)\nThe heading of these conditions shall not affect the interpretation or\nconstruction thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0003",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 3,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 366,
    "char_end": 567,
    "char_count": 201,
    "text": "2)\n\"Writing\" or \"Written\" includes matter either in whole or in part, in\nmanuscript, typewritten, lithographed, cyclostyled, photographed or\nprinted under or over signature or seal, as the case may be.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0004",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 4,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 569,
    "char_end": 837,
    "char_count": 268,
    "text": "3)\nWords in the singular include the plural and vice-versa.\n\n4)\nWords importing the masculine gender shall be taken to include the\nfeminine gender and words importing persons shall include any\ncompany or association or body of individuals, whether incorporated\nor not.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0005",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 5,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 839,
    "char_end": 1085,
    "char_count": 246,
    "text": "5)\nTerms and expression not herein defined shall have the meanings\nassigned to them in the Indian Sale of Goods Act, 1930 (as amended)\nor the Indian Contract Act, 1872 (as amended) or the General Clauses\nAct, 1897 (as amended) as the case may be.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0006",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 6,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 1087,
    "char_end": 1270,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "6)\nAny reference to ‘Goods’ shall be deemed to include the incidental\nWorks/Services also while any reference to ‘Services’ shall be\ndeemed to include the incidental Works/Goods also.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0007",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 7,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 1272,
    "char_end": 1424,
    "char_count": 152,
    "text": "7)\nAny generic reference to GCC shall also imply a reference to SCC as\nwell.\n\n8)\nIn case of conflict, provisions of SCC shall prevail over those in GCC.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0008",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 8,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 1426,
    "char_end": 1557,
    "char_count": 131,
    "text": "9)\nAny reference to ‘Contract’ shall be deemed to include all other\ndocuments (inter-alia GCC, SCC) as described in GCC-clause 2.5.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0009",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 9,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 1559,
    "char_end": 1717,
    "char_count": 158,
    "text": "10) Any reference to any legal Act, Government Policies or orders shall\nbe deemed to include all amendments to such instruments, from time\nto time, till date.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0010",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 10,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 1719,
    "char_end": 2335,
    "char_count": 616,
    "text": "11) “Allied Firms” are all business entities that are within the ‘controlling\nownership interest’ (ownership of or entitlement to more than twenty-\nfive percent of the company's shares or capital or profits) or ‘control’(\nincluding the right to appoint a majority of the directors or to control\nthe management or policy decisions including by virtue of their\nshareholding or management rights or shareholder agreements or\nvoting agreements) of the principal firm acting alone or together or\nthrough one or more juridical persons. All successor firms or assigns\nof the principal firm shall be considered allied firms.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0011",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 11,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 2337,
    "char_end": 2486,
    "char_count": 149,
    "text": "12) \"Bid\" (including the term ‘tender’, ‘offer’, ‘quotation’ or ‘proposal’ in\nspecific  contexts)  means  an  offer  to  supply  goods,  services  or",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0012",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 12,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 2488,
    "char_end": 2587,
    "char_count": 99,
    "text": "execution of works made as per the terms and conditions set out in a\ndocument inviting such offers.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0013",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 13,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 2589,
    "char_end": 3052,
    "char_count": 463,
    "text": "13) \"Bidder\" (including the term 'Bidder', 'consultant' or 'service provider'\nin specific contexts) means any person or firm or company, including\nany member of a consortium or joint venture (that is an association of\nseveral persons, or firms or companies), every artificial juridical\nperson not falling in any of the descriptions of bidders stated\nhereinbefore, including any agency branch or office controlled by such\nperson, participating in a Tender Process.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0014",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 14,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 3054,
    "char_end": 3537,
    "char_count": 483,
    "text": "14) “Bill of Quantities” (including the term Price Schedule or BOQ) means\nthe priced and completed Bill of Quantities forming part of the bid.\n15) \"Consignee\" means the person to whom the goods are required to be\ndelivered as specified in the Contract. If the goods are required to be\ndelivered to a person as an interim consignee for the purpose of\ndispatch to another person as provided in the Contract then that\n\"another\" person is the consignee, also known as ultimate consignee.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0015",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 15,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 3539,
    "char_end": 4769,
    "char_count": 1230,
    "text": "16) “Contract” (including the terms ‘Purchase Order’ or ‘Supply Order’ or\n‘Withdrawal  Order’  or  ‘Work  Order’  or  ‘Consultancy  Contract’  or\n‘Contract for Services’, ‘Rate Contract’ or ‘Framework Contract’ or\n‘Letter of Intent – LoI’ (letter or memorandum communicating to the\ncontractor the acceptance of his bid) or ‘Agreement’ or a ‘Repeat\nOrder’ accepted/acted upon by the contractor or a ‘formal Agreement’,\nunder specific contexts), means a formal legal agreement in writing\nrelating to the subject matter of procurement, entered into between\nthe Procuring Entity and the contractor on mutually acceptable terms\nand conditions and which are in compliance with all the relevant\nprovisions of the laws of the country;\n17) “Contractor” (including the terms ‘Supplier’ or ‘Service Provider’ or\n‘Consultant’ or ‘Firm’ or ‘Vendor’ or ‘Manufacturer’ or ‘Successful\nBidder’ under specific contexts) means the person, firm, company, or\na Joint Venture with whom the contract is entered into and shall be\ndeemed to include the contractor's successors (approved by the\nProcuring Entity), agents, subcontractor, representatives, heirs,\nexecutors, and administrators as the case may be unless excluded by\nthe terms of the contract.;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0016",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 16,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 4771,
    "char_end": 4900,
    "char_count": 129,
    "text": "18) “Day”, “Month”, “Year” shall mean calendar day/ month or year (unless\nreference to financial year is clear from the context).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0017",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 17,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 4902,
    "char_end": 5136,
    "char_count": 234,
    "text": "19) \"Drawing\" means the drawing or drawings specified in or annexed to\nthe Specifications or the Tender Document/Contract;\n20) \"Earnest Money Deposit\" (EMD) means monetary guarantee to be\nfurnished by a Tenderer along with its tender.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0018",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 18,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 5138,
    "char_end": 5417,
    "char_count": 279,
    "text": "21) \"Goods\" (including the terms ‘Stores’, ‘Material(s)’ in specific contexts)\nincludes all articles, material, commodity, livestock, medicines,\nfurniture,\nfixtures,\nraw\nmaterial,\nconsumables,\nspare\nparts,\ninstruments, machinery, equipment, industrial plant, vehicles, aircrafts,",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0019",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 19,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 5419,
    "char_end": 6077,
    "char_count": 658,
    "text": "ships, railway rolling stock assemblies, subassemblies, accessories,\na group of machines comprising an integrated production process or\nsuch other categories of goods or intangible products like technology\ntransfer, licenses, patents or other intellectual properties (but excludes\nbooks, publications, periodicals, etc., for a library) under specific\ncontext), procured or otherwise acquired by a Procuring Entity. Any\nreference to Goods shall be deemed to include certain small work or\nsome services, which are incidental or consequential to the supply of\nsuch\ngoods,\nsuch\nas\ntransportation,\ninsurance,\ninstallation,\ncommissioning, training and maintenance.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0020",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 20,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 6079,
    "char_end": 6249,
    "char_count": 170,
    "text": "22) \"Government\" means the Central Government or a State Government\nas the case may be and includes agencies and Public Sector\nEnterprises under it, in specific contexts;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0021",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 21,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 6251,
    "char_end": 6484,
    "char_count": 233,
    "text": "23) \"Inspection\" means activities such as measuring, examining, testing,\nanalysing, gauging one or more characteristics of the goods or\nservices or works, and comparing the same with the specified\nrequirement to determine conformity.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0022",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 22,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 6486,
    "char_end": 6671,
    "char_count": 185,
    "text": "24) \"Inspecting Officer\" means the person, or organisation specified in the\ncontract for the purpose of inspection under the contract and includes\nhis / their authorised representative;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0023",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 23,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 6673,
    "char_end": 6960,
    "char_count": 287,
    "text": "25) “Intellectual Property Rights” (IPR) means the rights of the intellectual\nproperty owner concerning a tangible or intangible possession/\nexploitation of such property by others. It includes rights to Patents,\nCopyrights, Trademarks, Industrial Designs, Geographical indications\n(GI).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0024",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 24,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 6962,
    "char_end": 7113,
    "char_count": 151,
    "text": "26) “Joint Venture” means a Joint Venture or a Consortium (that is an\nassociation of several persons, or firms or companies - also referred\nto as JV/C)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0025",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 25,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 7115,
    "char_end": 7227,
    "char_count": 112,
    "text": "27) \"Purchaser\" means BRBNMPL - the organization purchasing goods\nand services as incorporated in the documents;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0026",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 26,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 7229,
    "char_end": 7406,
    "char_count": 177,
    "text": "28) \"Purchase Officer\" means the officer signing the acceptance of tender\nand includes any officer who has authority to execute the relevant\ncontract on behalf of the Purchaser;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0027",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 27,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 7408,
    "char_end": 7510,
    "char_count": 102,
    "text": "29) “Parties”: The parties to the contract are the \"Contractor\" and the\n\"Purchaser\", as defined above;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0028",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 28,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 7512,
    "char_end": 7819,
    "char_count": 307,
    "text": "30) \"Performance  Security\"  (includes  the  terms  ‘Security  Deposit’  or\n‘Performance Bond’ or ‘Performance Bank Guarantee’ or other\nspecified financial instruments in specific contexts) means monetary\nguarantee to be furnished by the successful Tenderer for due\nperformance of the contract placed on it.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0029",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 29,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 7821,
    "char_end": 8048,
    "char_count": 227,
    "text": "31) “Place of Delivery”: The delivery of the stores shall be deemed to take\nplace on delivery of the stores in accordance with the terms of the\ncontract, after approval by the Inspecting Officer, if so provided in the\ncontract:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0030",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 30,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 8050,
    "char_end": 8159,
    "char_count": 109,
    "text": "a)     The consignee at his premises; or\n\nb)     Where so provided, the interim consignee at his premises; or",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0031",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 31,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 8161,
    "char_end": 8264,
    "char_count": 103,
    "text": "c)\nA carrier or other person named in the contract for the purpose\nof transmission to the consignee; or",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0032",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 32,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 8266,
    "char_end": 8388,
    "char_count": 122,
    "text": "d)\nThe consignee at the destination station in case of contract\nstipulating for delivery of stores at destination station.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0033",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 33,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 8390,
    "char_end": 9100,
    "char_count": 710,
    "text": "32) “Procurement” or “public procurement” (or ‘Purchase’, or ‘Government\nProcurement/Purchase’\nincluding\nan\naward\nof\nPublic-Private\nPartnership projects, in specific contexts) means the acquisition of\nGoods/Services/works by way of purchase, lease, license or\notherwise, either using public funds or any other source of funds (e.g.\ngrant, loans, gifts, private investment etc.) of goods, works or services\nor any combination thereof, by a Procuring Entity, whether directly or\nthrough an agency with which a contract for procurement services is\nentered into, but does not include any acquisition without\nconsideration. The term “procure” / “procured” or “purchase” /\n“purchased” shall be construed accordingly;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0034",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 34,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 9102,
    "char_end": 9234,
    "char_count": 132,
    "text": "33) “Scheduled Commercial Bank” means a bank, defined as a scheduled\nbank under section 2(e) of the Reserve Bank of India Act, 1934.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0035",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 35,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 9236,
    "char_end": 9782,
    "char_count": 546,
    "text": "34) “Services”  is  defined  by  exception  as  any  subject  matter  of\nprocurement other than goods or works, except those incidental or\nconsequential to the service, and includes physical, maintenance,\nprofessional, intellectual, training, consultancy and advisory services\nor any other service classified or declared as such by a Procuring\nEntity but does not include appointment of an individual made under\nany law, rules, regulations or order issued in this behalf. It includes\n‘Consultancy Services’ and ‘Other (Non-consultancy) Services’.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0036",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 36,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 9784,
    "char_end": 10078,
    "char_count": 294,
    "text": "35) \"Specification\"  or  \"Technical  Specification\"  means  the  drawing/\ndocument/standard or any other details governing the construction,\nmanufacture or supply of goods or performance of services that\nprescribes the requirement to which goods or services have to\nconform as per the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0037",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 37,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 10080,
    "char_end": 10297,
    "char_count": 217,
    "text": "36) “Signed” means ink signed or digitally signed with a valid Digital\nSignature as per IT Act 2000 (as amended from time to time). It also\nincludes stamped, except in the case of Letter of Award or\namendment thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0038",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 38,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 10299,
    "char_end": 10818,
    "char_count": 519,
    "text": "37) “Tender”; “Tender Document”; “Tender Enquiry” or “Tender Process”:\n‘Tender Process’ is the whole process from the publishing of the\nTender Document till the resultant award of the contract. ‘Tender\nDocument’ means the document (including all its sections,\nappendices, forms, formats, etc.) published by the Procuring Entity to\ninvite bids in a Tender Process. The Tender Document and Tender\nProcess may be generically referred to as “Tender\" or \"Tender\nEnquiry\", which would be clear from context without ambiguity.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0039",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 39,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 10820,
    "char_end": 11148,
    "char_count": 328,
    "text": "38) “Test” means such test as is prescribed by the particulars governing\nthe construction, manufacture or supply of Goods as may be\nprescribed by the contract or considered necessary by the Inspecting\nOfficer whether performed or made by the Inspecting Officer or any\nagency acting under the direction of the Inspecting Officer;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0040",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 40,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 11150,
    "char_end": 12019,
    "char_count": 869,
    "text": "39) “Works” refer to any activity, sufficient in itself to fulfil an economic or\ntechnical function, involving construction, fabrication, repair, overhaul,\nrenovation, decoration, installation, erection, excavation, dredging,\nand so on, which make use of a combination of one or more of\nengineering design, architectural design, material and technology,\nlabour, machinery and equipment. Supply of some materials or certain\nservices may be incidental or consequential to and part of such works.\nThe term “Works” includes (i) civil works for the purposes of roads,\nrailway, bridges, buildings, irrigation systems, water supply, sewerage\nfacilities, dams, tunnels and earthworks; and so on, and (ii)\nmechanical and electrical works involving fabrication, installation,\nerection, repair and maintenance of a mechanical or electrical nature\nrelating to machinery and plants.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0041",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 41,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 12021,
    "char_end": 12979,
    "char_count": 958,
    "text": "1.2 Abbreviations:\n\n\"AAEC\"\nmeans \"Appreciable Adverse Effect on Competition\" as\nper Competition Act\n\"BG\"\nmeans Bank Guarantee\n\"BL or B/L\"\nmeans Bill of Lading\n“BOQ”\nmeans Bill of Quantities\n“BSD”\nmeans Bid Securing Declaration\n“BNPMIPL”\nmeans Bank Note Paper Mill India Private Limited\n“BRBNMPL”\nmeans  Bhartiya  Reserve  Bank  Note  Mudran  Private\nLimited\n\"CD”\nmeans Custom Duty\n“CFR”\nmeans Cost and Freight (port of destination)\n\"CIF\"\nmeans Cost, Insurance and Freight (port of destination)\n\"CMD\"\nmeans Chairman and Managing Director\n\"CPSU\"\nmeans Central Public Sector Undertaking\n“DAP”\nmeans Delivered at Place (Destination)\n\"DDO\"\nmeans Direct Demanding Officer in Rate Contracts\n“DEA”\nmeans Department of Economic Affairs\n“DoCC”\nmeans Currency and Coins Division in Department of\nEconomic Affairs\n\"DGS&D\"\nmeans Directorate General of Supplies and Disposals\n\"DP”\nmeans Delivery Period\n“DPIIT”\nmeans Department for Promotion of Industry and\nInternal Trade",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0042",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 42,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 6,
    "char_start": 12981,
    "char_end": 14710,
    "char_count": 1729,
    "text": "“DSC”\nmeans Digital Signature Certificate\n\"ECS\"\nmeans Electronic clearing system\n“EFT/NEFT”\nmeans (National) Electronic Funds Transfer\n“EMD”\nmeans Earnest money deposit\n\"EOI\"\nmeans Expression of Interest (Tendering System)\n“e-RA”\nmeans Electronic Reverse Auction\n\"ERV\"\nmeans Exchange rate variations\n\"FAS\"\nmeans Free Alongside Ship (port of loading)\n\"FOB\"\nmeans Freight on Board (port of loading)\n\"FOR\"\nmeans Free on Rail (named Station)\n\"GCC\"\nmeans General Conditions of Contract\n“GeM”\nmeans Government e-Marketplace\n“GIT”\nmeans General Instructions to Tenderers\n“GoI”\nmeans Government of India\n“GST”\nmeans Goods and Services Tax\n\"H1, H2 etc.\"\nmeans First Highest, Second Highest Offers etc. in\nDisposal Tenders\n“HSN”\nmeans Harmonized System of Nomenclature\n“IEM”\nmeans Independent External Monitor\nIncoterms\nmeans International Commercial Terms, 2000 (of ICC)\n“INR”\nmeans Indian Rupee\n“IPR”\nmeans Intellectual Property Rights\n“ITC (HS)”\nmeans Indian Tariff Classification (Harmonised System)\n\"L1, L2 etc.\"\nmeans First or second Lowest Offer etc.\n\"LC\"\nmeans Letter of Credit\n\"LD or L/D\"\nmeans Liquidated Damages\n“LoI”\nmeans Letter of Intent [analogous to LoA – Letter of\nAward (Acceptance) or Notification of Award of Contract]\n\"LSI\"\nmeans Large Scale Industry\n“MII”\nmeans Make in India\n“MoF”\nmeans Ministry of Finance\n“MSE”\nmeans Micro and Small Scale Enterprise\n“MSME”\nmeans Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises\n“MSMED”\nmeans MSME Development (Act)\n\"NIT\"\nmeans Notice Inviting Tenders\n\"NSIC\"\nmeans National small industries corporation\n“OEM”\nmeans Original Equipment Manufacturer\n“PAN”\nmeans Permanent Account Number\n\"PQB\"\nmeans Pre-qualification bidding\n\"PSU\"\nmeans Public Sector Undertaking\n\"PVC\"\nmeans Price variation clause",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0043",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 43,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 14712,
    "char_end": 15195,
    "char_count": 483,
    "text": "“RBI”\nmeans Reserve Bank of India\n\"RC\"\nmeans Rate contract\n“RCM”\nmeans Reverse Charge Mechanism\n“RFI”\nmeans Request for Information\n“RFP”\nmeans Request for Proposal\n“RFQ”\nmeans Request for Qualification\n\"RR or R/R\"\nmeans Railway Receipt\n\"SBD\" or \"TD\"\nmeans Standard Bid Document / Tender Document\n\"SCC\"\nmeans Special Conditions of Contract\n\"SIT\"\nmeans Special Instructions to Tenderers\n\"SPMCIL\"\nmeans Security Printing and Minting Corporation Limited\n\"SSI\"\nmeans Small Scale Industry",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0044",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 44,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 15197,
    "char_end": 16532,
    "char_count": 1335,
    "text": "2.\nA.\n2.1\nApplication\nThe General Conditions of Contract incorporated in this section shall be\napplicable for this purchase to the extent the same are not superseded by\nthe Special Conditions of Contract (SCC) prescribed under Section V of this\ndocument.\n2.2 General Conditions of the contract shall not be changed from one tender to\nother.\nB.\nThe Contract\n2.3 Language of Contract\nUnless otherwise stipulated in SCC, the contract shall be written in the\nOfficial Language or English. All correspondence and other contract\ndocuments, which the parties exchange, shall also be written/translated\naccordingly in that language. For purposes of interpretation of the contract,\nthe English documents/translation shall prevail.\n2.4 Severability\nIf any provision or condition of this Contract is prohibited or rendered invalid\nor unenforceable, such prohibition, invalidity or unenforceability shall not\naffect the validity or enforceability of any other provisions and conditions of\nthis Contract.\n2.5 Contract Documents and their Precedence\nThe following conditions and documents in indicated order of precedence\n(higher to lower) shall be considered an integral part of the contract,\nirrespective of whether these are not appended/referred to in it. Any generic\nreference to ‘Contract’ shall imply reference to all these documents as well:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0045",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 45,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 16534,
    "char_end": 17071,
    "char_count": 537,
    "text": "(i)\nValid and authorized Amendments issued to the contract.\n(ii)    the Agreement consisting of the initial paragraphs, recitals and other\nclauses set forth immediately before the GCC and including the\nformats annexed to it and signatures of Procuring Entity;\n(iii) the Letter of Intent (LoI)\n(iv)   Final written submissions made by the contractor during negotiations,\nif any;\n(v)\nthe SCC\n(vi) the GCC\n(vii)  the contractor’s bid;\n(viii) any other document listed in the SCC as forming part of this Contract.\n(ix) Integrity Pact, if any",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0046",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 46,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 17073,
    "char_end": 17263,
    "char_count": 190,
    "text": "C.\nGoverning Laws and Jurisdiction\n\n2.6 The Contract, its meaning and interpretation, and the relation between the\nParties shall be governed by the Laws of India for the time being in force.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0047",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 47,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 17265,
    "char_end": 17977,
    "char_count": 712,
    "text": "2.7   Irrespective of the place of delivery, or the place of performance or the place\nof payments under the contract, the contract shall be deemed to have been\nmade at the place from which the Letter of Intent (LoI, or the contract\nAgreement, in the absence of LoI) has been issued. The courts at Kolkata\nor Bengaluru shall alone have jurisdiction to decide any dispute arising out\nor in respect of the contract.\n2.8 Besides GCC and SCC, the following Laws shall be applicable:\n(i)\nIndian Contracts Act, 1872\n(ii)\nSale of Goods Act, 1930\n(iii) Arbitration and Conciliation\nAct, 1996 and Arbitration and\nReconciliation Amendment Act, 2015\n(iv) Competition Act, 2002 as amended by Competition (Amendment Act),\n2007",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0048",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 48,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 17979,
    "char_end": 18309,
    "char_count": 330,
    "text": "D.\nContractor’s Obligations and restrictions on its Rights\n\n2.9  Changes in Constitution / financial stakes / responsibilities of a\nContract’s Business: The Contractor must proactively keep the Procuring\nEntity informed of any changes in its constitution / financial stakes /\nresponsibilities during the execution of the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0049",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 49,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 18311,
    "char_end": 18769,
    "char_count": 458,
    "text": "2.10 Obligation to Maintain Eligibility and Qualifications: The contract has\nbeen awarded to the contractor based on specific eligibility and qualification\ncriteria. The Contractor is contractually bound to maintain such eligibility\nand qualifications during the execution of the contract. Any change which\nwould vitiate the basis on which the contract was awarded to the contractor\nshould be pro-actively brought to the notice of the Procuring Entity within",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0050",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 50,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 18771,
    "char_end": 18974,
    "char_count": 203,
    "text": "seven (07) days of it coming to the Contractor’s knowledge. These changes\ninclude but are not restricted to change regarding declarations made by it\nin its bid in Section XVIII: Eligibility Declarations.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0051",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 51,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 18976,
    "char_end": 19719,
    "char_count": 743,
    "text": "2.11 Consequences of a breach of Obligations: Should the Contractor or any\nof its Partners or its Subcontractors or the Personnel commit a default or\nbreach of its obligations, the Contractor shall remedy such breaches within\n21 days, keeping the Procuring Entity informed. However, at its discretion,\nthe Procuring Entity shall be entitled, and it shall be lawful on his part, to\ntreat it as a breach of contract and avail any or all remedies thereunder.\nThe decision of the Procuring Entity as to any matter or thing concerning or\narising out of GCC clause or on any question whether the contractor or any\npartner of the contractor firm has committed a default or breach of any of\nthe conditions shall be final and binding on the contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0052",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 52,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 19721,
    "char_end": 20379,
    "char_count": 658,
    "text": "E.\nPermits, Approvals and Licenses\n\n2.12 Whenever the supply of Goods and incidental Works/Services requires that\nthe contractor obtain permits, approvals, and licenses from local public\nauthorities, it shall be the contractor's sole responsibility to obtain these and\nkeep these current and valid. Such requirements may include but not be\nrestricted to export licence or environmental clearance, if required. If\nrequested by the contractor, the Procuring Entity shall make its best effort\nto assist the contractor in complying with such requirements in a timely and\nexpeditious manner, without any dilution of the Contractor’s responsibility\nin this regard.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0053",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 53,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 20381,
    "char_end": 20976,
    "char_count": 595,
    "text": "3.\nUse of contract documents and information\n\n3.1   The supplier shall not, without BRBNMPL's prior written consent, disclose\nthe contract or any provision thereof including any specification, drawing,\nsample or any information furnished by or on behalf of BRBNMPL in\nconnection therewith, to any person other than the person(s) employed by\nthe supplier in the performance of the contract emanating from this tender\ndocument. Further, any such disclosure to any such employed person shall\nbe made in confidence and only so far as necessary for the purposes of\nsuch performance for this contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0054",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 54,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 20978,
    "char_end": 21623,
    "char_count": 645,
    "text": "3.2   During the process of procurement of Security or Sensitive Machinery and\nItems, Tender Documents and the specifications / drawings of such items\nwould be issued only to Vendors having security clearance within the\nvalidity of such clearance and he shall maintain absolute secrecy and\nstrictly control the number of copies and access to the documents and\ncopies thereof, in addition to safeguards mentioned in sub-para above.\n3.3   Further, the supplier shall not, without BRBNMPL's prior written consent,\nmake use of any document or information mentioned in GCC sub-clause\n3.1 above except for the sole purpose of performing this contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0055",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 55,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 21625,
    "char_end": 21771,
    "char_count": 146,
    "text": "3.4   Except the contract issued to the supplier, each and every other document\nmentioned in GCC sub-clause 3.1 above shall remain the property of",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0056",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 56,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 21773,
    "char_end": 21951,
    "char_count": 178,
    "text": "BRBNMPL and, if advised by BRBNMPL, all copies of all such documents\nshall be returned to BRBNMPL on completion of the supplier’s performance\nand obligations under this contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0057",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 57,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 21953,
    "char_end": 22435,
    "char_count": 482,
    "text": "3.5   All deliverables, outputs, plans, drawings, specifications, designs, reports,\nand other documents and software submitted by the contractor under this\nContract shall become and remain the property of BRBNMPL and subject\nto laws of copyright and must not be shared with third parties or reproduced,\nwhether in whole or part, without BRBNMPL’s prior written consent. The\ncontractor may retain a copy of such documents and software but shall not\nuse it for any commercial purpose.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0058",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 58,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 22437,
    "char_end": 23152,
    "char_count": 715,
    "text": "4.\nIndemnities for breach of IPR Rights\n\n4.1  The contractor shall indemnify and hold harmless, free of costs, the\nProcuring Entity and its employees and officers from and against all suits,\nactions or administrative proceedings, claims, demands, losses, damages,\ncosts, and expenses of any nature, including attorney’s fees and expenses,\nwhich may arise in respect of the Goods or Services provided by the\ncontractor under this Contract, as a result of any infringement or alleged\ninfringement of any patent, utility model, registered design, copyright, or\nother Intellectual Proprietary Rights (IPR) or trademarks, registered or\notherwise existing on the date of the contract arising out of or in connection\nwith:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0059",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 59,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 23154,
    "char_end": 23460,
    "char_count": 306,
    "text": "(i)     Any design, data, drawing, specification, or other documents or Goods\nor Services provided or designed by the contractor for or on behalf of\nthe Procuring Entity.\n(ii)    The sale by the Procuring Entity in any country of the Services/\nproducts produced by the Goods supplied by the contractor, and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0060",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 60,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 23462,
    "char_end": 23610,
    "char_count": 148,
    "text": "(iii)   The installation of the Goods by the contractor/Delivery of the services\nor the use of the Goods or Services at the Procuring Entity’s Site.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0061",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 61,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 23612,
    "char_end": 23830,
    "char_count": 218,
    "text": "4.2   Such indemnity shall not cover any use of the Goods or Services or any\npart thereof or any products produced thereby:\n(i)     other than for the purpose indicated by or to be reasonably inferred\nfrom the contract",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0062",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 62,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 23832,
    "char_end": 23924,
    "char_count": 92,
    "text": "(ii)    neither any infringement resulting from the use of the Services or any\npart thereof,",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0063",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 63,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 23926,
    "char_end": 24491,
    "char_count": 565,
    "text": "(iii)  or any service/products produced thereby in association or\ncombination with any other service, equipment, plant, or materials not\nsupplied by the contractor.\n4.3   If any proceedings are brought, or any claim is made against the Procuring\nEntity arising out of the matters referred above, the Procuring Entity shall\npromptly give the contractor a notice thereof. At its own expense and in the\nProcuring Entity’s name, the contractor may conduct such proceedings and\nnegotiations to settle any such proceedings or claim, keeping the Procuring\nEntity informed.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0064",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 64,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 24493,
    "char_end": 24783,
    "char_count": 290,
    "text": "4.4   If the contractor fails to notify the Procuring Entity within twenty-eight (28)\ndays after receiving such notice that it intends to conduct any such\nproceedings or claim, then the Procuring Entity shall be free to conduct the\nsame on its behalf at the risk and cost to the contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0065",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 65,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 24785,
    "char_end": 25028,
    "char_count": 243,
    "text": "4.5   At the contractor’s request, the Procuring Entity shall afford all available\nassistance to the contractor in conducting such proceedings or claim and\nshall be reimbursed by the contractor for all reasonable expenses incurred\nin so doing.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0066",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 66,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 25030,
    "char_end": 25598,
    "char_count": 568,
    "text": "5.\nEligible Goods/Services - Country of Origin and Minimum Local Content\n\n5.1 Unless otherwise stipulated in SCC or Contract, the country of origin of\n‘Goods’ and ‘incidental Works/ Service’ to be supplied under the contract\nshall have their origin in India or other countries and must conform to the\ndeclaration made by the contractor in its bid regarding but not limited to i)\nrestrictions on certain countries with land-borders with India; ii) minimum\nlocal content and location of value addition (Make in India Policy); iii)\nContractor’s status as MSE or Start-up.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0067",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 67,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 25600,
    "char_end": 25818,
    "char_count": 218,
    "text": "5.2   The term “origin” used in this clause means where the goods (including\nsubcontracted components) are mined, grown, produced, or manufactured\nor from where the incidental Works/ Services are arranged and supplied.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0068",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 68,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 25820,
    "char_end": 26380,
    "char_count": 560,
    "text": "6.\nPerformance Security\n\n6.1  Within twenty-one (21) days (or any other period mentioned in Tender\nDocument or Contract) after the issue of notification of award (LoI or the\ncontract, if LoI is skipped) by BRBNMPL, the supplier shall furnish to\nBRBNMPL performance security for an amount of three to ten percent (3-\n10%) of the total value of the contract, valid up to sixty (60) days (or any\nother period mentioned in Tender Document or Contract) after the date of\ncompletion of all contractual obligations by the supplier, including the\nwarranty obligations.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0069",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 69,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 26382,
    "char_end": 26735,
    "char_count": 353,
    "text": "6.2  For multi-year Service contracts which may be of 5-7 years or more,\nprocuring entities may consider to proportionately keep reducing\nperformance security in proportion to the balance service period, wherever\nfeasible. Wherever it is decided to take lower or proportionately reducing\nperformance security, tender conditions may be suitably modified.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0070",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 70,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 26737,
    "char_end": 26884,
    "char_count": 147,
    "text": "6.3   The Performance security shall be denominated in Indian Rupees or in the\ncurrency of the contract and shall be in one of the following forms:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0071",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 71,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 26886,
    "char_end": 27295,
    "char_count": 409,
    "text": "a.     Insurance Surety Bond\nb.\nAccount Payee Demand Draft drawn on any scheduled commercial\nbank in India, in favour of Bharatiya Reserve Bank Note Mudran\nPrivate Limited as indicated in the relevant clause of NIT in reference\nto EMD.\nc.\nBank Guarantee (including e-Bank Guarantee) issued/confirmed by\nany scheduled commercial bank in India, in the prescribed form as\nprovided in section XV of this document.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0072",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 72,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 27297,
    "char_end": 27508,
    "char_count": 211,
    "text": "6.4   In the event of any loss due to supplier's failure to fulfil its obligations in\nterms of the contract, the amount of the performance security shall be\npayable to BRBNMPL to compensate BRBNMPL for the same.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0073",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 73,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 27510,
    "char_end": 27798,
    "char_count": 288,
    "text": "6.5   In the event of any amendment issued to the contract, the supplier shall,\nwithin twenty-one days of issue of the amendment, furnish the\ncorresponding amendment to the Performance Security (as necessary),\nrendering the same valid in all respects in terms of the contract, as\namended.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0074",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 74,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 27800,
    "char_end": 27976,
    "char_count": 176,
    "text": "6.6   If the contractor during the currency of the Contract fails to maintain the\nrequisite Performance Security, it shall be lawful for the Procuring Entity at\nits discretion:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0075",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 75,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 27978,
    "char_end": 28112,
    "char_count": 134,
    "text": "(i)\nto  terminate  the  Contract  for  Default  besides  availing  any  or  all\ncontractual remedies provided for breaches/default, or",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0076",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 76,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 28114,
    "char_end": 28359,
    "char_count": 245,
    "text": "(ii)    without terminating the Contract:\n\na)\nrecover from the contractor the amount of such security deposit\nby deducting the amount from the pending bills of the contractor\nunder the contract or any other contract with the Procuring Entity,\nor",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0077",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 77,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 28361,
    "char_end": 28489,
    "char_count": 128,
    "text": "b)\ntreat it as a breach of contract and avail any or all availing any\nor all contractual remedies provided for breaches/default.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0078",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 78,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 28491,
    "char_end": 28710,
    "char_count": 219,
    "text": "6.7 Subject to GCC sub-clause 6.3 above, BRBNMPL will release the\nperformance security without any interest to the supplier on completion of\nthe supplier's all contractual obligations including the warranty obligations.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0079",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 79,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 28712,
    "char_end": 29170,
    "char_count": 458,
    "text": "6.8 Non-receipt of Performance Security and Contract by BRBNMPL\n\nFailure of the successful tenderer in providing performance security within\n21 days of receipt of notification of award and / or returning contract copy\nduly signed within stipulated time shall make the tenderer liable for\nannulment of the award and forfeiture of its EMD (or enforcement of Bid\nSecurity Declaration), besides taking other administrative punitive actions\nby BRBNMPL against it.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0080",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 80,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 29172,
    "char_end": 29929,
    "char_count": 757,
    "text": "6.9 No Claim Certificate and Release of Contract Securities\n\nAfter mutual reconciliations of outstanding payments and assets on either\nside, the contractor shall submit a ‘No-claim certificate’ to the Procuring\nEntity requesting the release of its contractual securities, if any. The\nProcuring Entity shall release the contractual securities without any interest\nif no outstanding obligation, asset, or payments are due from the contractor.\nThe contractor shall not be entitled to make any claim whatsoever against\nthe Procuring Entity under or arising out of this Contract, nor shall the\nProcuring Entity entertain or consider any such claim, if made by the\ncontractor, after he shall have signed a \"No Claim\" Certificate in favour of\nthe Procuring Entity.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0081",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 81,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 29931,
    "char_end": 30281,
    "char_count": 350,
    "text": "7.\nTechnical Specifications and Standards\n\n7.1   Scope of Supply/Services: The Goods & Services to be provided by the\nsupplier under this contract shall conform to the technical specifications and\nquality  control  parameters  mentioned  in  'Technical  Specification'  and\n'Quality Control Requirements' under Sections VII and VIII of this document.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0082",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 82,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 30283,
    "char_end": 30690,
    "char_count": 407,
    "text": "7.2   Incidental  Works/Services:  If  so  stipulated,  the  contractor  shall  be\nrequired to perform specified incidental Works/Services (e.g., Installation,\nCommissioning, Operator’s Training etc. in case of Supply of Capital\nGoods/Machinery & Plant) as an integral part of the Goods in the contract\nor perform/deliver specified incidental Works/Goods as an integral part of\nthe Services in the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0083",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 83,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 30692,
    "char_end": 31290,
    "char_count": 598,
    "text": "8.\nPacking and Marking\n\n8.1   The packing for the goods to be provided by the supplier should be strong\nand durable enough to withstand, without limitation, the entire journey\nduring transit including transhipment (if any), rough handling, open storage\netc. without any damage, deterioration etc. As and if necessary, the size,\nweights and volumes of the packing cases shall also take into consideration,\nthe remoteness of the final destination of the goods and availability or\notherwise of transport and handling facilities at all points during transit up\nto final destination as per the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0084",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 84,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 31292,
    "char_end": 31759,
    "char_count": 467,
    "text": "8.2   The  quality  of  packing,  the  manner  of  marking  within  &  outside  the\npackages and provision of accompanying documentation shall strictly\ncomply with the requirements as provided in Technical Specifications and\nQuality Control Requirements under Sections VII and VIII and in SCC under\nSection V. in case the packing requirements are amended due to issue of\nany amendment to the contract, the same shall also be taken care of by the\nsupplier accordingly.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0085",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 85,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 31761,
    "char_end": 32160,
    "char_count": 399,
    "text": "8.3 Packing instructions:\n\nUnless otherwise mentioned in the Technical Specification and Quality\nControl Requirements under Sections VII and VIII and in SCC under\nSection V, the supplier shall make separate packages for each consignee\n(in case there is more than one consignee mentioned in the contract) and\nmark each package on three sides with the following with indelible paint of\nproper quality:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0086",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 86,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 32162,
    "char_end": 32412,
    "char_count": 250,
    "text": "a)     contract number and date\nb)\nbrief description of goods including quantity\nc)\nthe gross weight of the package\nd)\npacking list reference number\ne)\ncountry of origin of goods\nf)\nconsignee's name and full address and\ng)\nsupplier's name and address",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0087",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 87,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 32414,
    "char_end": 32447,
    "char_count": 33,
    "text": "9.\nInspection and Quality Control",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0088",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 88,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 32449,
    "char_end": 34176,
    "char_count": 1727,
    "text": "9.1   BRBNMPL and / or its nominated representative(s) will, without any extra\ncost to BRBNMPL, inspect and/or test the ordered goods and the related\nservices to confirm their conformity to the contract specifications and other\nquality control details incorporated in the contract. BRBNMPL shall inform\nthe supplier in advance, in writing, BRBNMPL's programme for such\ninspection and, also the identity of the officials to be deputed for this\npurpose.\n9.2 The  Technical  Specification  and  Quality  Control  Requirements\nincorporated in the contract shall specify what inspections and tests are to\nbe carried out and, also, where and how they are to be conducted. If such\ninspections and tests are conducted in the premises of the supplier or its\nsubcontractor(s), all reasonable facilities and assistance, including access\nto relevant drawings, design details and production data, shall be furnished\nby the supplier to BRBNMPL's inspector at no charge to BRBNMPL.\n9.3   If during such inspections and tests the contracted goods fail to conform to\nthe required specifications and standards, BRBNMPL's inspector may\nreject them and the supplier shall either replace the rejected goods or make\nall alterations necessary to meet the specifications and standards, as\nrequired, free of cost to BRBNMPL and resubmit the same to BRBNMPL's\ninspector for conducting the inspections and tests again.\n9.4   In case the contract stipulates pre-despatch inspection of the ordered\ngoods at suppliers’ premises, the supplier shall put up the goods for such\ninspection to BRBNMPL's inspector well ahead of the contractual delivery\nperiod, so that BRBNMPL's inspector is able to complete the inspection\nwithin the contractual delivery period.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0089",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 89,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 34177,
    "char_end": 35389,
    "char_count": 1212,
    "text": "9.5   If the supplier tenders the goods to BRBNMPL's inspector for inspection at\nthe last moment without providing reasonable time to the inspector for\ncompleting the inspection within the contractual delivery period, the\ninspector may carry out the inspection and complete the formality beyond\nthe contractual delivery period at the risk and expense of the supplier. The\nfact that the goods have been inspected after the contractual delivery period\nwill not have the effect of keeping the contract alive and this will be without\nany prejudice to the legal rights and remedies available to BRBNMPL under\nthe terms & conditions of the contract.\n9.6   BRBNMPL's contractual right to inspect, test and, if necessary, reject the\ngoods after the goods' arrival at the final destination shall have no bearing\nof the fact that the goods have previously been inspected and cleared by\nBRBNMPL's inspector during pre-despatch inspection mentioned above.\n9.7   Goods accepted by BRBNMPL and/or its inspector at initial inspection and\nin final inspection in terms of the contract shall in no way dilute BRBNMPL's\nright to reject the same later, if found deficient concerning ‘Technical\nSpecifications and Quality Assurance’.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0090",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 90,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 35391,
    "char_end": 35527,
    "char_count": 136,
    "text": "10. Terms of Delivery\n\n10.1 Goods shall be delivered by the supplier in accordance with the terms of\ndelivery specified in the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0091",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 91,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 35529,
    "char_end": 37259,
    "char_count": 1730,
    "text": "10.2 Time is the Essence of the contract: The time for and the date for\ndelivering the Goods stipulated in the contract or as extended shall be\ndeemed to be of the essence of the contract. Delivery must be completed\nnot later than the date(s) so specified or extended.\n10.3 Terms of delivery (e.g., F.O.R. destination/CIF/DAP etc.) shall determine\nthe point at which the responsibilities and property in goods passes over\nfrom the contractor to the Procuring Entity. These terms also determine the\ntime of delivery.\n10.4 Transfer of Title of Goods: Unless otherwise stated in the contract,\nnotwithstanding any inspection and approval by the Inspecting Officer on\nthe contractor's premises, or any payments made to the contractor, property\nin the Goods (and resultant rights and liabilities) shall not pass on to the\nProcuring Entity until the Goods have been received, inspected, and\naccepted by the consignee. The Contractor shall be responsible for all loss,\ndestruction, damage, or deterioration of or to the Goods from any cause\nwhatsoever while the Goods after approval by the Inspecting Officer are\nawaiting despatch or delivery or are in the course of transit from the\ncontractor to the consignee or, as the case may be, interim consignee. The\nContractor shall alone be entitled and responsible for making claims against\nany carrier in respect of non-delivery, short delivery, mis-delivery, loss,\ndestruction, damage, or deterioration of the Goods entrusted to such carrier\nby the contractor for transmission to the consignee or the interim consignee\nas the case may be.\n10.5 Quantity  Tolerance:  Unless  otherwise  stipulated  in  the  contract,  the\nobligation for completing supplies shall be considered complete if the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0092",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 92,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 37260,
    "char_end": 37460,
    "char_count": 200,
    "text": "Goods have been supplied to the tolerance of ± 5% of the quantity or of the\ntotal value of goods ordered in the contract. Only the supplied quantity shall\nbe paid for as per the terms of the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0093",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 93,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 37462,
    "char_end": 38401,
    "char_count": 939,
    "text": "11. Transportation of Goods\n\n11.1 Part Supplies: The supplier shall not arrange part-shipments and / or\ntranshipments without the express / prior written consent of BRBNMPL.\n11.2 Instructions for transportation of domestic goods including goods\nalready imported by the supplier under its own arrangement: In case\nno instruction is provided in this regard in the SCC, the supplier will arrange\ntransportation of the ordered goods as per its own procedure.\n11.3 Shipping Arrangement for Foreign Contracts: In the case of FOB/FAS\ncontracts, shipping arrangements shall be made by BRBNMPL. The\nContractor shall give adequate notice to the Forwarding Agents/Nominees\nabout the readiness of the cargo from time to time and at least six weeks'\nnotice in advance of the required position for finalising the shipping\narrangements. In the case of CFR contracts, the Contractor shall arrange\nshipment in accordance with the instructions from BRBNMPL.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0094",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 94,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 38403,
    "char_end": 38566,
    "char_count": 163,
    "text": "11.4 Airlifting: Should the Purchaser intend to airlift all or some of the stores the\nContractor shall pack the stores accordingly on receipt of intimation to that",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0095",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 95,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 38568,
    "char_end": 38686,
    "char_count": 118,
    "text": "effect from the Purchaser. Such deliveries will be agreed upon well in\nadvance and paid for as may be mutually agreed.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0096",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 96,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 38688,
    "char_end": 38930,
    "char_count": 242,
    "text": "12. Insurance:\n\nUnless otherwise instructed in the SCC, the supplier shall make arrangements\nfor insuring the goods against loss or damage incidental to manufacture or\nacquisition, transportation, storage and delivery in the following manner:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0097",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 97,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 38932,
    "char_end": 39714,
    "char_count": 782,
    "text": "(i)    In case of supply of domestic goods on CIF/FOR destination basis, the\nsupplier shall be responsible till the entire stores contracted for arrive in\ngood condition at destination. The transit risk in this respect shall be\ncovered by the Supplier by getting the stores duly insured. The insurance\ncover shall be obtained by the Supplier in its own name and not in the name\nof BRBNMPL or its Consignee.\n(ii)    In the case of FOB and CFR offers for import of Goods, insurance shall be\narranged by the Purchaser. However, the supplier must give sufficient\nnotice to the Purchaser prior to the date of shipment, so that the Insurance\nCover for the shipment can be activated. The Supplier must co-ordinate so\nas to ensure that the Shipment sails only with Insurance cover in place.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0098",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 98,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 39716,
    "char_end": 40246,
    "char_count": 530,
    "text": "(iii)   In case of Import of Goods, even in case where the insurance is paid by the\nPurchaser, and loss or damage shall be made good by the Contractor free\nof cost, without waiting for the settlement of insurance claim. The payment\nafter settlement of insurance claim shall be reimbursed by the Purchaser to\nthe Contractor. It will be entirely the responsibility of the Contractor to make\ngood loss/damage without waiting for settlement of insurance claim so that\nmachine is commissioned within the time specified in the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0099",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 99,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 40248,
    "char_end": 40507,
    "char_count": 259,
    "text": "13. Spare parts\n\n13.1 If specified in the List of Requirements and in the resultant contract, the\nsupplier shall supply / provide any or all of the following materials,\ninformation etc. pertaining to spare parts manufactured and / or supplied by\nthe supplier:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0100",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 100,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 40509,
    "char_end": 40745,
    "char_count": 236,
    "text": "a)\nThe spare parts as selected by BRBNMPL to be purchased from the\nsupplier, subject to the condition that such purchase of the spare parts\nshall not relieve the supplier of any contractual obligation including\nwarranty obligations; and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0101",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 101,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 40747,
    "char_end": 40978,
    "char_count": 231,
    "text": "b)\nIn case the production of the spare parts is discontinued:\n\ni.\nsufficient    advance    notice    to    BRBNMPL    before    such\ndiscontinuation to provide adequate time to BRBNMPL to\npurchase the required spare parts etc., and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0102",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 102,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 40980,
    "char_end": 41168,
    "char_count": 188,
    "text": "ii.   immediately  following  such  discontinuation,  providing\nBRBNMPL, free of cost, the designs, drawings, layouts and\nspecifications of the spare parts, as and if requested by\nBRBNMPL.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0103",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 103,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 41170,
    "char_end": 41363,
    "char_count": 193,
    "text": "13.2 Supplier shall carry sufficient inventories to assure ex-stock supply of\nconsumable spares for the goods so that the same are supplied to\nBRBNMPL promptly on receipt of order from BRBNMPL.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0104",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 104,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 41365,
    "char_end": 41580,
    "char_count": 215,
    "text": "14. Incidental services\n\n14.1 Subject to the stipulation, if any, in the SCC (Section V) and the Technical\nSpecification (Section VII), the supplier shall be required to perform any or\nall of the following services:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0105",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 105,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 41582,
    "char_end": 42057,
    "char_count": 475,
    "text": "a)\nProviding required jigs and tools for  assembly,  start-up   and\nmaintenance of the goods\nb)\nSupplying required number of operation & maintenance manual for\nthe goods\nc)\nInstallation and commissioning of the goods\nd)\nTraining of BRBNMPL's operators for operating and maintaining the\ngoods\ne)\nProviding after sales service during the tenure of the contract\nf)\nProviding maintenance service after expiry of the warranty period of\nthe goods if so incorporated in the contract",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0106",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 106,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 42059,
    "char_end": 42432,
    "char_count": 373,
    "text": "14.2 Prices to be paid to the supplier by BRBNMPL for any of the required\nincidental services, if not already included in the contract price during the\nplacement of the contract, shall be settled and decided in advance by\nBRBNMPL and the supplier. However, such prices shall not exceed the\ncontemporary rates charged by the supplier to other customers for similar\nservices.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0107",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 107,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 42434,
    "char_end": 42831,
    "char_count": 397,
    "text": "15. Distribution of Despatch Documents for Clearance / Receipt of Goods\n\n15.1 The supplier shall send all the relevant despatch documents well in time to\nBRBNMPL to enable BRBNMPL to clear or receive (as the case may be)\nthe goods in terms of the contract. Unless otherwise specified in the SCC,\nthe usual documents involved and the drill to be followed in general for this\npurpose are as follows:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0108",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 108,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 42833,
    "char_end": 43208,
    "char_count": 375,
    "text": "15.2 For Domestic Goods, including goods already imported by the supplier\nunder its own arrangement, within 24 hours of despatch, the supplier shall\nnotify BRBNMPL, consignee, and others concerned if mentioned in the\ncontract, the complete details of despatch and also supply the following\ndocuments to them by registered post / speed post (or as instructed in the\ncontract):",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0109",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 109,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 43210,
    "char_end": 43502,
    "char_count": 292,
    "text": "(a)\nSupplier's Invoice indicating, inter alia description and specification of\nthe goods, quantity, unit price, total value;\n(b)\nPacking list;\n(c)\nInsurance certificate;\n(d)\nRailway receipt / Road Consignment note;\n(e)\nManufacturer's guarantee certificate and in-house inspection\ncertificate;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0110",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 110,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 43504,
    "char_end": 43694,
    "char_count": 190,
    "text": "(f)\nInspection certificate issued by BRBNMPL's inspector\n(g)\nExpected date of arrival of goods at destination and\n(h)\nAny other document(s), as and if specifically mentioned in the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0111",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 111,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 43696,
    "char_end": 44012,
    "char_count": 316,
    "text": "15.3 For Imported Goods, within 3 days of dispatch, the supplier will Notify\nBRBNMPL, consignee and other concerned if mentioned in the contract,\nthe complete details of dispatch and also supply the following documents\nto them by Courier (or as instructed in the Contract), besides advance\nintimation by Fax / email:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0112",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 112,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 44014,
    "char_end": 44476,
    "char_count": 462,
    "text": "(a)\nClean on Board Airway Bill/Bill of Lading (B/L)\n(b)\nOriginal Invoice\n(c)\nPacking List (with item-wise gross and net weight)\n(d)\nCertificate of Origin from Seller's Chamber of Commerce\n(e)\nCertificate of pre-despatch inspection by BRBNMPL’s representative/\nnominee\n(f)\nCertificate of Quality and current manufacture from OEM\n(g)\nDangerous Cargo Certificate, if any.\n(h)\nInsurance Policy of 110% if CIP/CIF contract.\n(i)\nPerformance Bond / Warranty Certificate",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0113",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 113,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 44478,
    "char_end": 44819,
    "char_count": 341,
    "text": "15.4 Receipt of Consignment - Preliminary Acknowledgement: At the time\nof the delivery at the destination, the consignee shall receive the Goods on\na \"subject to inspection and acceptance in terms of contract\" basis and shall\nissue the preliminary receipt to acknowledge having received the claimed\nquantity (not the quality) of consignment.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0114",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 114,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 44821,
    "char_end": 45441,
    "char_count": 620,
    "text": "16. Warranty\n\n16.1 In general, the supplier should warrant that the goods supplied under the\ncontract is new, unused and incorporate all recent improvements in design\nand materials unless prescribed otherwise by BRBNMPL in the contract.\nThe supplier should further warrant that the goods supplied under the\ncontract shall have no defect arising from design, materials (except when\nthe design adopted and/ or the material used are as per BRBNMPL's\nspecifications) or workmanship or from any act or omission of the supplier,\nthat may develop under normal use of the supplied goods under the\nconditions prevailing in India.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0115",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 115,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 45443,
    "char_end": 46078,
    "char_count": 635,
    "text": "16.2 Unless otherwise specified in the SCC, this warranty shall remain valid for\ntwelve months after the goods or any portion thereof as the case may be,\nhave been delivered to the final destination and installed and commissioned\nat the final destination and accepted by BRBNMPL in terms of the contract\nor for fifteen months from the date of despatch from the supplier's premises\nfor domestic goods (including goods already imported by the supplier under\nits own arrangement) or for eighteen months after the date of shipment from\nthe port of loading in the source country for imported goods offered from\nabroad, whichever is earlier.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0116",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 116,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 46080,
    "char_end": 47819,
    "char_count": 1739,
    "text": "16.3 Obligations of the contractor under the warranty clause shall survive even\nthough:\na)\nThe Goods may have been inspected, accepted, installed/\ncommissioned and paid for by BRBNMPL.\nb)\nThe contract is terminated for any reason whatsoever.\n16.4 BRBNMPL shall promptly notify in writing to the contractor, if during the\nperiod above, the said goods/stores/articles are discovered not to conform\nto the description and quality or have deteriorated, otherwise than by fair\nwear and tear (the decision of BRBNMPL in that behalf being final and\nconclusive).\n16.5 Upon receipt of such notice, the supplier shall, with all reasonable speed\n(or within the period, if specified in the SCC or contract), repair or replace\nthe defective goods or parts thereof, free of cost, at the ultimate destination.\nThe supplier shall take over the replaced parts / goods after providing their\nreplacements and no claim, whatsoever shall lie on BRBNMPL for such\nreplaced parts/goods thereafter.\n16.6 A penalty of 0.5% (half per cent) of the contract value for the delay in\nresponse time beyond specified time as detailed above shall be recoverable\nfrom the Performance/Warrantee Guarantee. The maximum penalty for\nwarranty failure will be 5% (Five percent) of the contract value during the\nwhole warranty period. If there is further such delay after reaching this limit,\nBRBNMPL shall be entitled to encashment of whole of Performance/\nWarrantee Guarantee Bonds.\n16.7 In the event of any rectification of a defect or replacement of any defective\ngoods during the warranty period, the warranty for the rectified / replaced\ngoods shall remain till the original warranty period.\n16.8 If the supplier, having been notified, fails to rectify / replace the defect(s)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0117",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 117,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 47820,
    "char_end": 48023,
    "char_count": 203,
    "text": "within a reasonable period (or within the period, if specified in the SCC or\ncontract), it shall amount to breach of Contract for default and BRBNMPL\nshall avail any or all remedial action(s) thereunder.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0118",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 118,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 48025,
    "char_end": 48255,
    "char_count": 230,
    "text": "17. Assignment\n\n17.1 The Supplier shall not sublet, transfer, or assign, either in whole or in part,\nits contractual duties, responsibilities and obligations to perform the\ncontract, except with BRBNMPL's prior written permission.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0119",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 119,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 48257,
    "char_end": 48669,
    "char_count": 412,
    "text": "18. Sub Contracts\n\n18.1 The Supplier shall notify BRBNMPL in writing of all sub contracts awarded\nunder the contract if not already specified in its tender. Such notification, in\nits original tender or later, shall not relieve the Supplier from any of its\nliability or obligation under the terms and conditions of the contract.\n18.2 Sub contract shall be only for bought out items and incidental Works/\nServices.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0120",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 120,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 48671,
    "char_end": 49021,
    "char_count": 350,
    "text": "18.3 Sub contracts shall also comply with the provisions of GCC Clause 5\n(“Country of Origin\").\n18.4 If the Contractor sublets or assigns this contract or any part thereof without\nsuch permission, the Procuring Entity shall be entitled, and it shall be lawful\non his part, to treat it as a breach of contract and avail any or all remedies\nthereunder.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0121",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 121,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 49023,
    "char_end": 49457,
    "char_count": 434,
    "text": "19. Modification of contract\n\n19.1 Once a contract has been concluded, the terms and conditions thereof will\ngenerally not be varied. However, if necessary, BRBNMPL may suo-moto\nor, on request from the supplier, by a written order given to the supplier at\nany time during the currency of the contract, amend the contract by making\nalterations and modifications within the general scope of contract in any one\nor more of the following:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0122",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 122,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 49459,
    "char_end": 49823,
    "char_count": 364,
    "text": "(a)\nSpecifications, drawings, designs etc. where goods to be supplied\nunder the contract are to be specially manufactured for BRBNMPL,\n(b)\nmode of packing,\n(c)\nincidental services to be provided by the supplier\n(d)\nmode of despatch,\n(e)\nplace of delivery, and\n(f)\nany other area(s) of the contract, as felt necessary by BRBNMPL\ndepending on the merits of the case.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0123",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 123,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 49825,
    "char_end": 50442,
    "char_count": 617,
    "text": "19.2 In the event of any such modification / alteration causing increase or\ndecrease in the cost of goods and services to be supplied and provided, or\nin the time required by the supplier to perform any obligation under the\ncontract, an equitable adjustment shall be made in the contract price and/\nor contract delivery schedule, as the case may be, and the contract\namended accordingly. If the supplier doesn't agree to the adjustment made\nby BRBNMPL, the supplier shall convey its views to BRBNMPL within\ntwenty-one days from the date of the supplier's receipt of BRBNMPL's\namendment / modification of the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0124",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 124,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 50444,
    "char_end": 50768,
    "char_count": 324,
    "text": "19.3 Option Clause: By a suitable provision in the SCC, the Purchaser may\nreserve the right to increase the ordered quantity by 25% at any time, till\nfinal delivery date of the contract, by giving reasonable notice even though\nthe quantity ordered initially has been supplied in full before the last date of\nDelivery Period.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0125",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 125,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 50770,
    "char_end": 51168,
    "char_count": 398,
    "text": "19.4 Repeat Order: By a suitable provision in the SCC, the Purchaser may\nreserve the right to procure additional 50% of the ordered quantity within 6\nmonths from the date of last supply by placing repeat order against the\nprevious order with same rate and terms and conditions. However, both\noptional quantity and repeat order quantity together shall not exceed 50%\nof the initial ordered quantity.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0126",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 126,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 51170,
    "char_end": 51765,
    "char_count": 595,
    "text": "20. Prices\n\n20.1 Prices to be charged by the supplier for supply of goods and provision of\nservices in terms of the contract shall not vary from the corresponding\nprices quoted by the supplier in its tender or during negotiations, if any, and\nincorporated in the contract except for any price adjustment authorized in\nthe SCC.\n20.2 Price Variation: If the Price Variation clause is applicable as per the\ncontract, the price shall be subject to adjustment to take care of the changes\nin the cost of labour, material, and fuel/power components as per the price\nvariation formula specified therein.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0127",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 127,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 51767,
    "char_end": 52440,
    "char_count": 673,
    "text": "20.3 Exchange Rate Variation: The offer of the tenderer should indicate import\ncontent and the currency used for calculating import content. The Base\nExchange rate of each significant currency used for calculating the Foreign\nExchange content of the contract shall be as prevailing on the last deadline\nfor submission of Techno-commercial Bids, and variation beyond the base\nExchange Rate shall be calculated up to the midpoint of the delivery period,\nunless firm has already indicated the time schedule within which material\nwill be imported by the firm. In case delivery period is refixed / extended,\nERV will not be admissible, if this is due to default of the supplier.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0128",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 128,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 52442,
    "char_end": 52745,
    "char_count": 303,
    "text": "Documents for claiming ERV:\n(i)\nA bill of ERV claim enclosing working sheet\n(ii)\nBanker's Certificate/debit advice detailing F.E. paid and exchange\nrate prevailing on the date as applicable.\n(iii) Copies of import order/agreement placed on supplier\n(iv) Invoice of supplier for the relevant import order",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0129",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 129,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 52747,
    "char_end": 53279,
    "char_count": 532,
    "text": "21. Taxes and Duties\n\n21.1 Supplier shall be entirely responsible for all taxes, duties, fees, levies etc.\nincurred until delivery of the contracted goods to BRBNMPL. Further\ninstruction, if any, shall be as provided in the SCC.\n21.2 If applicable under relevant tax laws and rules, BRBNMPL shall deduct from\nall payments and deposit required taxes to respective authorities on\naccount of GST Reverse Charge Mechanism; Tax Deducted at Source\n(TDS), and Tax Collected at Source (TCS) relating to Income Tax, labour\ncess, royalty etc.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0130",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 130,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 53281,
    "char_end": 53943,
    "char_count": 662,
    "text": "21.3 The payment of GST and GST Cess to the contractor shall be made only\non the latter submitting a GST compliant Bill / invoice indicating the\nappropriate HSN code and applicable GST rate thereon duly supported with\ndocumentary evidence as per the provision of relevant GST Act and the\nRules made there under. The delivery shall be shown being made in the\nname, location/ state, and GSTIN of the consignee only; the location of the\nprocurement office of the procuring entity has no bearing on the invoicing.\n21.4 The supply of Goods or services or both, if imported into India, shall be\nconsidered as supply under inter-state commerce / trade and shall attract",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0131",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 131,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 53945,
    "char_end": 54097,
    "char_count": 152,
    "text": "integrated tax (IGST). The IGST rate and GST cess shall be applicable on\nthe ‘Custom Assessable Value’ plus the ‘Basic Customs duty applicable\nthereon’.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0132",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 132,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 54099,
    "char_end": 54898,
    "char_count": 799,
    "text": "21.5 While claiming reimbursement of duties, taxes etc. (like GST) from the\nProcuring Entity, as and if permitted under the contract, the contractor shall\nalso certify that in case it gets any refund out of such taxes and duties from\nthe concerned authorities at a later date, it (the contractor) shall refund to\nthe Procuring Entity, the Procuring Entity’s share out of such refund\nreceived by the contractor. The Contractor shall also refund the appropriate\namount to the Procuring Entity immediately on receiving the same from the\nconcerned authorities.\n21.6 All necessary adjustment vouchers such as Credit Notes/ Debit Notes for\nany short/ excess supplies or revision in prices or any other reason under\nthe contract shall be submitted to the Procuring Entity in compliance with\nGST provisions.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0133",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 133,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 54900,
    "char_end": 55259,
    "char_count": 359,
    "text": "21.7 Liquidated  damages  or  any  other  recoveries  should  be  shown  as\ndeductions on the invoice, and GST shall be applicable only on the nett\nbalance payment due.\n21.8 In case of Price Variation or Exchange Rate variation, or any other variation\nis applicable, GST shall be applicable on the nett invoice value after the\nvariation is taken into account.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0134",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 134,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 55261,
    "char_end": 55511,
    "char_count": 250,
    "text": "21.9 GST shall be paid as per the rate at which it is liable to be assessed or has\nbeen assessed provided the transaction of the sale is legally liable to such\ntaxes and is payable as per the terms of the contract subject to the following\nconditions:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0135",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 135,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 55513,
    "char_end": 56782,
    "char_count": 1269,
    "text": "(i)     The Procuring Entity shall not pay a higher GST rate if leviable due to\nany misclassification of HSN number or incorrect GST rate\nincorporated in the contract due to contractor’s fault. Wherever the\ncontractor invoices the Goods at GST rate or HSN number, which is\ndifferent from that incorporated in the contract, payment shall be made\nas per GST rate, which is lower of the GST rates incorporated in the\ncontract or billed.\n(ii)   However, the Procuring Entity shall not be responsible for the\ncontractor's tax payment or duty under a misapprehension of the law.\n(iii)   Bidder is informed that he shall be required to adjust his basic price to\nthe extent required by a higher tax rate billed as per invoice to match\nthe all-inclusive price mentioned in the contract.\n(iv)  In case of profiteering by the contractor relating to GST tax, the\nProcuring Entity shall treat it as a violation of the Code of Integrity in\nthe contract and avail any or all punitive actions thereunder, in addition\nto recovery and action by the GST authorities under the Act.\n(v)\nThe contractor should issue Receipt vouchers immediately on receipt\nof all types of payments along with tax invoices after adjusting\nadvance payments, if any, as per Contractual terms and GST\nProvisions.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0136",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 136,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 56784,
    "char_end": 57596,
    "char_count": 812,
    "text": "(vi)  Liquidated damages or any other recoveries should be shown as\ndeductions on the invoice, and GST shall be applicable only on the\nnett balance payment due.\n21.10Statutory Variation Clause: Unless otherwise stated in the contract,\nstatutory increase in applicable GST rate only during the original delivery\nperiod shall be to Procuring Entity’s account. Any increase in the rates of\nGST beyond the original completion date during the extended delivery\nperiod shall be borne by the contractor. The benefit of any reduction in GST\nrate must be passed on to the Procuring Entity during the original and\nextended delivery period. However, GST rate amendments shall be\nconsidered for quoted HSN code only, against documentary evidence,\nprovided such an increase of GST rates after the last date of bid submission.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0137",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 137,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 57598,
    "char_end": 58032,
    "char_count": 434,
    "text": "21.11Duties/Taxes on Raw Materials: The Procuring Entity is not liable for any\nclaim from the contractor on account of fresh imposition and/ or increase\n(including statutory increase) of GST, customs duty, or other duties on raw\nmaterials and/ or components used directly in the manufacture of the\ncontracted Goods taking place during the pendency of the contract unless\nsuch liability is expressly agreed to in terms of the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0138",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 138,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 58034,
    "char_end": 58142,
    "char_count": 108,
    "text": "22. Terms and Mode of Payment: Unless specified otherwise in SCC, the terms of\npayments would be as follows:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0139",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 139,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 58144,
    "char_end": 58604,
    "char_count": 460,
    "text": "22.1 Unless otherwise specified in SCC, usual payment term is 100% on receipt\nand acceptance of goods by the consignee (Stores section) and on\nproduction of all required documents by the supplier.\n22.2 For Domestic Goods: Unless otherwise specified in the SCC, payments to\nsuppliers are usually made by account payee cheque or through ECS only.\nIn case of non-payment through EFT, or where EFT facility is not available,\npayment may be released through cheque.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0140",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 140,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 58606,
    "char_end": 58933,
    "char_count": 327,
    "text": "22.2.1 Where the terms of delivery is FOR dispatching Station, the payment\nterms, depending on the value and nature of the goods, mode of\ntransportation etc. maybe  60% to 90% (as specified in SIT) on proof\nof dispatch and other related documents and balance on receipt at\nsite and acceptance by the consignee (Stores section).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0141",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 141,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 58935,
    "char_end": 59544,
    "char_count": 609,
    "text": "22.2.2 Where the terms of delivery is delivery at site / CIF Destination / FOR\ndestination, usual payment term is 100% on receipt and acceptance\nof goods by the consignee (Stores section) and on production of all\nrequired documents by the supplier.\n22.2.3Where goods to\nbe\nsupplied also\nneed\ninstallation and\ncommissioning by the supplier, the payment terms are generally as\nunder:\n(a)\nFor a contract with terms of delivery as FOR dispatching station\ni.\n60%  on  proof  of  dispatch  along  with  other  specified\ndocuments\nii.\n30% on receipt of the goods at site by the consignee\n(Stores section) and balance",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0142",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 142,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 59546,
    "char_end": 59659,
    "char_count": 113,
    "text": "iii.     10% on successful installation and commissioning and final\nacceptance by the consignee (User department)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0143",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 143,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 59661,
    "char_end": 59905,
    "char_count": 244,
    "text": "(b)\nFor a contract with terms of delivery as Delivery at site/CIF\nDestination/FOR destination\ni.\n90% on receipt and acceptance of goods by the consignee\n(Stores section) at destination and on production of all\nrequired documents by the supplier",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0144",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 144,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 59907,
    "char_end": 60015,
    "char_count": 108,
    "text": "ii.\n10% on successful installation and commissioning and final\nacceptance by the consignee (User department)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0145",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 145,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 60017,
    "char_end": 60539,
    "char_count": 522,
    "text": "22.3 For Imported Goods: Unless otherwise specified in SCC, payments are\nmade through an irrevocable Letter of Credit (LC).\n(a)\nCases where Installation, Erection and Commissioning (if applicable)\nare not the responsibility of the Supplier - 90% net FOB/FAS/\nCFR/CIF/CIP price is to be paid against invoice, shipping documents,\ninspection certificate (wherever applicable), manufacturers' test\ncertificate, etc. and balance 10% on receipt of goods and after\nascertaining its suitability by the consignee (User department).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0146",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 146,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 60541,
    "char_end": 61097,
    "char_count": 556,
    "text": "(b)\nCases  where  Installation,  Erection  and  Commissioning  are  the\nresponsibility of the Supplier - 80% to 90% net FOB/FAS/CFR/CIF/\nCIP price (as specified in the SCC) will be paid against invoice,\ninspection certificate (where applicable), shipping documents etc. and\nbalance 10% - 20% within 21-30 days of successful installation and\ncommissioning at the consignee's premises and final acceptance by\nthe consignee (User department).\n22.4 Unless specified otherwise in the SCC, the following general conditions will\napply for payment to the supplier.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0147",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 147,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 61099,
    "char_end": 61288,
    "char_count": 189,
    "text": "22.5 In Domestic Contracts, payments shall only be made in Indian Rupees. In\nGlobal Tenders, payment to foreign bidders shall be made in the currency/\ncurrencies authorized in the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0148",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 148,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 61290,
    "char_end": 61822,
    "char_count": 532,
    "text": "22.6 The supplier shall send its claim for payment in writing as per Section XIX -\n\"Proforma for Bill for Payments\", when contractually due, along with\nrelevant documents etc., duly signed with date, as specified in SCC and in\na manner as also specified therein.\n22.7 While claiming payment, the supplier is also to certify in the bill that the\npayment being claimed is strictly in terms of the contract and all the\nobligations on the part of the supplier for claiming that payment has been\nfulfilled as required under the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0149",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 149,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 61824,
    "char_end": 61913,
    "char_count": 89,
    "text": "22.8 The important documents which the supplier is to furnish while claiming\npayment are:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0150",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 150,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 61915,
    "char_end": 62113,
    "char_count": 198,
    "text": "a)\nOriginal Invoice (GST compliant)\nb)\nPacking List (with item-wise gross and net weight)\nc)\nCertificate of country of origin of the goods from seller's Chamber of\nCommerce in case of imported goods",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0151",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 151,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 62115,
    "char_end": 63685,
    "char_count": 1570,
    "text": "d)\nCertificate of pre-dispatch inspection by BRBNMPL's representative /\nnominee\ne)\nManufacturer's test certificate\nf)\nPerformance / Warrantee Bond\ng)\nCertificate of insurance\nh)\nClean on Bill of lading / Airway bill / Rail receipt or any other dispatch\ndocument, issued by a government agency (like postal department)\nor an agency duly authorized by the concerned ministry / department\ni)\nConsignee's Certificate confirming receipt and acceptance of goods\nin case of payment after receipt and acceptance\nj)\nDangerous Cargo Certificate, if any, in case of imported goods.\nk)\nAny other document specified.\n22.9 While claiming reimbursement of duties, taxes (like GST, Customs duty and\nany other similar duties and taxes) from BRBNMPL, as and if permitted\nunder the contract, the supplier shall also certify that, in case it gets any\nrefund out of such taxes and duties from the concerned authorities at a later\ndate, it (the supplier) shall refund to BRBNMPL. The supplier shall also\nrefund the applicable amount to BRBNMPL immediately on receiving the\nsame from the concerned authorities.\n22.10In case where the supplier is not in a position to submit its bill for the\nbalance payment for want of receipt copies of Inspection Note from the\nconsignee and the consignee has not complained about the non-receipt,\nshortage, or defects in the supplies made, balance amount will be paid by\nthe paying authority without consignee's receipt certificate after three\nmonths from the date of the preceding part payment for the goods in\nquestion, subject to the following conditions:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0152",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 152,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 63686,
    "char_end": 63840,
    "char_count": 154,
    "text": "(a) The  supplier  will  make  good  any  defect  or  deficiency  that  the\nconsignee (s) may report within six months from the date of despatch\nof goods.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0153",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 153,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 63841,
    "char_end": 63969,
    "char_count": 128,
    "text": "(b) Delay in supplies, if any, has been regularized.\n(c) The contract price where it is subject to variation has been finalized.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0154",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 154,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 63970,
    "char_end": 64485,
    "char_count": 515,
    "text": "(d) The supplier furnishes the following undertakings:\n“I/We,                                      certify that I/We have not received back\nthe Inspection Note duly receipted by the consignee or any\ncommunication from BRBNMPL or the consignee about non-receipt,\nshortage or defects in the goods supplied. I / We agree to make good\nany defect or deficiency that the consignee may report within three\nmonths from the date of receipt of this balance payment or six months\nfrom the date of dispatch whichever is later.”",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0155",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 155,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 64487,
    "char_end": 64866,
    "char_count": 379,
    "text": "22.11 Withholding and lien in respect of sums claimed: Whenever any claim\nor claims for payment of a sum of money arises against the contractor, out\nof or under the contract, BRBNMPL shall be entitled, and it shall be lawful\non his part, to withhold and also have a lien to retain such sum or sums, in\nwhole or in part pending finalisation or adjudication of any such claim from:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0156",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 156,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 64868,
    "char_end": 65154,
    "char_count": 286,
    "text": "(i)\nany security or retention money, if any, deposited by the contractor.\n\n(ii)    any sum(s) payable till now or hereafter to the contractor under the\nsame Contract or any other contract with BRBNMPL if the security is\ninsufficient or if no security has been taken from the contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0157",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 157,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 65156,
    "char_end": 65456,
    "char_count": 300,
    "text": "22.12 Payment Against Time-Barred Claims: All claims against BRBNMPL\nshall be legally time-barred after three years calculated from the date when\nthe payment falls due unless the payment claim has been under\ncorrespondence. BRBNMPL is entitled to, and it shall be lawful for it to\nreject such claims.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0158",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 158,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 65458,
    "char_end": 65847,
    "char_count": 389,
    "text": "23. Delay in the supplier's performance\n\n23.1 The time for and the date specified in the contract or as extended for the\ndelivery of the stores shall be deemed to be the essence of the contract\nand the supplier shall deliver the goods and perform the services under the\ncontract within the time schedule specified by BRBNMPL in the List of\nRequirements and as incorporated in the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0159",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 159,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 65849,
    "char_end": 66141,
    "char_count": 292,
    "text": "23.2 Subject to the provision under GCC clause 28, any unexcused delay by the\nsupplier in maintaining its contractual obligations towards delivery of goods\nand performance of services shall render the supplier liable to any or all of\nthe following sanctions besides any administrative action:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0160",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 160,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 66143,
    "char_end": 66269,
    "char_count": 126,
    "text": "a)\nImposition of liquidated damages,\nb)\nForfeiture of its performance security and\nc)\nTermination of the contract for default.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0161",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 161,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 66271,
    "char_end": 66900,
    "char_count": 629,
    "text": "23.3 If at any time during the currency of the contract, the supplier encounters\nconditions hindering timely delivery of the goods and performance of\nservices, the supplier shall promptly inform BRBNMPL in writing about the\nsame and its likely duration and make a request to BRBNMPL for extension\nof the delivery schedule accordingly. On receiving the supplier's\ncommunication, BRBNMPL shall examine the situation as soon as possible\nand, at its discretion, may agree to extend the delivery schedule, with or\nwithout liquidated damages for completion of supplier's contractual\nobligations by issuing an amendment to the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0162",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 162,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 66902,
    "char_end": 67089,
    "char_count": 187,
    "text": "23.4 When the period of delivery is extended due to unexcused delay by the\nsupplier, the amendment letter extending the delivery period shall, inter alia\ncontain the following conditions:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0163",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 163,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 67091,
    "char_end": 67377,
    "char_count": 286,
    "text": "(i)    Liquidated Damages: BRBNMPL shall recover from the supplier,\nunder the provisions of the clause 24 of the General Conditions of\nContract, liquidated damages on the goods and services, which the\nSupplier has failed to deliver within the delivery period stipulated in\nthe contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0164",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 164,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 67379,
    "char_end": 67533,
    "char_count": 154,
    "text": "(ii)\nDenial Clause:\n\na)\nThat no increase in price on account of any ground, whatsoever,\nincluding any stipulation in the contract for increase in price on",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0165",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 165,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 67535,
    "char_end": 68002,
    "char_count": 467,
    "text": "any other ground and, also including statutory increase in or\nfresh imposition of customs duty, Goods and Services Tax or on\naccount of any other duties and taxes which may be levied in\nrespect of the goods and services specified in the contract, which\ntakes place after the date of delivery stipulated in the contract\nshall be admissible on such of the said goods and services as\nare delivered and performed after the date of the delivery\nstipulated in the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0166",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 166,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 68004,
    "char_end": 68315,
    "char_count": 311,
    "text": "b)\nNotwithstanding any stipulation in the contract for an increase in\nprice on any other ground, including price variation clause or\nforeign exchange rate variation, or any other variation clause, no\nsuch increase after the original delivery date shall be admissible\non such goods delivered after the said date.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0167",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 167,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 68317,
    "char_end": 69175,
    "char_count": 858,
    "text": "c)\nBut nevertheless, BRBNMPL shall be entitled to the benefit of\nany decrease in price on account of reduction in or remission of\ncustoms duty, Goods and Services Tax or any other duty or tax\nor levy or on account of any other ground as stipulated in the\nprice variation clause or foreign exchange rate variation or any\nother variation clause, which takes place after the expiry of the\ndate of delivery stipulated in the contract.\n23.5 The supplier shall not despatch the goods after expiry of the delivery period.\nThe supplier is required to apply to BRBNMPL for extension of delivery\nperiod and obtain the same before despatch. In case the supplier\ndespatches the goods without obtaining an extension, it would be doing so\nat its own risk and no claim for payment for such supply and / or any other\nexpense related to such supply shall lie against BRBNMPL.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0168",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 168,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 69177,
    "char_end": 70065,
    "char_count": 888,
    "text": "24. Liquidated damages\n\n24.1 Subject to GCC clause 28, if the supplier fails to deliver any or all of the\nGoods or fails to perform the services within the time frame(s) incorporated\nin the contract, BRBNMPL shall, without prejudice to other rights and\nremedies available to BRBNMPL under the contract, deduct from the\ncontract price, as liquidated damages, a sum equivalent to the 0.5% percent\n(or any other percentage if prescribed in the SCC) of the delivered price of\nthe delayed goods and / or services for each week of delay or part thereof\nuntil actual delivery or performance, subject to a maximum deduction of the\n10% (or any other percentage if prescribed in the SCC) of the delayed\n‘goods' or ‘services' contract price(s). During the above-mentioned delayed\nperiod of supply and / or performance, the denial clause incorporated under\nGCC sub-clause 23.4 above shall also apply.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0169",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 169,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 70067,
    "char_end": 70157,
    "char_count": 90,
    "text": "25. Custody and Return of BRBNMPL’s Materials / Equipment / Documents\nloaned to Contractor",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0170",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 170,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 70159,
    "char_end": 70303,
    "char_count": 144,
    "text": "25.1 Whenever stores are required to be issued to the firm/contractor for\nfabrication or prototypes or sub-assemblies are issued for guidance in",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0171",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 171,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 70305,
    "char_end": 70490,
    "char_count": 185,
    "text": "fabrication, these would be issued against appropriate Bank Guarantee as\nspecified in SCC. In addition to the Bank Guarantee, appropriate insurance\nmay be asked if specified in the SCC.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0172",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 172,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 70492,
    "char_end": 70705,
    "char_count": 213,
    "text": "25.2 All drawings and samples issued to the contractor in connection with the\ncontract must be returned by him. Final payment will be withheld if this is\nnot done, besides any other sanction deemed fit by BRBNMPL.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0173",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 173,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 70707,
    "char_end": 71027,
    "char_count": 320,
    "text": "26. Breach of Contract - Termination for default\n\n26.1 BRBNMPL, without prejudice to any other contractual rights and remedies\navailable to it for breach of contract, such as removal from the list of\nregistered supplier, may, by written notice of default sent to the supplier,\nterminate the contract in whole or in part:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0174",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 174,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 71029,
    "char_end": 71193,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "(i)     If the supplier fails to deliver any or all of the stores or services within\nthe time period(s) specified in the contract, or any extension thereof\ngranted.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0175",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 175,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 71195,
    "char_end": 71454,
    "char_count": 259,
    "text": "(ii)    If the supplier fails to perform any other obligation (including Code of\nEthics or obligation to maintain eligibility and Qualifications based on\nwhich contract was awarded) within the period specified in the\ncontract or any extension thereof granted.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0176",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 176,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 71456,
    "char_end": 71640,
    "char_count": 184,
    "text": "(iii)  If the supplier is found to have made any false or fraudulent\ndeclaration or statement to get the contract or he is found to be\nindulging in unethical or unfair trade practices.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0177",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 177,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 71642,
    "char_end": 71855,
    "char_count": 213,
    "text": "(iv)   When the item offered by the supplier repeatedly fails in the inspection\nand/or the supplier is not in a position to either rectify the defects or\noffer items conforming to the contracted quality standards.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0178",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 178,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 71857,
    "char_end": 72022,
    "char_count": 165,
    "text": "(v)    When both parties mutually agree to terminate the contract.\n\n(vi)  Any special circumstances, which must be recorded to justify the\ntermination of a contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0179",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 179,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 72024,
    "char_end": 72262,
    "char_count": 238,
    "text": "(vii)  In pursuance of an award given by a Court of Law.\n\n26.2 In the event BRBNMPL terminates the contract in whole or in part, pursuant\nto GCC sub-clause 26.1 above, BRBNMPL may take recourse to any one\nor more of the following actions:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0180",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 180,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 72264,
    "char_end": 72656,
    "char_count": 392,
    "text": "(i)     Invoke the performance security;\n\n(ii)    Invoke the risk purchase clause - BRBNMPL may procure goods and/\nor services similar to those undelivered, with such terms and\nconditions and in such manner as it deems fit at the \"Risk and Cost\"\nof the supplier and the supplier shall be liable to BRBNMPL for the\nextra expenditure, if any, incurred by BRBNMPL for arranging such\nprocurement;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0181",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 181,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 72658,
    "char_end": 72833,
    "char_count": 175,
    "text": "(iii)   Any other action as deemed appropriate.\n\n26.3 Unless otherwise instructed by BRBNMPL, the supplier shall continue to\nperform the contract to the extent not terminated.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0182",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 182,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 72835,
    "char_end": 72934,
    "char_count": 99,
    "text": "26.4 All  warranty  obligations,  if  any,  shall  continue  to  survive  despite  the\ntermination.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0183",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 183,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 72936,
    "char_end": 73393,
    "char_count": 457,
    "text": "26.5 Limitation of Liability: Except in cases of criminal negligence or wilful\nmisconduct, the aggregate liability of the contractor to the Procuring Entity,\nwhether under the contract, in tort or otherwise, shall not exceed the total\nContract Price, provided that this limitation shall not apply to the cost of\nrepairing or replacing defective equipment, or to any obligation of the\ncontractor to indemnify the Procuring Entity concerning IPR infringement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0184",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 184,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 73395,
    "char_end": 74149,
    "char_count": 754,
    "text": "27. Breach of Contract - Termination for insolvency\n\n27.1 In the event the supplier becomes bankrupt or otherwise insolvent or loses\nsubstantially the technical or financial capability (based on which he was\nselected for award of contract) or liquidation proceedings are commenced\nagainst it by a third party or by own volition, BRBNMPL reserves the right\nto terminate the contract, at any time, by serving written notice to the\nsupplier, without any adverse consequence to BRBNMPL and without\nbeing liable to pay any compensation, whatsoever, to the supplier, subject\nto further condition that such termination will not prejudice or affect any\nrights of action or remedies which have accrued or will accrue prior to\ntermination or thereafter to BRBNMPL.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0185",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 185,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 74151,
    "char_end": 74744,
    "char_count": 593,
    "text": "27.2 Upon such termination, BRBNMPL shall be deemed to be the owner of the\nstores/materials manufactured by the supplier and retain first right and lien\nover the stores/materials including the raw material purchased by the\nsupplier for performance of the contract and require the stores/materials to\nbe delivered under the contract, which is terminated on account of\nbankruptcy or insolvency or likely bankruptcy or insolvency of the supplier\nand such stores in possession of the supplier shall be earmarked and be\ndelivered to BRBNMPL before the start of the bankruptcy or insolvency\nprocess.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0186",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 186,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 74746,
    "char_end": 75151,
    "char_count": 405,
    "text": "27.3 In the event the supplier is aware or apprehends that it is likely to go into\nliquidation whether on account of liquidation proceedings commenced by a\nthird party or by way of voluntary liquidation, then the supplier shall forthwith\ninform BRBNMPL as soon as it is aware that a third party has issued notice\nthat it intends to commence liquidation proceedings or well before it files for\nliquidation.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0187",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 187,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 75153,
    "char_end": 75612,
    "char_count": 459,
    "text": "27.4 Escrow Arrangement\n\n(i)    The Supplier shall deposit with a third party escrow agent mutually\nagreed to by the parties, a copy of Software and its source code and\nobject code for safe keeping with instructions for it to be released\nforthwith to BRBNMPL, in the event the Supplier fails to make the\nsource code/object code accessible to BRBNMPL whenever required\nand/or in the event the Supplier is likely to go into liquidation or goes\ninto liquidation.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0188",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 188,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 75614,
    "char_end": 76160,
    "char_count": 546,
    "text": "(ii)\nIn the event, the Supplier apprehends that it is likely to go into\n\nliquidation whether on account of liquidation proceedings commenced\nby a third party or in the event it anticipates filing for bankruptcy, then\nthe Supplier shall inform BRBNMPL in advance and engage with it to\ndetermine the sale and possession of BRBNMPL’s  software and its\nsource code. In the event Supplier fails to do so, the third party escrow\nagent shall be instructed under the Escrow Agreement to release the\nSoftware and its source code to BRBNMPL as noted above.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0189",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 189,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 76162,
    "char_end": 76575,
    "char_count": 413,
    "text": "(iii)   For the purpose of this Clause, the term ‘Software’ shall collectively\nmean, the full and final version of the Software to be delivered to\nBRBNMPL in source code and object code forms, together with any\nand\nall\nimprovements,\ncorrections,\nmodifications,\nupdates,\nenhancements or other changes, whether or not included in the full\nand final version including all System Documentation and User\nDocumentation.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0190",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 190,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 76577,
    "char_end": 77080,
    "char_count": 503,
    "text": "(iv) The term ‘System Documentation’ shall mean any and all\ndocumentation used in the development and updating of the Software,\nincluding but not limited to, customer requirements and specifications\ndesign or development specifications, test and error reports, and\nrelated correspondence and memoranda. And the term ‘User\nDocumentation’ shall mean the end-user instruction manual that\nusually accompanies the Software instructing end users in the use of\nthe Software in both printed and electronic form.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0191",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 191,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 77082,
    "char_end": 78319,
    "char_count": 1237,
    "text": "28. Force Majeure\n\n28.1 In the event of any unforeseen event directly interfering with the supply of\nstores arising during the currency of the contract, such as war, hostilities,\nacts  of  the  public  enemy,  civil  commotion,  sabotage,  fires,  floods,\nexplosions, epidemics, quarantine restrictions, strikes, lockouts, or acts of\nGod, the Contractor shall, within a week from the commencement thereof,\nnotify the same in writing to the Purchaser with reasonable evidence thereof.\nUnless  otherwise  directed  by  BRBNMPL  in  writing,  the  supplier  shall\ncontinue to perform its obligations under the contract as far as reasonably\npractical, and shall seek all reasonable alternative means for performance\nnot prevented by the Force Majeure event. If the force majeure condition(s)\nmentioned above be in force for a period of 90 days or more at any time,\neither party shall have the option to terminate the contract on expiry of 90\ndays of commencement of such force majeure by giving 14 days' notice to\nthe other party in writing. In case of such termination, no damages shall be\nclaimed by either party against the other, save and except those which had\noccurred under any other clause of this contract prior to such termination.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0192",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 192,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 78321,
    "char_end": 78609,
    "char_count": 288,
    "text": "28.2 Notwithstanding the provisions contained in GCC clauses 23, 24 and 26,\nthe supplier shall not be liable for imposition of any such sanction so long\nthe delay and / or failure of the supplier in fulfilling its obligations under the\ncontract is the result of an event of Force Majeure.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0193",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 193,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 78611,
    "char_end": 78758,
    "char_count": 147,
    "text": "28.3 In case due to a Force Majeure event BRBNMPL is unable to fulfil its\ncontractual  commitment  and  responsibility,  BRBNMPL  will  notify  the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0194",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 194,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 78760,
    "char_end": 78869,
    "char_count": 109,
    "text": "supplier  accordingly  and  subsequent  actions  taken  on  similar  lines\ndescribed in above sub-paragraphs.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0195",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 195,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 78871,
    "char_end": 79715,
    "char_count": 844,
    "text": "29. Termination for convenience\n\n29.1 BRBNMPL reserves the right to terminate the contract, in whole or in part\nfor its (BRBNMPL's) convenience, by serving written notice on the supplier\nat any time during the currency of the contract. The notice shall specify that\nthe termination is for the convenience of BRBNMPL. The notice shall also\nindicate inter-alia, the extent to which the supplier's performance under the\ncontract is terminated, and the date with effect from which such termination\nwill become effective.\n29.2 The goods and services which are complete and ready in terms of the\ncontract for delivery and performance within thirty days after the supplier's\nreceipt of the notice of termination shall be accepted by BRBNMPL\nfollowing the contract terms, conditions and prices. For the remaining goods\nand services, BRBNMPL may decide:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0196",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 196,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 79717,
    "char_end": 80052,
    "char_count": 335,
    "text": "a.\nto get any portion of the balance completed and delivered at the\ncontract terms, conditions and prices; and / or\nb.    to cancel the remaining portion of the goods and/or services and\ncompensate the supplier by paying an agreed amount for the cost\nincurred by the supplier towards the remaining portion of the goods\nand/or services.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0197",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 197,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 80054,
    "char_end": 80219,
    "char_count": 165,
    "text": "30. Fall Clause\n\nThis clause shall be applicable only if explicitly invoked in SCC. Nevertheless,\nFall Clause shall be expressly applicable in case of Rate Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0198",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 198,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 80221,
    "char_end": 80899,
    "char_count": 678,
    "text": "30.1 The  price  charged  for  the  Goods  supplied  under  the  contract by  the\ncontractor shall in no event exceed the lowest price at which the contractor\nsells the Goods or offers to sell Goods of identical description, to any\npersons/organisations including the Procuring Entity or any Department or\nUndertaking of the Central Government, as the case may be during the\ncurrency of the contract. Contractor shall forthwith notify such reduction or\nsale or offer of sale to the Procuring Entity and the price payable under the\ncontract for the Goods supplied after the date of coming into force of such\nreduction or sale or offer of sale shall stand correspondingly reduced.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0199",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 199,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 80901,
    "char_end": 81094,
    "char_count": 193,
    "text": "30.2 The above stipulation shall, however, not apply to:\n(i)\nExports by the contractor\n(ii)    Sale of Goods as original equipment at prices lower than the prices\ncharged for normal replacement",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0200",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 200,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 81096,
    "char_end": 81194,
    "char_count": 98,
    "text": "(iii)   Sale of perishable Goods having a limited shelf life, such as drugs that\nhave expiry dates",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0201",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 201,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 81196,
    "char_end": 81331,
    "char_count": 135,
    "text": "30.3 The  contractor  shall  furnish  the  following  certificate  with  each  bill  for\npayment of supplies made against the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0202",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 202,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 81333,
    "char_end": 81970,
    "char_count": 637,
    "text": "“We certify that there has been no reduction in the sale price of the Goods\nof description identical to the Goods supplied to BRBNMPL under the\ncontract herein, and such Goods have not been offered/sold by me/us to\nany person / organisation including any Ministry/Department/Attached and\nSubordinate Office/Public Sector Undertaking of Central or State\nGovernment(s) as the case may be upto the date of bill / the date of\ncompletion of Contract at a price lower than the price charged under this\ncontract except for the quantity of Goods categories under (i), (ii) and (iii) of\nsub-clause (30.2) above, details of which are as follows:-”",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0203",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 203,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 81972,
    "char_end": 82543,
    "char_count": 571,
    "text": "31. Notices\n\n31.1 Notice, if any, relating to the contract given by one party to the other, shall\nbe sent in writing or by cable or telex or facsimile and confirmed in writing,\nthe procedure will also provide the sender of the notice, the proof of receipt\nof the notice by the receiver. The addresses of the parties for exchanging\nsuch notices will be the addresses as incorporated in the contract.\n31.2 The effective date of a notice shall be either the date when delivered to the\nrecipient or the effective date specifically mentioned in the notice,\nwhichever is later.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0204",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 204,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 82545,
    "char_end": 82962,
    "char_count": 417,
    "text": "32. Code of Ethics, Obligations, Penalties and Punishments\n\n32.1 Code of Ethics: Officers and staff of  BRBNMPL as well as Bidders,\nSuppliers, Contractors, and Consultants under BRBNMPL contracts shall\nobserve the highest standard of ethics and should not indulge in following\nprohibited practices, either directly or indirectly, at any stage during the\nprocurement process or during execution of resultant contracts:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0205",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 205,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 82964,
    "char_end": 83195,
    "char_count": 231,
    "text": "(i)     “Corrupt practice” making offer, solicitation or acceptance of bribe,\nreward or gift or any material benefit, in exchange for an unfair\nadvantage in the procurement process or to otherwise influence the\nprocurement process;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0206",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 206,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 83197,
    "char_end": 83543,
    "char_count": 346,
    "text": "(ii)    “Fraudulent practice” any omission, or misrepresentation that may\nmislead or attempt to mislead so that financial or other benefit may be\nobtained, or an obligation avoided. This includes making false\ndeclaration or providing false information for participation in a tender\nprocess or to secure a contract or in execution of the contract;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0207",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 207,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 83545,
    "char_end": 83957,
    "char_count": 412,
    "text": "(iii)  “Anti-competitive practice” - any collusion, bid rigging or anti-\ncompetitive arrangement, or any other practice coming under the\npurview of The Competition Act, 2002, between two or more bidders,\nwith or without the knowledge of the procuring entity, that may impair\nthe transparency, fairness, and the progress of the procurement\nprocess or to establish bid prices at artificial, non-competitive levels;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0208",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 208,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 83959,
    "char_end": 84143,
    "char_count": 184,
    "text": "(iv)   “Coercive practice” harming or threatening to harm, persons, or their\nproperty to influence their participation in the procurement process or\naffect the execution of a contract;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0209",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 209,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 84145,
    "char_end": 84774,
    "char_count": 629,
    "text": "(v)\n“Conflict of interest” – participation by a bidding firm or any of its\naffiliates who are either involved in the Consultancy Contract from\nwhich particular procurement is linked; or if they are part of more than\none bid in the procurement; or if their personnel have relationship or\nfinancial or business transactions with any officer in Procuring entity,\nwho are directly or indirectly related to tender or execution process of\ncontract; or improper use of information obtained by the (prospective)\nbidder from the procuring entity with an intent to gain unfair advantage\nin the procurement process or for personal gain; and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0210",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 210,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 84776,
    "char_end": 85356,
    "char_count": 580,
    "text": "(vi) “Obstructive practice” - materially impede procuring entity’s\ninvestigation into allegations of one or more of the above mentioned\nprohibited practices either by deliberately destroying, falsifying,\naltering; or by concealing of evidence material to the investigation; or\nby making false statements to investigators and/or by threatening,\nharassing or intimidating any party to prevent it from disclosing its\nknowledge of matters relevant to the investigation or from pursuing\nthe investigation; or by impeding the procuring entity’s rights of audit\nor access to information;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0211",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 211,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 85358,
    "char_end": 85808,
    "char_count": 450,
    "text": "32.2 Obligations for proactive disclosures:\n\n(i)    Procuring authorities as well as bidders, suppliers, contractors, and\nconsultants, are obliged under this Code of Ethics to suo-moto\nproactively declare any conflict of interest (coming under the definition\nmentioned above – pre-existing or as and when these arise at any\nstage) in any procurement process or execution of contract. Failure to\ndo so would amount to violation of this code of ethics.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0212",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 212,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 85810,
    "char_end": 86111,
    "char_count": 301,
    "text": "(ii)    Any bidder must declare, whether asked or not in a bid document, any\nprevious transgressions of such code of ethics with any entity in any\ncountry during the last three years or of being debarred by any other\nprocuring entity. Failure to do so would amount to violation of this code\nof ethics.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0213",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 213,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 86113,
    "char_end": 86648,
    "char_count": 535,
    "text": "32.3 Penalties and Punishments\n\nA particular violation of ethics may span more than one of above-mentioned\nunethical practices. Without prejudice to and in addition to the rights of the\nprocuring entity to other penal provision as per the bid-documents or\nContract, If the Procuring Entity comes to a conclusion that a (prospective)\nbidder or contractor directly or through an agent has violated this Code of\nEthics in competing for the contract or in executing a contract, the Procuring\nEntity may take appropriate measures including:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0214",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 214,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 86650,
    "char_end": 86898,
    "char_count": 248,
    "text": "32.3.1  if his bids are under consideration in any procurement\n\n(i)     Rejection and exclusion of the bidder from the procurement process;\n(ii)    Calling   off  of  any  pre-contract  negotiations  and   forfeiture  or\nencashment of bid security;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0215",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 215,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 86900,
    "char_end": 87679,
    "char_count": 779,
    "text": "(iii)   Forfeiture or encashment of any other security or bond relating to the\nprocurement;\n(iv)   Cancellation of the relevant contract and recovery of compensation\nfor loss incurred by the procuring entity;\n(v)\nRecovery of payments made by the procuring entity along with interest\nthereon at prevailing rate;\n(vi)  Holiday Listing, Removal from the list of approved vendors and\nbanning/debarment of the bidder from participation in future\nprocurements of the procuring entity for a period not less than one\nyear;\n(vii)  In   case   of   Anti-competitive   practices,   information   for   further\nprocessing may be filed with the Competition Commission of India.\n(viii) Initiation of suitable disciplinary or criminal proceedings against any\nindividual staff found responsible.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0216",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 216,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 87681,
    "char_end": 88214,
    "char_count": 533,
    "text": "33. Resolution of disputes\n\nIn case of any dispute or difference or question arising out of or in connection\nwith or in relation to the contract or related documents, including, without\nlimitation, their existence, interpretation, performance, or termination (whether\nduring the course of supply or after its completion and whether before or after\nthe determination, abandonment or breach of contract), the Parties (the\nPURCHASER and the SELLER) shall endeavor to settle such disputes or\ndifferences amicably in the following manner:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0217",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 217,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 88216,
    "char_end": 89426,
    "char_count": 1210,
    "text": "33.1 Adjudication\n\nAfter exhausting efforts to resolve the Dispute with the Purchasing Officer\nexecuting the contract on behalf of the Procuring Entity, the contractor shall\ngive a ‘Notice of Adjudication’ specifying the matters which are in question,\nor subject of the dispute or difference indicating the relevant contractual\nclause, as also the amount of claim item-wise to Head of Procurement or\nany other authority mentioned in the contract (hereinafter called the\n“Adjudicator”) for invoking resolution of the dispute through Adjudication.\nDuring his adjudication, the Adjudicator shall give adequate opportunity to\nthe contractor to present his case. Within 60 days after receiving the\nrepresentation, the Adjudicator shall make and notify decisions in writing on\nall matters referred to him. The parties shall not initiate, during the\nadjudication proceedings, any conciliation or arbitral or judicial proceedings\nin respect of a dispute that is the subject matter of the adjudication\nproceedings. If not satisfied by the decision in adjudication, or if the\nadjudicator fails to notify his decision within the abovementioned time-frame,\nthe contractor may proceed to invoke the process of Conciliation.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0218",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 218,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 89428,
    "char_end": 89639,
    "char_count": 211,
    "text": "33.2 Conciliation through Expert Settlement Committee (ESC)\n\nIf the Parties fail to resolve their dispute or difference by Adjudication then\neither Party can send a notice invoking Conciliation through an Expert",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0219",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 219,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 89641,
    "char_end": 90012,
    "char_count": 371,
    "text": "Settlement Committee (ESC) to the other Party within 15 days from the date\nof failure to resolve the dispute. The date of the last meeting held in the\nprocess of Adjudication shall be taken as date of failure to resolve the\ndispute through mutual consultation. The other Party shall have to respond\nwithin 15 days from the date of receipt of notice invoking Conciliation.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0220",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 220,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 90014,
    "char_end": 90457,
    "char_count": 443,
    "text": "33.3 Arbitration\n\n(i)     If  the  Parties  fail  to  reach  an  amicable  settlement  through  the\nprocesses of Mutual Consultation and Conciliation through ESC, then\neither Party (the PURCHASER or the SELLER) may within thirty (30)\ndays of such failure give a written notice to the other Party requiring\nthat all matters in dispute or difference or in question be arbitrated\nupon in accordance with The Arbitration and Conciliation Act 1996.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0221",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 221,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 90458,
    "char_end": 90744,
    "char_count": 286,
    "text": "(ii)    Only the matters specified in such written notice which are in question\nor subject of dispute or difference, as also the amount of claim /\ncounter-claims, shall be referred to the arbitration and no other matter\nwhich has not been specified shall be referred to the arbitration.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0222",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 222,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 90745,
    "char_end": 91076,
    "char_count": 331,
    "text": "(iii)   The claims and counter claims raised by the Parties at the time of\ninvocation of the arbitration shall be final and binding on the Parties\nand no change shall be allowed in the same at any stage during\narbitration under any circumstances. Withdrawal of claims/counter\nclaims may however be done by the Parties at any stage.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0223",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 223,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 91077,
    "char_end": 91844,
    "char_count": 767,
    "text": "(iv)   The matters in dispute or difference or in question may be referred by\neither Party to a sole Arbitrator if the total value of the claim/counter-\nclaim is up to ₹50 lakh and to a panel of three Arbitrators if the total\nvalue of claim/counter-claim is more than ₹50 lakh. For this purpose,\nBRBNMPL shall maintain a panel of qualified and experienced\npersons who will function as Arbitrators.\n(v)\nAppointment of Sole Arbitrator: MD, BRBNMPL shall appoint the\nSole Arbitrator from its panel of Arbitrators with the written consent of\nthe other Party. The complexities of the dispute, the qualification and\nthe experience of the person shall be kept in view while making such\nappointment. The award of the sole Arbitrator shall be final and\nbinding on all parties.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0224",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 224,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 91845,
    "char_end": 92395,
    "char_count": 550,
    "text": "(vi)   Appointment of three Arbitrators: MD, BRBNMPL shall appoint an\nArbitrator from its panel of Arbitrators. The complexities of the dispute,\nthe qualification and the experience of the person shall be kept in view\nwhile making such appointment. Likewise, the other Party shall\nappoint its Arbitrator. The two Arbitrators so appointed shall appoint\nthe third Arbitrator, who will be the Presiding Arbitrator. The decision\nof the majority of the Arbitrators shall be the Award of the Arbitral\nTribunal and shall be final and binding on all parties.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0225",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 225,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 92396,
    "char_end": 92678,
    "char_count": 282,
    "text": "(vii)  The Arbitrator or Arbitrators appointed under this clause shall have\nthe power to extend the time to make the award with the consent of\nthe Parties as per the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996 as\namended till date. The fees of Arbitrator(s) and all other incidental cost",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0226",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 226,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 92680,
    "char_end": 93467,
    "char_count": 787,
    "text": "incurred during the arbitration proceedings shall be borne equally by\nthe parties.\n(viii) The arbitration proceeding shall be held in Bengaluru or any other\nplace in India as decided by the PURCHASER and shall be conducted\nin English language. All documentation to be reviewed by the\nArbitrators and / or submitted by the Parties shall be written or\ntranslated into English.\n(ix)   The Arbitration Proceedings shall be governed by The Arbitration and\nConciliation Act 1996, as amended from time to time including\nprovisions in force at the time the reference is made.\n(x)\nPending reference to arbitration, the Parties shall continue to perform\ntheir contractual obligations under the Agreement and disputes or\ndifferences or questions, if any, will finally be settled in the arbitration.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0227",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 227,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 93469,
    "char_end": 94045,
    "char_count": 576,
    "text": "34. Jurisdiction\n\nNotwithstanding any other Court or Courts having jurisdiction to decide the\nquestion(s) forming the subject matter of the reference, if the same had been the\nsubject matter of a suit, any and all actions and proceedings arising out of or\nrelating to the contract or any Award arising therefrom, shall lie only in the Court\nof competent civil jurisdiction in this behalf at Bengaluru/Kolkata and only the\nsaid Court(s) at Bengaluru/Kolkata shall have jurisdiction to entertain and take\nany such actions and/or proceedings to the exclusion of all other Courts.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0228",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 228,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 94047,
    "char_end": 94231,
    "char_count": 184,
    "text": "35. Governing Law\n\nThe Contract shall be governed in all respects by the by the laws of the Republic\nof India for the time being in force without application of the doctrine of Renvoi.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0229",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 229,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 94233,
    "char_end": 95431,
    "char_count": 1198,
    "text": "35. Secrecy\n\n35.1 If the Contract declares the subject matter of this Contract as coming under\nthe Official Secrets Act, 1923 or if the contract is marked as “Secret”, the\nContractor shall take all reasonable steps necessary to ensure that all\npersons employed in any work in connection with the contract, have full\nknowledge of the Official Secrets Act and any regulations framed\nthereunder.\n35.2. Any information obtained in the course of the execution of the contract by\nthe Contractor, his servants or agents or any person so employed, as to\nany matter whatsoever, which would or might be directly or indirectly, of use\nto any enemy of India, must be treated secret and shall not at any time be\ncommunicated to any person.\n35.3. Any breach of the aforesaid conditions shall entitle the Purchaser to cancel\nthe contract and to purchase or authorise the purchase of the stores at the\nrisk and cost of the Contractor, In the event of such cancellation, the stores\nor parts manufactured in the execution of the contract shall be taken by the\nPurchaser at such price as he considers fair and reasonable and the\ndecision of the Purchaser as to such price shall be final and binding on the\nContractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0230",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 230,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 95433,
    "char_end": 95568,
    "char_count": 135,
    "text": "Part II: Additional General Conditions of Contract for specific Types of\nTenders in addition / modification to clauses mentioned above:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0231",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 231,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 95570,
    "char_end": 95698,
    "char_count": 128,
    "text": "36. Disposal / Sale of Scrap by Tender\n\n36.1 During the currency of contract, no variation in price or rate shall be\nadmissible.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0232",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 232,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 95700,
    "char_end": 96003,
    "char_count": 303,
    "text": "36.2 Payment and Default\n\n36.2.1  Payment may be made in the form of Account Payee Demand Draft\ndrawn on any scheduled commercial bank in India in favour of\nBharatiya Reserve Bank Note Mudran Private Limited or through\nOnline Transfer or through other Electronic Mode of Payment as\nmentioned in the NIT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0233",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 233,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 96005,
    "char_end": 96201,
    "char_count": 196,
    "text": "36.2.2  No interest will be paid to the purchaser for the amounts paid or\ndeposited with the BRBNMPL and subsequently found refundable\nto the purchaser under any of the conditions of the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0234",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 234,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 96203,
    "char_end": 96799,
    "char_count": 596,
    "text": "36.2.3  If the purchaser fails to deposit sale value for a sold lot within the\nallowed period as per relevant clause BRBNMPL may forfeit the\nsecurity deposit. Requests for an extension of this period, made by\nthe purchaser may be considered by the BRBNMPL and may at its\ndiscretion, on the merits of the case, allow further time not\nexcluding 50 days from the date of the contract. Interest shall be\nleviable on such amount at a rate 2% per annum higher than the\nPLR of State Bank of India, from the date of expiry of the payment\ndate to actual date of payment (actual date of payment inclusive).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0235",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 235,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 96801,
    "char_end": 97166,
    "char_count": 365,
    "text": "36.2.4  The lot or lots in respect of which forfeiture has been made, shall\nbe deemed to have been abandoned by the purchaser to all intents\nand purposes and may be re-sold or otherwise disposed of at the\ndiscretion of the BRBNMPL without reference to the purchaser\nconcerned and without incurring any liability on part of BRBNMPL\nwhatsoever in respect there under.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0236",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 236,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 97168,
    "char_end": 97483,
    "char_count": 315,
    "text": "36.2.5  In case extension is granted by BRBNMPL and due to late payment\nof sale amount the delivery cannot be completed by the purchaser,\nin accordance with the relevant clause of Special Conditions of\nTender sale, then ground rent shall also be leviable as per relevant\nclause of Special Conditions of Tender sale.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0237",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 237,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 97485,
    "char_end": 97654,
    "char_count": 169,
    "text": "36.2.6 On production of proof of having made payment, nominated\nauthority shall issue a delivery order authorizing the purchaser to\ntake delivery of the Scrap Materials.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0238",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 238,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 97656,
    "char_end": 98020,
    "char_count": 364,
    "text": "36.3 Deliveries, Delays and Breach of Contact\n\n36.3.1  The Title of goods or material sold shall not be deemed to have\nbeen passed to the Purchaser / Bidder until and unless the full and\nfinal payment has been made by the purchaser, in accordance with\nthe contract to the BRBNMPL and the authorized Officer has issued\nthe Delivery Order in favour of the purchaser.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0239",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 239,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 98022,
    "char_end": 98193,
    "char_count": 171,
    "text": "The materials sold may be removed from the premises only on\nproduction of the cash receipt for the payment and a delivery order\nfrom the Officer authorized by the BRBNMPL.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0240",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 240,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 98195,
    "char_end": 98353,
    "char_count": 158,
    "text": "36.3.2 Unless specified otherwise in SIT, delivery period for lifting of\nmaterial shall be within 60 days from the date of finalization of\ncontract agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0241",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 241,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 98355,
    "char_end": 98612,
    "char_count": 257,
    "text": "36.3.3  The work of delivery will be supervised by Stock Holder or his\nauthorized representative, representative of accounts Department\nand Security Staff duly authorized by BRBNMPL for the propose of\ndelivery. Delivery will be allowed during working hours.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0242",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 242,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 98614,
    "char_end": 99218,
    "char_count": 604,
    "text": "36.3.4  No delivery of materials sold shall be given on Sundays, Gazetted\nholidays and other shall holidays observed by BRBNMPL. The\ndelivery of the goods or material shall be effected from the premises\nconcerned only during its normal working hours. In order to\ncomplete the delivery within the working hours all loading must\ncease half an hour before the normal closing time of the concerned\npremises. The decision of the BRBNMPL with regard to the working\nhour shall be final and binding on the purchaser. Purchaser will not\nbe allowed to lift the Scrap Material from more than one location at\na time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0243",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 243,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 99220,
    "char_end": 99582,
    "char_count": 362,
    "text": "36.3.5  The purchased stores will be carried away by the purchaser at his\nrisk and no claims against the BRBNMPL will be entertained for\nshortage in weight which may be discovered after the materials\nhave left the premises wherefrom delivery is taken. If required the\npurchaser shall provide his own bags, cases or other receptacles\nfor the removal of the scrap.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0244",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 244,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 99584,
    "char_end": 100063,
    "char_count": 479,
    "text": "36.3.6  The BRBNMPL shall not be responsible for any accident that may\noccur to purchaser's labours/servants for any reasons whatsoever.\nThe purchaser will himself have to ensure the safety of his workers\nand shall be liable to pay claims, whatsoever if any. BRBNMPL will\nnot carry any responsibility of such payments. The purchaser will\nbe responsible to supply personal protection equipment to his\nlabour/servant and staff and no additional charges are admissible\nfor the same.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0245",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 245,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 100065,
    "char_end": 100203,
    "char_count": 138,
    "text": "36.3.7  The materials sold, shall be removed by the purchaser within the\nperiod specified in relevant clause of Special Condition of Sale.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0246",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 246,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 100205,
    "char_end": 100526,
    "char_count": 321,
    "text": "36.3.8  If due to any default on the part of the BRBNMPL, the purchaser is\nunable to remove the materials sold within the specified period, the\nBRBNMPL may extend the period therefore and in such an event\npurchaser will be entitled to take delivery of the goods or the\nmaterials sold within such extended Delivery period.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0247",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 247,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 100528,
    "char_end": 100796,
    "char_count": 268,
    "text": "36.3.9  If contractor fails to lift sold scrap within the specified  period,\npenalty shall be levied at the rate of 0.5% per day of the value of\nun-removed Scrap. Moreover the material shall remain at the\npurchaser's risk until removal thereof. Further BRBNMPL will be",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0248",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 248,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 100798,
    "char_end": 101238,
    "char_count": 440,
    "text": "entitled to charge the ground rent as stated in relevant Para of SCC,\nfor the area in which the materials sold are kept or stored - which\nwould be recovered by the BRBNMPL from the Purchaser before\nremoval of the material and in the event of default in payment\nthereof, the BRBNMPL at may its discretion shall be entitled to\norder the re-sale of such materials and forfeit the Security deposit\nor sale amount or both, paid by the purchaser.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0249",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 249,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 101240,
    "char_end": 101659,
    "char_count": 419,
    "text": "36.3.10 If the purchaser makes slow progress with his contract and the\nBRBNMPL is of opinion that he may fail to fulfil the contract within\nthe time specified in the conditions of sale, it will be lawful for the\nBRBNMPL to cancel the whole contract or such portion thereof as\nmay not have been completed and the BRBNMPL shall be at liberty\nto dispose of the goods in any manner at the risk and expense of\nthe purchaser.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0250",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 250,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 101661,
    "char_end": 102377,
    "char_count": 716,
    "text": "36.3.11 The  purchaser  will  have  to  comply  with  the  provisions  of  the\nContract Labour (Regulations and Abolition Act 1970 and Central\nRules 1971 and obtain license from the Assistant Labour\nCommissioner or the competent authorities empowered to issue\nsuch license. Any failure on the part of the purchaser in this regard\nwill be at his risk and consequences. He shall comply with\nWorkman's Compensation Act 1923, Payment of Wages Act 1936,\nand Minimum Wages Act, 1948 and all the other related statutory\nand legal provisions and obligations, the purchaser shall also\nindemnity the BRBNMPL against any claim / liabilities that may\noccur to the contractor's labours and servants due to any reasons\nwhatsoever.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC064-0251",
    "doc_id": "DOC-064",
    "paragraph_index": 251,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 102379,
    "char_end": 102974,
    "char_count": 595,
    "text": "36.3.12 If  the  purchaser  makes  default  in  complying  with  any  of  the\ncondition of the contract, the sale of lot or lots in respect of which\nsuch default is made may be cancelled and such lot or lots may be\nput up again for sale and in such an event if a lower price is offered\nand accepted for such lot or lots then the purchaser shall be liable\nto pay the difference in price thereof together with all expenses\noccasioned by such resale in default to the BRBNMPL provided\nfurther that the purchaser in default shall not be entitled to claim\nany profit which may arise from such resale.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
