    "char_start": 20439,
    "char_end": 20988,
    "char_count": 549,
    "text": "2.9\nABNORMAL RATES\n\n2.9.1 The Tenderer is expected to quote rate for each item after careful analysis of cost\ninvolved for the performance of the completed item considering all specifications and\nConditions of Contract. In case, it is noticed that the rates quoted by the Tenderer for any\nitem are unusually higher or unusually lower, it will be sufficient cause for the rejection\nof the tender/bid unless the Employer is convinced about the reasonableness after\nscrutiny of the analysis for such rate(s) to be furnished by the Tenderer (on demand).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0093",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 93,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 20990,
    "char_end": 21115,
    "char_count": 125,
    "text": "2.9.2   In case of Abnormally High Rated (AHR) item(s), the same shall be dealt as per AHR\nclause in the SCC (as applicable).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
