    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0121",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 121,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 26680,
    "char_end": 26798,
    "char_count": 118,
    "text": "The Service Provider shall provide skilled / qualified /experienced personnel, if specified\nin the SCC /Scope of Work.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0122",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 122,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 26800,
    "char_end": 27059,
    "char_count": 259,
    "text": "While engaging the contractual manpower, Service Provider is required to make effort to\nprovide opportunity of employment to the people belonging to Scheduled Castes and\nweaker sections of society also in order to have a fair representation of these sections.",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0123",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 123,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 27061,
    "char_end": 27691,
    "char_count": 630,
    "text": "2.13  CONTRACT PERFORMANCE SECURITY (CPS)\n\n2.13.1 The Service Provider shall provide Contract Performance Security (CPS) to the Employer,\nwithin 30 days from the date of notification of award (i.e. FOA/Letter of Acceptance) or\nthe date specified in the notification of award whichever is earlier, for an amount\nmentioned therein. The CPS shall be returned/refunded three months after Contract\ncompletion period and Defects Liability Period (DLP), if any. All costs associated with\nCPS shall be borne by the Service Provider. No charges or interest shall be payable by\nthe Employer even if the CPS is in the form of a Demand Draft.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0124",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 124,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 27693,
    "char_end": 28370,
    "char_count": 677,
    "text": "2.13.2 The Service Provider shall furnish the CPS in the form of a Demand Draft or a Bank\nGuarantee or an irrevocable Letter of Credit from any Indian scheduled bank or a branch\nof an International bank situated in India and registered with Reserve Bank of India as\nscheduled foreign bank. However, for other than the Nationalized Indian Banks, the\nbanks whose BGs are furnished, must be commercial banks having net worth in excess of\nRs. 100 crores and a declaration to this effect should be made by such commercial bank\neither in the bank guarantee itself or separately on a letter head. The bank guarantee or\nthe Letter of Credit shall be submitted in the prescribed format.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0125",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 125,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 28372,
    "char_end": 28957,
    "char_count": 585,
    "text": "2.13.3 If the Service Provider or their employees /agents / representatives or Sub-Service\nProvider (if authorized by Employer) shall damage, break, deface or destroy any property\n/equipment belonging to the Employer or third party(ies) during the execution of this\nContract, the same shall be made good by the Service Provider at his own expenses and\nin default thereof, the EIC may cause the same to be made good by other agencies and\nrecover expenses plus 15% overhead from the Service Provider. The decision of EIC in\nthis matter shall be final and binding on the Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0126",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 126,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 28959,
    "char_end": 29389,
    "char_count": 430,
    "text": "2.13.4 All compensation, claim or other sums of money payable by the Service Provider to the\nEmployer under terms of this  Contract may be deducted from or paid by the encashment\nof a sufficient part of his Contract Performance Security or from any sums which may be\ndue or may become due to the Service Provider by the Employer on any account\nwhatsoever and in the event of his CPS being reduced by reasons of any such deductions",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0127",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 127,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 29391,
    "char_end": 29432,
    "char_count": 41,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0128",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 128,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 29434,
    "char_end": 29563,
    "char_count": 129,
    "text": "------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n14",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0129",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 129,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 29565,
    "char_end": 30036,
    "char_count": 471,
    "text": "or sale of aforesaid, the Service Provider shall within ten days thereafter make good in\nform of  bank draft(s)/BG/LC (as the case may be) as aforesaid any sum or sums which\nmay have been deducted from or realised by encashment of his CPS, or any part thereof.\nThe Service Provider shall pay to the Employer on demand without protest any balance\nremaining due. In this regard no interest shall be payable by the Employer to Service\nProvider for such sum deposited as CPS.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0130",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 130,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 30038,
    "char_end": 30556,
    "char_count": 518,
    "text": "2.13.5 The CPS deposit shall cover the entire Contract value including extra jobs/ services. As\nlong as the CPS submitted at the time of award take cares the extra jobs/ services\nexecuted and total executed value are within the awarded Contract price, there is no need\nfor additional CPS . As soon as the total executed value is likely to exceed the ceiling of\nawarded Contract Value, the Service Provider should furnish additional CPS through DD\nor submit amendment to existing BG/LC to effect the enhancement of CPS.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0131",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 131,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 30558,
    "char_end": 30795,
    "char_count": 237,
    "text": "2.13.6 Failure of the successful bidder to comply with the requirements of Clause 2.13 shall\nconstitute sufficient grounds for the annulment of the award, the forfeiture of CPS and\nany other actions or remedies available to the Employer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0132",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 132,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 30797,
    "char_end": 30880,
    "char_count": 83,
    "text": "2.14  FAILURE BY THE SERVICE PROVIDER TO COMPLY WITH THE\nPROVISIONS OF THE CONTRACT",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0133",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 133,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 30882,
    "char_end": 31312,
    "char_count": 430,
    "text": "2.14.1 If the Service Provider refuses or fails to provide the Service or any part thereof with such\ndiligence as will ensure its performance within the time specified in the Contract or\nextension thereof or fails to perform any of his obligation under the Contract or in any\nmanner commits a breach of any of the provisions of the Contract it shall be open to the\nEmployer at its option by written notice to the Service Provider:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0134",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 134,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 31314,
    "char_end": 32207,
    "char_count": 893,
    "text": "a)\nTO DETERMINE THE CONTRACT in which event the Contract shall stand\nterminated and shall cease to be in force and effect on and from the date\nappointed by the Employer on that behalf, whereupon the Service Provider shall\nstop forthwith any of the Service then in progress, except such Service as the\nEmployer may, in writing, require to be done to safeguard any property or work\nor installations from damage, and the Employer, for its part, may take over the\nService remaining unfinished by the Service Provider and complete the same\nthrough another service provider or by other means, at the risk and cost of the\nService Provider, and any of his sureties if any, shall be liable to the Employer for\nany excess cost occasioned by such service having to be so taken over and\nobtained by the Employer over and above the cost at the rates specified in the\nschedule of quantities and rate/prices.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0135",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 135,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 32209,
    "char_end": 32689,
    "char_count": 480,
    "text": "b)\nWITHOUT DETERMINING THE Contract to take over the Service of the\nService Provider or any part thereof and complete the same through other service\nprovider or by other means at the risk and cost of the Service Provider. The\nService Provider and any of his sureties are liable to the Employer for any excess\ncost over and above the cost at the rates specified in the Schedule of Quantities/\nrates, occasioned by such services having been taken over and completed by the\nEmployer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0136",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 136,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 32691,
    "char_end": 32732,
    "char_count": 41,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0137",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 137,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 32734,
    "char_end": 32863,
    "char_count": 129,
    "text": "------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n15",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0138",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 138,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 32865,
    "char_end": 32957,
    "char_count": 92,
    "text": "2.14.2  In such events of Clause 2.14.1(a) or (b) above, the following shall be applicable:-",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0139",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 139,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 32959,
    "char_end": 33585,
    "char_count": 626,
    "text": "a)\nThe whole or part of the Contract Performance Security furnished by the Service\nProvider is liable to be forfeited without prejudice to the right of the Employer to\nrecover from the Service Provider the excess cost referred to in the sub-clause\naforesaid. The Employer shall also have the right of taking possession and\nutilising in completing the services or any part thereof, such as materials,\nequipment and plants available at service site belonging to the Service Provider as\nmay be necessary and the Service Provider shall not be entitled for any\ncompensation for use or damage to such materials, equipment and plant.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0140",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 140,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 33587,
    "char_end": 34280,
    "char_count": 693,
    "text": "b)\nThe amount that may have become due to the Service Provider on account of\nservice already executed by him shall not be payable to him until after the expiry\nof Six (6) calendar months reckoned from the date of termination of Contract or\nfrom the taking over of the Service or part thereof by the Employer as the case\nmay be, during which period the responsibility for faulty material or workmanship\nin respect of such service shall, under the Contract, rest exclusively with the\nService Provider. This amount shall be subject to deduction of any amounts due\nfrom the Contract to the Employer under the terms of the Contract authorised or\nrequired to be reserved or retained by the Employer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0141",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 141,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 34282,
    "char_end": 34663,
    "char_count": 381,
    "text": "2.14.3 Before taking any action as per Clause 2.14.1(a) or (b) if in the judgment of the Employer,\nthe default or defaults committed by the Service Provider is/are curable and can be cured\nby the Service Provider if an opportunity given to him, then the Employer may issue\nNotice in writing calling the Service Provider to cure the default within such time\nspecified in the Notice.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0142",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 142,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 34665,
    "char_end": 35330,
    "char_count": 665,
    "text": "2.14.4 The Employer shall also have the right to proceed or take action as per 2.14.1(a) or (b)\nabove, in the event that the Service Provider becomes bankrupt, insolvent, compounds\nwith his creditors, assigns the Contract in favour of his creditors or any other person(s) or\nbeing a company or a corporation goes into voluntary liquidation, provided that in the\nsaid events it shall not be necessary for the Employer to give any prior notice to the\nService Provider.\n2.14.5 Termination of the Contract as provided for in sub- clause 2.14.1(a) above shall not\nprejudice or affect their rights of the Employer which may have accrued upto the date of\nsuch termination.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0143",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 143,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 35332,
    "char_end": 35427,
    "char_count": 95,
    "text": "2.15  SERVICE PROVIDER REMAINS LIABLE TO PAY COMPENSATION IF\nACTION NOT TAKEN UNDER CLAUSE 2.14",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0144",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 144,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 35429,
    "char_end": 35875,
    "char_count": 446,
    "text": "2.15.1 If in any case in which any of the powers conferred upon the Employer by clause 2.14\nthereof shall have become exercisable and the same had not been exercised, the non-\nexercise thereof shall not constitute a waiver of any of the conditions hereof and such\npowers shall notwithstanding be exercisable in the event of any further case of default by\nthe Service Provider for which by any clause or clauses hereof he is declared liable to pay",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0145",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 145,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 35877,
    "char_end": 35918,
    "char_count": 41,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0146",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 146,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 35920,
    "char_end": 36049,
    "char_count": 129,
    "text": "------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n16",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0147",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 147,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 36051,
    "char_end": 37046,
    "char_count": 995,
    "text": "compensation amounting to the whole of his Contract Performance Security, and the\nliability of the Service Provider for past and future compensation shall remain unaffected.\nIn the event of the Employer putting in force the power under above sub-clause 2.14 (a)\nor 2.14 (b) vested in him under the preceding clause he may, if he so desired, take\npossession of all or any tools and plants, materials and stores at the site thereof belonging\nto the Service Provider or procured by him and intended to be used for the execution of\nthe Service or any part thereof paying or allowing for the same in account at the Contract\nrates or in case of these not being applicable, at current market rates to be certified by the\nEIC whose certificate thereof shall be final, otherwise the EIC may give notice in writing\nto the Service Provider or Service Provider‟s Representatives requiring him to remove\nsuch tools, plant, materials or stores from the premises (within a time to be specified in\nsuch notice).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0148",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 148,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 37048,
    "char_end": 38210,
    "char_count": 1162,
    "text": "Failure of any action by the Service Provider for removal of material/tools/plant/store etc.\nwithin the period mentioned in notice of EIC, the Employer shall also be entitled to\nrecover handling and storage charges @5% of the estimated value of material\ntools/plant/store for each month or part of a month without relieving the Servicer\nProvider from any other related liability. In the event of the Service Provider‟s failure  to\nremove the same within a  period of 6 months or as decided by the EIC,  the EIC may\ntake action for removal  through auction or private sale on behalf of the Service Provider\nand at his risk in all respects. The Service Provider shall be liable to pay the Employer the\nhandling & storage charges per month or a part of the month from the date of serving the\nnotice by the EIC to the date of removal of the materials by the Employer plus overhead\ncharges @ 15% of sale value of such materials. In case of negative or zero sale value, the\noverhead charges shall be applicable on the handling & storage charges. The decision of\nEIC w.r.t. such removal and the amount of the proceeds shall be final and binding on the\nService Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0149",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 149,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 38212,
    "char_end": 38921,
    "char_count": 709,
    "text": "2.16  CHANGE IN CONSTITUTION\n\n2.16.1 Where the Service Provider is a partnership firm, the prior approval of the Employer shall\nbe obtained in writing, before any change is made in the constitution of the firm. Where\nthe Service Provider is an individual or a Hindu undivided family business concern, such\napproval as aforesaid shall, likewise be obtained before such Service Provider enters into\nany agreement with other parties, where under, the reconstituted firm would have the\nright to carry out the service hereby undertaken by the Service Provider. In either case if\nprior approval as aforesaid is not obtained, the Contract shall be deemed to have been\nallotted in contravention of clause 2.23 hereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0150",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 150,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 38923,
    "char_end": 39355,
    "char_count": 432,
    "text": "2.17  TERMINATION OF CONTRACT\n\n2.17.1 TERMINATION OF CONTRACT FOR DEATH\n\nIf the Service Provider is an individual or a proprietary concern and the individual or the\nproprietor dies or if the Service Provider is a partnership concern and one of the partner\ndies then unless, the Employer is satisfied that the legal representative of the individual or\nthe proprietary concern or the surviving partners are capable of carrying out and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0151",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 151,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 39357,
    "char_end": 39398,
    "char_count": 41,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0152",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 152,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 39400,
    "char_end": 39529,
    "char_count": 129,
    "text": "------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n17",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0153",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 153,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 39531,
    "char_end": 40157,
    "char_count": 626,
    "text": "completing Contract, the Employer is entitled to cancel the Contract for the uncompleted\npart without being in any way liable for any compensation payment to the estate of the\ndeceased  Service Provider and/or to the surviving partners of the Service Provider's firm\non account of the cancellation of Contract. The decision of the Employer/EIC in such\nassessment shall be final & binding on the parties. In the event of such cancellation, the\nEmployer shall not hold the estate of the deceased Service Provider and/or the surviving\npartners of Service Provider's firm liable for any damages for non-completion of the\nContract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0154",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 154,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 40159,
    "char_end": 41057,
    "char_count": 898,
    "text": "2.17.2 TERMINATION OF CONTRACT IN CASE OF LIQUIDATION / BANKRUPTCY,\nETC\n\nIf the Service Provider shall dissolve or become bankrupt or insolvent or cause or suffer\nany receiver to be appointed of his business of any assets thereof compound with his\nCreditors, or being a corporation commence to be wound up, not being a member's\nvoluntary winding up for the purpose of amalgamation or reconstruction, or carry on its\nbusiness under a Receiver for the benefits of its Creditors any of them, Employer shall be\nat liberty to terminate the Contract forthwith upon coming to know of the happening of\nany such event as aforesaid by notice in writing to the Service Provider or to give the\nReceiver or Liquidator or other person, the option of carrying out the Contract subject to\nhis providing a guarantee up to an amount to be agreed upon by the Employer for due and\nfaithful performance of the Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0155",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 155,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 41059,
    "char_end": 41166,
    "char_count": 107,
    "text": "2.17.3 TERMINATION\nOF\nCONTRACT\nFOR\nCORRUPT\n/\nFRADULENT\n/\nCOLLUSIVE / COERCIVE PRACTICES AND NON-PERFORMANCE",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0156",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 156,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 41168,
    "char_end": 41485,
    "char_count": 317,
    "text": "If the Bidder/Service Provider is found to have indulged in Corrupt/ Fraudulent\n/Collusive/Coercive practices, the Contract shall be terminated and the Bidder/ Service\nProvider shall be banned for future business with BCPL. The detailed procedure for\nbanning including suspension is elaborated in the tender document.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0157",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 157,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 41487,
    "char_end": 41900,
    "char_count": 413,
    "text": "Due to non-performance of the Service Provider leading to termination of the Contract,\nthe Service Provider initially shall be put on suspension list and thereafter on holiday list\nof Employer for a period mentioned in the detailed procedure, to be reckoned from the\ndate of communication by Owner/Employer. The detailed procedure for evaluation of\nperformance in this regard is elaborated in the tender document.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0158",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 158,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 41902,
    "char_end": 42257,
    "char_count": 355,
    "text": "2.17.4 TERMINATION FOR CONVENIENCE\n\nNotwithstanding anything contained in the Contract, the Employer may, by 30 (Thirty)\ndays written notice, terminate the Contract in whole or in part. In addition to the payment\nmentioned at clause 2.18, the Service Provider shall be compensated for de-mobilization\nand other costs incurred at mutually negotiated terms.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0159",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 159,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 42259,
    "char_end": 42436,
    "char_count": 177,
    "text": "In case of such termination, the obligation of the Employer to pay, shall be limited to the\nextent of work/job completed by the Service Provider as per provision of the Contract",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0160",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 160,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 42438,
    "char_end": 42479,
    "char_count": 41,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0161",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 161,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 42481,
    "char_end": 42610,
    "char_count": 129,
    "text": "------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n18",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0162",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 162,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 42612,
    "char_end": 42717,
    "char_count": 105,
    "text": "upto the date of termination, subject to the Service Provider complying with other terms\nof the Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0163",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 163,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 42719,
    "char_end": 42916,
    "char_count": 197,
    "text": "Notwithstanding the termination of the Contract, the parties shall continue to be bound by\nthe provisions of this Contract that reasonably require some action or forbearance after\nsuch termination.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0164",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 164,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 42918,
    "char_end": 43461,
    "char_count": 543,
    "text": "2.18\nAMOUNT PAYABLE IN CASE OF TERMINATION\n\n2.18.1 In all cases of termination herein set forth, the obligation of the Employer to pay, shall be\nlimited to the extent of service rendered by Service Provider as per provision of the\nContract upto the date of termination, subject to the Service Provider complying with\nother terms of the Contract. Notwithstanding the termination of the Contract, the parties\nshall continue to be bound by the provisions of this Contract that reasonably require some\naction or forbearance after such termination.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0165",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 165,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 43463,
    "char_end": 43828,
    "char_count": 365,
    "text": "2.19  MEMBERS OF THE EMPLOYER NOT INDIVIDUALLY LIABLE\n\n2.19.1 No Director, or official or employee of the Employer shall in any way be personally\nbound or liable for the acts or obligations of the Employer under the Contract or\nanswerable for any default or omission in the observance or performance of any of the\nacts, matters or things which are herein contained.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0166",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 166,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 43830,
    "char_end": 44173,
    "char_count": 343,
    "text": "2.20  EMPLOYER NOT BOUND BY PERSONAL REPRESENTATIONS\n\n2.20.1 The Service Provider shall not be entitled to any increase on the scheduled rates or any\nother right or claim whatsoever by reason of any representation, explanation statement or\nalleged representation, promise or guarantees given or alleged to have been given to him\nby any person.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0167",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 167,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 44175,
    "char_end": 44620,
    "char_count": 445,
    "text": "2.21  FORCE MAJEURE\n\n2.21.1  In the event of either party being rendered unable by Force Majeure to perform any\nobligations required to be performed by them under the Contract the relative obligation of\nthe party affected by such Force Majeure shall upon notification to the other party be\nsuspended for the period during which Force Majeures event lasts. The cost and loss\nsustained by the either party shall be borne by the respective parties.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0168",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 168,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 44622,
    "char_end": 45112,
    "char_count": 490,
    "text": "The term \"Force Majeures\" as employed herein shall include:\n\n(a)\nact of terrorism;\n(b)\nriot, war, invasion, act of foreign enemies, hostilities (whether war be declared or\nnot), civil war, rebellion, revolution, insurrection of military or usurped power;\n(c)\nionising radiation or contamination, radio activity from any nuclear fuel or from\nany nuclear waste from the combustion of nuclear fuel, radioactive toxic\nexplosive or other hazardous properties of any explosive assembly or nuclear",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0169",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 169,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 45114,
    "char_end": 45155,
    "char_count": 41,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0170",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 170,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 45157,
    "char_end": 45286,
    "char_count": 129,
    "text": "------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n19",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0171",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 171,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 45288,
    "char_end": 46018,
    "char_count": 730,
    "text": "component;\n(d)\nepidemics, earthquakes, flood, fire, hurricanes, typhoons or other physical natural\ndisaster, but excluding weather conditions regardless of severity; and\n(e)\nfreight embargoes, strikes at national or state-wide level or industrial disputes at a\nnational or state-wide level in any country where Works/Services are performed,\nand which affect an essential portion of the Works/Services but excluding any\nindustrial dispute which is specific to the performance of the Works/Services or\nthe Contract.\nFor the avoidance of doubt, inclement weather, third party breach, delay in supply of\nmaterials (other than due to a nationwide transporters‟ strike) or commercial hardship\nshall not constitute a Force Majeure event.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0172",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 172,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 46020,
    "char_end": 46439,
    "char_count": 419,
    "text": "2.21.2  Notification of Force Majeure\n\nThe affected party shall notify within 10 (ten) days of becoming aware of or the date it\nought to have become aware of the occurrence of an event of Force Majeure giving full\nparticulars of the event of Force Majeure and the reasons for the event of Force Majeure\npreventing the affected party from, or delaying the affected party in performing its\nobligations under the Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0173",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 173,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 46441,
    "char_end": 47012,
    "char_count": 571,
    "text": "2.21.3  Right of either party to terminate\n\nIf an event of Force Majeure occurs and its effect continues for a period of 180 (one\nhundred eighty) days or more in a continuous period of 365 (three hundred sixty five)\ndays after notice has been given under this clause, either party may terminate the\nContract by issuing a written notice of 30 (thirty) days to the other party.\nFurther, the Service Provider shall with all reasonable diligence remove from the Site all\nthe Service Provider's equipment and shall give similar facilities to his Sub Service\nProvider to do so.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0174",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 174,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 47014,
    "char_end": 47284,
    "char_count": 270,
    "text": "2.21.4  Payment in case of termination due to Force Majeure\n\nThe Contract Price attributable to the Works/Services performed till the date of the\ncommencement of the relevant event of Force Majeure with effective recovery/ retention\nshall be payable to Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0175",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 175,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 47286,
    "char_end": 47360,
    "char_count": 74,
    "text": "The Service Provider has no entitlement and Employer has no liability for:",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0176",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 176,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 47362,
    "char_end": 47494,
    "char_count": 132,
    "text": "a)\nany costs, losses, expenses, damages or the payment of any part of the Total\nContract Price during an event of Force Majeure; and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0177",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 177,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 47496,
    "char_end": 47592,
    "char_count": 96,
    "text": "b)\nany delay costs in any way incurred by the Service Provider due to an event of\nForce Majeure.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0178",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 178,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 47594,
    "char_end": 47747,
    "char_count": 153,
    "text": "2.21.5 Time for performance of the relative obligation suspended by the Force Majeure shall\nthen stand extended by the period for which such cause lasts.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0179",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 179,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 47749,
    "char_end": 47790,
    "char_count": 41,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0180",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 180,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 47792,
    "char_end": 47921,
    "char_count": 129,
    "text": "------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n20",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0181",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 181,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 47923,
    "char_end": 48843,
    "char_count": 920,
    "text": "2.21.6 Outbreak of War:\n\nIf during the currency of the Contract there shall be an out break of war whether declared\nor not, in that part of the World which whether financially or otherwise materially affect\nthe execution of the Work, the Service Provider shall unless and until the Contract is\nterminated under the provisions in this clause continue to use his best endeavour to\ncomplete the execution of the Work/Services, provided always that the Employer shall be\nentitled, at any time after such out break of war to terminate or re-negotiate the Contract\nby giving notice in writing to the Service Provider and upon such notice being given the\nContract shall, save as to the rights of the parties under this clause and to the operation of\nthe clauses entitled settlement of Disputes and Arbitration hereof, be terminated but\nwithout prejudice to the right of either party in respect of any antecedent breach thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0182",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 182,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 48845,
    "char_end": 49519,
    "char_count": 674,
    "text": "2.22  PRICE REDUCTION SCHEDULE\n\n2.22.1 Time is the essence of the Contract. In case the Service Provider fails to mobilize / deploy\nthe required manpower and the complete equipments so as to commence the Services\nwithin Mobilisation Period and complete the Services within the stipulated period, then,\nunless such failure is due to Force Majeure as defined in Clause 2.21 herein above or due\nto Employer's defaults, the total Value of Contract shall be reduced by ½ (half) % of the\ntotal Value of Contract per complete week of delay or part thereof subject to a maximum\nof 5 (five) % of the total Value of Contract, by way of reduction in price for delay and not\nas penalty.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0183",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 183,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 49521,
    "char_end": 49685,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "The Employer shall be at liberty to adjust or deduct the said amount from amount due to\nthe Service Provider / it‟s Contract Performance Security payable on demand.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0184",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 184,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 49687,
    "char_end": 49820,
    "char_count": 133,
    "text": "The decision of the EIC with respect to applicability of Price Reduction Schedule shall be\nfinal and binding on the Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0185",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 185,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 49822,
    "char_end": 50182,
    "char_count": 360,
    "text": "2.22.2 The parties agree that this is a genuine pre-estimate of the loss/damage which will be\nsuffered by the Employer on account of delay on the part of the Service Provider and the\nsaid amount will be adjusted for the amount payable to the Service Provider, without\nthere being any proof of the actual loss or damages having been caused by such\ndelay/breach.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0186",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 186,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 50184,
    "char_end": 50418,
    "char_count": 234,
    "text": "2.22.3 The Price Reduction will be calculated on the basis of total Value of Contract / executed\nValue of Contract (as the case may be) excluding taxes and duties where such taxes and\nduties have been shown separately in the Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0187",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 187,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 50420,
    "char_end": 50734,
    "char_count": 314,
    "text": "2.22.4 As mentioned above, in case of delay in execution of Contract, Service Provider will\nraise invoice for reduced value as per Price Reduction Clause. If Service Provider has\nraised the invoice for full value, then Service Provider will issue Credit Note towards the\napplicable Price Reduction Schedule amount.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0188",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 188,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 50736,
    "char_end": 50959,
    "char_count": 223,
    "text": "In case Service Provider fails to submit the invoice for reduced value or does not issue\ncredit note as mentioned above, BCPL will release the payment to Service Provider after\neffecting the Price Reduction Schedule clause.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0189",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 189,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 50961,
    "char_end": 51002,
    "char_count": 41,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0190",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 190,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 51004,
    "char_end": 51133,
    "char_count": 129,
    "text": "------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n21",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0191",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 191,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 51135,
    "char_end": 51328,
    "char_count": 193,
    "text": "In the event any financial implication arises on BCPL due to issuance of invoice without\nreduction in price or non-issuance of Credit Note, the same shall be to the account of\nService Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0192",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 192,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 51330,
    "char_end": 51743,
    "char_count": 413,
    "text": "2.23\nASSIGNMENT/SUBLET\n\n2.23.1 The Service Provider shall not, save with previous written consent  of the Engineer-in-\ncharge, sublet, transfer or assign the Contract or any part thereof or interest therein or\nbenefit or advantage thereof in any manner whatsoever. Provided, nevertheless, that any\nsuch consent shall not relieve the Service Provider from any obligation, duty or\nresponsibility under the Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0193",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 193,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 51745,
    "char_end": 52215,
    "char_count": 470,
    "text": "2.23.2 The basic scope of Services cannot be sublet. However, on specific request of the Service\nProvider and subject to written consent of Employer, the Service Provider may sublet\nallied/incidental jobs related to the Services. Such consent shall not relieve the Service\nProvider from any obligation, duty or responsibility under the Contract and Service\nProvider shall be fully responsible for the Services hereunder and the execution and\nperformance of the Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0194",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 194,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 52217,
    "char_end": 52363,
    "char_count": 146,
    "text": "2.23.3 Sub-letting of whole Contract is prohibited. An undertaking to this effect will be given by\nService Provider along with each invoice/ bill.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0195",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 195,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 52365,
    "char_end": 53173,
    "char_count": 808,
    "text": "2.24\nLIENS\n\n2.24.1 If, at any time there should be evidence of any lien or claim for which the Employer might\nhave become liable and which is chargeable to the Service Provider, the Employer shall\nhave the right to retain out of any payment then due or thereafter to become due an\namount sufficient to completely indemnify the Employer against such lien or claim and if\nsuch lien or claim be valid, the Employer may pay and discharge the same and deduct the\namount so paid from any money which may be or may become due and payable to the\nService Provider. If any lien or claim remain unsettled after all payments are made, the\nService Provider shall refund or pay to the Employer all money that the latter may be\ncompelled to pay in discharging such lien or claim including all costs and reasonable\nexpenses.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0196",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 196,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 53175,
    "char_end": 53325,
    "char_count": 150,
    "text": "2.24.2 The Employer shall have lien on all materials, equipments including those brought by the\nService Provider for the purpose of providing service.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0197",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 197,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 53327,
    "char_end": 53889,
    "char_count": 562,
    "text": "2.24.3 The final payment shall not become due until the Service Provider delivers to the EIC a\ncomplete release or waiver of all liens arising or which may arise out of his agreement or\nreceipt in full or certification by the Service Provider in a form approved by EIC that all\ninvoices for labour, materials, services have been paid in lien thereof and if required by\nthe EIC in any case an affidavit that so far as the Service Provider has knowledge or\ninformation the releases and receipts include all the labour and material for which a lien\ncould be filled.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0198",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 198,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 53891,
    "char_end": 53981,
    "char_count": 90,
    "text": "2.24.4 Service Provider will indemnify and hold the Employer harmless, for a period of two",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0199",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 199,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 53983,
    "char_end": 54024,
    "char_count": 41,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0200",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 200,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 54026,
    "char_end": 54155,
    "char_count": 129,
    "text": "------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n22",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0201",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 201,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 54157,
    "char_end": 54952,
    "char_count": 795,
    "text": "years after the issue of Completion/Execution Certificate, from all liens and other\nencumbrances against the Employer on account of debts or claims alleged to be due from\nthe Service Provider or his Sub-Service Provider to any person and on behalf of\nEmployer, the Service Provider will defend at his own expense, any claim or litigation\nbrought against the Employer or the Service Provider including Sub-Service Provider in\nconnection therewith. Service Provider shall defend or contest at his own expense, any\nfresh claim or litigation against the Employer by any person including his Sub-Service\nProvider, till its satisfactory settlement even after the expiry of two years from the date of\nissue of Completion/Execution Certificate.\n2.25   DELAYS BY EMPLOYER OR HIS AUTHORISED REPRESENTATIVE",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0202",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 202,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 54954,
    "char_end": 55329,
    "char_count": 375,
    "text": "2.25.1 In case the Service Provider's performance is delayed due to any act or omission on the\npart of the Employer or his authorized Representative, then the Service Provider shall be\ngiven due extension of time for the completion of the Service, to the extent such omission\non the part of the Employer has caused delay in the Service Provider's performance of his\nServices.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0203",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 203,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 55331,
    "char_end": 55825,
    "char_count": 494,
    "text": "2.25.2 No adjustment in Contract Price shall be allowed for reasons of such delays and\nextensions granted except as provided in Tender Document, where the Employer reserves\nthe right to seek indulgence of Service Provider to maintain the agreed Time Schedule of\nCompletion. In such an event the Service Provider shall be obliged to provide Service for\nadditional time beyond stipulated time including Off-days / Holidays or by enhancing\nresources to achieve the completion date/interim targets.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0204",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 204,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 55827,
    "char_end": 56051,
    "char_count": 224,
    "text": "2.26  NO WAIVER OF RIGHTS\n\n2.26.1  None of the terms and conditions of this Contract shall be deemed waived by either party\nunless such waiver is executed in writing by the duly authorized representative of both\nthe parties.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0205",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 205,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 56053,
    "char_end": 56136,
    "char_count": 83,
    "text": "2.27  CERTIFICATE NOT TO AFFECT RIGHT OF EMPLOYER AND LIABILITY\nOF SERVICE PROVIDER",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0206",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 206,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 56138,
    "char_end": 56926,
    "char_count": 788,
    "text": "2.27.1 No interim payment certificate(s) issued by the EIC of the Employer, nor any sum paid\non account by the Employer, nor any extension of time for execution of the service\ngranted by Employer shall affect or prejudice the rights of the Employer against the\nService Provider or relieve the Service Provider of his obligations for the due\nperformance of the Contract, or be interpreted as approval of the Service done and no\ncertificate shall create liability for the Employer to pay for alterations, amendments,\nvariations or additional services not ordered, in writing, by Employer or discharge the\nliability of the Service Provider for the payment of damages whether due, ascertained, or\ncertified or not or any sum against the payment of which he is bound to indemnify the\nEmployer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0207",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 207,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 56928,
    "char_end": 57050,
    "char_count": 122,
    "text": "2.28  LANGUAGE AND MEASURES\n\n2.28.1 All documents pertaining to the Contract including Specifications, Schedules, Notices,",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0208",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
