  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0302",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 302,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 88466,
    "char_end": 88844,
    "char_count": 378,
    "text": "respect to the operations conducted hereunder, shall be endorsed by the underwriter in\naccordance with the following policy wording:“ The insurers hereby waive their rights of\nsubrogation against any individual, Employer, affiliates or assignees for whom or with\nwhom the assured may be operating to the extent of the Contractual indemnities\nundertaken by the Service Provider”.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0303",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 303,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 88846,
    "char_end": 89060,
    "char_count": 214,
    "text": "4.5.10 Deductible: That portion of any loss not covered by insurance provided for in this article\nsolely by reason of deductible provision in such insurance policies shall be to the account\nof the Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0304",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 304,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 89062,
    "char_end": 90608,
    "char_count": 1546,
    "text": "4.6\nTAXES AND DUTIES\n\n4.6.1 The Service Provider, unless specified otherwise elsewhere in the Contract agrees to and\ndoes hereby accept full and exclusive liability for the payment of any and all Taxes,\nDuties, including GST now or hereafter imposed, increased, modified from time to time\nin respect of Services and materials and all contributions and taxes for unemployment\ncompensation, insurance and old age pensions or annuities now or hereafter imposed by\nany Central or State Government authorities which are imposed with respect to or\ncovered by the wages, salaries, or other compensations paid to the persons employed by\nthe Service Provider and the Service Provider shall be responsible for the compliance of\nall Sub-Service Providers, with all applicable Central, State,  Municipal and local law and\nregulation and requirement of any Central, State or local Government agency or\nauthority. Service Provider further agrees to defend, indemnify and hold Employer\nharmless from any liability or penalty which may be imposed by the Central, State or\nLocal authorities by reason or any violation by Service Provider or Sub- Sub-Service\nProvider of such laws, suits or proceedings that may be brought against the Employer\narising under, growing out of, or by reason of the service provided for by this Contract,\nby third parties, or by Central or State Government authority or any administrative sub-\ndivision thereof. Tax deductions will be made as per the rules and regulations in force in\naccordance with acts prevailing from time to time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0305",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 305,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 90610,
    "char_end": 90827,
    "char_count": 217,
    "text": "4.6.2 Service Provider shall ensure timely submission of correct invoice(s) with all required\nsupporting document(s) as per Contract within a period specified in Contracts to enable\nEmployer to avail Input Tax Credit.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0306",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 306,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 90829,
    "char_end": 91231,
    "char_count": 402,
    "text": "If Input Tax credit with respect to GST is not available to Employer for any reason which\nis not attributable to Employer, then Employer shall not be obligated or liable to pay or\nreimburse GST charged in the invoice(s)  and shall be entitled to / deduct/ setoff /recover\nthe such GST together with all penalties and interest if any, against any amounts paid or\npayable by Employer to Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0307",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 307,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 91233,
    "char_end": 91753,
    "char_count": 520,
    "text": "4.6.3 Where Employer has the obligation to discharge tax liability under reverse charge\nmechanism and Employer has paid or is /liable to pay GST to the Government on which\ninterest or penalties becomes payable as per rules (as amended from time to time) for any\nreason which  is not  attributable to Employer or Input Tax credit with respect to such\npayments  is  not available to Employer for any reason which  is not  attributable to\nEmployer, then Employer shall be entitled to  deduct/ setoff / recover such  amounts",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0308",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 308,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 91755,
    "char_end": 91796,
    "char_count": 41,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0309",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 309,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 91798,
    "char_end": 91927,
    "char_count": 129,
    "text": "------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n35",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0310",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 310,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 91929,
    "char_end": 92013,
    "char_count": 84,
    "text": "against any amounts paid or payable by Employer to Service Provider.\n\n4.7\nINCOME TAX",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0311",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 311,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 92015,
    "char_end": 93021,
    "char_count": 1006,
    "text": "4.7.1  Income Tax deduction shall be made from all payments of the Service Provider as per\nrules and regulation in force in accordance with the Income Tax Act prevailing from time\nto time. As per the provisions of the income Tax Act, 1961, Permanent Account No.\n(PAN) is compulsorily required to be mentioned in Tax Deduction at Source (TDS)\ncertificate issued to the payee. Therefore, the bidder must submit the details of PAN / the\ncopy of application filed for allotment of PAN (if PAN no. not available) to EIC\nimmediately on receipt of FOA/Contract Document, failing which, TDS will be applied\nas per applicable law and TDS certificate will not be issued. Therefore, in case the\nService Provider does not furnish PAN, EMPLOYER shall deduct at source as provided\nin the Income Tax Act 1961, or in the relevant Finance Act, or as directed in the orders\nu/s 195(3) or 197 or 195(2), as the case may be, or at such higher rate as may be required\nby Section 206AA of Income Tax Act 1961, from time to time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0312",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 312,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 93023,
    "char_end": 93716,
    "char_count": 693,
    "text": "4.7.2  In case of foreign bidder, the Service Provider must apply through the local embassy /\nconsulate of India for obtaining PAN card. In case, foreign Service Provider don‟t have\nthe PAN, then amount will be deducted and deposited as per law and TDS certificate will\nalso not be provided. Further, such Service Provider shall comply all other provisions\nmentioned elsewhere in the Tender Document related to making remittances to non-\nresidents including Permanent Establishment, Tax Residency Certificate (TRC) if non-\nresident desire to avail benefits available under Double Tax Avoidance Agreement\n(DTAA), Withholding Tax etc., as per Income Tax Act, 1961 (as amended from time to\ntime).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0313",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 313,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 93718,
    "char_end": 94371,
    "char_count": 653,
    "text": "4.8\nSTATUTORY VARIATIONS\n\n4.8.1  All duties, taxes (except where otherwise expressly provided in the Contract) as may be\nlevied / imposed in consequences of execution of the Jobs/Services or in relation thereto\nor in connection therewith as per the Acts, Laws, Rules, Regulations in force on the due\ndate of submission of Bid for this Contract shall be to Service Provider‟s account. Any\nincrease / decrease in such duties, taxes after the due date of submission of bid but within\nthe Contractual completion date as stipulated in the Contract will be to the account of\nEmployer subject to submission of documentary proof to the satisfaction of Employer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0314",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 314,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 94373,
    "char_end": 95114,
    "char_count": 741,
    "text": "4.8.2  Any increase in the duties and taxes after the Contractual completion period will be to the\nService Provider‟s account, where delay in completion /mobilization period is\nattributable to the Service Provider and the taxes & duties are not cenvatable (i.e. Input\nTax Credit (ITC) not available). In case of applicability of ITC / cenvatable taxes &\nduties, payment shall be made as per the prevailing rates during the currency of the\nContract. However, any benefit of decrease in duties and taxes after the Contractual\ncompletion will be passed on to the Employer.\n4.8.3 In the event of introduction of any new legislation or any change or amendment or\nenforcement of any Act or Law, rules or regulations of Government of India or State",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0315",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 315,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 95116,
    "char_end": 95157,
    "char_count": 41,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0316",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 316,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 95159,
    "char_end": 95288,
    "char_count": 129,
    "text": "------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n36",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0317",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 317,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 95290,
    "char_end": 96102,
    "char_count": 812,
    "text": "Government(s) or Public Body which becomes effective after the due date of submission\nof Bid for this Contract but within the Contractual completion period (including extended\nperiod allowed due to reasons attributed to Employer) and which results in increased cost\nof the jobs/services under the Contract through increased liability of taxes, (other than\npersonnel and Corporate taxes), duties, the Service Provider shall be indemnified for any\nsuch increased cost by the Employer subject to the production of documentary  proof to\nthe satisfaction of the Employer to the extent which directly is attributable to such\nintroduction of new legislation or change or amendment as mentioned above and\nadjudication by the competent authority & the courts wherever levy of such taxes / duties\nare disputed by Employer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0318",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 318,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 96104,
    "char_end": 96780,
    "char_count": 676,
    "text": "4.8.4  Similarly, in the event of introduction of new legislation or any change or amendment or\nenforcement of any Act or Law, rules or regulations of Government of India or State\nGovernment(s) or Public Body which becomes effective after the due date of submission\nof Bid for this Contract and which results in any decrease in the cost of the services/ jobs\nthrough reduced liability of taxes, (other than personnel and Corporate taxes) duties, the\nService Provider shall pass on the benefits of such reduced cost, taxes or duties to the\nEmployer, to the extent which is directly attributable to such introduction of new\nlegislation or change or amendment as mentioned above.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0319",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 319,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 96782,
    "char_end": 97315,
    "char_count": 533,
    "text": "4.9\nDAMAGES TO PROPERTY, ANY PERSON AND THIRD PARTY\n\ni)\nService Provider shall be responsible for making good to the satisfaction of the\nEmployer any loss or any damage to structures and properties belonging to the\nEmployer or being executed or procured or being procured by the Employer or of\nother agencies within in the premises of the Employer, if such loss or damage is\ndue to fault and/or the Negligence or Willful Misconduct or omission of the\nService Provider, his employees, agents, representatives or Sub-Service Providers.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0320",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 320,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 97317,
    "char_end": 98069,
    "char_count": 752,
    "text": "ii)\nThe Service Provider shall take sufficient care in moving his equipments and\nmaterials from one place to another so that they do not cause any damage to any\nperson or to the property of the Employer or any third party including overhead\nand underground cables and in the event of any damage resulting to the property\nof the Employer or of a third party during the movement of the aforesaid\nequipment or materials the cost of such damages including eventual loss of\nproduction, operation or services in any plant or establishment as estimated by the\nEmployer or ascertained or demanded by the third party shall be borne by the\nService Provider. Third party liability risk shall be Rupees One lakh for single\naccident and limited to Rupees Ten lakhs.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0321",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 321,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 98071,
    "char_end": 98435,
    "char_count": 364,
    "text": "iii)\nThe Service Provider shall indemnify and keep the Employer harmless of all\nclaims for damages to property other than Employer's property arising under or by\nreason of this agreement, if such claims result from the fault and/or Negligence or\nWillful Misconduct or omission of the Service Provider, his employees, agents,\nrepresentative of Sub-Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
