    "paragraph_index": 372,
    "page_start": 42,
    "page_end": 42,
    "char_start": 111854,
    "char_end": 112043,
    "char_count": 189,
    "text": "6.1\nDISPUTE RESOLUTION\n1.\nPRE-LITIGATION GRIEVANCE/DISPUTE REDRESSAL MECHANISM:\ni)\nAny issue should be first referred to EIC (for LOA/contracts)/Dealing C&P\nExecutive (for Purchase Orders).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0373",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 373,
    "page_start": 42,
    "page_end": 42,
    "char_start": 112044,
    "char_end": 112270,
    "char_count": 226,
    "text": "(ii)   In case issue is not resolved by above, Vendor/Supplier/Contractor/Consultant\nmay submit their issue to “Samadhan Committee”. The same will be addressed by\nSamadhan Committee within 15days from the date of issue raised.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0374",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 374,
    "page_start": 42,
    "page_end": 42,
    "char_start": 112271,
    "char_end": 113926,
    "char_count": 1655,
    "text": "(iii)  In case, Vendor/Supplier/ Contractor/Consultant is not satisfied with the decision\nof the Samadhan Committee, there is a provision of escalation of issue to higher\nauthority in BCPL. This option is available two times only, one is at Chief General\nManager (O&M) and the other one is Chief Operating Officer.\n(iv)\nHowever, in case no mutual settlement is arrived at after exercising all pre-\nlitigation grievance/dispute redressal mechanism as above, the matter shall be\nsettled by arbitration in accordance with the provision of arbitration of the Indian\nArbitration & Conciliation Act, 1996 and any statutory modification or re-\nenactment thereof and the Rules made there under and for the time being in force\nas stated below:\n2.\nARBITRATION\nAll issue(s)/dispute(s) excluding the matters that have been specified as excepted\nmatters and listed at clause no. 2.6 and which cannot be resolved through pre-\nlitigation grievance/dispute redressal mechanism, such issue(s)/dispute(s) shall be\nreferred to arbitration for adjudication by Sole Arbitrator.\nThe party invoking the Arbitration shall have the option to either opt for Ad-hoc\nArbitration as provided at Clause 2.1 below or Institutionalized Arbitration as\nprovided at Clause 2.2 below, the remaining clauses from 2.3 to 2.7 shall apply to\nboth Ad-hoc and Institutional Arbitration:-\n2.1\nOn invocation of the Arbitration clause by either party, BCPL shall suggest a\npanel of three independent and distinguished persons (Retd. Supreme Court &\nHigh Court Judges only) to the other party from the Panel of Arbitrators\nmaintained by „Delhi International Arbitration Centre (DIAC) to select any one",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0375",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 375,
    "page_start": 43,
    "page_end": 43,
    "char_start": 113928,
    "char_end": 113969,
    "char_count": 41,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0376",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "paragraph_index": 376,
