    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 23090,
    "char_end": 23202,
    "char_count": 112,
    "text": "-\nEmployer’s personnel(s), and /or\n-\nany other Contractor(s) / Service Provider(s) employed by Employer, and /or",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0091",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 91,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 23204,
    "char_end": 23257,
    "char_count": 53,
    "text": "-\npersonnel of public authority(ies)/third party(ies)",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0092",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 92,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 23259,
    "char_end": 23488,
    "char_count": 229,
    "text": "Further, the Service Provider shall execute the job carefully without causing damage to\nthe existing facility(ies) and facility(ies) of third party(ies) and in case of such happening\nshall immediately bring to the notice of EIC..",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0093",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 93,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 23490,
    "char_end": 24095,
    "char_count": 605,
    "text": "Further, the coordination and inspection of the day-to-day job under the Contract shall be\nthe responsibility of the Engineer-in-Charge (EIC). The EIC or his authroised\nrepresentative including any statutory authority shall at all reasonable times, have full\npower and authority to access and inspect the Services wherever in progress either on the\nSite or at the Service Provider’s premises/workshops and the Service Provider shall\nafford or procure every facility and assistance to carry out such inspection. Such\nInspection shall not release the Service Provider from any obligation under the Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0094",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 94,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 24097,
    "char_end": 24475,
    "char_count": 378,
    "text": "2.11  SERVICE PROVIDER’s REPRESENTATIVE & PERSONNEL:\n\n2.11.1 Service Provider shall appoint a person (“Service Provider’s Representative”) who shall\nbe responsible for and authorized to represent it at all times during the progress of the\nService and to receive and to act on any request made by Employer in the performance of\nthe Service pursuant to the terms of this Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0095",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 95,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 24477,
    "char_end": 24849,
    "char_count": 372,
    "text": "2.11.2 Service Provider's Representative shall have full authority to represent and bind the\nService Provider in relation to any matter concerning the Service Provider’s performance\nof the services under the Contract and Employer shall be entitled to rely on all the\ndecisions of the Service Provider’s Representative as if they were the decisions of the\nService Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0096",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 96,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 24851,
    "char_end": 25090,
    "char_count": 239,
    "text": "2.11.3 Service Provider's Representative shall supervise, coordinate and ensure the quality of all\naspects of his obligations under this Contract. Service Provider shall not change its\nRepresentative without the prior approval of Employer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0097",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 97,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 25092,
    "char_end": 25267,
    "char_count": 175,
    "text": "2.11.4 Service Provider's Representative shall liaise with Employer for the proper coordination\nand timely completion of the Services and on any matter pertaining to the same.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0098",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 98,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 25269,
    "char_end": 25544,
    "char_count": 275,
    "text": "2.11.5 Service Provider's Representative shall extend full cooperation to Employer’s\nrepresentatives/inspector in the manner required by them for supervision /inspection/\nobservation of equipment, material, procedures, performance, reports and records\npertaining to Services.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0099",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 99,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 25546,
    "char_end": 25743,
    "char_count": 197,
    "text": "2.11.6 Service Provider's Representative shall have complete charge of his personnel engaged in\nthe performance of the Service and to ensure compliance of rules and regulations and\nsafety practice.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0100",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 100,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 25745,
    "char_end": 25928,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n13",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0101",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 101,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 25930,
    "char_end": 26330,
    "char_count": 400,
    "text": "2.11.7 If the Service Provider’s Representative is found not acceptable to the EIC, the Service\nProvider shall, as soon as practicable, having regard to the requirement of replacing him,\nafter receiving notice of such withdrawal, remove the representative and shall not\nthereafter employ him again on the Services in any capacity and shall replace him by\nanother representative acceptable to the EIC.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0102",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 102,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 26332,
    "char_end": 26488,
    "char_count": 156,
    "text": "2.12\nSERVICE PROVIDER’S EMPLOYEES / PERSONNEL:\n\nThe Service Provider in connection with performing the Services and remedying of any\ndefects, shall provide:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0103",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 103,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 26490,
    "char_end": 26571,
    "char_count": 81,
    "text": "(a)\nonly such skilled and experienced personnel(s) in their respective areas; and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0104",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 104,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 26573,
    "char_end": 26736,
    "char_count": 163,
    "text": "(b)\nsuch skilled, semi-skilled and un-skilled labour as is necessary for the proper and\ntimely fulfilling of the Service Provider’s obligations under the Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0105",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 105,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 26738,
    "char_end": 26856,
    "char_count": 118,
    "text": "The Service Provider shall provide skilled / qualified /experienced personnel, if specified\nin the SCC /Scope of Work.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0106",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 106,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 26858,
    "char_end": 27117,
    "char_count": 259,
    "text": "While engaging the contractual manpower, Service Provider is required to make effort to\nprovide opportunity of employment to the people belonging to Scheduled Castes and\nweaker sections of society also in order to have a fair representation of these sections.",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0107",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 107,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 27119,
    "char_end": 27750,
    "char_count": 631,
    "text": "2.13  CONTRACT PERFORMANCE SECURITY (CPS):\n\n2.13.1 The Service Provider shall provide Contract Performance Security (CPS) to the Employer,\nwithin 30 days from the date of notification of award (i.e. FOA/Letter of Acceptance) or\nthe date specified in the notification of award whichever is earlier, for an amount\nmentioned therein. The CPS shall be returned/refunded three months after Contract\ncompletion period and Defects Liability Period (DLP), if any. All costs associated with\nCPS shall be borne by the Service Provider. No charges or interest shall be payable by\nthe Employer even if the CPS is in the form of a Demand Draft.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0108",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 108,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 27752,
    "char_end": 28429,
    "char_count": 677,
    "text": "2.13.2 The Service Provider shall furnish the CPS in the form of a Demand Draft or a Bank\nGuarantee or an irrevocable Letter of Credit from any Indian scheduled bank or a branch\nof an International bank situated in India and registered with Reserve Bank of India as\nscheduled foreign bank. However, for other than the Nationalized Indian Banks, the\nbanks whose BGs are furnished, must be commercial banks having net worth in excess of\nRs. 100 crores and a declaration to this effect should be made by such commercial bank\neither in the bank guarantee itself or separately on a letter head. The bank guarantee or\nthe Letter of Credit shall be submitted in the prescribed format.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0109",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 109,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 28431,
    "char_end": 29016,
    "char_count": 585,
    "text": "2.13.3 If the Service Provider or their employees /agents / representatives or Sub-Service\nProvider (if authorized by Employer) shall damage, break, deface or destroy any property\n/equipment belonging to the Employer or third party(ies) during the execution of this\nContract, the same shall be made good by the Service Provider at his own expenses and\nin default thereof, the EIC may cause the same to be made good by other agencies and\nrecover expenses plus 15% overhead from the Service Provider. The decision of EIC in\nthis matter shall be final and binding on the Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0110",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 110,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 29018,
    "char_end": 29201,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n14",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0111",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 111,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 29203,
    "char_end": 30105,
    "char_count": 902,
    "text": "2.13.4 All compensation, claim or other sums of money payable by the Service Provider to the\nEmployer under terms of this  Contract may be deducted from or paid by the encashment\nof a sufficient part of his Contract Performance Security or from any sums which may be\ndue or may become due to the Service Provider by the Employer on any account\nwhatsoever and in the event of his CPS being reduced by reasons of any such deductions\nor sale of aforesaid, the Service Provider shall within ten days thereafter make good in\nform of  bank draft(s)/BG/LC (as the case may be) as aforesaid any sum or sums which\nmay have been deducted from or realised by encashment of his CPS, or any part thereof.\nThe Service Provider shall pay to the Employer on demand without protest any balance\nremaining due. In this regard no interest shall be payable by the Employer to Service\nProvider for such sum deposited as CPS.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0112",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 112,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 30107,
    "char_end": 30625,
    "char_count": 518,
    "text": "2.13.5 The CPS deposit shall cover the entire Contract value including extra jobs/ services. As\nlong as the CPS submitted at the time of award take cares the extra jobs/ services\nexecuted and total executed value are within the awarded Contract price, there is no need\nfor additional CPS . As soon as the total executed value is likely to exceed the ceiling of\nawarded Contract Value, the Service Provider should furnish additional CPS through DD\nor submit amendment to existing BG/LC to effect the enhancement of CPS.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0113",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 113,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 30627,
    "char_end": 30864,
    "char_count": 237,
    "text": "2.13.6 Failure of the successful bidder to comply with the requirements of Clause 2.13 shall\nconstitute sufficient grounds for the annulment of the award, the forfeiture of CPS and\nany other actions or remedies available to the Employer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0114",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 114,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 30866,
    "char_end": 30950,
    "char_count": 84,
    "text": "2.14  FAILURE BY THE SERVICE PROVIDER TO COMPLY WITH THE\nPROVISIONS OF THE CONTRACT:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0115",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 115,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 30952,
    "char_end": 31382,
    "char_count": 430,
    "text": "2.14.1 If the Service Provider refuses or fails to provide the Service or any part thereof with such\ndiligence as will ensure its performance within the time specified in the Contract or\nextension thereof or fails to perform any of his obligation under the Contract or in any\nmanner commits a breach of any of the provisions of the Contract it shall be open to the\nEmployer at its option by written notice to the Service Provider:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0116",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 116,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 31384,
    "char_end": 32277,
    "char_count": 893,
    "text": "a)\nTO DETERMINE THE CONTRACT in which event the Contract shall stand\nterminated and shall cease to be in force and effect on and from the date\nappointed by the Employer on that behalf, whereupon the Service Provider shall\nstop forthwith any of the Service then in progress, except such Service as the\nEmployer may, in writing, require to be done to safeguard any property or work\nor installations from damage, and the Employer, for its part, may take over the\nService remaining unfinished by the Service Provider and complete the same\nthrough another service provider or by other means, at the risk and cost of the\nService Provider, and any of his sureties if any, shall be liable to the Employer for\nany excess cost occasioned by such service having to be so taken over and\nobtained by the Employer over and above the cost at the rates specified in the\nschedule of quantities and rate/prices.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0117",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 117,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 32279,
    "char_end": 32427,
    "char_count": 148,
    "text": "b)\nWITHOUT DETERMINING THE Contract to take over the Service of the\nService Provider or any part thereof and complete the same through other service",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0118",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 118,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 32429,
    "char_end": 32612,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n15",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0119",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 119,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 32614,
    "char_end": 32945,
    "char_count": 331,
    "text": "provider or by other means at the risk and cost of the Service Provider. The\nService Provider and any of his sureties are liable to the Employer for any excess\ncost over and above the cost at the rates specified in the Schedule of Quantities/\nrates, occasioned by such services having been taken over and completed by the\nEmployer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0120",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 120,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 32947,
    "char_end": 33039,
    "char_count": 92,
    "text": "2.14.2  In such events of Clause 2.14.1(a) or (b) above, the following shall be applicable:-",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0121",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 121,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 33041,
    "char_end": 33667,
    "char_count": 626,
    "text": "a)\nThe whole or part of the Contract Performance Security furnished by the Service\nProvider is liable to be forfeited without prejudice to the right of the Employer to\nrecover from the Service Provider the excess cost referred to in the sub-clause\naforesaid. The Employer shall also have the right of taking possession and\nutilising in completing the services or any part thereof, such as materials,\nequipment and plants available at service site belonging to the Service Provider as\nmay be necessary and the Service Provider shall not be entitled for any\ncompensation for use or damage to such materials, equipment and plant.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0122",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 122,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 33669,
    "char_end": 34362,
    "char_count": 693,
    "text": "b)\nThe amount that may have become due to the Service Provider on account of\nservice already executed by him shall not be payable to him until after the expiry\nof Six (6) calendar months reckoned from the date of termination of Contract or\nfrom the taking over of the Service or part thereof by the Employer as the case\nmay be, during which period the responsibility for faulty material or workmanship\nin respect of such service shall, under the Contract, rest exclusively with the\nService Provider. This amount shall be subject to deduction of any amounts due\nfrom the Contract to the Employer under the terms of the Contract authorised or\nrequired to be reserved or retained by the Employer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0123",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 123,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 34364,
    "char_end": 34745,
    "char_count": 381,
    "text": "2.14.3 Before taking any action as per Clause 2.14.1(a) or (b) if in the judgment of the Employer,\nthe default or defaults committed by the Service Provider is/are curable and can be cured\nby the Service Provider if an opportunity given to him, then the Employer may issue\nNotice in writing calling the Service Provider to cure the default within such time\nspecified in the Notice.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0124",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 124,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 34747,
    "char_end": 35412,
    "char_count": 665,
    "text": "2.14.4 The Employer shall also have the right to proceed or take action as per 2.14.1(a) or (b)\nabove, in the event that the Service Provider becomes bankrupt, insolvent, compounds\nwith his creditors, assigns the Contract in favour of his creditors or any other person(s) or\nbeing a company or a corporation goes into voluntary liquidation, provided that in the\nsaid events it shall not be necessary for the Employer to give any prior notice to the\nService Provider.\n2.14.5 Termination of the Contract as provided for in sub- clause 2.14.1(a) above shall not\nprejudice or affect their rights of the Employer which may have accrued upto the date of\nsuch termination.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0125",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 125,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 35414,
    "char_end": 35509,
    "char_count": 95,
    "text": "2.15  SERVICE PROVIDER REMAINS LIABLE TO PAY COMPENSATION IF\nACTION NOT TAKEN UNDER CLAUSE 2.14",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0126",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 126,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 35511,
    "char_end": 35694,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n16",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0127",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 127,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 35696,
    "char_end": 37138,
    "char_count": 1442,
    "text": "2.15.1 If in any case in which any of the powers conferred upon the Employer by clause 2.14\nthereof shall have become exercisable and the same had not been exercised, the non-\nexercise thereof shall not constitute a waiver of any of the conditions hereof and such\npowers shall notwithstanding be exercisable in the event of any further case of default by\nthe Service Provider for which by any clause or clauses hereof he is declared liable to pay\ncompensation amounting to the whole of his Contract Performance Security, and the\nliability of the Service Provider for past and future compensation shall remain unaffected.\nIn the event of the Employer putting in force the power under above sub-clause 2.14 (a)\nor 2.14 (b) vested in him under the preceding clause he may, if he so desired, take\npossession of all or any tools and plants, materials and stores at the site thereof belonging\nto the Service Provider or procured by him and intended to be used for the execution of\nthe Service or any part thereof paying or allowing for the same in account at the Contract\nrates or in case of these not being applicable, at current market rates to be certified by the\nEIC whose certificate thereof shall be final, otherwise the EIC may give notice in writing\nto the Service Provider or Service Provider’s Representatives requiring him to remove\nsuch tools, plant, materials or stores from the premises (within a time to be specified in\nsuch notice).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0128",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 128,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 37140,
    "char_end": 38302,
    "char_count": 1162,
    "text": "Failure of any action by the Service Provider for removal of material/tools/plant/store etc.\nwithin the period mentioned in notice of EIC, the Employer shall also be entitled to\nrecover handling and storage charges @5% of the estimated value of material\ntools/plant/store for each month or part of a month without relieving the Servicer\nProvider from any other related liability. In the event of the Service Provider’s failure  to\nremove the same within a  period of 6 months or as decided by the EIC,  the EIC may\ntake action for removal  through auction or private sale on behalf of the Service Provider\nand at his risk in all respects. The Service Provider shall be liable to pay the Employer the\nhandling & storage charges per month or a part of the month from the date of serving the\nnotice by the EIC to the date of removal of the materials by the Employer plus overhead\ncharges @ 15% of sale value of such materials. In case of negative or zero sale value, the\noverhead charges shall be applicable on the handling & storage charges. The decision of\nEIC w.r.t. such removal and the amount of the proceeds shall be final and binding on the\nService Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0129",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 129,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 38304,
    "char_end": 39014,
    "char_count": 710,
    "text": "2.16  CHANGE IN CONSTITUTION:\n\n2.16.1 Where the Service Provider is a partnership firm, the prior approval of the Employer shall\nbe obtained in writing, before any change is made in the constitution of the firm. Where\nthe Service Provider is an individual or a Hindu undivided family business concern, such\napproval as aforesaid shall, likewise be obtained before such Service Provider enters into\nany agreement with other parties, where under, the reconstituted firm would have the\nright to carry out the service hereby undertaken by the Service Provider. In either case if\nprior approval as aforesaid is not obtained, the Contract shall be deemed to have been\nallotted in contravention of clause 2.23 hereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0130",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 130,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 39016,
    "char_end": 39199,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n17",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0131",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 131,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 39201,
    "char_end": 40261,
    "char_count": 1060,
    "text": "2.17  TERMINATION OF CONTRACT:\n\n2.17.1 TERMINATION OF CONTRACT FOR DEATH\n\nIf the Service Provider is an individual or a proprietary concern and the individual or the\nproprietor dies or if the Service Provider is a partnership concern and one of the partner\ndies then unless, the Employer is satisfied that the legal representative of the individual or\nthe proprietary concern or the surviving partners are capable of carrying out and\ncompleting Contract, the Employer is entitled to cancel the Contract for the uncompleted\npart without being in any way liable for any compensation payment to the estate of the\ndeceased  Service Provider and/or to the surviving partners of the Service Provider's firm\non account of the cancellation of Contract. The decision of the Employer/EIC in such\nassessment shall be final & binding on the parties. In the event of such cancellation, the\nEmployer shall not hold the estate of the deceased Service Provider and/or the surviving\npartners of Service Provider's firm liable for any damages for non-completion of the\nContract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0132",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 132,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 40263,
    "char_end": 41162,
    "char_count": 899,
    "text": "2.17.2 TERMINATION OF CONTRACT IN CASE OF LIQUIDATION / BANKRUPTCY,\nETC.\n\nIf the Service Provider shall dissolve or become bankrupt or insolvent or cause or suffer\nany receiver to be appointed of his business of any assets thereof compound with his\nCreditors, or being a corporation commence to be wound up, not being a member's\nvoluntary winding up for the purpose of amalgamation or reconstruction, or carry on its\nbusiness under a Receiver for the benefits of its Creditors any of them, Employer shall be\nat liberty to terminate the Contract forthwith upon coming to know of the happening of\nany such event as aforesaid by notice in writing to the Service Provider or to give the\nReceiver or Liquidator or other person, the option of carrying out the Contract subject to\nhis providing a guarantee up to an amount to be agreed upon by the Employer for due and\nfaithful performance of the Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0133",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 133,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 41164,
    "char_end": 41271,
    "char_count": 107,
    "text": "2.17.3 TERMINATION\nOF\nCONTRACT\nFOR\nCORRUPT\n/\nFRADULENT\n/\nCOLLUSIVE / COERCIVE PRACTICES AND NON-PERFORMANCE",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0134",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 134,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 41273,
    "char_end": 41612,
    "char_count": 339,
    "text": "If the Bidder/Service Provider is found to have indulged in Corrupt/ Fraudulent\n/Collusive/Coercive practices, the Contract shall be terminated and the Bidder/ Service\nProvider shall be banned for future business with GAIL Gas. The detailed procedure for\nbanning including suspension in this regard may be referred as enclosed with tender.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0135",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 135,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 41614,
    "char_end": 42030,
    "char_count": 416,
    "text": "Due to non-performance of the Service Provider leading to termination of the Contract,\nthe Service Provider initially shall be put on suspension list and thereafter on holiday list\nof Employer for a period mentioned in the detailed procedure, to be reckoned from the\ndate of communication by Owner/Employer. The detailed procedure for evaluation of\nperformance in this regard may be referred as enclosed with tender.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0136",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 136,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 42032,
    "char_end": 42215,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n18",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0137",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 137,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 42217,
    "char_end": 42572,
    "char_count": 355,
    "text": "2.17.4 TERMINATION FOR CONVENIENCE\n\nNotwithstanding anything contained in the Contract, the Employer may, by 30 (Thirty)\ndays written notice, terminate the Contract in whole or in part. In addition to the payment\nmentioned at clause 2.18, the Service Provider shall be compensated for de-mobilization\nand other costs incurred at mutually negotiated terms.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0138",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 138,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 42574,
    "char_end": 42857,
    "char_count": 283,
    "text": "In case of such termination, the obligation of the Employer to pay, shall be limited to the\nextent of work/job completed by the Service Provider as per provision of the Contract\nupto the date of termination, subject to the Service Provider complying with other terms\nof the Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0139",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 139,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 42859,
    "char_end": 43056,
    "char_count": 197,
    "text": "Notwithstanding the termination of the Contract, the parties shall continue to be bound by\nthe provisions of this Contract that reasonably require some action or forbearance after\nsuch termination.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0140",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 140,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 43058,
    "char_end": 43602,
    "char_count": 544,
    "text": "2.18\nAMOUNT PAYABLE IN CASE OF TERMINATION:\n\n2.18.1 In all cases of termination herein set forth, the obligation of the Employer to pay, shall be\nlimited to the extent of service rendered by Service Provider as per provision of the\nContract upto the date of termination, subject to the Service Provider complying with\nother terms of the Contract. Notwithstanding the termination of the Contract, the parties\nshall continue to be bound by the provisions of this Contract that reasonably require some\naction or forbearance after such termination.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0141",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 141,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 43604,
    "char_end": 43970,
    "char_count": 366,
    "text": "2.19  MEMBERS OF THE EMPLOYER NOT INDIVIDUALLY LIABLE:\n\n2.19.1 No Director, or official or employee of the Employer shall in any way be personally\nbound or liable for the acts or obligations of the Employer under the Contract or\nanswerable for any default or omission in the observance or performance of any of the\nacts, matters or things which are herein contained.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0142",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 142,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 43972,
    "char_end": 44316,
    "char_count": 344,
    "text": "2.20  EMPLOYER NOT BOUND BY PERSONAL REPRESENTATIONS:\n\n2.20.1 The Service Provider shall not be entitled to any increase on the scheduled rates or any\nother right or claim whatsoever by reason of any representation, explanation statement or\nalleged representation, promise or guarantees given or alleged to have been given to him\nby any person.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0143",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 143,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 44318,
    "char_end": 44608,
    "char_count": 290,
    "text": "2.21  FORCE MAJEURE:\n\n2.21.1  In the event of either party being rendered unable by Force Majeure to perform any\nobligations required to be performed by them under the Contract the relative obligation of\nthe party affected by such Force Majeure shall upon notification to the other party be",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0144",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 144,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 44610,
    "char_end": 44793,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n19",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0145",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 145,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 44795,
    "char_end": 44950,
    "char_count": 155,
    "text": "suspended for the period during which Force Majeures event lasts. The cost and loss\nsustained by the either party shall be borne by the respective parties.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0146",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 146,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 44952,
    "char_end": 45956,
    "char_count": 1004,
    "text": "The term \"Force Majeures\" as employed herein shall include:\n\n(a)\nact of terrorism;\n(b)\nriot, war, invasion, act of foreign enemies, hostilities (whether war be declared or\nnot), civil war, rebellion, revolution, insurrection of military or usurped power;\n(c)\nionising radiation or contamination, radio activity from any nuclear fuel or from\nany nuclear waste from the combustion of nuclear fuel, radioactive toxic\nexplosive or other hazardous properties of any explosive assembly or nuclear\ncomponent;\n(d)\nepidemics, earthquakes, flood, fire, hurricanes, typhoons or other physical natural\ndisaster, but excluding weather conditions regardless of severity; and\n(e)\nfreight embargoes, strikes at national or state-wide level or industrial disputes at a\nnational or state-wide level in any country where Works/Services are performed,\nand which affect an essential portion of the Works/Services but excluding any\nindustrial dispute which is specific to the performance of the Works/Services or\nthe Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0147",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 147,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 45958,
    "char_end": 46174,
    "char_count": 216,
    "text": "For the avoidance of doubt, inclement weather, third party breach, delay in supply of\nmaterials (other than due to a nationwide transporters’ strike) or commercial hardship\nshall not constitute a Force Majeure event.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0148",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 148,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 46176,
    "char_end": 46595,
    "char_count": 419,
    "text": "2.21.2  Notification of Force Majeure\n\nThe affected party shall notify within 10 (ten) days of becoming aware of or the date it\nought to have become aware of the occurrence of an event of Force Majeure giving full\nparticulars of the event of Force Majeure and the reasons for the event of Force Majeure\npreventing the affected party from, or delaying the affected party in performing its\nobligations under the Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0149",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 149,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 46597,
    "char_end": 47168,
    "char_count": 571,
    "text": "2.21.3  Right of either party to terminate\n\nIf an event of Force Majeure occurs and its effect continues for a period of 180 (one\nhundred eighty) days or more in a continuous period of 365 (three hundred sixty five)\ndays after notice has been given under this clause, either party may terminate the\nContract by issuing a written notice of 30 (thirty) days to the other party.\nFurther, the Service Provider shall with all reasonable diligence remove from the Site all\nthe Service Provider's equipment and shall give similar facilities to his Sub Service\nProvider to do so.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0150",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 150,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 47170,
    "char_end": 47440,
    "char_count": 270,
    "text": "2.21.4  Payment in case of termination due to Force Majeure\n\nThe Contract Price attributable to the Works/Services performed till the date of the\ncommencement of the relevant event of Force Majeure with effective recovery/ retention\nshall be payable to Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0151",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 151,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 47442,
    "char_end": 47625,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n20",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0152",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 152,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 47627,
    "char_end": 47701,
    "char_count": 74,
    "text": "The Service Provider has no entitlement and Employer has no liability for:",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0153",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 153,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 47703,
    "char_end": 47835,
    "char_count": 132,
    "text": "a)\nany costs, losses, expenses, damages or the payment of any part of the Total\nContract Price during an event of Force Majeure; and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0154",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 154,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 47837,
    "char_end": 47933,
    "char_count": 96,
    "text": "b)\nany delay costs in any way incurred by the Service Provider due to an event of\nForce Majeure.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0155",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 155,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 47935,
    "char_end": 48088,
    "char_count": 153,
    "text": "2.21.5 Time for performance of the relative obligation suspended by the Force Majeure shall\nthen stand extended by the period for which such cause lasts.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0156",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 156,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 48090,
    "char_end": 49010,
    "char_count": 920,
    "text": "2.21.6 Outbreak of War:\n\nIf during the currency of the Contract there shall be an out break of war whether declared\nor not, in that part of the World which whether financially or otherwise materially affect\nthe execution of the Work, the Service Provider shall unless and until the Contract is\nterminated under the provisions in this clause continue to use his best endeavour to\ncomplete the execution of the Work/Services, provided always that the Employer shall be\nentitled, at any time after such out break of war to terminate or re-negotiate the Contract\nby giving notice in writing to the Service Provider and upon such notice being given the\nContract shall, save as to the rights of the parties under this clause and to the operation of\nthe clauses entitled settlement of Disputes and Arbitration hereof, be terminated but\nwithout prejudice to the right of either party in respect of any antecedent breach thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0157",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 157,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 49012,
    "char_end": 49687,
    "char_count": 675,
    "text": "2.22  PRICE REDUCTION SCHEDULE:\n\n2.22.1 Time is the essence of the Contract. In case the Service Provider fails to mobilize / deploy\nthe required manpower and the complete equipments so as to commence the Services\nwithin Mobilisation Period and complete the Services within the stipulated period, then,\nunless such failure is due to Force Majeure as defined in Clause 2.21 herein above or due\nto Employer's defaults, the total Value of Contract shall be reduced by ½ (half) % of the\ntotal Value of Contract per complete week of delay or part thereof subject to a maximum\nof 5 (five) % of the total Value of Contract, by way of reduction in price for delay and not\nas penalty.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0158",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 158,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 49689,
    "char_end": 49853,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "The Employer shall be at liberty to adjust or deduct the said amount from amount due to\nthe Service Provider / it’s Contract Performance Security payable on demand.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0159",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 159,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 49855,
    "char_end": 49988,
    "char_count": 133,
    "text": "The decision of the EIC with respect to applicability of Price Reduction Schedule shall be\nfinal and binding on the Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0160",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 160,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 49990,
    "char_end": 50350,
    "char_count": 360,
    "text": "2.22.2 The parties agree that this is a genuine pre-estimate of the loss/damage which will be\nsuffered by the Employer on account of delay on the part of the Service Provider and the\nsaid amount will be adjusted for the amount payable to the Service Provider, without\nthere being any proof of the actual loss or damages having been caused by such\ndelay/breach.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0161",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 161,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 50352,
    "char_end": 50535,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n21",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0162",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 162,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 50537,
    "char_end": 50771,
    "char_count": 234,
    "text": "2.22.3 The Price Reduction will be calculated on the basis of total Value of Contract / executed\nValue of Contract (as the case may be) excluding taxes and duties where such taxes and\nduties have been shown separately in the Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0163",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 163,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 50773,
    "char_end": 51087,
    "char_count": 314,
    "text": "2.22.4 As mentioned above, in case of delay in execution of Contract, Service Provider will\nraise invoice for reduced value as per Price Reduction Clause. If Service Provider has\nraised the invoice for full value, then Service Provider will issue Credit Note towards the\napplicable Price Reduction Schedule amount.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0164",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 164,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 51089,
    "char_end": 51316,
    "char_count": 227,
    "text": "In case Service Provider fails to submit the invoice for reduced value or does not issue\ncredit note as mentioned above, GAIL Gas will release the payment to Service Provider\nafter effecting the Price Reduction Schedule clause.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0165",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 165,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 51318,
    "char_end": 51515,
    "char_count": 197,
    "text": "In the event any financial implication arises on GAIL Gas due to issuance of invoice\nwithout reduction in price or non-issuance of Credit Note, the same shall be to the\naccount of Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0166",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 166,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 51517,
    "char_end": 51931,
    "char_count": 414,
    "text": "2.23\nASSIGNMENT/SUBLET:\n\n2.23.1 The Service Provider shall not, save with previous written consent  of the Engineer-in-\ncharge, sublet, transfer or assign the Contract or any part thereof or interest therein or\nbenefit or advantage thereof in any manner whatsoever. Provided, nevertheless, that any\nsuch consent shall not relieve the Service Provider from any obligation, duty or\nresponsibility under the Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0167",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 167,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 51933,
    "char_end": 52403,
    "char_count": 470,
    "text": "2.23.2 The basic scope of Services cannot be sublet. However, on specific request of the Service\nProvider and subject to written consent of Employer, the Service Provider may sublet\nallied/incidental jobs related to the Services. Such consent shall not relieve the Service\nProvider from any obligation, duty or responsibility under the Contract and Service\nProvider shall be fully responsible for the Services hereunder and the execution and\nperformance of the Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0168",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 168,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 52405,
    "char_end": 52551,
    "char_count": 146,
    "text": "2.23.3 Sub-letting of whole Contract is prohibited. An undertaking to this effect will be given by\nService Provider along with each invoice/ bill.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0169",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 169,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 52553,
    "char_end": 53362,
    "char_count": 809,
    "text": "2.24\nLIENS:\n\n2.24.1 If, at any time there should be evidence of any lien or claim for which the Employer might\nhave become liable and which is chargeable to the Service Provider, the Employer shall\nhave the right to retain out of any payment then due or thereafter to become due an\namount sufficient to completely indemnify the Employer against such lien or claim and if\nsuch lien or claim be valid, the Employer may pay and discharge the same and deduct the\namount so paid from any money which may be or may become due and payable to the\nService Provider. If any lien or claim remain unsettled after all payments are made, the\nService Provider shall refund or pay to the Employer all money that the latter may be\ncompelled to pay in discharging such lien or claim including all costs and reasonable\nexpenses.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0170",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 170,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 53364,
    "char_end": 53547,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n22",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0171",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 171,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 53549,
    "char_end": 53699,
    "char_count": 150,
    "text": "2.24.2 The Employer shall have lien on all materials, equipments including those brought by the\nService Provider for the purpose of providing service.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0172",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 172,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 53701,
    "char_end": 54263,
    "char_count": 562,
    "text": "2.24.3 The final payment shall not become due until the Service Provider delivers to the EIC a\ncomplete release or waiver of all liens arising or which may arise out of his agreement or\nreceipt in full or certification by the Service Provider in a form approved by EIC that all\ninvoices for labour, materials, services have been paid in lien thereof and if required by\nthe EIC in any case an affidavit that so far as the Service Provider has knowledge or\ninformation the releases and receipts include all the labour and material for which a lien\ncould be filled.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0173",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 173,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 54265,
    "char_end": 55092,
    "char_count": 827,
    "text": "2.24.4 Service Provider will indemnify and hold the Employer harmless, for a period of two\nyears after the issue of Completion/Execution Certificate, from all liens and other\nencumbrances against the Employer on account of debts or claims alleged to be due from\nthe Service Provider or his Sub-Service Provider to any person and on behalf of\nEmployer, the Service Provider will defend at his own expense, any claim or litigation\nbrought against the Employer or the Service Provider including Sub-Service Provider in\nconnection therewith. Service Provider shall defend or contest at his own expense, any\nfresh claim or litigation against the Employer by any person including his Sub-Service\nProvider, till its satisfactory settlement even after the expiry of two years from the date of\nissue of Completion/Execution Certificate.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0174",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 174,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 55094,
    "char_end": 55530,
    "char_count": 436,
    "text": "2.25   DELAYS BY EMPLOYER OR HIS AUTHORISED REPRESENTATIVE:\n\n2.25.1 In case the Service Provider's performance is delayed due to any act or omission on the\npart of the Employer or his authorized Representative, then the Service Provider shall be\ngiven due extension of time for the completion of the Service, to the extent such omission\non the part of the Employer has caused delay in the Service Provider's performance of his\nServices.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0175",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 175,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 55532,
    "char_end": 56026,
    "char_count": 494,
    "text": "2.25.2 No adjustment in Contract Price shall be allowed for reasons of such delays and\nextensions granted except as provided in Tender Document, where the Employer reserves\nthe right to seek indulgence of Service Provider to maintain the agreed Time Schedule of\nCompletion. In such an event the Service Provider shall be obliged to provide Service for\nadditional time beyond stipulated time including Off-days / Holidays or by enhancing\nresources to achieve the completion date/interim targets.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0176",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 176,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 56028,
    "char_end": 56253,
    "char_count": 225,
    "text": "2.26  NO WAIVER OF RIGHTS:\n\n2.26.1  None of the terms and conditions of this Contract shall be deemed waived by either party\nunless such waiver is executed in writing by the duly authorized representative of both\nthe parties.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0177",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 177,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 56255,
    "char_end": 56339,
    "char_count": 84,
    "text": "2.27  CERTIFICATE NOT TO AFFECT RIGHT OF EMPLOYER AND LIABILITY\nOF SERVICE PROVIDER:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0178",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 178,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 56341,
    "char_end": 56524,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n23",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0179",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 179,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 56526,
    "char_end": 57314,
    "char_count": 788,
    "text": "2.27.1 No interim payment certificate(s) issued by the EIC of the Employer, nor any sum paid\non account by the Employer, nor any extension of time for execution of the service\ngranted by Employer shall affect or prejudice the rights of the Employer against the\nService Provider or relieve the Service Provider of his obligations for the due\nperformance of the Contract, or be interpreted as approval of the Service done and no\ncertificate shall create liability for the Employer to pay for alterations, amendments,\nvariations or additional services not ordered, in writing, by Employer or discharge the\nliability of the Service Provider for the payment of damages whether due, ascertained, or\ncertified or not or any sum against the payment of which he is bound to indemnify the\nEmployer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0180",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 180,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 57316,
    "char_end": 57650,
    "char_count": 334,
    "text": "2.28  LANGUAGE AND MEASURES:\n\n2.28.1 All documents pertaining to the Contract including Specifications, Schedules, Notices,\nCorrespondence, operating and maintenance Instructions or any other writing shall be\nwritten in English/Hindi language. The Metric System of measurement shall be used in\nthe Contract unless otherwise specified.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0181",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 181,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 57652,
    "char_end": 58045,
    "char_count": 393,
    "text": "2.29  RELEASE OF INFORMATION:\n\n2.29.1 The Service Provider shall not communicate or use in advertising, publicity, sales\nreleases or in any other medium, photographs, or other reproduction of the Service under\nthis Contract or description of the site dimensions, quantity, quality or other information\nconcerning the Service unless prior written permission has been obtained from the\nEmployer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0182",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 182,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 58047,
    "char_end": 58233,
    "char_count": 186,
    "text": "2.30  COMPLETION PERIOD, CONTRACT PERIOD AND COMPLETION OF\nCONTRACT:\n\n2.30.1 The Completion Period of Service and Contract Period shall be as mentioned in Special\nConditions of Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0183",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 183,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 58235,
    "char_end": 58448,
    "char_count": 213,
    "text": "2.30.2 Unless terminated under the provisions of any other relevant clause, this Contract shall be\ndeemed to have been completed at the expiration of the Defect Liability Period as\nprovided for under the Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0184",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 184,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 58450,
    "char_end": 59044,
    "char_count": 594,
    "text": "2.31  INDEPENDENT CAPACITY\n\n2.31.1 The parties intend that an independent Service Provider relationship will be created by\nthis Contract. The Service Provider and his/her employees or agents performing under\nthis Contract are not employees or agents of the Employer. The Service Provider will\nneither hold himself/herself out as nor claim to be an officer or employee of the\nEmployer by reasons hereof, nor will the Service Provider make any claim of right,\nprivilege or benefit that would accrue to such employee under law. Conduct and control\nof work will be solely with the Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0185",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 185,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 59046,
    "char_end": 59244,
    "char_count": 198,
    "text": "2.32   NOTICE\n\nGeneral Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n24",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0186",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 186,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 59246,
    "char_end": 59696,
    "char_count": 450,
    "text": "2.32.1 TO THE SERVICE PROVIDER: Any notice to be given to the Service Provider or his\nduly authorised representative at the job Site under the terms of the Contract may be\nserved by the Employer by facsimile / e-mail or through registered post/Courier at the\naddress/contact information furnished by the Service Provider. Proof of issue of any such\nnotice could be conclusive of the Service Provider having been duly informed of all\ncontents therein.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0187",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 187,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 59698,
    "char_end": 59951,
    "char_count": 253,
    "text": "2.32.2  TO THE EMPLOYER: Any notice to be given to the EIC of the Employer under the\nterms of the Contract may be served by the Service Provider, by facsimile / e-mail or\ndelivering the same through registered post /Courier at the concerned site office.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0188",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 188,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 59953,
    "char_end": 60267,
    "char_count": 314,
    "text": "2.32.3 Either party may change a nominated address to another address in the country where the\nServices are being provided by prior notice to the other party, with a copy to EIC and the\nEIC may do so by prior notice to both the parties. The decision of EIC in this regard shall\nbe final and binding on the parties.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0189",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 189,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 60269,
    "char_end": 60640,
    "char_count": 371,
    "text": "2.33\nCONFIDENTIALITY:\n\nThe Service Provider, it’s Sub-Service Provider and their personnel shall not, either\nduring the term or within two (2) years after the expiration of this Contract, disclose any\nproprietary or confidential information related to Service/project, this Contract, or\nEmployer’s business or operations without the prior written consent of the Employer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0190",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 190,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 60642,
    "char_end": 60874,
    "char_count": 232,
    "text": "2.34\nINTELLECTUAL PROPERTY RIGHT:\n\nThe Service Provider shall retain the copy right and other intellectual property rights in\nthe Service Provider’s document and other design documents made by (or on behalf of)\nthe Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0191",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 191,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 60876,
    "char_end": 61487,
    "char_count": 611,
    "text": "Subject to the confidentiality obligations, by signing the Contract, within the Contract\nPrice, the Service Provider shall be deemed to give to the Employer a non-terminable,\ntransferable, non-exclusive and royalty-free right to copy, use and communicate the\nService Provider’s documents for the operation, maintenance, repair of the Service and\nStatutory purposes, but not for any other purpose. Such documents of the Service\nProvider shall not be used, copied or communicated to a third party by or on behalf of the\nEmployer for the purposes other than those permitted, without the Service Provider’s\nConsent.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0192",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 192,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 61489,
    "char_end": 61672,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n25",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0193",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 193,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 61674,
    "char_end": 61714,
    "char_count": 40,
    "text": "SECTION - III\n3.0 PERFORMANCE OF SERVICE",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0194",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 194,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 61716,
    "char_end": 62367,
    "char_count": 651,
    "text": "3.1\nEXECUTION OF SERVICES:\n\n3.1.1 All Services shall be provided in strict conformity with the provisions of the Contract\nDocuments and with such explanatory detailed specification and instruction as may be\nfurnished from time to time to the Service Provider by EIC. The Service Provider shall\nundertake to perform all Services under this Contract with all reasonable skill, diligence\nand care in accordance with sound industry practice or international / national standards,\nwherever applicable (as the case may be) to the satisfaction of the Employer and accept\nfull responsibility for the satisfactory quality of such services as performed by them.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0195",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 195,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 62369,
    "char_end": 63021,
    "char_count": 652,
    "text": "3.2\nCHANGES IN SERVICES:\n\n3.2.1 During the performance of the Services, EIC / Employer may make a change in the\nServices within the general scope of this Contract including, but not limited to, changes\nin methodology and minor additions to or deletions from the Services and Service\nProvider shall render the service as changed. Changes of this nature will be affected by a\nwritten order (i.e. Amendment) by the Employer. The time of completion of the said job\nmay be extended for the part of the particular job at the discretion of Engineer-In-Charge,\nfor only such alterations or substitutions of the Services, as he may consider just and\nreasonable.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0196",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 196,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 63023,
    "char_end": 63604,
    "char_count": 581,
    "text": "3.2.2 If any change result in an increase in compensation payable to Service Provider or in\nterms of a credit to be passed on to  Employer, Service Provider shall submit to EIC an\nestimate of the amount of such compensation or credit in a form prescribed by Employer.\nSuch estimates shall be based on the rates shown in the Schedule of Rates. Upon review\nof Service Provider's estimate, Employer shall establish and set forth in the written order\nthe amount of the compensation or credit for the change or a basis for determining a\nreasonable compensation or credit for the change.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0197",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 197,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 63606,
    "char_end": 64812,
    "char_count": 1206,
    "text": "3.3\nACTION AND COMPENSATION IN CASE OF POOR SERVICE:\n\n3.3.1 If it shall appear to the EIC that any service has been rendered with unsound, imperfect or\nunskilled way, or with materials /manpower of any inferior description, or that any\nmaterials / manpower provided by the Service Provider for the execution of the Service\nare unsound, or of a quality inferior to that Contracted for, or otherwise not in accordance\nwith the Contract, the Service Provider shall on demand in writing from the EIC or his\nauthorized representative specifying the Service, materials or manpower complained of\nnotwithstanding that the same may have been inadvertently passed, certified and paid for,\nforthwith rectify the service so specified and at his own cost and in the event of failure to\ndo so within the period specified by the EIC in his demand aforesaid, the Service\nProvider shall be liable to pay compensation at the rate of 1 % (One percent) of the\nestimated cost of the whole Service, for every week limited to a maximum of 10% (ten\npercent) of the value of the whole Service, in event of his failure to do so the EIC may on\nexpiry of notice period rectify/re-execute the Service as the case may be at the risk and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0198",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 198,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 64814,
    "char_end": 64997,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n26",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0199",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 199,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 64999,
    "char_end": 65201,
    "char_count": 202,
    "text": "expense in all respects of the Service Provider or may terminate the contract due to non-\nperformance. The decision of the EIC as to any question arising under this clause shall be\nfinal and conclusive.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0200",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 200,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 65203,
    "char_end": 66040,
    "char_count": 837,
    "text": "3.4\nSUSPENSION OF SERVICES:\n\n3.4.1  Subject to the provisions of sub-para 3.4.2 of this clause, the Service Provider shall, if\nordered in writing by the EIC, temporarily suspend the Services or any part thereof for\nsuch written order and not proceed with the Service therein ordered to be suspended until,\nhe shall have received a written order to proceed therewith. The Service Provider shall\nnot be entitled to claim compensation for any loss or damage sustained by him by reason\nof temporary suspension of the Services aforesaid. An extension of time for completion,\ncorresponding with the delay caused by any such suspension of the Services as aforesaid\nwill be granted to the Service Provider should he apply for the same provided that the\nsuspension was not consequent to any default or failure on the part of the Service\nProvider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0201",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 201,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 66042,
    "char_end": 66225,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "3.4.2  In case of suspensions of entire Service, ordered in writing by EIC, for a period of more\nthan two months, the Service Provider shall have the option to terminate the Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0202",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 202,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 66227,
    "char_end": 67287,
    "char_count": 1060,
    "text": "3.5\nDEFECTS LIABILITY PERIOD:\n\n3.5.1  The Service Provider unless otherwise specified elsewhere in the tender document shall\nguarantee the installation/Service for a period of 12 months from the date of completion\nof Service mentioned in the Completion Certificate issued by the EIC. Any damage or\ndefect that may arise or lie undiscovered at the time of issue of Completion Certificate,\nconnected in any way with the equipment or materials supplied by him or in the\nworkmanship, shall be rectified or replaced by the Service Provider at his own expense as\ndeemed necessary by the EIC. In case of default, the EIC may carry out such services by\nother service provider(s) and deduct actual cost incurred towards labour, supervision and\nmaterials consumables or otherwise plus 15% towards overheads from any sums that may\nthen be or at any time thereafter, become due to the Service Provider or from his Contract\nPerformance Security, or the proceeds of sale thereof or a sufficient part on thereof. The\ndecision of EIC in this regard shall be final and binding.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0203",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 203,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 67289,
    "char_end": 68196,
    "char_count": 907,
    "text": "3.5.2  If the Service Provider feels that any variation in Service or in quality of materials or\nproportions would be beneficial or necessary to fulfill the guarantees called for, he shall\nbring this to the notice of the EIC in writing. If during the period of liability any portion\nof the Service/Equipment, is found defective and is rectified/ replaced, the period of\nliability of 12 months for such equipment/ portion of Service shall be operative from the\ndate such rectification/ replacement are carried out and Contract Performance Guarantee\nshall be furnished separately for the extended period of liability for that portion of\nService/ Equipment only. However, in no such case extension will exceed 24 months\nfrom the date of initial DLP. Notwithstanding the above provisions the supplier's,\nguarantees/warrantees for the replaced/rectified Equipment/Service shall also be passed\non to the Employer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0204",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 204,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 68198,
    "char_end": 68381,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n27",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0205",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 205,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 68383,
    "char_end": 69077,
    "char_count": 694,
    "text": "3.6\nCOMPLETION CERTIFICATE:\n\n3.6.1 APPLICATION FOR COMPLETION CERTIFICATE: When the Service Provider\nfulfills his obligation under the Contract he shall be eligible to apply for Completion\nCertificate. The EIC shall normally issue to the Service Provider the Completion\nCertificate within one month after receiving any application thereof from the Service\nProvider after verifying from the completion documents and satisfying himself that the\nService has been rendered in accordance with and as set out in the Contract Documents.\nThe Service Provider, after obtaining the Completion Certificate, is eligible to present the\nfinal bill for the Service executed by him under the terms of Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0206",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 206,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 69079,
    "char_end": 69261,
    "char_count": 182,
    "text": "Completion of jobs/services for issuance of completion certificate shall constitute\ncompletion of jobs/ services as per provisions of LOA/Contract duly accepted and\ncertified by EIC.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0207",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 207,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 69263,
    "char_end": 69894,
    "char_count": 631,
    "text": "3.6.2  COMPLETION CERTIFICATE: Within one month from receipt of application from\nService Provider  after the completion of the Service in all respects as specified above at\nclause no. 3.6.1, the Service Provider shall be furnished with a certificate by the EIC of\nsuch completion, but no certificate shall be given nor shall the Service be deemed to have\nbeen rendered until all scaffolding, Equipment(s) & machine(s), surplus materials and\nrubbish brought for/ generated during execution of service is cleared off the Site\ncompletely. EIC’s certification about completion of service in all aspects shall be binding\nand conclusive.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0208",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 208,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 69896,
    "char_end": 70041,
    "char_count": 145,
    "text": "3.6.3  COMPLETION CERTIFICATE DOCUMENTS:  For the purpose of Completion, the\nfollowing documents will be deemed to form the completion documents:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0209",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 209,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 70043,
    "char_end": 70313,
    "char_count": 270,
    "text": "i)\nThe technical documents according to which the Service was carried out.\nii)\nMaterial appropriation, Statement for the materials issued by the Employer for the\nService and list of surplus materials returned to the Employer's store duly\nsupported by necessary documents",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0210",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 210,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 70315,
    "char_end": 70470,
    "char_count": 155,
    "text": "3.6.4 EXECUTION CERTIFICATE:\nExecution Certificate against Rate/ Maintenance contract shall be issued by EIC against\nwritten request from Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0211",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 211,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 70472,
    "char_end": 71139,
    "char_count": 667,
    "text": "3.7\n FINAL DECISION & FINAL CERTIFICATE:\n\n3.7.1 Upon expiry of the period of liability and subject to the Engineer-in-Charge being\nsatisfied that the Service Provider has in all respect duly made-up any shortfall and\nperformed all his obligations under the Contract, the Engineer-in- Charge shall (without\nprejudice to the rights of the Employer to retain the provisions of relevant Clause hereof)\notherwise give a certificate herein referred to as the Final Certificate to that effect. The\nService Provider shall not be considered to have fulfilled the whole of his obligations\nunder Contract until Final Certificate shall have been given by the Engineer-In- Charge.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0212",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 212,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 71141,
    "char_end": 71324,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n28",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0213",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 213,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 71326,
    "char_end": 72384,
    "char_count": 1058,
    "text": "3.8\nLIMITATION OF LIABILITY\n\n3.8.1 Notwithstanding anything contrary contained herein, the aggregate total liability of\nService Provider to Employer under the Contract shall not exceed the Total Contract\nValue, except that this clause shall not limit the liability of the Service Provider for\nfollowing:\n(a) In the event of breach of any Applicable Law;\n(b) In the event of fraud, willful misconduct or illegal or unlawful acts, or gross\nNegligence of the Service Provider or any person acting on behalf of the Service\nProvider; or\n(c) In the event of acts or omissions of the Service Provider which are contrary to the\nmost elementary rules of diligence which a conscientious Service Provider would have\nfollowed in similar circumstances; or\n(d) In the event of any claim or loss or damage arising out of infringement of Intellectual\nProperty; or\n(e) For any damage to any third party, including death or injury of any third party caused\nby the Service Provider or any person or firm acting on behalf of the Service Provider in\nexecuting the Works/Services.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0214",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 214,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 72386,
    "char_end": 72633,
    "char_count": 247,
    "text": "However, neither party shall be liable to the other Party for any indirect nor consequential\nloss or damage like loss of use, loss of profit, loss of production or business interruption\nwhich is connected with any claim arising under the Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0215",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 215,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 72635,
    "char_end": 73398,
    "char_count": 763,
    "text": "3.9\nINDEMNITY:\n\n3.9.1 If any action is brought before a Court, Tribunal or any other Authority against the\nEmployer or an officer or agent of the Employer, for the failure, omission or neglect on\nthe part of the Service Provider to perform any acts, matters, covenants or things under\nthe Contract, or damage or injury caused by the alleged omission or negligence on the\npart of the Service Provider, his agents, representatives or his Sub- Service Provider's, or\nin connection with any claim based on lawful demands of Sub-Service Provider's\nservicemen suppliers or employees, the Service Provider, shall in such cases indemnify\nand keep the Employer and/or their representatives harmless from all losses, damages,\nexpenses or decrees arising out of such action.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0216",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 216,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 73400,
    "char_end": 73583,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n29",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0217",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 217,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 73585,
    "char_end": 73597,
    "char_count": 12,
    "text": "SECTION – IV",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0218",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 218,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 73599,
    "char_end": 74499,
    "char_count": 900,
    "text": "4.0\nPAYMENT, INSURANCE AND TAXES\n\n4.1\nDEDUCTION FROM THE CONTRACT PRICE:\n\n4.1.1 All costs, damages or expenses which Employer may have paid or incurred, which under\nthe provisions of the Contract, the Service Provider is liable to pay to the Employer. All\nsuch claims shall be claimed by the Employer from the Service Provider regularly as and\nwhen they fall due. Such claims shall be paid by the Service Provider within 15 (fifteen)\ndays of the receipt of the corresponding bills/ claims and if not paid by the Service\nProvider within the said period, the Employer may, then, deduct the amount from any\nimmediate moneys due to the Service Provider like R.A Bills, Final Bills, Contract\nPerformance Security or any payment becoming due to the Service Provider under the\nContract or may be recovered by actions of law or otherwise, if the Service Provider fails\nto satisfy the Employer of such claims.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0219",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 219,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 74501,
    "char_end": 75425,
    "char_count": 924,
    "text": "4.2\nSCHEDULE OF RATES AND PAYMENTS:\n\n4.2.1  SERVICE PROVIDER'S REMUNERATION:\n\nThe price to be paid by the Employer to Service Provider for the whole of the Service to\nbe done and for the performance of all the obligations undertaken by the Service Provider\nunder the Contract Documents shall be ascertained by the application of the respective\nSchedule of Rates (the inclusive nature of which is more particularly defined by way of\napplication but not of limitation, with the succeeding sub-clause of this clause) and\npayment to be made accordingly for the Services actually executed and approved by the\nEngineer-in-Charge. The sum so ascertained shall (except only as and to the extent\nexpressly provided herein) constitute the sole and inclusive remuneration of the Service\nProvider under the Contract and no further or other payment whatsoever shall be or\nbecome due or payable to the Service Provider under the Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0220",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 220,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 75427,
    "char_end": 76175,
    "char_count": 748,
    "text": "4.2.2  SCHEDULE OF RATES TO BE INCLUSIVE:\n\nThe prices/rates quoted by the Service Provider shall remain firm till the issue of Final\nCertificate and shall not be subject to escalation. Schedule of Rates shall be deemed to\ninclude and cover all costs, expenses and liabilities of every description and all risks of\nevery kind to be taken in rendering the services to the Employer by the Service Provider.\nThe Service Provider shall be deemed to have known the nature, scope, magnitude and\nthe extent of the service though the Contract Document may not fully and precisely\nfurnish/specify them. The Tenderer shall deemed to include the requisite services as may\nbe required to complete the Services properly including remedying of any defect therein.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0221",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 221,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 76177,
    "char_end": 76360,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n30",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0222",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 222,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 76362,
    "char_end": 76443,
    "char_count": 81,
    "text": "4.2.3 SCHEDULE\nOF\nRATES\nTO\nCOVER\nCONSTRUCTION\nEQUIPMENTS,\nMATERIALS, LABOUR ETC.:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0223",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 223,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 76445,
    "char_end": 77153,
    "char_count": 708,
    "text": "Without in any way limiting the provisions of the preceding sub-clause the Schedule of\nRates shall be deemed to include and cover the cost of all construction equipment,\ntemporary work (except as provided for herein), pumps, materials, labour, insurance,\nfuel, consumables, stores & appliances and such other items / equipments / materials as\nrequired for carrying out the services by the Service Provider and all other matters in\nconnection with each item in the Schedule of Rates and the execution of the Service or\nany portion thereof finished, complete in every respect and maintained as shown or\ndescribed in the Contract Documents or as may be ordered in writing during the\ncontinuance of the Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0224",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 224,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 77155,
    "char_end": 78027,
    "char_count": 872,
    "text": "4.2.4 SCHEDULE OF RATES TO COVER ROYALTIES, RENTS AND CLAIMS:\n\nThe Schedule of Rates (i.e., Value of Contract) shall be deemed to include and cover the\ncost of all royalties and fees for the articles and processes, protected by letters, patent or\notherwise incorporated in or used in connection with the Service, also all royalties, rents\nand other payments in connection with obtaining materials of whatsoever kind for the\nService and shall include an indemnity to the Employer which the Service Provider\nhereby gives against all actions, proceedings, claims, damages, costs and expenses arising\nfrom the incorporation in or use in the Service of any such articles, processes or\nmaterials, octroi or other municipal or local Board Charges, if levied on materials,\nequipment or machineries to be brought to site for use for Services shall be borne by the\nService Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0225",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 225,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 78029,
    "char_end": 78658,
    "char_count": 629,
    "text": "4.2.5  SCHEDULE OF RATES TO COVER TAXES AND DUTIES:\n\nNo exemption or reduction of Customs Duties, GST, Works Contract Tax or any port\ndues, transport charges, stamp duties or Central or State Government or local Body or\nMunicipal Taxes or duties, taxes or charges (from or of any other body), entry tax,\nwhatsoever, will be granted or obtained, all of which expenses shall be deemed to be\nincluded in and covered by the Schedule of Rates, unless mentioned specifically\nelsewhere in the Tender Document. The Service Provider shall also obtain and pay for all\npermits/licenses or other privileges necessary to complete the Service.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0226",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 226,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 78660,
    "char_end": 79098,
    "char_count": 438,
    "text": "4.2.6  SCHEDULE OF RATES TO COVER RISKS OF DELAY:\n\nThe Schedule of Rates shall be deemed to include and cover the risk of all possibilities of\ndelay and interference with the Service Provider's conduct/peformance of Services which\noccurs from any causes including orders of the Employer in the exercise of his power and\non account of extension of time granted due to various reasons and for all other possible\nor probable causes of delay.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0227",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 227,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 79100,
    "char_end": 79328,
    "char_count": 228,
    "text": "4.2.7  SCHEDULE OF RATES CANNOT BE ALTERED:\n\nGeneral Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n31",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0228",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 228,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 79330,
    "char_end": 80101,
    "char_count": 771,
    "text": "For Service under unit rate basis, no alteration will be allowed in the Schedule of Rates\nby reason of services or any part of them being modified, altered, extended, diminished\nor committed. The Schedule of Rates are fully inclusive of rates which have been fixed\nby the Service Provider and agreed to by the Employer and cannot be altered. For\nlumpsum Contracts, the payment will be made according to the Service actually carried\nout, for which purpose an item wise, or work wise Schedule of Rates shall be furnished,\nsuitable for evaluating the value of Service provided and preparing running account bill.\nPayment for any additional Service which is not covered in the Schedule of Rates shall\nonly be released on issuance of Amendment to LOA/Contract by the Employer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0229",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 229,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 80103,
    "char_end": 80266,
    "char_count": 163,
    "text": "4.3\nPROCEDURE FOR BILLING OF SERVICES:\n\n4.3.1   BILLING PROCEDURE:\n\nFollowing procedures shall be adopted for billing of services executed by the Service\nProvider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0230",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 230,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 80268,
    "char_end": 80599,
    "char_count": 331,
    "text": "4.3.1.1 The Bill(s) complete in all respect with details and enclosure(s) is to be submitted  by\nService Provider in line with terms of  the Contract. Employer shall make all endeavour\nto release payments of undisputed amount of the bills submitted within 15 (Fifteen) days\nfrom the date of certification by the Engineer-in-Charge.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0231",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 231,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 80601,
    "char_end": 80900,
    "char_count": 299,
    "text": "4.3.1.2 COMPUTERISED\nBILLING\nSYSTEM:\nGAIL\nGas\nLimited\nhas\nintroduced\nComputerised Billing System whereby whenever the Bill(s) are submitted in GAIL Gas\nby a Service Provider, a receipt number is usually generated. The Service Provider may\nalso know the status of the Bill through GAIL Gas’s website.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0232",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 232,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 80902,
    "char_end": 81117,
    "char_count": 215,
    "text": "4.3.2  MODE OF MEASUREMENT:\n\nThe payment shall be made based on the mode of measurement as specified in the\nContract. Otherwise, the mode of measurement shall be adopted as per latest Indian\nStandard Specifications.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0233",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 233,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 81119,
    "char_end": 82223,
    "char_count": 1104,
    "text": "4.4\nNOTICE OF CLAIMS FOR ADDITIONAL PAYMENTS:\n\n4.4.1  Should the Service Provider consider that he is entitled to any extra payment for any\nextra/additional Job(s)/Service(s) or material change in original Specifications carried out\nby him in respect of job, he shall forthwith give notice in writing to the Engineer-in-\nCharge that he claims extra payment. Such notice shall be given to the Engineer-in-\nCharge upon which Service Provider bases such claims and such notice shall contain full\nparticulars of the nature of such claim with full details of amount claimed. Irrespective of\nany provision in the Contract to the contrary, the Service Provider must intimate his\nintention to lodge claim on the Employer within 10 (ten) days of the commencement of\nhappening of the event and quantify the claim within 30 (thirty) days, failing which the\nService Provider will lose his right to claim any compensation/reimbursement/damages\netc.. Failure on the part of Service Provider to put forward any claim without the\nnecessary particulars as above within the time above specified shall be an absolute waiver",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0234",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 234,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 82225,
    "char_end": 82408,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n32",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0235",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 235,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 82410,
    "char_end": 82572,
    "char_count": 162,
    "text": "thereof. No omission by Employer to reject any such claim and no delay in dealing\ntherewith shall be waiver by Employer of any of these rights in respect thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0236",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 236,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 82574,
    "char_end": 84014,
    "char_count": 1440,
    "text": "4.4.2  Engineer-in-Charge shall review such claims within a reasonable period of time and\ncause to discharge these in a manner considered appropriate after due deliberations\nthereon. However, Service Provider shall be obliged to carry on with the Jobs/services\nduring the period in which his claims are under consideration by the Employer,\nirrespective of the outcome of such claims, where additional payments for Services\nconsidered extra are justifiable in accordance with the Contract provisions, Employer\nshall arrange to release the same in the same manner as for normal job payments. Such of\nthe extra services so admitted by Employer shall be governed by all the terms, conditions,\nstipulations and specifications as are applicable for the Contract. The rates for extra\nservices shall generally be the unit rates provided for in the Contract. In the event unit\nrates for extra services so executed are not available as per Contract, payments may either\nbe released on day work basis for which daily/hourly rates for workmen and hourly rates\nfor equipment rental shall apply, or on the unit rate for Services executed shall be derived\nby interpolation/ extrapolation of unit rates already existing in the Contract. In all the\nmatters pertaining to applicability of rate and admittance of otherwise of an extra service\nclaim(s) of Service Provider, the decision of Engineer-in-Charge shall be final and\nbinding on the Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0237",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 237,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 84016,
    "char_end": 84574,
    "char_count": 558,
    "text": "4.5\nINSURANCE:\n\n4.5.1 Service Provider shall, at his own expense, arrange appropriate insurance to cover all\nrisks assumed by the Service Provider under this Contract in respect of its personnel\ndeputed under this Contract as well as Service Provider’s equipment, tools and any other\nbelongings of the Service Provider or their personnel during the entire period of their\nengagement in connection with this Contract. Employer will have no liability on this\naccount. The Personnel covered must be covered to meet the liability under Employee\nCompensation Act.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0238",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 238,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 84576,
    "char_end": 84691,
    "char_count": 115,
    "text": "4.5.2 The provisions of this Clause shall in no way limit the liability of the Service Provider\nunder the Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0239",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 239,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 84693,
    "char_end": 85006,
    "char_count": 313,
    "text": "4.5.3 If the Service Provider neglects, fails, or refuses to obtain or maintain insurances required\nto be effected, or fails to provide certification etc., the Employer has the right to procure\nand maintain policies at Service Provider’s expense plus administrative cost of 10% of\nthe amount of Insurance premium.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0240",
