    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 87263,
    "char_end": 87629,
    "char_count": 366,
    "text": "i)\ntype and amounts of insurance as required herein;\nii)\ninsurance company or companies carrying the aforesaid coverage;\niii)\neffective and expiry dates of policies;\niv)\nthat the Employer may give advance notice for any material change in the policy.\nwaiver of subrogation endorsement has been attached to all policies; and\nv)\nthe territorial limits of all policies.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0252",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 252,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 87631,
    "char_end": 88128,
    "char_count": 497,
    "text": "4.5.7 If any of the above policies expire or are cancelled during the terms of the service, and\nService Provider fails for any reason to renew such policies, the Employer may replace\nsame and recover the charges towards  premium plus administrative charges from Service\nProvider. Should there be a lapse in any insurance required to be carried out by the\nService Provider hereunder for any reason, losses & penalty, if any resulting there from\nshall be to the sole account of the Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0253",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 253,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 88130,
    "char_end": 88313,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n34",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0254",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 254,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 88315,
    "char_end": 88491,
    "char_count": 176,
    "text": "4.5.8 Service Provider shall require all its Sub-Service Providers to provide such foregoing\ninsurance cover as the Service Provider is obligated to provide under the Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0255",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 255,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 88493,
    "char_end": 88952,
    "char_count": 459,
    "text": "4.5.9 WAIVER OF SUBROGATION: All insurance policies of the Service Provider with\nrespect to the operations conducted hereunder, shall be endorsed by the underwriter in\naccordance with the following policy wording:“ The insurers hereby waive their rights of\nsubrogation against any individual, Employer, affiliates or assignees for whom or with\nwhom the assured may be operating to the extent of the Contractual indemnities\nundertaken by the Service Provider”.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0256",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 256,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 88954,
    "char_end": 89168,
    "char_count": 214,
    "text": "4.5.10 Deductible: That portion of any loss not covered by insurance provided for in this article\nsolely by reason of deductible provision in such insurance policies shall be to the account\nof the Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0257",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 257,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 89170,
    "char_end": 90717,
    "char_count": 1547,
    "text": "4.6\nTAXES AND DUTIES:\n\n4.6.1 The Service Provider, unless specified otherwise elsewhere in the Contract agrees to and\ndoes hereby accept full and exclusive liability for the payment of any and all Taxes,\nDuties, including GST now or hereafter imposed, increased, modified from time to time\nin respect of Services and materials and all contributions and taxes for unemployment\ncompensation, insurance and old age pensions or annuities now or hereafter imposed by\nany Central or State Government authorities which are imposed with respect to or\ncovered by the wages, salaries, or other compensations paid to the persons employed by\nthe Service Provider and the Service Provider shall be responsible for the compliance of\nall Sub-Service Providers, with all applicable Central, State,  Municipal and local law and\nregulation and requirement of any Central, State or local Government agency or\nauthority. Service Provider further agrees to defend, indemnify and hold Employer\nharmless from any liability or penalty which may be imposed by the Central, State or\nLocal authorities by reason or any violation by Service Provider or Sub- Sub-Service\nProvider of such laws, suits or proceedings that may be brought against the Employer\narising under, growing out of, or by reason of the service provided for by this Contract,\nby third parties, or by Central or State Government authority or any administrative sub-\ndivision thereof. Tax deductions will be made as per the rules and regulations in force in\naccordance with acts prevailing from time to time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0258",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 258,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 90719,
    "char_end": 90936,
    "char_count": 217,
    "text": "4.6.2 Service Provider shall ensure timely submission of correct invoice(s) with all required\nsupporting document(s) as per Contract within a period specified in Contracts to enable\nEmployer to avail Input Tax Credit.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0259",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 259,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 90938,
    "char_end": 91340,
    "char_count": 402,
    "text": "If Input Tax credit with respect to GST is not available to Employer for any reason which\nis not attributable to Employer, then Employer shall not be obligated or liable to pay or\nreimburse GST charged in the invoice(s)  and shall be entitled to / deduct/ setoff /recover\nthe such GST together with all penalties and interest if any, against any amounts paid or\npayable by Employer to Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0260",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 260,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 91342,
    "char_end": 91525,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n35",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0261",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 261,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 91527,
    "char_end": 92116,
    "char_count": 589,
    "text": "4.6.3 Where Employer has the obligation to discharge tax liability under reverse charge\nmechanism and Employer has paid or is /liable to pay GST to the Government on which\ninterest or penalties becomes payable as per rules (as amended from time to time) for any\nreason which  is not  attributable to Employer or Input Tax credit with respect to such\npayments  is  not available to Employer for any reason which  is not  attributable to\nEmployer, then Employer shall be entitled to  deduct/ setoff / recover such  amounts\nagainst any amounts paid or payable by Employer to Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0262",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 262,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 92118,
    "char_end": 93141,
    "char_count": 1023,
    "text": "4.7\nINCOME TAX:\n\n4.7.1  Income Tax deduction shall be made from all payments of the Service Provider as per\nrules and regulation in force in accordance with the Income Tax Act prevailing from time\nto time. As per the provisions of the income Tax Act, 1961, Permanent Account No.\n(PAN) is compulsorily required to be mentioned in Tax Deduction at Source (TDS)\ncertificate issued to the payee. Therefore, the bidder must submit the details of PAN / the\ncopy of application filed for allotment of PAN (if PAN no. not available) to EIC\nimmediately on receipt of FOA/Contract Document, failing which, TDS will be applied\nas per applicable law and TDS certificate will not be issued. Therefore, in case the\nService Provider does not furnish PAN, EMPLOYER shall deduct at source as provided\nin the Income Tax Act 1961, or in the relevant Finance Act, or as directed in the orders\nu/s 195(3) or 197 or 195(2), as the case may be, or at such higher rate as may be required\nby Section 206AA of Income Tax Act 1961, from time to time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0263",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 263,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 93143,
    "char_end": 93836,
    "char_count": 693,
    "text": "4.7.2  In case of foreign bidder, the Service Provider must apply through the local embassy /\nconsulate of India for obtaining PAN card. In case, foreign Service Provider don’t have\nthe PAN, then amount will be deducted and deposited as per law and TDS certificate will\nalso not be provided. Further, such Service Provider shall comply all other provisions\nmentioned elsewhere in the Tender Document related to making remittances to non-\nresidents including Permanent Establishment, Tax Residency Certificate (TRC) if non-\nresident desire to avail benefits available under Double Tax Avoidance Agreement\n(DTAA), Withholding Tax etc., as per Income Tax Act, 1961 (as amended from time to\ntime).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0264",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 264,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 93838,
    "char_end": 94492,
    "char_count": 654,
    "text": "4.8\nSTATUTORY VARIATIONS:\n\n4.8.1  All duties, taxes (except where otherwise expressly provided in the Contract) as may be\nlevied / imposed in consequences of execution of the Jobs/Services or in relation thereto\nor in connection therewith as per the Acts, Laws, Rules, Regulations in force on the due\ndate of submission of Bid for this Contract shall be to Service Provider’s account. Any\nincrease / decrease in such duties, taxes after the due date of submission of bid but within\nthe Contractual completion date as stipulated in the Contract will be to the account of\nEmployer subject to submission of documentary proof to the satisfaction of Employer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0265",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 265,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 94494,
    "char_end": 94847,
    "char_count": 353,
    "text": "4.8.2  Any increase in the duties and taxes after the Contractual completion period will be to the\nService Provider’s account, where delay in completion /mobilization period is\nattributable to the Service Provider and the taxes & duties are not cenvatable (i.e. Input\nTax Credit (ITC) not available). In case of applicability of ITC / cenvatable taxes &",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0266",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 266,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 94849,
    "char_end": 95032,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n36",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0267",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 267,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 95034,
    "char_end": 95249,
    "char_count": 215,
    "text": "duties, payment shall be made as per the prevailing rates during the currency of the\nContract. However, any benefit of decrease in duties and taxes after the Contractual\ncompletion will be passed on to the Employer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0268",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 268,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 95251,
    "char_end": 96235,
    "char_count": 984,
    "text": "4.8.3 In the event of introduction of any new legislation or any change or amendment or\nenforcement of any Act or Law, rules or regulations of Government of India or State\nGovernment(s) or Public Body which becomes effective after the due date of submission\nof Bid for this Contract but within the Contractual completion period (including extended\nperiod allowed due to reasons attributed to Employer) and which results in increased cost\nof the jobs/services under the Contract through increased liability of taxes, (other than\npersonnel and Corporate taxes), duties, the Service Provider shall be indemnified for any\nsuch increased cost by the Employer subject to the production of documentary  proof to\nthe satisfaction of the Employer to the extent which directly is attributable to such\nintroduction of new legislation or change or amendment as mentioned above and\nadjudication by the competent authority & the courts wherever levy of such taxes / duties\nare disputed by Employer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0269",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 269,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 96237,
    "char_end": 96913,
    "char_count": 676,
    "text": "4.8.4  Similarly, in the event of introduction of new legislation or any change or amendment or\nenforcement of any Act or Law, rules or regulations of Government of India or State\nGovernment(s) or Public Body which becomes effective after the due date of submission\nof Bid for this Contract and which results in any decrease in the cost of the services/ jobs\nthrough reduced liability of taxes, (other than personnel and Corporate taxes) duties, the\nService Provider shall pass on the benefits of such reduced cost, taxes or duties to the\nEmployer, to the extent which is directly attributable to such introduction of new\nlegislation or change or amendment as mentioned above.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0270",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 270,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 96915,
    "char_end": 97448,
    "char_count": 533,
    "text": "4.9\nDAMAGES TO PROPERTY, ANY PERSON AND THIRD PARTY\n\ni)\nService Provider shall be responsible for making good to the satisfaction of the\nEmployer any loss or any damage to structures and properties belonging to the\nEmployer or being executed or procured or being procured by the Employer or of\nother agencies within in the premises of the Employer, if such loss or damage is\ndue to fault and/or the Negligence or Willful Misconduct or omission of the\nService Provider, his employees, agents, representatives or Sub-Service Providers.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0271",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 271,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 97450,
    "char_end": 98202,
    "char_count": 752,
    "text": "ii)\nThe Service Provider shall take sufficient care in moving his equipments and\nmaterials from one place to another so that they do not cause any damage to any\nperson or to the property of the Employer or any third party including overhead\nand underground cables and in the event of any damage resulting to the property\nof the Employer or of a third party during the movement of the aforesaid\nequipment or materials the cost of such damages including eventual loss of\nproduction, operation or services in any plant or establishment as estimated by the\nEmployer or ascertained or demanded by the third party shall be borne by the\nService Provider. Third party liability risk shall be Rupees One lakh for single\naccident and limited to Rupees Ten lakhs.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0272",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 272,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 98204,
    "char_end": 98387,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n37",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0273",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 273,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 98389,
    "char_end": 98753,
    "char_count": 364,
    "text": "iii)\nThe Service Provider shall indemnify and keep the Employer harmless of all\nclaims for damages to property other than Employer's property arising under or by\nreason of this agreement, if such claims result from the fault and/or Negligence or\nWillful Misconduct or omission of the Service Provider, his employees, agents,\nrepresentative of Sub-Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0274",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 274,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 98755,
    "char_end": 98938,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n38",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0275",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 275,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 98940,
    "char_end": 98951,
    "char_count": 11,
    "text": "SECTION – V",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0276",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 276,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 98953,
    "char_end": 99090,
    "char_count": 137,
    "text": "5.0\nLAWS, HEALTH, SAFETY & ENVIRONMENT\n\n5.1\nLABOUR LAWS:\n\ni)\nNo labour below the age of 18 (eighteen) years shall be employed on the Job.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0277",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 277,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 99092,
    "char_end": 99207,
    "char_count": 115,
    "text": "ii)\nThe Service Provider shall not pay less than what is provided under law to\nlabourers engaged by him on the Job.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0278",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 278,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 99209,
    "char_end": 99337,
    "char_count": 128,
    "text": "iii)\nThe Service Provider shall at his expense comply with all labour laws and keep\nthe Employer indemnified in respect thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0279",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 279,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 99339,
    "char_end": 99446,
    "char_count": 107,
    "text": "iv)\nThe Service Provider shall pay equal wages for men and women in accordance\nwith applicable labour laws.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0280",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 280,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 99448,
    "char_end": 99800,
    "char_count": 352,
    "text": "v)\nIf the Service Provider is covered under the Contract labour (Regulation and\nAbolition) Act, he shall obtain a license from licensing authority (i.e. office of the\nlabour commissioner) by payment of necessary prescribed fee and the deposit, if\nany, before starting the Job under the Contract. Such fee/deposit shall be borne by\nthe Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0281",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 281,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 99802,
    "char_end": 100151,
    "char_count": 349,
    "text": "vi)\nThe Service Provider shall employ labour in sufficient numbers either directly or\nthrough Sub- Service Provider's to maintain the required rate of progress and of\nquality to ensure workmanship of the degree specified in the Contract while also\nensuring that workman is not stressed due to long hour of working and to the\nsatisfaction of the EIC.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0282",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 282,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 100153,
    "char_end": 100857,
    "char_count": 704,
    "text": "vii)\nThe Service Provider shall furnish to the EIC the distribution return of the number\nand description, by trades of the service people employed on the services. The\nService Provider shall also submit on the 4th and 19th of every month to the EIC\na true statement showing in respect of the second half of the preceding month and\nthe first half of the current month (1) the accidents that occurred during the said\nfortnight showing the circumstances under which they happened and the extent of\ndamage and injury caused by them and (2) the number of female workers who\nhave been allowed Maternity Benefit as provided in the Maternity Benefit Act\n1961 on Rules made thereunder and the amount paid to them.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0283",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 283,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 100859,
    "char_end": 101331,
    "char_count": 472,
    "text": "viii)\nThe Service Provider shall comply with the provisions of the payment of Wage\nAct 1936, Employee Provident Fund Act 1952, Minimum Wages Act 1948.\nEmployers Liability Act 1938. Servicemen's Compensation Act 1923, Industrial\nDisputes Act 1947, the Maternity Benefit Act 1961 and Contract Labour\nRegulation and Abolition Act 1970, Employment of Children Act 1938 or any\nmodifications thereof or any other law relating thereto and rules made thereunder\nfrom time to time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0284",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 284,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 101333,
    "char_end": 101516,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n39",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0285",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 285,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 101518,
    "char_end": 102080,
    "char_count": 562,
    "text": "ix)\nThe EIC shall on a report having been made by an Inspecting Officer as defined\nin Contract Labour (Regulation and Abolition) Act 1970 have the power to deduct\nfrom the money due to the Service Provider any sum required or estimated to be\nrequired for making good the loss suffered by a worker or workers by reason of\nnon- fulfilment of the Conditions of the Contract for the benefit of workers, non-\npayment of wages or of deductions made from his or their wages which are not\njustified by the terms of the Contract or non-observance of the said regulations.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0286",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 286,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 102082,
    "char_end": 103422,
    "char_count": 1340,
    "text": "x)\nThe Service Provider shall indemnify the Employer against any payments to be\nmade under and for the observance of the provisions of the aforesaid Acts without\nprejudice to his right to obtain indemnity from his Sub-Service Provider's. In the\nevent of the Service Provider committing a default or breach of any of the\nprovisions of the aforesaid Acts as amended from time to time, of furnishing any\ninformation or submitting or filling and Form/ Register/ Slip under the provisions\nof these Acts which is materially incorrect then on the report of the inspecting\nOfficers, the Service Provider shall without prejudice to any other liability pay to\nthe Employer a sum not exceeding Rs.10000.00 as Liquidated Damages for every\ndefault, breach or furnishing, making, submitting, filling materially incorrect\nstatement as may be fixed by the EIC and in the event of the Service Provider's\ndefault continuing in this respect, the Liquidated Damages may be enhanced to\nRs.5000.00 per day for each day of default subject to a maximum of one percent\nof the estimated cost of the Services put to the Contract. The EIC shall deduct\nsuch amount from bills or Contract Performance Security of the Service Provider\nand credit the same to the Welfare Fund constitute under these acts. The decision\nof the EIC in this respect shall be final and binding.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0287",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 287,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 103424,
    "char_end": 103793,
    "char_count": 369,
    "text": "5.2\nSAFETY REGULATIONS:\n\ni)\nIn respect of all labour, directly employed in the Service for the performance of\nService Provider's part of this agreement, the Service Provider shall at his own\nexpense arrange for all the safety provisions as per safety codes of C.P.W.D.,\nIndian Standards Institution. The Electricity Act, The Mines Act and such other\nacts as applicable.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0288",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 288,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 103795,
    "char_end": 104194,
    "char_count": 399,
    "text": "ii)\nThe Service Provider shall observe and abide by all fire and safety regulations of\nthe Employer. Before starting service, Service Provider shall consult with\nEmployer's safety Engineers or EIC and must make good to the satisfaction of the\nEmployer any loss or damage due to fire to any portion of the service done or to\nbe done under this agreement or to any of the Employer's existing property.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0289",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 289,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 104196,
    "char_end": 104348,
    "char_count": 152,
    "text": "5.3\nFIRST AID AND INDUSTRIAL INJURIES:\n\ni)\nService Provider shall maintain first aid facilities for its employees and those of\nits Sub-Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0290",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 290,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 104350,
    "char_end": 104516,
    "char_count": 166,
    "text": "ii)\nService Provider shall make outside arrangements for ambulance service and for\nthe treatment of industrial injuries. Names of those providing these services shall",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0291",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 291,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 104518,
    "char_end": 104701,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n40",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0292",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 292,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 104703,
    "char_end": 104834,
    "char_count": 131,
    "text": "be furnished to Employer prior to start and their telephone numbers shall be\nprominently posted in Service Provider's field office.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0293",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 293,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 104836,
    "char_end": 105058,
    "char_count": 222,
    "text": "iii)\nAll critical industrial injuries shall be reported promptly to Employer, and a copy\nof Service Provider's report covering each personal injury requiring the attention\nof a physician shall be furnished to the Employer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0294",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 294,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 105060,
    "char_end": 105430,
    "char_count": 370,
    "text": "5.4\nGENERAL RULES:\n\n5.4.1 Smoking within the battery area, tank farm, dock limits or any such area identified by\nEIC or mentioned in SCC or any guideline, is strictly prohibited. Violators of the no\nsmoking rules shall be discharged immediately after imposing the applicable penalty(ies).\nDecision of EIC in the matter shall be final and binding on the Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0295",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 295,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 105432,
    "char_end": 105721,
    "char_count": 289,
    "text": "5.5\nCARE IN HANDLING INFLAMMABLE GAS:\n\n5.5.1 The Service Provider has to ensure all precautionary measures and exercise utmost care\nin handling the inflammable gas cylinder/inflammable liquids/paints etc. as required\nunder the law and/or as advised by the fire Authorities of the Employer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0296",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 296,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 105723,
    "char_end": 106352,
    "char_count": 629,
    "text": "5.6\nPRESERVATION OF PLACE:\n\n5.6.1 The Service Provider shall take requisite precautions and use his best endeavors to\nprevent any riotous or unlawful behavior by or amongst his worker / personnel employed\nfor the services and for the preservation of peace and protection of the inhabitants and\nsecurity of property in the neighborhood of the Site. In the event of the Employer\nrequiring the maintenance of a Special Police Force at or in the vicinity of the site during\nthe tenure of services, the expenses thereof shall be borne by the Service Provider and if\npaid by the Employer shall be recoverable from the Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0297",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 297,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 106354,
    "char_end": 107176,
    "char_count": 822,
    "text": "5.7\nENVIRONMENT:\n\n5.7.1 Employer acknowledges their commitment to conduct their respective operations in a\nmanner which not only complies with all relevant environmental protection and pollution\ncontrol legislation but also such operations do not cause environmental damage or\npollution and in a manner which acknowledges other cultural and associated\nconsiderations. In recognition of this commitment, the Service Provider shall perform the\nservices in such a way as to avoid or minimize environmental damage or pollution and\nfully recognize the special aspects of the environment as communicated by Employer or\nas applicable. Service Provider shall comply with, and the Service Provider shall ensure\ncompliance with all applicable environmental protection and pollution control legislation\nas it relates to the services.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0298",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 298,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 107178,
    "char_end": 107301,
    "char_count": 123,
    "text": "5.7.2 In the furtherance of any laws, regulations and rules promulgated by the Government of\nIndia, Service Provider shall:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0299",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 299,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 107303,
    "char_end": 107486,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n41",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0300",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 300,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 107488,
    "char_end": 107691,
    "char_count": 203,
    "text": "-\nEmploy good international oil & gas  industry practices, including as required,\nadvanced techniques, practices and methods of operation for the prevention of\nenvironmental damage in conducting the job;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0301",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 301,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 107693,
    "char_end": 107913,
    "char_count": 220,
    "text": "-\nTake necessary and adequate steps to prevent environmental damage and, where\nsome adverse impact on the environment is unavoidable, minimize such damage and\nthe consequential effects thereof of property and people; and",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0302",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 302,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 107915,
    "char_end": 108033,
    "char_count": 118,
    "text": "-\nAdhere to the guidelines, limitations or restrictions, if any, imposed by the\nenvironmental clearance as applicable.",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0303",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 303,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 108035,
    "char_end": 108825,
    "char_count": 790,
    "text": "5.7.3 If during the Service Provider's performance of the services, the Employer is of the\nopinion that the Service Provider is either not conducting the services in strict compliance\nwith this Contract or is conducting the services in such a way as to endanger the\nenvironment or in such a way as to risk being in breach of any environmental protection\nor pollution control legislation, then the Employer shall notify the Service Provider in\nwriting of the conduct involved and the Service Provider shall initiate corrective action to\nthe reasonable satisfaction of the Employer within twenty four (24) hours of the conduct\nso notified or as decided by EIC. Employer may, require Service Provider to discontinue\nthe Service in whole or in part until Service Provider has taken such action.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0304",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 304,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 108827,
    "char_end": 109199,
    "char_count": 372,
    "text": "5.7.4 The Service Provider shall notify the Employer as soon as reasonably practicable of any\nspillage or potential spillage of petroleum or any act of pollution or potentially polluting\nevent. For each and any such event the Service Provider shall record the relevant\ninformation on the incident report form and shall deliver the completed form to the\nEmployer forthwith.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0305",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 305,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 109201,
    "char_end": 109958,
    "char_count": 757,
    "text": "5.7.5 After completion of the entire job as per this Contract and prior to Demobilization,\nService Provider shall at its expense satisfactorily dispose off all rubbish, remove all\ntemporary work, equipment and materials belonging to Service Provider and return to\nEmployer warehouse all surplus spares and salvageable Employer supplied materials.\nFurther, the Service Provider can take away the brought out Service Provider supplied\nsurplus Material (i.e. Materials brought by the Service Provider for work/Services at site\nunder Contract, not used by them for work/Services and leftover at the Site) subject to\nprior written consent of the EIC. The payment made, if any, towards such surplus\nMaterial will be recovered from the payment of Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0306",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 306,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 109960,
    "char_end": 110154,
    "char_count": 194,
    "text": "Service Provider shall leave the premises in a neat and safe condition. Service Provider\nshall be required to leave all, sites and surrounding area as it existed at the\ncommencement of Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0307",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 307,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 110156,
    "char_end": 110185,
    "char_count": 29,
    "text": "5.7.6 Service Provider shall:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0308",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 308,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 110187,
    "char_end": 110529,
    "char_count": 342,
    "text": "Ensure that the pertinent completed environmental impact studies including the Rapid\nEnvironmental Impact Assessment carried out by Employer are made available to its\nPersonnel and to its Sub-Service Providers to develop adequate and proper awareness of\nthe measures and methods of environmental protection to be used in carrying out the job;",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0309",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 309,
    "page_start": 42,
    "page_end": 42,
    "char_start": 110531,
    "char_end": 110714,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n42",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0310",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 310,
    "page_start": 42,
    "page_end": 42,
    "char_start": 110716,
    "char_end": 110951,
    "char_count": 235,
    "text": "Ensure and maintain at his own cost all lights, guards, fencing, warning signs and\nwatching, when and where necessary or required by the EIC, for the protection of the\nServices or for the safety and convenience of the public or others.",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0311",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 311,
    "page_start": 42,
    "page_end": 42,
    "char_start": 110953,
    "char_end": 111132,
    "char_count": 179,
    "text": "Ensure that the Contracts entered into between Service Provider and its Sub Service\nProviders (if allowed) relating to the Services shall include the provisions stipulated\nherein;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0312",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 312,
    "page_start": 42,
    "page_end": 42,
    "char_start": 111134,
    "char_end": 111453,
    "char_count": 319,
    "text": "-\nbe responsible for the removal from the Site or for otherwise making safe in\naccordance with applicable Indian laws and directives any materials generated or\nreleased by Service Provider during its activities at the Site which are toxic or\nsimilarly hazardous to the health or safety of persons or to the environment;",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0313",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 313,
    "page_start": 42,
    "page_end": 42,
    "char_start": 111455,
    "char_end": 111895,
    "char_count": 440,
    "text": "-\nbe liable for and shall indemnify, protect, defend and hold harmless Employer from\nand against any and all demands, claims, suits and causes of action and any and all\nliability, costs, expenses, settlements and judgments incurred in connection therewith\n(including court costs and attorney’s fees incurred by Employer) arising out of such\ntoxic or hazardous materials for which the Service Provider is responsible pursuant to\nthis Clause.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0314",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 314,
    "page_start": 43,
    "page_end": 43,
    "char_start": 111897,
    "char_end": 112080,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n43",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0315",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 315,
    "page_start": 43,
    "page_end": 43,
    "char_start": 112082,
    "char_end": 112134,
    "char_count": 52,
    "text": "SECTION – VI\n6.0\nDISPUTE RESOLUTION AND ARBITRATION:",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0316",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 316,
    "page_start": 43,
    "page_end": 43,
    "char_start": 112136,
    "char_end": 112812,
    "char_count": 676,
    "text": "6.1\nDISPUTE RESOLUTION:\n\n6.1.1 GAIL Gas Limited has framed the Conciliation Rules 2010 in conformity with\nsupplementary to Part – III of the Indian Arbitration and Conciliation Act 1996 for\nspeedier, cost effective and amicable settlement of disputes through conciliation. A copy\nof the said rules made available on GAIL Gas’s web site https://gailgas.com for\nreference. Unless otherwise specified, the matters where decision of the Engineer-in-\nCharge is deemed to be final and binding as provided in the Contract and the\nissues/disputes which cannot be mutually resolved within a reasonable time, all disputes\nshall be settled in accordance with the Conciliation Rules 2010.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0317",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 317,
    "page_start": 43,
    "page_end": 43,
    "char_start": 112814,
    "char_end": 113019,
    "char_count": 205,
    "text": "6.1.2 Any dispute(s)/difference(s)/issue(s) of any kind whatsoever between/amongst the Parties\narising under/out of/in connection with this Contract shall be settled in accordance with\nthe aforesaid rules.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0318",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 318,
    "page_start": 43,
    "page_end": 43,
    "char_start": 113021,
    "char_end": 113604,
    "char_count": 583,
    "text": "6.1.3 In case of any dispute(s)/difference(s)/issue(s), a Party shall notify the other Party (ies) in\nwriting about such a dispute(s) / difference(s) / issue(s) between / amongst the Parties and\nthat such a Party wishes to refer the dispute(s)/ difference(s)/issue(s) to Conciliation.\nSuch Invitation for Conciliation shall contain sufficient information as to the\ndispute(s)/difference(s)/issue(s) to enable the other Party (ies) to be fully informed as to\nthe nature of the dispute(s)/ difference(s) /issue(s), the amount of monetary claim, if any,\nand apparent cause(s) of action.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0319",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 319,
    "page_start": 43,
    "page_end": 43,
    "char_start": 113606,
    "char_end": 113830,
    "char_count": 224,
    "text": "6.1.4 Conciliation proceedings commence when the other Party(ies) accept(s) the invitation to\nconciliate and confirmed in writing. If the other Party (ies) reject(s) the invitation, there\nwill be no conciliation proceedings.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0320",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 320,
    "page_start": 43,
    "page_end": 43,
    "char_start": 113832,
    "char_end": 114192,
    "char_count": 360,
    "text": "6.1.5 If the Party initiating conciliation does not receive a reply within thirty days from the date\non which he/she sends the invitation, or within such other period of time as specified in\nthe invitation, he/she may elect to treat this as a rejection of the invitation to conciliate. If\nhe/she so elects, he/she shall inform the other Party(ies) accordingly.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0321",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 321,
    "page_start": 43,
    "page_end": 43,
    "char_start": 114194,
    "char_end": 114780,
    "char_count": 586,
    "text": "6.1.6 Where Invitation for Conciliation has been furnished, the Parties shall attempt to settle\nsuch dispute(s) amicably under Part-III of the Indian Arbitration and Conciliation Act,\n1996 and GAIL Gas Limited Conciliation Rules, 2013. It would be only after exhausting\nthe option of Conciliation as an Alternate Dispute Resolution Mechanism that the Parties\nhereto shall go for Arbitration in terms of clause no. 6.2. For the purpose of this clause,\nthe option of ‘Conciliation’ shall be deemed to have been exhausted, even in case of\nrejection of ‘Conciliation’ by any of the Parties.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0322",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 322,
    "page_start": 43,
    "page_end": 43,
    "char_start": 114782,
    "char_end": 115003,
    "char_count": 221,
    "text": "6.1.7 The cost of Conciliation proceedings including but not limited to fees for Conciliator(s),\nAirfare, Local Transport, Accommodation, cost towards conference facility etc. shall be\nborne by the Parties in equal share.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0323",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 323,
    "page_start": 44,
    "page_end": 44,
    "char_start": 115005,
    "char_end": 115188,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n44",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0324",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 324,
    "page_start": 44,
    "page_end": 44,
    "char_start": 115190,
    "char_end": 115516,
    "char_count": 326,
    "text": "6.1.8 The Parties shall freeze claim(s) of interest, if any, and shall not claim the same during\nthe pendency of Conciliation proceedings. The Settlement Agreement, as and when\nreached/agreed upon, shall be signed between the Parties and Conciliation proceedings\nshall stand terminated on the date of the Settlement Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0325",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 325,
    "page_start": 44,
    "page_end": 44,
    "char_start": 115518,
    "char_end": 116922,
    "char_count": 1404,
    "text": "6.2\nARBITRATION:\n\n6.2.1  If the issues/disputes which cannot be resolved through dispute resolution mechanism\npursuant to clause no. 6.1, all disputes such shall be referred to arbitration by Sole\nArbitrator. The Employer shall suggest a panel of three independent and distinguished\npersons to the /Service Provider to select any one among them to act as the Sole\nArbitrator. In the event of failure of the other parties to select the Sole Arbitrator within\n30 days from the receipt of the communication suggesting the panel of arbitrators, the\nright of selection of the sole arbitrator by the other party shall stand forfeited and the\nEmployer shall have discretion to proceed with the appointment of the Sole Arbitrator.\nThe decision of Employer on the appointment of the sole arbitrator shall be final and\nbinding on the parties. The award of sole arbitrator shall be final and binding on the\nparties and unless directed/awarded otherwise by the sole arbitrator, the cost of\narbitration proceedings shall be shared equally by the parties. The Arbitration\nproceedings shall be in English language and seat/venue shall be New Delhi, India.\nSubject to the above, the provisions of Indian Arbitration & Conciliation Act 1996 and\nthe Rules and amendment thereof shall be applicable. All matter relating to this Contract\nare subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the court situated in the state of Delhi.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0326",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 326,
    "page_start": 44,
    "page_end": 44,
    "char_start": 116924,
    "char_end": 117841,
    "char_count": 917,
    "text": "Contractor may please note that the Arbitration & Conciliation Act 1996 was enacted by\nthe Indian Parliament and is based on United Nations Commission on International\nTrade Law (UNCITRAL model law), which were prepared after extensive consultation\nwith Arbitral Institutions and centers of International Commercial Arbitration. The\nUnited Nations General Assembly vide resolution 31/98 adopted the UNCITRAL\nArbitration rules on 15 December 1976.\nNotwithstanding anything contained contrary in GCC and other Contract Documents, in\ncase it  is found that the Bidder/Service Provider indulged in fraudulent/ coercive\npractices at the time of bidding or during execution of the contract as mentioned in\n“Procedure for action in case of Corrupt/ Fradulent/ Collusive /Coersive Practices”, the\nService Provider / Bidder shall be banned (in terms of aforesaid procedure) from the date\nof issuance of such order for banning.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0327",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 327,
    "page_start": 44,
    "page_end": 44,
    "char_start": 117843,
    "char_end": 118155,
    "char_count": 312,
    "text": "The Bidder/Service Provider understands and agrees that in such cases of banning, the\ndecision of Employer shall be final and binding on such Bidder/Service Provider and the\nArbitration Clause mentioned in the GCC and other Contract Documents shall not be\napplicable for any issue /dispute arising in the matter.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0328",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 328,
    "page_start": 44,
    "page_end": 44,
    "char_start": 118157,
    "char_end": 118336,
    "char_count": 179,
    "text": "6.2.2 SETTLEMENT OF COMMERCIAL DISPUTES BETWEEN PUBLIC SECTOR\nENTERPRISE(S) INTER SE AND PUBLIC SECTOR ENTERPRISE(S) AND\nGOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT (S) THROUGH ADMINISTRATIVE MECHANISM",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0329",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 329,
    "page_start": 45,
    "page_end": 45,
    "char_start": 118338,
    "char_end": 118521,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "General Conditions of Contract - Services\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n45",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0330",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 330,
    "page_start": 45,
    "page_end": 45,
    "char_start": 118523,
    "char_end": 118604,
    "char_count": 81,
    "text": "FOR RESOLUTION OF CPSEs DISPUTES (AMRCD) IN THE DEPARTMENT OF\nPUBLIC ENTERPRISES:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0331",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 331,
    "page_start": 45,
    "page_end": 45,
    "char_start": 118606,
    "char_end": 119112,
    "char_count": 506,
    "text": "In the event of any dispute or difference relating to the interpretation and application of\nthe provisions of commercial contract(s) between Central Public Sector Enterprises\n(CPSEs) inter se and also between CPSEs and Government Departments / Organizations\n(excluding disputes concerning Railways, Income Tax, Customs & Excise Departments),\nsuch dispute or difference shall be taken up by either party for resolution through\nAMRCD as mentioned in DPE OM No. 4(1)/2013-DPE (GM) / FTS-1835 dated\n22.05.2018.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0332",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 332,
    "page_start": 45,
    "page_end": 45,
    "char_start": 119114,
    "char_end": 119567,
    "char_count": 453,
    "text": "6.3\nJURISDICTION:\n\n6.3.1 The Contract shall be governed by and constructed according to the laws in force in\nIndia. The Service Provider hereby submits to the jurisdiction of the Courts situated at\nNew Delhi/Delhi only for the purposes of disputes, actions and proceedings arising out of\nthe Contract and it is agreed that the Courts at New Delhi/Delhi only will have the\nexclusive jurisdiction to hear and decide such disputes, actions and proceedings.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC066-0333",
    "doc_id": "DOC-066",
    "paragraph_index": 333,
    "page_start": 45,
    "page_end": 45,
    "char_start": 119569,
    "char_end": 119814,
    "char_count": 245,
    "text": "6.4\nCONTINUANCE OF THE CONTRACT:\n\nNotwithstanding the fact that settlement of dispute(s) (if any) may be pending, the parties\nhereto shall continue to be governed by and perform the Services in accordance with the\nprovisions under this Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
