    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "12",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0054",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 54,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 40207,
    "char_end": 40849,
    "char_count": 642,
    "text": "14 FIELD MANAGEMENT & CONTROLLING/COORDINATING AUTHORITY:\n14.1  The field management will be the responsibility of the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE, who will be nominated by the EMPLOYER. The\nENGINEER-IN-CHARGE may also authorize his representatives to assist in performing his duties and functions.\n14.2  The ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall coordinate the works of various agencies engaged at site to ensure minimum disruption of\nwork carried out by different agencies. It shall be the responsibility of the CONTRACTOR to plan and execute the work strictly\nin accordance with site instructions to avoid hindrance to the work being executed by other agencies.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0055",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 55,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 40851,
    "char_end": 41826,
    "char_count": 975,
    "text": "15 NOTE TO SCHEDULE OF RATES:\n15.1  The Schedule of Rates should be read in conjunction with all the other sections of the tender.\n15.2  The tenderer shall be deemed to have studied the DRAWINGS, SPECIFICATIONS and details of work to be done within TIME\nSCHEDULE and to have acquainted him of the condition prevailing at site.\n15.3  Rates must be filled in the Schedule of Rates of original Tender Documents. If quoted in separate typed sheets no variation in\nitem description or specification shall be accepted. Any exceptions taken by the tenderer to the Schedule of Rates shall be\nbrought out in the terms and conditions of the offer.\n15.4  The quantities shown against the various items are only approximate. Any increase or decrease in the quantities shall not\nform the basis of alteration of the rates quoted and accepted.\n15.5  The EMPLOYER reserves the right to interpolate the rates for such items of work falling between similar items of lower and\nhigher magnitude.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0056",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 56,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 41828,
    "char_end": 43527,
    "char_count": 1699,
    "text": "16 POLICY FOR TENDERS UNDER CONSIDERATION:\n16.1  Only Those Tenders which are complete in all respects and are strictly in accordance with the Terms and Conditions and\nTechnical Specifications of Tender Document, shall be considered for evaluation. Such Tenders shall be deemed to be under\nconsideration immediately after opening of Tender and until such time an official intimation of acceptance /rejection of\nTender is made by BCPL to the Bidder.\n16.2  Zero Deviation: Bidders to note that this is a ZERO DEVIATION TENDER. BCPL will appreciate submission of offer based on the\nterms and conditions in the enclosed General Conditions of Contract (GCC), Special Conditions of Contract (SCC), Instructions\nto Bidders (ITB), Scope of Work, technical specifications etc. to avoid wastage of time and money in seeking clarifications on\ntechnical/ commercial aspects of the offer. Bidder may note that no technical and commercial clarifications will be sought for\nafter the receipt of the bids. In case of any deviation/nonconformity observed in the bid, it will be liable for rejection.\n17 AWARD OF CONTRACT:\n17.1  The Acceptance of Tender will be intimated to the successful Tenderer by BCPL either by Telex/ Telegram/ Fax or by Letter or\nlike means-defined as LETTER OF ACCEPTANCE OF TENDER.\n17.2 BCPL will be the sole judge in the matter of award of CONTRACT and the decision of BCPL shall be final and binding.\n18 CLARIFICATION OF TENDER DOCUMENT:\n18.1  The Tender is required to carefully examine the Technical Specifications, Conditions of Contract, Drawings and other details\nrelating to WORK and given in Tender Document and fully inform himself as to all conditions and matters which may in any",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0057",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 57,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 43528,
    "char_end": 45319,
    "char_count": 1791,
    "text": "way affect the WORK or the cost thereof. In case the Tenderer is in doubt about the completeness or correctness of any of the\ncontents of the Tender Documents he should request in writing for an interpretation/clarification to BCPL in triplicate. BCPL\nwill then issue interpretation/clarification to Tenderer in writing. Such clarifications and or interpretations shall form part of\nthe Specifications and Documents and shall accompany the tender which shall be submitted by tenderer within time and date\nas specified in invitations to tender.\n18.2  Verbal clarification and information given by BCPL or its employee(s) or its representatives shall not in any way be binding on\nBCPL.\n19 LOCAL CONDITIONS:\n19.1  It will be imperative on each tenderer to inform himself of all local conditions and factors which may have any effect on the\nexecution of WORK covered under the Tender Document. In their own interest, the tenderer are requested to familiarise\nthemselves with the Indian Income Tax Act 1961, Indian Companies Act 1956, Indian Customs Act 1962 and other related Acts\nand Laws and Regulations of India with their latest amendments, as applicable BCPL shall not entertain any requests for\nclarifications from the tenderer regarding such local conditions.\n19.2  It must be understood and agreed that such factors have properly been investigated and considered while submitting the\ntender. No claim for financial or any other adjustments to VALUE OF CONTRACT, on lack of clarity of such factors shall be\nentertained.\n20 ABNORMAL RATES:\n20.1  The tenderer is expected to quote rate for each item after careful analysis of cost involved for the performance of the\ncompleted item considering all specifications and Conditions of Contract. This will avoid loss of profit or gain in case of",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0058",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 58,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 45320,
    "char_end": 45693,
    "char_count": 373,
    "text": "curtailment or change of specification for any item. In case it is noticed that the rates quoted by the tenderer for any item are\nunusually high or unusually low, it will be sufficient cause for the rejection of the tender unless the EMPLOYER is convinced\nabout the reasonableness after scrutiny of the analysis for such rate(s) to be furnished by the tenderer (on demand).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
