  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0060",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 60,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 45699,
    "char_end": 47498,
    "char_count": 1799,
    "text": "SECTION-IV GENERAL OBLIGATIONS\n21 PRIORITY OF CONTRACT DOCUMENTS\n21.1  Except if and the extent otherwise provided by the Contract, the provisions of the General Conditions of Contract and Special\nConditions shall prevail over those of any other documents forming part of the CONTRACT. Several documents forming the\nCONTRACT are to be taken as mutually explanatory of one another, but in case of ambiguities or discrepancies the same shall\nbe explained and adjusted by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE who shall thereupon issue to the Contractor instructions thereon and\nin such event, unless otherwise provided in the Contract, the priority of the documents forming the Contract shall be as\nfollows :\n(i)\nThe Contract Agreement ;\n(ii)\nThe Letter of Acceptance;\n(iii)\nThe (Instructions to Bidders)ITB;\n(iv)\nSpecial Conditions of Contract (SCC);\n(v)\nGeneral Conditions of Contract (GCC)\n(vi)\nAny other document forming part of the Contract. Works shown in the DRAWING but not mentioned in the\nSPECIFICATIONS OR described in the SPECIFICATIONS without being shown in the DRAWINGS shall nevertheless be\ndeemed to be included in the same manner as if they had been specifically shown upon the DRAWINGS and\ndescribed in the SPECIFICATIONS.\n21.2  Headings and Marginal Notes: All headings and marginal notes to the clauses of these General Conditions of Contract or to\nthe SPECIFICATIONS or to any other Tender Document are solely for the purpose of giving a concise indication and not a\nsummary of the contents thereof, and they shall never be deemed to be part thereof or be used in the interpretation or\nconstruction thereof the CONTRACT.\n21.3  Singular and Plural: In CONTRACT DOCUMENTS unless otherwise stated specifically, the singular shall include the plural and\nvice versa wherever the context so requires.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0061",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 61,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 47499,
    "char_end": 47678,
    "char_count": 179,
    "text": "21.4  Interpretation: Words implying `Persons' shall include relevant `Corporate Companies / Registered Associations/ Body of\nIndividuals/ Firm of Partnership' as the case may be.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0062",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 62,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 47680,
    "char_end": 49249,
    "char_count": 1569,
    "text": "22 SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT:\n22.1  Special Conditions of Contract shall be read in conjunction with the General Conditions of Contract, specification of Work,\nDrawings and any other documents forming part of this CONTRACT wherever the context so requires.\n22.2  Notwithstanding the sub-division of the documents into these separate sections and volumes every part of each shall be\ndeemed to be supplementary to and complementary of every other part and shall be read with and into the CONTRACT so far\nas it may be practicable to do so.\n22.3  Where any portion of the General Condition of Contract is repugnant to or at variance with any provisions of the Special\nConditions of Contract, unless a different intention appears the provisions of the Special Conditions of Contract shall be\ndeemed to over-ride the provisions of the General Conditions of Contract and shall to the extent of such repugnancy, or\nvariations, prevail.\n22.4  Wherever it is mentioned in the specifications that the CONTRACTOR shall perform certain WORK or provide certain facilities,\nit is understood that the CONTRACTOR shall do so at his cost and the VALUE OF CONTRACT shall be deemed to have included\ncost of such performance and provisions, so mentioned.\n22.5  The materials, design and workmanship shall satisfy the relevant INDIAN STANDARDS, the JOB SPECIFICATIONS contained\nherein and CODES referred to. Where the job specification stipulate requirements in addition to those contained in the\nstandard codes and specifications, these additional requirements shall also be satisfied.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0063",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 63,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 49251,
    "char_end": 50987,
    "char_count": 1736,
    "text": "23 CONTRACTOR TO OBTAIN HIS OWN INFORMATION:\n23.1 The CONTRACTOR in fixing his rate shall for all purpose whatsoever reason may be, deemed to have himself independently\nobtained all necessary information for the purpose of preparing his tender and his tender as accepted shall be deemed to\nhave taken into account all contingencies as may arise due to such information or lack of same. The correctness of the details,\ngiven in the Tender Document to help the CONTRACTOR to make up the tender is not guaranteed. The CONTRACTOR shall be\ndeemed to have examined the CONTRACT DOCUMENTS, to have generally obtained his own information in all matters\nwhatsoever that might affect the carrying out of the works at the schedules rates and to have satisfied himself to the\nsufficiency of his tender. Any error in description of quantity or omission therefrom shall not vitiate the CONTRACT or release\nthe CONTRACTOR from executing the work comprised in the CONTRACT according to DRAWINGS and SPECIFICATIONS at the\nscheduled rates. He is deemed to have known the scope, nature and magnitude of the WORKS and the requirements of\nmaterials and labour involved etc., and as to what all works he has to complete in accordance with the CONTRACT documents\nwhatever be the defects, omissions or errors that may be found in the DOCUMENTS. The CONTRACTOR shall be deemed to\nhave visited surroundings, to have satisfied himself to the nature of all existing structures, if any, and also as to the nature and\nthe conditions of the Railways, Roads, Bridges and Culverts, means of transport and communication, whether by land, water\nor air, and as to possible interruptions thereto and the access and egress from the site, to have made enquiries, examined and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0064",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 64,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 50988,
    "char_end": 51357,
    "char_count": 369,
    "text": "satisfied himself as to the sites for obtaining sand, stones, bricks and other materials, the sites for disposal of surplus\nmaterials, the available accommodation as to whatever required, depots and such other buildings as may be necessary for\nexecuting and completing the works, to have made local independent enquiries as to the sub-soil, subsoil water and variations",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
