    "char_start": 68474,
    "char_end": 69252,
    "char_count": 778,
    "text": "31 CHANGE IN CONSTITUTION:\n31.1  Where the CONTRACTOR is a partnership firm, the prior approval of the EMPLOYER shall be obtained in writing, before any\nchange is made in the constitution of the firm. Where the CONTRACTOR is an individual or a Hindu undivided family business\nconcern, such approval as aforesaid shall, likewise be obtained before such CONTRACTOR enters into any agreement with\nother parties, where under, the reconstituted firm would have the right to carry out the work hereby undertaken by the\nCONTRACTOR. In either case if prior approval as aforesaid is not obtained, the CONTRACT shall be deemed to have been\nallotted in contravention of clause 37 hereof and the same action may be taken and the same consequence shall ensure as\nprovided in the said clause.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0083",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
