    "paragraph_index": 85,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 69286,
    "char_end": 71013,
    "char_count": 1727,
    "text": "32.1  TERMINATION OF CONTRACT FOR DEATH: If the CONTRACTOR is an individual or a proprietary concern and the individual or\nthe proprietor dies or if the CONTRACTOR is a partnership concern and one of the partner dies then unless, the EMPLOYER is\nsatisfied that the legal representative of the individual or the proprietary concern or the surviving partners are capable of\ncarrying out and completing CONTRACT, he (the EMPLOYER)is entitled to cancel the CONTRACT for the uncompleted part\nwithout being in any way liable for any compensation payment to the estate of the diseased CONTRACTOR and/or to the\nsurviving partners of the CONTRACTOR'S firm on account of the cancellation of CONTRACT. The decision of the EMPLOYER in\nsuch assessment shall be final and binding on the parties. In the event of such cancellation, the EMPLOYER shall not hold the\nestate of the diseased CONTRACTOR and/or the surviving partners of the CONTRACTOR'S firm liable for any damages for non-\ncompletion of CONTRACT.\n32.2  TERMINATION OF CONTRACT IN CASE OF LIQUIDATION / BANKRUPTCY ETC. If the Contractor shall dissolve or become\nbankrupt or insolvent or cause or suffer any receiver to be appointed of his business of any assets thereof compound with his\nCreditors, or being a corporation commence to be wound up, not being a member’s voluntary winding up for the purpose of\namalgamation or reconstruction, or carry on its business under a Receiver for the benefits of its Creditors any of them,\nEMPLOYER shall be at liberty :- To terminate the contract forthwith upon coming to know of the happening of any such event\nas aforesaid by notice in writing to the Contractor or to give the Receiver or liquidator or other person, the option of carrying",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0086",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 86,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 71014,
    "char_end": 72169,
    "char_count": 1155,
    "text": "out the contract subject to his providing a guarantee upto an amount to be agreed upon by EMPLOYER for due and faithful\nperformance of the contract.\n32.3 TERMINATION OF CONTRACT FOR NON-PERFORMANCE AND SUBSEQUENTLY PUTTING THE CONTRACTOR ON HOLIDAY: In\ncase of termination of CONTRACT herein set forth (under clause 29.0) except under conditions of Force Majeure and\ntermination after expiry of contract, the CONTRACTOR shall be put under holiday [i.e. neither any enquiry will be issued to the\nparty by BCPL. against any type of tender nor their offer will be considered by BCPL against any ongoing tender (s) where\ncontract between BCPL and that particular CONTRACTOR (as a bidder) has not been finalized] for three years from the date of\ntermination by BCPL to such CONTRACTOR.\n33 MEMBERS OF THE EMPLOYER NOT INDIVIDUALLY LIABLE :\n33.1  No Director, or official or employee of the EMPLOYER/ CONSULTANT shall in any way be personally bound or liable for the\nacts or obligations of the EMPLOYER under the CONTRACT or answerable for any default or omission in the observance or\nperformance of any of the acts, matters or things which are herein contained.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0087",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 87,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 72171,
    "char_end": 72504,
    "char_count": 333,
    "text": "34 EMPLOYER NOT BOUND BY PERSONAL REPRESENTATIONS:\n34.1  The CONTRACTOR shall not be entitled to any increase on the scheduled rates or any other right or claim whatsoever by\nreason of any representation, explanation statement or alleged representation, promise or guarantees given or alleged to\nhave been given to him by any person.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0088",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 88,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 72506,
    "char_end": 73000,
    "char_count": 494,
    "text": "35 CONTRACTOR'S OFFICE AT SITE:\n35.1 The CONTRACTOR shall provide and maintain an office at the site for the accommodation of his agent and staff and such\noffice shall be open at all reasonable hours to receive instructions, notice or other communications. The CONTRACTOR at all\ntime shall maintain a site instruction book and compliance of these shall be communicated to the ENGINEER-IN CHARGE from\ntime to time and the whole document to be preserved and handed over after completion of works.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0089",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 89,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 73002,
    "char_end": 74697,
    "char_count": 1695,
    "text": "36 CONTRACTOR'S SUBORDINATE STAFF AND THEIR CONDUCT\n36.1  The CONTRACTOR, on or after award of the WORK shall name and depute a qualified engineer having sufficient experience in\ncarrying out work of similar nature, to whom the equipments, materials, if any, shall be issued and instructions for works\ngiven. The CONTRACTOR shall also provide to the satisfaction of the ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE sufficient and qualified staff to\nsuperintend the execution of the WORK, competent sub-agents, foremen and leading hands including those specially qualified\nby previous experience to supervise the types of works comprised in the CONTRACT in such manner as will ensure work of the\nbest quality, expeditious working. Whenever in the opinion of the ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE additional properly qualified\nsupervisory staff is considered necessary, they shall be employed by the CONTRACTOR without additional charge on accounts\nthereof. The CONTRACTOR shall ensure to the satisfaction of the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE that SUB- CONTRACTORS, if any, shall\nprovide competent and efficient supervision, over the work entrusted to them.\n36.2  If and whenever any of the CONTRACTOR's or SUB- CONTRACTOR'S agents, sub-agents, assistants, foremen, or other\nemployees shall in the opinion of ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE be guilty of any misconduct or be incompetent or insufficiently\nqualified or negligent in the performance of their duties of that in the opinion of the EMPLOYER or the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE,\nit is undesirable for administrative or any other reason for such person or persons to be employed in the works, the\nCONTRACTOR, is so directed by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE, shall at once remove such person or persons from employment",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0090",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 90,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 74698,
    "char_end": 75158,
    "char_count": 460,
    "text": "thereon. Any person or persons so removed from the works shall not again be employed in connection with the WORKS\nwithout the written permission of the ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE. Any person so removed from the WORK shall be immediately\nre-placed at the expense of the CONTRACTOR by a qualified and competent substitute. Should the CONTRACTOR be\nrequested to repatriate any person removed from the works he shall do so and shall bear all costs in connection herewith.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
