    "char_count": 1001,
    "text": "certified in writing by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE to be reasonable, and without making any payment or allowance to the\nCONTRACTOR for the use of the temporary said works, construction plant and stock or being liable for any loss or\ndamage thereto, and if the EMPLOYER shall by reason of his taking possession of the WORK or of the WORK being\ncompleted by other CONTRACTOR (due account being taken of any such extra work or works which may or be omitted)\nthen the amount of such excess as certified by the ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE shall be deducted from any money which may\nbe due for work done by the CONTRACTOR under the CONTRACT and not paid for. Any deficiency shall forthwith be\nmade good and paid to the EMPLOYER by the CONTRACTOR and the EMPLOYER shall have power to sell in such manner\nand for such price as he may think fit all or any of the construction plant, materials etc. constructed by or belonging to\nand to recoup and retain the said deficiency or any part thereof out of proceeds of the sale.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0099",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 99,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 82563,
    "char_end": 84286,
    "char_count": 1723,
    "text": "39 CONTRACTOR'S RESPONSIBILITY WITH THE MECHANICAL, ELECTRICAL, INTERCOMMUNICATION SYSTEM, AIR\nCONDITIONING CONTRACTORS AND OTHER AGENCIES:\n39.1  Without repugnance of any other condition, it shall be the responsibility of the CONTRACTOR executing the work of civil\nconstruction, to work in close cooperation and coordinate the WORK with the Mechanical, Electrical, Air-conditioning and\nIntercommunication Contractor's and other agencies or their authorised representatives, in providing the necessary grooves,\nrecesses,  cuts and opening etc., in wall, slabs beams and columns etc. and making good the same to the desired finish as per\nspecification, for the placement of electrical, intercommunication cables, conduits, air-conditioning inlets and outlets grills\nand other equipments etc. where required. For the above said requirements in the false ceiling and other partitions, the\nCONTRACTOR before starting-up the work shall in consultation with the Electrical, Mechanical, Intercommunication, Air-\nconditioning contractor and other agencies prepare and put-up a joint scheme, showing the necessary openings, grooves,\nrecesses, cuts, the methods of fixing required for the WORK of the aforesaid, and the finishes therein, to the ENGINEER-IN-\nCHARGE and get the approval. The CONTRACTOR before finally submitting the scheme to the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall have\nthe written agreement of the other agencies. The ENGINEER- IN-CHARGE, before communicating his approval to the scheme,\nwith any required modification, shall get the final agreement of all the agencies, which shall be binding. No claim shall be\nentertained on account of the above. The CONTRACTOR shall confirm in all respects with provision of any statutory",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0100",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 100,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 84287,
    "char_end": 84654,
    "char_count": 367,
    "text": "regulations, ordinances or byelaws of any local or duly constituted authorities or public bodies which may be applicable from\ntime to time to the WORK or any temporary works. The CONTRACTOR shall keep the EMPLOYER indemnified against all\npenalties and liabilities of every kind, arising out of non- adherence to such stains, ordinances, laws, rules, regulations, etc.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
