    "char_start": 89341,
    "char_end": 89663,
    "char_count": 322,
    "text": "right. With respect to any subcontract entered into by CONTRACTOR pursuant to the provisions of the relevant clause hereof,\nthe CONTRACTOR shall obtain from the SUB-CONTRACTOR an undertaking to provide the EMPLOYER with the same patent\nprotection that CONTRACTOR is required to provide under the provisions of this clause.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0108",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 108,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 89665,
    "char_end": 91374,
    "char_count": 1709,
    "text": "44 LIENS:\n44.1  If, at any time there should be evidence or any lien or claim for which the EMPLOYER might have become liable and which is\nchargeable to the CONTRACTOR, the EMPLOYER shall have the right to retain out of any payment then due or thereafter to\nbecome due an amount sufficient to completely indemnify the EMPLOYER against such lien or claim and if such lien or claim\nbe valid, the EMPLOYER may pay and discharge the same and deduct the amount so paid from any money which may be or\nmay become due and payable to the CONTRACTOR. If any lien or claim remain unsettled after all payments are made, the\nCONTRACTOR shall refund or pay to the EMPLOYER all money that the latter may be compelled to pay in discharging such lien\nor claim including all costs and reasonable expenses. EMPLOYER reserves the right to do the same.\n44.2  The EMPLOYER shall have lien on all materials, equipments including those brought by the CONTRACTOR for the purpose of\nerection, testing and commissioning of the WORK.\n44.3  The final payment shall not become due until the CONTRACTOR delivers to the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE a complete release or\nwaiver of all liens arising or which may arise out of his agreement or receipt in full or certification by the CONTRACTOR in a\nform approved by ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE that all invoices for labour, materials, services have been paid in lien thereof and if\nrequired by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE in any case an affidavit that so far as the CONTRACTOR has knowledge or information\nthe releases and receipts include all the labour and material for which a lien could be filled.\n44.4  CONTRACTOR will indemnify and hold the EMPLOYER harmless, for a period of two years after the issue of FINAL",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
