    "paragraph_index": 115,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 94822,
    "char_end": 95703,
    "char_count": 881,
    "text": "48 CERTIFICATE NOT TO AFFECT RIGHT OF EMPLOYER AND LIABILITY OF CONTRACTOR:\n48.1  No interim payment certificate(s) issued by the Engineer-in- Charge of the EMPLOYER, nor any sum paid on account by the\nEMPLOYER, nor any extension of time for execution of the work granted by EMPLOYER shall affect or prejudice the rights of\nthe Employer against the CONTRACTOR or relieve the CONTRACTOR of his obligations for the due performance of the\nCONTRACT, or be interpreted as approval of the WORK done or of the equipment supplied and no certificate shall create\nliability for the EMPLOYER to pay for alterations, amendments, variations or additional works not ordered, in writing, by\nEMPLOYER or discharge the liability of the CONTRACTOR for the payment of damages whether due, ascertained, or certified\nor not or any sum against the payment of which he is bound to indemnify the EMPLOYER.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
