    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 96041,
    "char_end": 96604,
    "char_count": 563,
    "text": "50 TRANSFER OF TITLE:\n50.1  The title of Ownership of supplies furnished by the CONTRACTOR shall not pass on to the EMPLOYER for all Supplies till the\nsame are finally accepted by the EMPLOYER after the successful completion of PERFORMANCE TEST and GUARANTEE TEST\nand issue of FINAL CERTIFICATE.\n50.2  However, the EMPLOYER shall have the lien on all such works performed as soon as any advance or progressive payment is\nmade by the EMPLOYER to the CONTRACTOR and the CONTRACTOR shall not subject these works for use other than those\nintended under this CONTRACT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0118",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 118,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 96606,
    "char_end": 96984,
    "char_count": 378,
    "text": "51 RELEASE OF INFORMATION:\n51.1  The CONTRACTOR shall not communicate or use in advertising, publicity, sales releases or in any other medium, photographs,\nor other reproduction of the Work under this CONTRACT or description of the site dimensions, quantity , quality or other\ninformation, concerning the Work unless prior written permission has been obtained from the EMPLOYER.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0119",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 119,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 96986,
    "char_end": 97357,
    "char_count": 371,
    "text": "52 BRAND NAMES:\n52.1  The specific reference in the SPECIFICATIONS and documents to any material by trade name, make or catalogue number shall\nbe construed as establishing standard or quality and performance and not as limited competition.  However, TENDERER may\noffer other similar equipments provided it meets the specified standard design and performance requirements.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0120",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 120,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 97359,
    "char_end": 97604,
    "char_count": 245,
    "text": "53 COMPLETION OF CONTRACT:\n53.1  Unless otherwise terminated under the provisions of any other relevant clause, this CONTRACT shall be deemed to have been\ncompleted at the expiration of the PERIOD OF LIABILITY as provided for under the CONTRACT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0121",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 121,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 97606,
    "char_end": 97982,
    "char_count": 376,
    "text": "54 SPARES:\n54.1  The CONTRACTOR shall furnish to the EMPLOYER all spares required for COMMISSIONING of the  plants, recommendatory\nand/or mandatory spares, which are required essential by the manufacturer/supplier. The same shall be delivered at SITE,\n3(Three) months before COMMISSIONING. Also the CONTRACTOR should furnish the manufacturing drawings for fast wearing\nspares.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0122",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 122,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 97984,
    "char_end": 97986,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "22",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0123",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 123,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 97988,
    "char_end": 98349,
    "char_count": 361,
    "text": "54.2  The CONTRACTOR guarantees the EMPLOYER that before the manufacturers of the equipments, plants and machineries go\nout of production of spare parts for the equipment furnished and erected by him, he shall give at least twelve (12) months'\nadvance notice to the EMPLOYER, so that the latter may order his requirement of spares in one lot,  if he so desires.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0124",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 124,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 98351,
    "char_end": 99728,
    "char_count": 1377,
    "text": "SECTION-V PERFORMANCE OF WORK\n55 EXECUTION OF WORK:\n55.1  All the Works shall be executed in strict conformity with the provisions of the CONTRACT Documents and with such\nexplanatory detailed drawings, specification and instructions as may be furnished from time to time to the CONTRACTOR by\nthe ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE whether mentioned in the CONTRACT or not. The CONTRACTOR shall be responsible for ensuring\nthat works throughout are executed in the most substantial, proper and workmanlike manner with the quality of material and\nworkmanship in strict accordance with the SPECIFICATIONS and to the entire satisfaction of the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE. The\nCONTRACTOR shall provide all necessary materials equipment labour etc. for execution and maintenance of WORK till\ncompletion unless otherwise mentioned in the CONTRACT.\n56 CO-ORDINATION AND INSPECTION OF WORK:\n56.1  The coordination and inspection of the day-to-day work under the CONTRACT shall be the responsibility of the ENGINEER-IN-\nCHARGE. The written instruction regarding any particular job will normally be passed by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE or his\nauthorised representative. A work order book will be maintained by the CONTRACTOR for each sector in which the aforesaid\nwritten instructions will be entered. These will be signed by the CONTRACTOR or his authorised representative by way of\nacknowledgement within 12 hours.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0125",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 125,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 99730,
    "char_end": 100275,
    "char_count": 545,
    "text": "57 WORK IN MONSOON AND DEWATERING:\n57.1  Unless otherwise specified elsewhere in the tender, the execution of the WORK may entail working in the monsoon also. The\nCONTRACTOR must maintain a minimum labour force as may be required for the job and plan and execute the construction\nand erection according to the prescribed schedule. No extra rate will be considered for such work in monsoon.\n57.2  During monsoon and other period, it shall be the responsibility of the CONTRACTOR to keep the construction work site free\nfrom water at his own cost.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0126",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 126,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 100277,
    "char_end": 100821,
    "char_count": 544,
    "text": "58 WORK ON SUNDAYS AND HOLIDAYS:\n58.1  For carrying out Work on Sundays, and Holidays, the CONTRACTOR will approach the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE or his\nrepresentative at least two days in advance and obtain permission in writing. The CONTRACTOR shall observe all labour laws\nand other statutory rules and regulations in force. In case of any violations of such laws, rules and regulations, consequence if\nany, including the cost thereto shall be exclusively borne by the CONTRACTOR and the EMPLOYER shall have no liability\nwhatsoever on this account.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0127",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 127,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 100823,
    "char_end": 102086,
    "char_count": 1263,
    "text": "59 GENERAL CONDITIONS FOR CONSTRUCTION AND ERECTION WORK:\n59.1  The working time at the site of work is 48 hours per week. Overtime work is permitted in cases of need and the EMPLOYER\nwill not compensate the same. Shift working at 2 or 3 shifts per day will become necessary and the CONTRACTOR should take\nthis aspect into consideration for formulating his rates for quotation. No extra claims will be entertained by the EMPLOYER no\nthis account. For carrying out work beyond working hours the CONTRACTOR will approach the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE or his\nauthorized representative and obtain his prior written permission.\n59.2  The CONTRACTOR must arrange for the placement of workers in such a way that the delayed completion of the WORK or any\npart thereof for any reason whatsoever will not affect their proper employment. The EMPLOYER will not entertain any claim\nfor idle time payment whatsoever.\n59.3  The CONTRACTOR shall submit to the EMPLOYER/ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE reports at regular intervals regarding the state and\nprogress of WORK. The details and proforma of the report will mutually be agreed after the award of CONTRACT. The\nCONTRACTOR shall provide display boards showing progress and labour strengths at worksite, as directed by the ENGINEER-\nIN-CHARGE.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0128",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 128,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 102088,
    "char_end": 103082,
    "char_count": 994,
    "text": "60 ALTERATIONS IN SPECIFICATIONS, DESIGN AND EXTRA WORKS:\n60.1 The WORK covered under this CONTRACT having to be executed by the CONTRACTOR on a lumpsum firm price/item rate\nquoted by him, the EMPLOYER will not accept any proposals for changes in VALUE OF CONTRACT or  extension in time on\naccount of any such changes which may arise to the CONTRACTOR's scope of WORK as a result of detailed Engineering and\nthereafter during the execution of WORK. The only exception to this will be a case where the EMPLOYER requests in writing\nto the CONTRACTOR to upgrade the SPECIFICATIONS or the size of any major pieces of equipments, plant or machinery\nbeyond what is normally required to meet the scope of WORK as defined in the CONTRACT DOCUMENT. In such cases, a\nchange order will be initialled by the CONTRACTOR at the appropriate time for the EMPLOYER's prior approval giving the\nfull back-up data for their review and for final settlement of any impact on price within 30 (thirty) days thereafter.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0129",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 129,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 103084,
    "char_end": 103086,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "23",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0130",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 130,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 103088,
    "char_end": 104807,
    "char_count": 1719,
    "text": "60.2  The ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall have to make any alterations in, omission from, additions to or substitutions for, the\nSchedule of Rates, the original specifications, drawings, designs and instructions that may appear to him to be necessary or\nadvisable during the progress of the WORK and the CONTRACTOR shall be bound to carry out the such altered/ extra/ new\nitems of WORK in accordance with any instructions which may be given to him in writing signed by the ENGINEER-IN-\nCHARGE, and such alterations, omissions, additions or substitutions shall not invalidate the CONTRACT and any altered,\nadditional or substituted work which the CONTRACTOR may be directed to do in the manner above specified as part of the\nWORK shall be carried out by the CONTRACTOR on the same conditions in all respects on which he agreed to do the main\nWORK. The time of completion of WORK may be extended for the part of the particular job at the discretion of the ENGINEER-\nIN- CHARGE, for only such alterations, additions or substitutions of the WORK, as he may consider as just and reasonable. The\nrates for such additional, altered or substituted WORK under this clause shall be worked out in accordance with the following\nprovisions:-\nI.\nFor Item Rate Contract\na)\nIf the rates for the additional, altered or substituted WORK are specified in the CONTRACT for the WORK, the\nCONTRACTOR is bound to carry on the additional, altered or substituted WORK at the same rates as are specified in\nthe CONTRACT.\nb)\nIf the rates for the additional, altered or substituted WORK are not specifically provided in the CONTRACT for the\nWORK, the rates will be derived from the rates for similar class of WORK as are specified in the CONTRACT for the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0131",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 131,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 104808,
    "char_end": 106517,
    "char_count": 1709,
    "text": "WORK. The opinion of the ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE, as to whether or not the rates can be reasonably so derived from\nthe items in this CONTRACT will be final and binding on the CONTRACTOR.\nc)\nIf the rates for the altered, additional or substituted WORK cannot be determined in the manner specified in sub-\nclause(s) and (b) above, then the CONTRACTOR shall, within 7 days of the date of receipt of order to carry out the\nWORK, inform the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE of the rates which it is his intention to charge for such class of WORK,\nsupported by analysis of the rate or rates claimed, and the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall determine the rate or rates\non the basis of the prevailing market rates, labour cost at schedule of labour rates plus 10% to cover contractor's\nsupervision, overheads and profit and pay the CONTRACTOR accordingly. The opinion of the ENGINEER- IN-CHARGE\nas to current market rates of materials and the quantum of labour involved per unit of measurement will be final\nand binding on the CONTRACTOR.\nd)\nWhere the item of work will be executed through nominated specialist agency as approved by the ENGINEER-IN-\nCHARGE, then the actual amount paid to such nominated agency supported by documentary evidence and as\ncertified by ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall be considered plus 10% (ten percent) to cover all contingencies, overhead,\nprofits to arrive at the rates.\ne)\nProvisions contained in the Sub-clause (a) & (d) above shall, however, not apply for the following:- Where the value\nof additions of new items together with the value of alterations, additions/deletions or substitutions does not\nexceed by or is not less than plus/minus (+)25% of the VALUE OF CONTRACT. The item rates in the Schedule of Rates",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0132",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 132,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 106518,
    "char_end": 107544,
    "char_count": 1026,
    "text": "shall hold good for all such variations between the above mentioned limits, irrespective of any increase/decrease of\nquantities in the individual items of Schedule of Rates. Where the value of addition of new items together with the\nvalue of alterations, additions/deletions or substitutions reduces more than 25% of the contract value but is within\nthe following limits the tenderer shall be paid compensation for decrease in the value of work, as follows: S.No.\nRange of Variation Percentage compensation for decrease in the value of work in the respective range. a) Beyond\n(+) 25% No increase and/or upto& inclusive of decrease shall be (+) 50% applicable for the Schedule of Rates (The\nrates quoted for this increase shall be valid). b) Beyond (-) 25% upto&For reduction beyond inclusive of (-) 50%\n25%contractor shall be compensated by an amount equivalent to 10% of the reduction in value of the contract as\nawarded. For example if the actual contract value is 70% of awarded value then compensation shall be 10% of (75-",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0133",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 133,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 107545,
    "char_end": 108286,
    "char_count": 741,
    "text": "70) i.e. 0.5% of awarded contract value.\nII.\nFor Lumpsum Contracts: CONTRACTOR shall, within 7 days of the date of receipt of order to carry out the WORK, inform\nthe  ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE of the rates which it is his intention to charge for such class of WORK, supported by analysis\nof the rate or rates claimed, and the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall determine the rate or rates on the basis of the\nprevailing market rates, labour cost at schedule of labour rates plus 10% to cover contractor's supervision, overheads\nand profit and pay the CONTRACTOR accordingly. The opinion of the ENGINEER- IN-CHARGE as to current market rates of\nmaterials and the quantum of labour involved per unit of measurement will be final and binding on the CONTRACTOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0134",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 134,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 108288,
    "char_end": 109382,
    "char_count": 1094,
    "text": "61 DRAWINGS TO BE SUPPLIED BY THE EMPLOYER\n61.1  The drawings attached with tender are only for the general guidance to the CONTRACTOR to enable him to visualize the type\nof work contemplated and scope of work involved. The CONTRACTOR will be deemed to have studied the DRAWINGS and\nformed an idea about the WORK involved.\n61.2  Detailed working drawings on the basis of which actual execution of the WORK is to proceed, will be furnished from time to\ntime during the progress of the work. The CONTRACTOR shall be deemed to have gone through the DRAWINGS supplied to\nhim thoroughly and carefully and in conjunction with all other connected drawings and bring to the notice of the ENGINEER-\nIN-CHARGE discrepancies, if any, therein before actually carrying out the Work.\n61.3  Copies of all detailed working drawings relating to the WORK shall be kept at the CONTRACTOR's office on the site and shall\nbe made available to the ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE at any time during the CONTRACT. The drawings and other documents issued\nby the EMPLOYER shall be returned to the EMPLOYER on completion of the WORK.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0135",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 135,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 109384,
    "char_end": 109386,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "24",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0136",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 136,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 109388,
    "char_end": 111091,
    "char_count": 1703,
    "text": "62 DRAWINGS TO BE SUPPLIED BY THE CONTRACTOR:\n62.1  The drawings/date which are to be furnished by the CONTRACTOR are enumerated in the special conditions of contract, and\nshall be furnished within the specified time.\n62.2  Where approval/review of drawings before manufacture/ construction/fabrication has been specified, it shall be\nCONTRACTOR's responsibility to have these drawings prepared as per the directions of ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE and got\napproved before proceeding with manufacture/construction/fabrication as the case may be. Any change that may have\nbecome necessary in these drawings during the execution of the work shall have to be carried out by the CONTRACTOR to the\nsatisfaction of ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE at no extra cost. All final drawings shall bear the certification stamp as indicated below\nduly signed by both the CONTRACTOR and ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE.  \"Certified true for _____________________ (Name of\nWork) Agreement No.___________________________Signed:________________ (CONTRACTOR) (ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE)\n62.3  The DRAWINGS submitted by the CONTRACTOR shall be reviewed by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE as far as practicable within 3\n(Three) weeks and shall be modified by the CONTRACTOR, if any modifications and/or corrections are required by the\nENGINEER-IN-CHARGE. The CONTRACTOR shall incorporate such modifications and/or corrections and submit the final\ndrawings for approval. Any delays arising out of failure by the CONTRACTOR to rectify the drawing in good time shall not alter\nthe Contract Completion Time.\n62.4  As built drawings showing all corrections, adjustments etc. shall be furnished by the CONTRACTOR in six copies and one\ntransparent for record purposed to the EMPLOYER.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0137",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 137,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 111093,
    "char_end": 112852,
    "char_count": 1759,
    "text": "63 SETTING OUT WORKS:\n63.1  The ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall furnish the CONTRACTOR with only the four corners of the Works site and a level bench mark\nand the CONTRACTOR shall set out the Works and shall provide an efficient staff for the purpose and shall be solely\nresponsible for the accuracy of such setting out.\n63.2  The CONTRACTOR shall provide, fix and be responsible for the maintenance of all stakes, templates, level marks, profiles and\nother similar things and shall take all necessary precautions to prevent their removal or disturbance and shall be responsible\nfor the consequence of such removal or disturbance should the same take place and for their efficient and timely\nreinstatement. The CONTRACTOR shall also be responsible for the maintenance of all existing survey marks, boundary marks,\ndistance marks and center line marks, either existing or supplied and fixed by the CONTRACTOR. The work shall be set out to\nthe satisfaction of the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE. The approval there of joining with the CONTRACTOR by the ENGINEER- IN-\nCHARGE in setting out the work, shall not relieve the CONTRACTOR of any of his responsibility.\n63.3  Before beginning the Works, the CONTRACTOR shall at his own cost, provide all necessary reference and level posts, pegs,\nbamboos, flags, ranging rods, strings and other materials for proper layout of the works in accordance with the schemes for\nbearing marks acceptable to the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE. The center, longitudinal or face lines and cross lines shall be marked\nby means of small masonry pillars. Each pillar shall have distinct mark at the centre to enable theodolite to be set over it. No\nwork shall be started until all these points are checked and approved by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE in writing but such",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0138",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 138,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 112853,
    "char_end": 113370,
    "char_count": 517,
    "text": "approval shall not relieve the CONTRACTOR of any of his responsibilities. The CONTRACTOR shall also provide all labour,\nmaterial and other facilities, as necessary, for the proper checking of layout and inspection of the points during construction.\n63.4  Pillars bearing geodetic marks located at the sites of units of WORKS under construction should be protected and fenced by\nthe CONTRACTOR.\n63.5  On completion of WORK, the CONTRACTOR must submit the geodetic documents according to which the WORK was carried\nout.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0139",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 139,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 113372,
    "char_end": 113793,
    "char_count": 421,
    "text": "64 RESPONSIBILITY FOR LEVEL AND ALIGNMENT:\n64.1  The CONTRACTOR shall be entirely and exclusively responsible for the horizontal and vertical alignment, the levels and\ncorrectness of every part of the WORK and shall rectify effectively any errors or imperfections therein, such rectifications shall\nbe carried out by the CONTRACTOR, at his own cost, when instructions are issued to that effect by the ENGINEER- IN-CHARGE.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0140",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 140,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 113795,
    "char_end": 115034,
    "char_count": 1239,
    "text": "65 MATERIALS TO BE SUPPLIED BY CONTRACTOR:\n65.1  The CONTRACTOR shall procure and provide within the VALUE OF CONTRACT the whole of the materials required for the\nconstruction including steels, cement and other building materials, tools, tackles, construction plant and equipment for the\ncompletion and maintenance of the WORK except the materials which will be issued by the EMPLOYER and shall make his\nown arrangement for procuring such materials and for the transport thereof. The EMPLOYER may give necessary\nrecommendation to the respective authority if so desired by the CONTRACTOR but assumes no further responsibility of any\nnature. The EMPLOYER will insist on the procurement of materials which bear ISI stamp and/or which are supplied by reputed\nsuppliers.\n65.2  The CONTRACTOR shall properly store all materials either issued to him or brought by him to the SITE to prevent damages\ndue to rain, wind, direct exposure to sun, etc. as also from theft, pilferage, etc. for proper and speedy execution of his works.\nThe CONTRACTOR shall maintain sufficient stocks of all materials required by him.\n65.3  No material shall be despatched from the CONTRACTOR's stores before obtaining the approval in writing of the ENGINEER-IN-\nCHARGE.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0141",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 141,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 115036,
    "char_end": 115071,
    "char_count": 35,
    "text": "66 STORES SUPPLIED BY THE EMPLOYER:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
