  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0143",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 143,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 115077,
    "char_end": 116873,
    "char_count": 1796,
    "text": "66.1  If the SPECIFICATION of the WORK provides for the use of any material of special description to be supplied from the\nEMPLOYER's stores or it is required that the CONTRACTOR shall use certain stores to be provided by the ENGINEER-IN-\nCHARGE, such materials and stores, and price to be charged there for as hereinafter mentioned being so far as  practicable for\nthe convenience of the CONTRACTOR, but not so as in any way to control the meaning or effect of the CONTRACT, the\nCONTRACTOR shall be bound to purchase and shall be supplied such materials and stores as are from time to time required to\nbe used by him for the purpose of the CONTRACT only. The sums due from the CONTRACTOR for the value of materials\nsupplied by the EMPLOYER will be recovered from the running account bill on the basis of the actual consumption of materials\nin the works covered and for which the running account bill has been prepared. After the completion of the WORK, however,\nthe CONTRACTOR has to account for the full quantity of materials supplied to him as per relevant clauses in this document.\n66.2  The value of the stores/materials as may be supplied to the CONTRACTOR by the EMPLOYER will be debited to the\nCONTRACTOR's account at the rates shown in the schedule of materials and if they are not entered in the schedule, they will\nbe debited at cost price, which for the purpose of the CONTRACT shall include the cost of carriage and all other  expenses\nwhatsoever such as normal storage supervision charges which shall have been incurred in obtaining the same at the\nEMPLOYER's stores. All materials so supplied to the CONTRACTOR shall remain the absolute property of the EMPLOYER and\nshall not be removed on any account from the SITE of the WORK, and shall be at all times open for inspection to the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0144",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 144,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 116874,
    "char_end": 117135,
    "char_count": 261,
    "text": "ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE. Any such materials remaining unused at the time of the completion or termination of the CONTRACT\nshall be returned to the EMPLOYER's stores or at a place as directed by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE in perfectly good condition\nat CONTRACTOR's cost.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0145",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 145,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 117137,
    "char_end": 118830,
    "char_count": 1693,
    "text": "67 CONDITIONS FOR ISSUE OF MATERIALS:\n67.1 Materials specified as to be issued by the EMPLOYER will be supplied to the CONTRACTOR by the EMPLOYER form his stores. It\nshall be responsibility of the CONTRACTOR to take delivery of the materials and arrange for its loading, transport and\nunloading at the SITE of WORK at his own cost. The materials shall be issued between the working hours and as per the rules\nof the EMPLOYER as framed from time to time.\n67.2  The CONTRACTOR shall bear all incidental charges for the storage and safe custody of materials at site after these have been\nissued to him.\n67.3  Materials specified as to be issued by the EMPLOYER shall be issued in standard sizes as obtained from the manufacturers.\n67.4  The CONTRACTOR shall construct suitable Godowns at the SITE of WORK for storing the materials safe against damage by\nrain, dampness, fire, theft etc. He shall also employ necessary watch and ward establishment for the purpose.\n67.5  It shall be duty of the CONTRACTOR to inspect the materials supplied to him at the time of taking delivery and satisfy himself\nthat they are in good condition. After the materials have been delivered by the EMPLOYER, it shall be the responsibility of the\nCONTRACTOR to keep them in good condition and if the materials are damaged or lost, at any time, they shall be repaired\nand/or replaced by him at his own cost according to the instructions of the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE.\n67.6   The EMPLOYER shall not be liable for delay in supply or non-supply of any materials which the EMPLOYER has undertaken to\nsupply where such failure or delay is due to natural calamities, act of enemies, transport and procurement difficulties and any",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0146",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 146,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 118831,
    "char_end": 120542,
    "char_count": 1711,
    "text": "circumstances beyond the control of the EMPLOYER. In no case, the CONTRACTOR shall be entitled to claim any compensation\nor loss suffered by him on this account.\n67.7  It shall be responsibility of the CONTRACTOR to arrange in time all materials required for the WORK other than those to be\nsupplied by the EMPLOYER. If, however, in the opinion of the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE the execution of the WORK is likely to be\ndelayed due to the CONTRACTOR's inability to make arrangements for supply of materials which normally he has to arrange\nfor, the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall have the right at his own discretion to issue such materials, if available with the\nEMPLOYER or procure the materials from the market or as elsewhere and the CONTRACTOR will be bound to take such\nmaterials at the rates decided by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE. This, however, does not in any way absolve the CONTRACTOR\nfrom responsibility of making arrangements for the supply of such materials in part or in full, should such a situation occur nor\nshall this constitute a reason for the delay in the execution of the WORK.\n67.8  None of the materials supplied to the CONTRACTOR will be utilised by the CONTRACTOR for manufacturing item which can be\nobtained as supplied from standard manufacturer in finished form.\n67.9  The CONTRACTOR shall, if desired by the ENGINEER- IN-CHARGE, be required to execute an Indemnity Bond in the prescribed\nform for safe custody and accounting of all materials issued by the EMPLOYER.\n67.10\nThe CONTRACTOR shall furnish to the ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE sufficiently in advance a statement showing his\nrequirement of the quantities of the materials to be supplied by the EMPLOYER and the time when the same will be required",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0147",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 147,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 120543,
    "char_end": 121472,
    "char_count": 929,
    "text": "by him for the works, so as to enable the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE to make necessary arrangements for procurement and supply\nof the material.\n67.11\nAccount of the materials issued by the EMPLOYER shall be maintained by CONTRACTOR indicating the daily receipt,\nconsumption and balance in hand. This account shall be maintained in a manner prescribed by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE\nalong with all connected papers viz. requisitions, issues, etc., and shall be always available for inspection in the\nCONTRACTOR's office at SITE.\n67.12\nThe CONTRACTOR should see that only the required quantities of materials are got issued. The CONTRACTOR shall not be\nentitled to cartage and incidental charges for returning the surplus materials, if any, to the stores wherefrom they were issued\nor to the place as directed by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE.\n67.13\nMaterials/Equipment(s) supplied by EMPLOYER shall not be utilised for any purpose(s) than issued for.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0148",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 148,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 121474,
    "char_end": 121476,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "26",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0149",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 149,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 121478,
    "char_end": 122838,
    "char_count": 1360,
    "text": "68 MATERIAL PROCURED WITH ASSISTANCE OF EMPLOYER/RETURN OF SURPLUS:\n68.1  Notwithstanding anything contained to the contrary in any or all the clauses of this CONTRACT where any materials for the\nexecution of the CONTRACT are procured with the assistance of the EMPLOYER either by issue from EMPLOYER's stock or\npurchases made under order or permits or licences issued by Government, the CONTRACTOR shall hold the said materials as\ntrustee for the EMPLOYER and use such materials economically and solely for the purpose of the CONTRACT and not dispose\nthem off without the permission of the EMPLOYER and return, if required by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE, shall determine\nhaving due regard to the condition of the materials. The price allowed to the CONTRACTOR, however, shall not exceed the\namount charged to him excluding the storage charges, if any. The decision of the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall be final and\nconclusive in such matters. In the event of breach of the aforesaid condition, the CONTRACTOR shall, in terms of the licences\nor permits and/or criminal breach of trust, be liable to compensate the EMPLOYER at double rate or any higher rate, in the\nevent of those materials at that time having higher rate or not being available in the market, then any other rate to be\ndetermined by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE and his decision shall be final and conclusive.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0150",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 150,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 122840,
    "char_end": 123218,
    "char_count": 378,
    "text": "69 MATERIALS OBTAINED FROM DISMANTLING:\n69.1  If the CONTRACTOR in the course of execution of the WORK is called upon to dismantle any part for reasons other than those\nstipulated in Clauses 74 and 77 hereunder, the materials obtained in the WORK of dismantling etc., will be considered as the\nEMPLOYER's property and will be disposed off to the best advantage of  the EMPLOYER.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0151",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 151,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 123220,
    "char_end": 123673,
    "char_count": 453,
    "text": "70 ARTICLES OF VALUE FOUND:\n70.1  All gold, silver and other minerals of any description and all precious stones, coins, treasure relics, antiquities and other\nsimilar things which shall be found in, under or upon the SITE, shall be the property of the EMPLOYER and the CONTRACTOR\nshall duly preserve the same to the satisfaction of the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE and shall from time to time deliver the same to\nsuch person or persons indicated by the EMPLOYER.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0152",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 152,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 123675,
    "char_end": 124299,
    "char_count": 624,
    "text": "71 DISCREPANCIES BETWEEN INSTRUCTIONS:\n71.1  Should any discrepancy occur between the various instructions furnished to the CONTRACTOR, his agent or staff or any doubt\narises as to the meaning of any such instructions or should there be any misunderstanding between the CONTRACTOR's staff\nand the ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE's staff, the CONTRACTOR shall refer the matter immediately in writing to the ENGINEER-IN-\nCHARGE whose decision thereon shall be final and conclusive and no claim for losses alleged to have been caused by such\ndiscrepancies between instructions, doubts, or misunderstanding shall in any event be admissible.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0153",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 153,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 124301,
    "char_end": 124742,
    "char_count": 441,
    "text": "72 ACTION WHERE NO SPECIFICATION IS ISSUED:\n72.1  In case of any class of WORK for which there is no SPECIFICATION supplied by the EMPLOYER as mentioned in the Tender\nDocuments such WORK shall be carried out in accordance with Indian Standard Specifications and if the Indian Standard\nSpecifications do not cover the same, the WORK should be carried out as per standard Engineering Practice subject to the\napproval of the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0154",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 154,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 124744,
    "char_end": 126519,
    "char_count": 1775,
    "text": "73 INSPECTION OF WORKS:\n73.1  The ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE will have full power and authority to inspect the WORK at any time wherever in progress either on\nthe SITE or at the CONTRACTOR's premises/workshops wherever situated, premises/ workshops of any person, firm or\ncorporation where WORK in connection with the CONTRACT may be in hand or where materials are being or are to be\nsupplied, and the CONTRACTOR shall afford or procure for the ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE every facility and assistance to carry out\nsuch inspection. The CONTRACTOR shall, at all time during the usual working hours and at all other time at which reasonable\nnotice of the intention of the ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE or his representative to visit the WORK shall have been given to the\nCONTRACTOR, either himself be present or receive orders and instructions, or have a responsible agent duly accredited in\nwriting, present for the purpose. Orders given to the CONTRACTOR's agent shall be considered to have the same force as if\nthey had been given to the CONTRACTOR himself. The CONTRACTOR shall give not less than seven days notice in writing to\nthe ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE before covering up or otherwise placing beyond reach of inspection and measurement of any work\nin order that the same may be inspected and measured. In the event of breach of above the same shall be uncovered at\nCONTRACTOR's expense for carrying out such measurement or inspection.\n73.2  No material shall be dispatched from the CONTRACTOR's stores before obtaining the approval in writing of the Engineer-in-\nCharge. The CONTRACTOR is to provide at all time during the progress of the WORK and the maintenance period, proper\nmeans of access with ladders, gangways etc. and the necessary attendance to move and adopt as directed for inspection or",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0155",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 155,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 126520,
    "char_end": 126849,
    "char_count": 329,
    "text": "measurements of the WORK by the ENGINEER- IN-CHARGE.\n73.3  The CONTRACTOR shall make available to the ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE free of cost all necessary instruments and assistance in\nchecking or setting out of WORK and in the checking of any WORK made by the CONTRACTOR for the purpose of setting out\nand taking measurements of WORK.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0156",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 156,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 126851,
    "char_end": 126880,
    "char_count": 29,
    "text": "74 TESTS FOR QUALITY OF WORK:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0157",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 157,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 126882,
    "char_end": 126884,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "27",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0158",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 158,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 126886,
    "char_end": 128222,
    "char_count": 1336,
    "text": "74.1  All workmanship shall be of the respective kinds described in the CONTRACT DOCUMENTS and in accordance with the\ninstructions of the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE and shall be subjected from time to time to such test at CONTRACTOR's cost as the\nENGINEER-IN-CHARGE may direct at the place of manufacture or fabrication or on the site or at all or any such places. The\nCONTRACTOR shall provide assistance, instruments, labour and materials as are normally required for examining, measuring\nand testing any workmanship as may be selected and required by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE.\n74.2  All the tests that will be necessary in connection with the execution of the WORK as decided by the ENGINEER- IN-CHARGE\nshall be carried out at the field testing laboratory of the EMPLOYER by paying the charges as decided by the EMPLOYER from\ntime to time. In case of non- availability of testing facility with the EMPLOYER, the required test shall be carried out at the cost\nof CONTRACTOR at Government or any other testing laboratory as directed by ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE.\n74.3  If any tests are required to be carried out in conjunction with the WORK or materials or workmanship not supplied by the\nCONTRACTOR, such tests shall be carried out by the CONTRACTOR as per instructions of ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE and cost of\nsuch tests shall be reimbursed by the EMPLOYER.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0159",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 159,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 128224,
    "char_end": 128674,
    "char_count": 450,
    "text": "75 SAMPLES FOR APPROVAL:\n75.1  The CONTRACTOR shall furnish to the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE for approval, when requested or if required by the\nspecifications, adequate samples of all materials and finished to be used in the WORK. Such samples shall be submitted before\nthe WORK is commenced and in ample time to permit tests and examinations thereof. All materials furnished and finishes\napplied in actual WORK shall be fully equal to the approved samples.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0160",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 160,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 128676,
    "char_end": 130278,
    "char_count": 1602,
    "text": "76 ACTION AND COMPENSATION IN CASE OF BAD WORK:\n76.1  If it shall appear to the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE that any work has been executed with unsound, imperfect or unskilled\nworkmanship, or with materials of any inferior description, or that any materials or articles provided by the CONTRACTOR for\nthe execution of the WORK are unsound, or of a quality inferior to that contracted for, or otherwise not in accordance with\nthe CONTRACT, the CONTRACTOR shall on demand in writing from the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE or his authorised representative\nspecifying the WORK, materials or articles complained of notwithstanding that the same may have been inadvertently passed,\ncertified and paid for, forthwith rectify or remove and reconstruct the WORK so specified and provide other proper and\nsuitable materials or articles at his own cost and in the event of failure to do so within the period specified by the ENGINEER-\nIN-CHARGE in his demand aforesaid, the CONTRACTOR shall be liable to pay compensation at the rate of 1 % (One percent) of\nthe estimated cost of the whole WORK, for every week limited to a maximum of 10% (ten percent) of the value of the whole\nWORK, while his failure to do so shall continue and in the case of any such failure the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE may on expiry of\nnotice period rectify or remove and re-execute the WORK or remove and replaced with others, the materials or articles\ncomplained of to as the case may be at the risk and expense in all respects of the CONTRACTOR. The decision of the\nEngineering-in-charge as to any question arising under this clause shall be final and conclusive.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0161",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 161,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 130280,
    "char_end": 131294,
    "char_count": 1014,
    "text": "77 SUSPENSION OF WORKS:\n77.1  Subject to the provisions of sub-para (ii) of this clause, the CONTRACTOR shall, if ordered in writing by the ENGINEER-IN-\nCHARGE, or his representative, temporarily suspend the WORKS or any part thereof for such written order, proceed with the\nWORK therein ordered to be suspended until, he shall have received a written order to proceed therewith. The CONTRACTOR\nshall not be entitled to claim compensation for any loss or damage sustained by him by reason of temporary suspension of the\nWORKS aforesaid. An extension of time for completion, corresponding with the delay caused by any such suspension of the\nWORKS as aforesaid will be granted to the ONTRACTOR should he apply for the same provided that the suspension was not\nconsequent to any default or failure on the part of the CONTRACTOR.\n77.2  In case of suspensions of entire WORK, ordered in writing by ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE, for a period of more than two months,\nthe CONTRACTOR shall have the option to terminate the CONTRACT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0162",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 162,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 131296,
    "char_end": 132058,
    "char_count": 762,
    "text": "78 EMPLOYER MAY DO PART OF WORK:\n78.1  Upon failure of the CONTRACTOR to comply with any instructions given in accordance with the provisions of this CONTRACT\nthe EMPLOYER has the alternative right, instead of assuming charge of entire WORK, to place additional labour force, tools,\nequipments and materials on such parts of the WORK, as the EMPLOYER may designate or also engage another CONTRACTOR\nto carry out the WORK. In such cases, the EMPLOYER shall deduct from the amount which otherwise might become due to the\nCONTRACTOR, the cost of such work and material with ten percent (10%) added to cover all departmental charges and should\nthe total amount thereof exceed the amount due to the CONTRACTOR, the CONTRACTOR shall pay the difference to the\nEMPLOYER.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0163",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 163,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 132060,
    "char_end": 132582,
    "char_count": 522,
    "text": "79 POSSESSION PRIOR TO COMPLETION:\n79.1 The ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall have the right to take possession of or use any completed or partially completed WORK or\npart of the WORK. Such possession or use shall not be deemed to be an acceptance of any work completed in accordance with\nthe CONTRACT agreement. If such prior possession or use by the ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE delays the progress of WORK,\nequitable adjustment in the time of completion will be made and the CONTRACT agreement shall be deemed to be modified\naccordingly.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0164",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 164,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 132584,
    "char_end": 132586,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "28",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0165",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 165,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 132588,
    "char_end": 134311,
    "char_count": 1723,
    "text": "80 DEFECTS LIABILITY PERIOD (TWELVE MONTHS PERIOD OF LIABILITY FROM THE DATE OF ISSUE OF COMPLETION\nCERTIFICATE):\n80.1  The CONTRACTOR shall guarantee the installation/WORK for a period of 12 months from the date of completion ofWORK as\ncertified by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE which is indicated in the Completion Certificate. Any damage or defect that may arise\nor lie undiscovered at the time of issue of Completion Certificate, connected in any way with the equipment or materials\nsupplied by him or in the workmanship, shall be rectified or replaced by the CONTRACTOR at his own expense as deemed\nnecessary by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE or in default, the ENGINEER- IN-CHARGE may carry out such works by other work and\ndeduct actual cost incurred towards labour, supervision and materials consumables or otherwise plus 100% towards\noverheads (of which the certificate of ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall be final) from any sums that may then be or at any time\nthereafter, become due to the CONTRACTOR or from his Contract Performance Security, or the proceeds of sale thereof or a\nsufficient part on thereof.\n80.2  If the CONTRACTOR feels that any variation in WORK or in quality of materials or proportions would be beneficial or\nnecessary to fulfil the guarantees called for, he shall bring this to the notice of the ENGINEER- IN-CHARGE in writing. If during\nthe period of liability any portion of the WORK/equipment, is found defective and is rectified/ replaced, the period of liability\nfor such equipment/ portion of WORK shall be operative from the date such rectification/ replacement are carried out and\nContract Performance Guarantee shall be furnished separately for the extended period of liability for that portion of WORK/",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0166",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 166,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 134312,
    "char_end": 134826,
    "char_count": 514,
    "text": "equipment only. Notwithstanding the above provisions the supplier's, guarantees/warrantees for the replaced equipment\nshall also be passed on to the EMPLOYER.\n80.3  LIMITATION OF LIABILITY Notwithstanding anything contrary contained herein, the aggregate total liability of CONTRACTOR\nunder the Agreement or otherwise shall be limited to 100% of Agreement / Contract Value. However, neither party shall be\nliable to the other party for any indirect and consequential damages, loss of profits or loss of production.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0167",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 167,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 134828,
    "char_end": 136561,
    "char_count": 1733,
    "text": "81 CARE OF WORKS:\n81.1  From the commencement to completion of the WORK, the CONTRACTOR shall take full responsibility for the care for all\nworks including all temporary works and in case any damages, loss or injury shall happen to the WORK or to any part thereof\nor to any temporary works from any cause whatsoever, shall at his own cost repair and make good the same so that at\ncompletion the WORK shall be in good order and in conformity in every respects with the requirement of the CONTRACT and\nthe ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE's instructions.\n81.2  DEFECTS PRIOR TO TAKING OVER: If at any time, before the WORK is taken over, the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall: a) Decide\nthat any works done or materials used by the CONTRACTOR or by any SUB-CONTRACTOR is defective or not in accordance\nwith the CONTRACT, or that the works or any portion thereof are defective, or do not fulfill the requirements of CONTRACT\n(all such matters being hereinafter, called `Defects' in this clause), and b) As soon as reasonably practicable, gives to the\nCONTRACTOR notice in writing of the said decision, specifying particulars of the defects alleged to exist or to have occurred,\nthen the CONTRACTOR shall at his own expenses and with all speed make good the defects so specified. In case CONTRACTOR\nshall fail to do so, the EMPLOYER may take, at the cost of the CONTRACTOR, such steps as may in all circumstances, be\nreasonable to make good such defects. The expenditure so incurred by the EMPLOYER will be recovered from the amount due\nto the CONTRACTOR. The decision of the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE with regard to the amount to be recovered from the\nCONTRACTOR will be final and binding on the CONTRACTOR. As soon as the WORK has been completed in accordance with",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0168",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 168,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 136562,
    "char_end": 138319,
    "char_count": 1757,
    "text": "the CONTRACT (except in minor respects that do not affect their use for the purpose for which they are intended and except\nfor maintenance thereof provided in clause 80.1 of General Conditions of Contract) and have passed the tests on completion,\nthe ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall issue a certificate (hereinafter called Completion Certificate) in which he shall certify the date\non which the WORK have been so completed and have passed the said tests and the EMPLOYER shall be deemed to have\ntaken over the WORK on the date so certified. If the WORK has been divided into various groups in the CONTRACT, the\nEMPLOYER shall be entitled to take over any group or groups before the other or others and there upon the ENGINEER-IN-\nCHARGE shall issue a Completion Certificate which will, however, be for such group or groups so taken over only. In such an\nevent if the group /section/ part so taken over is related, to the integrated system of the work, not withstanding date of grant\nof Completion Certificate for group/ section/ part. The period of liability in respect of such group/ section/ part shall extend\n12 (twelve) months from the date of completion of WORK.\n81.3  DEFECTS AFTER TAKING OVER: In order that the CONTRACTOR could obtain a COMPLETION CERTIFICATE he shall make good,\nwith all possible speed, any defect arising from the defective materials supplied by the CONTRACTOR or workmanship or any\nact or omission of the CONTRACT or that may have been noticed or developed, after the works or groups of the works has\nbeen taken over, the period allowed for carrying out such WORK will be normally one month. If any defect be not remedied\nwithin a reasonable time, the EMPLOYER may proceed to do the WORK at CONTRACTOR's risk and expense and deduct from",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0169",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 169,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 138320,
    "char_end": 138922,
    "char_count": 602,
    "text": "the final bill such amount as may be decided by the EMPLOYER. If by reason of any default on the part of the CONTRACTOR a\nCOMPLETION CERTIFICATE has not been issued in respect of any portion of the WORK within one month after the date fixed\nby the CONTRACT for the completion of the WORK, the EMPLOYER shall be at liberty to use the WORK or any portion thereof\nin respect of which a completion certificate has not been issued, provided that the WORK or the portion thereof so used as\naforesaid shall be afforded reasonable opportunity for completing these works for the issue of Completion Certificate.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
