    "char_start": 138928,
    "char_end": 139502,
    "char_count": 574,
    "text": "82 GUARANTEE/TRANSFER OF GUARANTEE:\n82.1  For works like water-proofing, acid and alkali resisting materials, pre-construction soil treatment against termite or any other\nspecialized works etc. the CONTRACTOR shall invariably engage SUB-CONTRACTORS who are specialists in the field and firms\nof repute and such a SUB-CONTRACTOR shall furnish guarantees for their workmanship to the EMPLOYER, through the\nCONTRACTOR. In case such a SUB-CONTRACTOR/ firm is not prepared to furnish a guarantee to the EMPLOYER, the\nCONTRACTOR shall give that guarantee to the EMPLOYER directly.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0172",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 172,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 139504,
    "char_end": 140323,
    "char_count": 819,
    "text": "83 TRAINING OF EMPLOYER'S PERSONNEL:\n83.1  The CONTRACTOR undertakes to provide training to Engineering personnel selected and sent by the EMPLOYER at the works\nof the CONTRACTOR without any cost to the EMPLOYER. The period and the nature of training for the individual personnel\nshall be agreed upon mutually between the CONTRACTOR and the EMPLOYER. These engineering personnel shall be given\nspecial training at the shops, where the equipment will be manufactured and/ or in their collaborator's works and where\npossible, in any other plant where equipment manufactured by the CONTRACTOR or his collaborators is under installation or\ntest to enable those personnel to become familiar with the equipment being furnished by the CONTRACTOR. EMPLOYER shall\nbear only the to and fro fare of the said engineering personnel.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0173",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 173,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 140325,
    "char_end": 142055,
    "char_count": 1730,
    "text": "84 REPLACEMENT OF DEFECTIVE PARTS AND MATERIALS:\n84.1  If during the progress of the WORK, EMPLOYER shall decide and inform in writing to the CONTRACTOR, that the CONTRACTOR\nhas manufactured any plant or part of the plant unsound or imperfect or has furnished plant inferior to the quality specified,\nthe CONTRACTOR on receiving details of such defects or deficiencies shall at his own expenses within 7 (seven) days of his\nreceiving the notice, or otherwise within such time as may be reasonably necessary for making it good, proceed to alter, re-\nconstruct or remove such work and furnish fresh equipments upto the standards of the specifications. In case the\nCONTRACTOR fails to do so, EMPLOYER may on giving the CONTRACTOR 7 (seven) day's notice in writing of his intentions to\ndo so, proceed to remove the portion of the WORK so complained of and at the cost of CONTRACTOR's,\n84.2 all such works or furnish all such equipments provided that nothing in the clause shall be deemed to deprive the EMPLOYER of\nor affect any rights under the CONTRACT, the EMPLOYER may otherwise have in respect of such defects and deficiencies.\n84.3  The CONTRACTOR's full and extreme liability under this clause shall be satisfied by the payments to the EMPLOYER of the\nextra cost, of such replacements procured including erection/installation as provided for in the CONTRACT; such extra cost\nbeing the ascertained difference between the price paid by the EMPLOYER for such replacements and the CONTRACT price\nportion for such defective plants and repayments of any sum paid by the EMPLOYER to the CONTRACTOR in respect of such\ndefective plant. Should the EMPLOYER not so replace the defective plant the CONTRACTOR's extreme liability under this",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0174",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 174,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 142056,
    "char_end": 142179,
    "char_count": 123,
    "text": "clause shall be limited to the repayment of all such sums paid by the EMPLOYER under the CONTRACT for such defective\nplant.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0175",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 175,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 142181,
    "char_end": 142908,
    "char_count": 727,
    "text": "85 INDEMNITY\n85.1  If any action is brought before a Court, Tribunal or any other Authority against the Employer or an officer or agent of the\nEMPLOYER, for the failure, omission or neglect on the part of the CONTRACTOR to perform any acts, matters, covenants or\nthings under the CONTRACT, or damage or injury caused by the alleged omission or negligence on the part of the\nCONTRACTOR, his agents, representatives or his SUB- CONTRACTOR's, or in connection with any claim based on lawful\ndemands of SUB-CONTRACTOR's workmen suppliers or employees, the CONTRACTOR, shall in such cases indemnify and keep\nthe EMPLOYER and/or their representatives harmless from all losses, damages, expenses or decrees arising out of such action.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0176",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 176,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 142910,
    "char_end": 144080,
    "char_count": 1170,
    "text": "86 CONSTRUCTION AIDS, EQUIPMENTS, TOOLS & TACKLES:\n86.1  CONTRACTOR shall be solely responsible for making available for executing the WORK, all requisite CONSTRUCTION\nEQUIPMENTS, Special Aids, Barges, Cranes and the like, all Tools, Tackles and Testing Equipment and Appliances, including\nimports of such equipment etc. as required. In case of import of the same the rates applicable for levying of Custom Duty on\nsuch Equipment, Tools, & Tackles and the duty drawback applicable thereon shall be ascertained by the CONTRACTOR from\nthe concerned authorities of Government of India. It shall be clearly understood that EMPLOYER shall not in any way be\nresponsible for arranging to obtain Custom Clearance and/or payment of any duties and/or duty draw backs etc. for such\nequipments so imported by the CONTRACTOR and the CONTRACTOR shall be fully responsible for all taxes, duties and\ndocumentation with regard to the same. Tenderer in his own interest may contact, for any clarifications in the matter,\nconcerned agencies/Dept./Ministries of Govt. of India. All clarifications so obtained and interpretations thereof shall be solely\nthe responsibility of the CONTRACTOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0177",
