    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0183",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 183,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 149845,
    "char_end": 150857,
    "char_count": 1012,
    "text": "88 PROCEDURE FOR MEASUREMENT AND BILLING OF WORK IN PROGRESS:\n88.1  BILLING PROCEDURE: Following procedures shall be adopted for billing of works executed by the CONTRACTOR.\n88.1.1\nAll measurements shall be recorded in sextuplicate on standard measurement sheets supplied by EMPLOYER and\nsubmitted to EMPLOYER/CONSULTANT for scrutiny and passing.\n88.1.2\nEMPLOYER/CONSULTANT shall scrutinise and check the measurements recorded on the sheets and shall certify\ncorrectness of the same on the measurement sheets.\n88.1.3\nENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall pass the bills after carrying out the comprehensive checks in accordance with the terms and\nconditions of the CONTRACTS, within 7 days of submission of the bills, complete in all respects and send the same to the\nEmployer to effect payment to the CONTRACTOR.\n88.1.4\nBCPL shall make all endeavor to make payments of undisputed amount of the bills submitted based on the joint\nmeasurements within 15 (Fifteen) days from the date of certification by the Engineer-in-Charge.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0184",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 184,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 150859,
    "char_end": 150861,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "31",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0185",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 185,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 150863,
    "char_end": 152644,
    "char_count": 1781,
    "text": "88.1.5\nMeasurements shall be recorded as per the methods of measurement spelt out in EMPLOYER/CONSULTANT\nSPECIFICATIONS / CONTRACT DOCUMENT. EMPLOYER/CONSULTANT shall be fully responsible for checking the\nmeasurements quantitatively and qualitatively as recorded in the Measurement Books/ Bills.\n88.1.6\nWhile preparing the final bills overall measurements will not be taken again. Only volume of work executed since the last\nmeasured bill alongwith summary of final measurements will be considered for the final bill. However, a detailed check\nshall be made as to missing measurements and in case there are any missing items or measurements the same shall be\nrecorded.\n88.1.7\nCOMPUTERISED BILLING SYSTEM :BCPL has introduced Computerized Billing System whereby when the Bills are\nsubmitted in BCPL by a Contractor, a receipt number is generated. The Contractor can know the status of the Bill through\nBCPL’s website.(Not applicable in case of BCPL)\n88.2  SECURED ADVANCEON MATERIAL: Unless otherwise provided elsewhere in the tender, no `Secured Advance' on security of\nmaterials brought to site for execution of contracted items(s) shall be paid to the Contractor whatsoever.\n88.3  DISPUTE IN MODE OF MEASUREMENT: In case of any dispute as to the mode of measurement not covered by the CONTRACT\nto be adopted for any item of WORK, mode of measurement as per latest Indian Standard Specifications shall be followed.\n88.4  ROUNDING-OFF OF AMOUNTS: In calculating the amount of each item due to the CONTRACTOR in every certificate prepared\nfor payment, sum of less than 50 paise shall be omitted and the total amount on each certificate shall be rounded off to the\nnearest rupees, i.e., sum of less than 50 paise shall be omitted and sums of 50 paise and more upto one rupee shall be",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
