    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 186,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 152645,
    "char_end": 152667,
    "char_count": 22,
    "text": "reckoned as one rupee.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0187",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 187,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 152669,
    "char_end": 152861,
    "char_count": 192,
    "text": "89 LUMP SUM IN TENDER:\n89.1  The payment against any Lump sum item shall be made only on completion of that item as per the provision of the\nCONTRACT after certification by ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0188",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 188,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 152863,
    "char_end": 153914,
    "char_count": 1051,
    "text": "90 RUNNING ACCOUNT PAYMENTS TO BE REGARDED AS ADVANCE:\n90.1  All running account payments shall be regarded as payment by way of advance against the final payment only and not as\npayments for WORK actually done and completed and shall not preclude the requiring of bad, unsound and imperfect or\nunskilled work to be removed and taken away and reconstructed or re-erected or be considered as an admission of the due\nperformance of the CONTRACT, or any part thereof, in this respect, or of the accruing of any claim by the CONTRACTOR, nor\nshall it conclude, determine or affect in any way the powers of the EMPLOYER under these conditions or any of them as to the\nfinal settlement and adjustment of the accounts or otherwise, or in any other way vary or affect the CONTRACT. The final bill\nshall be submitted by the CONTRACTOR within one month of the date of physical completion of the WORK, otherwise, the\nENGINEER-IN-CHARGE's certificate of the measurement and of total amount payable for the WORK accordingly shall be final\nand binding on all parties",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0189",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 189,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 153916,
    "char_end": 155652,
    "char_count": 1736,
    "text": "91 NOTICE OF CLAIMS FOR ADDITIONAL PAYMENTS:\n91.1  Should the CONTRACTOR consider that he is entitled to any extra payment for any extra/additional WORKS or MATERIAL\nchange in original SPECIFICATIONS carried out by him in respect of WORK he shall forthwith give notice in writing to the\nENGINEER-IN-CHARGE that he claims extra payment. Such notice shall be given to the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE upon which\nCONTRACTOR bases such claims and such notice shall contain full particulars of the nature of such claim with full details of\namount claimed. Irrespective of any provision in the CONTRACT to the contrary, the CONTRACTOR must intimate his intention\nto lodge claim on the EMPLOYER within 10 (ten) days of the commencement of happening of the event and quantify the claim\nwithin 30 (thirty) days, failing which the CONTRACTOR will lose his right to claim any compensation/reimbursement/damages\netc. or refer the matter to arbitration. Failure on the part of CONTRACTOR to put forward any claim without the necessary\nparticulars as above within the time above specified shall be an absolute waiver thereof. No omission by EMPLOYER to reject\nany such claim and no delay in dealing therewith shall be waiver by EMPLOYER of any of these rights in respect thereof.\n91.2  ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall review such claims within a reasonable period of time and cause to discharge these in a manner\nconsidered appropriate after due deliberations thereon. However, CONTRACTOR shall be obliged to carry on with the WORK\nduring the period in which his claims are under consideration by the EMPLOYER, irrespective of the outcome of such claims,\nwhere additional payments for WORKS considered extra are justifiable in accordance with the CONTRACT provisions,",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0190",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 190,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 155653,
    "char_end": 156545,
    "char_count": 892,
    "text": "EMPLOYER shall arrange to release the same in the same manner as for normal WORK payments. Such of the extra works so\nadmitted by EMPLOYER shall be governed by all the terms, conditions, stipulations and specifications as are applicable for the\nCONTRACT. The rates for extra works shall generally be the unit rates provided for in the CONTRACT. In the event unit rates\nfor extra works so executed are not available as per CONTRACT, payments may either be released on day work basis for which\ndaily/hourly rates for workmen and hourly rates for equipment rental shall apply, or on the unit rate for WORK executed shall\nbe derived by interpolation/ extrapolation of unit rates already existing in the CONTRACT. In all the matters pertaining to\napplicability of rate and admittance of otherwise of an extra work claim of CONTRACTOR the decision of ENGINEER-IN-\nCHARGE shall be final and binding.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0191",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 191,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 156547,
    "char_end": 156549,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "32",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0192",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 192,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 156551,
    "char_end": 157905,
    "char_count": 1354,
    "text": "92 PAYMENT OF CONTRACTOR'S BILL:\n92.1  No payment shall be made for works estimated to cost less than Rs.10,000/- till the whole of the work shall have been\ncompleted and a certificate of completion given. But in case of works estimated to cost more than Rs.10,000/-, that\nCONTRACTOR on submitting the bill thereof be entitled to receive a monthly payment proportionate to the part thereof\napproved and passed by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE, whose certificate of such approval and passing of the sum so payable\nshall be final and conclusive against the CONTRACTOR. This payment will be made after making necessary\ncorrections/deductions as stipulated elsewhere in the CONTRACT DOCUMENT for materials, Contract Performance Security,\ntaxes etc.\n92.2  Payment due to the CONTRACTOR shall be made by the EMPLOYER by Account Payee cheque forwarding the same to\nregistered office or the notified office of the CONTRACTOR. In no case will EMPLOYER be responsible if the cheque is mislaid\nor misappropriated by unauthorised person/persons. In all cases, the CONTRACTOR shall present his bill duly pre-receipted on\nproper revenue stamp payment shall be made in Indian Currency.\n92.3  In general payment of final bill shall be made to CONTRACTOR within 60 days of the submission of bill on joint\nmeasurements, after completion of all the obligations under the CONTRACT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0193",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 193,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 157907,
    "char_end": 158373,
    "char_count": 466,
    "text": "93 RECEIPT FOR PAYMENT:\n93.1  Receipt for payment made on account of work when executed by a firm, must be signed by a person holding due power of\nattorney in this respect on behalf of the CONTRACTOR, except when the CONTRACTOR's are described in their tender as a\nlimited company in which case the receipts must be signed in the name of the company by one of its principal officers or by\nsome other person having authority to give effectual receipt for the company.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0194",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 194,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 158375,
    "char_end": 160054,
    "char_count": 1679,
    "text": "94 COMPLETION CERTIFICATE:\n94.1  APPLICATION FOR COMPLETION CERTIFICATE: When the CONTRACTOR fulfils his obligation under Clause 81.1 he shall be\neligible to apply for COMPLETION CERTIFICATE. The ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall normally issue to the CONTRACTOR the\nCOMPLETION CERTIFICATE within one month after receiving any application therefore from the CONTRACTOR after verifying\nfrom the completion documents and satisfying himself that the WORK has been completed in accordance with and as set out\nin the construction and erection drawings, and the CONTRACT DOCUMENTS. The CONTRACTOR, after obtaining the\nCOMPLETION CERTIFICATE, is eligible to present the final bill for the WORK executed by him under the terms of CONTRACT.\n94.2  COMPLETION CERTIFICATE: Within one month of the completion of the WORK in all respects, the CONTRACTOR shall be\nfurnished with a certificate by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE of such completion, but no certificate shall be given nor shall the\nWORK be deemed to have been executed until all scaffolding, surplus materials and rubbish is cleared off the SITE completely\nnor until the WORK shall have been measured by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE whose measurement shall be binding and\nconclusive. The WORKS will not be considered as complete and taken over by the EMPLOYER, until all the temporary works,\nlabour and staff colonies are cleared to the satisfaction of the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE. If the CONTRACTOR fails to comply with\nthe requirements of this clause on or before the date fixed for the completion of the WORK, the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE may at\nthe expense of the CONTRACTOR remove such scaffolding, surplus materials and rubbish and dispose off the same as he",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0195",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 195,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 160055,
    "char_end": 161090,
    "char_count": 1035,
    "text": "thinks fit and clean off such dirt as aforesaid, and the CONTRACTOR shall forthwith pay the amount of all expenses so incurred\nand shall have no claim in respect of any such scaffolding or surplus materials as aforesaid except for any sum actually realised\nby the sale thereof.\n94.3  COMPLETION CERTIFICATE DOCUMENTS: For the purpose of Clause 94.0 the following documents will be deemed to form the\ncompletion documents:\n(i)\nThe technical documents according to which the WORK was carried out. Six (6) sets of construction drawings showing\ntherein the modification and correction made during the course of execution and signed by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE.\n(ii)\nCOMPLETION CERTIFICATE for `embedded' and `covered' up work.\n(iii)\nCertificates of final levels as set out for various works.\n(iv)\nCertificates of tests performed for various WORKS.\n(v)\nMaterial appropriation, Statement for the materials issued by the EMPLOYER for the WORK and list of surplus\nmaterials returned to the EMPLOYER's store duly supported by necessary documents.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0196",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 196,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 161092,
    "char_end": 162023,
    "char_count": 931,
    "text": "95 FINAL DECISION AND FINAL CERTIFICATE:\n95.1  Upon expiry of the period of liability and subject to the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE being satisfied that the WORKS have been duly\nmaintained by the CONTRACTOR during monsoon or such period as hereinbefore provided in Clause 80 & 81 and that the\nCONTRACTOR has in all respect duly made-up any subsidence and performed all his obligations under the CONTRACT, the\nENGINEER-IN- CHARGE shall (without prejudice to the rights of the EMPLOYER to retain the provisions of relevant Clause\nhereof) otherwise give a certificate herein referred to as the FINAL CERTIFICATE to that effect and the CONTRACTOR shall not\nbe considered to have fulfilled the whole of his obligations under CONTRACT until FINAL CERTIFICATE shall have been given by\nthe ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE notwithstanding any previous entry upon the WORK and taking possession, working or using of the\nsame or any part thereof by the EMPLOYER.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0197",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 197,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 162025,
    "char_end": 162027,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "33",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0198",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 198,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 162029,
    "char_end": 162366,
    "char_count": 337,
    "text": "96 CERTIFICATE AND PAYMENTS ON EVIDENCE OF COMPLETION:\n96.1  Except the FINAL CERTIFICATE, no other certificates or payments against a certificate or on general account shall be taken to\nbe an admission by the EMPLOYER of the due performance of the CONTRACT or any part thereof or of occupancy or validity of\nany claim by the CONTRACTOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0199",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 199,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 162368,
    "char_end": 163142,
    "char_count": 774,
    "text": "97 DEDUCTIONS FROM THE CONTRACT PRICE:\n97.1  All costs, damages or expenses which EMPLOYER may have paid or incurred, which under the provisions of the CONTRACT,\nthe CONTRACTOR is liable/will be liable, will be claimed by the EMPLOYER. All such claims shall be billed by the EMPLOYER to\nthe CONTRACTOR regularly as and when they fall due. Such claims shall be paid by the CONTRACTOR within 15 (fifteen) days\nof the receipt of the corresponding bills and if not paid by the CONTRACTOR within the said period, the EMPLOYER may, then,\ndeduct the amount from any moneys due i.e., Contract Performance Security or becoming due to the CONTRACTOR under the\nCONTRACT or may be recovered by actions of law or otherwise, if the CONTRACTOR fails to satisfy the EMPLOYER of such\nclaims.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0200",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 200,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 163144,
    "char_end": 164743,
    "char_count": 1599,
    "text": "SECTION-VII TAXES AND INSURANCE\n98 TAXES, DUTIES, OCTROIETC:\n98.1  The CONTRACTOR agrees to and does hereby accept full and exclusive liability for the payment of any and all Taxes, Duties,\nincluding Excise duty, octroi etc. now or hereafter imposed, increased, modified, all the sales taxes, duties, octrois etc. now in\nforce and hereafter increased, imposed or modified, from time to time in respect of WORKS and materials and all\ncontributions and taxes for unemployment compensation, insurance and old age pensions or annuities now or hereafter\nimposed by any Central or State Government authorities which are imposed with respect to or covered by the wages, salaries,\nor other compensations paid to the persons employed by the CONTRACTOR and the CONTRACTOR shall be responsible for the\ncompliance of all SUB-CONTRACTORS, with all applicable Central, State, Municipal and local law and regulation and\nrequirement of any Central, State or local Government agency or authority. CONTRACTOR further agrees to defend, indemnify\nand hold EMPLOYER harmless from any liability or penalty which may be imposed by the Central, State or Local authorities by\nreason or any violation by CONTRACTOR or SUB-CONTRACTOR of such laws, suits or proceedings that may be brought against\nthe EMPLOYER arising under, growing out of, or by reason of the work provided for by this CONTRACT, by third parties, or by\nCentral or State Government authority or any administrative sub-division thereof. Tax deductions will be made as per the\nrules and regulations in force in accordance with acts prevailing from time to time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0201",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 201,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 164745,
    "char_end": 165108,
    "char_count": 363,
    "text": "99 SALES TAX/TURNOVER TAX:\n99.1  Tenderer should quote all inclusive prices including the liability of Sales Tax/Turnover Tax whether on the works contract as a\nwhole or in respect of bought out components used by the CONTRACTOR in execution of the CONTRACT.  EMPLOYER shall not\nbe responsible for any such liability of the CONTRACTOR in respect of this CONTRACT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0202",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 202,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 165110,
    "char_end": 165698,
    "char_count": 588,
    "text": "100 STATUTORY VARIATIONS / EXCISE DUTY\n100.1\nTenderer should quote prices inclusive of excise-duty and sales tax applicable on finished product. Any statutory\nvariations in Excise Duty and sales tax on finished product during the contractual completion period, shall be to the\nEmployer's account for which the Contractor will furnish documentary evidence(s) in support of their claims to BCPL.\nHowever, any increase in the rate of these taxes and duties (E.D. and S.T.) beyond the contractual completion period shall be\nto Contractor's account and any decrease shall be passed on to BCPL.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0203",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 203,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 165700,
    "char_end": 166832,
    "char_count": 1132,
    "text": "101 SERVICE TAX\n101.1 Vendors should submit a copy of service tax registration certificate while submitting the bids wherever service tax is\napplicable.\n101.2 Vendors charging service tax have to issue bills/invoices in accordance with rule 4A of Service Tax Rules, 1994\n101.3 Payments to the vendors will be released after submission of the above documents.\n101.4 Vendors should submit copies of challan and certificate from Chartered Accountant for deposit of service tax collected\n102  INSURANCE:\n102.0 GENERAL CONTRACTOR shall at his own expense arrange secure and maintain insurance with reputable insurance companies\nto the satisfaction of the EMPLOYER as follows: CONTRACTOR at his cost shall arrange, secure and maintain insurance as may be\nnecessary and to its full value for all such amounts to protect the WORKS in progress from time to time and the interest of\nEMPLOYER against all risks as detailed herein. The form and the limit of such insurance, as defined here in together with the under\nworks thereof in each case should be as acceptable to the EMPLOYER. However, irrespective of work acceptance the responsibility",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
