  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0212",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 212,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 175769,
    "char_end": 177405,
    "char_count": 1636,
    "text": "103\n DAMAGE TO PROPERTY OR TO ANY PERSON OR ANY THIRD PARTY\n103.1\nCONTRACTOR shall be responsible for making good to the satisfaction of the EMPLOYER any loss or any damage to\nstructures and properties belonging to the EMPLOYER or being executed or procured or being procured by the EMPLOYER\nor of other agencies within in the premises of all the work of the EMPLOYER, if such loss or damage is due to fault and/or\nthe negligence or willful acts or omission of the CONTRACTOR, his employees, agents, representatives or SUB-\nCONTRACTORs.\n103.2\nThe CONTRACTOR shall take sufficient care in moving his plants, equipments and materials from one place to another so\nthat they do not cause any damage to any person or to the property of the EMPLOYER or any third party including\noverhead and underground cables and in the event of any damage resulting to the property of the EMPLOYER or of a third\nparty during the movement of the aforesaid plant, equipment or materials the cost of such damages including eventual\nloss of production, operation or services in any plant or establishment as estimated by the EMPLOYER or ascertained or\ndemanded by the third party shall be borne by the CONTRACTOR. Third party liability risk shall be Rupees One lakh for\nsingle accident and limited to Rupees Ten lakhs.\n103.3\nThe CONTRACTOR shall indemnify and keep the EMPLOYER harmless of all claims for damages to property other than\nEMPLOYER's property arising under or by reason of this agreement, if such claims result from the fault and/or negligence\nor willful acts or omission of the CONTRACTOR, his employees, agents, representative of SUB-CONTRACTOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0213",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 213,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 177407,
    "char_end": 179190,
    "char_count": 1783,
    "text": "SECTION-VIII LABOUR LAWS\n104\nLABOUR LAWS:\n104.1\nNo labour below the age of 18 (eighteen) years shall be employed on the WORK.\n104.2\nThe CONTRACTOR shall not pay less than what is provided under law to labourers engaged by him on the WORK.\n104.3\nThe CONTRACTOR shall at his expense comply with all labour laws and keep the EMPLOYER indemnified in respect thereof.\n104.4\nThe CONTRACTOR shall pay equal wages for men and women in accordance with applicable labour laws.\n104.5\nIf the CONTRACTOR is covered under the Contract labour (Regulation and Abolition) Act, he shall obtain a license from\nlicensing authority (i.e. office of the labour commissioner) by payment of necessary prescribed fee and the deposit, if any,\nbefore starting the WORK under the CONTRACT. Such fee/deposit shall be borne by the CONTRACTOR.\n104.6\nThe CONTRACTOR shall employ labour in sufficient numbers either directly or through SUB- CONTRACTOR's to maintain\nthe required rate of progress and of quality to ensure workmanship of the degree specified in the CONTRACT and to the\nsatisfaction of the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE.\n104.7\nThe CONTRACTOR shall furnish to the ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE the distribution return of the number and description, by\ntrades of the work people employed on the works. The CONTRACTOR shall also submit on the 4th and 19th of every\nmonth to the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE a true statement showing in respect of the second half of the preceding month and\nthe first half of the current month (1) the accidents that occurred during the said fortnight showing the circumstances\nunder which they happened and the extent of damage and injury caused by them and (2) the number of female workers\nwho have been allowed Maternity Benefit as provided in the Maternity Benefit Act 1961 on Rules made thereunder and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0214",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 214,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 179191,
    "char_end": 179683,
    "char_count": 492,
    "text": "the amount paid to them.\n104.8\nThe CONTRACTOR shall comply with the provisions of the payment of Wage Act 1936, Employee Provident Fund Act 1952,\nand Minimum Wages Act 1948. Employers Liability Act 1938. Workmen's Compensation Act 1923, Industrial Disputes Act\n1947, the Maternity Benefit Act 1961 and Contract Labour Regulation and Abolition Act 1970, Employment of Children Act\n1938 or any modifications thereof or any other law relating thereto and rules made thereunder from time to time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0215",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 215,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 179685,
    "char_end": 179687,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "36",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0216",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 216,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 179689,
    "char_end": 181439,
    "char_count": 1750,
    "text": "104.9\nThe ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall on a report having been made by an Inspecting Officer as defined in Contract Labour\n(Regulation and Abolition) Act 1970 have the power to deduct from the money due to the CONTRACTOR any sum required\nor estimated to be required for making good the loss suffered by a worker or workers by reason of non- fulfillment of the\nConditions of the Contract for the benefit of workers, non-payment of wages or of deductions made from his or their\nwages which are not justified by the terms of the Contract or non-observance of the said regulations.\n104.10 The CONTRACTOR shall indemnify the EMPLOYER against any payments to be made under and for the observance of the\nprovisions of the aforesaid Acts without prejudice to his right to obtain indemnity from his SUB-CONTRACTOR's. In the\nevent of the CONTRACTOR committing a default or breach of any of the provisions of the aforesaid Acts as amended from\ntime to time, of furnishing any information or submitting or filling and Form/ Register/ Slip under the provisions of these\nActs which is materially incorrect then on the report of the inspecting Officers, the CONTRACTOR shall without prejudice\nto any other liability pay to the EMPLOYER a sum not exceeding Rs.50.00 as Liquidated Damages for every default, breach\nor furnishing, making, submitting, filling materially incorrect statement as may be fixed by the ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE and\nin the event of the CONTRACTOR's default continuing in this respect, the Liquidated Damages may be enhanced to\nRs.50.00 per day for each day of default subject to a maximum of one percent of the estimated cost of the WORK put to\ntender. The ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall deduct such amount from bills or Contract Performance Security of the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0217",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 217,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 181440,
    "char_end": 181603,
    "char_count": 163,
    "text": "CONTRACTOR and credit the same to the Welfare Fund constitute under these acts. The decision of the ENGINEER-IN-\nCHARGE in this respect shall be final and binding.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0218",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 218,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 181605,
    "char_end": 183328,
    "char_count": 1723,
    "text": "105\n IMPLEMENTATION OF APPRENTICES ACT, 1961:\n105.1\nThe CONTRACTOR shall comply with the provisions of the Apprentices Act, 1961 and the Rules and Orders issued\nthereunder from time to time. If he fails to do so, his failure will be a breach of the CONTRACT and the ENGINEER-IN-\nCHARGE may, at his discretion, cancel the CONTRACT. The CONTRACTOR shall also be liable for any pecuniary liability\narising on account of any violation by him of the provisions, of the Act.\n106\n CONTRACTOR TO INDEMNIFY THE EMPLOYER:\n106.1\nThe CONTRACTOR shall indemnify the EMPLOYER and every member, office and employee of the EMPLOYER, also the\nENGINEER-IN-CHARGE and his staff against all actions, proceedings, claims, demands, costs and expenses whatsoever\narising out of or in connection with the matters referred to in Clause 102.0 and elsewhere and all actions, proceedings,\nclaims, demands, costs and expenses which may be made against the EMPLOYER for or in respect of or arising out of any\nfailure by the CONTRACTOR in the performance of his obligations under the CONTRACT DOCUMENT. The EMPLOYER shall\nnot be liable for or in respect of or arising out of any failure by the CONTRACTOR in the performance of his obligations\nunder the CONTRACT DOCUMENT. The EMPLOYER shall not be liable for or in respect of any demand or compensation\npayable by law in respect or in consequence of any accident or injury to any workmen or other person. In the employment\nof the CONTRACTOR or his SUB-CONTRACTOR the CONTRACTOR shall indemnify and keep indemnified the EMPLOYER\nagainst all such damages and compensations and against all claims, damages, proceedings, costs, charges and expenses\nwhatsoever in respect thereof or in relation thereto.\n106.2",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0219",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 219,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 183329,
    "char_end": 184796,
    "char_count": 1467,
    "text": "PAYMENT OF CLAIMS AND DAMAGES: Should the EMPLOYER have to pay any money in respect of such claims or demands\nas aforesaid the amount so paid and the costs incurred by the EMPLOYER shall be charged to and paid by the\nCONTRACTOR and the CONTRACTOR shall not be at liberty to dispute or question the right of the EMPLOYER to make such\npayments notwithstanding the same, may have been made without the consent or authority or in law or otherwise to the\ncontrary.\n106.3\nIn every case in which by virtue of the provisions of Section 12, Sub-section (i) of workmen's compensation Act, 1923 or\nother applicable provision of Workmen Compensation Act or any other Act, the EMPLOYER is obliged to pay compensation\nto a workman employed by the CONTRACTOR in execution of the WORK, the EMPLOYER will recover from the\nCONTRACTOR the amount of the compensation so paid, and without prejudice to the rights of EMPLOYER under Section\n12, Sub- section (2) of the said act, EMPLOYER shall be at liberty to recover such amount or any part thereof by deducting\nit from the Contract Performance Security or from any sum due to the CONTRACTOR whether under this CONTRACT or\notherwise. The EMPLOYER shall not be bound to contest any claim made under Section 12, Sub-section (i) of the said act,\nexcept on the written request of the CONTRACTOR and upon his giving to the EMPLOYER full security for all costs for\nwhich the EMPLOYER might become liable in consequence of contesting such claim.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0220",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 220,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 184798,
    "char_end": 185550,
    "char_count": 752,
    "text": "107\n HEALTH AND SANITARY ARRANGEMENTS FOR WORKERS:\n107.1\nIn respect of all labour directly or indirectly employed in the WORKS for the performance of the CONTRACTOR's part of\nthis agreement, the CONTRACTOR shall comply with or cause to be complied with all the rules and regulations of the local\nsanitary and other authorities or as framed by the EMPLOYER from time to time for the protection of health and sanitary\narrangements for all workers.\n107.2\nThe CONTRACTOR shall provide in the labour colony all amenities such as electricity, water and other sanitary and health\narrangements. The CONTRACTOR shall also provide necessary surface transportation to the place of work and back to the\ncolony\nfor\ntheir\npersonnel\naccommodated\nin\nthe\nlabour\ncolony.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0221",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 221,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 185552,
    "char_end": 185554,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "37",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0222",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 222,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 185556,
    "char_end": 187335,
    "char_count": 1779,
    "text": "SECTION-IX APPLICABLE LAWS AND SETTLEMENT OF DISPUTES\n108\n ARBITRATION:\n108.1\nUnless otherwise specified, the matters where decision of the Engineer-in-Charge is deemed to be final and binding as\nprovided in the Agreement and the issues/disputes which cannot be mutually resolved within a reasonable time, all\ndisputes shall be referred to arbitration by Sole Arbitrator. The Employer [BCPL] shall suggest a panel of three independent\nand distinguished persons to the bidder/contractor/supplier/buyer (as the case may be) to select any one among them to\nact as the Sole Arbitrator. In the event of failure of the other parties to select the Sole Arbitrator within 30 days from the\nreceipt of the communication suggesting the panel of arbitrators, the right of selection of the sole arbitrator by the other\nparty shall stand forfeited and the EMPLOYER (BCPL) shall have discretion to proceed with the appointment of the Sole\nArbitrator. The decision of Employer on the appointment of the sole arbitrator shall be final and binding on the parties.\nThe award of sole arbitrator shall be final and binding on the parties and unless directed/awarded otherwise by the sole\narbitrator, the cost of arbitration proceedings shall be shared equally by the parties. The Arbitration proceedings shall be\nin English language and venue shall be Guwahati, India. Subject to the above, the provisions of (Indian) Arbitration &\nConciliation ACT 1996 and the Rules framed there under shall be applicable. All matter relating to this contract is subject\nto the exclusive jurisdiction of the court situated in the state of Delhi. Bidders/suppliers/contractors may please note that\nthe Arbitration & Conciliation Act 1996 was enacted by the Indian Parliament and is based on United Nations Commission",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0223",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 223,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 187336,
    "char_end": 188819,
    "char_count": 1483,
    "text": "on International Trade Law (UNCITRAL model law), which were prepared after extensive consultation with Arbitral\nInstitutions and centers of International Commercial Arbitration. The United Nations General Assembly vide resolution\n31/98 adopted the UNCITRAL Arbitration rules on 15 December 1976.\n108.2\nFOR THE SETTLEMENT OF DISPUTES BETWEEN GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT AND ANOTHER AND ONE GOVERNMENT\nDEPARTMENT AND PUBLIC ENTERPRISE AND ONE PUBLIC ENTERPRISE AND ANOTHER THE ARBITRATION SHALL BE AS\nFOLLOWS: \"In the event of any dispute or difference between the parties hereto, such dispute or difference shall be\nresolved amicably by mutual consultation or through the good offices of empowered agencies of the Government.  If such\nresolution is not possible, then, the unresolved dispute or difference shall be referred to arbitration of an arbitrator to be\nnominated by Secretary, Department of Legal Affairs (\"Law Secretary\") in terms of the Office Memorandum No.55/3/1/75-\nCF, dated the 19th December 1975 issued by the Cabinet Secretariat (Department of Cabinet Affairs), as modified from\ntime to time. The Arbitration Act 1940 (10 of 1940) shall not be applicable to the arbitration under this clause. The award\nof the Arbitrator shall be binding upon parties to the dispute. Provided, however, any party aggrieved by such award may\nmake a further reference for setting aside or revision of the award to Law Secretary whose decision shall bind the parties\nfinally and conclusively.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0224",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 224,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 188821,
    "char_end": 189218,
    "char_count": 397,
    "text": "109\n JURISDICTION:\n109.1\nThe CONTRACT shall be governed by and constructed according to the laws in force in INDIA. The CONTRACTOR hereby\nsubmits to the jurisdiction of the Courts situated at Guwahati for the purposes of disputes, actions and proceedings arising\nout of the CONTRACT, the courts at Guwahati only will have the jurisdiction to hear and decide such disputed, actions and\nproceedings.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0225",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 225,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 189220,
    "char_end": 190939,
    "char_count": 1719,
    "text": "SECTION-X SAFETY CODES\n110\n GENERAL:\n110.1\nCONTRACTOR shall adhere to safe construction practice and guard against hazardous, and unsafe working conditions and\nshall comply with EMPLOYER's safety rules as set forth herein. Prior to start of construction, CONTRACTOR will be\nfurnished copies of EMPLOYER's \"Safety Code\" for information and guidance, if it has been prepared.\n111\n SAFETY REGULATIONS:\n111.1\nIn respect of all labour, directly employed in the WORK for the performance of CONTRACTOR's part of this agreement, the\nCONTRACTOR shall at his own expense arrange for all the safety provisions as per safety codes of C.P.W.D., Indian\nStandards Institution. The Electricity Act, The Mines Act and such other acts as applicable.\n111.2\nThe CONTRACTOR shall observe and abide by all fire and safety regulations of the EMPLOYER. Before starting construction\nwork CONTRACTOR shall consult with EMPLOYER's safety Engineers or ENGINEER- IN-CHARGE and must make good to the\nsatisfaction of the EMPLOYER any loss or damage due to fire to any portion of the work done or to be done under this\nagreement or to any of the EMPLOYER's existing property.\n112\n FIRST AID AND INDUSTRIAL INJURIES:\n112.1\nCONTRACTOR shall maintain first aid facilities for its employees and those of its SUB-CONTRACTOR.\n112.2\nCONTRACTOR shall make outside arrangements for ambulance service and for the treatment of industrial injuries. Names\nof those providing these services shall be furnished to EMPLOYER prior to start of construction and their telephone\nnumbers shall be prominently posted in CONTRACTOR's field office.\n112.3\nAll critical industrial injuries shall be reported promptly to EMPLOYER, and a copy of CONTRACTOR's report covering each",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0226",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 226,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 190940,
    "char_end": 191030,
    "char_count": 90,
    "text": "personal injury requiring the attention of a physician shall be furnished to the EMPLOYER.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0227",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 227,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 191032,
    "char_end": 191051,
    "char_count": 19,
    "text": "113\n GENERAL RULES:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0228",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 228,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 191053,
    "char_end": 191055,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "38",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0229",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 229,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 191057,
    "char_end": 192768,
    "char_count": 1711,
    "text": "113.1\nSmoking within the battery area, tank farm or dock limits is strictly prohibited. Violators of the no smoking rules shall be\ndischarged immediately.\n114\n CONTRACTOR'S BARRICADES:\n114.1\nCONTRACTOR shall erect and maintain barricades required in connection with his operation to guard or protect:-\na)\nExcavations\nb)\nHoisting Areas.\nc)\nAreas adjudged hazardous by CONTRACTOR's or EMPLOYER's inspectors.\nd)\nEMPLOYER's existing property subject to damage by CONTRACTOR's Operations.\ne)\nRail Road unloading spots.\n114.2\nCONTRACTOR's employees and those of his SUB- CONTRACTOR's shall become acquainted with EMPLOYER's barricading\npractice and shall respect the provisions thereof.\n114.3\nBarricades and hazardous areas adjacent to, but not located in normal routes of travel shall be marked by red flasher\nlanterns at nights.\n115\n SCAFFOLDING:\n115.1\nSuitable scaffolding should be provided for workmen for all works that cannot safely be done from the ground or from\nsolid construction except such short period work as can be done safely from ladders. When a ladder is used an extra\nMazdoor shall be engaged for holding the ladder and if the ladder is used for carrying material as well, suitable footholds\nand handholds shall be provided on the ladder and the ladder shall be given an inclination not steeper than 1 in 4 (1\nhorizontal and 4 vertical).\n115.2\nScaffolding or staging more than 4 metres above the ground or floor, swing suspended from an overhead support or\nerected with stationary support shall have a guard rail properly attached, bolted, braced and otherwise retarded at least\none metre high above the floor or platform of such scaffolding or staging and extending along the entire length of the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0230",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 230,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 192769,
    "char_end": 194530,
    "char_count": 1761,
    "text": "outside and ends thereof with only such openings as may be necessary for the delivery of materials. Such scaffolding or\nstaging shall be so fastened as to prevent it from swaying from the building or structure.\n115.3\nWorking platform, gangway and stairway should be so constructed that they should not sag unduly or unequally and if the\nheight of platform of the gangway or the stairway is more than 4 metres above the ground level or floor level, they should\nbe closely boarded, should have adequate width and should be suitably fastened as in ii) above.\n115.4\nEvery opening in the floor of a building or in a working platform shall be provided with suitable means to prevent the fall\nof persons or materials by providing suitable fencing of railing whose minimum heights shall be 1 metre.\n115.5\nSafe-means of access shall be provided to all working platforms and other working places, every ladder shall be securely\nfixed. No portable single ladder shall be over 9 metres in length while the width between side rails in rung ladder shall in\nno case be less than 30 cms for ladder upto and including 3 metres in length. For longer ladder this width should be\nincreased 5mm for each additional foot of length. Uniform steps spacing shall not exceed 30 cms. Adequate precautions\nshall be taken to prevent danger from electrical equipment. No materials on any of the sites or work shall be so stacked or\nplaced to cause danger or inconvenience to any person or public. The CONTRACTOR shall also provide all necessary fencing\nand lights to protect the workers and staff from accidents, and shall be bound to bear the expenses of defense of every\nsuit, action or other proceeding of law that may be brought by any person for injury sustained owing to neglect of the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0231",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 231,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 194531,
    "char_end": 196279,
    "char_count": 1748,
    "text": "above precautions and pay any damages and costs which may be awarded in any such suit or action or proceeding to any\nsuch person or which may with the consent of the CONTRACTOR be paid to compromise any claim by any such person.\n116\n EXCAVATION AND TRENCHING:\n116.1\nAll trenches 1.2 metres or more in depth, shall at all times be supplied with at least one ladder for each 50 metres length\nor fraction thereof. Ladder shall be extended from bottom of the trenches to atleast 1 metre above the surface of the\nground. The sides of the trenches which are 1.5M in depth shall be stepped back to give suitable slope or securely held by\ntimber bracing, so as to avoid the danger of sides to collapse. The excavated materials shall not be placed within 1.5\nmetres of the edge of the trench or half of the trench width whichever is more. Cutting shall be done from top to bottom.\nUnder no circumstances undermining or under-cutting shall be done.\n117\n DEMOLITION/GENERAL SAFETY:\n117.1\nBefore any demolition work is commenced and also during the progress of the demolition work\na)\nAll roads and open areas adjacent to the work site shall either be closed or suitably protected.\nb)\nNo electric cable or apparatus which is liable to be a source of danger shall remain electrically charged.\nc)\nAll practical steps shall be taken to prevent danger to persons employed from risk of fire or explosion or flooding. No\nfloor, roof or other part of the building shall be so overloaded with debris or materials as to render it unsafe.\n117.2\nAll necessary personal safety equipment as considered adequate by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE, should be kept available\nfor the use of the persons employed on the SITE and maintained in condition suitable for immediate use, and the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0232",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 232,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 196280,
    "char_end": 196912,
    "char_count": 632,
    "text": "CONTRACTOR shall take adequate steps to ensure proper use of equipment by those concerned.\na)\nWorkers employed on mixing asphaltic materials, cement and lime mortars shall be provided with protective footwear\nand protective gloves.\nb)\nThose engaged in white washing and mixing or stacking or cement bags or any material which are injurious to the eyes be\nprovided with protective goggles.\nc)\nThose engaged in welding and cutting works shall be provided with protective face & eye shield, hand gloves, etc.\nd)\nStone breakers shall be provided with protective goggles and protective clothing and seated at sufficiently safe intervals.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0233",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 233,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 196914,
    "char_end": 196916,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "39",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0234",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 234,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 196918,
    "char_end": 198690,
    "char_count": 1772,
    "text": "e)\nWhen workers are employed in sewers and manholes, which are in use, the CONTRACTOR shall ensure that the manhole\ncovers are opened and are ventilated atleast for an hour before the workers are allowed to get into the manholes, and\nthe manholes so opened shall be cordoned off with suitable railing and provided with warning signals or\nf)\nboard to prevent accident to the public.\ng)\nThe CONTRACTOR shall not employ men below the age of 18 years and women on the work of painting with products\ncontaining lead in any form. Wherever men above the age of 18 years are employed on the work of lead painting, the\nfollowing precautions should be taken.\n1)\nNo paint containing lead or lead product shall be used except in the form of paste or readymade paint.\n2)\nSuitable face masks should be supplied for use by the workers when paint is applied in the form of spray or a\nsurface having lead paint dry rubbed and scrapped.\n3)\nOveralls shall be supplied by the CONTRACTOR to the workmen and adequate facilities shall be provided to\nenable the working painters to wash them during and on cessation of work.\n117.3\nWhen the work is done near any place where there is risk of drowning, all necessary safety equipment should be provided\nand kept ready for use and all necessary steps taken for prompt rescue of any person in danger and adequate provision\nshould be made for prompt first aid treatment of all injuries likely to be sustained during the course of the work.\n117.4\nUse of hoisting machines and tackles including their attachments, anchorage and supports shall conform to the following\nstandards or conditions:\na.\nThese shall be of good mechanical construction, sound materials and adequate strength and free from patent\ndefect and shall be kept in good working order.\nb.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0235",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 235,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 198691,
    "char_end": 200428,
    "char_count": 1737,
    "text": "Every rope used in hoisting or lowering materials or as means of suspension shall be of durable quality and\nadequate strength and free from patent defects.\nb)\nEvery crane driver or hoisting appliance operator shall be properly qualified and no person under the age of 21 years\nshould be in charge of any hoisting machine including any scaffolding, winch or give signals to the operator.\nc)\nIn case of every hoisting machine and of every chain ring hook, shackle, swivel, and pulley block used in hoisting or\nlowering or as means of suspension, the safe working load shall be ascertained by adequate means. Every hoisting\nmachine and all gears referred to above shall be plainly marked with the safe working load of the conditions under which\nit is applicable and the same shall be clearly indicated. No part of any machine or any gear referred to above in this\nparagraph shall be loaded beyond safe working load except for the purpose of testing.\nd)\nIn case of departmental machine, the safe working load shall be notified by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE. As regards\nCONTRACTOR's machines, the CONTRACTOR shall notify the safe working load of the machine to the ENGINEER-IN-\nCHARGE whenever he brings any machinery to SITE of WORK and get it verified by the Engineer concerned.\ne)\nMotors, gears, transmission lines, electric wiring and other dangerous parts of hoisting appliances should be provided\nwith efficient safeguards. Hoisting appliances should be provided with such means as to reduce to minimum the\naccidental descent of the load, adequate precautions should be taken to reduce the minimum risk of any part or parts of\na suspended load becoming accidentally displaced. When workers are employed on electrical installations which are",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0236",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 236,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 200429,
    "char_end": 202162,
    "char_count": 1733,
    "text": "already energised, insulating mats, wearing apparel, such as gloves, sleeves, and boots as may be necessary should be\nprovided. The workers shall not wear any rings, watches and carry keys or other materials which are good conductors of\nelectricity.\n117.5\nAll scaffolds, ladders and other safety devices mentioned or described herein shall be maintained in safe conditions and no\nscaffolds, ladder or equipment shall be altered or removed while it is in use. Adequate washing facilities should be\nprovided at or near places of work.\n117.6\nThese safety provisions should be brought to the notice of all concerned by displaying on a notice board at a prominent\nplace at the work-spot. The person responsible for compliance of the safety code shall be named therein by the\nCONTRACTOR.\n117.7\nTo ensure effective enforcement of the rules and regulations relating to safety precautions, the arrangements made by the\nCONTRACTOR shall be open to inspection by the Welfare Officer, ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE or safety Engineer of the\nAdministration or their representatives.\n117.8\nNotwithstanding the above clauses there is nothing in these to exempt the CONTRACTOR for the operations of any other\nAct or rules in force in the Republic of India. The work throughout including any temporary works shall be carried out in\nsuch a manner as not to interfere in any way whatsoever with the traffic on any roads or footpath at the site or in the\nvicinity thereto or any existing works whether the property of the Administration or of a third party. In addition to the\nabove, the CONTRACTOR shall abide by the safety code provision as per C.P.W.D. Safety code and Indian Standard Safety\nCode from time to time.\n118\n CARE IN HANDLING INFLAMMABLE GAS:\n118.1",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0237",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 237,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 202163,
    "char_end": 202401,
    "char_count": 238,
    "text": "The CONTRACTOR has to ensure all precautionary measures and exercise utmost care in handling the inflammable gas\ncylinder/inflammable liquids/paints etc. as required under the law and/or as advised by the fire Authorities of the\nEMPLOYER.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0238",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 238,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 202403,
    "char_end": 202405,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "40",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0239",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 239,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 202407,
    "char_end": 204198,
    "char_count": 1791,
    "text": "119\n TEMPORARY COMBUSTIBLE STRUCTURES:\n119.1\nTemporary combustible structures will not be built near or around work site.\n120\n PRECAUTIONS AGAINST FIRE:\n120.1\nThe CONTRACTOR will have to provide Fire Extinguishers, Fire Buckets and drums at worksite as recommended by\nENGINEER-IN-CHARGE. They will have to ensure all precautionary measures and exercise utmost care in handling the\ninflammable gas cylinders/ inflammable liquid/ paints etc. as advised by ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE. Temporary combustible\nstructures will not be built near or around the work-site.\n121\n EXPLOSIVES:\n121.1\nExplosives shall not be stored or used on the WORK or on the SITE by the CONTRACTOR without the permission of the\nENGINEER-IN-CHARGE in writing and then only in the manner and to the extent to which such permission is given. When\nexplosives are required for the WORK they will be stored in a special magazine to be provided at the cost of the\nCONTRACTOR in accordance with the Explosives Rules. The CONTRACTOR shall obtain the necessary license for the storage\nand the use of explosives and all operations in which or for which explosives are employed shall be at sole risk and\nresponsibility of the CONTRACTOR and the CONTRACTOR shall indemnify the EMPLOYER against any loss or damage\nresulting directly or indirectly therefrom.\n122\n MINES ACT:\n122.1\nSAFETY CODE: The CONTRACTOR shall at his own expense arrange for the safety provisions as required by the ENGINEER-\nIN-CHARGE in respect of all labour directly employed for performance of the WORKS and shall provide all facilities in\nconnection therewith. In case the CONTRACTOR fails to make arrangements and provides necessary facilities as aforesaid,\nthe ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE shall be entitled to do so and recover the costs thereof from the CONTRACTOR.\n122.2",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0240",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 240,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 204199,
    "char_end": 205197,
    "char_count": 998,
    "text": "Failure to comply with Safety Code or the provisions relating to report on accidents and to grant of maternity benefits to\nfemale workers shall make the CONTRACTOR liable to pay Company Liquidated Damages an amount not exceeding Rs.50/-\nfor each default or materially incorrect statement. The decision of the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE in such matters based on\nreports from the Inspecting Officer or from representatives of ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall be final and binding and\ndeductions for recovery of such Liquidated Damages may be made from any amount payable to the CONTRACTOR from all\nthe provisions of the Mines Act, 1952 or any statutory modifications or re-enactment thereof the time being in force and\nany Rules and Regulations made there under in respect of all the persons employed by him under this CONTRACT and shall\nindemnify the EMPLOYER from and against any claim under the Mines Act or the rules and regulations framed there under\nby or on behalf of any persons employed by him or otherwise.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0241",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 241,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 205199,
    "char_end": 206951,
    "char_count": 1752,
    "text": "123\n PRESERVATION OF PLACE:\n123.1\nThe CONTRACTOR shall take requisite precautions and use his best endeavors to prevent any riotous or unlawful\nbehaviour by or amongst his worker and others employed or the works and for the preservation of peace and protection\nof the inhabitants and security of property in the neighborhood of the WORK. In the event of the EMPLOYER requiring the\nmaintenance of a Special Police Force at or in the vicinity of the site during the tenure of works, the expenses thereof shall\nbe borne by the CONTRACTOR and if paid by the EMPLOYER shall be recoverable from the CONTRACTOR.\n124\n OUTBREAK OF INFECTIOUS DISEASES:\n124.1\nThe CONTRACTOR shall remove from his camp such labour and their facilities who refuse protective inoculation and\nvaccination when called upon to do so by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE's representative. Should Cholera, Plague or other\ninfectious diseases break out the CONTRACTOR shall burn the huts, beddings, clothes and other belongings or used by the\ninfected parties and promptly erect new huts on healthy sites as required by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE failing which\nwithin the time specified in the Engineer's requisition, the work may be done by the EMPLOYER and the cost thereof\nrecovered from the CONTRACTOR.\n125\n USE OF INTOXICANTS:\n125.1\nThe unauthorised sale of spirits or other intoxicants, beverages upon the work in any of the buildings, encampments or\ntenements owned, occupied by or within the control of the CONTRACTOR or any of his employee is forbidden and the\nCONTRACTOR shall exercise his influence and authority to the utmost extent to secure strict compliance with this\ncondition. In addition to the above, the CONTRACTOR shall abide by the safety code provision as per C.P.W.D. safety code",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0242",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 242,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 206952,
    "char_end": 207002,
    "char_count": 50,
    "text": "and Indian Standard Code framed from time to time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
