    "char_end": 218765,
    "char_count": 1744,
    "text": "3. In consideration of the due provision, execution and completion of the said WORK the CONTRACTOR does hereby agree to pay\nsuch sums as may be due to the EMPLOYER for the services rendered by the EMPLOYER to the CONTRACTOR, such as power\nsupply, water supply and others as set for in the said CONTRACT and such other sums as may become payable to the EMPLOYER\ntowards the controlled items of consumable materials or towards loss, damage to the EMPLOYER'S equipment, materials\nconstruction plant and machinery, such payments to be made at such time and in such manner as is provided in the CONTRACT. It\nis specifically and distinctly understood and agreed between the EMPLOYER and the CONTRACTOR that the CONTRACTOR shall\nhave no right, title or interest in the SITE made available by the EMPLOYER for execution of the works or in the building, structures\nor work executed on the said SITE by the CONTRACTOR or in the goods, articles, materials etc., brought on the said SITE (unless the\nsame specifically belongs to the CONTRACTOR) and the CONTRACTOR shall not have or deemed to have any lien whatsoever\ncharge for unpaid bills will not be entitled to assume or retain possession or control of the SITE or structures and the EMPLOYER\nshall have an absolute and unfettered right to take full possession of SITE and to remove the CONTRACTOR, their servants, agents\nand materials belonging to the CONTRACTOR and lying on the SITE. The CONTRACTOR shall be allowed to enter upon the SITE for\nexecution of the WORK only as a licensee simpliciter and shall not have any claim, right, title or interest in the SITE or the\nstructures erected thereon and the EMPLOYER shall be entitled to terminate such license at any time without assigning any reason.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC067-0263",
    "doc_id": "DOC-067",
    "paragraph_index": 263,
    "page_start": 45,
    "page_end": 45,
    "char_start": 218766,
    "char_end": 219397,
    "char_count": 631,
    "text": "The materials including sand, gravel, stone, loose, earth, rock etc., dug up or excavated from the said SITE shall, unless otherwise\nexpressly agreed under this CONTRACT, exclusively belong to the EMPLOYER and the CONTRACTOR shall have no right to claim\nover the same and such excavation and materials should be disposed off on account of the EMPLOYER according to the instruction\nin writing issued from time to time by the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE In Witness whereof the parties have executed these presents in\nthe day and the year first above written. Signed and Delivered for and on Signed and Delivered for and on behalf of EMPLOYER.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
