    "char_end": 1591,
    "char_count": 1,
    "text": ":",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0009",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 9,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 1593,
    "char_end": 2057,
    "char_count": 464,
    "text": "SCOPE OF WORK\nSCHEDULE – B\n:\nPROGRAMME OF WORK\nSCHEDULE – C\n:\nTECHNICAL DOCUMENTATION\nSCHEDULE – D\n:\nSITE CONDITIONS\nSCHEDULE – E\n:\nSUPPLIES BY OWNER / CONSULTANT\nSCHEDULE – F\n:\nSCHEDULE OF RATES FOR EXTRA ITEMS\nSCHEDULE – G\n:\nPAYMENT SCHEDULE\nSCHEDULE – H\n:\nSITE  FACILITIES\nSCHEDULE – L\n;\nPROFORMA BANK GUARANTEE FOR\nPERFORMANCE BOND\nSCHEDULE – N\n;\nPROFORMA FOR RELEASE CERTIFICATE\nSCHEDULE – P\n:\nSAFETY PRACTICES\nSCHEDULE – Q\n:\nSPECIAL  CONDITIONS  OF  CONTRACT",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0010",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 10,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 2059,
    "char_end": 2142,
    "char_count": 83,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 5 of 46\n\nARTICLE-1 DEFINITIONS",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0011",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 11,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 2144,
    "char_end": 2317,
    "char_count": 173,
    "text": "The following expressions shall have the meanings specified against the\nrespective item, wherever used in this document, unless repugnant to the context\nand meaning thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0012",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 12,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 2319,
    "char_end": 2565,
    "char_count": 246,
    "text": "1.1\nCONTRACT means this Agreement including the Articles, Schedules,\nAnnexes and Appendices as listed in the List of Titles forming part hereof\nand any written amendments thereto executed by authorized signatories on\nbehalf of the parties hereto.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0013",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 13,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 2567,
    "char_end": 2678,
    "char_count": 111,
    "text": "1.2\n'DATE OF CONTRACT' means the Date on which CONTRACT is signed by\neither party after signature by the other.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0014",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 14,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 2680,
    "char_end": 2794,
    "char_count": 114,
    "text": "1.3\n'WORK' means all duties, responsibilities and obligations to be discharged\nby CONTRACTOR pursuant to CONTRACT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0015",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 15,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 2796,
    "char_end": 2998,
    "char_count": 202,
    "text": "1.4\n'EQUIPMENT' means any item of plant and machinery, equipment\naccessory or thing to be supplied by OWNER and erected / installed by\nCONTRACTOR\nor\nto\nbe\nsupplied\nand\nerected\n/\ninstalled\nby\nCONTRACTOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0016",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 16,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 3000,
    "char_end": 3097,
    "char_count": 97,
    "text": "1.5\n'PROJECT' means the facility being set up by OWNER as per details and\nlocation in SCHEDULE-D.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0017",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 17,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 3099,
    "char_end": 3220,
    "char_count": 121,
    "text": "1.6\n'SITE' means the land in possession of OWNER where PROJECT is being\nset up and WORK is to be performed by CONTRACTOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0018",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 18,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 3222,
    "char_end": 3430,
    "char_count": 208,
    "text": "1.7\n'INITIAL CONTRACT PRICE' means the value of WORK contracted initially\nas per SCHEDULE-F and excluding value of EQUIPMENT, services and\nany material provided by OWNER/CONSULTANT free of cost to\nCONTRACTOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0019",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 19,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 3432,
    "char_end": 3672,
    "char_count": 240,
    "text": "1.8\n'CONTRACT PRICE' means the aggregate sum payable by OWNER\n/ CONSULTANT to CONTRACTOR for work performed as per CONTRACT\nbut excluding value of EQUIPMENT, services and any material provided by\nOWNER/CONSULTANT free of cost to CONTRACTOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0020",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 20,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 3674,
    "char_end": 3770,
    "char_count": 96,
    "text": "1.9\n'OWNER/CONSULTANT'S REPRESENTATIVE' shall have same meaning\nas defined in Article-6.1hereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0021",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 21,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 3772,
    "char_end": 3856,
    "char_count": 84,
    "text": "1.10 'ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE' shall have same meaning as defined in Article-\n6.2 hereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0022",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 22,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 3858,
    "char_end": 3951,
    "char_count": 93,
    "text": "1.11 'CONTRACTOR'S REPRESENTATIVE' shall have the same meaning as\ndefined in Article-7hereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0023",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 23,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 6,
    "char_start": 3953,
    "char_end": 4139,
    "char_count": 186,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 6 of 46\n\n1.12 'ZERO DATE' means the date on which CONTRACTOR'S responsibilities\nfor time- schedule commence as defined inArticle-4.1.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0024",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 24,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 6,
    "char_start": 4141,
    "char_end": 4696,
    "char_count": 555,
    "text": "ARTICLE-2 PERFORMANCEBOND\n\n2.1\nWithin fifteen (15) days of the ZERO DATE, CONTRACTOR shall provide\nOWNER with a Bank Guarantee as per proforma given in SCHEDULE-L\nhereof, from a Nationalized Bank in India for a sum calculated at ten (10)\npercent of the initial Contract Price, towards security for due and faithful\nperformance of CONTRACTOR. The Bank Guarantee shall be kept valid\nuntil all obligations of CONTRACTOR including the warranties vide Article-\n30\nare\nfulfilled\nand\na\ndischarge\ncertificate\nis\nissued\nby\nOWNER/CONSULTANT (also refer Schedule–B).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0025",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 25,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 6,
    "char_start": 4698,
    "char_end": 5166,
    "char_count": 468,
    "text": "2.2\nHowever, in case the amount of Performance Bond is less than Rs.10, 000-\nCONTRACTOR shall deposit with OWNER either in cash or as Demand\nDraft drawn in favour of OWNER and payable at State Bank of India,\nUdyogamandal, Kerala State, for a sum calculated at ten (10) percent of the\ninitial Contract Price in lieu of the Bank Guarantee referred to in Article-2.1\nwithin\n15\ndays\nof\nZERO\nDATE.\nNo\ninterest\nis\npayable\nby\nOWNER/CONSULTANT to CONTRACTOR for such deposits.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0026",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 26,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 6,
    "char_start": 5168,
    "char_end": 5461,
    "char_count": 293,
    "text": "ARTICLE-3 SCOPE OFSERVICES\n\n3.1.\nCONTRACTOR shall carry out WORK as described in detail in the\nSCHEDULE-A, Schedule of Work, all in conformity with the drawings,\nspecifications,\ncodes,\nstandards\nand\ninstructions\nprovided\nby\nOWNER/CONSULTANT from time to time or specified herein as applicable.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0027",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 27,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 6,
    "char_start": 5463,
    "char_end": 5758,
    "char_count": 295,
    "text": "3.2.\nCONTRACTOR'S responsibility includes preparation of any detailed\nworking drawings, cutting diagrams, fabrication drawings and / or such other\ntechnical documentation as may be necessary to elaborate the information\nprovided by OWNER/CONSULTANT in the manner described in Article-\n5.4hereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0028",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 28,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 6,
    "char_start": 5760,
    "char_end": 6019,
    "char_count": 259,
    "text": "3.3.\nCONTRACTOR shall also purchase and provide for use in carrying out\nWORK, pre-fabricated or otherwise, such items of materials and supplies as\nare required for carrying out WORK in addition to EQUIPMENT and\nmaterials directly provided by OWNER/CONSULTANT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0029",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 29,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 6,
    "char_start": 6021,
    "char_end": 6285,
    "char_count": 264,
    "text": "3.4.\nThe quantities indicated in SCHEDULE-A and / or Schedule-F are only\napproximate and CONTRACTOR shall carry out all items of WORK in\nrequired quantities as per drawings and specifications provided by\nOWNER/CONSULTANT, subject to provisions of Article-15hereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0030",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 30,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 6287,
    "char_end": 6424,
    "char_count": 137,
    "text": "3.5.\nWork shall be executed with all due diligence, in the manner specified\n\nGENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 7 of 46",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0031",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 31,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 6426,
    "char_end": 6687,
    "char_count": 261,
    "text": "herein, to the satisfaction of OWNER/CONSULTANT'S REPRESENTATIVE within\nthe time schedule agreed to herein for the respective item. CONTRACTOR shall\npost at SITE appropriate number of qualified and competent supervisory staff for\nday-to day supervision of work.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0032",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 32,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 6689,
    "char_end": 7001,
    "char_count": 312,
    "text": "3.6.\nWorkmen engaged by CONTRACTOR shall be qualified, experienced and\ncompetent for the respective item of works and will be subject to craft-test\nprescribed by ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE. Where necessary, supervisors and\nworkmen engaged by CONTRACTOR shall hold licenses / permits for\ncarrying out the respective work.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0033",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 33,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 7003,
    "char_end": 7264,
    "char_count": 261,
    "text": "3.7.\nCONTRACTOR further undertakes to co-operate with OWNER /\nCONSULTANT as well as other Contractors appointed by OWNER /\nCONSULTANT and operating at SITE and agrees to freely exchange\ntechnical information as may be reasonably asked for by OWNER /\nCONSULTANT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0034",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 34,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 7266,
    "char_end": 8073,
    "char_count": 807,
    "text": "ARTICLE-4 TIME-SCHEDULE\n\n4.1.\nCONTRACTOR shall carry out work in a phased manner and hand over the\nrespective items to OWNER/CONSULTANT after carrying out such tests as\nare prescribed herein within the programme given in SCHEDULE-B,\nPROGRAMME OF WORK. The responsibilities of CONTRACTOR in\nrespect of programme vide SCHEDULE-B will be effective from the date on\nwhich Letter of Intent has been issued by OWNER/CONSULTANT and\nindicated as 'ZERO DATE' in the said SCHEDULE–B, provided that\nOWNER / CONSULTANT gives CONTRACTOR, any mobilisation advance\nif agreed to herein within 15 days of receipt from CONTRACTOR the related\ninvoice along with the Performance Bond vide Article-2 hereof and the Bank\nGuarantee towards Security for such advance payment vide Article-14\nhereof, both in the prescribed proforma.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0035",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 35,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 8075,
    "char_end": 8788,
    "char_count": 713,
    "text": "4.2.\nTime is the essence of the CONTRACT and CONTRACTOR understands\nthe necessity of achieving the stage-wise targets in the specified sequence\nas set-forth in SCHEDULE-B and hereby undertakes to mobilise the\nrequired resources and exercise due diligence to adhere to them. During\nthe implementation of CONTRACT, OWNER/CONSULTANT may issue to\nCONTRACTOR, where applicable, instructions/ requirements in respect of\npriorities and sequence in the overall interest of the PROJECT and\nCONTRACTOR shall fully co-operate with OWNER/CONSULTANT in\nfollowing these instructions and submit to OWNER/CONSULTANT detailed\nworking programmes for achievement of these, which shall be reviewed and\napproved by ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0036",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 36,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 8790,
    "char_end": 9145,
    "char_count": 355,
    "text": "4.3.\nWithin 30 days of ZERO DATE, CONTRACTOR shall give to OWNER /\nCONSULTANT in triplicate a detailed programme for assembling materials,\nsubmission of fabrication drawing/cutting diagrams, etc. mobilisation of\nConstruction Equipment, Tools and Tackles, mobilisation of skilled and\nunskilledlabourinvariouscategories/disciplinesatvariousphasesofwork,pre-",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0037",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 37,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 9147,
    "char_end": 9643,
    "char_count": 496,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 8 of 46\n\nfabrication in shop, pre-fabrication at SITE, assignment of supervisory personnel\nand such other activities, matching with the Programme of work vide SCHEDULE-\nB. In the event OWNER/CONSULTANT is not satisfied that the programme\nproposed by CONTRACTOR is adequate to meet targets set forth in SCHEDULE-\nB, CONTRACTOR shall modify the programme suitably to the satisfaction of\nOWNER/CONSULTANT and carry out the activities accordingly.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0038",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 38,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 9645,
    "char_end": 9971,
    "char_count": 326,
    "text": "4.4\nCONTRACTOR recognizes possibility of inclement weather conditions at\nSITE and agrees to take all reasonable precautions and measures\nnecessary to permit execution of WORK as per agreed programme despite\nsuch adverse conditions and CONTRACTOR shall not be entitled for any\nadditional  payment what so ever, on this account.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0039",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 39,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 9973,
    "char_end": 10124,
    "char_count": 151,
    "text": "4.5\nCONTRACTOR shall not be entitled for extension of time schedule for any\nreason whatsoever except as provided in Articles-15.7,32.2 and 40.3\nhereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0040",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 40,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 10126,
    "char_end": 10672,
    "char_count": 546,
    "text": "ARTICLE-5 TECHNICAL DOCUMENTS\n\n5.1.  The Technical Documents enclosed as part of SCHEDULE-C  hereof  are,\nunless otherwise specified, preliminary and typical and are intended only to\ngenerally represent the nature of WORK to be executed. OWNER /\nCONSULTANT will be issuing to CONTRACTOR, from time to time, final\nand more detailed drawings and documents as are listed in SCHEDULE-C\nas also new drawings whenever necessary to depict the scope of work.\nCONTRACTOR shall execute WORK only based on documents bearing the\nstamp \"GOOD FORCONSTRUCTION\".",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0041",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 41,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 10674,
    "char_end": 10960,
    "char_count": 286,
    "text": "5.2\nDocuments once issued by OWNER/CONSULTANT for construction may\nsubsequently be revised without prejudice to Article-15 hereof; and as soon\nas the revised issues are received CONTRACTOR shall withdraw the\nprevious issue from the field and return to OWNER/CONSULTANT for\ncancellation.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0042",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 42,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 10962,
    "char_end": 11940,
    "char_count": 978,
    "text": "5.3\nCONTRACTOR shall carryout the WORK in strict conformity with the\ndrawings, specifications and such other documents and instructions\nprovided by OWNER/CONSULTANT and standards and codes of practice\nprescribed by OWNER/CONSULTANT for the respective items of WORK.\nWhere OWNER/CONSULTANT'S own standards are referred to, the same\nwill be provided by OWNER/CONSULTANT; but where other published\nstandards/codes of practice are prescribed, CONTRACTOR shall make own\narrangements to be equipped with copies of such documents for use in\nexecution of WORK and failure to do so shall be deemed negligence in\nperformance of CONTRACT. In the event of any conflict or contradiction\nbetween\nany\ntwo\nor\nmore\nof\nthe\ndocuments\nprovided\nby\nOWNER/CONSULTANT or between such documents and the prescribed\ncodes/standards, CONTRACTOR shall bring the same to the attention of\nENGINEER-IN CHARGE as soon as it is noticed by CONTRACTOR; and\nthe decision of the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall be followed.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0043",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 43,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 11942,
    "char_end": 12940,
    "char_count": 998,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 9 of 46\n\n5.4\nWherever necessary, CONTRACTOR shall prepare detailed working drawings,\ncutting diagrams, fabrication drawings and/ or such other technical documents all\nin conformity with Technical Information provided by OWNER/CONSULTANT\nand as may be necessary for execution of WORK and submit same to\nOWNER/CONSULTANT in required number of copies well in advance in\ncommencement of related WORK. OWNER/CONSULTANT shall return one copy\nto CONTRACTOR with comments, if any, within Ten\n(10) working days of receipt from CONTRACTOR and CONTRACTOR shall\nexecute\nWORK\nonly\nbased\non\ndocuments\nreviewed/\napproved\nby\nOWNER/CONSULTANT. However, CONTRACTOR is solely responsible to\nensure that WORK is executed as per designs; drawings, specifications and\nother technical information provided by OWNER/CONSULTANT and review\n/comments\nby\nOWNER/CONSULTANT\nin\nthe\naforesaid\nmanner\nof\nCONTRACTOR'S documents shall not absolve CONTRACTOR of his\nresponsibility.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0044",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 44,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 12942,
    "char_end": 13277,
    "char_count": 335,
    "text": "5.5\nInstallation of special items of EQUIPMENT shall be taken up only after thorough\nstudy of Manufacturer's instructions for handling, assembly and installation,\ndetailed circuit diagram, etc. as may be applicable as per SCHEDULE-A and\nCONTRACTOR shall ensure availability of such information for EQUIPMENT\nsupplied by the CONTRACTOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0045",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 45,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 13279,
    "char_end": 13748,
    "char_count": 469,
    "text": "ARTICLE-6 OWNER/CONSULTANT’SREPRESENTATIVE\n\n6.1\nAll obligations of OWNER under CONTRACT shall, unless otherwise specifically\nmentioned, be carried out through FACT Engineering & Design Organization\n(FEDO) the Design & Engineering CONSULTANT of OWNER. The Resident\nConstruction\nManager\nappointed\nby\nFEDO\nat\nSITE\nshall\nbe\nOWNER/CONSULTANT'S\nREPRESENTATIVE,\nand\nshall\nrepresent\nOWNER/CONSULTANT for all matters concerning this CONTRACT except as\notherwise provided herein.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0046",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 46,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 13750,
    "char_end": 14339,
    "char_count": 589,
    "text": "6.2\nAll\ninstructions\nand\norders\nto\nCONTRACTOR\nshall\nbe\nissued\nby\nOWNER/CONSULTANT'S\nREPRESENTATIVE\nand/or\nan\nENGINEER-IN-\nCHARGE nominated by him and communicated in writing to CONTRACTOR'S\nREPRESENTATIVE, if available at SITE or to CONTRACTOR at the address\ngiven in Article-47. WORK shall be executed under direction and to the\nsatisfaction of the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE, all in accordance with the\nprovisions. CONTRACTOR shall proceed with WORK in accordance with the\ndecisions, orders and/or instructions issued by OWNER/CONSULTANT'S\nREPRESENTATIVE or the ENGINEER-IN CHARGE provided that;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0047",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 47,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 14341,
    "char_end": 14635,
    "char_count": 294,
    "text": "i)\nIf the CONTRACTOR shall without undue delay after being given a decision,\norder or instruction otherwise than in writing, require it to be confirmed in\nwriting, such decision, order or instruction shall not be effective until written\nconfirmation thereof has been received by CONTRACTOR, and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0048",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 48,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 14637,
    "char_end": 14775,
    "char_count": 138,
    "text": "ii) If the CONTRACTOR disagrees with or questions a written decision, order\n\nGENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 10 of 46",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0049",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 49,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 14777,
    "char_end": 15227,
    "char_count": 450,
    "text": "or instruction given by ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE he may give notice in writing\nto ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE within seven (7) days of receipt of such decision,\norder or instruction stating reasons there for; but issue of such notice shall\nnot relieve CONTRACTOR of the obligation to proceed with WORK in\naccordance with the decision, order or instruction in respect of which the\nnotice has been issued, without prejudice to other remedial measures\nprovided herein.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0050",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 50,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 15229,
    "char_end": 15404,
    "char_count": 175,
    "text": "6.3\nOWNER/CONSULTANT\nmay\nchange\nthe\nOWNER/CONSULTANT’S\nREPRESENTATIVE and/or ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE at any time, and shall\ninform CONTRACTOR promptly, in writing, of such changes.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0051",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 51,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 15406,
    "char_end": 16042,
    "char_count": 636,
    "text": "ARTICLE-7 CONTRACTOR'S REPRESENTATIVE\n\n7.1\nCONTRACTOR shall be represented at SITE by a technically qualified,\ncompetent and experienced Engineer whose name along with qualification and\nexperience shall be intimated to OWNER/CONSULTANT in writing at least two\n(2) weeks prior to commencement of CONTRACTOR'S activities at SITE for\napproval by OWNER/CONSULTANT. The said representative shall be present at\nSITE during working hours and any orders, instructions or other communications\ndelivered to him by OWNER/CONSULTANT, OWNER / CONSULTANT'S\nREPRESENTATIVE and/or ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall be deemed to have\nbeen received by CONTRACTOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0052",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 52,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 16044,
    "char_end": 16200,
    "char_count": 156,
    "text": "7.2\nAny communication received by OWNER/CONSULTANT from CONTRACTOR'S\nREPRESENTATIVE shall be deemed issued by CONTRACTOR and shall be\nbinding on CONTRACTOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0053",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 53,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 16202,
    "char_end": 16312,
    "char_count": 110,
    "text": "7.3\nCONTRACTOR shall not change the Representative at SITE without prior written\napproval of OWNER/CONSULTANT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0054",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 54,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 16314,
    "char_end": 16945,
    "char_count": 631,
    "text": "ARTICLE-8 CONTRACTOR TO INFORM HIMSELF\n\n8.1\nCertain information pertaining to SITE and considered relevant for the execution\nof WORK are given in SCHEDULE-D, SITE CONDITIONS. Some of the\ninformation given therein are likely to be typical and are intended only to give a\ngeneral idea about SITE. CONTRACTOR is deemed to have visited the SITE\nand the locality and to have gathered clear idea of the locality, weather\nconditions, and access to SITE, space availability, sub-soil conditions, availability\nof materials, availability and terms of service by labour and such other\ninformation that may have influence on execution of WORK.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0055",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 55,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 16947,
    "char_end": 17178,
    "char_count": 231,
    "text": "8.2\nCONTRACTOR is deemed to have carefully examined specifications, schedules\nand drawings and also to have satisfied himself on the nature and extend of\nWORK to be executed before submission of a tender and entering into\nCONTRACT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0056",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 56,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 17180,
    "char_end": 17281,
    "char_count": 101,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 11 of 46\n\nARTICLE-9 SUPPLIES BY OWNER/CONSULTANT",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0057",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 57,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 17283,
    "char_end": 17842,
    "char_count": 559,
    "text": "9.1\nEQUIPMENT\n\n9.1.1\nEQUIPMENT and any materials to be provided by OWNER / CONSULTANT\nwill\nbe\nissued\nby\nOWNER/CONSULTANT\nand\nhanded\nover\nto\nCONTRACTOR at the place of storage. Place of storage will be\nOWNER/CONSULTANT'S store at SITE or the open storage yard at SITE or\nat ground level near the plant premises where EQUIPMENT is to be erected\ndepending upon OWNER/CONSULTANT'S convenience and all moving and\nhandling from the place of storage to the actual place of WORK or the\nbasement on which EQUIPMENT is to be erected, is to be carried out by\nCONTRACTOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0058",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 58,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 17844,
    "char_end": 18011,
    "char_count": 167,
    "text": "9.1.2\nIt is likely that EQUIPMENT stored out-door are in the packing case and\nCONTRACTOR shall have to open the packing cases and inspect the items\nbefore taking over.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0059",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 59,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 18013,
    "char_end": 18434,
    "char_count": 421,
    "text": "9.1.3\nEQUIPMENT items which are shipped in parts will have to be assembled by\nCONTRACTOR prior to installation. Any special tools provided by\nManufacturer for this purpose will be made available to CONTRACTOR\nagainst appropriate receipt; but all other tools and tackles will have to be\nprovided\nby\nCONTRACTOR.\nSpecial\ntools,\nif\nany\nprovided\nby\nOWNER/CONSULTANT shall be returned to OWNER/CONSULTANT\nimmediately after use.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0060",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 60,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 18436,
    "char_end": 19034,
    "char_count": 598,
    "text": "9.1.4\nEQUIPMENT shall be handled by CONTRACTOR very carefully in a\nprofessional and workman like manner. In the event of any damage to\nEQUIPMENT or part thereof due to negligence or use of wrong tool or wrong\npractices in dismantling, handling, assembling and / or installation or careless\nstorage after taking over by CONTRACTOR, CONTRACTOR shall not only\nbe liable to pay the cost of repair/ replacement but also liquidated damages\nvide Article-31 hereof for delay in completion of the related WORK beyond\nthe guaranteed date to the extent such delay as occurred on account of\nrepair/replacement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0061",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 61,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 19036,
    "char_end": 19171,
    "char_count": 135,
    "text": "9.2\nMATERIALS\n\n9.2.1\nMaterials issued by OWNER/CONSULTANT for use in fabrication /\ninstallation by CONTRACTOR are listed in SCHEDULE-E.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0062",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 62,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 19173,
    "char_end": 19693,
    "char_count": 520,
    "text": "9.2.2\nMaterials will be issued to CONTRACTOR from OWNER / CONSULTANT'S\nStore at SITE against appropriate indent in the form provided by\nOWNER/CONSULTANT, countersigned by the ENGINEER- IN-CHARGE\nand transport from store to place of WORK will have to be done by\nCONTRACTOR. CONTRACTOR shall hold such material in safe custody\nand shall maintain proper accounts of its use. Such accounts shall be\navailable for inspection by OWNER/CONSULTANT, if required. No material\nshall\nbe\nremoved\nfrom\nSITE\nwithout\nwritten\napproval\nof",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0063",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 63,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 19695,
    "char_end": 19775,
    "char_count": 80,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 12 of 46\n\nOWNER/CONSULTANT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0064",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 64,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 19777,
    "char_end": 19859,
    "char_count": 82,
    "text": "9.2.3\nMaterials will be issued only during normal working hours of the SITE Store.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0065",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 65,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 19861,
    "char_end": 20692,
    "char_count": 831,
    "text": "9.2.4\nThe maximum cutting allowance and wastages permissible for each item of\nmaterial is shown in SCHEDULE-Q. CONTRACTOR is not entitled to receive\nfrom OWNER/CONSULTANT quantities in excess of those legitimately\nrequired\nincluding\nthe\ncutting\nallowance\nand\nwastages\nand\nOWNER/CONSULTANT may refuse issue of excess quantities required\nconsequent to wastage in any manner by CONTRACTOR. In such cases\nCONTRACTOR may have to make his own arrangements for the additional\nquantities, required at his own cost and carry out WORK within the agreed\ntime. However, OWNER/CONSULTANT may issue such additional\nquantities, if available, and recover from the bills of CONTRACTOR at rate\nspecified for this purpose in SCHEDULE–E in the absence of such rates at\nOWNER/CONSULTANT'S book value or market rate whichever is higher,\nplus 15%thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0066",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 66,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 20694,
    "char_end": 21034,
    "char_count": 340,
    "text": "9.2.5\nIn case of urgency, OWNER/CONSULTANT may at the request of\nCONTRACTOR and at the sole discretion of OWNER/CONSULTANT issue\nto CONTRACTOR any material required for the WORK butnot included in\nSCHEDULE-E and cost of such issues shall be paid by CONTRACTOR to\nOWNER/CONSULTANT'S account in advance at price specified by\nOWNER/CONSULTANT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0067",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 67,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 21036,
    "char_end": 21235,
    "char_count": 199,
    "text": "9.2.6\nAny excess materials drawn by CONTRACTOR, but not used in WORK shall\nbe returned to OWNER/CONSULTANT'S Store at SITE and receipt obtained;\nand credit will be given for the quantity so returned.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0068",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 68,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 21237,
    "char_end": 21559,
    "char_count": 322,
    "text": "9.2.7\nCONTRACTOR shall return to OWNER the cut pieces and scraps of material\nissued by OWNER/CONSULTANT as well as any containers in which they\nare issued. Such items shall be properly accounted and delivered at the\ndump-yard at SITE indicated by OWNER/CONSULTANT and no credit will\nbe given to CONTRACTOR on this account.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0069",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 69,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 21561,
    "char_end": 21934,
    "char_count": 373,
    "text": "9.2.8\nIn case it is observed that CONTRACTOR has used materials in quantity less\nthan what is legitimately required and the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE is not\nsatisfied with the reason given by CONTRACTOR, CONTRACTOR shall\nhave to dismantle the work so executed and re-do the same at no cost to\nOWNER/CONSULTANT. In any case the contract price will be adjusted for\nsuch short-usage.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0070",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 70,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 21936,
    "char_end": 22562,
    "char_count": 626,
    "text": "9.2.9\nOWNER/CONSULTANT gives no assurance that material to be issued by\nOWNER/CONSULTANT will be readily available as and when indented by\nCONTRACTOR, CONTRACTOR is advised to give a monthly programme of\nhis requirement for each calendar month at least 30 days prior to the first of\nthe calendar month. This programme should indicate the expected\nrequirement in sizes, and quantities and the dates on which required. If\nCONTRACTOR fails to take such advance action, he shall not be entitled for\nany extension of time-schedule consequent to delay by OWNER/CONSULTANT in\nissue of materials, even if such delay has affected WORK.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0071",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 71,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 22564,
    "char_end": 22672,
    "char_count": 108,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 13 of 46\n\nARTICLE-10\nMATERIALS / EQUIPMENT BYCONTRACTOR",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0072",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 72,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 22674,
    "char_end": 23315,
    "char_count": 641,
    "text": "10.1 CONTRACTOR shall procure in time at his own cost and use in WORK all\nMATERIALS / EQUIPMENT required in carrying out WORK other than\nEQUIPMENT and materials issued by OWNER/CONSULTANT vide Article-9\nhereof. Materials so procured and brought to SITE shall be stored by\nCONTRACTOR at place allotted for the purpose by ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE\nand security arrangements shall be made by CONTRACTOR. CONTRACTOR\nshall provide such materials in sufficient quantities and in time so that WORK can\nbe proceeded with uninterruptedly and shall take advance action in procurement\nof items which are in scarce supply or availability of which are seasonal.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0073",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 73,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 23317,
    "char_end": 24257,
    "char_count": 940,
    "text": "10.2 MATERIALS / EQUIPMENT provided by CONTRACTOR shall be brand new and\nof specification agreed to herein or as approved by ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE.\nMATERIALS / EQUIPMENT brought to SITE shall be used in WORK only after\napproval by ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE and if so required by him, CONTRACTOR\nshall provide test certificates and / or samples for verifying the quality. Mill\ncertificates covering physical and analytical tests are to be produced as called for\nby ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE at no extra cost. If any further tests are to be carried\nout CONTRACTOR shall arrange for the same at no additional cost to\nOWNER/CONSULTANT. CONTRACTOR shall declare the manufacturer's name\nof such MATERIALS / EQUIPMENT and provide, if asked for, evidence relating\nto the source and purchase there from. Decision by ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE\nshall be final and binding on CONTRACTOR in respect of whether the material\nprovided is conforming to agreed specification or not.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0074",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 74,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 24259,
    "char_end": 24348,
    "char_count": 89,
    "text": "10.3 Rejected MATERIALS / EQUIPMENT shall be removed by CONTRACTOR from\nSITE immediately.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0075",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 75,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 24350,
    "char_end": 24773,
    "char_count": 423,
    "text": "10.4 Approval\nby\nENGINEER-IN-CHARGE\nor\nany\nother\nrepresentative\nof\nOWNER/CONSULTANT shall not relieve CONTRACTOR of his responsibility to\nuse material of specified quality suitable for WORK and re-work necessitated\nconsequent to use of sub-standard MATERIALS / EQUIPMENT shall be promptly\ncarried out by CONTRACTOR, free of cost to OWNER/CONSULTANT,\nirrespective of whether the item was approved by OWNER/CONSULTANT or not.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0076",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 76,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 24775,
    "char_end": 24999,
    "char_count": 224,
    "text": "ARTICLE-11 QUALITY OF WORK\n\n11.1 CONTRACTOR shall execute WORK in the most substantial, professional and\nworkman-like manner in full conformity to the drawing and specifications and\ninstructions provided by OWNER/CONSULTANT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0077",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 77,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 25001,
    "char_end": 25341,
    "char_count": 340,
    "text": "11.2 CONTRACTOR shall be responsible for the dimensional accuracy of WORK\ncarried out within the measurement tolerance specified. In case where no\nmeasurement tolerance is specified, decision of ENGINEER-IN-CHANGE shall\nbe final in respect of whether an item of WORK carried out conforms to required\nstandard of dimensional accuracy or not.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0078",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 78,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 25343,
    "char_end": 25568,
    "char_count": 225,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 14 of 46\n\n11.3 Any designs carried out by CONTRACTOR shall be done in a professional and\nengineer-like manner in conformity with applicable standards and codes of\npractice.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0079",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 79,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 25570,
    "char_end": 26143,
    "char_count": 573,
    "text": "11.4 CONTRACTOR shall be responsible to ensure that WORK executed conforms to\napplicable statutory regulations in force on the date on which Letter of Intent is\nissued by OWNER/CONSULTANT. In the event of any change in such statutory\nregulations or any new regulations becoming effective after the date of Letter of\nIntent that have influence on WORK, CONTRACTOR shall promptly notify\nOWNER/CONSULTANT of the consequent changes required in WORK and its\nimpact, if any, on cost and time-schedule agreed to herein and the provisions of\nArticle-15 hereof will thereafter apply",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0080",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 80,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 26145,
    "char_end": 26747,
    "char_count": 602,
    "text": "ARTICLE-12 INSPECTION BY OWNER/CONSULTANT\n\n12.1 ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE\nor\nany\nother\ndesignated\nrepresentative\nof\nOWNER/CONSULTANT shall at all reasonable times be entitled to inspect\nWORK or any part thereof. CONTRACTOR shall provide all necessary\nassistance to OWNER/CONSULTANT and shall make available all necessary\nscaffolding, tools and testing equipment to enable OWNER/CONSULTANT to\ncarry out such inspection / tests. CONTRACTOR shall uncover any part of\nWORK or make openings for inspection as ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE may direct\nand\nmake\ngood\nsuch\npart\nto\nthe\nreasonable\nsatisfaction\nof\nOWNER/CONSULTANT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0081",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 81,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 26749,
    "char_end": 27342,
    "char_count": 593,
    "text": "12.2 On receiving notice from CONTRACTOR that WORK or part thereof is ready for\ninspection, ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall without unreasonable delay attend for\nthe purpose of inspecting the related item of WORK. When tests are completed\nsatisfactorily, CONTRACTOR shall give the test certificates within Five (5) days\nof completion of tests for signature by ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE. ENGINER-IN-\nCHARGE may waive at his discretion, right to attend any tests; but this shall not\nrelieve CONTRACTOR of his responsibility to carry out necessary tests at each\nstage of WORK and provide the test certificates.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0082",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 82,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 27344,
    "char_end": 27823,
    "char_count": 479,
    "text": "12.3\nWhenever it is necessary to cover up any item or WORK in respect of which\nprevious inspection is desired and CONTRACTOR has been notified accordingly\nin writing, CONTRACTOR shall give five (5) days’ notice in writing to\nENGINEER-IN-CHARGE before the said item is covered up. No such WORK\nshall be covered up or built upon unless it has been inspected and approved by\nENGINEER-IN-CHARGE or his consent in writing to this being done without prior\ninspection has been obtained.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0083",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 83,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 27825,
    "char_end": 28027,
    "char_count": 202,
    "text": "12.4 CONTRACTOR will, if so required by OWNER/CONSULTANT, provide specified\nnumbers of test certificates, material analysis certificates and / or radiographic /\nNDT examination reports at no extra cost.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0084",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 84,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 28029,
    "char_end": 28332,
    "char_count": 303,
    "text": "12.5 All tests shall be carried out as per procedure agreed to herein. If no such\nprocedure is agreed to herein the procedure laid out in applicable standards /\ncodes and as approved by ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall be followed. If in  the\nopinion of ENGINEER-IN–CHARGE any tests carried out are not properly",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0085",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 85,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 28334,
    "char_end": 28473,
    "char_count": 139,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 15 of 46\n\nconducted, CONTRACTOR shall have to repeat the same at no additional cost to",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0086",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 86,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 28475,
    "char_end": 28864,
    "char_count": 389,
    "text": "OWNER/CONSULTANT.\n\n12.6 If in the opinion of ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE results of any tests carried out is not\nreasonably satisfactory, he may reject the portion of WORK for which the test is\nnot satisfactory and CONTRACTOR shall dismantle the rejected portion and redo\nthe same at no additional cost and such repair/ rework shall be subjected to\nfurther inspection/test in the above-said manner.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0087",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 87,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 28866,
    "char_end": 29062,
    "char_count": 196,
    "text": "12.7 That an item of WORK has been approved at the time of setting out or in stage-\nwise inspection/test does not relieve CONTRACTOR of his responsibilities under\nArticle-21 and Article–30thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0088",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 88,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 29064,
    "char_end": 29436,
    "char_count": 372,
    "text": "12.8 OWNER/CONSULTANT reserves the right to engage or for participation of\nrepresentatives of OWNER/CONSULTANT'S Licensor or collaborator or any third\nparty inspection agency that OWNER/CONSULTANT may appoint for  the\npurpose, in inspection and testing of WORK and such representative may\nexercise with CONTRACTOR such authorities as OWNER/CONSULTANT may\ndelegate to them.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0089",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 89,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 29438,
    "char_end": 29736,
    "char_count": 298,
    "text": "ARTICLE-13\nPRICE\n\n13.1 In consideration of WORK, OWNER shall pay CONTRACTOR the sum specified\nin SCHEDULE-F, PRICES. The sum specified in SCHEDULE-F include all costs\nto CONTRACTOR in carrying out WORK except cost of any material to be issued\nfree of cost by OWNER/CONSULTANT vide Article-9 hereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0090",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 90,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 29738,
    "char_end": 30382,
    "char_count": 644,
    "text": "13.2 The price specified in SCHEDULE-F is inclusive of all costs such as labour,\nmaterials to be supplied by CONTRACTOR, materials to be provided by\nOWNER/CONSULTANT at CONTRACTOR'S cost, supervision, incidental\ncharges such as loading and unloading, hoisting, setting out, temporary facilities,\nprotective works, safety measures, tools and implements, construction\nequipment,\nhire\ncharges\nof\nconstruction\nequipment\nprovided\nby\nOWNER/CONSULTANT, royalties, licenses, testing and calibration, removal of\ndebris and clearing SITE on completion of WORK and maintenance of WORK\nrequired hereunder and any other cost incidental to carrying out WORK.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0091",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 91,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 30384,
    "char_end": 30634,
    "char_count": 250,
    "text": "13.3 Without prejudice to provisions under Article-15, all prices shall remain firm till\ncompletionofWORKandshallnotbesubjecttoescalationofanydescriptionincluding\nthose on account of delays due to Force Majeure, unless otherwise stated in\nSCHEDULE-F.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0092",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 92,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 30636,
    "char_end": 30763,
    "char_count": 127,
    "text": "13.4 All statutory deductions will be made at source in accordance with the rules and\nregulations prevailing from time to time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0093",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 93,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 30765,
    "char_end": 31057,
    "char_count": 292,
    "text": "13.5 Amounts specified in SCHEDULE-F are subject to deduction of Income Tax and\nOWNER/CONSULTANT shall withhold from the same such amount as is due at\nrates prevailing at the time of payment and remit the same to income tax\nauthorities to the account of CONTRACTOR and provide CONTRACTOR with",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0094",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 94,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 31059,
    "char_end": 31269,
    "char_count": 210,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 16 of 46\n\nappropriate certificate of tax deduction. Any statutory variation in the rate of\ndeduction of income tax shall not lead to any adjustment in Price.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0095",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 95,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 31271,
    "char_end": 31413,
    "char_count": 142,
    "text": "ARTICLE-14\nTERMS OFPAYMENT\n\n14.1 OWNER/CONSULTANT shall make payments to CONTRACTOR in installments\nas specified in SCHEDULE-G PAYMENTSCHEDULE",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0096",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 96,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 31415,
    "char_end": 31653,
    "char_count": 238,
    "text": "14.2 CONTRACTOR shall make all claims in the standard printed bill form prescribed\nby the OWNER/CONSULTANT and claims shall be serially numbered. Claims\nshall be made in triplicate copies and shall be submitted to the ENGINEER-IN-\nCHARGE.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0097",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 97,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 31655,
    "char_end": 31921,
    "char_count": 266,
    "text": "14.3 In case mobilisation advance is agreed to in SCHEDULE-G, CONTRACTOR\nshall submit along with the invoice a Bank Guarantee from a Nationalised Bank in\nIndia, in the proforma vide SCHEDULE-M and payment will be made within 15\ndays of receipt of the said documents.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0098",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 98,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 31923,
    "char_end": 32248,
    "char_count": 325,
    "text": "14.4 Claims for part - payments shall not be more frequent than once a month. Any\ndeduction to be made for materials issued by OWNER/CONSULTANT or for hire\nchanges of construction equipment provided by OWNER/CONSULTANT will be\ndeducted from the respective part bill and CONTRACTOR shall show such\ndeductions also in the bill.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0099",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 99,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 32250,
    "char_end": 32604,
    "char_count": 354,
    "text": "14.5 All part - payments shall be treated as payments on account and not as value of\nWORK done and on satisfactory completion of WORK and issue of taking over\ncertificate CONTRACTOR will be paid the total amount due after deduction of\nany liquidated damages due under CONTRACT, less payments already made\nand any other recoveries due from the CONTRACTOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0100",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 100,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 32606,
    "char_end": 32766,
    "char_count": 160,
    "text": "ARTICLE-15 CHANGE IN WORK\n\n15.1 Any modification in specification and / or quantity of WORK due to any of the\nfollowing reasons will constitute a CHANGE INWORK.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0101",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 101,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 32768,
    "char_end": 32964,
    "char_count": 196,
    "text": "i)\nIncrease or decrease in quantity of WORK as per final designs provided by\nOWNER/CONSULTANT as compared to those specified in SCHEDULE-F\nhereof, hereinafter referred to as \"Variation inQuantity\"",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0102",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 102,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 32966,
    "char_end": 33250,
    "char_count": 284,
    "text": "ii) Variation in specifications for any item of WORK as per final design given by\nOWNER/CONSULTANT\nas\ncompared\nto\nSCHEDULE-F\nhereof\nor\nconsequent to changes made after date of Letter of Intent in applicable\nstatutory regulations hereinafter referred to as \"Variation in Specification\"",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0103",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 103,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 33252,
    "char_end": 33430,
    "char_count": 178,
    "text": "iii) Any new items of WORK not specified or included in SCHEDULE-A and for\nwhich any price or rate of cost is not specified in SCHEDULE-F hereinafter\nreferred to as\" Extra Item\".",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0104",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 104,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 33432,
    "char_end": 33565,
    "char_count": 133,
    "text": "iv) Any re-work necessitated by change in design by OWNER / CONSULTANT\n\nGENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 17 of 46",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0105",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 105,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 33567,
    "char_end": 33681,
    "char_count": 114,
    "text": "of an item of WORK already executed by CONTRACTOR as per\nCONTRACT, hereinafter referred to as \"Requested Re-work\".",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0106",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 106,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 33683,
    "char_end": 33838,
    "char_count": 155,
    "text": "Any modification or rework executed by CONTRACTOR by way of rectification of\nmistakes or making good defective WORK shall not be treated as CHANGE IN\nWORK.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0107",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 107,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 33840,
    "char_end": 34360,
    "char_count": 520,
    "text": "15.2 In the case of \"Variation in Quantity\" of an item of WORK the Contract value for\nthe item shall be adjusted pro-rata. In case aggregate increase or decrease in\nvalue of Contract due to Variation in Quantity and / or any other reason exceeds\n25% of the Initial Contract Price as per Schedule-F the adjustment in price for\nsuch variations beyond the Initial 25% margin shall be discussed and agreed\nbetween the parties. However, CONTRACTOR'S prices shall be firm for variation\nup to (+) 25% of Initial Contract value.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0108",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 108,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 34362,
    "char_end": 34927,
    "char_count": 565,
    "text": "15.3 In the event CONTRACTOR is called upon to carry out WORK with variation in\nspecification but generally falling within the categories of WORK covered by\nCONTRACT, CONTRACTOR shall carry out the related CHANGE IN WORK\nwithout any extension of time-schedule. However, the price payable for the items\naffected by said variation in specification shall be determined based on rates\nagreed to in CONTRACT for other similar items; and in the absence of agreed\nrates for similar items it shall be determined in such manner as is specified for\nthe purpose in SCHEDULE-F.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0109",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 109,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 34929,
    "char_end": 35120,
    "char_count": 191,
    "text": "15.4 If CONTRACTOR is called upon to carry out any extra item, consideration\nreceivable by CONTRACTOR for extra items shall be determined in the same\nmanner as specified in Article 15.3above.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0110",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 110,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 35122,
    "char_end": 35363,
    "char_count": 241,
    "text": "15.5 In the event CONTRACTOR is called upon to carry out any Requested Re- work,\nhe shall be compensated for any dismantling, demolishing or reconstruction as is\napplicable and determined in the same manner as provided in Article 15.3 above.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0111",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 111,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 35365,
    "char_end": 35650,
    "char_count": 285,
    "text": "15.6 Notwithstanding the above, if specific provisions are made for the adjustment\nofpriceormethodofdeterminingthesameinSCHEDULE-FortheSpecialConditions\nof\nContract vide SCHEDULE-Q provisions therein shall prevail over such provisions in the\nArticle-5 which are in conflict  with them.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0112",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 112,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 35652,
    "char_end": 35988,
    "char_count": 336,
    "text": "15.7 In the event CHANGE IN WORK is of a substantial nature and is likely to affect\nCONTRACTOR'S obligations in respect of Time Schedule, CONTRACTOR shall\nrequest ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE in writing of any extension of time schedule\nrequire giving reasons therefore as such extension shall be effective only when\napproved by OWNER/CONSULTANT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0113",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 113,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 35990,
    "char_end": 36466,
    "char_count": 476,
    "text": "ARTICLE–16 VARIATIONS &OMISSIONS\n\n16.1 CONTRACTOR shall not alter any of WORK except as directed in writing by\nENGINEER-IN-CHARGE. OWNER/CONSULTANT shall have full powers during\nexecution of CONTRACT to alter, amend, omit, add or otherwise vary WORK,\nfrom time to time by issue of written notice therefore to CONTRACTOR and\nCONTRACTOR shall carry out such variations and be bound by CONTRACT so\nfar as applicable as though the said variation is stated in CONTRACT. In case, in",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0114",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 114,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 36468,
    "char_end": 36975,
    "char_count": 507,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 18 of 46\n\nthe opinion of CONTRACTOR, the said variation will involve an increase or\ndecrease in the Contract Price or any of the other obligations of CONTRACTOR\nhereunder, subject to provisions under Article-15, CONTRACTOR shall within\nseven (7) days of receipt of the said notice advise ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE of\nthat effect and only on receipt of written acceptance of same from ENGINEER-\nIN-CHARGE, CONTRACTOR shall give effect to the requested variation.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0115",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 115,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 36977,
    "char_end": 37155,
    "char_count": 178,
    "text": "16.2 The difference in Contract Price; if any, occasioned by such variations shall be\nadded to or decreased from the Contract price and paid in the same manner as\nContract Price.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0116",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 116,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 37157,
    "char_end": 37751,
    "char_count": 594,
    "text": "ARTICLE-17 ACCESS TOSITE\n\n17.1 OWNER/CONSULTANT shall provide CONTRACTOR access to SITE and place\nwithin SITE where WORK is to be performed at all reasonable times, subject to\nArticle-24 and 26 hereof. Unless specified elsewhere to the Contrary,\nOWNER/CONSULTANT shall also provide suitable road for transport of\nEQUIPMENT and Materials from the nearest public thoroughfare or\nOWNER/CONSULTANT'S Store to the place of work. Any approach road,\nbridges over trenches, ladders or such other means of access required in the\narea of work shall be made by CONTRACTOR at no cost to OWNER /\nCONSULTANT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0117",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 117,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 37753,
    "char_end": 38396,
    "char_count": 643,
    "text": "17.2 The access to SITE or place of work shall not be exclusive to CONTRACTOR but\nonly such as to enable him to execute WORK. OWNER/CONSULTANT reserves\nthe right to grant access to SITE and place of WORK to other contractors\nengaged by OWNER/CONSULTANT for carrying out work relating to PROJECT\nand CONTRACTOR shall fully co-operate with such other contractors and carry\nout WORK without causing any hardship to others. OWNER/CONSULTANT'S\nrepresentatives and / or representative of any third-party engaged by\nOWNER/CONSULTANT for inspection and/ or any statutory authorities shall at all\nreasonable times have access to SITE and place of work.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0118",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 118,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 38398,
    "char_end": 38541,
    "char_count": 143,
    "text": "17.3 Access to SITE granted herein shall not be construed as grant of any right of\npossession or Title to CONTRACTOR over SITE or part thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0119",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 119,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 38543,
    "char_end": 38860,
    "char_count": 317,
    "text": "AR TICLE-18 CONSTRUCTION POWER & WATER\n\n18.1 OWNER/CONSULTANT shall provide CONTRACTOR with supply of electric\npower at nominal supply voltage of 415 V in 3 phase 50 C/s, 4 wire system at\none points at the outgoing terminals of OWNER/CONSULTANT'S switchgear in\nthe manner and for the purposes specified in SCHEDULE-H.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0120",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 120,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 38862,
    "char_end": 39410,
    "char_count": 548,
    "text": "18.2 CONTRACTOR shall make his own arrangements to lay cables along such\nroutes and in such manner as ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE approves and to\ndistribute the power to various consuming units and lighting system installed by\nCONTRACTOR, all in accordance with applicable statutory rules and regulations,\nCONTRACTOR shall apply for, pay any fees related thereto and obtain statutory\napprovals for such installations that CONTRACTOR sets up and engage, where\nnecessary, licensed electricians for attending to operation and up-keep for the\nsaid installation.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0121",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 121,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 39412,
    "char_end": 40150,
    "char_count": 738,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 19 of 46\n\n18.3 OWNER/CONSULTANT shall provide CONTRACTOR with supply of water for\nuse in WORK carried out at SITE at one point in a manner and for the purposes\nas specified in SCHEDULE-H. CONTRACTOR shall make his own arrangements\nfor laying pipelines from the above point to place of WORK and for distribution\ntherein along a route and in manner approved by ENGINEER- IN-CHARGE.\nCONTRACTOR shall ensure that the installations made by CONTRACTOR are\nleak proof and that proper valves are provided at all distribution points in order to\navoid any wastage of water. For use in higher elevations necessary surface tank\nand pumping arrangements shall be provided by CONTRACTOR at his cost.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0122",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 122,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 40152,
    "char_end": 40748,
    "char_count": 596,
    "text": "18.4 Supply of power and water by OWNER/CONSULTANT in the above-said manner\nis free of cost to CONTRACTOR. OWNER/CONSULTANT shall endeavor to\nmaintain supply of power and water uninterruptedly so that WORK can be\nproceeded with without interruption. However, in the event of any interruption in\nthese supplies for short intervals of time due to any repair or maintenance of\nOWNER/CONSULTANT'S supply system or due to extraneous reasons,\nCONTRACTOR shall fully co-operate by re-scheduling the day's WORK and shall\nnot be entitled for any extension of Time -Schedule or compensation for idle\nwages.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0123",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 123,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 40750,
    "char_end": 41343,
    "char_count": 593,
    "text": "ARTICLE-19 CONSTRUCTION EQUIPMENT\n\n19.1 CONTRACTOR shall provide all tools, tackles, hoisting equipment, safety\nappliances, ladders, scaffolding, test equipment and such other facilities as are\nrequired for carrying out WORK and OWNER/CONSULTANT does not undertake\nto provide any such facility except as provided here under CONTRACTOR'S\nequipment shall be used solely for the purpose of WORK and shall not be removed from\nSITE by CONTRACTOR without written permission of OWNER/CONSULTANT.\nCONTRACTOR shall be responsible to maintain and safeguard CONTRACTOR'S\nequipment against damage or loss.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0124",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 124,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 41345,
    "char_end": 41815,
    "char_count": 470,
    "text": "19.2 Construction equipment available with OWNER/CONSULTANT and the hire\ncharges for each are described in SCHEDULE-J. These equipment will be\noperated by OWNER/CONSULTANT'S crew and the hire changes include all\nrunning expenses. The hire changes will be reckoned for the period commencing\nwith the time at which it is released for use by CONTRACTOR up to time when it\nis released by CONTRACTOR or time up to which CONTRACTOR has intended\nfor his use whichever is later.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0125",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 125,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 41817,
    "char_end": 42576,
    "char_count": 759,
    "text": "19.3 Construction equipment available with OWNER/CONSULTANT are limited and\nare intended for the common use of the PROJECT and OWNER/CONSULTANT\ndoes not undertake .to place these at the disposal of CONTRACTOR without\nspecific prior commitment. CONTRACTOR shall discuss with ENGINEER-IN-\nCHARGE the requirements and programme of use well in advance and the\nequipment will be made available only during such times as the ENGINEER-IN-\nCHARGE agrees to. That OWNER/CONSULTANT'S construction equipment was\nnot available in the time or for adequate duration shall not entitle CONTRACTOR\nfor any increase in price or extension of Time Schedule unless agreed to\notherwise in SCHEDULE-F and in such cases CONTRACTOR shall have to\nmake his own alternative arrangements.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0126",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 126,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 42578,
    "char_end": 42970,
    "char_count": 392,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 20 of 46\n\n19.4 OWNER/CONSULTANT'S construction equipment placed at the disposal of\nCONTRACTOR shall be used by CONTRACTOR only for the purposes they are\nintended for and within its prescribed limits of application and CONTRACTOR\nshall be liable to bear cost of repair / replacement in case of any damage due to\nmisuse or wrong application.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0127",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 127,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 42972,
    "char_end": 43216,
    "char_count": 244,
    "text": "ARTICLE-20 ACCOMMODATION AT SITE & COMMUNICATION FACILITIES\n\n20.1 OWNER/CONSULTANT does not undertake to provide any covered area or\nprotected accommodation of any kind for use by CONTRACTOR for office, store,\nshop or residential accommodation.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0128",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 128,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 43218,
    "char_end": 43612,
    "char_count": 394,
    "text": "20.2 OWNER/CONSULTANT shall allot leveled ground at convenient place in SITE\nwithin reasonable distance of the place of WORK where CONTRACTOR may\nbuild temporary structures for site office; store and fabrication shop and\nCONTRACTOR\nshall\nmake\narrangements\nfor\nfencing\nand\nsecurity.\nCONTRACTOR shall also make suitable arrangements for sanitation and\nhygiene in the place allotted to CONTRACTOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0129",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 129,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 43614,
    "char_end": 43927,
    "char_count": 313,
    "text": "20.3 CONTRACTOR shall make his own arrangements for residential accommodation\nof staff and workmen, facilities for food and canteen and shall not set up any\nhutments, barracks or other form of residential units at any place within SITE or on\nother land belonging to OWNER/CONSULTANT unless specifically agreed to.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0130",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 130,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 43929,
    "char_end": 44203,
    "char_count": 274,
    "text": "20.4 CONTRACTOR shall make his own arrangements for any telephone / telex / fax /\nemail communication facilities he needs in carrying out WORK. In case of\nemergency, OWNER/CONSULTANT may permit use of available facility for\nwhich charges if any shall be borne by CONTRACTOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0131",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 131,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 44205,
    "char_end": 44897,
    "char_count": 692,
    "text": "ARTICLE-21 TESTS ON COMPLETION & TAKING OVER\n\n21.1 CONTRACTOR shall give ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE fifteen (15) days’ notice in\nwriting of the date on which he will be ready to carry out tests specified in\nSCHEDULE-A for the WORK or section of WORK if WORK is so divided in\nSCHEDULE-A. Unless otherwise agreed, these tests shall take place within ten\n(10) days after the date so notified by CONTRACTOR on such day / days as\nENGINEER-IN-CHARGE notifies CONTRACTOR in writing. Tests shall be held\nas per procedure laid out in SCHEDULE-K hereof and within three (3) days of\ncompletion of tests CONTRACTOR shall submit to ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE\nthree (3) copies of the report of the tests for his approval.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0132",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 132,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 44899,
    "char_end": 45506,
    "char_count": 607,
    "text": "21.2 If in the opinion of ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE the tests on completion are being\nunduly delayed he may by notice in writing call upon the CONTRACTOR to make\nsuch tests within ten (10) days of receipt of such notice; and unless otherwise\nagreed, CONTRACTOR shall make the said tests on such day within the said 10\ndays as the ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE may fix and of which he shall give notice to\nENGINEER-IN-CHARGE. If CONTRACTOR shall fail to make the tests within the\ntime aforesaid, OWNER/CONSULTANT shall be entitled to proceed with the\ntests and all tests as made shall be at the risk and expense of CONTRACTOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0133",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 133,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 45508,
    "char_end": 45962,
    "char_count": 454,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 21 of 46\n\n21.3 ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE may require CONTRACTOR at any time before\ncommencement of a test or during the performance of the test to postpone or\nsuspend the test if in his opinion the arrangements made by CONTRACTOR for\ncarrying out the tests are inadequate or unsatisfactory; and in such case\nCONTRACTOR shall re-schedule the tests and conduct it in such manner as\nENGINEER-IN-CHARGE approves.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0134",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 134,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 45964,
    "char_end": 46914,
    "char_count": 950,
    "text": "21.4 Should any part of WORK fail to achieve the performance specified or to pass the\ntests prescribed in any other manner, CONTRACTOR shall at his own expense\neffect such changes consistent with good engineering practice, as are necessary\nto enable the WORK to pass further tests and conduct a fresh test after duly\nnotifying ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE. If during the further tests, the WORK or any\npart thereof fails to achieve the performance specified, the WORK shall not be\nconsidered acceptable and CONTRACTOR shall replace, re-do or otherwise\nrectify them entirely at his own cost until they become acceptable, all within the\ntime schedule agreed to vide Article–4, provided that in case the failure to pass\ntests is within permissible limits as Engineer-in- charge considers acceptable,\nOWNER/CONSULTANT\nmay\nat\nits\nown\ndiscretionaccepttheWORKuponappropriatedeductioninContractpriceasmay\nbe\nprovided for elsewhere in CONTRACT or as mutually agreed to.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0135",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 135,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 46916,
    "char_end": 47746,
    "char_count": 830,
    "text": "21.5 As soon as WORK has been completed in all respects in accordance with\nCONTRACT and has passed the prescribed tests, OWNER/CONSULTANT shall\nissue a certificate taking over the WORK (hereinafter referred to as Taking Over\nCertificate), stating the date on which WORK has been so completed and passed\nthe\ntests,\nand\nthe\nWORK\nshall\nbe\ndeemed\ntaken\nover\nby\nOWNER/CONSULTANT on the said date. In the event of WORK being divided\nby this CONTRACT into two or more sections or not being completed in all\nrespects but only to such an extent that it can be put to use by\nOWNER/CONSULTANT without hindering or being hindered by the execution of\npart remaining to be completed, OWNER/CONSULTANT shall be entitled  to take\nover any section or sections before the other or the others by issuing a Taking\nOver Certificate in respect thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0136",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 136,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 47748,
    "char_end": 48388,
    "char_count": 640,
    "text": "21.6 If by reason of any default on the part of CONTRACTOR a Taking Over\nCertificate has not been issued in respect of every portion of WORK or every\nportion of a section of W ORK within Thirty (30) days of the date on which it\nshould have been issued as per Time Schedule agreed in CONTRACT,\nOWNER/CONSULTANT shall be at liberty, without prejudice to other rights\nherein of OWNER/CONSULTANT to use the WORK of any portion thereof in\nrespect of which a Taking Over Certificate has not been issued, provided that\nCONTRACTOR is afforded reasonable opportunity to take such steps as may be\nnecessary to permit issue of Taking Over Certificate.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0137",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 137,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 48390,
    "char_end": 48609,
    "char_count": 219,
    "text": "21.7 Issue of Taking Over Certificate or acceptance of WORK or part thereof in any\nother manner after passing prescribed tests or otherwise shall not relieve\nCONTRACTOR of his warranty obligations vide Article-30hereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0138",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 138,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 48611,
    "char_end": 48719,
    "char_count": 108,
    "text": "ARTICLE-22 TEMPORARY STRUCTURES\n\n22.1 Any temporary structure set up at SITE by CONTRACTOR shall be of sound",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0139",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 139,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 48721,
    "char_end": 49258,
    "char_count": 537,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 22 of 46\n\nconstruction taking into account safety of EQUIPMENT and workmen and\nCONTRACTOR shall be solely responsible for any damage or consequence\nthereof of the same. If in the opinion of ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE such\nconstructions are not of appropriate design or construction and are likely to\nimperil safety of EQUIPMENT and/or workmen he may notify CONTRACTOR\naccordingly and Contractor shall forthwith forbid its use until it is replaced or\nsuitably modified in an acceptable manner.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0140",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 140,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 49260,
    "char_end": 49602,
    "char_count": 342,
    "text": "22.2 Any temporary construction made by CONTRACTOR in connection with WORK\nshall be dismantled and removed by CONTRACTOR and the entire area where\nWORK was performed cleared of any surplus or scrap materials, rubbish or\ndebris within Thirty (30) days of issue of Taking over Certificate or such earlier\ndate as ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE may require.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0141",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 141,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 49604,
    "char_end": 49983,
    "char_count": 379,
    "text": "22.3 If any temporary structure set up by CONTRACTOR at SITE including any power\nand water lines obstruct implementation of PROJECT in any manner at any stage\nof WORK, CONTRACTOR shall immediately on receipt of notice thereof from\nENGINEER-IN-CHARGE dismantle and remove or shift the temporary structure or line,\nat his own cost, in such a manner that the obstruction is removed.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0142",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 142,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 49985,
    "char_end": 50260,
    "char_count": 275,
    "text": "ARTICLE-23 INSURANCE AND LIABILITY FOR DAMAGE\n\n23.1 CONTRACTOR shall during execution of WORK, properly cover up and protect\nany part of work liable to damage by exposure to weather and shall take every\nreasonable precaution against accident or damage to work from any cause.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0143",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 143,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 50262,
    "char_end": 50536,
    "char_count": 274,
    "text": "23.2 All equipments and materials brought to SITE by CONTRACTOR for use in\nexecution of WORK shall be at sole risk of CONTRACTOR. Only such materials\nas are actually used in WORK so as to form part thereof will be covered by the\ninsurance cover arranged by OWNER/CONSULTANT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0144",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 144,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 50538,
    "char_end": 50849,
    "char_count": 311,
    "text": "23.3 OWNER/CONSULTANT shall have covered by storage-cum-erection insurance\npolicies EQUIPMENT, materials supplied by OWNER / CONSULTANT,\nOWNER/CONSULTANT'S construction equipment, WORK executed at SITE and\nOWNER/CONSULTANT'S personnel. These policies apply only to insurance\nrisks at SITE and no other location.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0145",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 145,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 50851,
    "char_end": 51221,
    "char_count": 370,
    "text": "23.4 CONTRACTOR shall take care not to cause any damage to any equipment,\nmaterials and or construction of and or any work executed by any other\nContractors or other third parties doing work at SITE and CONTRACTOR\nIndemnifies\nOWNER/CONSULTANT\nagainst\nany\nliabilities,\nwhatsoever,\nconsequent to damage caused by CONTRACTOR or CONTRACTOR'S workmen\nin the aforesaid manner.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0146",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 146,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 51223,
    "char_end": 51603,
    "char_count": 380,
    "text": "23.5 CONTRACTOR indemnifies OWNER/CONSULTANT against any loss, damage\nor other liabilities in consequence of any negligent act or omission by\nCONTRACTOR or CONTRACTOR'S Workmen or theft or pilferage of any\nmaterial and / or EQUIPMENT handed over to CONTRACTOR by\nOWNER/CONSULTANT. CONTRACTOR shall take appropriate insurance as\nmay be required to cover the above responsibilities.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0147",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 147,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 51605,
    "char_end": 51692,
    "char_count": 87,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 23 of 46\n\nARTICLE-24 WORKING HOURS",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0148",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 148,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 51694,
    "char_end": 51958,
    "char_count": 264,
    "text": "24.1 All days observed as Holidays by OWNER/CONSULTANT shall be Holidays and\nall other days shall be working days at SITE, CONTRACTOR shall be given, on\nrequest, the calendar of such Holidays for each year. CONTRACTOR shall carry\nout WORK normally on working days.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0149",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 149,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 51960,
    "char_end": 52928,
    "char_count": 968,
    "text": "24.2 Working hours shall be 8 hours per day on all working days and timing will be as\nENGINEER-IN-CHARGE may notify from time to time. Contractor's workmen will\nbe permitted to enter SITE only thirty (30) minutes prior to commencement of\nworking hours and shall leave SITE within thirty (30) minutes of close of working\nhours. However in special circumstances such as when ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE\nis satisfied that nature of WORK for the time being carried out is such that it shall\nhave to be proceeded with uninterruptedly even beyond normal working hours or when\nCONTRACTOR is behind schedule and would not be able to complete WORK within\nnormal working hours. OWNER/CONSULTANT shall permit CONTRACTOR to and\nCONTRACTOR shall perform WORK beyond normal working hours and any overtime\nwages or other costs receivable by CONTRACTOR'S workmen shall be fully borne by\nCONTRACTOR. CONTRACTOR shall seek for permission for engaging in WORK\nbeyond normal hours well in advance.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0150",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 150,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 52930,
    "char_end": 53319,
    "char_count": 389,
    "text": "ARTICLE-25 SAFETY\n\n25.1 CONTRACTOR shall execute WORK in a safe and secure manner always\nensuring safety of personnel engaged in WORK, EQUIPMENT, Materials,\nConstruction Equipment and the WORK itself in all its phases. Safety codes for\nConstruction specified in SCHEDULE-P shall be strictly adhered to and any\nviolation of these will be deemed willful negligence on the part of\nCONTRACTOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0151",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 151,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 53321,
    "char_end": 53623,
    "char_count": 302,
    "text": "25.2 In the event of any accident occurring at SITE in connection with WORK,\nCONTRACTOR shall submit a report of same to ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE\nimmediately, and/in any case within 24 hours of its occurrence, and shall fully co-\noperate with OWNER/CONSULTANT in any enquiry held in connection with the\nsame.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0152",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 152,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 53625,
    "char_end": 53985,
    "char_count": 360,
    "text": "ARTICLE-26 CONSULTANT'S REGULATIONS & RULES\n\n26.1 CONTRACTOR shall observe and ensure that his supervisors and workmen\nobserve all rules and regulations of OWNER/CONSULTANT applicable to SITE\nas may be communicated by OWNER/CONSULTANT from time to time.\nCONTRACTOR shall ensure that his supervisors and workmen engaged at SITE\nfunction in a disciplined manner.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0153",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 153,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 53987,
    "char_end": 54429,
    "char_count": 442,
    "text": "26.2 Entry to SITE of CONTRACTOR'S men shall at all times be subject to security\nregulations of OWNER/CONSULTANT and controlled by issue of passes.\nPasses will be issued against application by CONTRACTOR in appropriate form\nwithin seven days of receipt of such application. OWNER/CONSULTANT may\nreject issue of pass or cancel a pass issued earlier to any person whose\npresence at SITE, in the opinion of OWNER/CONSULTANT is detrimental to the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0154",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 154,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 54431,
    "char_end": 54523,
    "char_count": 92,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 24 of 46\n\ninterest of OWNER/CONSULTANT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0155",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 155,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 54525,
    "char_end": 55006,
    "char_count": 481,
    "text": "26.3 In the event of any person or persons including CONTRACTOR'S\nREPRESENTATIVE engaged by CONTRACTOR for WORK violates any of the\nregulations of OWNER/CONSULTANT or does not function in a disciplined\nmanner or is not, in the assessment of OWNER/CONSULTANT, competent to\ncarry out the work for which he is engaged OWNER / CONSULTANT, may\ncancel the entry passes issued to such person / persons without any notice and\nCONTRACTOR shall make arrangements for substitutes immediately.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0156",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 156,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 55008,
    "char_end": 55341,
    "char_count": 333,
    "text": "ARTICLE-27 STATUTORY REGULATIONS\n\n27.1 CONTRACTOR shall in all matters arising out of performance of CONTRACT\nconfirm at his own expense with all Acts, Orders, Regulations, Rules and By-\nLaws of Government of India, State Governments, local bodies and other\nauthorities there under for the time being in force and applicable to WORK.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0157",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 157,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 55343,
    "char_end": 55681,
    "char_count": 338,
    "text": "27.2 Where any temporary installations, facilities or apparatus set up by\nCONTRACTOR for carrying out WORK is subject to statutory regulations.\nCONTRACTOR shall ensure that these conform to such regulations applicable\nand also apply for pay necessary fees and obtain any approval required there\nunder, prior to putting the same in to use.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0158",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 158,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 55683,
    "char_end": 56578,
    "char_count": 895,
    "text": "27.3 Where WORK or any part thereof, other than those covered by Article-27.2\nabove, is subject to statutory regulations / approval, OWNER shall apply for such\napprovals and pay the fees; but CONTRACTOR shall provide at his own expense\nall information and assistance necessary to make such applications and to satisfy\nthe Inspecting Authority representing the related statutory body that WORK\ncarried out conforms to applicable regulation. Any WORK or part thereof rejected\nfor non-compliance with statutory regulations shall be modified or replaced by\nCONTRACTOR at no cost to OWNER/CONSULTANT within the agreed Time-\nSchedule so as to make it conform to applicable regulations. CONTRACTOR\nshall not be responsible for any such liability if it has occurred due to the sole\nreason that EQUIPMENT, designs or materials supplied by OWNER /\nCONSULTANT do not conform to such applicable regulations.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0159",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 159,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 56580,
    "char_end": 56901,
    "char_count": 321,
    "text": "ARTICLE-28 LAWS RELATING TO LABOUR\n\n28.1 CONTRACTOR shall comply with all Acts, Rules, Orders, Regulations, By- laws\nof Government of India; State Government. Local Bodies or an Office, authority\nor unit, there under pertaining to employment or labour at SITE and procure any\nlicense that is required for such employment.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0160",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 160,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 56903,
    "char_end": 57409,
    "char_count": 506,
    "text": "28.2 CONTRACTOR shall be deemed Employer for these purposes and shall\ndischarge all obligations of Employer. CONTRACTOR shall maintain such\nregisters and records and display such information and notices as are required\nunder these provisions and such registers shall at all-time be available for\ninspection by OWNER/CONSULTANT. Where the law require that any act of\nCONTRACTOR shall be carried out only in the presence of a representative of\nOWNER/CONSULTANT and witnessed by OWNER / CONSULTANT it shall be",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0161",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 161,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 57411,
    "char_end": 57778,
    "char_count": 367,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 25 of 46\n\nso carried and CONTRACTOR shall request ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE for the\npresence of OWNER/CONSULTANT'S representative. Any information or reports\nrequired from CONTRACTOR by OWNER/CONSULTANT, periodically or\notherwise, for discharge of OWNER/CONSULTANTS obligations under such\nlaws shall be provided promptly.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0162",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 162,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 57780,
    "char_end": 58206,
    "char_count": 426,
    "text": "28.3. Payment of workmen Compensation and implementation of labour laws with regard\nto workmen employed by CONTRACTOR are CONTRACTOR'S liability and in\ncase OWNER/CONSULTANT is compelled to incur any expense or any other\namount on behalf of CONTRACTOR'S workmen, OWNER/CONSULTANT is\nentitled to recover that amount from any bills payable to CONTRACTOR or in any\nother manner as is provided in Article - 44 hereof or otherwise.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0163",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 163,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 58208,
    "char_end": 59071,
    "char_count": 863,
    "text": "28.4 Contractor shall be responsible for all obligations under ESI Act, P. F. Act,\nBuilding and Other Construction Worker's Welfare Cess Act, 1996, Rules and\nRegulations there under and such other Acts and Regulations as may be\nrelevant. Deduction towards ESI, PF, Building and Other Construction Worker's\nWelfare Cess etc. required as per applicable statutory regulations shall be made\nby the Contractor and the amounts so deducted along with the Contractor's own\ncontributions as applicable shall be deposited with appropriate authorities.\nEvidence of this shall be produced by the Contractor when called upon to do so\nby OWNER/CONSULTANT and  in  any  case every quarter. In case\nOWNER/CONSULTANT is called upon to pay any  such expenses, these shall\nbe reimbursed fully by CONTRACTOR and OWNER/CONSULTANT shall be\nentitled to recover the same from CONTRACTOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0164",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 164,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 59073,
    "char_end": 59575,
    "char_count": 502,
    "text": "28.5 CONTRACTOR indemnifies OWNER/CONSULTANT against any claims from\nany person or persons engaged by CONTRACTOR in connection with WORK\nand in the event OWNER/CONSULTANT becomes directly liable for any\npayment consequent to breach or non-observance by CONTRACTOR of the\nprovisions hereof, such amounts shall be payable by CONTRACTOR to\nOWNER/CONSULTANT, AND OWNER/CONSULTANT may recover such dues\nfrom any amount receivable by CONTRACTOR under CONTRACT without\nprejudice to any other mode of recovery.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0165",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 165,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 59577,
    "char_end": 60107,
    "char_count": 530,
    "text": "28.6 In the event of  any  dispute  between  CONTRACTOR  and  persons engaged\nby CONTRACTOR at SITE, CONTRACTOR shall amicably resolve such\ndisputes in such a way that WORK can be proceeded with uninterruptedly. In the\nevent such disputes cannot be resolved in the above- said manner,\nCONTRACTOR shall immediately notify ENGINEER-IN- CHARGE of the\nexistence of such a dispute and the nature thereof; but CONTRACTOR shall\nhimself be responsible to take such measures as are necessary and permissible\nto have the situation resolved.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0166",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 166,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 60109,
    "char_end": 60333,
    "char_count": 224,
    "text": "28.7 CONTRACTOR may have access to OWNER'S qualified first-aid personnel and\nambulance in case of accidents where such facility is available. CONTRACTOR\nshall however provide a first-aid post for attending to minor injuries.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0167",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 167,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 60335,
    "char_end": 60424,
    "char_count": 89,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 26 of 46\n\nARTICLE-29 APPRENTICES ACT",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0168",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 168,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 60426,
    "char_end": 60600,
    "char_count": 174,
    "text": "29.1 CONTRACTOR shall comply with provisions of the Apprentices Act, 1961 and\nany amendments thereto as well as any Rules made or orders issued there\nunder from time to time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0169",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 169,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 60602,
    "char_end": 60812,
    "char_count": 210,
    "text": "29.2 CONTRACTOR shall submit to OWNER / CONSULTANT periodically statement\ngiving the number of workmen engaged by CONTRACTOR in each category and\nthe number of apprentices engaged in the corresponding category.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0170",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 170,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 60814,
    "char_end": 61227,
    "char_count": 413,
    "text": "ARTICLE–30 WARRANTY AND MAINTENANCE PERIOD\n\n30.1 CONTRACTOR warrants that WORK will be carried out in full conformity with\ndrawings, designs and specifications provided by OWNER/CONSULTANT, in\ncompliance with applicable statutory regulations for the time being in force, in\naccordance with recognized standards and codes of practice, as per good\nengineering practice and in a professional and workman-like manner.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0171",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 171,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 61229,
    "char_end": 62185,
    "char_count": 956,
    "text": "30.2 In the event of any defect being noticed in the quality or workmanship of WORK\nor any part thereof or any material provided and used by CONTRACTOR in\nWORK, within a period twelve (12) months from the date if issue of completion\ncertificate by OWNER/CONSULTANT it shall be rectified or replaced by\nCONTRACTOR at his own expense as deemed necessary by the Engineer-in-\nCharge. If CONTRACTOR fails to do so within reasonable period or if in the\nopinion of OWNER/CONSULTANT, CONTRACTOR is unable to do so, or the\nrepair / replacement cannot wait till CONTRACTOR is able to do it,\nOWNER/CONSULTANT may either directly or through such other agencies as\nOWNER/CONSULTANT may deem fit, get defective part of WORK made good,\nall at the risk and cost of CONTRACTOR. Notwithstanding the period specified\nabove, in case of civil constructions, the period of warranty will extend at least up\nto the end of first monsoon after the WORK is taken over videArticle-21.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0172",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 172,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 62187,
    "char_end": 62289,
    "char_count": 102,
    "text": "30.3 An item of WORK so repaired or replaced shall carry a further warranty as per\nArticle-30.2 above.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0173",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 173,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 62291,
    "char_end": 62617,
    "char_count": 326,
    "text": "30.4 During the period of warranty, CONTRACTOR'S representative shall be available\nat SITE or at such place from where he can come to SITE immediately on\nrequest\nby\nOWNER/CONSULTANT\nand\nhe\nshall\nbe\nauthorized\nby\nCONTRACTOR to carry out any repairs or maintenance as CONTRACTOR is\nobliged to carry out under the above warranty.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0174",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 174,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 62619,
    "char_end": 62990,
    "char_count": 371,
    "text": "30.5 CONTRACTOR shall not be liable for any defect owing to defective design,\nspecifications, drawings or information provided by OWNER/CONSULTANT in\nwriting based on which WORK has been executed or to defective EQUIPMENT\nor material provided by OWNER/CONSULTANT or to improper use of WORK by\nOWNER/CONSULTANT. Normal wear and tear shall not be treated as defect in\nWORK.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0175",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 175,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 62992,
    "char_end": 63130,
    "char_count": 138,
    "text": "30.6 On expiry of the said warranty period or on completion of CONTRACTOR'S\n\nGENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 27 of 46",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0176",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 176,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 63132,
    "char_end": 63448,
    "char_count": 316,
    "text": "obligations under the warranty, whichever is later, OWNER/CONSULTANT shall\nissue to CONTRACTOR a Discharge Certificate, stating that CONTRACTOR is\ndischarged of these warranties and release any amounts retained or other form of\nsecurity held by OWNER/CONSULTANT in lieu of security by CONTRACTOR for said\nwarranties.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0177",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 177,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 63450,
    "char_end": 63624,
    "char_count": 174,
    "text": "ARTICLE-31 GUARANTEE FOR TIME SCHEDULE & CONTRACT PRICE REDUCTION\n\n31.1 CONTRACTOR guarantees that WORK will be executed as per time schedule\nagreed to herein vide Article-4.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0178",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 178,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 63626,
    "char_end": 64780,
    "char_count": 1154,
    "text": "31.2 In the event of any delay in completion of WORK or part thereof as per agreed\nschedule, due to reasons other than those specifically exempted vide Articles-\n15.7, 32.2 and 40.3 hereof, OWNER/CONSULTANT may deduct from the\nconsiderations due to CONTRACTOR under CONTRACT or otherwise recover\nfrom CONTRACTOR, a sum calculated at half of one percent (0.5%) of the\nContract Price due to CONTRACTOR for the portion of WORK agreed to be\ncarried out by CONTRACTOR till the date on which the delayed item is due to be\ncompleted, for each week of delay, subject to a maximum of seven and a half\n(7.5%) percent of total Contract Price. Any payments recovered from\nCONTRACTOR for delays in earlier stages of WORK shall be reduced from the\nsums due under this Article-31.2. It is understood and agreed that such amounts\ndue represent the losses suffered by OWNER/CONSULTANT because of delay\nin\nWORK\nby\nCONTRACTOR\nand\nit\nshall\nnot\nbe\nnecessary\nfor\nOWNER/CONSULTANT to establish the actual amount of losses suffered,\nirrespective of whether the WORK or part thereof could be put to any use by\nOWNER/CONSULTANT had it been completed by CONTRACTOR as per\nschedule.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0179",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 179,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 64782,
    "char_end": 65002,
    "char_count": 220,
    "text": "31.3 For the purposes of Article-31.2 completion of WORK or part thereof shall mean\ntaking over by OWNER/CONSULTANT of WORK or part thereof (as is\napplicable) after satisfactory completion of tests vide Article-21hereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0180",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 180,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 65004,
    "char_end": 65487,
    "char_count": 483,
    "text": "ARTICLE-32 DELAY BY CONSULTANT\n\n32.1 In case of any delay in supply by OWNER/CONSULTANT of Designs and\nDrawings, EQUIPMENT, materials, Construction Equipment, Power and water for\nconstruction and/or any other item to be supplied by OWNER / CONSULTANT as\nper CONTRACT, or in the interruption of supply thereof, CONTRACTOR shall be\ninformed in advance of such delay, wherever possible, and CONTRACTOR shall\nre-schedule WORK in such a manner that no infructuous expenditure is incurred.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0181",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 181,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 65489,
    "char_end": 65827,
    "char_count": 338,
    "text": "32.2 In case delay by OWNER/CONSULTANT is of a substantial nature and has\naffected WORK or part thereof in such a manner that it cannot be proceeded with\nas per agreed schedule, the time-schedule for the part so affected shall be\nextended correspondingly. Decision of ENGINEER-IN-CHARGE shall be final in\nrespect of any extension of time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0182",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 182,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 65829,
    "char_end": 65985,
    "char_count": 156,
    "text": "32.3 In any case CONTRACTOR shall not be entitled for any financial\ncompensation or increase in Contract Price in consequence of such delay or interruption.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0183",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 183,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 65987,
    "char_end": 66091,
    "char_count": 104,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 28 of 46\n\nARTICLE-33 SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0184",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 184,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 66093,
    "char_end": 66403,
    "char_count": 310,
    "text": "33.1 The Special Conditions of CONTRACT specified vide SCHEDULE-Q hereof shall\nform part of CONTRACT; and wherever the provisions under Special Conditions\nof CONTRACT are in conflict with any of the provisions vide Article-2 to Article-48\nhereof, provisions in the Special Conditions of Contract shall prevail.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0185",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 185,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 66405,
    "char_end": 66600,
    "char_count": 195,
    "text": "33.2 Definitions vide Article-1 hereof shall apply to special Conditions of contract also\nand any supplementary Definitions given therein need not necessarily apply to\nother sections of CONTRACT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0186",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 186,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 66602,
    "char_end": 66865,
    "char_count": 263,
    "text": "ARTICLE-34 SUB-LETTING AND ASSIGNMENT\n\n34.1 CONTRACT shall be binding and inure to the benefit of the parties hereto and to\ntheir successors in right and shall not be assignable by either unless the other\nparty has given its consent in writing to such assignment.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0187",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 187,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 66867,
    "char_end": 67514,
    "char_count": 647,
    "text": "34.2 CONTRACTOR shall not sub-let or sub-contract any or all of its obligations under\nCONTRACT\nto\nany\nother\nparty\nwithout\nprior\nwritten\nconsent\nof\nOWNER/CONSULTANT. In the event of CONTRACTOR sub-letting the WORK\nor part thereof to any other party or engaging any sub-contractor,\nCONTRACTOR shall still be responsible to OWNER/CONSULTANT for\nperformance of the whole CONTRACT and shall ensure that such other party to\nwhom WORK or part thereof is sub-let or sub-contracted perform the portion of\nWORK so sub-let or sub-contracted as per provisions herein and the persons\nemployed at SITE by such other party shall be deemed employed by\nCONTRACTOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0188",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 188,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 67516,
    "char_end": 67737,
    "char_count": 221,
    "text": "ARTICLE-35 CLAIMS\n\n35.1  Claims by CONTRACTOR for any disputed items shall be lodged with\nENGINEER-IN-CHARGE within thirty (30) days of disallowance of the same\nfailing which the claim shall be deemed to have been waived.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0189",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 189,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 67739,
    "char_end": 68050,
    "char_count": 311,
    "text": "ARTICLE-36 PATENTS\n\n36.1 OWNER/CONSULTANT warrant on their part that any design or instruction given\nby OWNER/CONSULTANT shall not be such as will cause CONTRACTOR to\ninfringe any Letters of Patent, Registered Designs, Trade Marks, Copy-right or\nother protected right valid in India, in the performance of WORK.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0190",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 190,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 68052,
    "char_end": 68750,
    "char_count": 698,
    "text": "36.2 Subject to Article-36.1 CONTRACTOR indemnifies OWNER/CONSULTANT\nagainst any claim for infringement by CONTRACTOR of any Letters of Patent\nRegistered Design, Registered trade mark of Copy-right or other protected right valid in\nIndia in performance of CONTRACT. In the event of any action being brought against or\nclaims or demands being made on OWNER / CONSULTANT because of any\ninfringement or alleged infringement by CONTRACTOR of any of the said rights,\nCONTRACTOR shall immediately be notified of the same and CONTRACTOR shall\nwithin a reasonable period of time and at its own cost, make such modifications in\nWORK as would make it non-infringing upon any such rights or any such claims or",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0191",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 191,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 68752,
    "char_end": 69310,
    "char_count": 558,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 29 of 46\n\ndemands or otherwise procure for OWNER/CONSULTANT such rights as would enable\nOWNER/CONSULTANT to continue with the use of WORK without infringement of such\nrights. OWNER/CONSULTANT shall not settle such action or satisfy or compromise any\nsuch claims without the written consent of CONTRACTOR and in the event of any such\ninfringement or alleged infringement leading to litigation CONTRACTOR shall conduct\nthe same and OWNER/CONSULTANT shall co-operate with CONTRACTOR in all\nreasonable manner.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0192",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 192,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 69312,
    "char_end": 70306,
    "char_count": 994,
    "text": "ARTICLE-37 SECRECY\n\n37.1 All drawings, designs, specifications, and other documents and information\ncontained herein and any instruction given by OWNER/CONSULTANT in the\nperformance of CONTRACT, whether patented or patentable or not, shall always\nremain the exclusive property of OWNER/CONSULTANT and CONTRACTOR at\nno time shall question or dispute such right of OWNER/CONSULTANT. For a\nperiod of fifteen (15) years from the DATE OF CONTRACT, CONTRACTOR shall\nkeep the above documents and information and the knowledge that\nOWNER/CONSULTANT'S employees information contained in said documents\nfor PROJECT as secret and confidential and shall not reproduce them or divulge\nthem\nto\nany\nthird-party\nwithout\nthe\nspecific\nwritten\napproval\nof\nOWNER/CONSULTANT and shall not use them for any purpose other than those\ncovered by the intents of CONTRACT. Such documents are given on loan by\nOWNER/CONSULTANT to CONTRACTOR for the limited purpose of execution\nof WORK and are subject to return on demand.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0193",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 193,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 70308,
    "char_end": 70524,
    "char_count": 216,
    "text": "37.2 CONTRACTOR shall not publish or cause to be published any information on\nPROJECT,\nCONTRACT\nand\nWORK\ncovered\nby\nCONTRACT\nor\nCONTRACTOR'S participation in it without the prior written consent of OWNER\n/CONSULTANT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0194",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 194,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 70526,
    "char_end": 70631,
    "char_count": 105,
    "text": "37.3 The provisions of this article shall survive expiry or earlier termination /\nsuspension of CONTRACT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0195",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 195,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 70633,
    "char_end": 71091,
    "char_count": 458,
    "text": "ARTICLE-38 NON-WAIVER\n\n38.1  Any failure by either party at any time, or from time to time to enforce or  require\nstrict observance performance of any of the terms and conditions of CONTRACT,\nor to exercise any rights hereunder, shall not constitute a waiver\nofsuchtermsandconditionsorrights,unlesssuchrightshavelapsedunderspecific\nprovisions elsewhere in CONTRACT, and shall not affect or impair same or the\nright of either party any time to avail the same.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0196",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 196,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 71093,
    "char_end": 71323,
    "char_count": 230,
    "text": "AR TICLE-39 LANGUAGE & UNITS\n\n39.1  CONTRACT is drawn up in the English Language. All correspondence  between\nthe parties in performance of CONTRACT shall be in the English Language.\nMetric system of measurement shall be followed.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0197",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 197,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 71325,
    "char_end": 71418,
    "char_count": 93,
    "text": "ARTICLE-40 FORCE MAJEURE\n\n40.1 Neither CONTRACTOR nor OWNER/CONSULTANT shall be considered in",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0198",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 198,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 71420,
    "char_end": 71861,
    "char_count": 441,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 30 of 46\n\ndefault in performance of CONTRACT if such performance is prevented or\ndelayed due to circumstances of force Majeure provided that the party so\naffected notifies the other in writing promptly, in any case within fifteen (15) days\nof its occurrence, of the existence of a situation of Force Majeure giving evidence\nthere for. For the purposes of this Article Force Majeure means:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0199",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 199,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 71863,
    "char_end": 71985,
    "char_count": 122,
    "text": "i)\nWar or hostilities\n\nii)\nRiot or civil commotion\n\niii) Earthquake, flood, tempest, lightning or other natural calamities",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0200",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 200,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 71987,
    "char_end": 72081,
    "char_count": 94,
    "text": "iv) Accident, fire or explosion on SITE not caused by willful negligence of\nCONTRACTOR, and/or",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0201",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 201,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 72083,
    "char_end": 72211,
    "char_count": 128,
    "text": "v)\nLabour strike or lock-out exceeding ten (10) days in duration not caused by\nany deliberate act of indiscretion by CONTRACTOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0202",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 202,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 72213,
    "char_end": 72702,
    "char_count": 489,
    "text": "40.2 If the situation of Force Majeure extends for a period exceeding thirty (30) days\nthe parties shall meet together and discuss the further course of action, provided\nthat if CONTRACTOR'S performance is affected OWNER / CONSULTANT may\nat his option and at any time remove from the scope of CONTRACTOR the\nportion of WORK so affected and have it executed by any other agency as\nOWNER/CONSULTANT may deem fit and reduce from the consideration\npayable to CONTRACTOR a proportionate amount.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0203",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 203,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 72704,
    "char_end": 73074,
    "char_count": 370,
    "text": "40.3 CONTRACTOR shall be entitled for extension of time-schedule vide Article-4 for\nthe performance of the portion of WORK affected by the situation of Force\nMajeure by a reasonable period but shall not be entitled to any financial\ncompensation such as idle wages or escalation in cost. Decision by ENGINEER-\nIN-CHARGE shall be final in respect of any extension of time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0204",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 204,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 73076,
    "char_end": 73729,
    "char_count": 653,
    "text": "ARTICLE-41 SETTLEMENT OF DISPUTES AND ARBITRATION\n\n41.1  If any dispute (s) arises out of or in connection with this contract, or in respect  of\nany defined legal relationship associated therewith or derived there from, the\nparties agree to submit the disputes to arbitration under the ICADR(International\nCentre for Alternative Dispute Resolution) Arbitration Rules 1996. The authority\nto appoint the Arbitrator shall be the International Centre for Alternative Dispute\nResolution. The number of Arbitrator shall be one and the language of the\narbitration proceedings shall be English. The place of arbitration proceedings\nshall be Ernakulam in Kerala.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0205",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 205,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 73731,
    "char_end": 73833,
    "char_count": 102,
    "text": "ARTICLE-42 LAW AND LEGAL JURISDICTION\n\n42.1 CONTRACT shall be governed and construed by Laws of India.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0206",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 206,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 73835,
    "char_end": 73978,
    "char_count": 143,
    "text": "42.2 Any legal proceedings relating to CONTRACT shall be limited to courts of law\nunder the jurisdiction of the Kerala High Court at Ernakulam.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0207",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 207,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 73980,
    "char_end": 74080,
    "char_count": 100,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 31 of 46\n\nARTICLE-43 SUSPENSION AND TERMINATION",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0208",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 208,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 74082,
    "char_end": 74365,
    "char_count": 283,
    "text": "43.1 In the event OWNER/CONSULTANT is unable or unwilling to complete or is\ncompelled to postpone its activities relating to PROJECT at any stage during the\ncurrency of CONTRACT, OWNER/CONSULTANT may either suspend or\nterminate CONTRACT by giving CONTRACTOR thirty (30) days’ notice.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0209",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 209,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 74367,
    "char_end": 75443,
    "char_count": 1076,
    "text": "43.2 If CONTRACTOR shall fail or neglect to execute work with all due diligence and\nexpedition or shall refuse or neglect to comply with any reasonable orders given\nto him in writing by OWNER/CONSULTANT in connection with work or shall\notherwise\ncommit breach\nof any of the provisions of CONTRACT,\nOWNER/CONSULTANT may give CONTRACTOR notice in writing requiring to\nmake good such failure, neglect or breach. Should CONTRACTOR fail to comply\nwith the notice within the time specified therein, then OWNER/CONSULTANT\nshall, without prejudice to other rights of OWNER/CONSULTANT under\nCONTRACT, be at liberty to have such WORK or portion of WORK as\nCONTRACTOR has failed or neglected to execute, executed directly or through\nany other agency OWNER/CONSULTANT deems fit at the risk and cost of\nCONTRACTOR; and OWNER/CONSULTANT shall have the free use of all of\nCONTRACTOR'S equipment, materials and other things for the time being\navailable at SITE for getting the WORK completed in the above-said manner to\nthe exclusion of any right of CONTRACTOR for fair wear and tear thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0210",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 210,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 75445,
    "char_end": 75861,
    "char_count": 416,
    "text": "OWNER/CONSULTANT shall further be entitled to apply the proceeds of such\nequipment and unused materials of CONTRACTOR and any balance amount\nthat may be due to CONTRACTOR for WORK actually executed towards any\nclaims on OWNER/CONSULTANT from third parties in consequence of failure,\nneglect, refusal or contravention by CONTRACTOR and / or towards any\nexpense that OWNER/CONSULTANT might have incurred in getting the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0211",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 211,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 75863,
    "char_end": 75990,
    "char_count": 127,
    "text": "WORK completed in the above-said manner, in excess of what OWNER /\nCONSULTANT would have had to pay CONTRACTOR as per CONTRACT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0212",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 212,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 75992,
    "char_end": 76341,
    "char_count": 349,
    "text": "43.3 If CONTRACTOR shall become bankrupt or insolvent or have a receiving order\nmade against him or shall compound with his creditors or shall commence to be\nwound up otherwise than for the purpose of reconstruction or shall carry on its\nbusiness under a Receiver for the benefit of its creditors, OWNER/CONSULTANT may\nat its sole discretion either;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0213",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 213,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 76343,
    "char_end": 76635,
    "char_count": 292,
    "text": "a) terminate CONTRACT forthwith by notice in writing to CONTRACTOR or the\nReceiver or the Liquidator or to any other person in whom the CONTRACT\nmay become rested and have the remaining WORK executed at the risk and\ncost of CONTRACTOR in the same manner as specified in Article-43.2\nabove ,or",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0214",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 214,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 76637,
    "char_end": 76872,
    "char_count": 235,
    "text": "b) give such Receiver, Liquidator or other person as aforesaid the option of\ncarrying out the CONTRACT subject to his providing security for the due and\nfaithful performance of CONTRACT up to such amount as may be mutually\nagreed upon.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0215",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 215,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 76874,
    "char_end": 78166,
    "char_count": 1292,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 32 of 46\n\n43.4 In the event of suspension of CONTRACT vide Article-43.1 above, immediately\non receipt of notice therefore from OWNER/CONSULTANT, CONTRACTOR\nshall suspend all activities at SITE expect those essentially to be carried out to\nsafe-guard and secure WORK for the time being in progress in a safe manner\nwithout\nwastage\nof\nmaterials\nand\ntemporarily\ndisband\nor\nreassign\nCONTRACTOR'S workmen except those essentially required at SITE such as for\nsecurity of CONTRACTOR'S equipments and materials. CONTRACTOR shall re-\nmobilise its workmen and re-commence WORK within fifteen (15) days of receipt\nof notice from OWNER/CONSULTANT requiring CONTRACTOR to do so. All\ncosts reasonably incurred by CONTRACTOR in connection with temporarily\nwinding up WORK, maintenance of SITE during period of suspension and\nremobilisation on\nwithdrawal\nof\nsuspension\norder\nshall be\npaid\nby\nOWNER/CONSULTANT in addition to Contract Price specified herein, and the\namount of such additional sum shall be mutually agreed to between the parties\nbase on detailed information provided by CONTRACTOR. CONTRACTOR shall\nfurther be entitled for extension of time- schedule corresponding to the period of\nsuspension including permitted period for re-mobilisation.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0216",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 216,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 78168,
    "char_end": 79221,
    "char_count": 1053,
    "text": "43.5 In the event of termination of CONTRACT vide Article-43.1 above, immediately\non receipt of notice therefore from OWNER/CONSULTANT, CONTRACTOR\nshall take all steps for winding up work such as cancellation of any pending\norders and termination of any sub-contracts that CONTRACTOR might have\nentered into with others in connection with WORK, safe-guarding and securing of\nany WORK in progress in a safe manner, disbanding of workmen, removal of\ntemporary construction made by CONTRACTOR at SITE and return of all\nEQUIPMENT,\nspecial\ntools,\nun-used\nmaterials\nand\ndocuments\nthat\nOWNER/CONSULTANT\nhas\nsupplied\nto\nCONTRACTOR.\nOWNER/CONSULTANT shall pay CONTRACTOR for the portion of WORK\nexecuted till such termination less amounts already paid, together with any\nreasonable cost necessarily incurred by CONTRACTOR pursuant to such\ntermination as may be mutually agreed upon between the parties hereto based\non detailed information provided by CONTRACTOR. CONTRACTOR shall not be\nentitled for any payment in respect of the portion of WORK left unexecuted.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0217",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 217,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 79223,
    "char_end": 79453,
    "char_count": 230,
    "text": "43.6 Upon termination of CONTRACT for any reason, obligations of the parties hereto\nshall cease except for the liabilities of either party to the other in respect of\nobligations that accrued prior to, the date of such termination.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0218",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 218,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 79455,
    "char_end": 79758,
    "char_count": 303,
    "text": "ARTICLE-44 RECOVERY OF DUES FROM CONTRACTOR\n\n44.1 OWNER/CONSULTANT shall have recourse to CONTRACTOR for any costs,\nclaims, demands, proceedings, damages and expenses whatsoever arising out\nof or in connection with any failure of CONTRACTOR to perform any of his\nobligations under the terms of CONTRACT.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0219",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 219,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 79760,
    "char_end": 79988,
    "char_count": 228,
    "text": "44.2 Any amount due from CONTRACTOR as per CONTRACT shall be deducted\nfrom money due or becoming due to CONTRACTOR under CONTRACT or\nunder any other account or may be recovered by arbitration vide Article-41 or by\naction at law.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0220",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 220,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 79990,
    "char_end": 80084,
    "char_count": 94,
    "text": "GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\nMM/172/E21051\nR0\nPage 33 of 46\n\nARTICLE-45 CONSEQUENTIAL LOSSES",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0221",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 221,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 80086,
    "char_end": 80189,
    "char_count": 103,
    "text": "45.1 Liabilities of either party to the other are limited to  those  specifically  provided\nfor herein.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0222",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "paragraph_index": 222,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 80191,
    "char_end": 80480,
    "char_count": 289,
    "text": "45.2 Neither\nOWNER/CONSULTANT\nnor\nCONTRACTOR\nshall\nunder\nany\ncircumstances be liable in respect of any in direct or consequential loss or  loss\nof business or loss of profit suffered by the other party in connection with or\narising out of CONTRACT except as specified in Article-31 hereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0223",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
