    "char_end": 13787,
    "char_count": 106,
    "text": "E7\n\nwith the entire works or any portion thereof without priorwritten approval of the Engineer-\nin-charge.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0042",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 42,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 13789,
    "char_end": 15430,
    "char_count": 1641,
    "text": "When the contractor has made himself liable for action under any of the cases aforesaid, the\nEngineer-in-charge on behalf of the President of India/Director, NIT Megha;aya shall have powers:\na) To determine the contract as aforesaid (of which termination notice in writing to thecontractor\nunder the hand of the Engineer-in-charge shall be conclusive evidence).Upon such\ndetermination, Performance Guarantee under the contract shall be liableto be forfeited and\nshall be absolutely at the disposal of the Government.\nb) After giving notice to the contractor to measure up the work of the contractor and totake such\nwhole, or the balance or part thereof, as shall be un-executed out of hishands and to give it\nto another contractor to complete the work. The contractor,whose contract is determined as\nabove, shall not be allowed to participate in thetendering process for the balance work.\nIn the event of above courses being adopted by the Engineer-in-charge, the contractor shall have no\nclaim to compensation for any loss sustained by him by reasons of his having purchased or\nprocured any materials or entered into any engagements or made any advances on account or with\na view to the execution of the work or the performance of the contract. And in case action is taken\nunder any of the provision aforesaid, the contractor shall not be entitled to recover or be paid any\nsum for any work thereof or actually performed under the contract unless and until the Engineer-in-\ncharge has certified in writing the performance of such work and the value payable in respect thereof\nand he shall only be entitled to be paid the value so certified.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0043",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 43,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 15432,
    "char_end": 16088,
    "char_count": 656,
    "text": "CLAUSE 3A\nCLOSING OF CONTRACT BY EITHER PARTY\nIn case the work cannot be started due to reasons not within the control of the contractor within 1/8th\nof the stipulated time for completion of work or one month whichever is higher, either party may\nclose the contract. In case contractor wants to close the contract, he shall give notice to the\ndepartment stating the failure on the part of department. In such eventuality, the Performance\nGuarantee of the contractor shall be refunded within following time limits, without any interest. The\ncontractor will not be eligible for any compensation for any damages what so ever caused due to\nclosing of contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0044",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 44,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 16090,
    "char_end": 16227,
    "char_count": 137,
    "text": "If the Tendered value of work is,\nupto Rs. 45 lac : 15 days.\nmore than Rs.45 lac& upto Rs.2.5 Cr : 21 days.\nexceeds Rs. 2.5 Cr : 30 days.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0045",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 45,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 16229,
    "char_end": 16323,
    "char_count": 94,
    "text": "CLAUSE 4\nCONTRACTORS REMAIN LIABLE TO PAY COMPENSATION, EVEN IF ACTION NOTTAKEN\nUNDER CLAUSE 3",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0046",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 46,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 16325,
    "char_end": 17312,
    "char_count": 987,
    "text": "In any case in which any of the power conferred upon the Engineer-in-charge by clause-3 thereof\nshall have become exercisable and the same shall not be exercised, the non-exercise hereof shall\nnot construe a waiver of any of the conditions hereof and such powers shall not be withstanding\nexercisable in the event of any future case of default by the contractor and the liability of the\nContractor for compensation shall remain unaffected (for which by any clause or clause hereof, he is\ndeclared liable to pay compensation amounting to the extent of his security deposit and the liability\nof the Contractor for past and future compensations shall remain unaffected). In the event of the\nEngineer-in-charge putting in force all or any of the powers vested in him under the preceding\nclauses he may, if he so desires after giving a notice in writing to the Contractor, take possession of\n(or at the sole discretion of Engineer-in-charge which shall be final) use as on hire (the amount of",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0047",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 47,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 17314,
    "char_end": 18541,
    "char_count": 1227,
    "text": "E8\n\nthe hire money being also in the final determination of the Engineer-in-charge) all or any tools, plant,\nmaterials and stores in or upon the words or the site then of belongings to the Contractor or\nprocured by the Contractor and intended to be used for the execution of the work or any part thereof\npaying or allowing for the same in account at the contract rates, or in case of these not being\napplicable at current market rates to be certified by the Engineer-in-charge whose certificate thereof\nshall be final, otherwise the Engineer-incharge may by notice in writing to the Contractor or his clerk\nof the works, foreman or authorised agents requesting him/them to remove such tools, plant,\nmaterials or stores from the premises (within a time to be specified in such notice) and in the event\nof the\nContractor failing to comply with any such requisition, the Engineer-in-charge may remove them at\nthe Contractor’s expenses or sell by auction or private sale on account of the Contractor and at his\nrisk in all respects and the certificate of the Engineer-in-charge as to the expenses of any such\nremoval and the amount of the proceeds and expenses of any such sale shall be final and\nconclusive against the Contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0048",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 48,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 18543,
    "char_end": 19142,
    "char_count": 599,
    "text": "CLAUSE 5\nTIME AND EXTENSION FOR DELAY\nThe time allowed for execution of the Works as specified in the Schedule ‘F’ or the extended time in\naccordance with these conditions shall be the essence of the Contract. The execution of the works\nshall commence from such time period as mentioned in schedule ‘F’ or from the date of handing\nover of the site whichever is later. If the Contractor commits default in commencing the execution of\nthe work as aforesaid, Government shall without prejudice to any other right or remedy available in\nlaw, be at liberty to forfeit thePerformance Guarantee absolutely.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0049",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 49,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 19144,
    "char_end": 20250,
    "char_count": 1106,
    "text": "5.1As soon as possible after the Contract is concluded, the Contractor shall submit aTime and\nProgress Chart for each mile stone and get it approved by the Department. The Chart shall be\nprepared in direct relation to the time stated in theContract documents for completion of items of the\nworks. It shall indicate theforecast of the dates of commencement and completion of various trades\nofsections of the work and may be amended as necessary by agreement between theEngineer-in-\nCharge and the Contractor within the limitations of time imposed inthe Contract documents, and\nfurther to ensure good progress during the execution of the work, the contractor shall in all cases in\nwhich the time allowed for any work,exceeds one month (save for special jobs for which a separate\nprogramme hasbeen agreed upon) complete the work as per mile stones given in Schedule ‘ F’.\na) Project Management shall be done by using project management software forworks costing more\nthan Rs.5 Crore.\nb) The project management shall be done using MS Project software for works costingmore than Rs.\n5 Crore and up to Rs. 20 Cr.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0050",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 50,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 20252,
    "char_end": 20351,
    "char_count": 99,
    "text": "For works costing more than Rs. 20 Crore, project management shall be done usingPrimavera\nSoftware.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0051",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 51,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 20353,
    "char_end": 20993,
    "char_count": 640,
    "text": "Programme Chart\n(i)\nThe Contractor shall prepare an integrated programme chart in MSProject/Primavera\nsoftware for the execution of work, showing clearly all activitiesfrom the start of work to\ncompletion, with details of manpower, equipment &machinery required for the fulfillment\nof the programme within the stipulated periodor earlier and submit the same for approval\nto the Engineer-in-Charge within tendays of award of the contract. A recovery of Rs.\n2500/- (for works costing upto Rs.20Crores)/ Rs. 5000/- (for works costing more than Rs.\n20 Crores) shall be made onper day basis in case of delay in submission of the above\nprogramme.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0052",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 52,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 20995,
    "char_end": 21757,
    "char_count": 762,
    "text": "E9\n\n(ii)\nThe programme chart should include the following:\n\na) Descriptive note explaining sequence of the various activities.\nb)  Network (PERT/CPM/BAR CHART).\nc) Programme of procurement of machinery/equipments having adequate capacity,\ncommensurate with the quantum of work to be done within the stipulated period,by\nthe contractor. In addition to above to achieve the progress of Work as\nperprogramme, the contractor must bring at site adequate shuttering materialrequired\nfor cement, Concrete and R.C.C. works etc. for three floors within onemonth from the\ndate of start of work till the completion of RCC work as perrequirement of work. The\ncontractor shall submit shuttering schedule adequateto complete structure work\nwithin laid down physical milestone.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0053",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 53,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 21759,
    "char_end": 23170,
    "char_count": 1411,
    "text": "(iii)\nIf at any time, it appears to the Engineer-in-Charge that the actual progress of workdoes\nnot conform to the approved programme referred above or after reschedulingof\nmilestones, the contractor shall produce a revised programme within 7 (seven)days,\nshowing the modifications to the approved programme to ensure timelycompletion of the\nwork . The modified schedule of programme shall be approved bythe Engineer in Charge.\nA recovery of Rs. 2500/-(for works costing upto Rs. 20Crores)/Rs. 5000/- (for works\ncosting more than Rs. 20 Crores) shall be made onper day basis in case of delay in\nsubmission of the modified programme.\n(iv)\nThe submission for approval by the Engineer-in-Charge of such programme or\nsuchparticulars\nshall\nnot\nrelieve\nthe\ncontractor\nof\nany\nof\nthe\nduties\nor\nresponsibilitiesunder the contract. This is without prejudice to the right of Engineer-in-\nChargetotake action against the contractor as per terms and conditions of the agreement.\n(v)\nThe contractor shall submit the progress report using MS Project/Primavera softwarewith\nbase line programme referred above for the work done during previous monthto the\nEngineer-In-charge on or before 5thday of each month failing which arecovery Rs. 2500/-\n(for works costing upto Rs. 20 Crores)/Rs. 5000/-(for workscosting more than Rs. 20\nCrores) shall be made on per day basis in case of delay insubmission of the monthly\nprogress report.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0054",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 54,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 23172,
    "char_end": 23258,
    "char_count": 86,
    "text": "5.2If the work(s) be delayed by:\n\ni)\nforce majeure, or\n\nii)\nabnormally bad weather, or",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
