    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 23653,
    "char_end": 23751,
    "char_count": 98,
    "text": "(vii)\nnon-availability or break down of tools and Plant to be supplied or supplied\nbyGovernment or",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0059",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 59,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 23753,
    "char_end": 23876,
    "char_count": 123,
    "text": "E10\n\n(viii)\nAny other cause which, in the absolute discretion of the Engineer-in-Charge is\nbeyond the Contractor’s control.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0060",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 60,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 23878,
    "char_end": 24254,
    "char_count": 376,
    "text": "Then upon the happening of any such event causing delay, the contractor\nshallimmediately give notice thereof in writing to the authority as indicated in schedule 'F'\nbut shall nevertheless use constantly his best endeavors to prevent or make good\nthedelay and shall do all that may be reasonably required to the satisfaction of\ntheEngineer-in-charge to proceed with the works.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0061",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 61,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 24256,
    "char_end": 24614,
    "char_count": 358,
    "text": "5.3 Request for rescheduling of milestones and extension of time, to be eligible forconsideration,\nshall be made by the Contractor in writing within fourteen days of thehappening of the event causing\ndelay on the prescribed form Engineer-in-charge.The Contractor may also, if practicable, indicate in\nsuch a request the period for which extension is desired.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0062",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 62,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 24616,
    "char_end": 25206,
    "char_count": 590,
    "text": "5.4 In any such case, Engineer-in-charge may give a fair and reasonable extension oftime and\nreschedule the mile stones for completion of work. Such extension orrescheduling of the milestones\nshall be communicated to the Contractor by Engineer-in-charge in writing, within 3 months or 4\nweeks of the date of receipt of such requestrespectively. Non application by the contractor for\nextension of time/ rescheduling ofthe milestones shall not be a bar for giving a fair and reasonable\nextension/rescheduling of the milestones by Engineer-in-charge and this shall be binding on\nthecontractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0063",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 63,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 25208,
    "char_end": 25586,
    "char_count": 378,
    "text": "CLAUSE 6\nMEASUREMENT OF WORKDONE\nEngineer-in-charge shall, except as other wise provided, ascertain and determine bymeasurement,\nthe value in accordance with the contract of work done. All measurement ofall items having financial\nvalue shall be entered in Measurement Book and / or level fieldbook so that a complete record is\nobtained of all works performed under the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0064",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 64,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 25588,
    "char_end": 26855,
    "char_count": 1267,
    "text": "All measurements and levels shall be taken jointly by the Engineer-in-charge or hisauthorized\nrepresentative and by the contractor or his authorized representative from timeto time during the\nprogress of the work and such measurements shall be signed and datedby the Engineer-in-charge\nand the contractor or their representatives in token of theiracceptance. If the contractor objects to\nany of the measurements recorded, a note shall bemade to that effect with reason and signed by\nboth the parties.If for any reason the contractor or his authorized representative is not available and\nthework of recording measurements is suspended by the Engineer-in-charge or hisrepresentative,\nthe Engineer-in-charge and the Department shall not entertain any claimfrom contractor for any loss\nor damages on this account. If the contractor or his authorizedrepresentative does not remain\npresent at the time of such measurements after thecontractor or his authorized representative has\nbeen given a notice in writing three (3) daysin advance or fails to countersign or to record objection\nwithin a week from the date of themeasurement, then such measurements recorded in his absence\nby the Engineer-in-chargeor his representative shall be deemed to be accepted by the contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0065",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 65,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 26857,
    "char_end": 27601,
    "char_count": 744,
    "text": "The contractor shall, without extra charge, provide all assistance with every appliance,labour and\nother things necessary for measurements and recording levels.Except where any general or detailed\ndescription of the work expressly shows to thecontrary, measurements shall be taken in accordance\nwith the procedure set forth in thespecifications notwithstanding any provisions in the relevant\nStandard Method ofmeasurement or any general or local custom. In the case of items which are not\ncoveredby specifications, measurements shall be taken in accordance with the relevant\nstandardmethod of measurement issued by the Bureau of Indian Standards and if for any item\nnosuch standard is available, then a mutually agreed method shall be followed.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0066",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 66,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 27603,
    "char_end": 28575,
    "char_count": 972,
    "text": "E11\n\nThe contractor shall give, not less than seven days notice to the Engineer-in-Charge or\nhisauthorized representative in-charge of the work, before covering up or otherwise placingbeyond\nthe reach of measurement any work in order that the same may be measured andcorrect\ndimensions thereof be taken before the same covered up or placed beyond thereach of\nmeasurement and shall not cover up and place beyond reach of measurementany work without\nconsent in writing of the Engineer-in-charge or his authorizedrepresentative in-charge of the work\nwho shall within the aforesaid period of seven daysinspect the work, and if any work shall be\ncovered up or placed beyond the reach ofmeasurements without such notice having been given or\nthe Engineer-in-charge’s consentbeing obtained in writing, the same shall be uncovered at the\nContractor’s expense or indefault thereof no payment or allowance shall be made for such work or\nthe materials withwhich the same was executed.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0067",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 67,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 28577,
    "char_end": 29803,
    "char_count": 1226,
    "text": "Engineer-in-charge or his authorized representative may cause either themselves orthrough another\nofficer of the Department to check the measurements recorded jointly orotherwise as aforesaid and\nall provisions stipulated herein above shall be applicable tosuch checking of measurements or\nlevels.It is also a term of this contract that recording of measurements of any item of work in\nthemeasurement book and /or its payment in the interim, on account or final bill shall not\nbeconsidered as conclusive evidence as to the sufficiency of any work or material to which itrelates\nnor shall it relieve the contractor from liabilities from any over measurement ordefects noticed till\ncompletion of the defects liability period.\nDOS/ ISRO\nCLAUSE 6A\nCOMPUTERIZED MEASUREMENT BOOK\nEngineer-in-charge shall, except as other wise provided, ascertain and determine bymeasurement\nthe value of work done in accordance with the contract.All measurements of all items having\nfinancial value shall be entered by the contractor andcompiled in the shape of the Computerized\nMeasurement Book having pages of A04 sizeas per the format of the Department so that a complete\nrecord is obtained of all the items ofworks performed under the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0068",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 68,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 29805,
    "char_end": 30479,
    "char_count": 674,
    "text": "All such measurements and levels recorded by the contractor or his authorized representative from\ntime to time, during the progress of the work shall be got checked bythe contractor from the\nEngineer-in-charge or his authorized representative as per intervalor programme fixed in\nconsultation with Engineer-in-charge or his authorizedrepresentative. After the necessary\ncorrections made by the Engineer-in-charge, themeasurement sheets shall be returned to the\ncontractor for incorporating the correctionsand for resubmission to the Engineer-in-charge for the\ndated signature by the Engineer-in-chargeand the contractor or their representatives in token of their\nacceptance.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0069",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 69,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 30481,
    "char_end": 31123,
    "char_count": 642,
    "text": "Whenever\nbill\nis\ndue\nfor\npayment,\nthe\ncontractor\nwould\ninitially\nsubmit\ndraft\ncomputerizedmeasurement sheets and these measurements would be got checked/ test checked\nfromthe Engineer-in-charge and /or his authorized representative. The contractor will,thereafter,\nincorporate such changes as may be done during these checks/test checks inhis draft computerized\nmeasurements, and submit to the Institute a computerizedmeasurement book, duly bound, and with\nits pages machine numbered. The Engineer-in-chargeand/or his authorized representative would\nthereafter check this MB, and record thenecessary certificates for their checks/test checks.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0070",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 70,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 31125,
    "char_end": 31509,
    "char_count": 384,
    "text": "The final, fair, computerized measurement book given by the contractor, duly bound, withits pages\nmachine numbered, should be 100% correct, and no cutting or over writing in themeasurements\nwould thereafter be allowed. If at all any error is noticed, the contractorshall have to submit a fresh\ncomputerized MB with its pages duly machine numbered andbound after getting the earlier MB",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0071",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 71,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 31511,
    "char_end": 31930,
    "char_count": 419,
    "text": "E12\n\ncancelled by the Institute. Thereafter, the MB shallbe taken in the Engineering Section Office\nrecords, and allotted a number as per the Register ofComputerized MBs. This should be done\nbefore the corresponding bill is submitted to theAccounts Section for payment. The contractor shall\nsubmit two spare copies of suchcomputerized MBs for the purpose of reference and record by the\nvarious officers of theInstitute.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0072",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 72,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 31932,
    "char_end": 32344,
    "char_count": 412,
    "text": "The contractor shall also submit to the Institute separately his computerized Abstract ofCost and bill\nbased on these measurements, duly bound, and its pages machine numberedalong with two spare\ncopies of the ‘bill’. Thereafter, this bill will be processed by  Engineering Section Office and allotted a\nnumber as per the computerized record in the same way as done forthe measurement book meant\nfor measurements.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0073",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 73,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 32346,
    "char_end": 33133,
    "char_count": 787,
    "text": "The contractor shall, without extra charge, provide all assistance with every appliance,labour and\nother things necessary for checking of measurements/levels by the Engineer-in-chargeor his\nrepresentative.Except where any general or detailed description of the work expressly shows to\nthecontrary, measurements shall be taken in accordance with the procedure set forth in\nthespecifications notwithstanding any provision in the relevant Standard Method ofmeasurement or\nany general or local custom. In the case of items which are not coveredby specifications,\nmeasurement shall be taken in accordance with the relevant standardmethod of measurement\nissued by the Bureau of Indian Standards and if for any item nosuch standard is available, then a\nmutually agreed method shall be followed.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0074",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 74,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 33135,
    "char_end": 34216,
    "char_count": 1081,
    "text": "The contractor shall give not less than seven days notice to the Engineer-in-charge or hisauthorized\nrepresentative in charge of the work before covering up or otherwise placingbeyond the reach of\nchecking and /or test checking the measurement of any work in orderthat the same may be checked\nand /or test checked and correct dimensions thereof betaken before the same is covered up or\nplaced beyond the reach of checking and /or testchecking measurement and shall not cover up and\nplace beyond reach of measurementany work without consent in writing of the Engineer-in-charge or\nhis authorizedrepresentative in-charge of the work who shall within the aforesaid period of seven\ndaysinspect the work, and if any work shall be covered or placed beyond the reach of\ncheckingand/or test checking measurements without such notice having been given or theEngineer-\nin-charge’s consent being obtained in writing the same shall be uncovered at theContractor’s\nexpense, or default thereof no payment or allowance shall be made for suchwork or the materials\nwith which the same was executed.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0075",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 75,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 34218,
    "char_end": 34940,
    "char_count": 722,
    "text": "Engineer-in-charge or his authorized representative may cause either themselves orthrough another\nofficer of the Institute to check the measurements recorded bycontractor and all provisions stipulated\nherein above shall be applicable to such checkingof measurements or levels.It is also a term of this\ncontract that checking and/or test checking the measurements ofany item of work in the\nmeasurement book and/or its payment in the interim, on account offinal bill shall not be considered\nas conclusive evidence as to the sufficiency of any work ormaterial to which it relates nor shall it\nrelieve the contractor from liabilities from any overmeasurement or defects noticed till completion of\nthe defects liability period.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0076",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 76,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 34942,
    "char_end": 35316,
    "char_count": 374,
    "text": "CLAUSE 7\nPAYMENT\nPayments will be made through monthly running account bills based on the worksexecuted on the\nbasis of recorded measurements. The running account bills shall besubmitted by the contractor for\nthe works executed on the basis of recorded measurementson the format of the Institute in triplicate\non or before the date of every month fixed byEngineer-In-Charge.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0077",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 77,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 35318,
    "char_end": 35696,
    "char_count": 378,
    "text": "E13\n\nEngineer-In-Charge shall arrange to have the bills verified by taking or causing to be takenwherever\nrequired the requisite measurement of the work. Payments on account of theamounts admissible\nshall be made by the Engineer-In-Charge certifying the sum to whichcontractor is considered entitled\nby way of running account bill at such rates decided by theEngineer-In-Charge.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0078",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 78,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 35698,
    "char_end": 36051,
    "char_count": 353,
    "text": "The amount admissible shall be paid by tenth working day after the day of presentation ofthe bill by\nthe contractor, together with all details. In the event of failure of the contractor tosubmit the bill,\nEngineer-In-Charge shall prepare or cause to be prepared such bill in whichevent no claim or what\nso ever on delay in payments shall be entertained.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0079",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 79,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 36053,
    "char_end": 36543,
    "char_count": 490,
    "text": "However in respect of i) AC works and ii) Mechanical works viz., cranes, Monorail, specialconveyor\nsystem, sliding doors, platforms, passenger/service lifts, compressed air facility,hot water\nguarantors, rotors, flash mixers and agitators etc., a) 76.5% pro-rata payment will be made on\ndelivery of equipment and subject to acceptance by conducting necessarytests. b) 13.5% pro-rata\npayment on completion of installation and c) 10.0% on completionof testing, commissioning and\nhanding over.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0080",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 80,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 36545,
    "char_end": 37520,
    "char_count": 975,
    "text": "All payments made against running accounts will be treated as intermediate advanceswhich will\nfinally be adjusted in the final bill, prepared on completion of the work and shallnot preclude the\nrequiring of bad, unsound and imperfect or unskilled work to be rejected,removed, taken away and\nreconstructed or re-erected. Any certificate given by theEngineer-in-Charge relating to the work\ndone or materials delivered forming part of suchpayment, may be modified or corrected by any\nsubsequent such certificate(s) or by thefinal certificate and shall not by itself be conclusive evidence\nthat any work or materials towhich it relates is/are in accordance with the contract and specifications.\nAny such interimpayment, or any part thereof shall not in any respect conclude, determine or affect\nin anyway powers of the Engineer-in-Charge under the contract or any of such payments betreated\nas final settlement and adjustment of accounts or in any way vary or affect thecontract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0081",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 81,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 37522,
    "char_end": 37854,
    "char_count": 332,
    "text": "Pending consideration of extension of date of completion, interim payments shall continueto be\nmade as herein provided without prejudice to the right of the department to takeaction under the\nterms of this contract for delay in the completion of work, if the extensionof date of completion is not\ngranted by the competent authority.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0082",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 82,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 37856,
    "char_end": 38349,
    "char_count": 493,
    "text": "Engineer-in-Charge in his sole discretion to the effect that the work has been completed upto the\nlevel in question make interim advance payments without detailed measurements forwork done\n(other than foundations, items to be covered under finishing items) up to lintellevel (including\nsunshade etc.) and slab level, for each floor working out at 75% of theassessed value. The advance\npayments so allowed shall be adjusted in the subsequentinterim bill by taking detailed\nmeasurements thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0083",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 83,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 38351,
    "char_end": 39158,
    "char_count": 807,
    "text": "CLAUSE 8\nCOMPLETION CERTIFICATE\nWithin ten days of the completion of work, the Contractor shall give notice of suchcompletion to the\nEngineer-in-charge and within ten days of receipt of such notice theEngineer-in-charge shall inspect\nthe work and if there is no defect in the work, shall furnishthe Contractor with a certificate of\ncompletion, otherwise a provisional certificate ofcompletion indicating the defects (a) to be rectified\nby the Contractor and/or (b) for whichpayment will be made at reduced rates shall be issued but no\nsuch certificate of completionprovisional or otherwise shall be issued nor shall the work be\nconsidered to be completeuntil the Contractor shall have removed from the premises on which the\nwork shall beexecuted all scaffolding surplus material and rubbish and all huts and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0084",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 84,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 39160,
    "char_end": 40322,
    "char_count": 1162,
    "text": "E14\n\nsanitaryarrangements required for this or their work people on the site in connection with executionof\nworks shall have been erected or constructed by the Contractor and cleaned off the dirtfrom all the\nwood works, doors, windows, walls, floors or which other parts of any buildingin upon or about the\nwork is to be executed or any of which he may had possession for thepurpose of execution thereof\nand not until the work shall have been measured by theEngineer-in-charge. If the Contractor shall\nfail to comply with requirements of this clauseas to removal of scaffoldings, surplus materials and\nrubbish and all huts and sanitaryarrangements as aforesaid and cleaning of dirt on or before the\ndate fixed for thecompletion of the work, the Engineer-in-charge may, at the expense of the\nContractor remove such scaffolding, surplus materials and rubbish etc., and dispose off the same\nashe thinks fit clean of such dirt as aforesaid, and the Contractor shall forthwith pay the amount of all\nexpense so incurred and shall have no claim in respect of any suchscaffolding or surplus materials\nas aforesaid except for any sum actually realized by thesale thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0085",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 85,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 40324,
    "char_end": 41118,
    "char_count": 794,
    "text": "CLAUSE 8A\nCONTRACTOR TO KEEP SITE CLEAN\nWhen the annual repair and maintenance work is carried out, the splashes and droppingsfrom\nwhitewashing, color washing, painting etc., on walls, floors, doors, windows etc., shallbe removed\nand the surface cleared simultaneously with the completion of these items ofwork in the individual\nrooms, quarters or premises etc., where the work is done withoutwaiting for the actual completion of\nall the other items or work in the contract. In case theContractor fails to comply with requirement of\nthis clause, the Engineer-in-charge shallhave the right to get this work done at the cost of the\nContractor either Departmentally orthrough another agency. Before taking such action, the\nEngineer-in-charge shall give tendays notice in writing to the Contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0086",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 86,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 41120,
    "char_end": 41316,
    "char_count": 196,
    "text": "CLAUSE 8B\nCOMPLETION PLAN\nThe contractor shall submit completion plan for all services viz., water, sewerage,\ndrainage,Electrical, A/c works etc., within thirty days of the completion of the work.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0087",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 87,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 41318,
    "char_end": 41658,
    "char_count": 340,
    "text": "In case, the contractor fails to submit the completion plan as aforesaid, she/ he shall beliable to pay\na sum equivalent to 2.5% of the value of the work subject to a ceiling ofRs.15,000 (Rs. Fifteen\nThousand only) as may be fixed by the EIC concerned and in thisrespect the decision of the EIC\nshall be final and binding on the contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0088",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 88,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 41660,
    "char_end": 42553,
    "char_count": 893,
    "text": "CLAUSE 9\nPAYMENT OF FINAL BILL\nThe final bill shall be submitted by the contractor in the same manner as specified ininterim bills\nwithin three months of physical completion of the work or within one month ofthe date of the final\ncertificate of completion furnished by the Engineer-in-Chargewhichever is earlier. No further claims\nshall be made by the contractor after submission ofthe final bill and these shall be deemed to have\nbeen waived and extinguished. Paymentsof those items of the bill in respect of which there is no\ndispute and of items in dispute, forquantities and rates as approved by Engineer-in-Charge, will, as\nfar as possible-be madewithin the period specified herein under, the period being reckoned from the\ndate of receiptof the bill by the Engineer-in- Charge or his authorized persons, complete with\naccount ofmaterials issued by the Institute and dismantled materials.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0089",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 89,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 42555,
    "char_end": 42666,
    "char_count": 111,
    "text": "If the Tendered value of work is,\n\nupto Rs. 45 lac\n\n: 2 months.\nmore than Rs.45 lac& upto Rs.2.5 Cr\n: 3 months.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0090",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 90,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 42668,
    "char_end": 42917,
    "char_count": 249,
    "text": "E15\n\nexceeds Rs. 2.5 Cr\n\n: 6 months.\n\nCLAUSE 9A\nPAYMENT OF CONTRACTOR’S BILL TO BANKS\nPayments due to the Contractor may, if so desired by him, be made to his bank instead ofdirect to\nhim provided that Contractor furnishes to the Engineer-in-charge;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0091",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 91,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 42919,
    "char_end": 43532,
    "char_count": 613,
    "text": "1) an authorization in the form of legally valid documents such as a power of\nattorneyconferring authority on the bank to receive payment and\n2) his own acceptance of the correctness of the account made out as being due to\nhimby Government or his signature on the bill or other claims preferred\nagainstGovernment before settlement by the Engineer-in-charge of the account or\nclaim bypayment to the Bank. While the receipt given by such bank shall constitute a\nfull andsufficient discharge for the payment, the Contractor should whenever\npossiblepresent his bills duly receipted and discharged through his bankers.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0092",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 92,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 43534,
    "char_end": 43684,
    "char_count": 150,
    "text": "Nothing herein contained shall operate to create in favour of the bank any rights or equitiesvis-à-vis\nthe President of India/Director, NIT Meghalaya.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0093",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 93,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 43686,
    "char_end": 45477,
    "char_count": 1791,
    "text": "CLAUSE 10\nMATERIALS SUPPLIED BY THE INSTITUTE\nIf the specification or schedule of items provided for the use any special description ofmaterials to be\nsupplied from Engineer-in-charge’s stores, or if it is required that theContractor shall use certain\nstores to be provided by the Engineer-in-charge as shown inschedule of materials hereto annexed\n(Schedule-B), the Contractor shall be bound toprocure and shall be supplied such materials and\nstores as are from time to time requiredto be used by him for the purpose of the Contract only and\nthe value of the quantity ofmaterials so supplied at the rates specified in the said schedule of\nmaterials may be set offor deducted from any sum then due, or thereafter to become due to the\nContractor underthe Contract, or otherwise or the proceeds of sale thereof if the same is held\ninGovernment securities, the same or a sufficient portion thereof being in this case sold forthe\npurpose. All materials so supplied to the Contractor shall remain absolute property ofGovernment,\nand shall not be removed on any account from the site of work, and shall beall times open to\ninspection by the Engineer-in-charge. Any such materials remainingunused and in perfectly good\ncondition at the time of the completion or determination of thecontract shall be returned to the\nEngineer-in-charge at a place directed by him, if by anotice in writing under his hand he shall so\nrequired, but the Contractor shall not be entitledto return any such materials unless with such\nconsent and shall have no claim forcompensation of any such materials so supplied to him as\naforesaid not being used by himor for any wastage in or damage to any such material. Provided that\nthe Contractor shall inno case be entitled to any compensation or damages on account of any delay",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0094",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 94,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 45478,
    "char_end": 46213,
    "char_count": 735,
    "text": "in supply ornon-supply thereof all any such materials and stores provided further that the\nContractorshall be bound to execute the entire work if the materials are supplied by the\nGovernmentwithin the scheduled time for completion of work plus 50% thereof (scheduled time plus\n6months if time of completion of the work exceeds 12 months) but if a part only of thematerials has\nbeen supplied within the aforesaid period then the Contractor shall be boundto do so much of the\nwork as may be possible with the materials and stores supplied in theaforesaid period. For the\ncompletion of the rest of the work, the Contractor shall be entitledto such extension of time as may\nbe determined by EIC whose decision in this regard shallbe final.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0095",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 95,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 46215,
    "char_end": 47463,
    "char_count": 1248,
    "text": "E16\n\nCLAUSE 10A\nMATERIALS TO BE PROVIDED BY THE CONTRACTOR\nThe contractor shall, at his own expense, provide all materials, required for the work otherthan those\nwhich are stipulated to be supplied by the Government.\nDOS/ ISRO\nThe contractor shall, at his own expense and without delay; supply to the Engineer-in-\nchargesamples of materials to be used on the work and shall get these approved inadvance. All\nsuch materials to be provided by the Contractor shall be in conformity withthe specifications laid\ndown or referred to in the contract. The contractor shall, if requestedby the Engineer-in-charge\nfurnish proof, to the satisfaction of the Engineer-in-charge thatthe materials so comply. The\nEngineer-in-charge shall within thirty days of supply ofsamples or within such further period as he\nmay require intimate to the Contractor in writingwhether samples are approved by him or not. If\nsamples are not approved, the Contractorshall forthwith arrange to supply to the Engineer-in-charge\nfor his approval, fresh samplescomplying with the specifications laid down in the contract. When\nmaterials are required tobe tested in accordance with specifications, approval of the Engineer-in-\ncharge shall beissued after the test results are received.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0096",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 96,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 47465,
    "char_end": 47984,
    "char_count": 519,
    "text": "The Contractor shall at his risk and cost submit the samples of materials to be tested oranalyzed\nand shall not make use of or incorporate in the work any materials representedby the samples until\nthe required tests or analysis have been made and materials finallyaccepted by the Engineer-in-\ncharge. The Contractor shall not be eligible for any claim orcompensation either arising out of any\ndelay in the work or due to any corrective measuresrequired to be taken on account of and as a\nresult of testing of materials.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0097",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 97,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 47986,
    "char_end": 48766,
    "char_count": 780,
    "text": "The contractor shall, at his risk and cost, make all arrangements and shall provide allfacilities that\nthe Engineer-in-charge may require for collecting, and preparing the requirednumber of samples of\nsuch tests at such time and to such place or places as may bedirected by the Engineer-in-charge\nand bear all charges and cost of testing unlessspecifically provided for otherwise elsewhere in the\ncontract or specifications. TheEngineer-in-charge or his authorized representative shall at all times\nhave access to theworks and to all workshops and places where work is being prepared or from\nwherematerials, manufactured articles or machinery are being obtained for the works and\nthecontractor shall afford every facility and every assistance in obtaining the right to suchaccess.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0098",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 98,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 48768,
    "char_end": 49465,
    "char_count": 697,
    "text": "The Engineer-in-charge shall have full powers to require the removal from the premises allmaterials\nwhich in his opinion are not in accordance with the specifications and in case ofdefault, the\nEngineer-in-charge shall be at liberty to employ at the expense of thecontractor, other persons to\nremove the same without being answerable or accountable forany loss or damage that may happen\nor arise to such materials. The Engineer-in-chargeshall also have full powers to require other proper\nmaterials to be substituted thereof and incase of default, the Engineer-in-charge may cause the\nsame to be supplied and all costwhich may attend such removal and substitution shall be borne by\nthe Contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0099",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 99,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 49467,
    "char_end": 49673,
    "char_count": 206,
    "text": "The contractor shall at his own expense, provide a material testing lab at the site forconducting\nroutine field tests. The lab shall be equipped atleast with the testing equipmentas specified in\nschedule F.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0100",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 100,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 49675,
    "char_end": 50002,
    "char_count": 327,
    "text": "CLAUSE 10B (i)\nSECURED ADVANCE\nThe contractor, on signing an indenture in the form to be specified by the Engineer-in-charge,shall\nbe entitled to be paid during the progress of the execution of the work upto90% of the assessed\nvalue of any materials which are in the opinion of the Engineer-in-chargenon-perishable, non-fragile",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0101",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 101,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 50004,
    "char_end": 50534,
    "char_count": 530,
    "text": "E17\n\nand non-combustible and are in accordance with thecontract and which have been brought on the\nsite in connection therewith and areadequately stored and/ or protected against damage by weather\nor other causes but whichhave not at the time of advance been incorporated in the works. When\nmaterials onaccount of which an advance has been made under this sub-clause are incorporated in\nthework, the amount of such advance shall be recovered/ deducted from the next paymentmade\nunder any of the clause or clauses of this contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0102",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 102,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 50536,
    "char_end": 50998,
    "char_count": 462,
    "text": "Such secured advance shall also be payable on other items of perishable nature, fragileand\ncombustible with the approval of the Engineer-in-charge, provided the contractorprovides a\ncomprehensive insurance cover for the full cost of such materials. The decisionof the Engineer-in-\ncharge shall be final and binding on the contractor in this matter. Nosecured advance shall however,\nbe paid on high-risk materials such as ordinary glass,sand, petrol, diesel, etc.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0103",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 103,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 51000,
    "char_end": 51482,
    "char_count": 482,
    "text": "CLAUSE 10B (ii)\nMOBILIZATION ADVANCE, INTEREST & RECOVERY\na) Mobilization advance at the rate of 10% of the tendered value, if requested by thecontractor\nin writing within one month of the order to commence the work or if considered reasonable by\nthe Engineer-in-charge.If circumstances are considered reasonable by the Engineer-In-\ncharge, this period forrequest by the contractor in writing for grant of mobilization advance\nmay be extendedin the discretion of Engineer-In-Charge.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0104",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 104,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 51484,
    "char_end": 52022,
    "char_count": 538,
    "text": "Such advance shall be made in two or more installments to be determined by theEngineer-\nin-charge at his sole discretion. The first installment of such advance shall bereleased by the\nEngineer-in-Charge to the contractor, on a request made by thecontractor to the Engineer-In-\nCharge in this behalf. The second and subsequentinstallments shall be released by the\nEngineer-In-Charge only after the contractor furnishes a proof of the satisfactory utilization of\nthe earlier installment to the entire satisfaction of the Engineer-In-Charge.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0105",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 105,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 52024,
    "char_end": 52481,
    "char_count": 457,
    "text": "Before any installment of advance is released, the contractor shall execute a BankGuarantee\nBond from Scheduled Bank for the amount equal to 110% of the amount of advance and\nvalid for the contract period. The above bank guarantee shall be keptrenewed from time to\ntime to cover the balance amount and likely period of completerecovery.\nProvided always that provision of Clause 10 B (ii) shall be applicable only when soexplicitly\nprovided in Schedule 'F '.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0106",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 106,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 52483,
    "char_end": 53221,
    "char_count": 738,
    "text": "b) Interest and recovery: The mobilization advance at (a) above bear a simple interest at the\nrate of 10% per annum and shall be calculated from the date of payment to the dateof\nrecovery, both dates inclusive, on the outstanding amount of advance. Recovery ofsuch\nsums advance shall be made by deduction from the contractors bills commencing after first\nten percent of the gross value of work is executed and paid on pro-rata percentage basis to\nthe gross value of work billed beyond ten percent in such a way that the entire advance is\nrecovered by the time eighty percent of the gross value of the contractor is executed and\npaid together with interest due on the entire outstanding amount upto the date of recovery of\nthe installment.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0107",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 107,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 53223,
    "char_end": 53353,
    "char_count": 130,
    "text": "CLAUSE 10C (i)\nREIMBURSEMENT OF ESCALATION CAUSED AS A DIRECT RESULT OF COMING INTO\nFORCE ANY FRESH LAW OR STATUTORY RULE OR ORDER",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0108",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 108,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 53355,
    "char_end": 53470,
    "char_count": 115,
    "text": "All tendered rates shall be inclusive of all taxes, duties, royalties and levies payable under respective\nstatutes.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0109",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 109,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 53472,
    "char_end": 54449,
    "char_count": 977,
    "text": "E18\n\nIf the prices of any materials incorporated in the works (not being a material supplied from the\nEngineer-in-charge stores in accordance with clause 10 thereof) and/or wages of labour increases/\ndecreases as a direct result of the coming into force of any fresh law or statutory rules or order and\nsuch increase/ decrease exceeds 10% of the price and/or wages prevailing at the time of receipt of\nthe tender for the work and the Contractor there upon necessarily and properly pays in respect of\nthe materials (incorporated in the work) such increased/ decreased price and/or in respect of labour\nengaged on the execution of the work at such increased/ decreased wages then the amount of the\ncontract shall accordingly be varied provided always that any increase/ decrease so payable/\ndeduction is not in the opinion of the Engineer-in-charge (whose decision is final and binding)\nattributable to delay in the execution of the contract within the control of the Contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0110",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 110,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 54451,
    "char_end": 54872,
    "char_count": 421,
    "text": "Provided however no reimbursement/ deduction shall be made if the increase/ decrease is not more\nthan 10% of the said prices/ wages and if so the reimbursement/ deduction shall be made only on\nthe excess over 10% and provided further that any such increase/decrease shall not be payable/\ndeduction, if such increase/ decrease has becomeoperative after the contract or extended date of\ncompletion of the works in question.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0111",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 111,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 54874,
    "char_end": 55291,
    "char_count": 417,
    "text": "The Contractor shall for the purpose of this condition keep such books of accounts andother\ndocuments as are necessary to show the amount increased claim or reductionavailable and shall\nallow inspection of the same by a duly authorized representative of theGovernment and further shall\nat the request of Engineer-in-charge, furnish any documentso kept and such other information as the\nEngineer-in-charge may require.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0112",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 112,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 55293,
    "char_end": 55628,
    "char_count": 335,
    "text": "The Contractor shall within a reasonable time of his becoming aware of any alteration inthe price of\nany such materials and or wages of labour give notice thereof to the Engineer-in-charge stating that\nthe same is given pursuance to this condition together with allinformation relating there to which he\nmay be in a position to supply.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0113",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 113,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 55630,
    "char_end": 55815,
    "char_count": 185,
    "text": "CLAUSE 10C (ii)\nPAYMENT DUE TO INCREASE/ DECREASE IN PRICES/ WAGES AFTER RECEIPT OF TENDER\nFOR WORKS (APPLICABLE ONLY FOR WORKS WITH STIPULATED PERIOD OF\nCOMPLETION MORE THAN 12 MONTHS)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0114",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 114,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 55817,
    "char_end": 56431,
    "char_count": 614,
    "text": "If the prices of materials (not being materials supplied at fixed prices by the Institute inaccordance\nwith clause 10) and/ or wages of labour required for execution of the workincrease, the contractor\nshall be compensated for such increase as per provisions detailedbelow and the amount of the\ncontract shall accordingly be varied, subject to the conditionthat such compensation for escalation in\nprices shall be available only for the work doneduring the stipulated period of the contract including\nthe justified period extended under theprovisions of clause 5 of the contract without any action under\nclause 2A.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0115",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 115,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 56433,
    "char_end": 56706,
    "char_count": 273,
    "text": "No such compensation shall be payable for a work for which the stipulated period ofcompletion is\nequal to or less than 12 (twelve) months. Such compensation for escalationin the prices of\nmaterials and labour, when due, shall be worked out based on the followingprovisions.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0116",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 116,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 56708,
    "char_end": 56929,
    "char_count": 221,
    "text": "(i) The base date for working out such escalation shall be the last stipulated date ofreceipt of\ntenders including extension, if any,\n(ii) The cost of work on which escalation will be payable shall be reckoned as below :-",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0117",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 117,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 56931,
    "char_end": 57818,
    "char_count": 887,
    "text": "Gross value of work done upto this quarter\n[A]\n\nE19\n\nGross value of work done upto the last\nquarter\n[B]\nGross value of work done since previous\nquarter (A-B)\n[C]\nFull assessed value of Secured Advance,\nfresh paid in this quarter\n[D]\nFull assessed value of Secured Advance,\nrecovered in this quarter\n[E]\nFull assessed value of Secured Advance for\nwhich escalation payable inthis quarter [D-E]\n[F]\nAdvance payment made during this quarter\n[G]\nAdvance payment recovered during this\nquarter\n[H]\nAdvance payment for which escalation is\npayable in this quarter [G-H]\n [ I ]\nExtra items /deviated quantities of items paid\nas per Clause 12 based onprevailing market\nrates during this quarter.\n[J]\nThen, M = C + F + I – J\nN = 0.85 M\nLess cost of material supplied by the\nDepartment as per Clause 10 andrecovered\nduring the quarter\n[K]\nCost of work for which escalation is applicable : W = N – (K)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0118",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 118,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 57820,
    "char_end": 58190,
    "char_count": 370,
    "text": "(iii)\nComponents of materials and labour shall be predetermined for every work andincorporated in\nthe condition of contract attached to the tender papers included inschedule ‘F’. The decision of\nthe Engineer-in-charge in working out such percentageshall be binding on the contractors.\n(iv) The compensation for materials shall be worked as per the formula given below :-",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0119",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 119,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 58192,
    "char_end": 58220,
    "char_count": 28,
    "text": "(a) Adjustment for Materials",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
