    "paragraph_index": 122,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 58254,
    "char_end": 58367,
    "char_count": 113,
    "text": "Where,\n\nVm = Variation in material cost i.e. increase or decrease in the amount in rupees to bepaid or\nrecovered.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0123",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 123,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 58369,
    "char_end": 58709,
    "char_count": 340,
    "text": "W = Cost of Work done worked out as indicated in sub-para (ii)\n\nXm = Component of materials expressed as percent to the total value of work as specifiedin\nSchedule F.\nMI = All India Wholesale Price Index for all commodities for the period under consideration\npublished by Economic Advisor to Govt. of India, Ministry of Industry & Commerce.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0124",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 124,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 58712,
    "char_end": 58942,
    "char_count": 230,
    "text": "MIo= All India Wholesale Price Index for all commodities valid on the last stipulated date of receipt\n of tender including extension, if any, as published by the Economic Advisor to Govt. of India,\nMinistry of Industry & Commerce.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0125",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 125,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 58944,
    "char_end": 60053,
    "char_count": 1109,
    "text": "E20\n\n(v)\nThe following principles shall be followed while working out the indices mentioned inPara (iv)\nabove\n(a) The compensation for escalation shall be worked out at quarterly intervals and shallbe with\nrespect to the cost of work done as per bills paid during the three calendarmonths of the said\nquarter. The first such payment shall be made at the end of threemonths after the month\n(excluding) in which the tender was accepted and thereafterat three months interval. At the\ntime of completion of the work, the last period forpayment might become less than 3 months,\ndepending on the actual date ofcompletion.\n(b) The index (MI) relevant to any quarter/ period for which such compensation is paidshall be\nthe arithmetical average of the indices relevant to the three calendar months.If the period\nupto date of completion after the quarter covered by the last suchinstallment of payment is\nless than three months, the index MI shall be the averageof the indices for the months falling\nwithin the period.\n(vi)\nThe compensation for escalation for labour shall be worked out as per the formulagiven\nbelow :-",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
