    "paragraph_index": 128,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 60087,
    "char_end": 60193,
    "char_count": 106,
    "text": "Where,\n\nVL =Variation in labour cost i.e. amount of increase or decrease in rupees to be paid orrecovered.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0129",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 129,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 60195,
    "char_end": 60375,
    "char_count": 180,
    "text": "W = Value of work done, worked out as indicated in sub-para (ii) above\n\nYL = Component of labour expressed as a percentage of the total value of the work asspecified in\nSchedule F.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0130",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 130,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 60377,
    "char_end": 60576,
    "char_count": 199,
    "text": "LI = Minimum daily Wage in rupees of an unskilled adult male mazdoor, fixed under anylaw,\nstatutory rule or order as applicable on the last date of the quarter previous tothe one under\nconsideration.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0131",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 131,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 60578,
    "char_end": 60782,
    "char_count": 204,
    "text": "LIo = Minimum daily wage in rupees of an unskilled adult male mazdoor fixed under anylaw, statutory\nrule or order as applicable on the last stipulated date of receipt oftender including extension, if any.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0132",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 132,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 60784,
    "char_end": 60893,
    "char_count": 109,
    "text": "(vii)\nThe following principles will be followed while working out the compensation as persub-para\n(vi) above.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0133",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 133,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 60895,
    "char_end": 61523,
    "char_count": 628,
    "text": "(a)\nThe minimum wage of an unskilled male mazdoor mentioned in sub-para (vi) aboveshall be\nthe higher of the wage notified by Government of India, Ministry of Labourand that notified by\nthe local administration both relevant to the place of work and theperiod of reckoning.\nDOS/ ISRO\n(b)\nThe escalation for labour also shall be paid at the same quarterly intervals whenescalation\ndue to increase in cost of materials is paid under this clause. If suchrevision of minimum\nwages takes place during any such quarterly intervals, theescalation compensation shall be\npayable at revised rates only for work done insubsequent quarters.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0134",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 134,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 61525,
    "char_end": 61799,
    "char_count": 274,
    "text": "E21\n\n(c)\nIrrespective of variations in minimum wages of any category of labour, for thepurpose of this\nclause, the variation in the rate for an unskilled adult male mazdooralone shall form the basis\nfor working out the escalation compensation payable onthe labour component.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0135",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 135,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 61801,
    "char_end": 62194,
    "char_count": 393,
    "text": "(viii) In the event, the price of materials and/ or wages of labour required for execution ofthe work\ndecrease/s, there shall be a downward adjustment of the cost of work sothat such price of\nmaterials and/or wages of labour shall be deductible from the costof work under this contract\nand in this regard the formula herein before stated underthis Clause 10C (ii) shall mutatis\nmutandis apply.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0136",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 136,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 62196,
    "char_end": 62550,
    "char_count": 354,
    "text": "CLAUSE 10D\nDISMANTLED MATERIALS ARE GOVERNMENT PROPERTY\n\nThe Contractor shall treat all materials obtained during dismantling of a structure, excavation of the\nsite for a work etc., as Government’s property and such materials shall be disposed off to the best\nadvantage of Government according to instructions in writing issued by the Engineer-in-charge.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0137",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 137,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 62552,
    "char_end": 64086,
    "char_count": 1534,
    "text": "CLAUSE 10E - DELETED\n\nCLAUSE 11\nWORK TO BE EXECUTED IN ACCORDANCE WITH SPECIFICATIONS, DRAWINGS, ORDERS,\nETC.,\nThe contractor shall execute the whole and every part of the work in the most substantial and\nworkmanlike manner both as regards materials and otherwise in every respect in strict accordance\nwith the specifications. The contractor shall also conform exactly, fully and faithfully to the design,\ndrawings and instructions in writing in respect of the work signed by the Engineer-in-Charge and the\ncontractor shall be furnished free of charge one copy of the contract documents together with\nspecifications, designs, drawings and instructions as are not included in the standard specifications\nof Central Public Works Department or in any Bureau of Indian Standard or any other, published\nstandard or code or, Schedule of Rates or any other printed publication referred to elsewhere in the\ncontract. The contractor shall comply with the provisions of the contract and with the care and\ndiligence execute and maintain the works and provide all labour and materials, tools and plants\nincluding for measurements and supervision of all works, structural plans and other things of\ntemporary or permanent nature required for such execution and maintenance in so far as the\nnecessity for providing these, is specified or is reasonably inferred from the contract. The Contractor\nshall take full responsibility for adequacy, suitability and safety of all the works and methods of\nconstruction.\nCLAUSE 11A\nACTION WHERE NO SPECIFICATION",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0138",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 138,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 64088,
    "char_end": 64566,
    "char_count": 478,
    "text": "In the case of any class of work for which there is no standard specifications such work shall be\ncarried out generally in accordance with CPWD specification and if there is no details of CPWD\nspecification book then it shall be executed as per Bureau of Indian Standard specification. In case\nthere is no such specification in Bureau of Indian Standards the work shall be carried out in all\nrespects in accordance with the instruction and requirement of the Engineer-in-charge.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0139",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 139,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 64568,
    "char_end": 64820,
    "char_count": 252,
    "text": "CLAUSE 12\nDEVIATIONS/ VARIATIONS EXTENT AND PRICING\nThe Engineer-in-charge shall have power (i) to make alteration in, omissions from, additions to, or\nsubstitutions for the original specifications, drawings, designs and instructions that may appear to",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0140",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 140,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 64822,
    "char_end": 66105,
    "char_count": 1283,
    "text": "E22\n\nhim to be necessary or advisable during the progress of the work, and (ii) to omit a part of the\nwork(s) in case of non-availability of a portion of the site or for any other reasons and the contractor\nshall be bound to carry out the works in accordance with any instructions given to him in writing\nsigned by the Engineer-in-charge and such alterations, omissions, additions or substitutions shall\nform part of the contract as if originally provided therein and any altered, additional or substituted\nwork which the contractor may be directed to do in the manner specified above as part of the works,\nshall be carried out by the contractor on the same conditions in all respects including price on which\nhe agreed to do the main work except as hereafter provided :\n12.1: The time for completion of the works shall, in the event of any deviations resulting in additional\ncost over the tendered value sum being ordered, be extended, if requested by the contractor, as\nfollows:\ni) In the proportion which the additional cost of the altered, additional or substituted work, bears to\nthe original tendered value plus.\nii) 25% of the time calculated in (i) above or such further additional time as may be considered\nreasonable by the Engineer-in-charge.\n12.2: Extra items and pricing",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0141",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 141,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 66107,
    "char_end": 66709,
    "char_count": 602,
    "text": "A. For major works:\nIn the case of Extra items (items that are completely new, and are in addition to the items contained\nin the contract) , the contractor may within 15 days of receipt of order or occurrence of the item(s),\nclaim rate supported by proper analysis, for the work and the Engineer-in-charge shall within\nprescribed time limit of the receipt of the claims supported by analysis after giving consideration to\nthe analysis of the rates submitted by the contractor, determine the rates on the basis of market\nrates and the contractor shall be paid in accordance with the rates so determined.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0142",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 142,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 66711,
    "char_end": 67135,
    "char_count": 424,
    "text": "B. For Maintenance works including works of up-gradation, aesthetic, special repair, addition/\nalteration:\nIn the case of Extra item(s) being the schedule items (SOR as mentioned in schedule ‘E’), these\nshall be paid as per the schedule rate plus plus/ minus percentage above/ below quoted contract\namount. Payment of Extra items in case of nonscheduled items (Non-SOR items) shall be made as\nper the prevailing market rate.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0143",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 143,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 67137,
    "char_end": 67865,
    "char_count": 728,
    "text": "12.3: Substituted item, pricing\n\nA. For major/ capital works:\nIn the case of substituted items (items that are taken up with partial substitution are in lieu of items of\nwork in the contract), the rate for the agreement item (to be substituted) and substituted item shall\nalso be determined in the manner as mentioned in the following para.\ni) If the market rate for the substituted item so determined is more than the market rate of the\nagreement item (to be substituted), the rate payable to the contractor for the substituted item shall\nbe the rate for the agreement item (to be substituted) so increased to the extent of the difference\nbetween the market rates of substituted item and the agreement item (to be substituted).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0144",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 144,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 67867,
    "char_end": 68255,
    "char_count": 388,
    "text": "ii) If the market rate for the substituted item so determined is less than the market rate of the\nagreement item (to be substituted), the rate payable to the contractor for the substituted item shall\nbe the rate for the agreement item (to be substituted) so decreased to the extent of the difference\nbetween the market rates of substituted item and the agreement item (to be substituted).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0145",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 145,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 68257,
    "char_end": 68363,
    "char_count": 106,
    "text": "B. For Maintenance works including works of up-gradation, aesthetic, special repair, addition/\nalteration:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0146",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 146,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 68365,
    "char_end": 68721,
    "char_count": 356,
    "text": "E23\n\nIn the case of Substituted item(s) being the schedule items (SOR as mentioned inSchedule ‘E’),\nthese shall be paid as per the schedule rate plus, plus/minus percentageabove/ below quoted\ncontract amount. Payment of Substituted items in case of nonscheduled items (Non – SOR as\nmentioned in Schedule ‘E’) shall be made as per theprevailing market rate.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0147",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 147,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 68723,
    "char_end": 69519,
    "char_count": 796,
    "text": "12.4: Deviated quantities, pricing\n\nA. For major/ capital works:\nIn the case of contract items, substituted items, contract cum substituted items, which exceed the\nlimits as below, the contractor may within fifteen days of receipt of order ofoccurrence of the excess,\nclaim revision of the rates, supported by proper analysis for thework in excess of the above\nmentioned limits, provided that if the rates so claimed are inexcess of the rates specified in the\nschedule of quantities, the Engineer-in-charge shallwithin prescribed time limit of receipt of the\nclaims supported by analysis, after givingconsideration to the analysis of the rates submitted by the\ncontractor, determine the rateson the basis of market rates and the contractor shall be paid in\naccordance with the ratesso determined.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0148",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 148,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 69521,
    "char_end": 69606,
    "char_count": 85,
    "text": "Prescribed time limits are as under:\n\nIf the Tendered value of work is\nupto Rs.45 lac",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0149",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 149,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 69608,
    "char_end": 69690,
    "char_count": 82,
    "text": ": 30 days.\nmore than Rs.45 lac and up to Rs. 2.5 Cr\n\n: 45 days.\nexceeds Rs. 2.5 Cr",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0150",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 150,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 69692,
    "char_end": 69810,
    "char_count": 118,
    "text": ": 60 days.\n\nB. For Maintenance works including works of up- gradation, aesthetic, special repair,addition/\nalteration:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0151",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 151,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 69812,
    "char_end": 70658,
    "char_count": 846,
    "text": "In the case of contract items, which exceed the deviation limits as specified in Schedule ‘E’,the\ncontractor shall be paid with rates specified in the schedule of quantities.\nDOS/\n12.5:\nA. For major/ capital works:\nThe provisions of the preceding paragraph shall also apply to the decrease in the rates ofitems for\nthe work in excess of limits laid down in Schedule ' E ', and the Engineer-inchargeshall after giving\nnotice to the contractor within one month of occurrence of theexcess and after taking into\nconsideration any reply received from him within fifteen days ofthe receipt of the notice, revise the\nrates for the work in question within one month of theexpiry of the said period of fifteen days having\nregard to the market rates.\nB. For Maintenance works including works of up-gradation, aesthetic, special repair,addition/\nalteration:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0152",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 152,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 70660,
    "char_end": 71151,
    "char_count": 491,
    "text": "In case of decrease in the rates prevailing in the market of items for the work in excess ofthe limits\nlaid down in Schedule E, the Engineer-in-Charge shall after giving notice to thecontractor within one\nmonth of occurrence of the excess and after taking into considerationany reply received from him\nwithin fifteen days of the receipt of the notice, revise the ratesfor the work in question within one\nmonth of the expiry of the said period of fifteen dayshaving regard to the market rates",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0153",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 153,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 71153,
    "char_end": 71417,
    "char_count": 264,
    "text": "For the purpose of operation of deviation limit, the following works shall be treated asworks relating\nto foundation unless & otherwise defined in the contract:\ni)\nFor Buildings: All works upto 1.2 metres above ground level or upto floor 1\nlevelwhichever is lower.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0154",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 154,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 71419,
    "char_end": 71984,
    "char_count": 565,
    "text": "E24\n\nii)\nFor abutments, piers and well steining: All works up to 1.2 m above the bed level.\niii)\nFor retaining walls, wing walls, compound walls, chimneys, over headreservoirs/tanks\nand other elevated structures: All works upto 1.2 metres above theground level.\niv)\nFor reservoirs/ tanks (other than overhead reservoirs/ tanks): All works upto 1.2metres\nabove the ground level.\nv)\nFor basement: All works upto 1.2 m above ground level or up to floor 1 levelwhichever is\nlower.\nvi)\nFor Roads, all items of excavation and filling including treatment of sub base.\nvii)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0155",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 155,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 71986,
    "char_end": 72476,
    "char_count": 490,
    "text": "12.6:\nThe contractor shall send to the Engineer-in-charge once every three months, an up-to dateaccount\ngiving complete details of all claims for additional payments to which thecontractor may consider\nhimself entitled and of all additional work ordered by the Engineer-in-charge which he has executed\nduring the preceding quarter failing which the contractorshall be deemed to have waived his right.\nHowever, the Director, NIT Meghalayamay authorize consideration of such claims on merits.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0156",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 156,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 72478,
    "char_end": 72914,
    "char_count": 436,
    "text": "12.7:\nAny operation incidental for proper execution of the item included in the Schedule ofquantities or in\nthe Schedule of rates mentioned above, whether or not, specificallyindicated in the description of the\nitem and the relevant specifications, shall be deemed tobe included in the rates quoted by the\ntenderer or the rate given in the said schedule ofrates as the case may be. Nothing extra shall be\nadmissible for such operations.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0157",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 157,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 72916,
    "char_end": 73652,
    "char_count": 736,
    "text": "CLAUSE 13\nFORE CLOSURE OF CONTRACT DUE TO ABANDONMENT OR REDUCTION IN\nSCOPE OF WORK\nIf at any time after acceptance of the tender, Engineer-in-Charge shall decide to abandonor reduce\nthe scope of the works for any reason whatsoever and hence not require thewhole or any part of the\nworks to be carried out, the Engineer-in-Charge shall give notice inwriting to that effect to the\ncontractor and the contractor shall act accordingly in the matter.The contractor shall have no claim\nto any payment of compensation or otherwisewhatsoever, on account of any profit or advantage\nwhich he might have derived from theexecution of the works in full but which he did not derive in\nconsequence of the foreclosureof the whole or part of the works.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0158",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 158,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 73654,
    "char_end": 73935,
    "char_count": 281,
    "text": "The contractor shall be paid at contract rates, full amount for works executed at site and, inaddition,\na reasonable amount as certified by the Engineer-in-Charge for the itemshereunder mentioned\nwhich could not be utilized on the work to the full extent in view of theforeclosure;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0159",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 159,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 73937,
    "char_end": 74120,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "(i) Any expenditure incurred on preliminary site work, e.g. temporary access roads,temporary labour\nhuts, staff quarters and site office, storage accommodation andwater storage tanks.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0160",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 160,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 74122,
    "char_end": 74854,
    "char_count": 732,
    "text": "(ii) Government/Institute shall have the option to take over contractor’s materials orany part thereof\neither brought to site or of which the contractor is legally bound toaccept delivery from suppliers (for\nincorporation in or incidental to the work)provided, however Government/ Institute shall be bound to\ntake over thematerials or such portions thereof as the contractor does not desire to retain.\nFormaterials taken over or to be taken over by Government/ Department, cost of suchmaterials as\ndetailed by Engineer-in- Charge shall be paid. The cost shall,however, take into account purchase\nprice, cost of transportation and deteriorationor damage which may have been caused to materials\nwhilst in the custody of thecontractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0161",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 161,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 74856,
    "char_end": 75378,
    "char_count": 522,
    "text": "E25\n\n(iii) If any materials supplied by Government/ Institute are rendered surplus, thesame except normal\nwastage shall be returned by the contractor to Government/Institute at rates not exceeding those at\nwhich these were originally issued, lessallowance for any deterioration or damage which may have\nbeen caused whilst the materials were in the custody of the contractor. In addition, cost of\ntransporting such materials from site to Government/ Institute stores, if so required byGovernment/\nInstitutet, shall be paid.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0162",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 162,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 75380,
    "char_end": 75616,
    "char_count": 236,
    "text": "(iv) Reasonable compensation for transfer of T & P from site to contractor’s permanentstores or to\nhis other works, whichever is less. If T & P are not transported to eitherof the said places, no cost of\ntransportation shall be payable.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0163",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 163,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 75618,
    "char_end": 76000,
    "char_count": 382,
    "text": "(v) Reasonable compensation for repatriation of contractor’s site staff and importedlabour to the\nextent necessary.\nDOS/ ISRO\nThe contractor shall, if required by the Engineer- in-Charge, furnish to him, books ofaccount, wage\nbooks, time sheets and other relevant documents and evidence as may benecessary to enable him\nto certify the reasonable amount payable under this condition.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0164",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 164,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 76002,
    "char_end": 76813,
    "char_count": 811,
    "text": "The reasonable amount of items on (i), (iv) and (v) above shall not be in excess of 2% ofthe cost of\nthe work remaining incomplete on the date of closure, i.e. total stipulated cost ofthe work as per\naccepted tender less the cost of work actually executed under the contractand less the cost of\ncontractor’s materials at site taken over by the Government/Instiute as per item (ii) above. Provided\nalways that against any payments due to thecontractor on this account or otherwise, the Engineer-\nin-Charge shall be entitled to recoveror be credited with any outstanding balances due from the\ncontractor for advance paid inrespect of any tool, plants and materials and any other sums which at\nthe date oftermination were recoverable by the Government/ Institute from the contractor underthe\nterms of the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0165",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 165,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 76815,
    "char_end": 77077,
    "char_count": 262,
    "text": "CLAUSE 14\nRISK AND COST\nIf contractor:\n\n(i)\nAt any time makes default during currency of work or does not execute any part ofthe work with\ndue diligence and continues to do so even after 7 days of notice inwriting, in this respect from\nthe Engineer-in-Charge; or",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0166",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 166,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 77079,
    "char_end": 77323,
    "char_count": 244,
    "text": "(ii) Commits default in complying with any of the terms and conditions of the contractand does not\nremedy it or takes effective steps to remedy it within 7 days even aftera notice in writing is given\nin that behalf by the Engineer-in-Charge; or",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0167",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 167,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 77325,
    "char_end": 77561,
    "char_count": 236,
    "text": "(iii) Fails to complete the work(s) or items of work with individual dates of completion,on or before\nthe date(s) so determined, and does not complete them within theperiod specified in the notice\ngiven in writing in that behalf by EIC.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0168",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 168,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 77563,
    "char_end": 77890,
    "char_count": 327,
    "text": "Engineer- in-Charge without invoking action under clause 3 may, without prejudice to anyother right\nor remedy against the contractor which have either accrued or accruethereafter to Government/\nInstitute, by a notice in writing to take the part work/partincomplete work of any item(s) out of his\nhands and shall have powers to:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0169",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 169,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 77892,
    "char_end": 78128,
    "char_count": 236,
    "text": "E26\n\n(a) Take possession of the site and any materials, constructional plant, implements,stores, etc.,\nthereon; and/or\n(b) Carry out the part work / part incomplete work of any item(s) by any means at therisk and cost\nof the contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0170",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 170,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 78130,
    "char_end": 78545,
    "char_count": 415,
    "text": "The Engineer-in-Charge shall determine the amount, if any, is recoverable from thecontractor for\ncompletion of the part work/ part incomplete work of any item(s) taken outof his hands and execute\nat the risk and cost of the contractor, the liability of contractoron account of loss or damage suffered\nby Government/Institute because of actionunder this clause shall not exceed 10% of the tendered\nvalue of the work.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0171",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 171,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 78547,
    "char_end": 79350,
    "char_count": 803,
    "text": "In determining the amount, credit shall be given to the contractor with the value of workdone in all\nrespect in the same manner and at the same rate as if it had been carriedout by the original\ncontractor under the terms of his contract, the value of contractor’smaterials taken over and\nincorporated in the work and use of plant and machinerybelonging to the contractor. The certificate\nof the Engineer-in-Charge as to the value of work done shall be final and conclusive against the\ncontractor provided always that action under this clause shall only be taken after giving notice in\nwriting to the contractor. Provided also that if the expenses incurred by the department are less than\nthe amount payable to the contractor at his agreement rates, the difference shall not be payable to\nthe contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0172",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 172,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 79352,
    "char_end": 79927,
    "char_count": 575,
    "text": "Any excess expenditure incurred or to be incurred by Government/ Institute in completing the part\nwork/ part incomplete work of any item(s) or the excess loss of damages suffered or may be\nsuffered by Government/Institute as aforesaid after allowing such credit shall without prejudice to\nany other right or remedy available to Government/Institute in law or per as agreement be recovered\nfrom any money due to the contractor or any account, and if such money is insufficient, the\ncontractor shall be called upon in writing and shall be liable to pay the same within 30 days.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0173",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 173,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 79929,
    "char_end": 80422,
    "char_count": 493,
    "text": "If the contractor fails to pay the required sum within the aforesaid period of 30 days, the Engineer-in-\nCharge shall have the right to sell any or all of the contractors’ unused materials, constructional\nplant, implements, temporary building at site etc. and adjust the proceeds of sale thereof towards the\ndues recoverable from the contractor under the contract and if thereafter there remains any balance\noutstanding, it shall be recovered in accordance with the provisions of the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0174",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 174,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 80424,
    "char_end": 80780,
    "char_count": 356,
    "text": "In the event of above course being adopted by the Engineer-in-Charge the contractor shall have no\nclaim to compensation for any loss sustained by him by reason of his having purchased or procured\nany materials or entered into any engagements or made any advance on any account or with a view\nto the execution of the work or the performance of the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0175",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 175,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 80782,
    "char_end": 81597,
    "char_count": 815,
    "text": "CLAUSE 15\nSUSPENSION OF WORK\nThe Contractor shall suspend the execution of work or any part or parts thereof, wherever called\nupon in writing by the Engineer-in-charge to do so and shall not resume work thereon until so\ndirected in writing by him. The Contractor will be allowed an extension of time for completion not less\nthan the period of suspension but no other claims in this respect for compensation or otherwise,\nhowever will be admissible.\nCLAUSE 16\nACTION IN CASE WORK NOT DONE AS PER SPECIFICATIONS\nAll works under or in course of execution or executed in pursuance of the contract, shall at all times\nbe open and accessible to the inspection and supervision of the Engineer-in-charge, his authorized\nsubordinates in charge of the work and all the superior officers, officer of the Quality Assurance unit",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0176",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 176,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 81599,
    "char_end": 82195,
    "char_count": 596,
    "text": "E27\n\nof the Government or any organization engaged by the Institutefor Quality Assurance and of the\nChief Technical Examiner’s office and the contractor shall, at all times, during the usual working\nhours and at all other times at which reasonable notice of the visit of such officers has been given to\nthe contractor, either himself be present to receive orders and instructions or have a responsible\nagent duly accredited in writing, present for that purpose. Orders given to the contractor’s agent\nshall be considered to have the same force as if they had been given to the contractor himself.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0177",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 177,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 82197,
    "char_end": 83693,
    "char_count": 1496,
    "text": "If it shall appear to the Engineer-in-charge or his authorized subordinate in-charge of the work or to\nthe Authority in charge of Quality Assurance or his subordinate officers or the officers of the\norganization engaged by the Institute for Quality Assurance or to the Chief Technical Examiner or\nhis subordinate officers that any work has been executed with unsound, imperfect, or unskillful\nworkmanship, or with materials or articles provided by him for the execution of the work which are\nunsound or of a quality inferior to that contracted or otherwise not in accordance with the contract,\nthe contractor shall, on demand in writing which shall be made within twelve months (six months in\nthe case of work costing Rs.10 lakhs and below except road work) of the completion of the work\nfrom the Engineer-in-charge specifying the work, materials or articles complained of notwithstanding\nthat the same may have been passed, certified and paid for forthwith rectify, or remove and\nreconstruct the work so specified in whole or in part, as the case may require or as the case may be,\nremove the materials or articles so specified and provide other proper and suitable materials or\narticles at his own charge and cost. In the event of the failing to do so within a period specified by\nthe Engineer-in-charge in his demand aforesaid, then the contractor shall be liable to pay\ncompensation at the same rate as under clause 2 of the contract (for non-completion of the work in\ntime) for this default.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0178",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 178,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 83695,
    "char_end": 84392,
    "char_count": 697,
    "text": "In such case the Engineer-in-charge may not accept the item of work at the rate applicable under\nthe contract but may accept such items at reduced rates as the authority specified in Schedule `F’\nmay consider reasonable during the preparation, of on account bills or final bill if the item is so\nacceptable without detriment to the safety and utility of the item and the structure or he may reject\nthe work outright without any payment and/or get it and other connected and incidental items\nrectified, or removed and re-executed at the risk and cost of the contractor. Decision of the\nEngineer-in-charge to be conveyed in writing in respect of the same will be final and binding on the\ncontractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0179",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 179,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 84394,
    "char_end": 85788,
    "char_count": 1394,
    "text": "CLAUSE 16A\nNOTICE TO BE GIVEN BEFORE COVERING UP\nThe Contractor shall give not less than seven days notice in writing to the Engineer-in-charge or his\nauthorized subordinate in charge of the work before covering up or otherwise placing beyond the\nreach of measurement any work in order that the same may be measured and correct dimensions\nthereof be taken before the same is covered up or placed beyond the reach of measurement and\nshall not cover up and placed beyond the reach of measurement any work without the consent in\nwriting of the Engineer-in-charge or his authorized subordinate in charge of the work shall within the\naforesaid period of seven days inspect the work and if any work shall be covered up or placed\nbeyond the reach of measurement without such notice having been given or the Engineer-in-\ncharge’s consent be obtained the same shall be uncovered at the Contractor’s expense, or in default\nthereof no payment or allowance shall be made for such work or the materials with which the same\nwas executed.\nCLAUSE 17A\nCONTRACTOR LIABLE FOR DAMAGES, DEFECTS DURING MAINTENANCE PERIOD\nIf the Contractor or his working people shall break, deface, injure or destroy any part of a building in\nwhich they may be working or any buildings, road, kerbs, fence, enclosure, water pipes, cables,\ndrains, electric and telephone posts or wire, trees, grass or grass land or cultivated ground",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0180",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 180,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 85790,
    "char_end": 86957,
    "char_count": 1167,
    "text": "E28\n\ncontiguous to the premises on which the work or any part of it is being executed, or if any damage\nshall happen to the work while in progress from any cause whatever or if any defects shrinkage or\nother faults appear in the work within twelve months after a certificate of final or otherwise of its\ncompletion shall have been given by the Engineer-in-charge as aforesaid arising out of defective or\nimproper materials or workmanship, the Contractor shall after receipt of notice in writing in that\nbehalf make the same good at his own expense, or in default the Engineer-in-charge may cause the\nsame to be made good by other workmen and deduct the expense (of which the certificate of the\nEngineer-in-charge shall be final) from any sums that may then, or at any time thereafter become\ndue to the Contractor, or from his Security Deposit or the proceeds of sale thereof, or of a sufficient\nportion thereof the Security Deposit of the Contractor shall not be refunded before the expiry of\ntwelve calendar months after the issue of the certificate of final or otherwise of completion of work,\nor till the final bill has been prepared and passed whichever is later.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0181",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 181,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 86959,
    "char_end": 87361,
    "char_count": 402,
    "text": "Engineer-in-Charge shall give notice to the contractor of any defects before the end of theDefect\nLiability Period, which begins on the date of completion. The Defect Liability Periodshall stand\nautomatically extended for as long as defects remain to be rectified. Every timenotice of defect is\ngiven, the contractor shall correct the notified defects within the periodspecified by Engineer-in-\ncharge.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0182",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 182,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 87363,
    "char_end": 87598,
    "char_count": 235,
    "text": "However, for contract exclusively for earth work or jungle clearance where defect liabilityperiod is not\nrelevant, Security Deposit if any paid may be refunded along with payment offinal bill subject to\nlabour clearance vide Clause 45.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0183",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 183,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 87600,
    "char_end": 87967,
    "char_count": 367,
    "text": "Further in case where the contract provides for completion in phases, the Engineer-in-chargeat his\ndiscretion may allow part refund of Security Deposit after expiry of 12 months(6 months in case of\nany works other than road work costing Rs.10,00,000 and below) fromthe date of completion for\neach phase but not before the payment of final bill for the entirecontract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0184",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 184,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 87969,
    "char_end": 89518,
    "char_count": 1549,
    "text": "CLAUSE 17B\nSPECIAL CONDITION ON TAKING INSURANCE POLICY FOR THE WHOLE WORK\nORDER VALUE BY THE CONTRACTORS'\nAs per Clause 17A of the Conditions of Contract, the Contractors' have to make good attheir own\nexpense the damages occurred due to any accident from any cause during thework in progress or\nnearing completion of the work. In order to fulfill this clause and also totake the responsibility of\nhanding over the site to the full satisfaction of the Engineer-in-Charge and till the contractor gets the\ncertificate or a letter of taking over the site facility/building/works, the contractor shall be responsible\nto re-do the works damaged from anycause. For this purpose, the contractor shall insure the whole\nwork the moment the workorder is received and before agreement is signed for the entire work order\nvalue undercontractor’s all risk insurance policy [CAR]. The third party liability and Cross-liability\nshallalso be covered under the policy. The Contractors' shall consult the insurance companiesand\nalso the principal employer i.e. the Engineer-in-Charge and take the insurance policyfor CAR. In\ncase of any accidents during the work or nearing completion of the work [otherthan during the defect\nliability period for which Clause-17A is applicable], the Contractors'are totally responsible to re-do\nthe damages and hand over site in acceptable condition tothe Engineer-in-Charge and await a letter\nfrom the Department that the site has been takenover. Till such time, the Contractors' are\nresponsible for all the damages from any cause.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0185",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 185,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 89520,
    "char_end": 89796,
    "char_count": 276,
    "text": "Note: Contractor should also obtain insurance policy to cover all the laborers engaged inthe work.\nIn the event of contractor failing to keep insurance alive, Institute reserves right to takeappropriate\naction including withholding the payments due to the Contactor.\nDOS/ ISRO",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0186",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 186,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 89798,
    "char_end": 90651,
    "char_count": 853,
    "text": "E29\n\nCLAUSE 18\nCONTRACTOR TO SUPPLY TOOLS AND PLANTS ETC.,\nThe Contractor shall supply and provide at his own cost all materials (except such specialmaterials,\nif any as may in accordance with the contract be supplied from the Engineer-incharge’sstores) plant,\ntools, appliances, implements, ladders, cartage, tackle, scaffoldingand temporary works requisite for\nthe proper execution of the work, whether original,altered or substituted and whether included in the\nspecification or other documents formingpart of the contract or referred to in these conditions or not\nor which may be necessary forthe purpose of satisfying or complying with the requirements of the\nEngineer-in-charge asto any matters as to which under these conditions he is entitled to be satisfied\nor which heis entitled to require together with carriage thereof to and from the work.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0187",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 187,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 90653,
    "char_end": 91194,
    "char_count": 541,
    "text": "The Contractor shall also supply without charge the requisite number of persons with themeans and\nmaterials necessary for the purpose of setting out works and counting,weighing and assisting in the\nmeasurement or examination at any time and from time totime of the work or materials failing his so\ndoing the same may be provided by theEngineer-in-charge at the expenses of the Contractor and\nthe expense may be deductedfrom any money due to the Contractor under the contract or the\nproceeds of sale thereof orof a sufficient portion thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0188",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 188,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 91196,
    "char_end": 92228,
    "char_count": 1032,
    "text": "CLAUSE 18A\nRECOVERY OF COMPENSATION PAID TO WORKMEN\nIn every case which by virtue of the provisions of section 12 sub-section (i) of theworkman’s\ncompensation act, 1923, Government/Institute is obliged to pay compensation toworkmen employed\nby the Contractor in execution of the work, Government will recoverfrom the Contractor the amount\nof the compensation so paid and without prejudice to therights of Government under section-12 sub-\nsection (2) of the said act, Government/Institute shall beat liberty to recover such amounts or any\npart thereof by deducting it from the securityDeposit or from any sum due by the\nGovernment/Institute to the contract whether under thiscontract or otherwise, Government/Institute\nshall not be bound to contest any claim made against itunder section 12, sub-section (1) of the said\nact except on the written request of theContractor and upon his giving to Government/Institute full\nsecurity for all costs for whichGovernment/Institute might become liable in consequence of\ncontesting such claim.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0189",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 189,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 92230,
    "char_end": 93203,
    "char_count": 973,
    "text": "CLAUSE 18B\nENSURING PAYMENT AND AMENITIES TO WORKERS IF CONTRACTOR FAILS\nIn every case in which by virtue of the provisions of the contract Labour (Regulation andAbolition Act\n1970)\nand\nof\nthe\nContract\nLabour\nRegulation\nand\nAbolition\nCentral\nRules,1971,\nGovernment/Institute is obliged to pay any amounts of wages to workman employed by\ntheContractor in execution of the works, or to incur any expenditure in providing welfare andhealth\namenities required to be provided under the above said act and the rules underclause 19 or under\nthe rules framed by Government/Institute from to time for the protection of healthand sanitary\narrangements for workers employed by Government Contractor, Government/Institutewill recover\nfrom the Contractor the amount of wages so paid or the amount of expenditureso incurred and\nwithout prejudice to the right of the Government/ Institute under section 20 subsection(2) and section\n21 sub-section (4) of the Contract Labour (R&A) act 1970",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0190",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 190,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 93205,
    "char_end": 93762,
    "char_count": 557,
    "text": "Government/Institute shall be at liberty to recover such amount or any part thereof by deducting\nitfrom any sum due by the Government/Institute to the contractor whether under this agreement\norotherwise Government/Institute shall not be bound to contest any claim made against it\nundersection 20 sub-section (1) and section 21 sub section (4) of the said Act except on thewritten\nrequest of the Contractor and upon his giving to the Government/Institute full security for allcosts for\nwhich Government/Institute might become liable in contesting such claim.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0191",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 191,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 93764,
    "char_end": 94139,
    "char_count": 375,
    "text": "E30\n\nCLAUSE 19\nLABOUR LAWS/ SAFETY PROVISIONS TO BE COMPLIED BY THE CONTRACTOR\nContractor shall follow all laws, regulations and acts of Central/ State Government andother\nstatutory bodies relating to engaging labourers in work, wages and all relatedprovisions and\nindemnify Government/Institute against payment to be made under and for theobservance of the\nsaid labour laws.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0192",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 192,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 94141,
    "char_end": 94597,
    "char_count": 456,
    "text": "Engineer-in-Charge concerned shall have the right to deduct from the money due to thecontractor,\nany sum required or estimated to be required for making good the loss sufferedby a worker or\nworkers by reason of non-fulfillment of any of the conditions of the contractfor the benefit of the\nworkers, non-payment of wages or of deductions made from his ortheir wages which are not justified\nby their terms of the contract or non-observance of theRegulations.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0193",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 193,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 94599,
    "char_end": 94793,
    "char_count": 194,
    "text": "Further, contractor at his own expense shall arrange and comply with the safety provisionsas per\nStandard safety manual and health & sanitary arrangements for theworkers as per the extant rules.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0194",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 194,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 94795,
    "char_end": 95078,
    "char_count": 283,
    "text": "CLAUSE 20\nMINIMUM WAGES ACT\nContractor shall comply with all the provisions of the Minimum Wages Act 1948, ContractLabour\n(Regulation and Abolition) act, 1970 and rules framed thereunder and other labourlaws affecting\nContract Labour that may be brought into force from time to time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0195",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 195,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 95080,
    "char_end": 96220,
    "char_count": 1140,
    "text": "CLAUSE 21\nWORK NOT TO BE SUBLET - ACTION IN CASE OF INSOLVENCY\nThe contract shall not be assigned or sublet without the written approval of the Engineer-in-\nchargeand if the Contractor shall assign or sublet this contract or attempt to do so orbecome\ninsolvent or commence any insolvency proceedings or make any composition withhis creditors or\nattempt to do so or if any bribe gratuity, gift, loan, perquisite reward oradvantage, pecuniary or\notherwise shall either directly or indirectly be given, promised oroffered by the Contractor or any of\nhis employees or agents to any public officer or personin the employ of the Government/Institute in\nany way relating to his Officer or Employment, or if anysuch officer or person shall become in any\nway directly or indirectly interested in thecontract, the Engineer-in-charge may thereupon on behalf\nof the President of India/Director, NIT Meghalaya shallhave power to adopt any of the course\nspecified in Clause 3 as he may best deem suited inthe interest of Government/Institute, in the event\nof any of those courses being adopted theconsequences specified in the said clause 3 shall ensure.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0196",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 196,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 96222,
    "char_end": 97122,
    "char_count": 900,
    "text": "CLAUSE 22\nCOMPENSATION PAYABLE ARE WITHOUT REFERNCE TO ACTUAL LOSS ORDAMAGES\nAll sums payable by way of compensation under any of these conditions shall beconsidered as\nreasonable compensation to be applied to the use of Government withoutreference to the actual loss\nor damage sustained and whether or not any damage shallhave been sustained.\nDOS/ ISRO\nCLAUSE 23\nCHANGE IN FIRM’S CONSTITUTION TO BE INTIMATED.\nWhere the Contractor is a partnership firm, the previous approval in writing of the Engineer-in-\ncharge shall be obtained before any change is made in the constitution of the firm.Where the\nContractor is an individual or a Hindu undivided family business concern suchapproval as aforesaid\nshall like wise be obtained before the Contractor enters into anypartnership agreement where under\nthe partnership firm would have the right to carryoutthe work hereby undertaken by the Contractor. If",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0197",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 197,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 97124,
    "char_end": 97370,
    "char_count": 246,
    "text": "E31\n\nprevious approval as aforesaid is notobtained, the contractor shall be deemed to have been\nassigned in contravention ofclause 21 hereof and the same action may be taken and the same\nconsequences shallensure as provided in the said clause 21.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0198",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 198,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 97372,
    "char_end": 98716,
    "char_count": 1344,
    "text": "CLAUSE 24 – DELETED\n\nCLAUSE 25\nSETTLEMENT OF DISPUTES AND ARBITRATION\na) If any dispute or differences of any kind whatsoever were to arise between theEngineer-in-\ncharge, Engineering Section and the Contractor regarding the following matters namely.\ni)\nThe meaning of the specifications, designs, drawings and instructions hereinbefore\nmentioned.\nii)\nThe quality of workmanship or materials used on the work and\niii) Any other question, claim, right, matters, thing whatsoever in any way arising outof or\nrelating to the contract, designs, drawings, specifications, estimates,instructions or orders,\nor those conditions or failure to execute the same whetherarising during the progress of the\nwork after the completion, termination orabandonment thereof, the dispute shall, in the first\nplace be referred to the Executive Engineer/ Director, NIT Meghalaya who has Jurisdiction\nover the work specified in thecontract with the details of claims, justification for the same\nwith supportingdocuments such as analysis of rates, cash vouchers and other relevant\nparticulars.The Executive Engineer/ Director, NIT Meghalaya shall within a period of sixty\ndays from thedate of being requested by the Contractor to do so or from the date of\nfurnishing ofrequired particulars whichever is later shall give written notice of his decision to\nthecontractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0199",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 199,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 98718,
    "char_end": 99043,
    "char_count": 325,
    "text": "If the Engineer-in-Charge/Executive Engineer fails to give notice of his decision within a periodof 60\ndays from the date of receipt of (i) the Contractor’s request in writing forsettlement of dispute or\ndifference as aforesaid or (ii) relevant particulars from theContractor in support of his claims\nwhichever is later. (OR)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0200",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 200,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 99045,
    "char_end": 99551,
    "char_count": 506,
    "text": "If the decision of the Engineer-in-Charge/Executive Engineer is not acceptable to theContractor, he\nmay approach the Director of the Institute within a period of15 days from the date of expiry of 60\ndays specified above. The Director of theInstitute shall within a period of further 90 days from the\ndate of receipt of requestfrom the contractor or from the date of receipt of relevant particulars from\nthecontractor in support of claims whichever is later give notice of his decision (s) to theContractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0201",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 201,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 99553,
    "char_end": 99888,
    "char_count": 335,
    "text": "b) Subject to other forms of settlement hereinafter provided the Director of the Institutedecision in\nrespect of every dispute or difference so referred shall be final andbinding upon the Contractor.\nThe said decision shall forthwith be given effect to andContractor shall proceed with the\nexecution of the work with all due diligence.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0202",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 202,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 99890,
    "char_end": 100047,
    "char_count": 157,
    "text": "c)  Remedy\n\n1. When Director of the Institute decision is not acceptable to Contractor OR\n2. Director of the Institute fails to give decision within 90 days.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0203",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 203,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 100049,
    "char_end": 100393,
    "char_count": 344,
    "text": "In case the decision of the Director of the Institute is not acceptable to theContractor or Director of\nthe Institute fails to give decision within 90 days specifiedabove, the Contractor may approach the\nLaw court specified in Schedule ‘F’ forsettlement of dispute after giving due written notice in this\nregard to the Director of theInstitute.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0204",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 204,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 100395,
    "char_end": 100684,
    "char_count": 289,
    "text": "E32\n\nd) Whether the claim is referred to the Engineer-in-Charge/Executive Engineer/ Director of the\nInstitute orto the Law Courts, as the case may be, the Contractor shall proceed to execute\nandcomplete the works with all due diligence pending settlement of the said dispute ordifferences.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0205",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 205,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 100686,
    "char_end": 100794,
    "char_count": 108,
    "text": "Obligations of the Engineer-in-charge and Contractor shall remain unsettled duringconsiderations of\ndispute.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0206",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 206,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 100796,
    "char_end": 101316,
    "char_count": 520,
    "text": "e) The reference of any dispute or dispute (s) or difference(s) to Engineer-in-Charge/Executive\nEngineer or the Director of the Institute or the Law Court may proceed notwithstanding that the work\nshall then be or be alleged to be complete provided alwaysthat the obligations of the Engineer-in-\ncharge and the Contractor shall not be alteredby reason of the said dispute or difference being\nreferred to Engineer-in-Charge/Executive Engineer / Director of the Institute or the Law Court during\nthe progress of the works.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0207",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 207,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 101318,
    "char_end": 102699,
    "char_count": 1381,
    "text": "CLAUSE 25A\nSETTLEMENT OF DISPUTES BETWEEN CMG AND CENTRAL GOVERNMENTENTERPRISES\nIn the event of the contract being entered into between National Institute of Technology Meghalaya\nand aCentral Government Public Enterprises, supersession of above clause 25 of condition\nofContract the following clause shall apply ‘In the event of any dispute or difference relatingto the\ninterpretation and application of the provisions of the contracts, such dispute ordifference shall be\nreferred by either party to the arbitration of one of arbitrators in theDepartment of Public Enterprises\nto be nominated by the Secretary to the Government ofIndia, in charge of the Bureau of Public\nEnterprises. The arbitration Act, 1940 shall not beapplicable to the arbitration under this clause. The\naward of the arbitration shall be bindingupon the parties to the dispute provided; however any party\naggrieved by such award maymake further reference for setting aside or revision of the award to the\nLaw Secretary,Additional Secretary, when so authorized by the Law secretary, Department of\nLegalAffairs, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India. Upon such reference the\ndisputeshall be decided by the Law Secretary or the Secretary, whose decision shall bind theparties\nfinally and conclusively. The parties to the dispute will share equally the cost ofArbitration as\nintimated by the Arbitrator.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0208",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 208,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 102701,
    "char_end": 103821,
    "char_count": 1120,
    "text": "Provisions of clause 25 shall not be applicable to contracts where this clause 25A isapplicable and\nthe contracts for which clause 25A is not applicable clause 25 will beapplicable.\nDOS/ ISRO\nCLAUSE 26\nPATENT RIGHTS\nThe Contractor shall fully indemnify the President of India/Director, NIT Meghalaya against any\naction, claim orproceeding relating to infringement or use of any patent or design on any alleged\npatent ordesign right and shall pay any royalties which may be payable in respect of any article\norpart thereof included in the contract. In the event of any claims made under or actionbrought\nagainst Government in respect of such matters as aforesaid the Contractor shallbe immediately\nnotified thereof and the Contractor shall be at liberty, at his own expense,to settle any dispute or to\nconduct any litigation that may arise there from. Provided thatthe Contractor shall not be liable to\nindemnify the President of India/Director, NIT Meghalaya if the infringement ofthe patent or design of\nany alleged patent or design right is the direct result of an orderpassed by the Engineer-in-charge in\nthis behalf.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0209",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 209,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 103823,
    "char_end": 103951,
    "char_count": 128,
    "text": "CLAUSE 27 – DELETED\n\nCLAUSE 28 – RENUMBERED AS CLAUSE 11A\n\nCLAUSE 29\nWITHHOLDING AND LIEN IN RESPECT OF SUMS DUE FROM CONTRACTOR",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0210",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 210,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 103953,
    "char_end": 105168,
    "char_count": 1215,
    "text": "E33\n\n(i) Whenever any claim or claims for payment of a sum of money arises out of or underthe contract\nor against the contractor, the Engineer-in-Charge or theGovernment/Institute shall be entitled to\nwithhold and also have a lien to retainsuch sum or sums in whole or in part from the security, if\nany deposited by thecontractor and for the purpose aforesaid, the Engineer-in-Charge or\ntheGovernment/Institute shall be entitled to withhold the security deposit, if any,furnished as the\ncase may be and also have a lien over the same pending finalizationor adjudication of any such\nclaim. In the event of the security being insufficient tocover the claimed amount or amounts or if\nno\nsecurity\nhas\nbeen\ntaken\nfrom\nthecontractor,\nthe\nEngineer-in-Charge\nor\nthe\nGovernment/Institute shall be entitled towithhold and have a lien to retain to the extent of such\nclaimed amount or amountsreferred to above, from any sum or sums found payable or which\nmay at any timethereafter become payable to the contractor under the same contract or any\nothercontract with the Engineer-in-Charge of the Government/ Institute or anycontracting person\nthrough the Engineer-in-Charge pending finalization of adjudicationof any such claim.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0211",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 211,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 105170,
    "char_end": 106106,
    "char_count": 936,
    "text": "It is an agreed term of the contract that the sum of money or moneys so withheldretained under\nthe lien referred to above by the Engineer-in-charge or Government/Institute will be kept withheld\nor retained as such by the Engineer-in-charge orGovernment till the claim arising out of or under\nthe contract is determined by thecompetent court and that the contractor will have no claim for\ninterest or damageswhatsoever on any account in respect of such withholding or retention under\nthe lienreferred to above and duly notified as such to the contractor . For the purpose of\nthisclause, where the contractor is a partnership firm or a limited company, the Engineer-in-\ncharge or the Government shall be entitled to withhold and also have a lien to retaintowards\nsuch claimed amount or amounts in whole or in part from any sum foundpayable to any\npartner/limited company at the case may be, whether in his individualcapacity or otherwise.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0212",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 212,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 106108,
    "char_end": 107124,
    "char_count": 1016,
    "text": "(ii) Government/Institute shall have the right to cause an audit and TechnicalExamination of the\nwork and the final bills of the Contractor including all supportingvouchers abstract etc., to be\nmade after payment of the final bill and if as a result ofsuch audit and Technical Examination any\nsum is found to have been over paid inrespect of any work done by the Contractor under the\ncontract or any work claimed byhim to have been done by him under contract and found not to\nhave been executed,the Contractor shall be liable to refund the amount of over payment and it\nshall belawful for Government/Institute to recover the same from him in the mannerprescribed in\nsub clause (1) of this clause or in any other manner equally permissibleand if it is found that the\nContractor was paid less than what was due to him under theContract in respect of any work\nexecuted by him under it, the amount of such underpayment shall be duly paid by\nGovernment/Institute to the contractor, without anyinterest thereon whatsoever.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0213",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 213,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 107126,
    "char_end": 107503,
    "char_count": 377,
    "text": "Provided that the Government/Institute shall not be entitled to recover any sumoverpaid, nor the\ncontractor shall be entitled to payment of any sum paid short where suchpayment has been agreed\nupon between the Engineer-in-Charge on the one hand and thecontractor on the other under any\nterm of the contract permitting payment for work afterassessment by the Engineer in Charge.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0214",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 214,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 107505,
    "char_end": 108140,
    "char_count": 635,
    "text": "CLAUSE 29A\nLIEN IN RESPECT OF CLAIMS IN OTHER CONTRACTS\nAny sum of money due and payable to the Contractor (including Security Depositreturnable to him)\nunder the contract may be withheld or retained by way of lien by theEngineer-in-charge or the\nGovernment/ Institute or any other contracting person orpersons through Engineer-in-charge against\nany claim of the Engineer-in-charge or theGovernment/ Institute or such other person or persons in\nrespect of payment of a sumof money arising out of or under any other contract made by the\nContractor with theEngineer in charge or Government/Institute or with such other person or persons.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0215",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 215,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 108142,
    "char_end": 108786,
    "char_count": 644,
    "text": "E34\n\nIt is an agreed term of the contract that the sum of the money so withheld or retained underthis\nclause by the Engineer-in-charge or the Government/ Institute will be kept withheldor retained as\nsuch by the Engineer-in-charge or the Government/ Institute or till hisclaim arising out of the same\ncontract or any other contract is either mutually settled ordetermined by the competent court, as the\ncase may be and that the contractor shall haveno claim for interest or damages whatsoever on this\naccount or on any other ground inrespect of any sum of money withheld or retained under this\nclause and duly notified assuch to the contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0216",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 216,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 108788,
    "char_end": 109106,
    "char_count": 318,
    "text": "CLAUSE 30\nTERMINATION OF CONTRACT ON DEATH OF THE CONTRACTOR\nWithout prejudice to any of the rights or remedies under this contract, if the Contractor dies,the\nEngineer-in-charge on behalf of the President/Director, NIT Meghalaya shall have the option of\nterminating thecontract without compensation to the Contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0217",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 217,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 109108,
    "char_end": 109694,
    "char_count": 586,
    "text": "CLAUSE 31\nWATER SUPPLY\nThe contractor(s) shall make his/their own arrangements for water required for the workand nothing\nextra will be paid for the same. This will be subject to the following conditions.\ni)\nThat the water used by the contractor(s) shall be fit for construction purposes tothe satisfaction\nof the Engineer-in-Charge.\nii) The Engineer-in-Charge shall make alternative arrangements for supply of water at therisk and\ncost of contractor(s) if the arrangements made by the contractor(s) forprocurement of water are\nin the opinion of the Engineer-in- Charge, unsatisfactory.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0218",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 218,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 109696,
    "char_end": 110526,
    "char_count": 830,
    "text": "Institute Supply, if available:\nWater, if available and sparable, may be supplied to the contractor by Institute only atthe single point\nsubject to the following conditions:-\ni)\nThe water charges @1 % shall be recovered on gross amount of the work done.\nii) The contractor(s) shall make his/their own arrangement of water connection and layingof\npipelines from existing main of source of supply.\niii) The Institute do not guarantee to maintain uninterrupted supply of water and it willbe incumbent\non the contractor(s) to make alternative arrangements for water at his/their own cost in the event\nof any temporary break down in the Government/Institutewater main so that the progress of\nhis/their work is not held up for want of water. Noclaim of damage or refund of water charges will\nbe entertained on account of suchbreak down.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0219",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 219,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 110528,
    "char_end": 111866,
    "char_count": 1338,
    "text": "Alternative water arrangements:\ni)\nWhere there is no piped water supply arrangement and the water is taken by theContractor from\nthe wells or hand pump constructed by the Government/Institute nocharge shall be recovered\nfrom the Contractor on that account. The Contractor shall,however, draw water at such hours of\nthe day that it does not interfere with the normaluse for which the hand pump and wells are\nintended. He will also be responsible for alldamage and abnormal repairs arising out of his use,\nthe cost of which shall berecoverable from him. The Engineer-in-charge shall be the final\nauthority to determinethe cost recoverable from the Contractor on this account.\nii) The Contractor shall be allowed to construct temporary wells in Government/Institute land for\ntaking water for construction purposes only after he has gotpermission of the Engineer-in-charge\nin writing. No charges shall be recovered fromthe Contractor on this account, but the Contractor\nshall be required to providenecessary safety arrangements to avoid any accidents or damage to\nadjacentbuildings, roads and service lines. He shall also be responsible, for any accidents\nordamage caused due to construction and subsequent maintenance of the wells andshall restore\nthe ground to its original condition after the wells are dismantled oncompletion of the work.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0220",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 220,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 111868,
    "char_end": 112865,
    "char_count": 997,
    "text": "E35\n\nCLAUSE 32\nELECTRICITY\nElectricity, if available in the premises and sparable, may be provided to the contractor bythe\nInstitute only at the single point subject to the following conditions:-\ni)\nThe Contractor has to make his own arrangement to tap Electricity from a 3 phase/single phase\nsupply from location decided by Engineer-in-charge. Electricity supply willbe made available only\non metered basis. Electric charges will be recovered at actuals.\nii) In all cases where/when the energy meter is not installed, defective energy meter is notreplaced\nor not rectified immediately, the consumption charges towards electricity willbe recovered on the\nbasis of the total wattage of the load multiplied by the number of hours utilized. In all such cases\nthe Contractor shall maintain a log book indicatingwattage of the load and hours of consumption\nand get the same attested by Engineer-in-charge at appropriate time without fail. The decision of\nEngineer-in-charge in thematter shall be final.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0221",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 221,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 112867,
    "char_end": 112972,
    "char_count": 105,
    "text": "Note: Please refer Guide lines for temporary power supply at site and general safetyprocedures,\nattached.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0222",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 222,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 112974,
    "char_end": 114274,
    "char_count": 1300,
    "text": "CLAUSE 33\nRETURN OF GOVERNMENT SURPLUS NATERIALS TO GOVERNMENT\nNot with standing any thing contained to the contrary in any or all the clauses of thiscontract where\nany materials for the execution of the contract are procured with theassistance of\nGovernment/Instituteeither by issue from Government/Institute stocks or purchase underorders\nmade or permits or licenses issued by the Government, the Contractor shall hold thesaid material as\ntrustee for Government/Institute and use such materials economically and solelyfor the purpose of\nthe contract and not dispose off them without the permission of theGovernment/Institute and return,\nif required by Engineer-in-charge all surplus, serviceable materialsthat may be left with him after the\ncompletion of the contract or at its termination for anyreason whatsoever on being paid or credited\nsuch price as the Engineer-in-charge shalldetermine having due regard to the condition of the\nmaterial. The price allowed to theContractor, however, shall not exceed the amount charged to him\nexcluding the storagecharges, if any. The contractor shall also not be entitled to cartage and\nincidental chargesfor returning the surplus materials from and to the stores where from they were\nissued.The decision of Engineer-in-charge shall be final and conclusive.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0223",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 223,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 114276,
    "char_end": 114655,
    "char_count": 379,
    "text": "In the event of breach of aforesaid conditions the contractor shall in addition to throwinghimself open\nto action for contravention of the terms of licenses or permits and/or forcriminal breach of trust, be\nliable to compensate the Government/Institute for all money,advantages or profits resulting or which\nin the usual course would have resulted to him byreason of such breach.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0224",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 224,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 114657,
    "char_end": 114750,
    "char_count": 93,
    "text": "CLAUSE 34 – DELETED\n\nCLAUSE 35 – DELETED\n\nCLAUSE 36\nEMPLOYMENT OF GRADUATE/ DIPLOMA ENGINEERS",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0225",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 225,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 114752,
    "char_end": 115017,
    "char_count": 265,
    "text": "Contractors Superintendence, Supervision, Technical Staff & Employees\n(i) The contractor shall provide all necessary superintendence during execution of thework and all\nalong thereafter as may be necessary for proper fulfilling of the obligationsunder the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0226",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 226,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 115019,
    "char_end": 115294,
    "char_count": 275,
    "text": "The contractor shall immediately after receiving letter of acceptance of the tender andbefore\ncommencement of the work, intimate in writing to the Engineer-in-Charge, thename(s),\nqualifications, experience, age, address(s) and other particulars along withcertificates, of the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0227",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 227,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 115296,
    "char_end": 116259,
    "char_count": 963,
    "text": "E36\n\nprincipal technical representative to be in charge of the work and othertechnical representative(s)\nwho will be supervising the work. Minimum requirement of suchtechnical representative(s) and their\nqualifications and experience shall not be lower thanspecified in Schedule ‘F’. The Engineer-in-\nCharge shall within 3 days of receipt of suchcommunication intimate in writing his approval or\notherwise of such a representative(s) tothe contractor. Any such approval may at any time be\nwithdrawn and in case of suchwithdrawal, the contractor shall appoint another such\nrepresentative(s) according to theprovisions of this clause. Decision of the tender accepting authority\nshall be final andbinding on the contractor in this respect. Such a principal technical representative\nandother technical representative(s) shall be appointed by the contractor soon after receipt ofthe\napproval from Engineer-in-charge and shall be available at site before start of work.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0228",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 228,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 116261,
    "char_end": 117204,
    "char_count": 943,
    "text": "All the provisions applicable to the principal technical representative under the Clause willalso be\napplicable to other technical representative(s). The principal technicalrepresentative and other\ntechnical representative (s) shall be present at the site of work forsupervision at all times when any\nconstruction activity is in progress and also presenthimself/themselves, as required, to the Engineer-\nin-Charge and/or his designatedrepresentative to take instructions. Instructions given to the principal\ntechnicalrepresentative or other technical representative(s) shall be deemed to have the same\nforceas if these have been given to the contractor. The principal technical representative andother\ntechnical representative(s) shall be actually available the decision of the Engineer-in-Charge as\nrecorded in the site order book and measurement recorded checked/testchecked in Measurement\nBooks shall be final and binding on the contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0229",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 229,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 117206,
    "char_end": 118692,
    "char_count": 1486,
    "text": "Further if the contractor fails to appoint suitable technical Principal technical representativeand/or\nother technical representative(s) and if such appointed persons are not effectivelypresent or are\nabsent by more than two days without duly approved substitute or do notdischarge their\nresponsibilities satisfactorily, the Engineer-in-Charge shall have full powersto suspend the execution\nof the work until such date as suitable other technicalrepresentative(s) is/are appointed and the\ncontractor shall be held responsible for the delayso caused to the work. The contractor shall submit\na certificate of employment of thetechnical representative(s) along with every on account bill/ final\nbill and shall produceevidence if at any time so required by the Engineer-in-Charge at site fully\nduring all stagesof execution of work, during recording/checking/ test checking of measurements of\nworksand whenever so required by the Engineer-in-Charge and shall also note down\ninstructionsconveyed by the Engineer-in- Charge or his designated representative(s) in the site\norderbook and shall affix his/ their signature in token of noting down the instructions and in tokenof\nacceptance\nof\nmeasurements/\nchecked\nmeasurements/test\nchecked\nmeasurements.The\nrepresentative(s) shall not look after any other work. Substitutes, duly approved byEngineer-in-\nCharge of the work in similar manner as aforesaid shall be provided in event ofabsence of any of the\nrepresentative(s) by more than two days.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0230",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 230,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 118694,
    "char_end": 119045,
    "char_count": 351,
    "text": "If the Engineer-in-Charge, whose decision in this respect is final and binding on thecontractor, is\nconvinced that no such technical representative(s) is/are effectively appointedor is/are effectively\nattending or fulfilling the provision of this clause, a recovery (nonrefundable)shall be effected from\nthe contractor as specified in Schedule ‘F’ and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0231",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 231,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 119047,
    "char_end": 119286,
    "char_count": 239,
    "text": "(ii) The contractor shall provide and employ on the site only such technical assistantsas are skilled\nand experienced in their respective fields and such foremen and supervisorystaff as are\ncompetent to give proper supervision to the work.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0232",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 232,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 119288,
    "char_end": 119429,
    "char_count": 141,
    "text": "The contractor shall provide and employ skilled, semiskilled and unskilled labour as isnecessary for\nproper and timely execution of the work.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0233",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 233,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 119431,
    "char_end": 119944,
    "char_count": 513,
    "text": "E37\n\nThe Engineer-in-Charge shall be at liberty to object to and require the contractor to removefrom the\nworks any person who in his opinion misconducts himself, or is incompetent ornegligent in the\nperformance of his duties or whose employment is otherwise consideredby the Engineer-in-Charge\nto be undesirable. Such person shall not be employed again atworks site without the written\npermission of the Engineer-in-Charge and the persons soremoved shall be replaced as soon as\npossible by competent substitutes.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0234",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 234,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 119946,
    "char_end": 120254,
    "char_count": 308,
    "text": "CLAUSE 37 – DELETED\n\nCLAUSE 38 – DELETED\n\nCLAUSE 38A – DELETED\n\nCLAUSE 39\nRELATIVE WORKING WITH INSTITUTE\nIt is presumed that the Contractor is not related to any of the officers of the National Institute of\nTechnology Meghalaya. If he has any such relatives full particulars of the same should be furnished.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0235",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 235,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 120256,
    "char_end": 120956,
    "char_count": 700,
    "text": "CLAUSE 40\nRESTRICTION FOR EMPLOYING RETIRED GOVERNMENT SERVANT\nNo Engineer of Gazetted rank or other Gazetted officer employed in Engineering orAdministrative\nduties in the Engineering Department of the Government of India shall workas a Contractor or\nemploy of contractor for a period of one year after his retirement fromGovernment service without\nthe previous permission of Government of India in writing.This contract is liable to be cancelled if\neither the Contractor or any of his employees isfound at any time to be such a person who had not\nobtained the permission of Governmentof India as aforesaid before submission of the tender or\nengagement in the Contractor’sservice as the case may be.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0236",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 236,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 120958,
    "char_end": 122613,
    "char_count": 1655,
    "text": "CLAUSE 41\nRETURN OF MATERIALS & RECOVERY FOR EXCESS MATERIAL ISSUED\ni) After completion of the work and also at any intermediate stage in the event of nonreconciliationof\nmaterials issued, consumed and in balance - (see Clause 10),theoretical quantity of materials\nissued by the Government/Institute for use in the work shallbe calculated on the basis and\nmethod given hereunder:-\na. Quantity of cement & bitumen shall be calculated on the basis of quantity ofcement &\nbitumen required for different items of work as shown in the Scheduleof Rates mentioned in\nSchedule ‘F’. In case any item is executed for whichstandard constants for the consumption\nof cement or bitumen are not availablein the above mentioned schedule/statement or cannot\nbe derived from the sameshall be calculated on the basis of standard formula to be laid down\nby theEngineer-in-Charge.\nb. Theoretical quantity of steel reinforcement or structural steel sections shall betaken as the\nquantity required as per design or as authorized by Engineer-in-Charge, including authorized\nlappages, chairs etc. plus 3% wastage due tocutting into pieces, such theoretical quantity\nbeing determined and comparedwith the actual issues each diameter wise, section wise and\ncategory wiseseparately.\nc. Theoretical quantity of G.I. & C.I. or other pipes, conduits, wires and cables, piglead and\nG.I./M.S. sheets shall be taken as quantity actually required andmeasured plus 5% for\nwastage due to cutting into pieces (except in the case ofG.I./M.S. sheets it shall be 10%),\nsuch determination & comparison being madediameter wise & category wise.\nd.  For any other material as per actual requirements.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0237",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 237,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 122615,
    "char_end": 123523,
    "char_count": 908,
    "text": "E38\n\nii) Over the theoretical quantities of materials so computed a variation shall be allowedas specified in\nSchedule ‘F’. The difference in the net quantities of material actuallyissued to the contractor and the\ntheoretical quantities including such authorizedvariation, if not returned by the contractor or if not\nfully reconciled to the satisfactionof the Engineer-in- Charge, within fifteen days of the issue of\nwritten notice by theEngineer-in-charge to this effect shall be recovered at the rates specified\ninSchedule ‘F’, without prejudice to the provision of the relevant conditions regarding return of\nmaterials governing the contract. Decision of Engineer-in-Charge in regard to theoretical quantities\nof materials, which should have been actually used as perthe Annexure of the standard schedule of\nrates and recovery at rates specified inSchedule ‘F’, shall be final & binding on the contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0238",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 238,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 123525,
    "char_end": 123718,
    "char_count": 193,
    "text": "For non scheduled items, the decision of the Engineer-in-Charge regarding theoretical quantities of\nmaterials which should have been actually used, shall be final and binding on the contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0239",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 239,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 123720,
    "char_end": 123964,
    "char_count": 244,
    "text": "iii) The said action under this clause is without prejudice to the right of the Government/Institute to\ntake action against the contractor under any other conditions of contract for not doing the work\naccording to the prescribed specifications.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0240",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 240,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 123966,
    "char_end": 124443,
    "char_count": 477,
    "text": "CLAUSE 42 – DELETED\n\nCLAUSE 43\nAPPRENTICE ACT TO BE COMPLIED WITH\nThe Contractor shall comply with the provisions of the Apprentices Act 1961 and the rules and\norders issued there under from time to time. If he fails to do so his failure will be a breach of the\ncontract and the Engineer-in-charge may in his discretion cancel the contract. The Contractor shall\nalso be liable for any pecuniary liability arising on account of any violation by him of the provisions of\nthe Act.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0241",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "paragraph_index": 241,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 124445,
    "char_end": 125339,
    "char_count": 894,
    "text": "CLAUSE 44 – DELETED\n\nCLAUSE 45\nRELEASE OF SECURITY DEPOSIT AFTER LABOUR CLEARANCE\nSecurity Deposit of the work shall not be refunded till the contractor produces a clearance certificate\nfrom the Labour Officer. As soon as the work is virtually complete the contractor shall apply for the\nclearance certificate to the Labour Officer under intimation to the Engineer- in- charge. The\nEngineer-in-charge, on receipt of the said communication, shall write to the Labour Officer to\nintimate if any complaint, its pending against the contractor in respect of the work. If no complaint is\npending, on record till after 3 months after completion of the work and/or no communication is\nreceived from the Labour Officer to this effect till six months after the date of completion, it will be\ndeemed to have received the clearance certificate and the Security Deposit will be released if\notherwise due./ I",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
