    "paragraph_index": 6,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 575,
    "char_end": 978,
    "char_count": 403,
    "text": "Page 3 of 28\n\nPART - A\nADDITIONAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\n1.\nThe following Additional Conditions of Contract shall be read in conjunction with General\nConditions of Contract. If there are any provisions in these Additional Conditions of Contract,\nwhich are at variance with the provisions of General Conditions of Contract, the provisions in\nthese Additional Conditions of Contract shall take precedence.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0007",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 7,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 980,
    "char_end": 1261,
    "char_count": 281,
    "text": "2.\nINTRODUCTION:\n\nChennai sub region office of ESIC covers the following Establishments under ARM works: -\n\nESI Hospital at K.K Nagar, Tamil Nadu is a 1000 bedded Hospital, located in\nChennai, Tamil Nadu having OPD/OT &24x7, Admin Block, Old Building, Staff\nQuarters and Hostels..",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0008",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 8,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 1263,
    "char_end": 1508,
    "char_count": 245,
    "text": "“Annual Repair and Maintenance of Electrical works of building including Operation of various Electro-\nMechanical, Equipment’s and plants in ESI Establishments at K.K Nagar, Chennai of Tamil Nadu Region\nfor FY 2023-24”” on Percentage Rate Basis.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0009",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 9,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 1510,
    "char_end": 1609,
    "char_count": 99,
    "text": "1. ESIC Hospital & Medical College, K.K Nagar, Chennai\n2. ESIC Staff Quarters at K.K Nagar, Chennai",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0010",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 10,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 1611,
    "char_end": 1766,
    "char_count": 155,
    "text": "EPI invites offer from the eligible BIDDERS on Percentage Rate Basis to execute the above\nworks and detailed scope of work is mentioned in subsequent para.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0011",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 11,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 1768,
    "char_end": 2116,
    "char_count": 348,
    "text": "The Bidder shall acquaint himself by a visit to the site, with the conditions prevailing at\nsite before submission of the bid. The information given here in under is for general\nguidance and shall not be contractually binding on EPI/ESIC. All relevant site data /\ninformation as may be necessary shall have to be obtained / collected by the Bidder.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0012",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 12,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 2118,
    "char_end": 2199,
    "char_count": 81,
    "text": "3.\nSCOPE OF WORK :\n\nThe project site for the work is clear and readily available.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0013",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 13,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 2201,
    "char_end": 2627,
    "char_count": 426,
    "text": "The brief scope of work included in this tender shall include (but not limited to) “Annual Repair and\nMaintenance of Electrical works of building including Operation of various Electro-Mechanical, Equipment’s\nand plants in ESI Establishments at K.K Nagar, Chennai of Tamil Nadu Region for FY 2023-24” on Percentage\nRate Basis.\n1. ESIC Hospital & Medical College, K.K Nagar, Chennai\n2. ESIC Staff Quarters at K.K Nagar, Chennai",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0014",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 14,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 2629,
    "char_end": 2719,
    "char_count": 90,
    "text": "Works shall be carried out including all required labour, tools and tackles.\n\nPage 4 of 28",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0015",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 15,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 2721,
    "char_end": 2985,
    "char_count": 264,
    "text": "The scope of work is indicative but not limited to the given below.\" (Here in after referred to\nas “Works’). The Contractor shall execute the works as per BOQ /as per Instruction of EIC of\nEPIL/ Client Engineers on suit to site basis to meet the ESIC requirements.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0016",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 16,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 2987,
    "char_end": 3485,
    "char_count": 498,
    "text": "The contractor will be responsible for Annual Repair and Maintenance of following works in\nthe ESIC Establishments / Campuses as indicated in the Bid Documents below:\n(1) Buildings Repair and Maintenance of Civil Works/Nature including materials\n(2) Building Repair and Maintenance of Electrical Works/Nature including consumables\n(3) Water Supply, Sanitary Plumbing Maintenance work\n(4) Sewage line Repair works & Sewage Disposal Work\n(5) External Service works inside campuses of ESIC Properties.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0017",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 17,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 3487,
    "char_end": 5251,
    "char_count": 1764,
    "text": "a) All the essential activities required for the functional completion of each item / scope of\nwork is also to be executed as directed by Engineer-in-Charge.\nb) All men, materials, machinery, tools and plants, infra-structure, resources etc., as required\nfor execution of “Works” shall be provided and arranged by CONTRACTOR for their\nportion of work. The amount/rate quoted in their offer by CONTRACTOR to EPI includes\nall charges, all direct and indirect cost of works, materials, labour, tools & tackles, plant &\nequipment, all taxes, duties, levies, royalties, and labour welfare cess etc., all\ntransportation charges including for cartage of issue materials, electricity and water\ncharges, site offices expenses, labour camp, bank guarantee charges, insurance charges\n(up to any port of India for imported materials only), ESI/EPF/ Statutory contributions,\npreparation of all required design & detailed engineering and all required drawings etc.,\nother expenses whatsoever, incurred on execution, completion and maintenance of the\n“Works” as per ‘Tender Documents’ and their own overheads and profit etc.\nCONTRACTOR shall comply with all the requirements laid down as per ‘Tender\nDocuments’ as per terms, conditions, specifications, drawings, documents etc. given in\nthe ‘Tender Documents’ for the completion, handing over, maintenance period etc. for the\nproject. The contractor will not be allowed to take out equipment’s from the site without\nthe written permission of ESIC/EPI.\nc) The contractor / vendor has to stack adequate quantity of repair & maintenance materials\nfor 15 days requirement. The required stacking arrangements including Sheds, yard as\nper CPWD norms shall be made by the contractor. No extra claims in this regard shall be\nentertained.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0018",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 18,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 5252,
    "char_end": 5880,
    "char_count": 628,
    "text": "d) The plant & equipment once brought to site for works shall not be allowed to be removed\nwithout the consent of EPI.\ne) The contractor has to procure all the construction materials as per approved makes as\nmentioned in Bid Document.\nf) Water and Power for the work shall be the responsibility of the contractor. EPI shall not be\nresponsible for arranging the same.\ng) The work executed by CONTRACTOR shall be subject to audit and quality control checks\nfrom Quality Control Division & Technical Audit of EPI, Client and chief Technical\nExaminer of Central Vigilance commission, Govt. of India. In the eventuality of any defect",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0019",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 19,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 5882,
    "char_end": 6501,
    "char_count": 619,
    "text": "Page 5 of 28\n\n/ sub-standard works as brought out in the report or noticed otherwise at any time during\nexecution, maintenance period etc., the same shall be made good by the CONTRACTOR\nat no extra cost to EPI.\nh) The CONTRACTOR shall ensure compliance with all Central, State and Local laws,\nRules, Regulations etc. as applicable or may be applicable during the course of execution,\nmaintenance etc. of the works and shall indemnify EPI against any claim for damages\nwhatsoever on such accounts. The CONTRACTOR shall keep EPI indemnified at all\ntimes against infringement of any Patent or Intellectual Property Rights.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0020",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 20,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 6503,
    "char_end": 7788,
    "char_count": 1285,
    "text": "3.1. Other Conditions of Work\n\n3.1.1. The Replacement of Consumables like Bulbs, Tube-lights etc. shall be limited to areas of\nOffice Buildings, Hospital Buildings, Public area of Staff Quarters only. Procurement of\nthese types of consumables inside the staff quarters shall be done by the allottee\nhimself.\n3.1.2. The work of essential Repair and Maintenance and operation of essential services shall\nunder no circumstances be held up.\n3.1.3. For each of the properties (or a group of properties so approved by EPI/ ESIC), the\ncontractor shall maintain a Complaint Book at the site and all complaints will be entered\nin the said book which shall be periodically seen by the Officers of EPI/ESIC and as soon\nas the work is completed, suitable remarks shall be given in the Register. This Register\nshould also be periodically seen by the Senior Officer of EPI and signed in token of\nhaving seen the same. The book shall also be available for scrutiny of ESIC and / or the\nOccupier of the property and their representatives.\n3.1.4. EPI can withdraw the work from the contractor at any time after giving fifteen days’ notice\nwithout assigning any reason thereof. In such an event, EPI will not accept any liability\non account of workers engaged by the contractor and on any other account.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0021",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 21,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 7790,
    "char_end": 8590,
    "char_count": 800,
    "text": "4.\nORDER OF PRECEDENCE:\nClause 42.1 of GCC stands amended as under:\nIn case of difference, contradiction, discrepancy, dispute with regard to Conditions of\nContract, Specifications, Drawings, Bill of Quantities and Rates quoted by the Contractor\nand other documents forming part of the contract, the following shall prevailing order of\nprecedence\n4.1\nContract Agreement which includes NIT, Special Instructions to Tenderer ,\nMemorandum.\n4.2\nLetter of Intent, detailed letter of Work Order\n4.3\nBill of Quantity/Schedule of Quantities\n4.4\nAdditional Conditions of Contract (EPIL ACC)\n4.5\nGeneral Conditions of Contract (EPILGCC).\n4.6\nCPWD Technical Specifications & DSR (Latest Edition)\n4.7\nTN PWD & TN TWAD Technical Specification & SSR/SOR (Latest Edition)\n4.8\nNational Building Code (Latest Edition)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0022",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 22,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 6,
    "char_start": 8592,
    "char_end": 8768,
    "char_count": 176,
    "text": "Page 6 of 28\n\n4.9\nBIS Specifications\n\n5.\nTIME SCHEDULE & PROGRESS\n\nThe clause No.’ 43.0’ of General Conditions of Contract (GCC) of this Tender document\nshall be read as under:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0023",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 23,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 6,
    "char_start": 8770,
    "char_end": 9259,
    "char_count": 489,
    "text": "The contract period for completion of entire work under scope shall be 7.50 (Seven and\nHalf) Months from the “COMMENCEMENT OF CONTRACT PERIOD” as specified. The\ncontractor should complete the all works including testing of materials as per scope of BOQ\nwithin above specified period and as per the instructions of Engineer-in-charge. However,\nEPIL is having liberty to Pre-close or extend the completion period as per the requirement at\nany point of time during the course of the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0024",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 24,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 6,
    "char_start": 9261,
    "char_end": 9515,
    "char_count": 254,
    "text": "6.\nCOMMENCEMENT OF CONTRACT PERIOD\n\nThe responsibility of the contractor shall start from the date of acceptance of LOI. The Actual\ndate of start shall be considered from the date of Signing of agreement / issue of Work order.\n7.\nDEFECT LIABILITY PERIOD:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0025",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 25,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 6,
    "char_start": 9517,
    "char_end": 9758,
    "char_count": 241,
    "text": "Defect Liability Period as per GCC Clause No: 74.0 is stands amended as below:\n\nThe Contractor shall be responsible for the rectification of defects in the works for a period  of\n06 Months (Six Months) from the date of completion of project.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0026",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 26,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 6,
    "char_start": 9760,
    "char_end": 9849,
    "char_count": 89,
    "text": "8.\nSECURITY DEPOSIT CUM PERFORMANCE BANK GUARANTEE Clause 9.0 of GCC is\namended as below:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0027",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 27,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 6,
    "char_start": 9851,
    "char_end": 10867,
    "char_count": 1016,
    "text": "8.1. In the event of award of work, contactor shall submit security deposit @ 5% (Five Percent\nonly) of the contract value of the accepted tender within 21 (twenty-one) days from the\ndate of issue of Letter of Intent (LOI). lf required, any extension of time beyond 21 days\nand up to 60 days may be granted by the Competent Authority. However a penal rate of\ninterest @12% per annum shall be charged for the delay in submission of Security Deposit\nafter 21(twenty-one) days i.e. from 22nd day to the date of submission of Security Deposit\nbut within 60 days after the date of issue of PO/ LOl. Further, if 60th day happens to be\ndeclared holiday in the concerned office of EPl, submission of Security Deposit can be\naccepted on the next working day. The SDPG shall be submitted in the form of Bank\nGuarantee (as per format in GCC), from any Nationalized bank / Scheduled Bank / or in the\nform of Insurance Security Bonds or Account Payee Demand Draft or Fixed Deposit\nReceipt or online Payment in an acceptable form.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0028",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 28,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 6,
    "char_start": 10869,
    "char_end": 11039,
    "char_count": 170,
    "text": "8.2. This SDPG shall remain valid up to 90 (ninety) days after the end of defects liability period\nand shall kept valid by proper renewal till the acceptance of EPI/ESIC.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
