    "char_start": 11433,
    "char_end": 11919,
    "char_count": 486,
    "text": "9.\nRETENTION MONEY\n\nClause no.10.0 of GCC stands amended as below.\n“The Retention Money shall be deducted from each running bill of the Contractor at 5% (five\npercent only) of the gross value of the Running Account bill. The Earnest Money Deposited\nby the tenderer in the form of Demand Draft will be treated as part of the Retention Money.\nThe Retention Money shall be refunded to the Contractor upon Completion of Work or on\npayment of the amount of the final bill whichever is later.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0032",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 32,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 11921,
    "char_end": 12033,
    "char_count": 112,
    "text": "10.\nSECURED ADVANCE:(Clause no 35 of GCC): -   - NA –\n\n11.\nMobilization Advance:(Clause no 8.0 of GCC):-   - NA-",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0033",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 33,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 12035,
    "char_end": 13709,
    "char_count": 1674,
    "text": "12.\nPAYMENT CONDITIONS:-\nClause no 37.0 of GCC stands good and the following clauses are also part of that,\n12.1. Interim RA Bills in the form of monthly running bills prepared by the contractor in soft as\nwell as Hard copies shall be based on the quantities executed and measured. The\nmeasurements accepted by the EPIL for corresponding item will be taken for payment.\n12.2. Billing - All the day to day maintenance work will be executed on the basis of the\ndemand received through Complaint Form/ Call Slips and payment will be made as per\nactual execution and as per certified measurement of the executed work at site. A\nsample Complaints Form is enclosed in ANNEXURE A of Technical Specification. The\nsame is to printed and kept in bulk with the concerned departments.\n12.2.1. The contractor will have to submit the bill in 02 (two) sets positively within 7th day of\neach following month with original Complaints Forms / Original call slips.\n12.2.2. Payment is to be made on submission of bill (02 sets) along with performance /\ncompletion certificate & necessary supporting documents after completion of work. An\nundertaking regarding compliance of all statutory liabilities i.e. minimum wages, ESI, PF\netc. (as applicable) must have to be submitted along with bill.\n12.2.3. All the monthly operation bills of Manpower must be supported with the following\ndocuments-\n Copy of work order issued by the competent authority.\n Copy of Attendance Register / Copy of BAS Attendance signed & sealed by contractor\n Wages slip of workers / labours signed by workers & certified by the contractor.\n Challan of deposited amount against ESI, PF etc. against individual workers.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0034",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 34,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 13711,
    "char_end": 14634,
    "char_count": 923,
    "text": "Page 8 of 28\n\n GST paid challan / copy of previous month.\n Bank statement regarding the wages paid to the workers electronically (without any type\nof cash transaction) through NEFT, RTGS or similar way.\n12.2.4. All the maintenance bills must be supported with the followings documents-\n Work ordered issued by the competent authority.\n Valid original work done Complaints Forms from the department concern.\n Monthly log book record for routine checks and maintenance throughout the hospital, if\nany.\n GST paid challan / copy of previous month.\n12.2.5. Any deduction made towards, safety, ESHS, Quality issues etc., if any, will be deducted\nfrom contractor on pro rata basis.\n12.2.6. Final Bill Payment shall be released upon receipt of the due deposit amount received\nfrom the owner / ESIC and also satisfying the submission of required documents as\nmentioned in Clause No.31 in this additional condition of contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0035",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 35,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 14636,
    "char_end": 15284,
    "char_count": 648,
    "text": "13.\nMETHOD OF MEASUREMENT\n\nFollowing clauses shall be read in conjunction with Clause no 36.0 of GCC\nMode of measurement shall be as per relevant clauses of technical specification of this\ntender. In case the same is not available the relevant IS 1200 in conjunction with IS\n3385 shall be adopted. In case the same is also not available; the standard procedure\nadopted in CPWD shall be adopted. In case the same is not available in CPWD also,\nthe measurement of the work done will be based on the mutual agreement between\nEPI/ESIC and contractor. In all the above cases, the interpretation of EPI / ESIC will be\nfinal and binding to the contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0036",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 36,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 15286,
    "char_end": 15464,
    "char_count": 178,
    "text": "Removable / dismantling and disposal of Loose concrete, if any shall be under the\nscope contractor. If contractor fails which EPI will execute the same in bidder’s risk and\ncost.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0037",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 37,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 15466,
    "char_end": 15870,
    "char_count": 404,
    "text": "14.\nQuantity, items & works as mentioned in the price bid are completely tentative in nature and\nthe same have been derived on the basis of last few years demand of the hospital &\nexecution at site which may increase/ decrease or deviate from the given Quantity, items &\nworks. However, prior approval should be taken from EPI/ESIC for any abnormal variation in\nquantities even if the situation warrants.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0038",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 38,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 15872,
    "char_end": 16101,
    "char_count": 229,
    "text": "15.\nTAXES AND DUTIES:\n\nThe following shall be also read in conjunction with clause no 13 of GCC:\n15.1.1.\nThe bidder/Contractor must be registered with GST and should have valid GSTIN\nnumber of the respective state of the project.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
