    "char_start": 28119,
    "char_end": 28433,
    "char_count": 314,
    "text": "33.\nLABOUR CAMP:\n\nThe Contractor shall be responsible for accommodation, feeding and sanitary necessities,\nfor their employed persons. The Contractor shall make his own arrangement for labour\ncamp for his labour. No labour camp shall be allowed inside the project site. EPIL shall not\nprovide land for labour camp.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0078",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 78,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 28435,
    "char_end": 29515,
    "char_count": 1080,
    "text": "34.\nTESTS AND INSPECTION:\n\n34.1. Clause no 53.1 of GCC stands good and in addition to that the following shall be\napplicable. Lab/testing equipment if any have to be procured and installed by contractor, if\nrequired. Later on expenditure can be shared after other contractor deployed.\n34.2. All works executed or under the course of execution in pursuance of this contract shall at\nall times be open to inspection and supervision of EPI. The work during its progress or after\nits completion may also be inspected, by Chief Technical Examiner of Government of India\n(CTE) and/ or an inspecting authority of State Government of State in which work is\nexecuted and/or by third party checks by Owner/ Clients. The compliance of observations/\nimprovements as suggested by the inspecting officers of EPI/CTE/ State authorities/\nOwners shall be obligatory on the part of the Contractor at the cost of Contractor. Any\nrecovery, penalty imposed by CTE due to non-performance, noncompliance of agreed\ncondition or otherwise whatsoever the same shall be recovered from RA Bill of contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
