    "text": "20. The CONTRACTOR shall not execute any work without knowledge of EPI / ESIC. Any\nincrease in the scope of work shall be in terms of ESIC/CPWD/CVC guidelines and with\nprior written approval of competent authority of ESIC/EPI else the CONTRACTOR\nshould bear the cost and expenditure.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0139",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 139,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 42011,
    "char_end": 42263,
    "char_count": 252,
    "text": "Page 21 of 28\n\n21. The work has to be carried out in an orderly manner without noise and obstruction to\nflow of traffic.\n22. All rubbles etc. should be disposed of at the earliest and the place is left clean and\norderly at the   end of each day’s work.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0140",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 140,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 42265,
    "char_end": 42594,
    "char_count": 329,
    "text": "CIVIL - MATERIALS\n23. Only Class- I, reputed brand, ISI marked materials would be used in repair work of civil\nmaintenance works.\n24. The Bidder/ Contractor should be provided any materials for civil works are as per ISI\nnorms and manufacturer.\n25. The Bidder/ Contractor should be maintained all statutory records and registers.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0141",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 141,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 42596,
    "char_end": 42659,
    "char_count": 63,
    "text": "(B) Manpower for Annual Repair and Maintenance of Civil works:-",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0142",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 142,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 42661,
    "char_end": 42882,
    "char_count": 221,
    "text": "1. Bidder/ Contractor must be Principal Employer of manpower required for\nmaintenance works i.e. manpower provided must be on direct pay roll of\nBidder/ Contractor and sub-letting shall not be allowed in any\ncircumstance.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0143",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 143,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 42883,
    "char_end": 43052,
    "char_count": 169,
    "text": "2. The Bidder/ Contractor shall be responsible to depute their Technical Staffs in\nthe concerned ESIC’S Establishments for Proper Monitoring of Maintenance of ARM\nworks.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0144",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 144,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 43053,
    "char_end": 43405,
    "char_count": 352,
    "text": "3. The Bidder/ Contractor shall have to display on notice board, its name along with\nTechnical Staff’s  name   to be contacted in 24 x 7 (Round the clock ) Operation and\nMaintenance of  ARM works by sharing their  Mobile nos., emails , Whats App\nnumber for lodging the complaints, tracking & updating the status up to closing\nfor customer satisfaction.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0145",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 145,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 43406,
    "char_end": 43633,
    "char_count": 227,
    "text": "4. The Bidder/ Contractor will provide Civil Engineer whenever it is required at site even\nafter working hours keeping in view nature of seriousness arise for health care\nexigencies as required by competent authority from EPIL.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0146",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 146,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 43634,
    "char_end": 43782,
    "char_count": 148,
    "text": "5. Bidder/ Contractor should facilitate Attendance Register / BAS attendance sheet for\ntheir manpower deployment in the concerned ESIC jurisdiction.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0147",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 147,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 43783,
    "char_end": 43987,
    "char_count": 204,
    "text": "6. Uniform, Identity Cards, Name Plates and identity cards should be provided to each\nStaff by the contractor. Bio - data of each staff should be maintained and whenever\nasked should be shown immediately.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0148",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 148,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 43988,
    "char_end": 44103,
    "char_count": 115,
    "text": "7. The Bidder/ Contractor shall have to maintain and provide all safety measures\nand precaution to their employees.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0149",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 149,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 44104,
    "char_end": 44378,
    "char_count": 274,
    "text": "8. Day to day maintenance activities has to be carried out by a mechanism of Service\nCentre established / provided in the ESIC’s  Establishments , where all sorts of\ncomplaints from users of the facilities are received, attended, monitored & updated in\nthe stipulated times.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0150",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 150,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 44379,
    "char_end": 44723,
    "char_count": 344,
    "text": "9. The Service Centre is to  be manned by various categories of unskilled / semi- skilled /\nskilled manpower  or  maintenance  staff e.g. Supervisor, Carpenter, Mason, Plumber,\nSewer man, Mason, Mate, Helpers etc. under the close supervision of engineering\npersonnel in appropriate number in order to carry out day to day maintenance activities",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0151",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 151,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 44725,
    "char_end": 44935,
    "char_count": 210,
    "text": "Page 22 of 28\n\nefficiently and effectively in all respect of ESIC ARM norms.\n10. Wages for Unskilled/semi–skilled/skilledmanpowerormaintenancestaffistobeasper\nthe latest CLC guidelines depicted in attached BOQ.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0152",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 152,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 44936,
    "char_end": 45046,
    "char_count": 110,
    "text": "11. Contractor shall install sufficient number of biometric attendance machine to\ncontinuous monitor of staff.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0153",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 153,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 45047,
    "char_end": 45260,
    "char_count": 213,
    "text": "12. The contractor will be under obligation to submit a certificate & documentary\nevidence that he has cleared /paid all monthly dues of his/its employees within first\n7 days of every month through their Bank A/C.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0154",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 154,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 45261,
    "char_end": 45470,
    "char_count": 209,
    "text": "13. Although ESIC shall ensure to clear bill submitted by contractor within 15 days of\nreceipt of the same, Disbursement of salary by contractor to its employee shall not\nhave any linkage to clearance of bill.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0155",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 155,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 45471,
    "char_end": 45603,
    "char_count": 132,
    "text": "14. The manpower may be increased or decreased by the order of Competent\nAuthority as per ESIC HOSPITAL/HEALTH CARE EXIGENCIES/EPIL.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0156",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 156,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 45604,
    "char_end": 45715,
    "char_count": 111,
    "text": "15. General working hours to be adhered  as per the  Time Periods set out by the\nconcerned ESIC establishments,",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0157",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 157,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 45716,
    "char_end": 45897,
    "char_count": 181,
    "text": "16. The established manpower shall be available on call around the clock in general\nshift/every shift for the smooth functioning of ESI Hospitals, ESID, ESIC staff\nquarters, BO etc.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0158",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 158,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 45898,
    "char_end": 46187,
    "char_count": 289,
    "text": "17. Whenever the need of specialized mason, painter, welder etc. arises, the same\nmay be arranged by the contractor on piece rate basis. The payment of all such\nadditional work will be on the basis of Minimum wages prescribed by State Govt.\nor any local authority whichever is  applicable.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0159",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 159,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 46188,
    "char_end": 46332,
    "char_count": 144,
    "text": "18. The Working Staff should be professionally qualified and must be trained. The\nContractor must submit the labour’s Qualification certificate.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0160",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 160,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 46333,
    "char_end": 46429,
    "char_count": 96,
    "text": "19. The contractor Bidder/ Contractor shall not execute any work without knowledge of\nEPIL/ESIC.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC070-0161",
    "doc_id": "DOC-070",
    "paragraph_index": 161,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 46430,
    "char_end": 46837,
    "char_count": 407,
    "text": "20. Deployment of adequate manpower like Electrician, Lift Operator, DG Operator,\nHelpers, Sewer man, Supervisor, etc. so as to ensure the smooth functioning of\nESI/ESIC Hospital, Offices, Dispensaries and Staff quarters etc. Labour required\nfor the same shall be deployed as decided by ESIC /EPIL Officer’s or as per the\nMaintenance manual 2023 of CPWD & maintenance of the buildings as require as\nper PAR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
