  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0074",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 74,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 43325,
    "char_end": 44201,
    "char_count": 876,
    "text": "ARTICLE 2:  TERM OF AGREEMENT\n\n2.1\nEffective Date\n2.1.1 This Agreement shall come into effect from …………… (Enter the date as on 90th day\nof the issuance of Letter of Award to the RPD, or any further date, as applicable) and\nsuch date shall be referred to as the Effective Date.\n2.1.2  The Parties agree that decisions pertaining to adoption of the Tariff and approval of\nthe same, for procurement of contracted capacity, shall be binding on all Parties\nconcerned, as contained in the Electricity Act, 2003 and any amendments thereof.\n2.1.3. The Buying Utility(ies), as the case may be shall, upon signing of the PSA between\nSECI and the Buying Utility(ies), apply to the State Electricity Regulatory\nCommission within the jurisdiction of which the Buying Utility is operating as a\nlicensee for approval of the power procurement in terms of Rule 8 of the Electricity\nRules 2005.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0075",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 75,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 44203,
    "char_end": 45395,
    "char_count": 1192,
    "text": "2.1.4 Notwithstanding the Effective Date, the condition precedent for the enforcement of\nthe obligations of either party against the other under this Agreement shall be the due\nfulfillment of the following:\n   A. Due Adoption of the Tariff by the Central Electricity Regulatory Commission\non the application/Petition filed for the said purpose;\n2.1.5.  The parties acknowledge and agree that the Scheduled Commercial Operation Date\nfor the RE Project has been agreed to in this agreement based on each of the\nConditions Precedent contained in Article 2.1.4 being duly accomplished not later\nthan 60 days of submission of such petition by SECI/RPD or within 120 days from\nthe date of signing of PSA, whichever is more. In the event of delay beyond the\ndeadline as above, of such fulfillment of Conditions Precedent, there shall be\ncorresponding extension of Scheduled Commercial Operation date and extension of\ntime for satisfaction of Conditions Subsequent, if the RPD has not started any work\nat site. Except for the above extensions of time there shall be no other financial\nimplications on the composite tariff applicable under this Agreement on account of\nsuch delay or extension in time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0076",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 76,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 45397,
    "char_end": 45561,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "SECI-RPD- PPA\n(Insert Project ID)                                                                                                                      Page 20 of 90",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0077",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 77,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 45563,
    "char_end": 46915,
    "char_count": 1352,
    "text": "2.1.6.  The parties further acknowledge and accept that in case any of the Conditions\nPrecedent remains to be fulfilled even after one (1) year from the Effective Date,\nunless the parties mutually agree otherwise, this agreement in regard to sourcing of\nRE Power as well as the Thermal Power to be complemented shall stand terminated\nfor all intent and purposes for non-satisfaction of Conditions Precedent with no\nobligation of any of the Parties to the other including to the Thermal Generator.\n2.2\nTerm of Agreement\n2.2.1 Subject to Article 2.3 and 2.4 of this Agreement, this Agreement shall be valid for a\nterm from the Effective Date until the Expiry Date. The Expiry Date of the\nAgreement  may be further extended upto 35 years, on such term and conditions as\nmutually agreed between the parties and approved by the Appropriate Commissions,\nprovided the arrangements with the land and infrastructure owning agencies, the\nrelevant transmission utilities and system operators permits operation of the Project\nbeyond such extended period.\n2.2.2 The RPD is free to operate their plants beyond the Expiry Date if other conditions like\nland lease / Right to Use of Land (as applicable), permits, approvals and clearances\netc. allow. In such case unless otherwise agreed by the SECI, SECI shall not be\nobligated to procure power beyond the Expiry Date.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
