    "paragraph_index": 107,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 66587,
    "char_end": 68332,
    "char_count": 1745,
    "text": "conditions shall be also the responsibility of the RPD to be obtained at his own cost.\nAll costs and charges including but not limited to the wheeling charges and losses\nup to and including at the Interconnection Point associated with this arrangement\nwill also be borne by the RPD.\n4.2.4   In case of Pooling substation, losses in the transmission line shall be apportioned\namong the RPDs who share such a Pooling arrangement and duly signed by all\nRPDs, based on their monthly generation.\n4.2.5   The arrangement of connectivity shall be made by the RPD through a dedicated\ntransmission line. The entire cost of transmission including cost of construction of\nline, any other charges, losses etc. from the Project up to the Interconnection Point\nwill be borne by the RPD. In case of non-availability of Grid and Transmission\nSystem during Term of this Agreement, for reasons not attributable to the RPD,\nprovisions of Article 4.10 shall be applicable.\n4.2.6    ISTS charges and losses on transmission of power, including waiver for RE power,\nshall be as per extant regulations. Government of India, from time to time, issues\norder for waiver of inter-state transmission system (ISTS) charges and losses on\ntransmission of wind/solar power till a certain date. In case the commissioning of\nthe Project gets delayed beyond the applicable date of ISTS waiver, arising out of\nany reasons whatsoever, SECI shall bear no liability with respect to transmission\ncharges and losses levied, if any. However, in case the commissioning of the project\ngets delayed beyond the applicable date of waiver of ISTS charges and losses due\nto reasons solely attributable to the RPD, the liability of inter-state transmission\ncharges and losses would be of the RPD.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0108",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 108,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 68333,
    "char_end": 68553,
    "char_count": 220,
    "text": "It is however, clarified that ISTS charges and losses corresponding to the energy\ninjected from the Thermal Power Component, beyond the Delivery Point(s) and\nupto the drawl point(s), shall be borne by the Buying Utility.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0109",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 109,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 68555,
    "char_end": 69153,
    "char_count": 598,
    "text": "4.3\nPurchase and sale of Contracted Capacity\n4.3.1   Subject to the terms and conditions of this Agreement, the RPD undertakes to\ngenerate and sell to SECI RE Power and further, complement / balance the supply\nof Thermal Power by the Thermal Generator to ensure RTC supply and SECI\nundertakes to purchase such power and pay the Tariff for all the energy supplied at\nthe Delivery Point corresponding to the Contracted Capacity.\n4.3.2 Power procured under this Agreement shall on back to back basis be allocated on a\npro-rata basis, to all the Buying Entities which have signed their respective Power",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0110",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 110,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 69155,
    "char_end": 69319,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "SECI-RPD- PPA\n(Insert Project ID)                                                                                                                      Page 30 of 90",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0111",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 111,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 69321,
    "char_end": 69537,
    "char_count": 216,
    "text": "Sale Agreements with SECI under the referred RfS. Any obligation of SECI being\nintermediary Procurer shall be deemed to be the obligation of Buying Entity(ies)\nwith which SECI has / will execute Power Sale Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0112",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 112,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 69539,
    "char_end": 71327,
    "char_count": 1788,
    "text": "4.4       Right to Contracted Capacity, Energy and Availability\n4.4.1    Under this Agreement, procurement of contracted capacity shall be in power (MW)\nterms. The RPD shall be obliged to make the RE Project complemented by Thermal\nGeneration available on a round-the-clock basis and in a composite manner for the\nContracted Capacity for scheduling of power by the Buying Utility as per Article 6.\nThe RPD shall deliver the power to the Buying Utility as scheduled by the Buying\nUtility on a day-ahead basis, as detailed out in Article 6.2 below. Further, the RPD\nshall be required to offer power such that at least 51% of the annual power offered\ncorresponds to RE Power, and the balance could be supplied from thermal sources.\nThe Buying Utility shall be entitled to use the power from this Project for fulfillment\nof its RPO in the proportion of contracted capacity of each component in the Project\nrespectively.\n  The RPD shall also be obliged to supply RE Power complemented with dispatchable\nThermal Power, in Round-The-Clock manner, keeping at least 85% Availability\nannually and also at least 85% Availability annually during the Peak Hours. Peak\nhours will be four hours out of 24 hours as determined by the POSOCO/RLDC from\ntime to time, where the Buying Entity(ies) is/are located.\n 4.4.2  The RPD, at its own risk and cost, shall be allowed to supply power in excess of\nblock-wise off-take by SECI/Buying Utility to any third party or power exchange\nwithout requiring any NOC from SECI/Buying Entity. However, in case at any point\nof time, the peak of capacity at the injection point reached is higher than the\nContracted Capacity and causes disturbance in the system at the point where power\nis injected, the RPD will not undertake the excess generation and reduce the output",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0113",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 113,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 71328,
    "char_end": 71895,
    "char_count": 567,
    "text": "to the rated capacity and shall further be liable to pay the penalty/charges (if\napplicable) as per applicable regulations / requirements / guidelines of CERC /\nSERC /SLDC or any other competent agency. Any energy produced and flowing\ninto the grid before Scheduled Commercial Operation Date shall not be to the\naccount of or at the cost of SECI/ Buying Entity(ies). SECI may however agree to\nbuy such power at a tariff as agreed to between SECI and the Buying Entity\n(including SECI’s trading margin), provided the Buying Utility consents for\npurchase of such power.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0114",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 114,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 71897,
    "char_end": 72061,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "SECI-RPD- PPA\n(Insert Project ID)                                                                                                                      Page 31 of 90",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0115",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 115,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 72063,
    "char_end": 73834,
    "char_count": 1771,
    "text": "4.4.3 Consequences of Shortfall in supplying / offering (as applicable) the Contracted\nCapacity -Subsequent to commissioning of first part capacity of the Contracted\nCapacity, if for any Contract Year, for the reasons solely attributable to the RPD\n(such reasons could be any reason other than Force Majeure, Grid Non-Availability\nbeyond control of the RPD and inability of the Buying Entity to offtake Scheduled\nPower/ Energy (as applicable) ):\ni.\nAnnual availability or annual Availability during Peak Hours is less than 85%:\nThe RPD shall pay to the SECI / Buying Entities (as applicable) for such\nshortfall in the Availability. Such amount will be pre-estimated damages\n(liquidated damages) calculated at the rate of 25% (twenty-five per cent) of the\ncost of this shortfall in energy terms, calculated at the maximum indexed\ncomposite tariff payable during that Contract Year.\nii.\nThe RPD shall also be liable to pay liquidated damages for any shortfall in\noffering RE power below the mandatory 51% of the total power offered in a\ncontract year. The liquidated damages corresponding to this shortfall in RE\npower shall be calculated at 25% of the maximum indexed composite tariff\npayable during the Contract Year for each unit of shortfall.\niii.\nFurther in case during two consecutive Contract Years, the RPD fails to meet\nthe requirement of minimum Annual availability or annual Availability during\nPeak Hours is less than 85% or there is shortfall in offering RE power below\nthe mandatory 51% of the total power offered in the Contract Year, SECI shall\nhave right to terminate this Agreement. Any liability arising out of such\ntermination shall be to the account of the RPD.\n            An illustration to the effect of (i) and (ii) above is attached at Schedule-4.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0116",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 116,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 73835,
    "char_end": 74525,
    "char_count": 690,
    "text": " 4.4.4. The RPD agrees that the methodology specified hereinabove for calculation of\ncompensation in the form of liquidated damages payable by the RPD for shortfall in\ngeneration, annual availability, peak-hour availability and/or the shortfall in RE\npower is a genuine and accurate pre-estimation of the actual loss that will be suffered\nby SECI. RPD shall further acknowledge that a breach of any of the obligations\ncontained herein result in injuries and that the amount of the damages or the method\nof calculating the damages specified in this document is a genuine and reasonable\npre-estimate of the damages that may be suffered by the SECI in each case specified\nunder this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0117",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 117,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 74527,
    "char_end": 74691,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "SECI-RPD- PPA\n(Insert Project ID)                                                                                                                      Page 32 of 90",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0118",
