    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0130",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 130,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 82403,
    "char_end": 83950,
    "char_count": 1547,
    "text": "4.8.2  The third party may verify the construction works/operation of the Project being\ncarried out by the RPD / thermal generator and if it is found that the construction\nworks/operation of the project is not as per the Prudent Utility Practices, it may seek\nclarifications from RPD or require the works to be stopped or to comply with the\ninstructions of such third party.\n4.9  Breach of Obligations\n4.9.1  Except as specifically provided under Article 4.4.2 & 4.10.1 (b), the Parties herein\nagree that during the subsistence of this Agreement, subject to SECI being in\ncompliance of its obligations & undertakings under this Agreement, the RPD would\nhave no right to negotiate or enter into any dialogue with any third party for the sale\nof Contracted Capacity of power which is the subject matter of this Agreement. It is\nthe specific understanding between the Parties that such bar will apply throughout\nthe entire term of this Agreement.\n4.10\nGeneration compensation for Off-take constraints\n4.10.1 a) Generation Compensation in offtake constraints due to Grid Unavailability: During\noperation, there can be some periods where the Project can generate power but due\nto temporary transmission unavailability, the power is not evacuated, for reasons not\nattributable to the RPD. In such cases, subject to the submission of documentary\nevidences from the competent authority, the generation compensation shall be\nrestricted and payable by the Buying Utility(ies) as under, and there shall be no other\nclaim, directly or indirectly against SECI:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0131",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 131,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 83952,
    "char_end": 84382,
    "char_count": 430,
    "text": "The above compensation will be paid to the RPD on an annual basis.\nb) Payment in case of reduced offtake: The RPD and the Buying Entity shall follow\nthe forecasting and scheduling process as per the regulations in this regard by the\nAppropriate Commission. In case the plant is available to supply power but the off-\ntake of power is not done by the Procurer, including non-dispatch of power due to\nDuration of Grid unavailability",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0132",
