    "char_start": 84907,
    "char_end": 85739,
    "char_count": 832,
    "text": "non-compliance with “Order No. 23/22/2019-R&R dated 28.06.2019 of Ministry of\nPower regarding Opening and maintaining of adequate Letter of Credit (LC) as\nPayment Security Mechanism under Power Purchase Agreements by Distribution\nLicensees” and any clarifications or amendment thereto, considering the principle of\n‘must run’ status for RE Power, and the Fixed charges for thermal power, the RPD\nshall be eligible for payment from the Buying Entity, corresponding to the reduced\nofftake, in terms of following manner. For claiming compensation, the RPD must sell\ntheir power in the power exchange as a price taker. Thus, the compensation would be\nlimited to the difference of the actual generation up to declared capacity subject to a\nmaximum of up to the contracted capacity and the quantum of power scheduled by the\nBuying Entity.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0135",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 135,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 85741,
    "char_end": 86016,
    "char_count": 275,
    "text": "Reduced\nofftake\nProvision for Generation Compensation\n\nGeneration Compensation =\n((Composite Tariff  x RE power (MW) offered but not scheduled\nby Procurer ) + (Fixed Charge x Thermal power (MW) offered\nbut not scheduled by Procurer) ) X 1000 X No. of hours of\nReduced Offtake",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0136",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 136,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 86018,
    "char_end": 86321,
    "char_count": 303,
    "text": "However, any amount realized by the RPD, by third party sale of\nsuch power which was offered but not scheduled, shall be shared\nwith the Procurer in the following manner, after deducting\nexpenses, if any, in such sale, and shall be adjusted against the\nGeneration compensation payable, on monthly basis.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0137",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 137,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 86323,
    "char_end": 87163,
    "char_count": 840,
    "text": "(a) For RE Power:\n90% of Net realization\n(b) For Thermal Power:\n 50% of Net realization above variable Charges\nComposite Tariff shall be the Applicable Tariff as per Article 9.\nThe RPD shall be eligible for payment from the Procurer, corresponding to the reduced\nofftake of power as per above mentioned methodology. The Payment is to be done as\npart of the energy bill for the successive month after receipt of Regional Energy\nAccounts (REA). No Trading Margin shall be applicable on this Payment. It is hereby\nclarified that for the purpose of Article 4.10, “generation” shall mean scheduled energy\nbased on Energy Accounts. The RPD shall not be eligible for any compensation in\ncase the Backdown is on account of events like consideration of grid security or safety\nof any equipment or personnel or other such conditions or Force Majeure.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0138",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 138,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 87165,
    "char_end": 87329,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "SECI-RPD- PPA\n(Insert Project ID)                                                                                                                      Page 37 of 90",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
