    "char_end": 87627,
    "char_count": 296,
    "text": "ARTICLE 5: SYNCHRONISATION, COMMISSIONING AND COMMERCIAL\nOPERATION\n5.1\nSynchronization, Commissioning and Commercial Operation\n5.1.1 The RPD shall give the concerned RLDC/SLDC and SECI and also to the Buying\nEntity at least sixty (60) days’ advanced preliminary written notice and at least thirty",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0140",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 140,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 87628,
    "char_end": 89418,
    "char_count": 1790,
    "text": "(30) days’ advanced final written notice, of the date on which it intends to\nsynchronize the RE Power Project to the Grid System. Further, to the extent of\nThermal Component as per the provisions of this Agreement, the RPD shall be\nrequired to make necessary arrangement for the demonstration of such thermal\ncapacity.\n5.1.2 Subject to Article 5.1.1, the RE Power Project may be synchronized by the RPD to\nthe Grid System when it meets all the connection conditions prescribed in applicable\nGrid Code then in effect and otherwise meets all other Indian legal requirements for\nsynchronization to the Grid System. Further, to the extent of Thermal Component\nas per the provisions of this Agreement, the RPD shall have demonstrated such\nthermal capacity.\n5.1.3 The synchronization equipment and all necessary arrangements / equipment including\nRTU for scheduling of power generated from the RE Project as well as thermal\nproject and transmission of data to the concerned authority as per applicable\nregulations shall be installed by the RPD at its generation facility at its own\ncost(similar dispensation would be required for the Thermal Project also). Further,\nthe RPD shall also ensure availability of any such system/ equipment (if applicable)\nat Thermal Power Generator’s facility. The RPD shall synchronize its system with\nthe Grid System only after the approval of synchronization scheme is granted by the\nhead of the concerned substation/Grid System and checking/verification is made by\nthe concerned authorities of the Grid System.\n5.1.4 The RPD shall immediately after each synchronization/tripping of generator, inform\nthe sub-station of the Grid System to which the generation facility including RE\nProject(s) is electrically connected in accordance with applicable Grid Code under",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0141",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 141,
