    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 90071,
    "char_end": 90233,
    "char_count": 162,
    "text": "UCOD shall only be done subject to the demonstration of the compliances as per\nSchedule-3 and subsequent upon the successful visit by the Commissioning\nCommittee.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0144",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 144,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 90235,
    "char_end": 91153,
    "char_count": 918,
    "text": "5.1.6.1The RPD shall be permitted for full commissioning as well as part commissioning of\nthe Contacted Capacity even prior to the SCD subject to availability of transmission\nconnectivity and Long Term Access (LTA). In cases of early part commissioning,\ntill SCD, the RPD will be free to sell the electricity generated, to any entity other\nthan the SECI/ Buying Entity(ies), only after giving the first right of refusal to the\nSECI/ Buying Utilities . The Buying Utilities shall provide refusal within 15 (fifteen)\nDays from the receipt of the request, beyond which it would be considered as deemed\nrefusal. In cases of early commissioning prior to SCD, the Buying Utilities may\npurchase the generated power till SCD, at the PPA tariff. Even in case of early part\ncommissioning or early full commissioning, the PPA will remain in force for a period\nof 25 (twenty-five) years from the SCD or the COD whichever is later.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0145",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 145,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 91155,
    "char_end": 92057,
    "char_count": 902,
    "text": "5.6.1.2 There can be part Commissioning of the Contracted Capacity. Part commissioning\nof the Contracted Capacity  shall mean that all equipment corresponding to the such\npart capacity have been installed and commissioned / demonstrated (as applicable)\nand corresponding energy has flown into the grid as well as compliances of all\nrequirements as per provisions of this Agreement read alongwith the RfS has been\ncomplied  and demonstrated. It may be noted that part commissioning of the capacity\nwill be admissible subject to the condition that “Round-the-Clock” supply of power\nis achieved by the commissioned part-capacity, in line with RfS and PPA conditions.\nIn case of part-commissioning of the Contracted Capacity, land corresponding to the\nsuch part RE capacity being commissioned, shall be required to be demonstrated by\nthe RPD prior to declaration of commissioning of the said part capacity.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0146",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 146,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 92059,
    "char_end": 92296,
    "char_count": 237,
    "text": "5.1.7 The Parties agree that for the purpose of commencement of the supply of electricity by\nRPD to SECI, liquidated damages for delay etc., the Scheduled Commercial\nOperation Date as defined in this Agreement shall be the relevant date.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0147",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 147,
