    "text": "SECI-RPD- PPA\n(Insert Project ID)                                                                                                                      Page 39 of 90",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0148",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 148,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 92464,
    "char_end": 93565,
    "char_count": 1101,
    "text": "ARTICLE 6: DISPATCH AND SCHEDULING\n\n6.1\nDispatch and Scheduling\n\n6.1.1 At the commencement of each Contract Year, the RPD shall declare changes in the\nrated capacity of the Thermal Power Component tied up under this Agreement.\nPursuant to this, the RPD shall be entirely responsible and shall be required to\ndeclare the Availability and Declared Capacity for the RE Project along with\nThermal Power Project and arrange for dispatch of RE power and the Thermal\nPower in a composite manner under this Agreement as per the applicable regulations\n/ requirements / guidelines of CERC / SERC /SLDC / RLDC or any other competent\nagency and same being recognized by the SLDC or any other competent authority /\nagency as per applicable regulation/ law / direction and maintain compliance to the\napplicable Codes/ Grid Code requirements and directions, if any, as specified by\nconcerned SLDC/RLDC from time to time. Any deviation from the Schedule will\nattract the provisions of applicable regulation / guidelines / directions and any\nfinancial implication on account of this shall be on the account of the RPD.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0149",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 149,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 93567,
    "char_end": 94177,
    "char_count": 610,
    "text": "6.1.2 The RPD shall be responsible for directly coordinating and dealing with the Thermal\nGenerator, Buying Entity(ies), State Load Dispatch Centres, Regional Power\nCommittees, and other authorities in all respects in regard to declaration of\navailability, scheduling and dispatch of power and due compliance with deviation\nand settlement mechanism and the applicable Grid code Regulations,\nacknowledging that the RPD and Buying Entity are the Grid connected entities and\nSECI as an Intermediary Procurer/ trading licensee is not a Grid connected entity in\nrespect of the power contracted under this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0150",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 150,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 94179,
    "char_end": 94631,
    "char_count": 452,
    "text": "6.1.3  The RPD shall be responsible for any deviation from scheduling and for any resultant\nliabilities on account of charges for deviation as per applicable prevailing\nregulations. For RE component of the total power supplied, DSM as per RE\nregulations shall be applicable, and for Thermal component, the DSM as per\nThermal regulations shall be applicable Deviation Settlement Mechanism (DSM)\ncharges on this account shall be directly paid by the RPD.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0151",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 151,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 94634,
    "char_end": 94723,
    "char_count": 89,
    "text": "6.1.4 Auxiliary power consumption will be treated as per the concerned State regulations.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0152",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 152,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 94725,
    "char_end": 94889,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "SECI-RPD- PPA\n(Insert Project ID)                                                                                                                      Page 40 of 90",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0153",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 153,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 94891,
    "char_end": 95055,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "6.1.5 It is to be noted that the summation of generation schedule of RE and Thermal Power\ncannot be more than the Contracted capacity in any 15 minutes’ time-block.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0154",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 154,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 95057,
    "char_end": 95093,
    "char_count": 36,
    "text": "6.2  Dispatch of Contracted Capacity",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0155",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 155,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 95095,
    "char_end": 96868,
    "char_count": 1773,
    "text": "6.2.1 The RPD shall install, operate and maintain the RE Project and ensure necessary\narrangements\nfor\nthe\nThermal\nPower\nComponent\nsuch\nthat the RTC Availability of the Contracted Capacity of the Project is supplied during\neach Contract Year for the entire Term of this Agreement.\n6.2.2  Unless otherwise notified by the RPD, the declared Availability shall be deemed to\nbe 100% (one hundred per cent) thereof at all times. The RPD shall confirm the\nAvailability from the RE Project as well as Thermal Project as per Applicable\nRegulations/Guidelines prevalent from time to time.\n6.2.3 Void.\n6.2.4 [Void].\n6.2.5 [Void].\n6.2.6 The Buying Utility shall, in accordance with Applicable Laws and Regulations\nthereunder, issue instructions to the RPD for schedule of electricity and dispatch\nthereof to the Grid during such period and in such volume as it may specify in its\ninstructions (the “Dispatch”). Provided that the Utility shall not as for dispatch in\nexcess of the declared Availability by the RPD, unless mutually agreed between the\nRPD and the Buying Utility(ies).\n6.2.7 The RPD shall plan the production and Dispatch of electricity and convey its\navailability for scheduling thereof by the SLDC or RLDC, as the case may be, and\nshall supply electricity in accordance with the provisions of the Grid Code and the\nElectricity Act, 2003.\n6.2.8 RPD agrees and undertakes that the fundamental and mandatory obligation of the\nRPD under this Agreement is to make available the RE Power and the Thermal\nPower in the manner specified under this Agreement to provide to the buying utility\npower on a Round-the-Clock basis.\n6.2.9 If the RPD is unable to provide thermal power to the SECI/Procurer up to the\nContracted Capacity from the Thermal Power Project due to scheduled or",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0156",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 156,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 96869,
    "char_end": 97112,
    "char_count": 243,
    "text": "unscheduled maintenance, the RPD is free to supply thermal power up to the\nContracted Capacity from an alternative generation source, situated within the same\nRLDC area as that of the Project, to meet its obligations under this Agreement. Such",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0157",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 157,
    "page_start": 41,
