    "text": "SECI-RPD- PPA\n(Insert Project ID)                                                                                                                      Page 42 of 90",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0160",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 160,
    "page_start": 42,
    "page_end": 42,
    "char_start": 98155,
    "char_end": 99584,
    "char_count": 1429,
    "text": "ARTICLE 7: METERING\n\n7.1\nMeters\n\n7.1.1 For installation of Meters, Meter testing, Meter calibration and Meter reading and all\nmatters incidental thereto, the RPD and SECI shall follow and be bound by the\nCentral Electricity Authority (Installation and Operation of Meters) Regulations,\n2006, the Grid Code, as amended and revised from time to time.\n7.1.2 The RPD shall bear all costs pertaining to installation, testing, calibration,\nmaintenance, renewal and repair of meters at RPD ’s side of Delivery Point.\n7.1.3 In addition to ensuring compliance of the applicable codes, the RPD shall install Main\n& Check meters at the Delivery Point, along with Stand-by meter(s) as per the\napplicable Central/State regulations. Further, it shall be the obligation and\nresponsibility of the RPD, to ensure metering arrangement at thermal power source\nin compliance with the Applicable Regulations, Guidelines & Laws and as per the\nrequirement of this Agreement.\n7.1.4 In case of pooling of multiple Projects, power from multiple Projects can be pooled at\na Pooling Substation prior to the Delivery point and the combined power can be fed\nat Delivery point through a common transmission line from the Pooling Substation.\nIn such cases, ABT compliant sub-meters as per relevant regulation/approvals are\nalso to be set up at pooling substation for individual projects in addition to the meters\nat Delivery Point as described in Article 7.1.3.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0161",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 161,
    "page_start": 42,
    "page_end": 42,
    "char_start": 99586,
    "char_end": 100552,
    "char_count": 966,
    "text": "7.2\nReporting of Metered Data and Parameters\n7.2.1 The grid connected RE power plants will install necessary equipment for regular\nmonitoring of solar irradiance (including GHI, DHI and solar radiation in the\nmodule plane), ambient air temperature, wind speed and other weather parameters\nand simultaneously for monitoring of the electric power (both DC and AC)\ngenerated from the RE Project.\n7.2.2 Online arrangement would  have  to  be  made  by  the  RPD  for submission of  above\ndata from RE Project regularly for the entire period of this Power Purchase\nAgreement to the SLDC, SECI and the concerned Ministry or concerned agency as\nper applicable regulation / directions. Further, RPD shall also be responsible for\nensuring online arrangement for submission of all required data as per provisions of\nthis Agreement during entire Term of this Agreement as per applicable guidelines,\nregulations, laws to SLDC, SECI and the concerned Ministry or concerned agency",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0162",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 162,
    "page_start": 43,
    "page_end": 43,
    "char_start": 100554,
    "char_end": 100718,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "SECI-RPD- PPA\n(Insert Project ID)                                                                                                                      Page 43 of 90",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0163",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 163,
    "page_start": 43,
    "page_end": 43,
    "char_start": 100720,
    "char_end": 100959,
    "char_count": 239,
    "text": "7.2.3 Reports on above parameters on monthly basis (or as required by regulation /\nguidelines) shall be submitted by the RPD to Ministry of New and Renewable\nEnergy/SECI/or authorized agency of SECI/ MNRE for entire Term of this\nAgreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
