  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0205",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 205,
    "page_start": 51,
    "page_end": 51,
    "char_start": 115525,
    "char_end": 115718,
    "char_count": 193,
    "text": "10.5     Disputed Bill\n\n10.5.1 If the SECI does not dispute a Monthly Bill or a Supplementary Bill raised by the\nRPD within thirty (30) days of receiving such Bill shall be taken as conclusive.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0206",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 206,
    "page_start": 51,
    "page_end": 51,
    "char_start": 115720,
    "char_end": 116012,
    "char_count": 292,
    "text": "10.5.2 If the SECI disputes the amount payable under a Monthly Bill or a Supplementary\nBill, as the case may be, it shall pay 50% of the invoice amount and it shall within\nfifteen (15) days of receiving such Bill, issue a notice (the \"Bill Dispute Notice\") to\nthe invoicing Party setting out:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0207",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 207,
    "page_start": 51,
    "page_end": 51,
    "char_start": 116014,
    "char_end": 116163,
    "char_count": 149,
    "text": "i) the details of the disputed amount;\n\nii) its estimate of what the correct amount should be; and\niii) all written material in support of its claim.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0208",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 208,
    "page_start": 51,
    "page_end": 51,
    "char_start": 116165,
    "char_end": 116664,
    "char_count": 499,
    "text": "10.5.3 If the RPD agrees to the claim raised in the Bill Dispute Notice issued pursuant to\nArticle 10.5.2, the RPD shall revise such Bill and present along with the next\nMonthly Bill. In such a case excess amount shall be refunded along with interest at\nthe same rate as Late Payment Surcharge, which shall be applied from the date on\nwhich such excess payment was made by the disputing Party to the invoicing Party\nand up to and including the date on which such payment has been received as refund.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0209",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 209,
    "page_start": 51,
    "page_end": 51,
    "char_start": 116666,
    "char_end": 116920,
    "char_count": 254,
    "text": "10.5.4 If the RPD does not agree to the claim raised in the Bill Dispute Notice issued\npursuant to Article 10.5.2, it shall, within fifteen (15) days of receiving the Bill\nDispute Notice, furnish a notice (Bill Disagreement Notice) to the SECI providing:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0210",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 210,
    "page_start": 51,
    "page_end": 51,
    "char_start": 116922,
    "char_end": 117401,
    "char_count": 479,
    "text": "i) reasons for its disagreement;\nii) its estimate of what the correct amount should be; and\niii) all written material in support of its counter-claim.\n10.5.5 Upon receipt of the Bill Disagreement Notice by the SECI under Article 10.5.4,\nauthorized representative(s) or a director of the board of directors/ member of board\nof the SECI and RPD shall meet and make best endeavors to amicably resolve such\ndispute within fifteen (15) days of receipt of the Bill Disagreement\nNotice.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0211",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 211,
    "page_start": 51,
    "page_end": 51,
    "char_start": 117403,
    "char_end": 117634,
    "char_count": 231,
    "text": "10.5.6 If the Parties do not amicably resolve the Dispute within fifteen (15) days of receipt\nof Bill Disagreement Notice pursuant to Article 10.5.4, the matter shall be referred\nto Dispute resolution in accordance with Article 16.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0212",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 212,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 117636,
    "char_end": 117800,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "SECI-RPD- PPA\n(Insert Project ID)                                                                                                                      Page 52 of 90",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0213",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 213,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 117802,
    "char_end": 118040,
    "char_count": 238,
    "text": "10.5.7 For the avoidance of doubt, it is clarified the despite a Dispute regarding an invoice,\nSECI shall, without prejudice to its right to Dispute, be under an obligation to make\npayment of 50% of the invoice amount in the Monthly Bill.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0214",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 214,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 118042,
    "char_end": 118593,
    "char_count": 551,
    "text": "10.6\nQuarterly and Annual Reconciliation\n\n10.6.1 The  Parties  acknowledge  that  all  payments  made  against  Monthly  Bills and\nSupplementary Bills shall be subject to quarterly reconciliation within 30 days of\nthe end of the quarter at the beginning of the following quarter of each Contract\nYear and annual reconciliation at the end of each  Contract Year within30 days to\ntake into account the Energy Accounts, Tariff adjustment payments, Tariff Rebate,\nLate Payment Surcharge, or any other reasonable circumstance provided under this\nAgreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0215",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 215,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 118595,
    "char_end": 119338,
    "char_count": 743,
    "text": "10.6.2 The Parties, therefore, agree that as soon as all such data in respect of any quarter of\na Contract Year or a full Contract Year as the case may be has been finally verified\nand adjusted, the RPD and SECI shall jointly sign such reconciliation statement.\nWithin fifteen  (15)  days  of  signing  of  a  reconciliation  statement,  the  RPD\nshall  make appropriate adjustments in the next Monthly Bill.  Late Payment\nSurcharge/ interest shall be payable in such a case from the date on which such\npayment had been made to the invoicing Party or the date on which any payment\nwas originally due, as may be applicable. Any Dispute with regard to the above\nreconciliation shall be dealt with in accordance with the provisions of Article 16.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0216",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 216,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 119340,
    "char_end": 119448,
    "char_count": 108,
    "text": "10.7\nPayment of Supplementary Bill\n\n10.7.1 RPD may raise a (\"Supplementary Bill\") for payment on account of:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0217",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 217,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 119450,
    "char_end": 119946,
    "char_count": 496,
    "text": "i) Adjustments required by the Energy Accounts (if applicable); or\nii) Change in Law as provided in Article 12, or\niii) Transmission charges and losses, wheeling charges, RLDC/SLDC/Scheduling\ncharges, SOC, MOC, maintenance, etc. and any other charges from the Delivery\nPoint upto the drawl point for the transmission of power being delivered from the\npower project including Thermal Power Component, or\niv) Payment under Article 4.10,\nAnd such Supplementary Bill shall be paid by the other Party.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0218",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 218,
    "page_start": 53,
    "page_end": 53,
    "char_start": 119948,
    "char_end": 120112,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "SECI-RPD- PPA\n(Insert Project ID)                                                                                                                      Page 53 of 90",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0219",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 219,
    "page_start": 53,
    "page_end": 53,
    "char_start": 120114,
    "char_end": 120775,
    "char_count": 661,
    "text": "10.7.2 SECI shall remit all amounts due under a Supplementary Bill raised by the RPD to\nthe RPD ’s Designated Account by the Due Date, except open access charges,\nRLDC or scheduling charges and transmission charges (if applicable). For\nSupplementary Bill on account of adjustment required by energy account and\npayments under Article 4.10, Rebate as applicable to Monthly Bills pursuant to\nArticle 10.3.5 shall equally apply. Payment will be made after realization of the\nsame from the Buying Utility under the Power Sale Agreement. No Late Payment\nSurcharge will be applicable other than that on the monthly energy payment and\nassociated debit and credit note.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0220",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 220,
    "page_start": 54,
    "page_end": 54,
    "char_start": 120777,
    "char_end": 120941,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "SECI-RPD- PPA\n(Insert Project ID)                                                                                                                      Page 54 of 90",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0221",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 221,
    "page_start": 54,
    "page_end": 54,
    "char_start": 120943,
    "char_end": 121658,
    "char_count": 715,
    "text": "ARTICLE 11: FORCE MAJEURE\n\n11.1 Definition of Force Majeure\n\nA ‘Force Majeure’ (FM) would mean one or more of the following acts, events or\ncircumstances or a combination of acts, events or circumstances or the\nconsequence(s) thereof taking place within the Indian territory, that wholly or partly\nprevents or unavoidably delays the performance by the Party (the Affected Party) of\nits obligations under the relevant Power Purchase Agreement, but only if and to the\nextent that such events or circumstances are not within the reasonable control,\ndirectly or indirectly, of the Affected Party and could not have been avoided if the\nAffected Party had taken reasonable care or complied with Prudent Utility Practices.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0222",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 222,
    "page_start": 54,
    "page_end": 54,
    "char_start": 121660,
    "char_end": 121765,
    "char_count": 105,
    "text": "An Affected Party means SECI or the RPD whose performance has been affected\nby an event of Force Majeure.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0223",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 223,
    "page_start": 54,
    "page_end": 54,
    "char_start": 121767,
    "char_end": 123165,
    "char_count": 1398,
    "text": "11.2 Categorization of Force Majeure Events:\n\n11.2.1 Natural Force Majeure Event\na) Act of God, including, but not limited to lightning, drought, fire and explosion\n(to the extent originating from a source external to the site), earthquake,\nvolcanic eruption, landslide, flood, cyclone, typhoon or tornado if it is\ndeclared / notified by the competent state / central authority / agency (as\napplicable), or verified to the satisfaction of  SECI / Buying Utility;\nb) radioactive contamination or ionising radiation originating from a source in\nIndia or resulting from another Force Majeure Event mentioned above\nexcluding circumstances where the source or cause of contamination or\nradiation is brought or has been brought into or near the Project by the\nAffected Party or those employed or engaged by the Affected Party;\nc) the discovery of geological conditions, toxic contamination or archaeological\nremains on the Project land that could not reasonably have been expected to\nbe discovered through an inspection of the Project land; or\nd) any event or circumstances of a nature analogous to any of the events as\nspecified under Article 11.2.1 (a), 11.2.1 (b) and 11.2.1 (c).\n11.2.2 Non-Natural Force Majeure Event\na) any act of war (whether declared or undeclared), invasion, armed conflict or act\nof foreign enemy, blockade, embargo, revolution, riot, insurrection, terrorist or\nmilitary action;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0224",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 224,
    "page_start": 55,
    "page_end": 55,
    "char_start": 123167,
    "char_end": 123331,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "SECI-RPD- PPA\n(Insert Project ID)                                                                                                                      Page 55 of 90",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0225",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 225,
    "page_start": 55,
    "page_end": 55,
    "char_start": 123333,
    "char_end": 125063,
    "char_count": 1730,
    "text": "b) nation/state-wide strike, lockout, boycotts or other industrial disputes which are\nnot directly and solely attributable to the actions of the Affected Party, but does\nnot include strike or labour unrest limited to the Affected Party or its contractors;\nc) nationalisation or any compulsory acquisition by any Indian Governmental\nInstrumentality/ State Government in national interest or expropriation of any\nmaterial Project assets or rights of the RPD , as a result of which the RPD or its\nshareholders are deprived (wholly or partly) of their rights or entitlements under\nthe Power Purchase Agreement. Provided that such action does not constitute\nremedies or sanctions lawfully exercised by the Procurer or any other\nGovernment Authority as a result of any breach of any of the Applicable Laws\nor the Applicable Permits by the RPD or the RPD related parties;\nd) action of a Government Authority having Material Adverse Effect including but\nnot limited to Change in Law, only if consequences thereof cannot be dealt with\nunder and in accordance with the provisions of Article 12 of this Agreement; any\nunlawful or unauthorised or without jurisdiction revocation of, or delay in, or\nrefusal, or failure to renew or grant without valid cause, any Permits of the RPD\nor any of the clearance, license, authorization to be obtained by the contractors\nto perform their respective obligations under the relevant PPA; provided that\nsuch delay, modification, denial, refusal or revocation did not result from the\nRPD’s or any contractor’s inability or failure to comply with any condition\nrelating to grant, maintenance or renewal of such Permits or clearance, license,\nauthorization, as the case may be.\n11.3\nForce Majeure Exclusions",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0226",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 226,
    "page_start": 55,
    "page_end": 55,
    "char_start": 125065,
    "char_end": 125792,
    "char_count": 727,
    "text": "11.3.1 Force Majeure shall not include (i) any event or circumstance which is within the\nreasonable control of the Parties and (ii) the following conditions, except to the extent\nthat they are consequences of an event of Force Majeure:\na. Unavailability, late delivery, or changes in cost of the plant, machinery,\nequipment, materials, spare parts or consumables for the Power Project;\nb.  Delay in the performance of any contractor, sub-contractor or their agents;\nc. Non-performance resulting from normal wear and tear typically experienced in\npower generation materials and equipment;\nd. Strikes at the facilities of the Affected Party;\ne. Insufficiency of finances or funds or the agreement becoming onerous to\nperform; and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0227",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 227,
    "page_start": 56,
    "page_end": 56,
    "char_start": 125794,
    "char_end": 125958,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "SECI-RPD- PPA\n(Insert Project ID)                                                                                                                      Page 56 of 90",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0228",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 228,
    "page_start": 56,
    "page_end": 56,
    "char_start": 125960,
    "char_end": 126306,
    "char_count": 346,
    "text": "f.\nNon-performance caused by, or connected with, the Affected Party’s:\n\ni.  Negligent or intentional acts, errors or omissions;\nii.  Failure to comply with an Indian Law/ Applicable Law; or\niii.  Breach of, or default under this Agreement.\ng. Any pre-existing dispute on project land/substation and/or right-of-way or other\nproject related issues",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0229",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 229,
    "page_start": 56,
    "page_end": 56,
    "char_start": 126308,
    "char_end": 127590,
    "char_count": 1282,
    "text": "11.3.2 Notwithstanding anything else contained in this Agreement, the non-availability of\nthermal power from the Thermal Project of the Thermal Generator to complement the\nRE Power for RTC supply shall, under no circumstances, except for Force Majeure\nevents affecting such source of thermal power and events under Article 6.2.9, be\nconsidered as a Force Majeure Event, excusing the obligation of the RPD. In such case\nalso, the RPD is free to supply thermal power up to the Contracted Capacity from an\nalternative generation source, situated within the same RLDC area as that of the RE\nProject, to meet its obligations under this Agreement. Such thermal power shall be\nsupplied to the SECI at the same Tariff as per the terms of this Agreement, without\ncreating any additional liability upon SECI/Buying Entity. In case the transmission\nand other incidental charges, including but not limited to application fees for open\naccess, RLDC/SLDC charges, etc., applicable from the alternative source of thermal\npower supply are higher than the applicable Transmission Charges from the Injection\nPoint to the Delivery Point, the RPD would be liable to bear such additional charges.\nFurther, the RPD shall provide documentary evidence for establishing the source of\nsupply for such tie up.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0230",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 230,
    "page_start": 56,
    "page_end": 56,
    "char_start": 127592,
    "char_end": 128465,
    "char_count": 873,
    "text": "11.4\nNotification of Force Majeure Event\n\n11.4.1 The Affected Party shall give notice to the other Party of any event of Force Majeure\nas soon as reasonably practicable, but not later than fifteen (15) days after the date\non which such Party knew or should reasonably have known of the commencement\nof the event of Force Majeure. If an event of Force Majeure results in a breakdown\nof communications rendering it unreasonable to give notice within the applicable\ntime limit specified herein, then the Party claiming Force Majeure shall give such\nnotice as soon as reasonably practicable after reinstatement of communications, but\nnot later than one (1) day after such reinstatement. The Party who receives the Force\nMajeure Notification, shall take a decision on the claim of occurrence of Force\nMajeure Event, within 30 days of the receipt of the intimation supported with",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0231",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 231,
    "page_start": 57,
    "page_end": 57,
    "char_start": 128467,
    "char_end": 128631,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "SECI-RPD- PPA\n(Insert Project ID)                                                                                                                      Page 57 of 90",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0232",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 232,
    "page_start": 57,
    "page_end": 57,
    "char_start": 128633,
    "char_end": 129803,
    "char_count": 1170,
    "text": "documentary evidence. It is to be noted that there shall have to be separate Force\nMajeure notice to be given by the Affected Party for RE and Thermal Power Project\ncomponents. Consequence of Force Majeure notice of one part shall not have any\nconsequence on the other part unless specified specifically by the Affected Party.\n11.4.2 Provided that such notice shall be a pre-condition to the Affected Party’s entitlement\nto claim relief under this Agreement. Such notice shall include full particulars of\nthe event of Force Majeure, its effects on the Party claiming relief and the remedial\nmeasures proposed. The Affected Party shall give the other Party regular (and not\nless than weekly) reports on the progress of those remedial measures and such other\ninformation as the other Party may reasonably request about the Force Majeure\nEvent.\n11.4.3 The Affected Party shall give notice to the other Party of (i) the cessation of the\nrelevant event of Force Majeure; and (ii) the cessation of the effects of such event\nof Force Majeure on the performance of its rights or obligations under the PPA, as\nsoon as practicable after becoming aware of each of these cessations.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0233",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 233,
    "page_start": 57,
    "page_end": 57,
    "char_start": 129805,
    "char_end": 130899,
    "char_count": 1094,
    "text": "11.5\nPerformance Excused\n\n11.5.1 The Affected Party, to the extent rendered unable to perform its obligations or part\nof the obligation thereof under the PPA as a consequence of the Force Majeure\nEvent, shall be excused from performance of the obligations, provided that the\nperiod shall not exceed 180 (one hundred and eighty) Days from the date of\nissuance of the FM Notice. The Parties may mutually agree to extend the period\nfor which performance is excused due to a Force Majeure Event.\n11.5.2 For the time period, as mutually agreed by the Parties, during which the\nperformance shall be excused, the RPD shall be entitled for a day to day extension\nof the period provided for Financial Closure or Scheduled Commercial Operation\nPeriod or the PPA period, as the case may be.\n          Provided always that a Party shall be excused from performance only to the extent\nreasonably warranted by the Force Majeure Event.\n          Provided further that, nothing shall absolve the Affected Party from any payment\nobligations accrued prior to the occurrence of the underlying Force Majeure Event.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0234",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 234,
    "page_start": 58,
    "page_end": 58,
    "char_start": 130901,
    "char_end": 131065,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "SECI-RPD- PPA\n(Insert Project ID)                                                                                                                      Page 58 of 90",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0235",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 235,
    "page_start": 58,
    "page_end": 58,
    "char_start": 131067,
    "char_end": 131330,
    "char_count": 263,
    "text": "11.6\nNo Liability for Other Losses\n\nSave as otherwise provided in this Agreement, no Party shall be liable in any manner,\nwhatsoever, to the other Parties in respect of any loss relating to or arising out of the\noccurrence or existence of any Force Majeure Event.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0236",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 236,
    "page_start": 58,
    "page_end": 58,
    "char_start": 131332,
    "char_end": 131923,
    "char_count": 591,
    "text": "11.7\nResumption of Performance\n\nDuring the period that a Force Majeure Event is subsisting, the Affected Party\nshall, in consultation with the other Parties, make all reasonable efforts to limit or\nmitigate the effects of such Force Majeure Event on the performance of its\nobligations under the PPA. The Affected Party shall also make efforts to resume\nperformance of its obligations under this Agreement as soon as possible and upon\nresumption, shall notify other Parties of the same in writing. The other Parties\nshall afford all reasonable assistance to the Affected Party in this regard.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0237",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 237,
    "page_start": 58,
    "page_end": 58,
    "char_start": 131925,
    "char_end": 132350,
    "char_count": 425,
    "text": "11.8\nDuty to Perform and Duty to Mitigate\n\nTo the extent not prevented by a Force Majeure Event pursuant to Article 11.2,\nthe Affected Party shall continue to perform its obligations pursuant to this\nAgreement, in line with provisions of Article 11.5. The Affected Party shall use\nits reasonable efforts to mitigate the effect of any Force Majeure Event as soon\nas practicable.\n11.9\nAvailable Relief for a Force Majeure Event",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0238",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 238,
    "page_start": 58,
    "page_end": 58,
    "char_start": 132352,
    "char_end": 133026,
    "char_count": 674,
    "text": "Subject to this Article 11:\na) no Party shall be in breach of its obligations pursuant to this Agreement\nexcept to the extent that the performance of its obligations was prevented,\nhindered or delayed due to a Force Majeure Event;\nb) every Party shall be entitled to claim relief in relation to a Force Majeure\nEvent in regard to its obligations, including but not limited to those specified\nunder Article 4.5;\nc) For avoidance of doubt, neither Party’s obligation to make payments of\nmoney due and payable prior to occurrence of Force Majeure events under\nthis Agreement shall be suspended or excused due to the occurrence of a\nForce Majeure Event in respect of such Party.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0239",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 239,
    "page_start": 59,
    "page_end": 59,
    "char_start": 133028,
    "char_end": 133192,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "SECI-RPD- PPA\n(Insert Project ID)                                                                                                                      Page 59 of 90",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0240",
