    "char_start": 135721,
    "char_end": 135840,
    "char_count": 119,
    "text": "ARTICLE 12: CHANGE IN LAW\n\n12.1\nDefinitions\n\nIn this Article 12, the following terms shall have the following meanings:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0244",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 244,
    "page_start": 60,
    "page_end": 60,
    "char_start": 135842,
    "char_end": 137612,
    "char_count": 1770,
    "text": "12.1.1 In this Article 12, the term Change in Law shall refer to the occurrence of any of the\nfollowing events enforced by the Government of India, after [Insert last date of bid\nsubmission], which have a direct effect on the Project (and TPower Component),\nincluding (i) the enactment of any new law; or (ii) an amendment, modification or\nrepeal of an existing law;  or (iii) the requirement to obtain a new consent, permit or\nlicense; or (iv) any modification to the prevailing conditions prescribed for obtaining\na consent, permit or license, not owing to any default of the RPD ; or (v) any change\nin the rates of any Taxes, duties or cess, which have a direct effect on the Project,\nalong with Thermal Power Component.\nHowever, Change in Law shall not include any change in taxes on corporate income\nor any change in any withholding tax on income or dividends.\n12.1.2 In the event a Change in Law results in any adverse financial loss/ gain to the RPD\nthen, in order to ensure that the RPD is placed in the same financial position as it\nwould have been had it not been for the occurrence of the Change in Law, the RPD\n/ SECI / Buying Utility(ies) shall be entitled for compensation by the other party,\nas the case may be, subject to the condition that the such ‘Change in Law ’ is\nrecognized by the Appropriate Commission. Compensation payment on account of\nsuch ‘Change in Law shall be determined and shall be effective from such date as\nmay be decided by the Appropriate Commission, and any such compensation shall\nbe limited to the RTC configuration corresponding to the Contracted Capacity only\n12.1.3  Notwithstanding anything in Clause 12.1.1 above, in case of change in rates of\nduties and taxes in respect of safeguard duty, GST and basic customs duty, then",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0245",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 245,
    "page_start": 60,
    "page_end": 60,
    "char_start": 137613,
    "char_end": 138117,
    "char_count": 504,
    "text": "such change will be treated as ‘Change in Law’ and the quantum of compensation\npayment on account of change in rates of such duties/taxes and shall be provided to\nthe affected party by the other party as per Article 12.2.3, subject to the provision\nthat Appropriate Commission recognizes such provisions at the time of adoption of\ntariff by the Appropriate Commission and any decision in this regard shall be\ngoverning on SPD and Buying Entity without the need for approaching the\nAppropriate Commission.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0246",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 246,
    "page_start": 61,
    "page_end": 61,
    "char_start": 138119,
    "char_end": 138283,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "SECI-RPD- PPA\n(Insert Project ID)                                                                                                                      Page 61 of 90",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0247",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 247,
    "page_start": 61,
    "page_end": 61,
    "char_start": 138285,
    "char_end": 139503,
    "char_count": 1218,
    "text": "12.1.4 Compensation Payment on account of ‘Change in Law’, either as determined by the\nAppropriate Commission as per Article 12.1.2 above or mutually agreed upon\nbetween the RPD and SECI/Buying Utility as per Article 12.1.3 above, can be paid\nto the affected party, by the other party, in terms of modifications in the PPA tariff.\nNotwithstanding anything contained above, the Buying Entity(ies) can also make\npayment of such Change in Law amount, either wholly or partly, as a onetime lump\npayment. The balance, if any, may be paid in terms of modifications in PPA.\n12.2\nRelief for Change in Law\n12.2.1 The aggrieved Party shall be required to approach the Central Electricity Regulatory\nCommission for seeking approval of Change in Law.\n12.2.2 The decision of the Central Electricity Regulatory Commission to acknowledge a\nChange in Law and the date from which it will become effective, provide relief for\nthe same, shall be final and governing on RPD and Buying Entities.\n12.2.3 In case of Change in Law/ Regulations as approved by the Appropriate Commission\npursuant to Article 12.2.1 or as provided under Article 12.1.3, the RPD/ SECI/\nBuying Entities (as the case may be) shall be entitled for relief as follows:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0248",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 248,
    "page_start": 61,
    "page_end": 61,
    "char_start": 139505,
    "char_end": 140051,
    "char_count": 546,
    "text": "Every net increase/decrease of Rs.1 lakh per MW in the RE Project Cost (i.e.\ncost incurred by the RPD for the supply and services in the Project concerned,\nupto Actual Commissioning Date of the last part capacity or Schedule\nCommissioning Date / extended Schedule Commissioning Date, whichever is\nearlier, for reasons other than those wherein such extension is on account of\npayment of liquidated damages, penalty or any other charges, as the case may\nbe), shall be liable for corresponding increase/decrease of an amount equal to\nRs 0.0036 /kWh.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0249",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 249,
    "page_start": 61,
    "page_end": 61,
    "char_start": 140053,
    "char_end": 140212,
    "char_count": 159,
    "text": "In regard to the thermal component, relief as granted by the Central Electricity\nRegulatory Commission shall be final and governing on RPD and Buying Entities.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0250",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 250,
    "page_start": 61,
    "page_end": 61,
    "char_start": 140214,
    "char_end": 140711,
    "char_count": 497,
    "text": "Any such change, shall be considered upto three digits after the decimal point, and\nremaining digits, if any, shall be ignored.\nFor e.g. in case the change in tariff payable is calculated as Rs. 0.14678/kWh, it\nshall be modified as Rs. 0.146/kWh.\n12.2.4  In case Change in Law results in delay in commissioning or supply of power, where\ncause and effect between these two can be clearly established, the SECI under\nintimation to the Buying Entities may provide suitable time-extension in Scheduled",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
