    "page_end": 66,
    "char_start": 148924,
    "char_end": 149343,
    "char_count": 419,
    "text": "13.3.4 Within a period of seven (7) days following the expiry of the Consultation Period\nunless the Parties shall have otherwise agreed to the contrary or the RPD Event of\nDefault giving rise to the Consultation Period shall have ceased to exist or shall have\nbeen   remedied, SECI   may terminate this Agreement under intimation the Buying\nEntities by giving a written Termination Notice of sixty (60) days to the RPD.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0272",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 272,
    "page_start": 66,
    "page_end": 66,
    "char_start": 149345,
    "char_end": 151096,
    "char_count": 1751,
    "text": "13.3.5 Subject to the terms of this Agreement, upon occurrence of a RPD Event of Default\nunder this Agreement, the RPD shall be liable to pay to SECI, liquidated damages,\nas provided in Article 4.6 of the PPA for failure to commission within stipulated\ntime and Article 4.4.1 for failure to supply power in terms of the PPA. For other\ncases, the RPD shall be liable pay to Buying Entity(ies), damages, equivalent to 6\n(six) months, or balance PPA period whichever is less, of charges calculated at\nApplicable Tariff for its Contracted Capacity. SECI shall have the right to recover\nthe said damages by way of forfeiture of bank guarantee/POI, if any, without\nprejudice to resorting to any other legal course or remedy. In addition to the levy of\ndamages as aforesaid, the lenders in concurrence with the Buying Entity and SECI,\nmay exercise their rights, if any, under Financing Agreements, to seek substitution\nof the RPD by a selectee for the residual period of the Agreement, for the purpose\nof securing the payments of the total debt amount from the RPD and performing the\nobligations of the RPD. However, in the event the lenders are unable to substitute\nthe defaulting RPD within the stipulated period, SECI may terminate the PPA and\nthe Buying Entity may acquire the RE Project assets for an amount equivalent to\n90% of the Debt Due (on the concerned RE Project(s)), failing which, the lenders\nmay exercise their mortgage rights and liquidate the RE Project assets. Provided that\nany substitution under this Agreement can only be made with the prior consent of\nSECI including the condition that the selectee meets the eligibility requirements of\nRequest for Selection (RfS) issued by SECI and accepts the terms and conditions of\nthis Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0273",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 273,
    "page_start": 67,
    "page_end": 67,
    "char_start": 151098,
    "char_end": 151262,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "SECI-RPD- PPA\n(Insert Project ID)                                                                                                                      Page 67 of 90",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0274",
