    "paragraph_index": 275,
    "page_start": 67,
    "page_end": 67,
    "char_start": 151695,
    "char_end": 152053,
    "char_count": 358,
    "text": "13.3.7 In the event the lenders are unable to substitute the defaulting RPD within the\nstipulated period, SECI may terminate the PPA and the Buying Utility may acquire\nthe RE Project assets for an amount equivalent to 90% of the debt due (for the RE\nProject(s)), failing which, the lenders may exercise their mortgage rights and\nliquidate the Project assets.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0276",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 276,
    "page_start": 67,
    "page_end": 67,
    "char_start": 152055,
    "char_end": 152379,
    "char_count": 324,
    "text": "13.4\nProcedure for cases of SECI Event of Default\n13.4.1 Upon the occurrence and continuation of any SECI Event of Default specified in\nArticle 13.2, the RPD shall have the right to deliver to SECI, a RPD Preliminary\nDefault Notice, which notice shall specify in reasonable detail the circumstances\ngiving rise to its issue.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0277",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 277,
    "page_start": 67,
    "page_end": 67,
    "char_start": 152381,
    "char_end": 152755,
    "char_count": 374,
    "text": "13.4.2 Following the issue of a RPD Preliminary Default Notice, the Consultation Period\nof ninety (90) days or such longer period as the Parties may agree, shall apply and\nit shall be the responsibility of the Parties to discuss as to what steps shall be taken\nwith a view to mitigate the consequences of the relevant Event of Default having\nregard to all the circumstances.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0278",
