    "char_end": 153563,
    "char_count": 677,
    "text": "13.4.4 After a period of two hundred ten (210) days following the expiry of the Consultation\nPeriod and unless the Parties shall have otherwise agreed to the contrary or SECI\nEvent of Default giving rise to the Consultation Period shall have ceased to exist or\nshall have been remedied, SECI under intimation to the Buying Entity and the RPD\nshall, subject to the prior consent of the RPD, novate its part of the PPA to any third\nparty, including its Affiliates within the stipulated period. In the event the aforesaid\nnovation is not acceptable to the RPD , or if no offer of novation is made by SECI\nwithin the stipulated period, then the RPD may terminate the PPA and at its",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0280",
