    "page_start": 72,
    "page_end": 72,
    "char_start": 161862,
    "char_end": 162471,
    "char_count": 609,
    "text": "SECI to effectively pay the amount to the RPD, the payment of money becoming due\nfrom the SECI to the RPD under this Agreement for supply of RE Power to the extent\nof the Contracted Capacity shall be as per:\n (i) the recourse under the Payment Security Mechanism provided in the PPA and\nPSA, as follows:\na) Letter of Credit;\n(b) State Government Guarantee/ Tri-Partite Agreement (TPA) signed\nbetween Reserve Bank of India, Central Government and State Government of\nthe Buying Entity, covering security for payment of energy charges, as\napplicable;\n(c) Payment Security Fund provided by the Buying Entity, and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0299",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 299,
    "page_start": 72,
    "page_end": 72,
    "char_start": 162473,
    "char_end": 163083,
    "char_count": 610,
    "text": "(ii) Payment security fund as referred in Article 10.1.1 of the PPA.\nSECI shall discharge the tariff payment obligation in terms of the provisions of this\nAgreement.\nAccordingly, in the event of the failure on the part of Buying Entity(ies), SECI shall\nproceed to take recourse to the above and make efforts for the payment of the principal\namount to the RPD at the earliest possible time. Further, the combined liability of\nSECI arising out of this Agreement and Power Sale Agreement shall be limited to the\nTrading Margin (i.e. Rs 0.07/kWh) received under Power Sale Agreement(s) for the\nContracted Capacity.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
