  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0374",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 374,
    "page_start": 85,
    "page_end": 85,
    "char_start": 185778,
    "char_end": 185976,
    "char_count": 198,
    "text": "Reg: M/s ________________(insert name of the PPA signing entity) (Project No.\n__________(insert project ID issued by SECI) – Issuance of Payment on Order\nInstrument for an amount of Rs._____________",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0375",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 375,
    "page_start": 85,
    "page_end": 85,
    "char_start": 185978,
    "char_end": 186904,
    "char_count": 926,
    "text": "Dear Sir,\n\n1.\nThe Ministry of New and Renewable Energy, Government of India vide its letter dated\n12th March 2020 has decided that to facilitate the promotion of solar and wind power\ndevelopment and implementation of the project by the Solar and Wind Power Developers\nwho have entered into financing and funding agreements with IREDA/REC/PFC, the\nsecurity by way of PBG in the form of Performance Bank Guarantee given by the\nDevelopers be allowed to be substituted by Letter of Undertaking/ Payment on Order\nInstrument issued by Non-Banking Finance Companies under the control of the Ministry\nof New and Renewable Energy and Ministry of Power. SECI and other nodal agencies\nappointed by the Government of India with whom the power developers have entered\ninto Power Purchase Agreement may accept the same in place of PBG. The Ministry of\nNew and Renewable Energy vide letter dated 12.03.2020 has, inter-alia, decided as\nunder:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0376",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 376,
    "page_start": 85,
    "page_end": 85,
    "char_start": 186906,
    "char_end": 188028,
    "char_count": 1122,
    "text": "6. After carefully examining the matter, the Ministry have decided as follows:\n\nb)\n (i) SECT or NTPC or any other implementing agency on behalf of MNRE\n(henceforth called implementing agencies) may release the Performance Bank\nGuarantee (PBG) of any project if RE developers are able to replace the same\nwith Letter(s) of Undertaking to pay in case situation of default of RE\ndeveloper in terms of Power Purchase Agreement (PPA) arises, from Indian\nRenewable Energy Development Agency Limited (IREDA) or Power Finance\nCorporation Limited (PFC) or REC Limited (REC), the three non-banking\nfinancial institutions under Ministry of New & Renewable Energy (MNRE)/\nMinistry of Power (MoP). These three financial institutions - IREDA or PFC\nor REC may issue such Letter(s) of Undertaking to pay only after securing\ntheir financial interests taking into account the security(ies) available with\nthem as per their policy and after due diligence. These non-banking financial\ninstitutions would ensure that the security(ies) available with them are enough\nto cover full risk/ or exposure, which may arise on account of issue of such",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0377",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 377,
    "page_start": 86,
    "page_end": 86,
    "char_start": 188030,
    "char_end": 188196,
    "char_count": 166,
    "text": "SECI-RPD PPA\n(Insert Project ID)                                                                                                                         Page 86 of 90",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0378",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 378,
    "page_start": 86,
    "page_end": 86,
    "char_start": 188198,
    "char_end": 188595,
    "char_count": 397,
    "text": "Letter(s) of Undertaking. Such Letter(s) may be termed as \"Payment on Order\ninstrument\" and will have same effect as that of a Bank Guarantee issued by\nany public sector bank. This \"Payment on Order instrument\" would have terms\nand conditions similar to that of any Bank Guarantee given by any public\nsector bank and would promise to pay the implementing agencies on demand\nwithin stipulated time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0379",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 379,
    "page_start": 86,
    "page_end": 86,
    "char_start": 188606,
    "char_end": 188870,
    "char_count": 264,
    "text": "(ii) RE developers can seek such Letters(s) by offering due security to the above\nmentioned three non-banking financial institutions mentioned above (IREDA,\nPFC & REC) for seeking replacement of their Bank Guarantees already\npledged with the implementing agencies.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC071-0380",
    "doc_id": "DOC-071",
    "paragraph_index": 380,
    "page_start": 86,
    "page_end": 86,
    "char_start": 188880,
    "char_end": 189055,
    "char_count": 175,
    "text": "(iii) For future projects, RE developers would be at liberty to either pledge Bank\nGuarantee(s) or Letter(s) of Undertaking as stated above towards\nPerformance Bank Guarantee.",
