  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC072-0123",
    "doc_id": "DOC-072",
    "paragraph_index": 123,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 81208,
    "char_end": 82590,
    "char_count": 1382,
    "text": "ARTICLE 9: APPLICABLE TARIFF\n9.1      Subsequent to commencement of power supply by the SPD on the terms contained in\nthis Agreement, the SPD shall be entitled to receive the Tariff of Rs. …………../ kWh\n[Insert the Tariff discovered through the bidding process conducted by SECI], fixed\nfor the entire term of this Agreement.\n9.2\nIn case of early part/full commencement of power supply from the project, till SCSD,\nthe SPD will be free to sell the electricity generated, to any entity other than the SECI/\nBuying Entity(ies), only after giving the first right of refusal to the SECI/Buying\nEntity(ies). SECI shall provide refusal within 15 (fifteen) days from the receipt of the\nrequest for early part/full commencement of power supply from the Project, beyond\nwhich it would be considered as deemed refusal. In case SECI/Buying Entity agree to\npurchase power from a date prior to the SCSD, such power shall be purchased at the\nApplicable Tariff.\n9.2\nAny excess generation over and above energy specified in Article 4.4.1, will be\npurchased by SECI at the Applicable Tariff, and provided the Buying Entity consents\nfor purchase of such excess generation. Any energy produced and flowing into the grid\nbefore SCSD shall not be at the cost of SECI. SECI may agree to buy such power\nprovided Buying Entity consents to purchase such energy at Applicable Tariff plus\nSECI’s Trading margin.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC072-0124",
    "doc_id": "DOC-072",
    "paragraph_index": 124,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 82592,
    "char_end": 83022,
    "char_count": 430,
    "text": "However, the SPD will not be allowed to sell energy generated prior to SCSD or excess\nenergy during any Contract Year to any other entity other than SECI (unless refused\nby SECI).\n9.3\nThe SPD may also sell the power which was offered on day ahead basis to the Buying\nEntity(ies) (within maximum CUF) but not scheduled by the Buying Entity(ies) to any\nthird party or power exchange without requiring NOC from the Buying Entity(ies)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
