    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 268,
    "char_end": 667,
    "char_count": 399,
    "text": "Solar Energy Corporation of India Limited, a company incorporated under the\nCompanies Act 1956, having its registered office at 1st Floor, A-Wing, D-3, District\nCentre, Saket, New Delhi-110017 (hereinafter referred to as “SECI”, which expression\nshall, unless repugnant to the context or meaning thereof, be deemed to include its\nsuccessors and permitted assignees) as a Party of the first part.\nAnd",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0004",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 4,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 669,
    "char_end": 1034,
    "char_count": 365,
    "text": "……..[Enter name of the Buying Entity/ Utility], a company incorporated under the\nCompanies Act 2013, having its registered office at ……………. (hereinafter referred to\nas “Buying Entity/ Buying Utility” which expression shall, unless repugnant to the\ncontext or meaning thereof, be deemed to include its successors and permitted assigns)\nas a Party of the second part.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0005",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 5,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 1036,
    "char_end": 1140,
    "char_count": 104,
    "text": "SECI and Buying Entity are individually referred to as ‘Party’ and collectively referred\nto as ‘Parties’",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0006",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 6,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 1142,
    "char_end": 1361,
    "char_count": 219,
    "text": "PAGE 2 OF 25\nWHEREAS:\n\nA. The Government of India has announced the Policy for promotion of the Solar\nPower in the country and has provided a target to achieve an aggregate\ninstalled capacity of 100 GW by the year 2022.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0007",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 7,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 1362,
    "char_end": 1729,
    "char_count": 367,
    "text": "B. The Ministry of Power, Government of India has issued the Guidelines for\nTariff Based Competitive Bidding Process for procurement of power from\nGrid connected Solar PV Power Projects vide Resolution dated 3rd August,\n2017, including subsequent amendments and clarifications thereof, if any,\nissued until ________ [Enter the last date of bid submission of the RfS].",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0008",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 8,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 1730,
    "char_end": 1934,
    "char_count": 204,
    "text": "C. SECI has been designated as a Nodal Agency for developing and facilitating\nthe establishment of the Grid connected Solar Power capacity in India in terms\nof the above Policy of the Government of India;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0009",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 9,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 1935,
    "char_end": 2283,
    "char_count": 348,
    "text": "D. SECI had initiated a Tariff Based Competitive Bid Process for procurement of\n1200 MW of the power generated from the Grid connected Solar PV Power\nProject on the terms and conditions contained in the Request for Selection\n(herein after referred to as ‘RfS’) issued by SECI vide RfS No ____________\nDated _______ and subsequent amendment, if any;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0010",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 10,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 2284,
    "char_end": 2785,
    "char_count": 501,
    "text": "E. SECI has signed/will sign Power Purchase Agreements (PPAs) with the Solar\nPower Developers (SPD) selected under the RfS mentioned herein below\n(hereinafter referred to as “SPDs”) for procurement of _______ MW Solar\nPower or the total capacity of projects selected under the provisions of Request\nfor Selection No. __________________ dated _______ and subsequent\namendment, if any) based on the above Guidelines, if it is less than ______\nMW, on a long-term basis, as indicated at Schedule-B of PSA;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0011",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 11,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 2786,
    "char_end": 3302,
    "char_count": 516,
    "text": "F. Buying Utility has agreed to purchase Solar power from the SECI under the\nabove RfS and accordingly, SECI has agreed to sign Power Purchase\nAgreements (PPAs) with Solar Power developers (hereinafter referred to as\n“SPDs”) for procurement of ____MW Solar Power on a long-term basis, as\nindicated at Schedule-B of PSA. Copy of the PPA(s) shall be submitted to\nBuying Utility within thirty (30) days of the signing of the PPA(s) and such\nPPA(s) shall become integral part of this Agreement (SECI-Buying Utility\nPSA).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0012",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 12,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 3304,
    "char_end": 4084,
    "char_count": 780,
    "text": "PAGE 3 OF 25\nG. Pursuant to the aforesaid objective, the Parties are desirous of entering into a\nPower Sale Agreement (“PSA”) i.e. a definitive agreement, regarding purchase\nof Power from the Project. Pending execution of the necessary agreements and\nother relevant documents in relation to the transaction contemplated herein, the\nParties wish to execute this PSA setting out the respective obligations of the\nParties and the steps necessary to complete the transactions contemplated\nherein.\nThe Parties have accordingly agreed to enter into this PSA to record their understanding\nand agreement with regard to the purchase of power to be generated from the Project and\nin respect to the matters incidental or ancillary thereto, upon the terms and conditions set\nout herein below.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0013",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 13,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 4086,
    "char_end": 4259,
    "char_count": 173,
    "text": "NOW, THEREFORE, IN CONSIDERATION OF THE PROMISES AND MUTUAL\nAGREEMENTS, COVENANTS AND CONDITIONS SET FORTH HEREIN, IT IS\nHEREBY AGREED BY AND BETWEEN THE PARTIES AS FOLLOWS:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0014",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 14,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 4261,
    "char_end": 4428,
    "char_count": 167,
    "text": "I\nThis Agreement shall come into effect from signing of this Agreement by both\nthe parties and such date shall be the Effective Date for the purpose of this\nAgreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0015",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 15,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 4430,
    "char_end": 5566,
    "char_count": 1136,
    "text": "II\nNotwithstanding the Effective Date, the condition precedent for the enforcement\nof the obligations of either Party against the other under this Agreement shall be\nthat, within 120 days after the Effective Date of the PPA, SECI and/or the Buying\nEntity shall obtain adoption of tariff from its State Electricity Regulatory\nCommission and/or CERC (as applicable), on the terms and conditions contained\nin this Agreement read with the terms and conditions contained in the Power\nPurchase Agreement entered into between SECI and the SPD. The Parties agree\nthat in the event the order of adoption of tariff as mentioned above is not issued\nby the SERC and/or CERC (as applicable) within the time specified above, this\nshall entail a corresponding extension in Scheduled Financial Closure and the\nScheduled Commissioning Date of the Projects for equal number of days for\nwhich the CERC/SERC order has been delayed beyond the above deadline.\nIII\nThe duration of this Agreement shall be coextensive and coterminous with the\nduration of the Power Purchase Agreement to be entered into between the SECI and\nthe SPD for all intent and purposes.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0016",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 16,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 5568,
    "char_end": 7353,
    "char_count": 1785,
    "text": "PAGE 4 OF 25\nV\nSubject to the terms and conditions contained herein, SECI hereby agrees to sell and\nmake available the electricity procured by SECI from the _____MW Solar PV\nPower Project to be set up by the SPD at various places in _____ [Enter the location\nof the Projects] on the terms and conditions contained in the PPA to be entered into\nbetween SECI and the SPD, as per the initialed PPA (Schedule \"A\") on a back to\nback basis, to Buying Entity.\nVI.\nBuying Entity hereby acknowledges and accepts that SECI is an Intermediary to\nfacilitate the promotion of Solar Power Projects and to purchase and re-sell the\nelectricity to the distribution licensees to enable them to fulfill the Renewable\nPurchase Obligation and, therefore, the sale of electricity by SECI to Buying Entity\nunder this Agreement shall be entirely on a back to back basis to the purchase of\nelectricity by SECI from the SPDs under the SECI-SPD PPA, with the intent that\nthere shall be no residual liability on the SECI towards the SPD which will not be\nfulfilled by the Buying Entity.\nVII.\nIn accordance with the above and except as otherwise specifically provided in this\nagreement, the rights and obligations of Buying Entity under this agreement shall\nbe available and enforceable entirely and effectively on a back to back basis to the\nrights and obligations of the SECI in the SECI-SPD PPA and in the event SECI is\nnot in a position to enforce its rights against the SPD or is subject to any obligation\nto be performed towards SPD, Buying Entity shall be liable to perform such\nobligation or shall be entitled to such rights only on a mutatis mutandis basis,\nwithout any additional or independent exposure whatsoever to SECI.\nVIII. Except as otherwise specifically provided in this agreement, Buying Entity",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0017",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 17,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 7354,
    "char_end": 7840,
    "char_count": 486,
    "text": "acknowledges and accepts that the terms and conditions of the SECI- SPD PPA\nshall mutatis mutandis apply to this Agreement between the parties. Buying Entity\nagrees to correspondingly fulfill, on back to back basis, all the obligations assumed\nby SECI towards SPD. Buying Entity further agrees, acknowledges and accepts\nthat as an Intermediary, SECI is not assuming any obligation to Buying Entity over\nand above the obligation which the SPD shall duly perform under the SECI – SPD\nPPA.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0018",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 18,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 7842,
    "char_end": 8084,
    "char_count": 242,
    "text": "IX.\nSECI has agreed with the SPD in regard to the payment of money becoming due to\nSPD under the SECI – SPD PPA and SECI shall be liable to discharge the payment\nobligation in terms of the provisions of the SECI- SPD PPA.  Accordingly, Buying",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0019",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 19,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 8086,
    "char_end": 9874,
    "char_count": 1788,
    "text": "PAGE 5 OF 25\nEntity agrees to effectively securitize the payment of money becoming due from\nBuying Entity to SECI as detailed in this Agreement.\nX.\nThe parties agree that in respect of the obligations other than the payment\nobligation specifically mentioned herein above, in the event Buying Entity has any\nclaim against SECI in regard to the performance of any obligation of SECI under\nthis Agreement or enforcement of any right of Buying Entity against SECI under\nthis Agreement, the same shall be subject to the ability of SECI to enforce the\ncorresponding obligations assumed by SPD to SECI under the SECI-SPD PPA.\nSECI shall not be required to perform and implement the obligations of SECI or\nagree to the enforcement of the rights of Buying Entity under this Agreement till\nsuch time the corresponding obligations under SECI-SPD PPA is duly\nimplemented by the SPD and in case of monetary obligations the amount is\nreceived by SECI from the SPD. In the event of any such claim arising at the\ninstance of Buying Entity, the parties shall discuss on the course of action to be\ninitiated by SECI against the SPD for enforcement of the corresponding obligation\nand all proceedings to be initiated by SECI against the SPD for such enforcement\nshall be pursued by SECI in consultation with Buying Entity.\nXI.\nThe parties hereby agree that the SPD shall be liable to pay compensation under\nthe SECI-SPD PPA for shortfall in energy supply from the contracted energy on an\nannual basis. The amount of such compensation shall be as determined by the\nrespective State Electricity Regulatory Commission of the corresponding Buying\nEntity/ any such Authority, and such compensation shall ensure that the Buying\nEntity is offset for all potential costs associated with low generation and supply of",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0020",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 20,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 9875,
    "char_end": 10713,
    "char_count": 838,
    "text": "power under the PPA. However, the minimum compensation payable to SECI by\nthe SPD shall be 25% (twenty-five percent) of the cost of this shortfall in energy\nterms, calculated at PPA tariff. This amount so collected from the SPD shall be\npassed on to the Buying Entity. In case the Buying Entity does not avail the\nremittance of such compensation within sixty (60) days of the end of\ncorresponding Contract Year, the Buying Entity shall have a right to recover the\nsame from the amount payable by Buying Entity against Monthly Invoices. The\nParties agree that as an intermediary, SECI shall have no legal obligation to pay\nany amount towards this compensation, except when the amount of such\ncompensation has been recovered from the SPD by SECI without any conditions\nand encumbrances and the amount is available for appropriation by SECI.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0021",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 21,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 6,
    "char_start": 10715,
    "char_end": 11549,
    "char_count": 834,
    "text": "PAGE 6 OF 25\n\nXII.\nThe parties agree that the various terms contained in the SECI–SPD PPA such as\nScope of Project, Terms of the Agreement, Performance Guarantee, Conditions\nSubsequent, Obligations of the respective Parties, Construction of the Power\nGeneration\nCapacity,\nSynchronization,\nCommissioning\nand\nCommercial\nOperation, Operation and Maintenance, Purchase and Sale of Solar Power,\nMeasuring and Metering and Dispatch of Power, Billing and Power Accounting\nand payments, Liabilities, Force Majeure, Events of Default, Termination,\nTransfer, Change in Law, Indemnity, Insurance, Assignment and Changes,\nFinancing and Bankability, Representations and Warranties, Governing Law,\nNotices and all other Miscellaneous Terms provided in the SECI- SPD PPA shall\nmutatis mutandis apply to this agreement between SECI and Buying Entity.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0022",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 22,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 6,
    "char_start": 11551,
    "char_end": 12183,
    "char_count": 632,
    "text": "XIII. The Buying Entity shall be responsible to for directly coordinating and dealing\nwith the SPD, Regional Load Dispatch Centers, Regional Power Committees, and\nother authorities in all respects in regard to declaration of availability, scheduling\nand despatch of Solar Power and due compliance with deviation and settlement\nmechanism and the applicable Grid code Regulations, acknowledging that the SPD\nand Buying Entity are the Grid connected entities and SECI as intermediary\nprocurers/ trading licensee is not a Grid connected entity in respect of the Solar\nPower contracted under this Agreement;\nArticle 1.  APPLICABLE TARIFF",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0023",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 23,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 6,
    "char_start": 12185,
    "char_end": 12999,
    "char_count": 814,
    "text": "1.1\nThe Tariff applicable for the sale of Solar Power by SECI to the Buying Entity\nunder this Agreement shall be the Tariff as applicable for payment by SECI to SPD\nunder the terms of the Power Purchase Agreement between SECI and the SPD\n(Individual SPDs tariff as per schedule B) fixed for entire term of agreement at\ndelivery point and in addition thereto a trading margin of Seven (7) paisa/kWh shall\nbe payable by the Buying Entity to SECI which SECI shall be entitled to appropriate\nas its income.\n1.2\nAs per provisions of the PPA, the SPDs are permitted for full as well as part\ncommissioning of the Project even prior to the SCD. In case of early part\ncommissioning of the Project(s) prior to SCD, Buying Entity may purchase the\npower @75% of the Applicable tariff as per the PPA, plus SECI’s Trading Margin",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0024",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 24,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 13001,
    "char_end": 13271,
    "char_count": 270,
    "text": "PAGE 7 OF 25\nof Rs 0.07/kWh (Seven Paisa per kWh). However, in case of early full\ncommissioning of the Project(s) prior to SCD, Buying Entity may purchase the\npower at the Applicable tariff as per the PPA, plus SECI’s Trading Margin of Rs\n0.07/kWh (Seven Paisa per kWh).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0025",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 25,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 13273,
    "char_end": 13954,
    "char_count": 681,
    "text": "Article 2.  BILLING AND PAYMENT\n2.1\nGeneral\nFrom the commencement of supply of power by SECI, the Buying Entity shall pay\nto SECI the monthly Tariff Payments, on or before the Due Date, in accordance with\nTariff as specified in Article 1. All Tariff Payments by the Buying Entity shall be in\nIndian Rupees.\nSECI shall issue to the Buying Entity a signed Monthly Bill on the first business day\nof the month prepared based on provisional solar energy of the preceding month\n(except for first month which shall be computed based on designed CUF and\ncapacity of project) and shall also include the following:\ni)\nAdjustments bill against the Provisional Bills based on applicable energy",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0026",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 26,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 13956,
    "char_end": 14674,
    "char_count": 718,
    "text": "account/JMR for the power supplied in the preceding months\nii)\nLate Payment Surcharge if any\niii)\nTaxes, duties Levies etc. as applicable\n2.2.\nPayment of Monthly Bills\n2.2.1\nThe Buying Entity shall pay the amount payable under the Monthly Bill on or before\nthe Due Date i.e. within 30 days of presentation of bill within official hours, to such\naccount of SECI, as shall have been previously notified to the Buying Entity in\naccordance with Article 2.2.2 below.\n2.2.2.   SECI shall open a bank account at New Delhi (“SECI’s Designated Account\") for\nall Tariff Payments to be made by the Buying Entity to SECI, and notify the Buying\nEntity of the details of such account at least ninety (90) Days before the dispatch of",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0027",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 27,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 14676,
    "char_end": 14851,
    "char_count": 175,
    "text": "PAGE 8 OF 25\nthe first Monthly Bill. The Buying Entity shall also designate a bank account at\n_________. The Buying Entity shall inform SECI the details of such account ninety",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0028",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 28,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 14852,
    "char_end": 16467,
    "char_count": 1615,
    "text": "(90) Days before the dispatch of the first Monthly Bill. SECI and the Buying Entity\nshall instruct their respective bankers to make all payments under this Agreement to\nthe Buying Entity’ Designated Account or SECI’s Designated Account, as the case\nmay be, and shall notify either Party of such instructions on the same day.\n2.3\nLate Payment Surcharge\n In In the event of payment of a Monthly Bill by the Buying Entity beyond 30 days\nafter the Due Date, a Late Payment Surcharge (LPS) shall be payable by the Buying\nEntity to SECI on the outstanding payment, at the base rate of Late Payment\nSurcharge applicable for the period for the first month of default. “Base rate of Late\nPayment Surcharge\" means the marginal cost of funds based lending rate for one\nyear of the State Bank of India, as applicable on the 1st April of the financial year in\nwhich the period lies, plus five percent and in the absence of marginal cost of funds\nbased lending rate, any other arrangement that substitutes it, which the Central\nGovernment may, by notification, in the Official Gazette, specify.\nThe Late Payment Surcharge shall be claimed by SECI through the Supplementary\nBill. Late Payment Surcharge shall be payable on the outstanding payment beyond\n30 days after the Due Date at the base rate of Late Payment Surcharge applicable for\nthe period for the first month of default. The rate of Late Payment Surcharge for the\nsuccessive months of default shall increase by 0.5 percent (50 bps) for every month\nof delay provided that the Late Payment Surcharge shall not be more than 3 percent\nhigher than the base rate at any time:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0029",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 29,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 16468,
    "char_end": 16792,
    "char_count": 324,
    "text": "(a) Provided that, if a distribution licensee has any payment including Late Payment\nSurcharge outstanding against a bill after the expiry of seven months beyond 30 days\nafter the Due Date of the bill, it shall be debarred from procuring power from a\npower exchange or grant of short term open access till such bill is paid.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
