    "char_end": 38839,
    "char_count": 810,
    "text": "The Generation Compensation as calculated above will be limited to the extent of\nshortfall in annual generation corresponding to the maximum CUF permitted as per\nArticle 2.11.3 and the same will be settled on annual basis.\nThe SPD shall not be eligible for any compensation in case the Backdown is on\naccount of events like consideration of grid security or safety of any equipment or\npersonnel or other such conditions. The Generation Compensation shall be paid as\npart of the energy bill for the successive month after receipt of Energy Accounts\n(REA)/SEA/JMR. No Trading Margin shall be applicable on the Generation\nCompensation as provided in Article 2.13.3 only.\n            It is hereby clarified that for the purpose of Article 2.13 “generation” shall mean\nenergy as applicable based on Energy Accounts.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0055",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 55,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 38841,
    "char_end": 38949,
    "char_count": 108,
    "text": "Duration of Backdown\nProvision for Generation Compensation\nHours of Backdown during a\nmonthly billing cycle.",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0056",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 56,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 38951,
    "char_end": 39230,
    "char_count": 279,
    "text": "Generation Compensation = 100% of\n[(Average Generation per hour during the\nmonth) X (number of backdown hours\nduring the month)] X PPA tariff\n Where, Average Generation per hour during\nthe month (kWh) = Total generation in the\nmonth (kWh) ÷ Total hours of generation in\nthe month",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0057",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 57,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 39232,
    "char_end": 40411,
    "char_count": 1179,
    "text": "PAGE 20 OF 25\nArticle 3: EVENTS OF DEFAULT AND TERMINATION\n3.1       Buying Entity Event of Default\n3.1.1 The occurrence and continuation of any of the following events, unless any such event\noccurs as a result of a Force Majeure Event, shall constitute a Buying Entity Event\nof Default:\n(i)\nAny amount subject to Article remains outstanding beyond a period of ninety\n(90) days after the Due Date and SECI is unable to recover the amount\noutstanding from the Buying Entity through the Letter of Credit, Payment\nSecurity Fund and; or\n(ii)\nThe Buying Entity fails to evacuate power from the Delivery Points for a\ncontinuous period of one year.\n(iii)\nif (a) the Buying Entity becomes voluntarily or involuntarily the subject of\nany bankruptcy or insolvency or winding up proceedings and such\nproceedings remain uncontested for a period of thirty (30) days, or (b) any\nwinding up or bankruptcy or insolvency order is passed against the Buying\nEntity, or (c) the Buying Entity goes into liquidation or dissolution or has a\nreceiver or any similar officer appointed over all or substantially all of its\nassets or official liquidator is appointed to manage its affairs, pursuant to\nLaw,",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0058",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 58,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 40413,
    "char_end": 40989,
    "char_count": 576,
    "text": "Provided that a dissolution or liquidation of the Buying Entity will not be a\nBuying Entity Event of Default if such dissolution or liquidation is for the\npurpose of a merger, consolidation or reorganization and where the resulting\ncompany retains creditworthiness similar to the Buying Entity and expressly\nassumes all obligations of the Buying Entity under this Agreement and is in a\nposition to perform them; or\n(iv)\nthe Buying Entity repudiates this Agreement and does not rectify such\nbreach within a period of thirty (30) days from a notice from SECI  in this\nregard; or",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0059",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 59,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 40991,
    "char_end": 42777,
    "char_count": 1786,
    "text": "PAGE 21 OF 25\n(v)\nexcept where due to any Buying Entity’s failure to comply with its material\nobligations, the Buying Entity is in breach of any of its material obligations\npursuant to this Agreement, and such material breach is not rectified by the\nBuying Entity within thirty (30) days of receipt of first notice in this regard\ngiven by SECI.\n(vi)\nOccurrence of any other event which is specified in this Agreement to be a\nmaterial breach/ default of the Buying Entity.\n3.2      Procedure for cases of Buying Entity Event of Default\n3.2.1  Upon the occurrence and continuation of any Buying Entity Event of Default under\nArticle 3.1, SECI shall have the right to deliver to the Buying Entity a notice, stating\nits intention to terminate this Agreement (SECI Preliminary Default Notice), which\nshall specify in reasonable detail, the circumstances giving rise to the issue of such\nnotice.\n3.2.2  Following the issue of SECI Preliminary Default Notice, the Consultation Period of\nsixty (60) days or such longer period as the Parties may agree, shall apply and it\nshall be the responsibility of the Parties to discuss as to what steps shall have to be\ntaken with a view to mitigate the consequences of the relevant Event of Default\nhaving regard to all the circumstances.\n3.2.3  During the Consultation Period, the Parties shall, save as otherwise provided in this\nAgreement, continue to perform their respective obligations under this Agreement.\n3.2.4  Within a period of seven (7) days following the expiry of the Consultation Period\nunless the Parties shall have otherwise agreed to the contrary or the Event of Default\ngiving rise to the Consultation Period shall have ceased to exist or shall have been\nremedied, the SECI may terminate this Agreement by giving a written Termination",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0060",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 60,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 42778,
    "char_end": 42986,
    "char_count": 208,
    "text": "Notice of thirty (30) days to the Buying Entity.\n3.2.5  Subject to the occurrence and continuation of default by as contained under Article\n3.1 and before expiry of time period of 30 days as per Clause 3.2.4,",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0061",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 61,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 42988,
    "char_end": 43194,
    "char_count": 206,
    "text": "3.2.6  Subject to the prior consent of the SECI, the Buying Entity shall novate its part of\nthe PSA to any third party, including its Affiliates within the period of 210 days\nbeyond the period as per 3.2.4,",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0062",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 62,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 43196,
    "char_end": 44398,
    "char_count": 1202,
    "text": "PAGE 22 OF 25\n3.2.7   In the event the aforesaid novation is not acceptable to SECI, or if no offer of\nnovation is made by the defaulting Buying Entity, then SECI on expiry of 30 days as\nprovided in article 3.2.4 may terminate the PSA and at its discretion require the\ndefaulting Buying Entity to either.\n(i) takeover the Project assets by making a payment of the termination\ncompensation equivalent to the amount of the debt due and the 110% (one\nhundred and ten per cent) of the adjusted equity to SPD less Insurance Cover, if\nany as per PPA, or\n(ii)  pay to the SPD, damages, amount equivalent to the last 6 (six) months average\nbilling, or balance PPA period whichever is less, of charges for its contracted\ncapacity, with the Project assets being retained by the SPD.\n3.3 Termination due to Force Majeure\nIf the Force Majeure Event or its effects continue to be present beyond a period of\ntwelve (12) months; either Party shall have the right to cause termination of the\nAgreement. In such an event this Agreement shall terminate on the date of such\nTermination Notice without any further liability to either Party from the date of such\ntermination.\n3.4.     Termination of back to back agreements",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0063",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 63,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 44400,
    "char_end": 45161,
    "char_count": 761,
    "text": "In case of termination of SECI-SPD PPA, this Agreement shall automatically\nterminate, Provided that in case of such termination as identified in this Article any\npending monetary liabilities of either Party shall survive on the termination of this\nAgreement. In the event of termination of PPA/PSA, any damages or charges\npayable to the STU/CTU, for the connectivity of the plant, shall be borne by the\nentity due to whose failure, the termination was triggered.\n ARTICLE 4: MISCELLANEOUS PROVISIONS\n4.1\nAmendment\n4.1.1  This Agreement may only be amended or supplemented by a written agreement\nbetween the Parties, with the approval of the Appropriate Commission, if necessary.\nSubject to the provisions of the RfS Document and keep this Agreement as principle",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0064",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 64,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 45163,
    "char_end": 45263,
    "char_count": 100,
    "text": "PAGE 23 OF 25\nAgreement, both Parties may execute further Agreement on similar terms and\nconditions.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0065",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 65,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 45265,
    "char_end": 45545,
    "char_count": 280,
    "text": "4.2\nThird Party Beneficiaries\n4.2.1  This Agreement is solely for the benefit of the Parties, SPD and their respective\nsuccessors and permitted assigns and shall not be construed as creating any duty,\nstandard of care or any liability to, any person not a party to this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0066",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 66,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 45547,
    "char_end": 46705,
    "char_count": 1158,
    "text": "4.3\nWaiver\n4.3.1  No waiver by either Party of any default or breach by the other Party in the\nperformance of any of the provisions of this Agreement shall be effective unless\nin writing duly executed by an authorized representative of such Party:\n4.3.2 Neither the failure by either Party to insist on any occasion upon the performance of\nthe terms, conditions and provisions of this Agreement nor time or other indulgence\ngranted by one Party to the other Parties shall act as a waiver of such breach or\nacceptance of any variation or the relinquishment of any such right or any other right\nunder this Agreement, which shall remain in full force and effect.\n4.4\nConfidentiality\n4.4.1  The Parties undertake to hold in confidence this Agreement and not to disclose the\nterms and conditions of the transaction contemplated hereby to third parties, except:\na)\nto their professional advisors;\nb)\nto their officers, contractors, employees, agents or representatives, financiers,\nwho need to have access to such information for the proper performance of\ntheir activities; or\nc)\ndisclosures required under Law without the prior written consent of the other\nParty.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC073-0067",
    "doc_id": "DOC-073",
    "paragraph_index": 67,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 46707,
    "char_end": 47144,
    "char_count": 437,
    "text": "4.5\nSeverability\n4.5.1  The invalidity or unenforceability, for any reason, of any part of this Agreement\nshall not prejudice or affect the validity or enforceability of the remainder of this\nAgreement, unless the part held invalid or unenforceable is fundamental to this\nAgreement.\n4.6 Notices\n4.6.1 All notices or other communications which are required to be given under this\nAgreement shall be in writing and in the English language.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
