    "text": "………………. [Insert name of the Solar Power Developer], a Company incorporated under\nthe Companies Act 1956 or Companies Act 2013, having its registered office at………….\n[Insert address of the registered office of Solar Power Developer] (hereinafter  referred to as\n“Solar Power Developer or SPD”, which expression shall, unless repugnant to the context or\nmeaning thereof, be deemed to include its successors and permitted assigns) as a Party of the\nFirst Part;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0010",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 10,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 798,
    "char_end": 801,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "And",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0011",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 11,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 803,
    "char_end": 1186,
    "char_count": 383,
    "text": "NTPC Limited, a company incorporated under the Companies Act 1956, having its registered\noffice at NTPC Bhawan, Scope Complex, 7, Institutional Area Lodhi Road New Delhi-110003\n(hereinafter referred to as “NTPC” or “Procurer” which expression shall, unless repugnant to\nthe context or meaning thereof, be deemed to include its successors and assignees) as a Party of\nthe Second Part;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0012",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 12,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 1188,
    "char_end": 1287,
    "char_count": 99,
    "text": "The SPD and NTPC are individually referred to as ‘Party’ and collectively referred to as\n‘Parties’.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0013",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 13,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 1289,
    "char_end": 1297,
    "char_count": 8,
    "text": "WHEREAS:",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0014",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 14,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 1299,
    "char_end": 1688,
    "char_count": 389,
    "text": "A.\nMinistry of Power, Government of India vide its Gazette Notification dated 27.08.2022\nhas notified the Guidelines for Tariff Based Competitive Bidding Process for\nProcurement of Power from Grid Connected RE Power Projects for utilization under\nscheme for flexibility in Generation and Scheduling of Thermal/ Hydro Power Stations\nthrough bundling with Renewable Energy and Storage Power.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0015",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 15,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 1690,
    "char_end": 2102,
    "char_count": 412,
    "text": "B.\nNTPC has appointed REC Power Development and Consultancy Limited (RECPDCL)\nas Bid Process Coordinator (BPC) for selection of solar power developers for setting up\nof 1250 MW ISTS-connected Solar PV Power projects in India under tariff-based\ncompetitive bidding under scheme for flexibility in Generation and Scheduling of\nThermal/ Hydro Power Stations through bundling with Renewable Energy and Storage\nPower.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0016",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 16,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 2104,
    "char_end": 2420,
    "char_count": 316,
    "text": "C.\nRECPDCL had initiated a Tariff Based Competitive Bid Process for procurement of\n1250 MW of the power generated from the ISTS connected Solar Power Project on the\nterms and conditions contained in the Request for Selection (herein after referred to as\n‘RFS’\nissued\nby\nRECPDCL\nvide\nRfS\nNo…………………………………….\ndated…………….",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0017",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 17,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 2422,
    "char_end": 2423,
    "char_count": 1,
    "text": "3",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0018",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 18,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 2425,
    "char_end": 2841,
    "char_count": 416,
    "text": "D.\nRECPDCL has issued the letter of award No……………. dated\non behalf of NTPC\nin favour of the  [Insert name of the Bidding Company] for development and\nestablishment   of the ……………MW   Solar Power Project as per the terms and\nconditions contained in the RfS and Power Purchase Agreement (PPA) circulated at the\ntime of the bidding and other bidding documents as well as the conditions contained in\nthe letter of award.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0019",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 19,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 2843,
    "char_end": 3294,
    "char_count": 451,
    "text": "E.\n[Insert Name of the Bidding Company/ Consortium] has been selected in the\ncompetitive bidding process {in case Bidding Company is executing the Project through\nSPV}, has constituted a Special Purpose Vehicle ………… [Insert Name of the SPV]\n(hereinafter referred to as ‘SPD’), for development, generation and supply of electricity\nfrom the ……MW Solar Power Project to be established by SPD anywhere in India and\nfor supply of such electricity to NTPC.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0020",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 20,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 3296,
    "char_end": 3600,
    "char_count": 304,
    "text": "F.\nNTPC has agreed to purchase such Solar Power from the SPD under Ministry of Power\n(MoP), Govt. of India scheme for flexibility in Generation and Scheduling of Thermal/\nHydro Power Stations through bundling with Renewable Energy and Storage Power or\nshall be sold by NTPC to third party/power exchange.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0021",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 21,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 3602,
    "char_end": 3951,
    "char_count": 349,
    "text": "G.\nIn terms of the RfS and the Bidding Documents, the SPD has furnished the Performance\nBank Guarantee (PBG)/ Payment on Order Instrument (POI) in the sum of Rs……….in\nfavour of NTPC as per the format provided as a part of the Bidding Documents and a\ncopy of the Bank Guarantee/ Payment on Order Instrument is also attached along with\nthis Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0022",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 22,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 3953,
    "char_end": 4219,
    "char_count": 266,
    "text": "H.\nThe SPD has fulfilled the terms of the bidding and the terms of the Letter of Award for\nsigning this Power Purchase Agreement as a definitive agreement for establishing the\nSolar Power Project of……………. MW for generation and sale of electricity by the SPD\nto NTPC;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0023",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 23,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 4221,
    "char_end": 4521,
    "char_count": 300,
    "text": "I.\nThe parties have agreed to execute this Power Purchase Agreement in terms of the\nprovisions of the RfS, the bidding documents and the Letter of Award in regard to the\nterms and conditions for establishment of the Solar Power Project and for generation and\nsupply of electricity by the SPD to NTPC.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0024",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 24,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 3,
    "char_start": 4523,
    "char_end": 4740,
    "char_count": 217,
    "text": "J.\nThe solar power shall be used for replacement of thermal energy of various thermal\npower stations. The tentative exhaustive but not limited, list of stations to be used for\nreplacement of thermal power is as under:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0025",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 25,
    "page_start": 3,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 4742,
    "char_end": 5116,
    "char_count": 374,
    "text": "Sl. No.\nStation\n1\nBarh-II\n2\nBongaigaon\n\n4\n3\nDadri-I\n4\nDadri-II\n5\nFarakka-I & II\n6\nFarakka-III\n7\nGadarwara\n8\nKudgi\n9\nMouda-I\n10\nMouda-II\n11\nRamagundam-I\n12\nRamagundam-III\n13\nSimhadri-I\n14\nSimhadri-II\n15\nSolapur\n16\nTanda-II\n17\nUnchahar-I\n18\nUnchahar-II\n19\nUnchahar-III\n20\nUnchahar-IV\n21\nBarauni TPS\n22\nLara,\n23\nMuzaffarpur\n24\nNabinagar\n25\nIndira Gandhi STPP,\n26\nMeja\n27\nVallur",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0026",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 26,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 5118,
    "char_end": 5290,
    "char_count": 172,
    "text": "Now therefore, in consideration of the premises and mutual agreements, covenants and\nconditions set forth herein, it is hereby agreed by and between the Parties as follows:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0027",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 27,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 5292,
    "char_end": 5293,
    "char_count": 1,
    "text": "5",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0028",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 28,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 5295,
    "char_end": 5697,
    "char_count": 402,
    "text": "ARTICLE 1\n\nDEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION\n\n1.1\nDefinitions\n\nThe terms used in this Agreement, unless as defined below or repugnant to the context, shall\nhave the same meaning as assigned to them by the Electricity Act, 2003 and the rules or\nregulations framed there under, including those issued / framed by the Appropriate\nCommission (as defined hereunder), as amended or re-enacted from time to time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0029",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 29,
    "page_start": 5,
    "page_end": 5,
    "char_start": 5699,
    "char_end": 7471,
    "char_count": 1772,
    "text": "“Act” or\n“Electricity\nAct, 2003”\nshall mean the Electricity Act, 2003 and shall include any\nmodifications, amendments and substitution from time to time;\n“Adjusted Equity”\nshall mean the Equity funded in Indian Rupees and adjusted on the\nfirst day of the current month (the “Reference Date”), in the manner\nset forth below, to reflect the change in its value on account of\ndepreciation and variations in Wholesale Price Index (WPI), and\nfor any Reference Date occurring between the first day of the month\nof Appointed Date (the date of achievement of Financial Closure)\nand the Reference Date;\ni. On or before Commercial Operation Date (COD), the\nAdjusted Equity shall be a sum equal to the Equity funded in\nIndian Rupees and expended on the Project, revised to the extent\nof one half of the variation in WPI occurring between the first\nday of the month of Appointed Date and Reference Date;\nii. An amount equal to the Adjusted Equity as on COD shall be\ndeemed to be the base (the “Base Adjusted Equity”);\niii. After COD, the Adjusted Equity hereunder shall be a sum equal\nto the Base Adjusted Equity, reduced by 0.333% (zero point\nthree three three percent) thereof at the commencement of each\nmonth following the COD [reduction of 1% (one percent) per\nquarter of a year] and the amount so arrived at shall be revised\nto the extent of variation in WPI occurring between the COD\nand the Reference Date;\nFor the avoidance of doubt, the Adjusted Equity shall, in the event of\ntermination, be computed as on the Reference Date immediately\npreceding the Transfer Date; provided that no reduction in the\nAdjusted Equity shall be made for a period equal to the duration, if\nany, for which the PPA period is extended, but the revision on\naccount of WPI shall continue to be made.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0030",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 30,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 6,
    "char_start": 7473,
    "char_end": 8447,
    "char_count": 974,
    "text": "6\n“Agreement” or\n\"Power Purchase\nAgreement\" or\n\"PPA\"\nshall mean this Power Purchase Agreement including its recitals and\nSchedules, amended or modified from time to time in accordance\nwith the terms hereof;\n\"Appropriate\nCommission\"\nUnless otherwise stated, Appropriate Commission shall mean\nCentral Electricity Regulatory Commission;\n\"Bill Dispute\nNotice\"\nshall mean the notice issued by a Party raising a Dispute regarding a\nMonthly Bill or a Supplementary Bill issued by the other Party;\n“Business Day”\nshall mean with respect to SPD and NTPC, a day other than Sunday\nor a statutory holiday, on which the banks remain open for business\nin Delhi;\n“Capacity\nUtilization Factor”\nor “CUF”\nshall have the same meaning as provided in CERC (Terms and\nConditions for Tariff determination from Renewable Energy\nSources) Regulations, 2009 as amended from time to time; However,\nfor avoidance of any doubt, it is clarified that the CUF shall be\ncalculated on the Contracted Capacity;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0031",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 31,
    "page_start": 6,
    "page_end": 6,
    "char_start": 8449,
    "char_end": 9919,
    "char_count": 1470,
    "text": "In any Contract Year, if ‘X’ MWh of energy has been metered out at\nthe Delivery Point for ‘Y’ MW Project capacity, CUF= (X MWh/(Y\nMW*8766)) X100%;\n“CERC”\nshall mean the Central Electricity Regulatory Commission of India,\nconstituted under sub – section (1) of Section 76 of the Electricity\nAct, 2003, or its successors;\n“CTU” or “Central\nTransmission\nUtility”\nshall mean the government company notified by the Central\nGovernment under Sub-Section (1) of Section 38 of the Electricity\nAct, 2003.\n“Change in Law”\nshall have the meaning ascribed thereto in Article 12 of this\nAgreement;\n“Commissioning”\nThe Project will be considered as commissioned if all equipment as\nper rated Project Capacity has been installed and energy has flown\ninto grid, in line with the Commissioning procedures defined in the\nPPA.\n“Commercial\nOperation Date\n(COD)”\nshall mean the date on which the commissioning certificate is issued\nupon successful commissioning (as per provisions of this\nAgreement) of the project or the last part capacity; of the Project as\nthe case may be;\n“Competent Court\nof Law”\nshall mean any court or tribunal or any similar judicial or quasi-\njudicial body in India that has jurisdiction to adjudicate upon issues\nrelating to this Agreement;\n“Consents,\nClearances and\nPermits”\nshall mean all authorizations, licenses, approvals, registrations,\npermits, waivers, privileges, acknowledgements, agreements, or\nconcessions required to be obtained from or provided by any",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0032",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 32,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 9921,
    "char_end": 10647,
    "char_count": 726,
    "text": "7\nconcerned authority for the purpose of setting up of the generation\nfacilities and/ or supply of power;\n“Consultation  Period”\nshall mean the period of ninety (90) days or such other longer period\nas the Parties may agree, commencing from the date of issuance of\nan SPD Preliminary Default Notice or NTPC Preliminary Default\nNotice as provided in Article 13 of this Agreement, for consultation\nbetween the Parties to mitigate the consequence of the relevant event\nhaving regard to all the circumstances;\n“Contract Year”\nshall mean the period beginning from the Effective Date and ending\non the immediately succeeding March 31 and thereafter each period\nof 12 months beginning on April 1 and ending on March 31 provided\nthat:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0033",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 33,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 10649,
    "char_end": 11056,
    "char_count": 407,
    "text": "(i) in the financial year in which the Scheduled Commissioning Date\nwould occur, the Contract Year shall end on the date immediately\nbefore the Scheduled Commissioning Date and a new Contract\nYear shall commence once again from the Scheduled\nCommissioning Date and end on the immediately succeeding\nMarch 31, and thereafter each period of twelve (12) months\ncommencing on April 1 and ending on March 31, and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0034",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 34,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 11058,
    "char_end": 12297,
    "char_count": 1239,
    "text": "(ii) provided further that the last Contract Year of this Agreement\nshall end on the last day of the Term of this Agreement\n\"Contracted\nCapacity\"\nshall mean …… [Insert the capacity] MW, which is the AC capacity\ncontracted with NTPC for supply by the SPD to NTPC at the\nDelivery Point from the Solar Power Project. It shall be equal to the\nProject Capacity as defined.\n“Day”\nshall mean a day, if not a Business Day, the immediately succeeding\nBusiness Day.\n“Debt Due”\nshall mean the aggregate of the following sums expressed in Indian\nRupees outstanding on the Transfer Date:\ni. The principal amount of the debt provided by the Senior\nLenders under the Financing Agreements for financing the Total\nProject Cost (the ‘Principal’) but excluding any part of the\nprincipal that had fallen due for repayment 2 (two) years prior to\nthe Transfer Date;\nii. All accrued interest, financing fees and charges payable under\nthe Financing Agreements on, or in respect of, the debt referred\nto in sub- clause (i) above until the Transfer Date but excluding:\n(i) any interest, fees or charges that had fallen due one year prior\nto the Transfer Date, (ii) any penal interest or charges payable\nunder the Financing Agreements to any Senior Lender, (iii) any",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0035",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 35,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 12299,
    "char_end": 12564,
    "char_count": 265,
    "text": "8\npre-payment charges in relation to accelerated repayment of\ndebt except where such charges\nhave arisen due to Utility Default, and (iv) any Subordinated\nDebt which is included in the Financial Package and disbursed\nby lenders for financing the Total Project Cost.",
