  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0060",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 60,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 32079,
    "char_end": 32388,
    "char_count": 309,
    "text": "2.2.2 The SPD is free to operate their plants beyond the Expiry Date if other conditions like\nland lease / Right to Use of Land (as applicable), permits, approvals and clearances\netc. allow. In such case unless otherwise agreed by the NTPC, NTPC shall not be\nobligated to procure power beyond the Expiry Date.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0061",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 61,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 32390,
    "char_end": 32562,
    "char_count": 172,
    "text": "2.3\nEarly Termination\n\n2.3.1\nThis Agreement shall terminate before the Expiry Date if either NTPC or SPD\nterminates the Agreement, pursuant to Article 13 of this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0062",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 62,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 32564,
    "char_end": 33446,
    "char_count": 882,
    "text": "2.4\nSurvival\n2.4.1\nThe expiry or termination of this Agreement shall not affect any accrued rights,\nobligations and liabilities of the Parties under this Agreement, including the right to\nreceive penalty as per the terms of this Agreement, nor shall it affect the survival of\nany continuing obligations for which this Agreement provides, either expressly or by\nnecessary implication, which are to survive after the Expiry Date or termination\nincluding those under Article 11 (Force Majeure), Article 13 (Events of Default and\nTermination), Article 14 (Liability and Indemnification), Article 16 (Governing  Law\nand Dispute Resolution), Article 17 (Miscellaneous Provisions), and other Articles and\nSchedules of this Agreement which expressly or by their nature survive the Term or\ntermination of this Agreement shall continue and survive any expiry or termination of\nthis Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0063",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 63,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 33448,
    "char_end": 33536,
    "char_count": 88,
    "text": "17\nARTICLE 3\nCONDITIONS SUBSEQUENT\n\n3.1\nSatisfaction of conditions subsequent by the SPD",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0064",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 64,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 33538,
    "char_end": 33897,
    "char_count": 359,
    "text": "The SPD agrees and undertakes to duly perform and complete all of the following activities\nincluding   Financial   Closure   at    the    SPD’s    own    cost   and    risk by\n[Enter\nthe\ndate as on 12 Months after the Effective Date], unless such completion is affected by any\nForce Majeure event, or for the activities specifically waived in writing by NTPC:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0065",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 65,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 33899,
    "char_end": 34029,
    "char_count": 130,
    "text": "The SPD shall make Project financing arrangements its Projects(s) and shall provide necessary\ncertificates to NTPC in this regard;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0066",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 66,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 34031,
    "char_end": 34192,
    "char_count": 161,
    "text": "The SPD shall submit to NTPC the relevant documents as stated above, complying with the\nConditions Subsequent, within twelve (12) months from the Effective Date.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0067",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 67,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 34194,
    "char_end": 34275,
    "char_count": 81,
    "text": "3.2\nConsequences of non-fulfilment of conditions subsequent and financial closure",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0068",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 68,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 34277,
    "char_end": 35004,
    "char_count": 727,
    "text": "3.2.1 In case of a failure on the part of SPD to fulfill the condition subsequent and submit\nthe documents as provided in Article 3.1, NTPC shall be entitled to encash the\nPerformance Bank Guarantee/Payment on Order Instrument submitted by the SPD,\nterminate this Agreement and remove the Project from the list of the selected Projects\nby giving a notice to the SPD in writing of at least seven (7) days, unless the delay\n(subject to the conditions that SPD has made / is making all possible efforts) is solely\non account of Force Majeure. Unless extended as per provisions of Article 3.2.2 (i) of\nthis Agreement in writing, the termination of the Agreement shall take effect upon the\nexpiry of the 7th day of the above Notice.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0069",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 69,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 35006,
    "char_end": 35995,
    "char_count": 989,
    "text": "3.2.2 (i) An extension, without any impact on the Scheduled Commissioning Date, can\nhowever be considered, on the sole request of SPD, on payment of Rs. 1000/- per day\nper MW to NTPC. Such extension charges are required to be paid to NTPC in\nadvance, for the period of extension required. In case of any delay in depositing this\nextension charge, SPD shall pay an interest on this extension charge for the days\nlapsed beyond due date of Financial Closure @ SBI-MCLR (1Year). In case such\ndelay in making payment of the extension charges to NTPC is more than 7 days, the\ntermination of the Agreement shall take effect upon the expiry of such 7th day. In case\nof the SPD meeting the requirements of conditions subsequent and financial closure\nbefore the last date of such proposed delay period, the excess amount deposited by the\nSPD shall be returned by NTPC without interest. This extension will not have any\nimpact on the Scheduled Commissioning Date. Any extension charges paid so by the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0070",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 70,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 35997,
    "char_end": 36409,
    "char_count": 412,
    "text": "18\nSPD, shall be returned to the SPD without any interest on achievement of successful\ncommissioning within the Scheduled Commissioning Date, on pro-rata basis, based on\nthe project capacity commissioned as on Scheduled Commissioned Date. However, in\ncase the SPD fails to commission the Contract Capacity by Scheduled Commissioning\nDate, the extension charges deposited by the SPD shall not be refunded by NTPC.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0071",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 71,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 36411,
    "char_end": 37083,
    "char_count": 672,
    "text": "3.2.3\nFor the avoidance of doubt, it is clarified that this Article shall survive the termination\nof this Agreement.\n3.2.4\nIn case of inability of the SPD to fulfil the conditions specified in Article 3.1 due to\nany Force Majeure event, the time period for fulfilment of the Conditions Subsequent\nand Financial Closure as mentioned in Article 3.1, shall be extended for the period of\nsuch Force Majeure event.\n3.2.5\nProvided that due to the provisions of this Article 3.2.4, any increase in the time\nperiod for completion of conditions subsequent and financial closure mentioned under\nArticle 3.2, shall also lead to an equal extension in the Scheduled Commissioning\nDate.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0072",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 72,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 37085,
    "char_end": 38179,
    "char_count": 1094,
    "text": "3.3\nPerformance Bank Guarantee/ Payment on Order Instrument\n\n3.3.1\nThe Performance Bank Guarantee (PBG)/ Payment on Order Instrument (POI) having\nvalidity from the date of submission of PBG/ POI until 6 months after the SCD\nsubmitted for a value of Rs........... (INR 8 Lakh/MW) to be furnished under this\nAgreement shall be for guaranteeing the commencement of the supply of power up to\nthe Contracted Capacity within the time specified in this Agreement.\n3.3.2\nThe failure on the part of the SPD to furnish and maintain the Performance Bank\nGuarantee/ POI shall be a material breach of the term of this Agreement on the part of\nthe SPD.\n3.3.3\nIf the SPD fails to commence supply of power from the Scheduled Commissioning\nDate specified in this Agreement or any further extension thereof granted by NTPC,\nsubject to conditions mentioned in Article 4.5, NTPC shall encash the Performance\nBank Guarantee/ POI equivalent to the amount calculated as per liquidated damage\napplicable under Article 4.6 as on the date of encashment without prejudice to the other rights\nof NTPC under this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0073",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 73,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 38181,
    "char_end": 38734,
    "char_count": 553,
    "text": "3.4\nReturn of Performance Bank Guarantee/ Payment on Order Instrument\n\n3.4.1\nSubject to Article 3.3, NTPC shall return / release the Performance Bank Guarantee/\nPayment on Order Instrument immediately after the successful Commissioning of the\nProject after taking into account any liquidated damages / penalties due to delays in\ncommissioning as per provisions stipulated in this Agreement.\n3.4.2\nThe return / release of the Performance Bank Guarantee/ Payment on Order\nInstrument shall be without prejudice to other rights of NTPC under this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0074",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 74,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 38736,
    "char_end": 38813,
    "char_count": 77,
    "text": "19\nARTICLE 4\nCONSTRUCTION & DEVELOPMENT OF THE PROJECT\n\n4.1\nSPD’s Obligations",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0075",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 75,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 38815,
    "char_end": 40019,
    "char_count": 1204,
    "text": "4.1.1\nThe SPD undertakes to be responsible, at SPD’s own cost and risk, for the following:\na)\nThe SPD shall be solely responsible and make arrangements for Land & associated\ninfrastructure for development of the Project and for Connectivity with the ISTS System\nfor confirming the evacuation of power by the Scheduled Commissioning date and all\nclearances related thereto.\nb) SPD shall be required to submit documents as mentioned below prior to commissioning\nof the Project:\n• Lease Agreement to establish possession/right to use 100% (hundred per cent) of\nthe required land in the name of the SPD for a period not less than the complete\nterm of the PPA, on or before the Scheduled Commissioning Date (SCD).\nWherever leasehold  land is involved, the lease should allow transfer/ mortgage of\nleasehold land lease rights to the lenders or Procurer, in case of default of the\nSPD.”\n•\nNo Objection Certificate (NoC)/Environmental Clearance (if applicable) for the\nProject.\n•\nForest Clearance (if applicable) for the land for the Project.\n•\nApproval for Water from the concerned authority (if applicable) required for the\nProject.\n• A letter from State Transmission Utility (STU)/Central Transmission Utility",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0076",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 76,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 40020,
    "char_end": 41088,
    "char_count": 1068,
    "text": "(CTU) [or solar power park developer, in case of selected site being a solar park]\nconfirming technical feasibility of connectivity of the plant to STU/CTU\nsubstation. If the Project site is located in the same State as the Procurer/End\nProcurer, State Govt. shall endeavor to provide necessary support to facilitate the\nconnectivity of the plant to STU/CTU substation.\nc)\nObtaining all Consents, Clearances and Permits as required and maintaining all\nConsents, Clearances and Permits in full force and effect during the Term of this\nAgreement. NTPC shall have no obligation to recommend to any department/agency or\nthe Govt. for the grant/permission for the Solar Power project. The SPD shall, on his\nown, obtain permissions/ sanctions from Government authorities, if any required for\nestablishing the project. Any steps that may be taken by NTPC in regard to grant of\nsuch consents and permits or any other approval that maybe required to be obtained by\nthe SPD shall only be a voluntary endeavour with no intention of being bound by any\nlegal or binding obligation.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0077",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 77,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 41090,
    "char_end": 42868,
    "char_count": 1778,
    "text": "20\nd) designing, constructing, erecting, commissioning, completing and testing the Power\nProject in accordance with the applicable Law, the Grid Code, the terms and conditions\nof this Agreement and Prudent Utility Practices.\ne)\nthe commencement of supply of power up to the Contracted Capacity to NTPC no later\nthan the Scheduled Commissioning Date and continuance of the supply of power\nthroughout the term of the Agreement;\nf)\nConnecting the Power Project switchyard with the Interconnection Facilities. The SPD\nshall make adequate arrangements to connect the Power Project switchyard with the\nInterconnection Facilities at Interconnection/ Metering.\ng) Owning the Power Project throughout the Term of Agreement free and clear of\nencumbrances, except those expressly permitted under Article 15.\nh) In case of Project being executed through SPVs: The Selected Bidder executing the\nproject, if being a single company, shall ensure that its shareholding in the SPV/ Project\ncompany incorporated for implementing the project and executing the PPA, shall not\nfall below 51% at any time prior to 01 (one) year after the SCD, except with the prior\napproval of NTPC. In the event the selected Bidder is a consortium, then the combined\nshareholding of the consortium members in the SPV/ Project Company executing the\nPPA, shall not fall below 51% at any time prior to 01 (one) year after SCD, except with\nthe prior approval of NTPC. However, in case the Project is being set up by a listed\nCompany, this condition will not be applicable.\nIn case of the selected Bidder itself executing the PPA, it shall ensure that its\npromotors shall not cede control (Control shall mean the ownership, directly or\nindirectly, of more than 50% of the voting shares of such Company or right to appoint",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0078",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 78,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 42869,
    "char_end": 44050,
    "char_count": 1181,
    "text": "majority Directors), till 01 (one) year after the SCD, except with the prior approval of\nNTPC. However, in case the Project is being set up by a listed Company, this condition\nwill not be applicable.\nIn case of companies having multiple promoters (but none of the shareholders having\nmore than 50% of voting rights and paid-up share capital), it shall be considered as a\ncompany under joint control. In such cases, the shareholding pattern in the company as\nsubmitted at the time of bidding, shall be maintained for a period of 01 (one) year after\nSCD.\nAny change in the shareholding after the expiry of 01 year after SCD can be undertaken\nunder intimation to NTPC. Transfer of controlling shareholding of the company\ndeveloping the project within the same group of companies will however be allowed\nafter SCD with the permission of NTPC, subject to the condition that the management\ncontrol remains within the same group of companies.\ni)\nfulfilling all obligations undertaken by the SPD under this Agreement.\nj)\nObtaining Connectivity and executing connectivity agreement as per provision of GNA\nregulation issued by CERC, for evacuation of the Contracted Capacity and maintaining",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0079",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 79,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 44052,
    "char_end": 45273,
    "char_count": 1221,
    "text": "21\nit throughout the term of the Agreement. It is further clarified that the Entities as\nindicated in the Detailed Procedure issued subsequently under the Central Electricity\nRegulatory Commission (Connectivity and General Network Access to the inter-State\nTransmission System) Regulations, 2022, will be responsible for their respective\nobligation as notified in the Detailed Procedure irrespective of the provisions of the RfS\nand PPA.\nk) The SPD shall be responsible to for directly coordinating and dealing with the\ncorresponding Load Dispatch Centers, Regional Power Committees, and other\nauthorities in all respects in regard to declaration of availability, scheduling and\ndispatch of Solar Power and due compliance with deviation and settlement mechanism\nand the applicable Grid code/State/Central Regulations.\nl)\nThe SPD shall fulfil the technical requirements according to criteria mentioned under\nAnnexure II–Technical requirement for Grid Connected Solar PV Power Projects. The\nmodules used in the Project shall be sourced only from the models and manufacturers\nincluded in List-I under the “Approved List of Models and Manufacturers” as\npublished by MNRE and valid as on the date of invoicing of such modules.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0080",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 80,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 45275,
    "char_end": 46466,
    "char_count": 1191,
    "text": "Further, Components used in Solar PV Projects except Photovoltaic Modules shall be\nstrict compliancy with MNRE Order F.No. 283/22/2019-GRID SOLAR, dated 09th\nFebruary, 2021 for public procurement (Preference to Make in India) to provide for\npurchase preference (linked with local content) in respect of Renewable Energy (RE)\nSector and its subsequent amendments and clarifications issued, if any, shall be\napplicable for this RfS.\nm) Further, the Project being implemented under this Agreement shall fulfil the criteria as\nper Central Electricity Authority (Technical Standards for Connectivity to the Grid)\nRegulations, 2007, and subsequent amendments and clarifications thereof,\nn) As part of scheduling of power from the Project, the SPD will be required to punch-in\ntheir respective schedules and subsequent revisions, by themselves, at the interfaces of\nall the RLDCs/ NLDCs concerned for the corridor of power flow, as per the Regulations\nin force/ procedure issued by Power System Operation Corporation Limited\n(POSOCO), under intimation to NTPC. The SPD shall be solely responsible for\ndiscrepancy identification and its rectification to avoid any rejection/less payment of\ninvoices.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0081",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 81,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 46468,
    "char_end": 46941,
    "char_count": 473,
    "text": "4.2\nInformation regarding Interconnection Facilities\n\n4.2.1 The SPD shall be required to obtain all information from the STU/CTU/Concerned\nAuthority with regard to the Interconnection Facilities as is reasonably necessary to\nenable it to design, install and operate all interconnection plant and apparatus on the\nSPD’s side of the Delivery Point to enable delivery of electricity at the Delivery\nPoint. The transmission of power up to the point of interconnection where the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0082",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 82,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 46943,
    "char_end": 48692,
    "char_count": 1749,
    "text": "22\nmetering is done for energy accounting shall be the responsibility of the SPD at his\nown cost.\n4.2.2 Penalties, fines and charges imposed by the CTU/ STU under any statute or\nregulations/guidelines in relation to delay in commissioning of Project shall be\nentirely dealt by the SPD and such amount claim by such agency(ies) shall be\npayable by SPD.\n4.2.3 The responsibility of getting connectivity with the transmission system up to the\nInterconnection Point, will lie with the SPD. The transmission of power up to the\npoint of interconnection where the metering is done for energy accounting shall be\nthe responsibility of the SPD at his own cost. The maintenance of Transmission\nsystem up to the designated point as per the applicable terms and conditions shall\nbe the responsibility of the SPD. All costs and charges including but not limited to\nthe wheeling charges and losses up to and including at the Interconnection Point\nassociated with this arrangement will also be borne by the SPD.\n4.2.4 In case of Pooling substation, losses in the transmission line shall be apportioned\namong the SPDs who share such a Pooling arrangement and duly signed by all\nSPDs, based on their monthly generation.\n4.2.5 The arrangement of connectivity shall be made by the SPD through a dedicated\ntransmission line. The entire cost of transmission including cost of construction of\nline, any other charges, losses etc. from the Project up to the Interconnection Point\nwill be borne by the SPD. In case of non-availability of Grid and Transmission\nSystem during Term of this Agreement, for reasons not attributable to the SPD,\nprovisions of Article 4.10 shall be applicable.\n4.2.6 ISTS charges and losses on transmission of power, including waiver for RE power,",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0083",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 83,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 48693,
    "char_end": 50019,
    "char_count": 1326,
    "text": "shall be applicable as per extant regulations. Government of India, from time to\ntime, issues order for waiver of inter-state transmission system (ISTS) charges and\nlosses on transmission of solar power till a certain date. In case the commissioning\nof the Project gets delayed beyond the applicable date of ISTS waiver, arising out\nof any reasons whatsoever, NTPC shall bear no liability with respect to\ntransmission charges and losses levied, if any.\nIn case the SCD of the Project is before the date till above ISTS waiver is\napplicable, and if the Project is granted extension in the SCD on account of Force\nMajeure, or for delay on the part of the transmission provider in providing the\ntransmission even after having taken the requisite steps in time; or on account of\ndelays on the part of any Government Agency, and the Project is commissioned\nbefore the extended SCD; it will get benefit of waiver of inter-state transmission\ncharges. However, in case the commissioning of the Project gets delayed beyond\nthe applicable date of ISTS waiver/extended SCD as above, due to reasons\nattributable to the SPD, the liability of transmission charges and losses would be to\nthe account of the SPD. In case of any extension in SCD beyond 30.06.2025,\ndecision on such extension requests will be taken by MNRE, in line with the OM",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0084",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 84,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 50021,
    "char_end": 50462,
    "char_count": 441,
    "text": "23\nissued by Ministry of Power vide No. 23/12/2016- R&R dated 30.11.2021, and\nsubsequent amendments/clarifications thereto, read in conjunction with CERC’s\norders and regulations notified in this regard. The provisions of PPA in regard to\nliability of the entities to pay the ISTS charges and losses shall stand modified by\nsuch exemption/waiver provided as per the above Order/Office Memoranda and\nregulations issued by CERC, as applicable.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0085",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 85,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 50464,
    "char_end": 50724,
    "char_count": 260,
    "text": "4.3\nPurchase and sale of Contracted Capacity\nSubject to the terms and conditions of this Agreement, the SPD undertakes to sell to\nNTPC and NTPC undertakes to pay Tariff for all the energy supplied at the Delivery\nPoint corresponding to the Contracted Capacity.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0086",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 86,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 50726,
    "char_end": 52516,
    "char_count": 1790,
    "text": "4.4\nRight to Contracted Capacity & Energy\n4.4.1 The SPD will be allowed to revise the CUF of the Project once within first year after\nCOD of the full project capacity. NTPC, in any Contract Year except for the\nContract Year ending on 31st March immediately after COD of the Project, shall not\nbe obliged to purchase any additional energy from the SPD beyond ..... Million\nkWh\n(MU). Subsequent to commissioning of the Project, if for any Contract Year, except\nfor the Contract Year ending on 31st  March immediately after COD of the Project, it\nis found that the SPD has not been able to supply minimum energy\nof………..Million kWh (MU) till the end of 10 years from the SCD and\n…………..Million kWh (MU) for the rest of the Term of the Agreement, on account\nof reasons solely attributable to the SPD, the noncompliance by SPD shall make the\nSPD liable to pay the compensation to NTPC. The lower limit will, however be\nrelaxable by NTPC to the extent of grid non- availability for evacuation which is\nbeyond the control of the SPD (as certified by the SLDC/RLDC). This compensation\nshall be applied to the amount of shortfall in generation during the Contract Year.\nSuch compensation shall ensure that the NTPC is/are offset for all potential costs\nassociated with low generation and supply of power under the PPA. However, the\nminimum compensation payable to NTPC by the SPD shall be 25% (twenty-five\npercent) of the cost of this shortfall in energy terms, calculated at PPA tariff. This\ncompensation shall not be applicable in events of Force Majeure identified under\nPPA with NTPC affecting supply of Solar Power by SPD.\n4.4.2 In case the availability is more than the maximum CUF specified, the SPD will be\nfree to sell it to any other entity provided first right of refusal will vest with the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0087",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 87,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 52517,
    "char_end": 52805,
    "char_count": 288,
    "text": "NTPC. In case the NTPC purchases the excess generation, the same may be done at\n75% (seventy-five per cent) of the PPA tariff.\n4.5\nExtensions of Time\n4.5.1 In the event that the SPD is prevented from performing its obligations under Article\n4.1 by the Scheduled Commissioning Date due to:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0088",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 88,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 52807,
    "char_end": 52928,
    "char_count": 121,
    "text": "24\na) any NTPC Event of Default; or\nb) Force Majeure Events affecting NTPC, or\nc) Force Majeure Events affecting the SPD,",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0089",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 89,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 52930,
    "char_end": 53639,
    "char_count": 709,
    "text": "the Scheduled Commissioning Date and the Expiry Date shall be deferred for a\nreasonable period but not less than ‘day for day’ basis, to permit the SPD or NTPC\nthrough the use of due diligence, to overcome the effects of the Force Majeure\nEvents affecting the SPD or NTPC, or till such time such Event of Default is\nrectified by NTPC.\n4.5.2 Subsequent to grant of connectivity, in case there is a delay in case of\noperationalization of  General Network Access (GNA) by the CTU and/or there is a\ndelay in readiness of the ISTS substation at the Delivery Point, including readiness\nof the power evacuation and transmission infrastructure of the ISTS network until\nSCD of the Project, and it is established that:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0090",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 90,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 53640,
    "char_end": 53819,
    "char_count": 179,
    "text": "(i) The SPD has complied with the complete application formalities as per RfS,\n(ii) The SPD has adhered to the applicable Procedure in this regard as notified\nby the CERC/CTU, and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0091",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 91,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 53820,
    "char_end": 55390,
    "char_count": 1570,
    "text": "(iii) The delay in operationalization of GNA and/or delay in readiness of the\nISTS substation at the Delivery Point, including readiness of the power\nevacuation and transmission infrastructure of the ISTS network, is a factor\nattributable to the CTU/transmission licensee and is beyond the control of\nthe SPD;\nThe above shall be treated as delays beyond the control of the SPD and SCD for\nsuch Projects shall be revised as the date as on 30 days subsequent to the readiness\nof the Interconnection Point and power evacuation infrastructure and/or\ngrant/operationalization  of GNA. Decision on requisite extension on account of the\nabove factor shall be taken by NTPC.\n4.5.3 In case of extension due to reasons specified in Article 4.5.1(b) and (c), and if such\nForce Majeure Event continues even after a maximum period of 180 days from the\ndate of the Force Majeure Notice, any of the Parties may choose to terminate the\nAgreement as per the provisions of Article 11.3. In case neither party terminates the\nAgreement under this clause, the Agreement shall stand terminated on the expiry of\ntwelve (12) months of the continuation of the Force Majeure event unless the\nparties mutually agree to extend the Agreement for the further period.\n4.5.4 If the Parties have not agreed within thirty (30) days after the affected Party’s\nperformance has ceased to be affected by the relevant circumstance, on the time\nperiod by which the Scheduled Commissioning Date or the Expiry Date should be\ndeferred, any Party may raise the Dispute to be resolved in accordance with Article\n16.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0092",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 92,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 55392,
    "char_end": 56493,
    "char_count": 1101,
    "text": "25\n4.5.5 As a result of such extension on account of Article 4.5.1 or Article 4.5.2, the newly\ndetermined Scheduled Commissioning Date and newly determined Expiry Date\nshall be deemed to be the Scheduled Commissioning Date and the Expiry Date for\nthe purposes of this Agreement.\n4.5.6 Not used.\n4.5.7 Delay in commissioning of the project beyond the scheduled commissioning date\nfor reasons other than those specified in Article 4.5.1 & Article 4.5.2 shall be an\nevent of default on part of the SPD and shall be subject to the consequences\nspecified in the Article 4.6.\n4.6\nLiquidated Damages not amounting to penalty for delay in Commissioning\n4.6.1 The Project shall be fully commissioned within the Scheduled Commissioning Date\nas defined in this Agreement. If the SPD is unable to commission the Project by the\nScheduled Commissioning Date for the reasons other than those specified in Article\n4.5.1 and 4.5.2, the SPD shall pay to NTPC, damages for the delay in such\ncommissioning and making the Contracted Capacity available for dispatch by the\nScheduled Commissioning Date as per the following:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0093",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 93,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 56495,
    "char_end": 57108,
    "char_count": 613,
    "text": "(a) Delay beyond the Scheduled Commissioning Date upto (& including) the\ndate as on 6 months after the Scheduled Commissioning Date, as part of the\nliquidated damages, the total PBG/POI amount for the Project shall be\nencashed on per-day basis and proportionate to the balance capacity not\ncommissioned. For example, in case of a Project of 240 MW capacity, if\ncommissioning of 100 MW capacity is delayed by 18 days beyond the SCD,\nthen the liquidated damages shall be: PBG/POI amount X (100/240) X\n(18/180). For the purpose of calculation of liquidated damages, ‘month’ shall\nbe considered consisting of 30 days.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0094",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 94,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 57110,
    "char_end": 57891,
    "char_count": 781,
    "text": "(b) For avoidance of doubt it is clarified that provisions of Article 4.6.1 will be\napplicable even in cases where no capacity (i.e. 0 MW) is commissioned.\n4.6.2 The maximum time period allowed for commissioning of the full Project Capacity\nwith encashment of Performance Bank Guarantee/ Payment on Order Instrument\nshall be limited to 6 months after the SCD of the Project. In case, the\nCommissioning of the Project is delayed beyond 6 months after the SCD, it shall be\nconsidered as an SPD Event of Default and provisions of Article 13 shall apply and\nthe Contracted Capacity shall stand reduced / amended to the Project Capacity\nCommissioned within 6 months after the SCD and the PPA for the balance\nCapacity will stand terminated and shall be reduced from the project capacity.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0095",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 95,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 57893,
    "char_end": 59079,
    "char_count": 1186,
    "text": "4.7\nAcceptance/Performance Test\n\n26\n4.7.1 Prior to synchronization of the Power Project, the SPD shall be required to get the\nProject certified for the requisite acceptance/performance test as may be laid down\nby Central Electricity Authority or an agency identified by the central government\nto carry out testing and certification for the Solar Power projects.\n4.8\nThird Party Verification\n4.8.1 The SPD shall be further required to provide entry to the site of the Power Project\nfree of all encumbrances at all times during the Term of the Agreement to NTPC\nand a third Party nominated by any Indian Governmental Instrumentality for\ninspection and verification of the works being carried out by the SPD at the site of\nthe Power Project. The SPD shall provide full support to NTPC and/or the third\nparty in this regard.\n4.8.2 The third party may verify the construction works/operation of the Power Project\nbeing carried out by the SPD and if it is found that the construction works/operation\nof the Power Project is not as per the Prudent Utility Practices, it may seek\nclarifications from SPD or require the works to be stopped or to comply with the\ninstructions of such third party.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0096",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 96,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 59081,
    "char_end": 59629,
    "char_count": 548,
    "text": "4.9\nBreach of Obligations\nThe Parties herein agree that during the subsistence of this Agreement, subject to\nNTPC being in compliance of its obligations & undertakings under this Agreement,\nthe SPD would have no right to negotiate or enter into any dialogue with any third\nparty for the sale of Contracted Capacity of power which is the subject matter of this\nAgreement. It is the specific understanding between the Parties that such bar will\napply throughout the entire term of this Agreement.\n4.10\nGeneration compensation for Off-take constraints",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0097",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 97,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 59631,
    "char_end": 59715,
    "char_count": 84,
    "text": "4.10.1 Offtake constraints due to Transmission Infrastructure / Grid Unavailability:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0098",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 98,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 59717,
    "char_end": 60297,
    "char_count": 580,
    "text": "After the scheduled commissioning date, if the plant is ready but the necessary\npower evacuation/ transmission infrastructure is not ready, for reasons not\nattributable to the SPD, then SCD for such projects may be revised as the date as on\n30th day subsequent to the readiness of the Delivery Point and power evacuation\ninfrastructure. Decision on requisite extension on account of the above factor shall\nbe taken by NTPC on case-to-case basis after examining the issue.\nOr\nThe SPD may seek compensation as per extant Central Electricity Regulatory\nCommission (CERC) Regulations.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0099",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 99,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 60299,
    "char_end": 60383,
    "char_count": 84,
    "text": "However, it is clarified that if the Project is ready for commissioning prior to the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0100",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 100,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 60385,
    "char_end": 61314,
    "char_count": 929,
    "text": "27\nScheduled Commissioning Date, but the offtake is constrained because of\ninadequate/incomplete power evacuation infrastructure, no compensation shall be\npermissible.\n4.10.2 Offtake constraints due to Backdown\n(a) The SPD and the NTPC shall follow the forecasting and scheduling process as\nper the regulations in this regard by the Appropriate Commission. No RE power\nplant qualified as must-run power plant defined as per Electricity (Promotion of\nGeneration of Electricity from Must-Run Power Plant) Rules 2021, duly\ncommissioned, shall be directed to back down by the NTPC as per provisions of\nthe Rules. In case such eventuality of Backdown arises, except for the cases\nwhere the Backdown is on account of events like consideration of grid security\nor safety of any equipment or personnel or other such conditions, the SPD shall\nbe eligible for a Minimum Generation Compensation, from the NTPC, in the\nmanner detailed below.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0101",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 101,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 61316,
    "char_end": 61424,
    "char_count": 108,
    "text": "Duration of\nBackdown\nProvision for Generation Compensation\nHours of\nBackdown during\na monthly billing\ncycle.",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0102",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 102,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 61426,
    "char_end": 62107,
    "char_count": 681,
    "text": "Minimum Generation Compensation =\n100% of [(Average Generation per hour during the\nmonth) × (number of backdown hours during the\nmonth) × PPA Tariff] Where, Average Generation per\nhour during the month (kWh) =\nTotal generation in the month (kWh) ÷ Total hours of\ngeneration in the month\n(b) The Generation Compensation is to be paid as part of the energy bill for the\nsuccessive month after receipt of Regional Energy Accounts (REA). Possible\nconditions for exclusion of Generation Compensation, on account of Backdown\npurposes, shall be clearly specified in the RfS and the PPA.\n(c) No back-down / curtailment to be ordered without giving formal/ written\ninstruction for the same.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0103",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 103,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 62109,
    "char_end": 62111,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "28",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0104",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 104,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 62113,
    "char_end": 62176,
    "char_count": 63,
    "text": "ARTICLE 5\nSYNCHRONISATION, COMMISSIONING & COMMERCIAL OPERATION",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0105",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 105,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 62178,
    "char_end": 63923,
    "char_count": 1745,
    "text": "5.1 Synchronization, Commissioning and Commercial Operation\n5.1.1\nThe SPD shall give the concerned RLDC/SLDC and NTPC at least sixty (60)\ndays’ advanced preliminary written notice and at least thirty (30) days’ advanced\nfinal written notice, of the date on which it intends to synchronize the Power\nProject to the Grid System.\n5.1.2\nSubject to Article 5.1.1, the Power Project may be synchronized by the SPD to\nthe Grid System when it meets all the connection conditions prescribed in\napplicable Grid Code then in effect and otherwise meets all other Indian legal\nrequirements for synchronization to the Grid System.\n5.1.3\nThe synchronization equipment and all necessary arrangements / equipment\nincluding RTU for scheduling of power generated from the Project and\ntransmission of data to the concerned authority as per applicable regulation shall\nbe installed by the SPD at its generation facility of the Power Project at its own\ncost. The SPD shall synchronize its system with the Grid System only after the\napproval of synchronization scheme is granted by the head of the concerned\nsubstation/Grid System and checking/verification is made by the concerned\nauthorities of the Grid System.\n5.1.4\nThe SPD shall immediately after each synchronization/tripping of generator,\ninform the sub-station of the Grid System to which the Power Project is\nelectrically connected in accordance with applicable Grid Code under intimation\nto NTPC. In addition, the SPD will inject in-firm power to grid time to time to\ncarry out operational/ functional test prior to commercial operation. For\navoidance of doubt, it is clarified that Synchronization / Connectivity of the\nProject with the grid shall not to be considered as Commissioning of the Project.\n5.1.5",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0106",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 106,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 63924,
    "char_end": 64706,
    "char_count": 782,
    "text": "The SPD shall commission the Project as detailed in “Schedule 3:\nCommissioning Procedure” within eighteen (18) Months of the Effective Date of\nPPA. Declaration of COD / UCOD shall only be done subject to the\ndemonstration of the compliances as per Schedule-3 and shall be as the extant\nRegulation Indian Electricity Grid Code (IEGC).\n5.1.6\nThere can be part Commissioning of the Project subject to the condition that   the\nminimum capacity for acceptance of first and subsequent part(s) commissioning shall   be\n50 MW. Part commissioning of the project shall mean that all equipment\ncorresponding to the part capacity have been installed and commissioned and\ncorresponding energy has flown into the grid.\n5.1.7\nThe Parties agree that for the purpose of commencement of the supply of",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0107",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 107,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 64708,
    "char_end": 64931,
    "char_count": 223,
    "text": "29\nelectricity by SPD to NTPC, liquidated damages for delay etc., the Scheduled\nCommissioning Date or extended Scheduled Commissioning Date as defined in\nthis Agreement shall be the relevant date.\n5.1.8\nEarly Commissioning:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0108",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 108,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 64933,
    "char_end": 65351,
    "char_count": 418,
    "text": "The SPD shall be permitted for full commissioning as well as part\ncommissioning of the Project even prior to the Scheduled Commissioning Date,\nsubject to availability of transmission connectivity and GNA. Early\ncommissioning of the Project will be allowed solely at the risk and cost of the\nSPD, and NTPC may purchase the energy from such early commissioned Project\nat the 75% (seventy-five percent) of the PPA tariff.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0109",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 109,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 65353,
    "char_end": 65641,
    "char_count": 288,
    "text": "While calculating the above value of 75% of the PPA tariff, the digits after 2\ndecimal places will be ignored. For e.g., in case the value of 75% of the PPA\ntariff is calculated as 2.4567/kWh, the tariff applicable for purchase in case of\nearly commissioning will be read as Rs. 2.45/kWh.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0110",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 110,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 65643,
    "char_end": 66704,
    "char_count": 1061,
    "text": "Such intimation for early commissioning shall be provided to NTPC at least 15\ndays before the proposed early commissioning date. In case there is no response\nprovided by NTPC within 7 days from the receipt of such intimation, such early\ncommissioned capacity shall be deemed to have been rejected by NTPC. In case\nNTPC does not agree to purchase such energy, early part/full commissioning of\nthe Project shall still be allowed and the SPD will be free to sell such energy to a\nthird party; subject to grant of connectivity and GNA, until SCD or the date of\ncommencement of procurement of power from the Project as notified by NTPC,\nwhichever is earlier. In such cases, a Provisional Commissioning Certificate will\nbe issued to SPD for period up to SCD or date of commencement of Power\nProcurement (whichever is earlier), along with a NOC for sale of Power to 3rd\nParty for such period. UCOD/COD of the Project under the PPA will be the date\non which the commissioning certificate is issued upon successful commissioning\nof the part/full capacity of the Project.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0111",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 111,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 66706,
    "char_end": 67587,
    "char_count": 881,
    "text": "30\nARTICLE 6\nDISPATCH AND SCHEDULING\n\n6.1 Dispatch and Scheduling\n\n6.1.1 The SPD shall be entirely responsible and shall be required to declare the\nAvailability and Declared Capacity for the Project and arrange for dispatch of\nContracted Capacity in a composite manner under this Agreement as per the\napplicable regulations / requirements / guidelines of CERC / SERC /SLDC / RLDC\nor any other competent agency and same being recognized by the SLDC or any other\ncompetent authority / agency as per applicable regulation/ law / direction and\nmaintain compliance to the applicable Codes/Grid Code requirements and directions,\nif any, as specified by concerned SLDC/RLDC from time to time. Any deviation\nfrom the Schedule will attract the provisions of applicable regulation / guidelines /\ndirections and any financial implication on account of this shall be on the account of\nthe SPD.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0112",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 112,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 67589,
    "char_end": 68022,
    "char_count": 433,
    "text": "6.1.2 The SPD shall be responsible for directly coordinating and dealing with NTPC, State\nLoad Dispatch Centre’s, Regional Power Committees, and other authorities in all\nrespects in regard to declaration of availability, scheduling and dispatch of Solar\nPower and due compliance with deviation and settlement mechanism and the\napplicable Grid code Regulations, acknowledging that the SPD and procurer are the\nGrid connected entities.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0113",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 113,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 68024,
    "char_end": 68266,
    "char_count": 242,
    "text": "6.1.3 The SPD shall be responsible for any deviation from scheduling and for any resultant\nliabilities on account of charges for deviation as per applicable prevailing\nregulations. UI charges on this account shall be directly paid by the SPD.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0114",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 114,
    "page_start": 30,
    "page_end": 30,
    "char_start": 68268,
    "char_end": 68365,
    "char_count": 97,
    "text": "6.1.4 Auxiliary power consumption will be treated as per the concerned Central/State\nregulations.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0115",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 115,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 68367,
    "char_end": 68708,
    "char_count": 341,
    "text": "31\nARTICLE 7\nMETERING\n\n7.1 Meters\n\n7.1.1 For installation of Meters, Meter testing, Meter calibration and Meter reading and\nall matters incidental thereto, the SPD shall follow and be bound by the Central\nElectricity Authority (Installation and Operation of Meters) Regulations, 2006, the\nGrid Code, as amended and revised from time to time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0116",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 116,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 68710,
    "char_end": 68869,
    "char_count": 159,
    "text": "7.1.2 The SPD shall bear all costs pertaining to installation, testing, calibration,\nmaintenance, renewal and repair of meters at SPD’s side of Delivery Point.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0117",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 117,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 68871,
    "char_end": 69086,
    "char_count": 215,
    "text": "7.1.3 In addition to ensuring compliance of the applicable codes, the SPD shall install\nMain & Check meters at the Interconnection Point, along with Stand-by meter(s) as\nper the applicable Central/State regulations.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0118",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 118,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 69088,
    "char_end": 69577,
    "char_count": 489,
    "text": "7.1.4 In case of pooling of multiple Projects, power from multiple Projects can be pooled\nat a Pooling Substation prior to the Delivery point and the combined power can be\nfed at Interconnection Point through a common transmission line from the Pooling\nSubstation. In such cases, ABT compliant sub-meters as per relevant\nregulation/approval are also to be set up at pooling substation for individual\nprojects in addition to the meters at Interconnection Point as described in clause\n7.1.3.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0119",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 119,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 69579,
    "char_end": 69977,
    "char_count": 398,
    "text": "7.2\nReporting of Metered Data and Parameters\n7.2.1\nThe grid connected Solar PV Power Projects will install necessary equipment for\nregular monitoring of solar irradiance (including GHI, DHI, and solar radiation in\nthe module plane), ambient air temperature, wind speed and other weather\nparameters and simultaneously for monitoring of the electric power (both DC and\nAC) generated from the Project.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0120",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 120,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 69979,
    "char_end": 70238,
    "char_count": 259,
    "text": "7.2.2\nOnline arrangement would have to be made by the SPD for submission of above\ndata regularly for the entire period of this Power Purchase Agreement to the\nSLDC, NTPC and the concerned Ministry or concerned agency as per applicable\nregulation / directions.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0121",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 121,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 70240,
    "char_end": 70457,
    "char_count": 217,
    "text": "7.2.3\nReports on above parameters on monthly basis, and/or as required by regulation /\nGuidelines, shall be submitted by the SPD to MNRE/NTPC/National Institute of\nSolar Energy through NTPC for entire Term of the PPA.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0122",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 122,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 70459,
    "char_end": 71050,
    "char_count": 591,
    "text": "32\nARTICLE 8\nINSURANCES\n\n8.1 Insurance\n\nThe SPD shall effect and maintain or cause to be effected and maintained, at its own\ncost and expense, throughout the Term of PPA, Insurances against such risks to keep\nthe Project in good condition and shall take Industrial All Risk insurance policy\ncovering risks against any loss or damage, with such deductibles and with such\nendorsements and co-insured(s), which the Prudent Utility Practices would ordinarily\nmerit maintenance of and as required under the Financing Agreements,\nImplementation and Support Agreement and under the applicable laws.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0123",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 123,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 71052,
    "char_end": 71744,
    "char_count": 692,
    "text": "8.2 Application of Insurance Proceeds\n\n8.2.1 In case of the Project not being implemented through Financing Agreement(s), save\nas expressly provided in this Agreement or the Insurances, the proceeds of any\ninsurance claim made due to loss or damage to the Power Project or any part of the\nPower Project shall be first applied to reinstatement, replacement or renewal of such\nloss or damage.\nIn case of the Project being financed through Financing Agreement(s), save as\nexpressly provided in this Agreement or the Insurances, the proceeds of any insurance\nclaim made due to loss or damage to the Power Project or any part of the Power\nProject shall be applied as per such Financing Agreements.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0124",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 124,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 71746,
    "char_end": 72032,
    "char_count": 286,
    "text": "8.2.2 If a Force Majeure Event renders the Power Project no longer economically and\ntechnically viable and the insurers under the Insurances make payment on a “total\nloss” or equivalent basis, NTPC shall have claim on such proceeds of such Insurance\nlimited to outstanding dues of NTPC.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0125",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 125,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 72034,
    "char_end": 72517,
    "char_count": 483,
    "text": "8.3\nEffect on liability of NTPC\n\nNotwithstanding any liability or obligation that may arise under this Agreement, any\nloss, damage, liability, payment, obligation or expense which is insured or not or for\nwhich the SPD can claim compensation, under any Insurance shall not be charged to\nor payable to NTPC. It is for the SPD to ensure that appropriate insurance coverage is\ntaken for payment by the insurer for the entire loss and there is no under insurance or\nshort adjustment etc.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0126",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 126,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 72519,
    "char_end": 72881,
    "char_count": 362,
    "text": "33\nARTICLE 9\nAPPLICABLE TARIFF\n\n9.1\nThe SPD shall be entitled to receive the Tariff of Rs. ......... / kWh [Insert the Tariff\ndiscovered through the bidding process conducted by RECPDCL], fixed for the\nentire term of this Agreement, with effect from the SCD, for the power sold by the\nSPD to the NTPC for the scheduled energy as reflected in the Energy Accounts.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0127",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 127,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 72883,
    "char_end": 73951,
    "char_count": 1068,
    "text": "9.2\nPursuant to Article 5.1.8, in case of early part-commissioning, till SCD, subject to\nthe consent for such purchase by the NTPC, NTPC may purchase the generation\n@......... .................................................................................. [Insert the value as per\n75% (seventy-five per cent) of the Applicable Tariff]. While calculating the above\nvalue of 75% of the PPA tariff, the digits after 2 decimal places will be ignored. For\ne.g., in case the value of 75% of the PPA tariff is calculated as 2.4567/kWh, the\ntariff applicable for purchase in case of early commissioning will be read as Rs.\n2.45/kWh. However, in case the entire Project capacity is commissioned prior to\nSCD, NTPC may purchase energy supplied from commissioning of full\ncapacity till SCD at ........................................................... [Insert Tariff]/kWh. In\nboth the cases of early part or full commissioning of the Project, the Applicable\nTariff for the commissioned Project shall be ........................ [Insert\nTariff]/kWh\nfrom and including the SCD.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0128",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 128,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 73953,
    "char_end": 74733,
    "char_count": 780,
    "text": "9.3\nAny excess generation over and above energy specified in Article 4.4.2, may be\npurchased by NTPC at a tariff of ........................................... (Insert value equal to\n75% of the tariff as per Article 9.1). While calculating the above value of 75% of\nthe PPA tariff, the digits after 2 decimal places will be ignored. For e.g., in case the\nvalue of 75% of the PPA tariff is calculated as 2.4567/kWh, the tariff applicable for\npurchase in case of early commissioning will be read as Rs. 2.45/kWh. Any energy\nproduced and flowing into the grid before SCD shall not be at the cost of NTPC.\nHowever, the SPD will not be allowed to sell energy generated prior to SCD or\nexcess energy during any Contract Year to any other entity other than NTPC\n(unless refused by NTPC).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0129",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 129,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 74735,
    "char_end": 75058,
    "char_count": 323,
    "text": "34\nARTICLE 10\nBILLING AND PAYMENT\n\n10.1 General\n\n10.1.1 From the commencement of supply of power, NTPC shall pay to the SPD the\nmonthly Tariff Payments subject to the adjustments as per provisions of this\nAgreement including Article 10.3, in accordance with Article 9. All Tariff Payments\nby NTPC shall be in Indian Rupees.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0130",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 130,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 75060,
    "char_end": 75336,
    "char_count": 276,
    "text": "10.1.2 For the purpose of payment of the bills raised by the SPD(s), in case Energy Account\nis published on cumulative basis, payment to the SPD(s) for the energy delivered\nshall be apportioned based on JMR taken for the SPD’s Project at the Pooling\nsubstation/metering Point.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0131",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 131,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 75338,
    "char_end": 75465,
    "char_count": 127,
    "text": "10.1.3 The SPD shall be required to make arrangements and payments for import of energy\n(if any) as per applicable regulations.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0132",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 132,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 75467,
    "char_end": 75909,
    "char_count": 442,
    "text": "10.2 Delivery and Content of Monthly Bills/Supplementary Bills\n\n10.2.1 The SPD shall issue to NTPC hard copy of a signed Monthly Bill/Supplementary Bill\nfor the immediately preceding Month/relevant period based on the issuance of\nEnergy Accounts along with all relevant documents (payments made by SPD for\ndrawl of power, payment of reactive energy charges, Metering charges or any other\ncharges as per guidelines of SERC/CERC, if applicable.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0133",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 133,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 75911,
    "char_end": 76342,
    "char_count": 431,
    "text": "Each Monthly Bill shall include all charges as per this Agreement for the energy\nsupplied for the relevant Month based on Energy Accounts issued by RPC or any\nother competent authority which shall be binding on both the Parties. The Monthly\nBill amount shall be the product of the energy as per Energy Accounts and the\nApplicable Tariff. Energy drawn from the grid will be regulated as per the applicable\nCentral/State regulations.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0134",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 134,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 76344,
    "char_end": 76568,
    "char_count": 224,
    "text": "10.2.2 As per applicable regulation(s) of the Appropriate Commission(s)/respective\nSERC(s), all charges pertaining to obtaining open access and scheduling of power, if\nany, up to the delivery point shall be borne by the SPD.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0135",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 135,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 76570,
    "char_end": 76832,
    "char_count": 262,
    "text": "10.3 Payment of Monthly Bills\n\n10.3.1 Subject to the provisions of Article 10.3.4, NTPC shall pay the amount payable\nunder the Monthly Bill/Supplementary Bill by the Due Date to such account of the\nSPD, as shall have been previously notified by the SPD as below.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0136",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 136,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 76834,
    "char_end": 76836,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "35",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0137",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 137,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 76838,
    "char_end": 76986,
    "char_count": 148,
    "text": "10.3.2 All payments required to be made under this Agreement shall also include any\ndeduction or set off for:\ni)\ndeductions required by the Law; and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0138",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 138,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 76988,
    "char_end": 77185,
    "char_count": 197,
    "text": "ii)\namount claimed by NTPC, if any, from the SPD, will be adjusted from the\nmonthly energy payment. In case of any excess payment adjustment, 1.25%\nsurcharge will be applicable on day-to-day basis.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0139",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 139,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 77187,
    "char_end": 77951,
    "char_count": 764,
    "text": "The SPD shall open a bank account (the “SPD’s Designated Account\") for all Tariff\nPayments (including Supplementary Bills) to be made by NTPC to the SPD, and\nnotify NTPC of the details of such account at least ninety (90) Days before the\ndispatch of the first Monthly Bill. NTPC shall also designate a bank account at New\nDelhi (\"NTPC Designated Account\") for payments to be made by the SPD to NTPC,\nif any, and notify the SPD of the details of such account ninety (90) Days before the\nScheduled Commissioning Date. NTPC and the SPD shall instruct their respective\nbankers to make all payments under this Agreement to the SPD’s Designated\nAccount or NTPC’s Designated Account, as the case may be, and shall notify either\nParty of such instructions on the same day.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0140",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 140,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 77953,
    "char_end": 78066,
    "char_count": 113,
    "text": "10.3.3 Late Payment Surcharge (LPSC)\n\nLPSC shall be applicable as per MoP LPSC Rules 2022 and amendments thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0141",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 141,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 78068,
    "char_end": 78422,
    "char_count": 354,
    "text": "10.3.4 Subject to the Article 9 of this Agreement, in the event of early Commissioning of\nthe Project and subject to acceptance by NTPC, the payment for the power fed to the\ngrid may be accounted from the date of UCOD, and SPD would be allowed to raise\nBills against such power as per Article 10.2.1, subject to the conditions as stipulated\nin Article 9.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0142",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 142,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 78424,
    "char_end": 78564,
    "char_count": 140,
    "text": "10.3.5 Rebate\n\nFor payment of any Bill on or before Due Date, the following Rebate shall be paid by\nthe SPD to NTPC in the following manner.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0143",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 143,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 78566,
    "char_end": 78711,
    "char_count": 145,
    "text": "a)\nA Rebate of 1.5% shall be payable to the NTPC for the payments made\nwithin a period of 10 (ten) days of the presentation of hard copy of Bill.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0144",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 144,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 78713,
    "char_end": 78860,
    "char_count": 147,
    "text": "b) Any payments made after ten (10) days of the date of presentation of Bill\nthrough hard copy up to the Due Date shall be allowed a rebate of 1 %.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0145",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 145,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 78862,
    "char_end": 79009,
    "char_count": 147,
    "text": "c)\nFor the above purpose, the date of presentation of Bill shall be the next\n\n36\nBusiness Day of delivery of the physical copy of the Bill at NTPC.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0146",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 146,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 79011,
    "char_end": 79244,
    "char_count": 233,
    "text": "d) No Rebate shall be payable on the Bills raised on account of Change in Law\n(except in case of annuity tariff model being implemented, where rebate will be\napplicable) relating to taxes, duties, cess etc. and on Supplementary Bill.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0147",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 147,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 79246,
    "char_end": 79421,
    "char_count": 175,
    "text": "For the above purpose date of presentation of bill shall be the same day of delivery in\nhard copy. However, for consideration of rebate, next business day shall be\nconsidered.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0148",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 148,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 79423,
    "char_end": 79478,
    "char_count": 55,
    "text": "10.4\nPayment Security Mechanism - Letter of Credit (LC)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0149",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 149,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 79480,
    "char_end": 79502,
    "char_count": 22,
    "text": "Letter of Credit (LC):",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0150",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 150,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 79504,
    "char_end": 79792,
    "char_count": 288,
    "text": "10.4.1 NTPC shall provide to the SPD, in respect of payment of its Monthly Bills and/or\nSupplementary Bills, a monthly unconditional, revolving and irrevocable letter of\ncredit (“Letter of Credit”), opened and maintained which may be drawn upon by the\nSPD in accordance with this Article.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0151",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 151,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 79794,
    "char_end": 80241,
    "char_count": 447,
    "text": "10.4.2 Before the start of supply, NTPC shall provide payment security to the SPD\nthrough Revolving Letter of Credit (LC) of an amount of 1 (one) month’s average\nbilling through a scheduled bank. NTPC shall open a Letter of Credit in favour of\nthe SPD, to be made operative from a date prior to the Due Date of its first Monthly\nBill under this Agreement. The Letter of Credit shall have a term of twelve (12)\nMonths and shall be renewed annually.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0152",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 152,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 80243,
    "char_end": 80442,
    "char_count": 199,
    "text": "10.4.3 Provided that the SPD shall not draw upon such Letter of Credit prior to the Due\nDate of the relevant Monthly Bill and/or Supplementary Bill, and shall not make\nmore than one drawl in a Month.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0153",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 153,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 80444,
    "char_end": 80654,
    "char_count": 210,
    "text": "10.4.4 Provided further that if at any time, such Letter of Credit amount falls short of the\namount specified in Article 10.4.2 due to any reason whatsoever, NTPC shall\nrestore such shortfall before next drawl.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0154",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 154,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 80656,
    "char_end": 80820,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "10.4.5 NTPC shall cause the scheduled bank issuing the Letter of Credit to intimate the\nSPD, in writing regarding establishing of such irrevocable Letter of Credit.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0155",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 155,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 80822,
    "char_end": 80916,
    "char_count": 94,
    "text": "10.4.6 NTPC shall ensure that the Letter of Credit shall be renewed not later than its\nexpiry.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0156",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 156,
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "char_start": 80918,
    "char_end": 81009,
    "char_count": 91,
    "text": "10.4.7 All costs relating to opening, maintenance of the Letter of Credit shall be borne by",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0157",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 157,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 81011,
    "char_end": 81477,
    "char_count": 466,
    "text": "37\nNTPC.\n\n10.4.8 If NTPC fails to pay undisputed Monthly Bill or Supplementary Bill or a part\nthereof within and including the Due Date, then, subject to Article 10.4.6 & 10.5.2,\nthe SPD may draw upon the Letter of Credit, and accordingly the bank shall pay, an\namount equal to such Monthly Bill or Supplementary Bill or part thereof, in\naccordance with Article 10.4.3 above, by presenting to the scheduled bank issuing\nthe Letter of Credit, the following documents:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0158",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 158,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 81479,
    "char_end": 81600,
    "char_count": 121,
    "text": "i)\na copy of the Monthly Bill or Supplementary Bill (only for energy related\nbills) which has remained unpaid to SPD and;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0159",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 159,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 81602,
    "char_end": 81783,
    "char_count": 181,
    "text": "a certificate from the SPD to the effect that the bill at item (i) above, or\nspecified part thereof, is in accordance with the Agreement and has remained\nunpaid beyond the Due Date;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0160",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 160,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 81785,
    "char_end": 82266,
    "char_count": 481,
    "text": "10.5\nDisputed Bill\n10.5.1\nIf the NTPC does not dispute a Monthly Bill or a Supplementary Bill raised by the\nSPD within thirty (30) days of receiving such Bill shall be taken as conclusive.\n10.5.2\nIf the NTPC disputes the amount payable under a Monthly Bill or a\nSupplementary\nBill, as the case may be, it shall pay 50% of the invoice amount and it shall within\nfifteen (15) days of receiving such Bill, issue a notice (the \"Bill Dispute Notice\")\nto the invoicing Party setting out:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0161",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 161,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 82268,
    "char_end": 82416,
    "char_count": 148,
    "text": "i) the details of the disputed amount;\nii) its estimate of what the correct amount should be; and\niii) all written material in support of its claim.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0162",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 162,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 82418,
    "char_end": 82917,
    "char_count": 499,
    "text": "10.5.3\nIf the SPD agrees to the claim raised in the Bill Dispute Notice issued pursuant to\nArticle 10.5.2, the SPD shall revise such Bill and present along with the next\nMonthly Bill. In such a case excess amount shall be refunded along with interest\nat the same rate as Late Payment Surcharge, which shall be applied from the date\non which such excess payment was made by the disputing Party to the invoicing\nParty and up to and including the date on which such payment has been received\nas refund.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0163",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 163,
    "page_start": 37,
    "page_end": 37,
    "char_start": 82919,
    "char_end": 83173,
    "char_count": 254,
    "text": "10.5.4\nIf the SPD does not agree to the claim raised in the Bill Dispute Notice issued\npursuant to Article 10.5.2, it shall, within fifteen (15) days of receiving the Bill\nDispute Notice, furnish a notice (Bill Disagreement Notice) to the NTPC\nproviding:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0164",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 164,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 83175,
    "char_end": 83329,
    "char_count": 154,
    "text": "38\n i) reasons for its disagreement;\nii) its estimate of what the correct amount should be; and\niii) all written material in support of its counter-claim.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0165",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 165,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 83331,
    "char_end": 83659,
    "char_count": 328,
    "text": "10.5.5\nUpon receipt of the Bill Disagreement Notice by the NTPC under Article 10.5.4,\nauthorized representative(s) or a director of the board of directors/ member of\nboard of the NTPC and SPD shall meet and make best endeavors to amicably\nresolve such dispute within fifteen (15) days of receipt of the Bill Disagreement\nNotice.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0166",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 166,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 83661,
    "char_end": 83892,
    "char_count": 231,
    "text": "10.5.6\nIf the Parties do not amicably resolve the Dispute within fifteen (15) days of\nreceipt\nof Bill Disagreement Notice pursuant to Article 10.5.4, the matter shall be referred\nto Dispute resolution in accordance with Article 16.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0167",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 167,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 83894,
    "char_end": 84173,
    "char_count": 279,
    "text": "10.5.7\nFor the avoidance of doubt, it is clarified the despite a Dispute regarding an\ninvoice,\nNTPC shall, without prejudice to its right to Dispute, be under an obligation to\nmake payment of 50% of the invoice amount in the Monthly Bill.\n10.6 Quarterly and Annual Reconciliation",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0168",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 168,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 84175,
    "char_end": 84675,
    "char_count": 500,
    "text": "10.6.1\nThe Parties acknowledge that all payments made against Monthly Bills and\nSupplementary Bills shall be subject to quarterly reconciliation within 30 days of\nthe end of the quarter at the beginning of the following quarter of each Contract\nYear and annual reconciliation at the end of each Contract Year within 30 days to\ntake into account the Energy Accounts, Tariff adjustment payments, Tariff\nRebate, Late Payment Surcharge, or any other reasonable circumstance provided\nunder this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0169",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 169,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 38,
    "char_start": 84677,
    "char_end": 85443,
    "char_count": 766,
    "text": "10.6.2\nThe Parties, therefore, agree that as soon as all such data in respect of any quarter\nof a Contract Year or a full Contract Year as the case may be has been finally\nverified and adjusted, the SPD and NTPC shall jointly sign such reconciliation\nstatement. Within fifteen (15) days of signing of a reconciliation statement, the\nSPD shall make appropriate adjustments in the next Monthly Bill. Late Payment\nSurcharge/ interest shall be payable in such a case from the date on which such\npayment had been made to the invoicing Party or the date on which any payment\nwas originally due, as may be applicable. Any Dispute with regard to the above\nreconciliation shall be dealt with in accordance with the provisions of Article 16.\n10.7\nPayment of Supplementary Bill",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0170",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 170,
    "page_start": 38,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 85445,
    "char_end": 85730,
    "char_count": 285,
    "text": "10.7.1 SPD may raise a (\"Supplementary Bill\") for payment on account of:\n\n39\ni)\nAdjustments required by the Energy Accounts (if applicable); or\nii)\nChange in Law as provided in Article 12, or\niii)\nPayment under Article 10.2 And such Supplementary Bill shall be paid\nby the other Party.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0171",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 171,
    "page_start": 39,
    "page_end": 39,
    "char_start": 85732,
    "char_end": 86156,
    "char_count": 424,
    "text": "10.7.2 NTPC shall remit all amounts due under a Supplementary Bill raised by the SPD to\nthe SPD’s Designated Account by the Due Date, except open access charges, RLDC\nor scheduling charges and transmission charges (if applicable). For Supplementary\nBill on account of adjustment required by energy account and payments under\nArticle 10.7, Rebate as applicable to Monthly Bills pursuant to Article 10.3.5 shall\nequally\napply.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0172",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 172,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 86158,
    "char_end": 86834,
    "char_count": 676,
    "text": "40\nARTICLE 11\nFORCE MAJEURE\n\n11.1\nDefinition of Force Majeure\n\nA ‘Force Majeure’ (FM) would mean one or more of the following acts, events or\ncircumstances or a combination of acts, events or circumstances or the consequence(s)\nthereof, that wholly or partly prevents or unavoidably delays the performance by the\nParty (the Affected Party) of its obligations under the relevant Power Purchase\nAgreement, but only if and to the extent that such events or circumstances are not\nwithin the reasonable control, directly or indirectly, of the Affected Party and could not\nhave been avoided if the Affected Party had taken reasonable care or complied with\nPrudent Utility Practices.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0173",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 173,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 86836,
    "char_end": 87284,
    "char_count": 448,
    "text": "11.2\nCategorization of Force Majeure Events:\n11.2.1 Natural Force Majeure Event\n\na) Act of God, including, but not limited to lightning, drought, fire and explosion\n(to the extent originating from a source external to the site), earthquake, volcanic\neruption, landslide, flood, cyclone, typhoon or tornado if it is declared / notified\nby the competent state / central authority / agency (as applicable), or verified to\nthe satisfaction of Procurer;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0174",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 174,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 87286,
    "char_end": 87649,
    "char_count": 363,
    "text": "b) radioactive contamination or ionizing radiation originating from a source in\nIndia or resulting from another Force Majeure Event mentioned above excluding\ncircumstances where the source or cause of contamination or radiation is\nbrought or has been brought into or near the Power Project by the Affected Party\nor those employed or engaged by the Affected Party;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0175",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 175,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 87651,
    "char_end": 87867,
    "char_count": 216,
    "text": "c) the discovery of geological conditions, toxic contamination or archaeological\nremains on the Project land that could not reasonably have been expected to be\ndiscovered through an inspection of the Project land; or",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0176",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 176,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 87869,
    "char_end": 88167,
    "char_count": 298,
    "text": "d) any event or circumstances of a nature analogous to any of the foregoing.\n11.2.2 Non-Natural Force Majeure Event\na) any act of war (whether declared or undeclared), invasion, armed conflict or act\nof foreign enemy, blockade, embargo, revolution, riot, insurrection, terrorist or\nmilitary action;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0177",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 177,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 88169,
    "char_end": 88254,
    "char_count": 85,
    "text": "b) nation/state-wide strike, lockout, boycotts or other industrial disputes which are",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0178",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 178,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 88256,
    "char_end": 88428,
    "char_count": 172,
    "text": "41\nnot directly and solely attributable to the actions of the Affected Party, but does\nnot include strike or labour unrest limited to the Affected Party or its\ncontractors;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0179",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 179,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 88430,
    "char_end": 89061,
    "char_count": 631,
    "text": "c) nationalization or any compulsory acquisition by any Indian Governmental\nInstrumentality/ State Government in national interest or expropriation of any\nmaterial Project assets or rights of the Generator, as a result of which the\nGenerator or its shareholders are deprived (wholly or partly) of their rights or\nentitlements under the Power Purchase Agreement. Provided that such action\ndoes not constitute remedies or sanctions lawfully exercised by the Procurer or\nany other Government Authority as a result of any breach of any of the\nApplicable Laws or the Applicable Permits by the Generator or the Generator\nrelated parties;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0180",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 180,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 89063,
    "char_end": 89906,
    "char_count": 843,
    "text": "d) action of a Government Authority having Material Adverse Effect including but\nnot limited to change in law, only if consequences thereof cannot be dealt with\nunder and in accordance with the provisions; any unlawful or unauthorized or\nwithout jurisdiction revocation of, or delay in, or refusal, or failure to renew or\ngrant without valid cause, any Permits of the Generator or any of the clearance,\nlicense, authorization to be obtained by the Contractors to perform their\nrespective obligations under the relevant PPA and/or the Project Documents;\nprovided that such delay, modification, denial, refusal or revocation did not\nresult from the Generator’s or any Contractors inability or failure to comply with\nany condition relating to grant, maintenance or renewal of such Permits or\nclearance, license, authorization, as the case may be.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0181",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 181,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 89908,
    "char_end": 90939,
    "char_count": 1031,
    "text": "Clarification: The phrase “Change in Law” would include changes brought out through\nchange in Law, Rules, Regulations or orders of competent authorities.\n11.2.3 Force Majeure Exclusions\nForce Majeure shall not include (i) any event or circumstance which is within the reasonable\ncontrol of the Parties and (ii) the following conditions, except to the extent that they are\nconsequences of an event of Force Majeure:\na) Unavailability, late delivery, or changes in cost of the plant, machinery,\nequipment, materials, spare parts or consumables for the Power Project;\nb) Delay in the performance of any contractor, sub-contractor or their agents;\nc) Non-performance resulting from normal wear and tear typically experienced in\npower generation materials and equipment;\nd) Strikes at the facilities of the Affected Party;\ne) Insufficiency of finances or funds or the agreement becoming onerous to\nperform; and\nf) Non-performance caused by, or connected with, the Affected Party’s:\ni. Negligent or intentional acts, errors or omissions;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0182",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 182,
    "page_start": 42,
    "page_end": 42,
    "char_start": 90941,
    "char_end": 91714,
    "char_count": 773,
    "text": "42\nii. Failure to comply with an Indian Law; or\niii. Breach of, or default under this Agreement.\n11.2.4 Notification of Force Majeure Event\na) The Affected Party shall give notice to the other Party of any event of Force\nMajeure as soon as reasonably practicable, but not later than seven (7) days after\nthe date on which such Party knew or should reasonably have known of the\ncommencement of the event of Force Majeure. If an event of Force Majeure\nresults in a breakdown of communications rendering it unreasonable to give\nnotice within the applicable time limit specified herein, then the Party claiming\nForce Majeure shall give such notice as soon as reasonably practicable after\nreinstatement of communications, but not later than one (1) day after such\nreinstatement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0183",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 183,
    "page_start": 42,
    "page_end": 42,
    "char_start": 91716,
    "char_end": 92219,
    "char_count": 503,
    "text": "b) Provided that such notice shall be a pre-condition to the Affected Party’s\nentitlement to claim relief under the PPA. Such notice shall include full\nparticulars of the event of Force Majeure, its effects on the Party claiming relief\nand the remedial measures proposed. The Affected Party shall give the other\nParty regular (and not less than weekly) reports on the progress of those\nremedial measures and such other information as the other Party may reasonably\nrequest about the Force Majeure Event.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0184",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 184,
    "page_start": 42,
    "page_end": 42,
    "char_start": 92221,
    "char_end": 93034,
    "char_count": 813,
    "text": "c) The Affected Party shall give notice to the other Party of (i) the cessation of the\nrelevant event of Force Majeure; and (ii) the cessation of the effects of such\nevent of Force Majeure on the performance of its rights or obligations under the\nPPA, as soon as practicable after becoming aware of each of these cessations.\n11.2.5 Performance Excused\na) The Affected Party, to the extent rendered unable to perform its obligations or\npart of the obligation thereof under the PPA as a consequence of the Force\nMajeure Event, shall be excused from performance of the obligations, provided\nthat the period shall not exceed 180 (one hundred and eighty) Days from the\ndate of issuance of the FM Notice. The Parties may mutually agree to extend the\nperiod for which performance is excused due to a Force Majeure Event.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0185",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 185,
    "page_start": 42,
    "page_end": 42,
    "char_start": 93036,
    "char_end": 93318,
    "char_count": 282,
    "text": "b) For the time period, as mutually agreed by the Parties, during which the\nperformance shall be excused, the generator shall be entitled for a day-to-day\nextension of the period provided for Financial Closure or Scheduled\nCommissioning Period or the PPA period, as the case may be.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0186",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 186,
    "page_start": 42,
    "page_end": 42,
    "char_start": 93320,
    "char_end": 93453,
    "char_count": 133,
    "text": "c) Provided always that a Party shall be excused from performance only to the\nextent reasonably warranted by the Force Majeure Event.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0187",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 187,
    "page_start": 43,
    "page_end": 43,
    "char_start": 93455,
    "char_end": 93457,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "43",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0188",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 188,
    "page_start": 43,
    "page_end": 43,
    "char_start": 93459,
    "char_end": 93625,
    "char_count": 166,
    "text": "d) Provided further that, nothing shall absolve the Affected Party from any\npayment obligations accrued prior to the occurrence of the underlying Force\nMajeure Event.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0189",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 189,
    "page_start": 43,
    "page_end": 43,
    "char_start": 93627,
    "char_end": 94582,
    "char_count": 955,
    "text": "11.2.6 No Liability for Other Losses\nSave as otherwise provided in the Guidelines, no Party shall be liable in any manner,\nwhatsoever, to the other Parties in respect of any Loss relating to or arising out of the\noccurrence or existence of any Force Majeure Event.\n11.2.7 Resumption of Performance\nDuring the period that a Force Majeure Event is subsisting, the Affected Party shall, in\nconsultation with the other Parties, make all reasonable efforts to limit or mitigate the effects of\nsuch Force Majeure Event on the performance of its obligations under the PPA. The Affected\nParty shall also make efforts to resume performance of its obligations under this Agreement as\nsoon as possible and upon resumption, shall notify other Parties of the same in writing. The\nother Parties shall afford all reasonable assistance to the Affected Party in this regard.\n11.3\nTermination Due to Force Majeure Event\n11.3.1 Termination due to Natural Force Majeure Event",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0190",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 190,
    "page_start": 43,
    "page_end": 43,
    "char_start": 94583,
    "char_end": 95232,
    "char_count": 649,
    "text": "(a) If, prior to the completion of the 180 (one hundred and eighty) Day period (or any\nextended period) for a Natural Force Majeure Event commencing from the date of\nissuance of the Force Majeure Notice, the Parties are of the reasonable view that a\nNatural Force Majeure Event is likely to continue beyond such 180 (one hundred and\neighty) Day period or any extended period agreed in pursuance of Article 11.2.5\n(Performance Excused); or that it is uneconomic or impractical to restore the affected\nUnit, then the Parties may mutually decide to terminate the PPA, and the termination\nshall take effect from the date on which such decision is taken.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0191",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 191,
    "page_start": 43,
    "page_end": 43,
    "char_start": 95233,
    "char_end": 95525,
    "char_count": 292,
    "text": "(b) Without prejudice to the provisions of Article above, the Affected Party shall, after the\nexpiry of the period of 180 (one hundred and eighty) Days or any other mutually\nextended period, be entitled to forthwith terminate the PPA in its sole discretion by\nissuing a notice to that effect.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0192",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 192,
    "page_start": 43,
    "page_end": 43,
    "char_start": 95526,
    "char_end": 95818,
    "char_count": 292,
    "text": "(c) On termination of the PPA\ni. No Termination Compensation shall be payable to the generator.\nii. The Generator shall be eligible for undisputed payments under outstanding\nMonthly Bill(s), before the occurrence of Force Majeure Event.\n11.4\nTermination due to Non-Natural Force Majeure Event",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0193",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 193,
    "page_start": 44,
    "page_end": 44,
    "char_start": 95820,
    "char_end": 95822,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "44",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0194",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 194,
    "page_start": 44,
    "page_end": 44,
    "char_start": 95824,
    "char_end": 96081,
    "char_count": 257,
    "text": "a) Upon occurrence of a Non-Natural Force Majeure Event, the Generator shall, at\nits discretion, have the right to terminate the PPA forthwith after the completion\nof the period of 180 (one hundred and eighty) Days from the date of the Force\nMajeure Notice.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0195",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 195,
    "page_start": 44,
    "page_end": 44,
    "char_start": 96083,
    "char_end": 96185,
    "char_count": 102,
    "text": "b) Notwithstanding anything in Article 11.2.6, on termination of the PPA pursuant\nto Article 11.4 (a).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0196",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 196,
    "page_start": 44,
    "page_end": 44,
    "char_start": 96187,
    "char_end": 96446,
    "char_count": 259,
    "text": "(i) the Procurer shall pay to the Generator, ‘Force Majeure Termination\nCompensation’ equivalent to the amount of the Debt Due and the 110%\n(one hundred and ten per cent) of the Adjusted Equity, as defined in\nthese Guidelines, and takeover the Project assets.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0197",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 197,
    "page_start": 44,
    "page_end": 44,
    "char_start": 96448,
    "char_end": 96590,
    "char_count": 142,
    "text": "(ii) the Generator shall be eligible for undisputed payments under\noutstanding Monthly Bill(s), before the occurrence of Force Majeure\nEvent.”",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0198",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 198,
    "page_start": 45,
    "page_end": 45,
    "char_start": 96592,
    "char_end": 96843,
    "char_count": 251,
    "text": "45\nARTICLE 12\nCHANGE IN LAW\n\nThe provisions for Change in Law shall be in accordance with the Electricity (Timely Recovery\nof Costs due to Change in Law) Rules, 2021 notified by MoP on 22nd October 2021 and\namendments thereof issued from time to time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0199",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 199,
    "page_start": 46,
    "page_end": 46,
    "char_start": 96845,
    "char_end": 96847,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "46",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0200",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 200,
    "page_start": 46,
    "page_end": 46,
    "char_start": 96849,
    "char_end": 96950,
    "char_count": 101,
    "text": "ARTICLE 13\nEVENTS OF DEFAULT AND TERMINATION\n\n13.1\nSPD Event of Default and the consequences thereof:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0201",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 201,
    "page_start": 46,
    "page_end": 46,
    "char_start": 96952,
    "char_end": 98679,
    "char_count": 1727,
    "text": "13.1.1 In the event the SPD is unable to commission the plant within the stipulated time\nperiod, or fails to supply power in terms of the PPA, or assigns or novates any of its\nrights or obligations contrary to the terms of the PPA, or repudiates the PPA, or\neffectuates a change in control or shareholding of its promoters in breach of the\nprovisions of the PPA, or commits any other acts or omissions as laid down in the\nPPA and is also unable to cure any of the aforesaid within the cure period, as may be\nprovided in the PPA, the SPD shall be construed to be in default.\n13.1.2 Upon being in default, the SPD shall be liable to pay to the NTPC, damages, as\nprovided in these Guidelines in Schedule 3 for failure to commission within\nstipulated time and Clause 4.4.1 for failure to supply power in terms of the PPA. For\nother cases, pay to the NTPC, damages, equivalent to 6 (six) months, or balance PPA\nperiod whichever is less, of charges for its contracted capacity. The NTPC shall have\nthe right to recover the said damages by way of forfeiture of bank guarantee, if any,\nwithout prejudice to resorting to any other legal course or remedy.\n13.1.3 In addition to the levy of damages as aforesaid, in the event of a default by the SPD,\nthe lenders shall be entitled to exercise their rights of substitution, in accordance with\nthe substitution agreement provided in the PPA and in concurrence with the NTPC.\nHowever, in the event the lenders are unable to substitute the defaulting SPD within\nthe stipulated period, the NTPC may terminate the PPA and acquire the Project\nassets for an amount equivalent to 90% of the debt due, failing which, the lenders\nmay exercise their mortgage rights and liquidate the Project assets.”",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0202",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 202,
    "page_start": 46,
    "page_end": 46,
    "char_start": 98681,
    "char_end": 99088,
    "char_count": 407,
    "text": "13.2\nNTPC Event of Default and the consequences thereof:\n\n13.2.1 If the Procurer is in default on account of reasons including inter alia failure to pay the\nmonthly and/or supplementary bills except disputed bills within the stipulated time\nperiod or repudiation of the PPA, the defaulting Procurer shall, subject to the prior\nconsent of the SPD, novate its part of the PPA to any third party, including its",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0203",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 203,
    "page_start": 47,
    "page_end": 47,
    "char_start": 99090,
    "char_end": 100839,
    "char_count": 1749,
    "text": "47\nAffiliates within the stipulated period.\n13.2.2 In the event the aforesaid novation is not acceptable to the SPD, or if no offer of\nnovation is made by the defaulting Procurer within the stipulated period, then the\nSPD may terminate the PPA and at its discretion, require the defaulting NTPC to\neither (i) takeover the Project assets by making a payment of the termination\ncompensation equivalent to the amount of the debt due and the 110% (one hundred\nand ten per cent) of the adjusted equity as defined below, less Insurance Cover, if\nany, or, (ii) pay to the SPD, damages, equivalent to 6 (six) months, or balance PPA\nperiod, whichever is less, of charges for its contracted capacity, with the Project\nassets being retained by the SPD.\n13.2.3 In the event of termination of PPA, any damages or charges payable to the STU/ CTU,\nfor the connectivity of the plant, shall be borne by the NTPC.\n13.2.4 Adjusted Equity means the Equity funded in Indian Rupees and adjusted on the first day\nof the current month (the “Reference Date”), in the manner set forth below, to reflect\nthe change in its value on account of depreciation and variations in Wholesale Price\nIndex (WPI), and for any Reference Date occurring between the first day of the\nmonth of Appointed Date (the date of achievement of Financial Closure) and the\nReference Date;\n(i)\nOn or before Commercial Operation Date (COD), the Adjusted Equity shall be a\nsum equal to the Equity funded in Indian Rupees and expended on the Project,\nrevised to the extent of one half of the variation in WPI occurring between the\nfirst day of the month of Appointed Date and Reference Date;\n(ii)\nAn amount equal to the Adjusted Equity as on COD shall be deemed to be the\nbase (the “Base Adjusted Equity”);",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0204",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 204,
    "page_start": 47,
    "page_end": 47,
    "char_start": 100840,
    "char_end": 101427,
    "char_count": 587,
    "text": "(iii) After COD, the Adjusted Equity hereunder shall be a sum equal to the Base\nAdjusted Equity, reduced by 0.333% (zero point three three three percent)\nthereof at the commencement of each month following the COD [reduction of\n1% (one percent) per quarter of an year] and the amount so arrived at shall be\nrevised to the extent of variation in WPI occurring between the COD and the\nReference Date;\nFor the avoidance of doubt, the Adjusted Equity shall, in the event of termination, be computed\nas on the Reference Date immediately preceding the Transfer Date; provided that no reduction",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0205",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 205,
    "page_start": 48,
    "page_end": 48,
    "char_start": 101429,
    "char_end": 103131,
    "char_count": 1702,
    "text": "48\nin the Adjusted Equity shall be made for a period equal to the duration, if any, for which the\nPPA period is extended, but the revision on account of WPI shall continue to be made.\n13.2.5 Debt Due means the aggregate of the following sums expressed in Indian Rupees\noutstanding on the Transfer Date:\n(i)\nThe principal amount of the debt provided by the Senior Lenders under the\nFinancing Agreements for financing the Total Project Cost (the ‘Principal’) but\nexcluding any part of the principal that had fallen due for repayment 2 (two)\nyears prior to the Transfer Date;\n(ii)\nAll accrued interest, financing fees and charges payable under the Financing\nAgreements on, or in respect of, the debt referred to in Clause 13.2.5 (i) above\nuntil the Transfer Date but excluding: (i) any interest, fees or charges that had\nfallen due one year prior to the Transfer Date, (ii) any penal interest or charges\npayable under the Financing Agreements to any Senior Lender, (iii) any pre-\npayment charges in relation to accelerated repayment of debt except where\nsuch charges have arisen due to Utility Default, and (iv) any Subordinated Debt\nwhich is included in the Financial Package and disbursed by lenders for\nfinancing the Total Project Cost.\nProvided that if all or any part of the Debt Due is convertible into Equity at the option of Senior\nLenders and/or the Concessionaire, it shall for the purposes of this Agreement be deemed not to\nbe Debt Due even if no such conversion has taken place and the principal thereof shall be dealt\nwith as if such conversion had been undertaken.\nProvided further that the Debt Due, on or after COD, shall in no case exceed 80% (eighty\npercent) of the Total Project Cost.”",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0206",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 206,
    "page_start": 49,
    "page_end": 49,
    "char_start": 103133,
    "char_end": 103135,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "49",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0207",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 207,
    "page_start": 49,
    "page_end": 49,
    "char_start": 103137,
    "char_end": 103903,
    "char_count": 766,
    "text": "ARTICLE 14\nLIABILITY AND INDEMNIFICATION\n\n14.1\nIndemnity\n\n14.1.1\nThe SPD shall indemnify, defend and hold NTPC harmless against:\na)\nany and all third-party claims against NTPC for any loss of or damage to\nproperty of such third party, or death or injury to such third party, arising out of a\nbreach by the SPD of any of its obligations under this Agreement; and\nb) any and all losses, damages, costs and expenses including legal costs, fines,\npenalties and interest actually suffered or incurred by NTPC from third party\nclaims arising by reason of a breach by the SPD of any of its obligations under\nthis Agreement, (provided that this Article 14 shall not apply to such breaches\nby the SPD, for which specific remedies have been provided for under this\nAgreement).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0208",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 208,
    "page_start": 49,
    "page_end": 49,
    "char_start": 103905,
    "char_end": 104536,
    "char_count": 631,
    "text": "14.2\nProcedure for claiming Indemnity\n\n14.2.1\nThird party claims\n\na)\nWhere the Indemnified Party is entitled to indemnification from the\nIndemnifying Party pursuant to Article 14.1.1(a) , the Indemnified Party shall\npromptly notify the Indemnifying Party of such claim referred to in Article\n14.1.1(a) in respect of which it is entitled to be indemnified.\nSuch notice shall be given as soon as reasonably practicable after the\nIndemnified Party becomes aware of such claim. The Indemnifying Party shall\nbe liable to settle the indemnification claim within thirty (30) days of receipt\nof the above notice. Provided however that, if:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0209",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 209,
    "page_start": 49,
    "page_end": 49,
    "char_start": 104538,
    "char_end": 104734,
    "char_count": 196,
    "text": "i) the Parties choose to refer the dispute in accordance with Article 16.3\nand\nii) the claim amount is not required to be paid/ deposited to such third\nparty pending the resolution of the Dispute,",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0210",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 210,
    "page_start": 49,
    "page_end": 49,
    "char_start": 104736,
    "char_end": 104987,
    "char_count": 251,
    "text": "The Indemnifying Party shall become liable to pay the claim amount to the\nIndemnified Party or to the third party, as the case may be, promptly following\nthe resolution of the Dispute, if such Dispute is not settled in favour of the\nIndemnified Party.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0211",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 211,
    "page_start": 50,
    "page_end": 50,
    "char_start": 104989,
    "char_end": 104991,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "50",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0212",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 212,
    "page_start": 50,
    "page_end": 50,
    "char_start": 104993,
    "char_end": 105458,
    "char_count": 465,
    "text": "b) The Indemnified Party may contest the claim by referring to the Appropriate\nCommission for which it is entitled to be Indemnified and the Indemnifying\nParty shall reimburse to the Indemnified Party all reasonable costs and expenses\nincurred by the Indemnified party. However, such Indemnified Party shall not\nsettle or compromise such claim without first getting the consent of the\nIndemnifying Party, which consent shall not be unreasonably withheld or\ndelayed.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0213",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 213,
    "page_start": 50,
    "page_end": 50,
    "char_start": 105460,
    "char_end": 105873,
    "char_count": 413,
    "text": "An Indemnifying Party may, at its own expense, assume control of the defense\nof any proceedings brought against the Indemnified Party if it acknowledges its\nobligation to indemnify such Indemnified Party, gives such Indemnified Party\nprompt notice of its intention to assume control of the defense, and employs an\nindependent legal counsel at its own cost that is reasonably satisfactory to the\nIndemnified Party.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0214",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 214,
    "page_start": 50,
    "page_end": 50,
    "char_start": 105875,
    "char_end": 106453,
    "char_count": 578,
    "text": "14.3\nIndemnifiable Losses\n\nWhere an Indemnified Party is entitled to Indemnifiable Losses from the Indemnifying\nParty the Indemnified Party shall promptly notify the Indemnifying Party of the\nIndemnifiable Losses actually incurred by the Indemnified Party. The Indemnifiable\nLosses shall be reimbursed by the Indemnifying Party within thirty (30) days of receipt of\nthe notice seeking Indemnifiable Losses by the Indemnified Party. In case of\nnonpayment of such losses after a valid notice under this Article 14.3, such event\nshall constitute a payment default under Article 13.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0215",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 215,
    "page_start": 50,
    "page_end": 50,
    "char_start": 106455,
    "char_end": 107507,
    "char_count": 1052,
    "text": "14.4\nLimitation on Liability\n\n14.4.1 Except as expressly provided in this Agreement, neither the SPD nor NTPC nor its/\ntheir respective officers, directors, agents, employees or affiliates (or their officers,\ndirectors, agents or employees), shall be liable or responsible to the other Party or its\naffiliates, officers, directors, agents, employees, successors or permitted assigns or\ntheir respective insurers for incidental, indirect or consequential damages, connected\nwith or resulting from performance or non- performance of this Agreement, or\nanything done in connection herewith, including claims in the nature of lost\nrevenues, income or profits (other than payments expressly required and properly\ndue under this Agreement), any increased expense of, reduction in or loss of power\ngeneration or equipment used therefore, irrespective of whether such claims are based\nupon breach of warranty, tort (including negligence, whether of NTPC , the SPD or\nothers), strict liability, contract, breach of statutory duty, operation of law or\notherwise.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0216",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 216,
    "page_start": 51,
    "page_end": 51,
    "char_start": 107509,
    "char_end": 107718,
    "char_count": 209,
    "text": "51\nNTPC shall have no recourse against any officer, director or shareholder of the SPD\nor any Affiliate of the SPD or any of its officers, directors or shareholders for such\nclaims excluded under this Article.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0217",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 217,
    "page_start": 51,
    "page_end": 51,
    "char_start": 107720,
    "char_end": 107921,
    "char_count": 201,
    "text": "14.5\nNTPC’s Liability\n\nIt is specifically agreed that the payment of money becoming due from the NTPC to the SPD\nunder this Agreement for supply of Solar Power to the extent of the Contracted Capacity.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0218",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 218,
    "page_start": 51,
    "page_end": 51,
    "char_start": 107923,
    "char_end": 108077,
    "char_count": 154,
    "text": "14.6\nDuty to Mitigate\n\nThe Parties shall endevour to take all reasonable steps so as mitigate any loss or damage which\nhas occurred under this Article 14.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0219",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 219,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 108079,
    "char_end": 108781,
    "char_count": 702,
    "text": "52\nARTICLE 15\nASSIGNMENTS AND CHARGES\n\n15.1 Assignments\n\nThis Agreement shall be binding upon, and inure to the benefit of the Parties and their\nrespective successors and permitted assigns. This Agreement shall not be assigned by any\nParty, except to the Project Lenders or Lender’s Representative as security for their debt\nunder the Financing Agreements, other than by mutual consent between the Parties to be\nevidenced in writing. Such assignment shall be agreed to by NTPC subject to the\ncompliance of provisions contained in this Agreement and more specifically to the\nprovisions of Article 4.1.1 of this Agreement. In no case, such assignment shall be\npermissible prior to the declaration of SCD.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0220",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 220,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 108783,
    "char_end": 108967,
    "char_count": 184,
    "text": "Provided that, NTPC shall permit assignment of any of SPD’s rights and obligations\nunder this Agreement in favour of the lenders to the SPD, if required under the Financing\nAgreements.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0221",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 221,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 108969,
    "char_end": 109118,
    "char_count": 149,
    "text": "Provided that, such consent shall not be withheld if NTPC seeks to transfer to any\ntransferee all of its rights and obligations under this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0222",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 222,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 109120,
    "char_end": 109630,
    "char_count": 510,
    "text": "Provided further that any successor(s) or permitted assign(s) identified after mutual\nagreement between the Parties may be required to execute a new agreement on the same\nterms and conditions as are included in this Agreement. An amount of Rs. 5 Lakh per\nTransaction as Facilitation Fee (non-refundable) shall be deposited by the SPD to NTPC.\nProvided further that, such consent shall not be withheld by the SPD if NTPC seeks to\ntransfer to any affiliate all of its rights and obligations under this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0223",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 223,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 109632,
    "char_end": 109904,
    "char_count": 272,
    "text": "In the event of Change in Shareholding/Substitution of Promoters triggered by the\nFinancial Institutions leading to signing of fresh PPA with a New Entity, an amount of\nRs. 10 Lakh per Transaction as Facilitation Fee (non-refundable) shall be deposited by\nthe SPD to NTPC.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0224",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 224,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 109906,
    "char_end": 110112,
    "char_count": 206,
    "text": "15.2 Permitted Charges\n\nSPD shall not create or permit to subsist any encumbrance over all or any of its rights and\nbenefits under this Agreement, other than as set forth in Article 15.1 and the Guidelines.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0225",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 225,
    "page_start": 53,
    "page_end": 53,
    "char_start": 110114,
    "char_end": 110426,
    "char_count": 312,
    "text": "53\nARTICLE 16\nGOVERNING LAW AND DISPUTE RESOLUTION\n\n16.1 Governing Law\n\nThis Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the Laws of India. Any\nlegal proceedings in respect of any matters, claims or disputes under this Agreement shall be\nunder the jurisdiction of appropriate courts in Delhi.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0226",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 226,
    "page_start": 53,
    "page_end": 53,
    "char_start": 110428,
    "char_end": 110871,
    "char_count": 443,
    "text": "16.2 Amicable Settlement and Dispute Resolution\n\n16.2.1\nAmicable Settlement\n\ni.\nEither Party is entitled to raise any claim, dispute or difference of whatever nature\narising under, out of or in connection with this Agreement (“Dispute”) by giving a\nwritten notice (Dispute Notice) to the other Party, which shall contain:\n(a) a description of the Dispute;\n(b) the grounds for such Dispute; and\n(c) all written material in support of its claim.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0227",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 227,
    "page_start": 53,
    "page_end": 53,
    "char_start": 110873,
    "char_end": 111129,
    "char_count": 256,
    "text": "ii.\nThe other Party shall, within thirty (30) days of issue of Dispute Notice issued\nunder Article 16.2.1(i), furnish:\n(a) counter-claim and defenses, if any, regarding the Dispute; and\n(b) all written material in support of its defenses and counter-claim.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0228",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 228,
    "page_start": 53,
    "page_end": 53,
    "char_start": 111131,
    "char_end": 111229,
    "char_count": 98,
    "text": "iii. Within thirty (30) days of issue of Dispute Notice by any Party pursuant to Article\n16.2.1(i)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0229",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 229,
    "page_start": 53,
    "page_end": 53,
    "char_start": 111231,
    "char_end": 111325,
    "char_count": 94,
    "text": "(a) if the other Party does not furnish any counter claim or defense under Article\n16.2.1 (ii)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0230",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 230,
    "page_start": 53,
    "page_end": 53,
    "char_start": 111327,
    "char_end": 111641,
    "char_count": 314,
    "text": "(b) or thirty (30) days from the date of furnishing counter claims or defense by the\nother Party, both the Parties to the Dispute shall meet to settle such Dispute\namicably. If the Parties fail to resolve the Dispute amicably within thirty (30)\ndays from the later of the dates mentioned in this Article 16.2.1(ii)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0231",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 231,
    "page_start": 53,
    "page_end": 53,
    "char_start": 111643,
    "char_end": 111732,
    "char_count": 89,
    "text": "(c) the Dispute shall be referred for dispute resolution in accordance with Article\n16.3.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0232",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 232,
    "page_start": 54,
    "page_end": 54,
    "char_start": 111734,
    "char_end": 112342,
    "char_count": 608,
    "text": "54\n16.3 Dispute Resolution:\n\nDispute Resolution by the Appropriate Commission:\n\nIn the event CERC is the Appropriate Commission, any dispute arises claiming any change\nin or regarding determination of the tariff or any tariff related matters, or which partly or\nwholly could result in change in tariff, such dispute shall be adjudicated by the CERC. All\nother disputes shall be resolved by arbitration under the Indian Arbitration and Conciliation\nAct, 1996. In the event SERC is the Appropriate Commission, then all disputes shall be\nadjudicated by the SERC or shall be referred for arbitration by the SERC.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0233",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 233,
    "page_start": 54,
    "page_end": 54,
    "char_start": 112344,
    "char_end": 112692,
    "char_count": 348,
    "text": "16.4 Parties to Perform Obligations:\n\nNotwithstanding the existence of any Dispute and difference referred to the Appropriate\nCommission and save as the Appropriate Commission may otherwise direct by a final or\ninterim order, the Parties hereto shall continue to perform their respective obligations (which\nare not in dispute) under this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0234",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 234,
    "page_start": 55,
    "page_end": 55,
    "char_start": 112694,
    "char_end": 112844,
    "char_count": 150,
    "text": "55\nARTICLE 17\nMISCELLANEOUS PROVISIONS\n\n17.1 Amendment\n\nThis Agreement may only be amended or supplemented by a written agreement\nbetween the Parties.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0235",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 235,
    "page_start": 55,
    "page_end": 55,
    "char_start": 112846,
    "char_end": 113116,
    "char_count": 270,
    "text": "17.2 Third Party Beneficiaries\n\nThis Agreement is solely for the benefit of the Parties and their respective successors\nand permitted assigns and shall not be construed as creating any duty, standard of\ncare or any liability to, any person not a party to this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0236",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 236,
    "page_start": 55,
    "page_end": 55,
    "char_start": 113118,
    "char_end": 113367,
    "char_count": 249,
    "text": "17.3 Waiver\n\n17.3.1 No waiver by either Party of any default or breach by the other Party in the performance\nof any of the provisions of this Agreement shall be effective unless in writing duly\nexecuted by an authorized representative of such Party.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0237",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 237,
    "page_start": 55,
    "page_end": 55,
    "char_start": 113369,
    "char_end": 113781,
    "char_count": 412,
    "text": "17.3.2\nNeither the failure by either Party to insist on any occasion upon the performance of\nthe terms, conditions and provisions of this Agreement nor time or other indulgence\ngranted by one Party to the other Parties shall act as a waiver of such breach or\nacceptance of any variation or the relinquishment of any such right or any other right\nunder this Agreement, which shall remain in full force and effect.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0238",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 238,
    "page_start": 55,
    "page_end": 55,
    "char_start": 113783,
    "char_end": 113973,
    "char_count": 190,
    "text": "17.4 Confidentiality\n\nThe Parties undertake to hold in confidence this Agreement and not to disclose the\nterms and conditions of the transaction contemplated hereby to third parties, except:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0239",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 239,
    "page_start": 55,
    "page_end": 55,
    "char_start": 113975,
    "char_end": 114190,
    "char_count": 215,
    "text": "a)\nto their professional advisors;\n\nb)\nto their officers, contractors, employees, agents or representatives, financiers,\nwho need to have access to such information for the proper performance of their\nactivities; or",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0240",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 240,
    "page_start": 55,
    "page_end": 55,
    "char_start": 114192,
    "char_end": 114280,
    "char_count": 88,
    "text": "c)\ndisclosures required under Law, without the prior written consent of the other\nParty.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0241",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 241,
    "page_start": 56,
    "page_end": 56,
    "char_start": 114282,
    "char_end": 114562,
    "char_count": 280,
    "text": "56\n17.5 Severability\n\nThe invalidity or unenforceability, for any reason, of any part of this Agreement shall\nnot prejudice or affect the validity or enforceability of the remainder of this\nAgreement, unless the part held invalid or unenforceable is fundamental to this\nAgreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0242",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 242,
    "page_start": 56,
    "page_end": 56,
    "char_start": 114564,
    "char_end": 114721,
    "char_count": 157,
    "text": "17.6 Notices\n\n17.6.1 All notices or other communications which are required to be given under this\nAgreement shall be in writing and in the English language.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0243",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 243,
    "page_start": 56,
    "page_end": 56,
    "char_start": 114723,
    "char_end": 114925,
    "char_count": 202,
    "text": "17.6.2 If to the SPD, all notices or other communications which are required must be\ndelivered personally or by registered post or facsimile or any other method duly\nacknowledged to the addresses below:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0244",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 244,
    "page_start": 56,
    "page_end": 56,
    "char_start": 114927,
    "char_end": 114988,
    "char_count": 61,
    "text": "Address\n:\nAttention\n:\nEmail\n:\nFax. No.\n:\nTelephone No.      :",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0245",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 245,
    "page_start": 56,
    "page_end": 56,
    "char_start": 114990,
    "char_end": 115164,
    "char_count": 174,
    "text": "17.6.3 If to NTPC, all notices or communications must be delivered personally or by\nregistered post or facsimile or any other mode duly acknowledged to the address(es)\nbelow:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0246",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 246,
    "page_start": 56,
    "page_end": 56,
    "char_start": 115166,
    "char_end": 115227,
    "char_count": 61,
    "text": "Address\n:\nAttention\n:\nEmail\n:\nFax. No.\n:\nTelephone No.      :",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0247",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 247,
    "page_start": 56,
    "page_end": 56,
    "char_start": 115229,
    "char_end": 115758,
    "char_count": 529,
    "text": "17.6.4 All notices or communications given by facsimile shall be confirmed by sending a\ncopy of the same via post office in an envelope properly addressed to the appropriate\nParty for delivery by registered mail. All notices shall be deemed validly delivered\nupon receipt evidenced by an acknowledgement of the recipient, unless the Party\ndelivering the notice can prove in case of delivery through the registered post that the\nrecipient refused to acknowledge the receipt of the notice despite efforts of the postal\nauthorities.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0248",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 248,
    "page_start": 57,
    "page_end": 57,
    "char_start": 115760,
    "char_end": 115762,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "57",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0249",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 249,
    "page_start": 57,
    "page_end": 57,
    "char_start": 115764,
    "char_end": 115957,
    "char_count": 193,
    "text": "17.6.5 Any Party may by notice of at least fifteen (15) days to the other Party change the\naddress and/or addresses to which such notices and communications to it are to be\ndelivered or mailed.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0250",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 250,
    "page_start": 57,
    "page_end": 57,
    "char_start": 115959,
    "char_end": 116272,
    "char_count": 313,
    "text": "17.7 Language\n\n17.7.1 All agreements, correspondence and communications between the Parties relating to\nthis Agreement and all other documentation to be prepared and supplied under the\nAgreement shall be written in English, and the Agreement shall be construed and\ninterpreted in accordance with English language.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0251",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 251,
    "page_start": 57,
    "page_end": 57,
    "char_start": 116274,
    "char_end": 116531,
    "char_count": 257,
    "text": "17.7.2 If any of the agreements, correspondence, communications or documents are prepared\nin any language other than English, the English translation of such agreements,\ncorrespondence, communications or documents shall prevail in matters of\ninterpretation.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0252",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 252,
    "page_start": 57,
    "page_end": 57,
    "char_start": 116533,
    "char_end": 116966,
    "char_count": 433,
    "text": "17.8 Restriction of Shareholders / Owners’ Liability\n\nParties expressly agree and acknowledge that none of the shareholders of the Parties\nhereto shall be liable to the other Parties for any of the contractual obligations of the\nconcerned Party under this Agreement. Further, the financial liabilities of the\nshareholder/s of each Party to this Agreement, shall be restricted to the extent\nprovided in the Indian Companies Act, 2013.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0253",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 253,
    "page_start": 57,
    "page_end": 57,
    "char_start": 116968,
    "char_end": 117300,
    "char_count": 332,
    "text": "17.9 Taxes and Duties\n\n17.9.1 The SPD shall bear and promptly pay all statutory taxes, duties, levies and cess,\nassessed/ levied on the SPD, contractors or their employees that are required to be\npaid by the SPD as per the Law in relation to the execution of the Agreement and\nfor supplying power as per the terms of this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0254",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 254,
    "page_start": 57,
    "page_end": 57,
    "char_start": 117302,
    "char_end": 117625,
    "char_count": 323,
    "text": "17.9.2 NTPC shall be indemnified and held harmless by the SPD against any claims that may\nbe made against NTPC in relation to the matters set out in Article 17.9.1.\n17.9.3 NTPC shall not be liable for any payment of, taxes, duties, levies, cess whatsoever\nfor discharging any obligation of the SPD by NTPC on behalf of SPD.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0255",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 255,
    "page_start": 57,
    "page_end": 57,
    "char_start": 117627,
    "char_end": 117753,
    "char_count": 126,
    "text": "17.10 Independent Entity\n\n17.10.1 The SPD shall be an independent entity performing its obligations pursuant to the\nAgreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0256",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 256,
    "page_start": 58,
    "page_end": 58,
    "char_start": 117755,
    "char_end": 118400,
    "char_count": 645,
    "text": "58\n17.10.2 Subject to the provisions of the Agreement, the SPD shall be solely responsible for\nthe manner in which its obligations under this Agreement are to be performed. All\nemployees and representatives of the SPD or contractors engaged by the SPD in\nconnection with the performance of the Agreement shall be under the complete\ncontrol of the SPD and shall not be deemed to be employees, representatives,\ncontractors of NTPC and nothing contained in the Agreement or in any agreement or\ncontract awarded by the SPD shall be construed to create any contractual relationship\nbetween any such employees, representatives or contractors and NTPC.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0257",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 257,
    "page_start": 58,
    "page_end": 58,
    "char_start": 118402,
    "char_end": 118891,
    "char_count": 489,
    "text": "17.11 Compliance with Law\n\nDespite anything contained in this Agreement but without prejudice to this Article, if\nany provision of this Agreement shall be in deviation or inconsistent with or\nrepugnant to the provisions contained in the Electricity Act, 2003, or any rules and\nregulations made there under, such provision of this Agreement shall be deemed to\nbe amended to the extent required to bring it into compliance with the aforesaid\nrelevant provisions as amended from time to time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0258",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 258,
    "page_start": 58,
    "page_end": 58,
    "char_start": 118893,
    "char_end": 119332,
    "char_count": 439,
    "text": "17.12 Breach of Obligations\n\nThe Parties acknowledge that a breach of any of the obligations contained herein\nwould result in injuries. The Parties further acknowledge that the amount of the\nliquidated damages or the method of calculating the liquidated damages specified in\nthis Agreement is a genuine and reasonable pre-estimate of the damages that may be\nsuffered by the non-defaulting party in each case specified under this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0259",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 259,
    "page_start": 58,
    "page_end": 58,
    "char_start": 119334,
    "char_end": 119610,
    "char_count": 276,
    "text": "17.13 Order of priority in application\n\nIn case of inconsistencies between the agreement(s) executed between the Parties,\napplicable Law including rules and regulations framed thereunder, the order of\npriority as between them shall be the order in which they are placed below:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0260",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 260,
    "page_start": 58,
    "page_end": 58,
    "char_start": 119612,
    "char_end": 119695,
    "char_count": 83,
    "text": "i.\nApplicable Law, rules and regulations framed thereunder;\n\nii.\nThe Grid Code; and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0261",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 261,
    "page_start": 58,
    "page_end": 58,
    "char_start": 119697,
    "char_end": 119906,
    "char_count": 209,
    "text": "iii.\nThe terms and conditions of this Agreement;\n\nIN WITNESS WHEREOF the Parties have caused the Agreement to be executed through\ntheir duly authorized representatives as of the date and place set forth above.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC074-0262",
    "doc_id": "DOC-074",
    "paragraph_index": 262,
