    "char_start": 0,
    "char_end": 647,
    "char_count": 647,
    "text": "No. PD- 13/6 6 I 2020-PPP ( Pa rt- 1 )/e-346833\nqrro uc+'r</GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nrf,{, frf, cfoc-fl *( q-flFt {arf,q\nMTNISTRY OF PORTS, SHTPPTNG AND WATERWAYS\n(vrffi+ ffi rrFftflt ft-.r/ pu il ic- P rivate- Pa ft n e rs h i p Wi n g )\n.{kd-64 1144/ Pa ri va ha n Bh awa n,\n1, {iq-< qr,i/t, Sansad Marg,\nc-tRdiNew Delhi - 110001\nft+iq,7 P\"red: 12th November, 2O2l\nTo\nChai rmen/Chairpersons/Chairman-cum-Managi\nng Di rector\nAll Major Ports/Kamarajar Port Limited\nSubject: Model Concession Agreement 2O2l for Public-Private-\nPartnership (PPP) in Major Pofts - Regarding.\nSir/Madam\nThe undersigned is directed to say that the Model Concession Agreement",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0001",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 1,
    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 1,
    "char_start": 648,
    "char_end": 2222,
    "char_count": 1574,
    "text": "(MCA) for implementation of private sector projects in Major Ports was initially\nformulated in 2008. Based on the learnings of the past projects and to enhance\nprivate sector investments, Model Concession Agreement, 2018 was formulated by this\nMinistry with the approval of the Cabinet in its meeting held on 3'd January, 2018.\n2.\nFurther, considering the change in policy environment due to enactment of\nMajor Port Authorities Act, 2O2L and exploring provision for further flexibility to\nrespond to dynamic market and regulatory conditions, the Ministry of Ports, Shipping\n& Watenruays (MoPSW) has decided to revise the existing Model Concession\nAgreement (MCA), 2018. In this context, this Ministry videits O.M. No. No.PD-\nL3|66|2O2O-PPPle-347158, dated 8th December, 2O2O constituted a Committee under\nthe chairmanship of Chairman, V.O. Chidambaranar Poft Trust to suggest changes in\nthe existing Model Concession Agreement, 2018 keeping in view rapidly changing\ntrade environment and aligned with Major Port Authorities Act, 202t; mitigate\nstakeholders' concerns; and also aligned with best practices followed across other\ninfrastructure sector.\n3.\nThe Committee submitted its draft report in July, 2021 and final document on\ndraft Model Concession Agreement in October,202L.\n4.\nEarlier the Cabinet, while giving approval to the Model Concession Agreement\n2018, in its meeting held on 3'd January, 2018 also approved that any future change in\nthe MCA shall be done with the concurrence of Ministry of Finance, NITI Aayog and\nDepartment of Legal Affairs.\n(Page 1 of 3)\nqr",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0002",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 2,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 2224,
    "char_end": 2463,
    "char_count": 239,
    "text": "-2-\n5.\nAccordingly, the draft Model Concession Agreement, 2021 along with the\nstatement indicating changes proposed in draft MCA, 2021 vis-i-vis the existing\nclauses in MCA, 2018 was circulated to NITI Aayog, Department of Economic Affairs",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0003",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 3,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 2464,
    "char_end": 3156,
    "char_count": 692,
    "text": "(DEA) (Ministry of Finance) and Department of Legal Affairs (DLq) for their\ncomments/observations on the draft Model Concession Agreement. Further,\ndeliberations were held on the comments/observations received from NITI Aayog,\nDepartment of Economic Affairs and Department of Legal Affairs on draft MCA, 2021\nand the final document on draft Model Concession Agreement (MCA), 2021 was\ncirculated to NITI Aayog, DEA and DLA for their final concurrence. DEA and DLA have\nconveyed their concurrence to the draft MCA, 2021. The NITI Aayog, however,\nsuggested some formulations on Minimum Guaranteed Cargo (MGC) which have duly\nbeen considered and incorporated in the Guiding Note to the MCA, 2021.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0004",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 4,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 3157,
    "char_end": 3428,
    "char_count": 271,
    "text": "6. The draft Model Concession Agreement,202l has accordingly been finalized. The\nsalient features of the Model Concession Agreement (MCA), 202L are as under:\n(i)\nRemedy to the concessionaire in the form of Change in Cargo and related\nbusiness revival plan (Afticle 13.2);",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0005",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 5,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 3429,
    "char_end": 3611,
    "char_count": 182,
    "text": "(ii) Levy and recovery of tariff revised to align in line with new Major Port\nAuthorities Act, 202L enabling the concessionaire to fix tariff based on market\nconditions (Articles 8);",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0006",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 6,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 3612,
    "char_end": 3784,
    "char_count": 172,
    "text": "(iii) Minimum Guaranteed Throughput (MGT) to be linked to royalty payment and\nproposed new bidding parameter in line with changes in tariff levying\nmechanism (Article 9.2);",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0007",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 7,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 3785,
    "char_end": 3916,
    "char_count": 131,
    "text": "(iv) Compensation to be provided for termination of concession agreement due to\nconcessionaire default prior to COD (Article 17.t)i",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0008",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 8,
    "page_start": 2,
    "page_end": 2,
    "char_start": 3917,
    "char_end": 4048,
    "char_count": 131,
    "text": "(v) Increasing draft of terminal by additional dredging during concession period and\nsharing cost & risk of dredging (Article 7.1);",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0009",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 9,
    "page_start": 2,
