    "char_start": 95298,
    "char_end": 96070,
    "char_count": 772,
    "text": "ARTICLE 5\nINDEPENDENT ENGINEER\n5.1\nIndependent Engineer\n(a) Independent Engineer shall be a technical consultancy firm selected in accordance with\nprovisions of the Model Request for Proposals for Selection of Technical Consultants, issued by\nthe Ministry of Finance, GOI vide OM 24(23)/PF-II/2008 dated May 21, 2009, or any substitute\nthereof. If any panel of such firms is prepared by Indian Ports Association for the purpose, then\nIndependent Engineer shall be selected out of that panel. The Concessioning Authority shall\ncomplete the selection process within a period of 3 months of the date of this Agreement. The\nConcessioning Authority shall in the procurement documents20 published by it, set out in\nreasonable detail the scope of work as indicated in Appendix 7.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0184",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 184,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 96071,
    "char_end": 96652,
    "char_count": 581,
    "text": "(b) The Independent Engineer selected pursuant to the aforesaid process shall be appointed for a\nperiod commencing from the Date of Award of Concession to [the date of expiry of 6 (six)\nmonths from the COD]. The scope of work of the Independent Engineer shall be substantially as\nset out in Appendix 7. On expiry or termination of the aforesaid appointment, the\nConcessioning Authority shall appoint an Independent Engineer for a further term of 3 (three)\nyears in accordance with the provisions of Appendix 7, and such procedure shall be repeated\nafter expiry of each appointment.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0185",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 185,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 96653,
    "char_end": 96801,
    "char_count": 148,
    "text": "(c) The costs and expenses of the Independent Engineer for their services shall be borne by the\nConcessioning Authority and Concessionaire, equally.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0186",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 186,
    "page_start": 40,
    "page_end": 40,
    "char_start": 96802,
    "char_end": 97262,
    "char_count": 460,
    "text": "(d) If the Concessioning Authority either on its own or on a report of the Concessionaire has reason\nto believe that the Independent Engineer is not discharging its duties in a fair, appropriate and\ndiligent manner, the Concessioning Authority may after giving the Independent Engineer due\nopportunity of being heard, terminate the appointment of the Independent Engineer and appoint\nanother firm in its place in accordance with the preceding clause (a) above.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
