  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0264",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 264,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 126180,
    "char_end": 126328,
    "char_count": 148,
    "text": "(k) prevent, with the assistance of concerned law enforcement agencies, any encroachment or\nunauthorized use of the Project Facilities and Services.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0265",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 265,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 126329,
    "char_end": 126736,
    "char_count": 407,
    "text": "(ii) Repairs and Maintenance\nThe Concessionaire shall at its own cost:\n(a) repair as necessary and maintain the Project Facilities and Services or any part thereof in\naccordance with the Scope of Work and for this purpose carry out routine preventive measures\nand maintenance of the Project Facilities and Services including resurveying of pavement,\nrepair structures and repair and refurbish equipment; and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0266",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 266,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 126737,
    "char_end": 127117,
    "char_count": 380,
    "text": "(b) maintain the Project Facilities and Services in accordance with the provisions of this Agreement\nand Good Industry Practice with the objective of providing adequate service standards and\nensuring that the Project Facilities and Services to be transferred to the Concessioning Authority\nupon expiry of the Concession Period are in good condition, normal wear and tear excepted.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0267",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 267,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 127118,
    "char_end": 127510,
    "char_count": 392,
    "text": "(iii) Replacement of Equipment\nThe Concessionaire shall at its cost, plan for replacement of the equipment well ahead of the time\nwhen the utility thereof is reasonably expected to expire and replace the equipment in accordance\nwith Good Industry Practice so as to ensure that the Project facilities and Services commensurate\nwith the Scope of Work, at all times during the Concession Period.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0268",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 268,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 127511,
    "char_end": 127772,
    "char_count": 261,
    "text": "(iv) Repairs, Replacement or Restoration\nThe Concessionaire shall at its own costs, promptly and diligently repair, replace or restore any of\nthe Project Facilities and Services or part thereof which may be lost, damaged, or destroyed for any\nreason whatsoever.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0269",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 269,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 127773,
    "char_end": 128217,
    "char_count": 444,
    "text": "(v) Removal / Replacement of Assets\nExcept as provided/authorized under this Agreement the Concessionaire shall not, without the prior\nwritten intimation to the Concessioning Authority, remove or replace any assets comprised in the\nProject Facilities and Services. Such notice shall contain the exact details of the assets that the\nConcessionaire intends to remove and/or replace, its reasons for doing so and the likely period for\nreplacement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0270",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 270,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 128218,
    "char_end": 128357,
    "char_count": 139,
    "text": "(vi) Payments to the Concessioning Authority\nThe Concessionaire shall make/ensure payments to the Concessioning Authority as per Article 9.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0271",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 271,
    "page_start": 52,
    "page_end": 52,
    "char_start": 128358,
    "char_end": 128843,
    "char_count": 485,
    "text": "(vii) Access for Inspection\nThe Concessionaire shall be obliged to extend all co-operation to Independent Engineer for\npurposes of verifying that the Project/the Project Facilities and Services are operated and\nmaintained in compliance with the Performance Standards and adhere to the Operations and\nMaintenance Standards and Safety Standards. Such verification shall be made annually.\nAdditionally, the Concessionaire shall upon prior intimation by the Concessioning Authority provide",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0272",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 272,
    "page_start": 53,
    "page_end": 53,
    "char_start": 128845,
    "char_end": 128847,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "49",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0273",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 273,
    "page_start": 53,
    "page_end": 53,
    "char_start": 128849,
    "char_end": 130551,
    "char_count": 1702,
    "text": "the authorized representatives of the Concessioning Authority access to the Port’s Assets/the\nProject Facilities and Services for inspection and review of operations and also to ascertain\ncompliance with any of the requirements under this Agreement. Without prejudice to the generality\nof this provision, it is agreed that the Concessionaire shall in particular extend all co-operation and\ninformation required by the Experts appointed by the Concessioning Authority for conducting a\nsafety audit and verifying that the Project/Project Facilities and Services are in strict compliance with\nthe Safety Standards.\n(viii)\nReports22\nThe Concessionaire shall provide to the Concessioning Authority, Monthly reports on cargo traffic,\nunit gross output/ discharge rates at berth, daily output rated per vessel, Tariff earned and collected\nin respect of Project Facilities and Services and effective working time to waiting within 15 (fifteen)\nDays following the end of each Month, and any other information relating to operations which the\nConcessioning Authority may require from time to time. If so desired by the Concessioning\nAuthority, the Concessionaire shall provide the reports in prescribed formats and in electronic form\nso as to provide online access to the Concessioning Authority and its representatives.\n(ix)\nComputer System and Network\nThe Concessionaire shall install, operate and maintain such computer system and network (such\nas Electronic Data Interchange and Port Community System) and follow such protocol as the\nConcessioning Authority may specify from time to time.\n(x)\nSecurity Arrangements\nThe Concessionaire may make his own arrangements for security in the Project Site/Port Assets",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0274",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 274,
    "page_start": 53,
    "page_end": 53,
    "char_start": 130552,
    "char_end": 131576,
    "char_count": 1024,
    "text": "and with respect to the Project provided the Concessionaire shall abide by the security regulations/\nprocedures prescribed by the Concessioning Authority or a Government Authority from time to time.\nIt shall also conform to and assist the Concessioning Authority or any authority responsible therefor\nin conforming to the International Ship and Port facility Security Code (“ISPS Code”) and such other\ncodes/requirements of International Maritime Organization as may be applicable to India from time\nto time.\n(xi)\nEmployment of Personnel\nThe Concessionaire shall employ qualified and skilled personnel required to operate the Project\nFacilities and Services. The terms of employment may be as deemed fit by the Concessionaire and\nthe Concessionaire shall comply with all Applicable Laws and bear all costs in this regard. Without\nprejudice to the generality of this provision, all requisite approvals for employment of personnel of\nforeign origin or nationality shall be obtained by the Concessionaire prior to engaging such",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0275",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 275,
    "page_start": 53,
    "page_end": 53,
    "char_start": 131578,
    "char_end": 131814,
    "char_count": 236,
    "text": "22 This provision may be modified depending on the Performance Standards stipulated on a project specific basis so as to ensure that the\nreports received by the Concessioning Authority will enable it to effectively evaluate performance.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0276",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 276,
    "page_start": 54,
    "page_end": 54,
    "char_start": 131816,
    "char_end": 131818,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "50",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0277",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 277,
    "page_start": 54,
    "page_end": 54,
    "char_start": 131820,
    "char_end": 133537,
    "char_count": 1717,
    "text": "personnel. Failure to obtain approval will not amount to a Force Majeure Event. All employees shall\nalways remain the Concessionaire’s responsibility.\nFurther, the Concessionaire shall comply with the requirements of employing the existing\npersonnel/ labour as agreed to and set out in Appendix 1123. All labour law compliances shall be\nthat of the Concessionaire alone.\n(xii)\nMinimum Guaranteed Cargo\nThe Concessionaire hereby unconditionally guarantees the Concessioning Authority annual cargo\nof the levels set out in Appendix 13 (“Minimum Guaranteed Cargo”) and agrees that except as\nprovided in this Agreement, it shall not be entitled to any relaxation of its guarantee in this respect.\n(xiii)\nIndemnity Against Claims for Loss of Goods\nNotwithstanding anything contained in the MPA Act or any other law for the time being in force, the\nConcessionaire shall be responsible for meeting any claim, action, suit or proceeding (the\n“Action”) by any third party alleging the loss, destruction or deterioration of goods of which charge\nhas been taken by the Concessionaire and indemnify, save and hold harmless the Concessioning\nAuthority, its officers, employees, agents and representatives (the “Indemnitees”) against all\nclaims which may be asserted against or suffered and legal fees and costs incurred and which\nrelate to any such goods, provided that notice of the Action received by the Indemnitee(s) shall be\nforwarded to the Concessionaire expeditiously and in any case within [●] Days of the receipt thereof\nby any of the Indemnitees. Provided further that the Indemnitees shall have the right but not the\nobligation, to contest, defend and litigate any Action by any third party alleged or asserted against",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0278",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 278,
    "page_start": 54,
    "page_end": 54,
    "char_start": 133538,
    "char_end": 134529,
    "char_count": 991,
    "text": "any of such Indemnitees in respect of, resulting from, related to or arising out of any matter for\nwhich it is to be indemnified hereunder, and reasonable costs and expenses thereof shall be\nindemnified by the Concessionaire. If the Concessionaire acknowledges in writing its obligation to\nindemnify the Indemnitees in respect of loss to the full extent, the Concessionaire shall be entitled,\nat its option, to assume and control the defence of such Action at its expense and through the\ncounsel of its choice; provided it gives prompt notice of its intention to do so to the Indemnitees and\nreimburses to them for the reasonable cost and expenses incurred by them prior to the assumption\nof such defence by the Concessionaire. In such case the Indemnitees shall not be entitled to settle\nor compromise any Action without the prior written consent of the Concessionaire, which consent\nshall not be unreasonably withheld or delayed. This indemnity shall survive termination of this\nAgreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0279",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 279,
    "page_start": 54,
