    "page_end": 55,
    "char_start": 134724,
    "char_end": 135143,
    "char_count": 419,
    "text": "(xiv)\nMaintenance of Complaint Portal\n(a) The Concessionaire shall maintain a “Complaint Portal” on its website which shall be available\nto all users of the Project Facilities and Services who shall be duly informed about availability of\nthe provision for lodging of complaints. The Complaint Portal will also be linked to the\nConcessioning Authority website with an alert system for real time access to the complaints.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0282",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 282,
    "page_start": 55,
    "page_end": 55,
    "char_start": 135144,
    "char_end": 135363,
    "char_count": 219,
    "text": "(b) Concessionaire shall take action for just and fair redressal of the grievance and submit a reply to\nthe complainant within thirty days from the date of receipt with a copy to Authority and maintain\na proof of reply.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0283",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 283,
    "page_start": 55,
    "page_end": 55,
    "char_start": 135364,
    "char_end": 135585,
    "char_count": 221,
    "text": "(c) If Concessionaire fails to address the grievance and the complaint makes a reference to\nConcessioning Authority, it will issue directions which shall be complied by the Concessionaire.\n7.1 (b) Rights of Concessionaire",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0284",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 284,
    "page_start": 55,
    "page_end": 55,
    "char_start": 135586,
    "char_end": 136531,
    "char_count": 945,
    "text": "(i) Refinancing\nUpon request made by the Concessionaire to this effect, the Concessioning Authority shall, in\nconformity with any regulations or guidelines that may be notified by the Government of India or the\nReserve Bank of India and other competent authority as applicable, as the case may be, permit and\nenable the Concessionaire to secure refinancing, in whole or in part, of the Debt Due on such terms\nas may be agreed upon between the Concessionaire and the entity providing such refinancing;\nprovided, however, that the refinancing hereunder shall always be subject to the prior written consent\nof the Concessioning Authority, which consent shall not be unreasonably withheld. For the avoidance\nof doubt, the tenure of debt refinanced hereunder may be determined mutually between the Senior\nLenders and the Concessionaire, but the repayment thereof shall be completed no later than 1 (one)\nyear prior to expiry of the Concession Period.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0285",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 285,
    "page_start": 55,
    "page_end": 55,
    "char_start": 136532,
    "char_end": 137389,
    "char_count": 857,
    "text": "(ii) Preferential and Priority Berthing\nNormally, except for the priority and preferential berthing that may be authorized in terms of\nguidelines issued by the Government from time to time, the Concessionaire shall manage and\noperate the Project Facilities and Services on a first come - first serve, common-user basis, open to\nany and all shipping lines, importers, exporters, shippers, consignees and receivers, and refrain\nfrom indulging in any unfair or discriminatory practice against any user or potential user thereof.\nHowever, if there is a requirement to offer preferential or priority berthing to any one or more\nshipping lines or vessel owners/operators to optimize the use of the Project Facilities and Services,\nit shall be done in accordance with the priority berthing norms agreed in writing between\nConcessionaire and Concessioning Authority",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0286",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 286,
    "page_start": 56,
    "page_end": 56,
    "char_start": 137391,
    "char_end": 137393,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "52",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0287",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 287,
    "page_start": 56,
    "page_end": 56,
    "char_start": 137395,
    "char_end": 137872,
    "char_count": 477,
    "text": "(iii) Unclaimed cargo\nThe Concessionaire may at its cost:\n(a) after obtaining prior written approval of the Commissioner of Customs or other competent\nGovernment Authority and in accordance with the provisions of Applicable Law, destroy or dispose\noff by way of public auction and/or tender, any unclaimed cargo, the charge of which has been\ntaken by Concessionaire under or pursuant to this Agreement, and always subject to provisions of\nMPA Act and other laws in this regard.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0288",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 288,
    "page_start": 56,
    "page_end": 56,
    "char_start": 137873,
    "char_end": 138477,
    "char_count": 604,
    "text": "(b) institute proceedings for recovery of unrealized charges, if any, in its name and/or defend any\nclaim made in respect of such cargo by consignee/owners. The Concessioning Authority agrees to\nprovide all reasonable assistance necessary in this regard to the Concessionaire.\n7.1 (c) Obligations of the Concessioning Authority\nIn addition to any of its other obligations in this Agreement, the Concessioning Authority shall\narrange for and provide the following:\n(i)\nMarine and Port Services\nThe Concessioning Authority shall provide/ cause to be provided, to the Concessionaire, the\nfollowing services:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0289",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 289,
    "page_start": 56,
    "page_end": 56,
    "char_start": 138478,
    "char_end": 138770,
    "char_count": 292,
    "text": "(a) scheduling the entry, berthing and sailing of the vessels, pilotage and towage on a non-\ndiscriminatory basis subject to priority berthing norms and the sailing schedule as determined by\nthe Deputy Conservator of the Port depending on individual ship characteristics and tidal\nconditions;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0290",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 290,
    "page_start": 56,
    "page_end": 56,
    "char_start": 138771,
    "char_end": 139078,
    "char_count": 307,
    "text": "(b) maintenance of the entrance channel draft at [●]m, provided this draft may be increased in\nfuture\nbased\non\nmutual\nagreement\nbetween\nthe\nConcessioning\nAuthority\nand\nConcessionaire(s) on cost sharing and any other aspects subject to such cost sharing\nmechanisms as may be determined under Clause (i) below",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0291",
