    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 387,
    "page_start": 74,
    "page_end": 74,
    "char_start": 177255,
    "char_end": 178878,
    "char_count": 1623,
    "text": "its obligations under this Agreement to obtain the Applicable Permits and to keep them in force and\neffect throughout the Concession Period.\n(b) Taxes and Duties\nAny levy or levies including increase therein of taxes, duties, cess and the hike, on account of/in\nrespect of Port’s Assets payable to the State Government or any statutory authority shall be met\nand paid by the Concessioning Authority.\n(c) Competing Facilities29\nThe Concessioning Authority shall not operationalise any additional facility within Port Limits for\nhandling _ (specify cargo) _either on its own or through any other Person until the earlier of (i) 5\n(five) years from the Scheduled Project Completion Date; or (ii) the average annual volume of cargo\nhandled at the Project Facilities and Services reaches a level of 70% of Project Capacity for 2 (two)\nconsecutive years (“Exclusivity Period”). Provided, this restriction shall not apply to the additional\nfacility envisaged at [●]30.\n(d) General Rights of Inspection and Verification\nThe Concessioning Authority may during the pendency of the Agreement itself or by Independent\nEngineer verify the performance of obligations of the Concessionaire as set out in this Agreement.\n12.3 Of the Concessioning Authority and the Concessionaire\n(a) Monitoring Arrangement\nThe parties shall furnish to each other periodical status reports relating to key milestones and\nobligations as per Appendix 17 “Monitoring Arrangement”\n(b) Compliance with Laws and Regulations\nThe Parties shall perform their respective obligations under this Agreement in accordance with the\nApplicable Laws and Applicable Permits.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0388",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 388,
    "page_start": 74,
    "page_end": 74,
    "char_start": 178880,
    "char_end": 179162,
    "char_count": 282,
    "text": "29 This provision may be retained on a project specific basis i.e. only for projects which in the reasonable judgement of the Concessioning\nAuthority would not be viable without such exclusivity.\n30 Details of additional facility planned within Port Limits and disclosed in the RFP.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0389",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 389,
