    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "71",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0390",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 390,
    "page_start": 75,
    "page_end": 75,
    "char_start": 179168,
    "char_end": 180962,
    "char_count": 1794,
    "text": "(c) Rights to Documents\n(i)\nConcessioning Authority’s Documents\nDocuments and computer programs or copies thereof, if any, provided by the Concessioning\nAuthority to the Concessionaire, shall always remain the property of the Concessioning Authority.\nSuch documents, computer programs and/or copies shall not be used by the Concessionaire for\nthe purposes other than for the Project. Such documents, computer programs and/or copies thereof\nshall, unless otherwise agreed upon by the Concessioning Authority, be returned by the\nConcessionaire to the Concessioning Authority on the Transfer Date.\n(ii)\nConcessionaire’s Documents\nDocuments and computer programs provided by the Concessionaire, or which are developed (and\nowned by the Concessionaire) for operation and/or maintenance of the Project /the Project Facilities\nand Services shall be handed over by the Concessionaire to the Concessioning Authority free of\ncost on the Transfer Date.\n(iii) Confidentiality\nAll confidential information and documents (whether financial, technical or otherwise) provided by\neither Party to the other shall not, unless compelled by law or the process of a Government Authority,\nbe disclosed to any Person without the consent of the other Party with the exception of providing\nsuch information to legal advisors/auditors of the concerned party on a need-to-know basis. This\ncovenant shall survive the Concession Period.\n(iv) Obligation to Cooperate\nThe Parties shall mutually cooperate with each other in order to achieve the objectives of this\nAgreement.\n(v)\nSubstitution Agreement\nThe Substitution Agreement envisaged by Appendix 3 hereunder, will/may be executed within 30\n(thirty) Days’ of notice by the Concessionaire to the Concessioning Authority of the Senior Lenders’\nreadiness to execute the same.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0391",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 391,
    "page_start": 76,
    "page_end": 76,
    "char_start": 180964,
    "char_end": 180966,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "72",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0392",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 392,
    "page_start": 76,
    "page_end": 76,
    "char_start": 180968,
    "char_end": 181192,
    "char_count": 224,
    "text": "ARTICLE 13\nCHANGE IN LAW AND CHANGE IN CARGO\n13.1 Change in Law\n13.1.1 “Change in Law” means the occurrence of any of the following after the Bid Date and having\nAdverse Impact as per the provisions of the Clause 13.1.2 (i):",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0393",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 393,
    "page_start": 76,
    "page_end": 76,
    "char_start": 181193,
    "char_end": 181378,
    "char_count": 185,
    "text": "(a) the enactment of any new Indian law;\n(b) the repeal, modification or re-enactment of any existing Indian law or any international treaty to\nwhich Government of India is a signatory;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0394",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 394,
    "page_start": 76,
    "page_end": 76,
    "char_start": 181379,
    "char_end": 181471,
    "char_count": 92,
    "text": "(c) the commencement of any Indian law which has not entered into effect until the Bid Date;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0395",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 395,
    "page_start": 76,
    "page_end": 76,
    "char_start": 181472,
    "char_end": 181720,
    "char_count": 248,
    "text": "(d) a change in the interpretation or application of any Indian law by a judgement of a court of record\nwhich has become final, conclusive and binding, as compared to such interpretation or\napplication by a court of record prior to the Bid Date; or",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0396",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 396,
    "page_start": 76,
    "page_end": 76,
    "char_start": 181721,
    "char_end": 181829,
    "char_count": 108,
    "text": "(e) any change in the rates of any of the Taxes that have a direct effect on the Project;\n13.1.2  The Remedy",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0397",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 397,
    "page_start": 76,
    "page_end": 76,
    "char_start": 181830,
    "char_end": 183154,
    "char_count": 1324,
    "text": "(i) If as a result of Change in Law, the Concessionaire suffers decrease in cargo traffic and reduction\nin revenue or an increase in costs or reduction in EBITDA or other financial burden, the aggregate\nfinancial effect of which results in either (a) reduction by more than 25% of EBITDA in the affected\nfinancial year as compared to the average EBITDA of the previous three financial years or from\nCOD till occurrence of Change in Law in case the Project is operational for less than three years\nfrom COD and this is enduring in nature due to the effect of Change in Law or (b) an increase in\nthe capital expenditure by more than 20% of the estimations before the occurrence of such\nChange in Law provided that such an increase in capital expenditure has been certified by the\nSenior Lender and the Independent Engineer, or (c) during construction period, the purpose for\nwhich the Project is being constructed becomes non permissible or unviable due to Change\nin Law (hereby (a), (b), (c) known as “Adverse Impact”), the Concessionaire may so notify the\nConcessioning Authority. Upon such notification, the Concessioning Authority and the\nConcessionaire shall meet, as soon as reasonably practicable but no later than 30 (thirty) days\nfrom the date of notice and set up a Conciliation & Settlement Committee (“Committee”);",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0398",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 398,
    "page_start": 77,
    "page_end": 77,
