    "char_end": 194955,
    "char_count": 426,
    "text": "ARTICLE 14\nFORCE MAJEURE\n14.1 Force Majeure Event\nAs used in this Agreement, Force Majeure Event means the occurrence of any of the Non-Political\nEvents, the Political Events or the Other Events in India, set out in Articles 14.2, 14.3 and 14.4\nrespectively, if it affects the performance by the Party claiming the benefit of Force Majeure (the\n“Affected Party”) of its obligations under this Agreement and which act or event:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0428",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 428,
    "page_start": 82,
    "page_end": 82,
    "char_start": 194956,
    "char_end": 195145,
    "char_count": 189,
    "text": "(a) is beyond the reasonable control of the Affected Party\n(b) the Affected Party could not have prevented or overcome by exercise of due diligence and\nfollowing Good Industry Practice; and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0429",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 429,
    "page_start": 82,
    "page_end": 82,
    "char_start": 195146,
    "char_end": 195562,
    "char_count": 416,
    "text": "(c) prevents the Affected Party from performing or discharging its obligations under this\nAgreement and thereby has Material Adverse Effect on the Affected Party\n14.2 Non-Political Events\nAny of the following events which prevent the Affected Party from performing any of its obligations\nfor a continuous period of not less than 7 (seven) Days from the date of its occurrence, shall\nconstitute a Non-Political Event:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0430",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 430,
    "page_start": 82,
    "page_end": 82,
    "char_start": 195563,
    "char_end": 196032,
    "char_count": 469,
    "text": "(a) act of God, epidemic, extremely adverse weather conditions, lightning, earthquake, cyclone,\nflood, volcanic eruption, chemical or radioactive contamination or ionizing radiation, fire or\nexplosion (to the extent of contamination or radiation or fire or explosion originating from a\nsource external to the Project Site and by reasons not attributable to the Concessionaire or the\nContractor or any of the employees or agents of the Concessionaire or the Contractor);",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0431",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 431,
    "page_start": 82,
    "page_end": 82,
    "char_start": 196033,
    "char_end": 196420,
    "char_count": 387,
    "text": "(b) strikes or boycotts (other than those involving the Concessionaire, Contractors or their\nrespective employees/representatives, or attributable to any act or omission of any of them),\nand not being an Other Event set forth in Article 14.4, labour disruptions or any other industrial\ndisturbances not arising on account of the acts or omissions of the Concessionaire or the\nContractor;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
