  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0538",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 538,
    "page_start": 104,
    "page_end": 104,
    "char_start": 239302,
    "char_end": 241045,
    "char_count": 1743,
    "text": "ARTICLE 19\nDISPUTE RESOLUTION\n19.1 Amicable Settlement\nIf any dispute or difference or claims of any kind arises between the Concessioning Authority and the\nConcessionaire in connection with construction, interpretation or application of any terms and\nconditions or any matter or thing in any way connected with or in connection with or arising out of this\nAgreement, whether before or after the termination of this Agreement, then the Parties shall meet\ntogether promptly, at the request of any Party, in an effort to resolve such dispute, difference or claim\nby discussion between them.\n19.2 Assistance of Expert [Deleted]\n19.3 Conciliation\nIn case any dispute is not resolved amicably as provided in Clause 19.1, the Concessionaire may\nagree to refer the matter to conciliation &settlement Committee established by the Concessioning\nAuthority as per provisions contained in Part-III of the Arbitration & Conciliation (Amendment) Act,\n2015(the “Conciliation & Settlement Committee”). The standard operating procedures for\nconciliation and settlement of disputes through the conciliatory process and the constitution of the\ncommittee shall be contained in the policy guidelines issued by the Concessioning Authority on the\nsubject, which shall be in alignment with the provisions contained in Sections 63 and 64 of the\nArbitration & Conciliation (Amendment) Act, 2015. In case the recommendations/decision of the\ncommittee is not acceptable to the Concessionaire, it shall be free to refer the dispute to arbitration in\naccordance with the provisions of Clause 19.4 or 19.5.\n19.4 Arbitration\n19.4.1 Any Dispute which is not resolved amicably as provided in Clause 19.1 and/or 19.3 shall be\nfinally settled by arbitration as set forth below: -",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0539",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 539,
    "page_start": 104,
    "page_end": 104,
    "char_start": 241046,
    "char_end": 241489,
    "char_count": 443,
    "text": "(i) The Dispute shall be referred to the Society for Affordable Redressal of Disputes - Ports\n(hereinafter called as SAROD - Ports). The dispute shall be dealt with in terms of Rules of\nSAROD - Ports. The detailed procedure for conducting Arbitration shall be governed by the Rules\nof SAROD - Ports and provisions of Arbitration & Conciliation Act, 1996, as amended from time to\ntime. The Dispute shall be governed by Substantive Law of India.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0540",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 540,
    "page_start": 105,
    "page_end": 105,
    "char_start": 241491,
    "char_end": 241494,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "101",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0541",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 541,
    "page_start": 105,
    "page_end": 105,
    "char_start": 241496,
    "char_end": 241768,
    "char_count": 272,
    "text": "(ii) The constitution of Arbitral Tribunal, code of conduct for Arbitrators and fees and expenses of\nSAROD - Ports and Arbitral Tribunal shall also be governed by the Rules of SAROD - Ports as\namended from time to time. The rules of SAROD – Ports are placed at Appendix-21",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0542",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 542,
    "page_start": 105,
    "page_end": 105,
    "char_start": 241769,
    "char_end": 241969,
    "char_count": 200,
    "text": "(iii) The seat of Arbitration shall be New Delhi, or a place selected by the Governing Body of SAROD\n- Ports and the language for all documents and communications between the parties shall be\nEnglish.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0543",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 543,
    "page_start": 105,
    "page_end": 105,
    "char_start": 241970,
    "char_end": 243077,
    "char_count": 1107,
    "text": "(iv) The expenses incurred by each party in connection with the preparation, presentation, etc., of\narbitral proceedings shall be borne by each party itself.\n19.4.2 Any Award made in any arbitration held pursuant to the Article 19 shall be final and binding on\nthe Parties as from the date it is made, and the Concessionaire and the Authority agree and\nundertake to carry out such Award without delay.\n19.4.3 The Concessionaire and the Concessioning Authority agree that an Award may be enforced\nagainst the Concessionaire or the Concessioning Authority, as the case may be, and their respective\nassets wherever situated.\n19.4.4 In the event that the Party against whom the Award has been granted, challenges the Award\nfor any reason in a Court of law, the other Party, subject to the order of the Court, shall be entitled to\nseek an interim relief as per the provisions of the Arbitration and Conciliation Act or rules made\nthereunder. The Parties acknowledge and agree that the Arbitration proceedings shall be video\nrecorded and one copy each of the video recording shall be provided to both the parties.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0544",
