    "char_start": 243078,
    "char_end": 243872,
    "char_count": 794,
    "text": "19.5. Adjudication by Adjudicatory Board\nIn the event of constitution of a statutory Adjudicatory Board or such other forum with powers to\nreceive and adjudicate upon disputes between the Concessionaire and the Concessioning Authority,\nall disputes not settled under Clause 19.3 through conciliation, can alternatively be referred to the\nAdjudicatory Board or such other forum with mutual consent of the parties in accordance with the\napplicable laws. For avoidance of doubt, parties hereto agree that notwithstanding anything\ncontained herein above, after adjudication by the statutory Adjudicatory Board or such other forum,\nthe parties cannot refer the dispute, difference or controversy of whatsoever nature again under\nClause 19.4 and the adjudication hereunder shall be final and binding.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0545",
