    "char_start": 249479,
    "char_end": 249721,
    "char_count": 242,
    "text": "ARTICLE 21\nMISCELLANEOUS PROVISIONS\n21.1 Datum\nThe datum to which all levels shall be referred for the purpose of the Project is the Chart Datum\n(0.000) which is _______m below mean sea level.\n21.2 Accounts and Audits\n21.2.1  Audited Accounts",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0571",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 571,
    "page_start": 109,
    "page_end": 109,
    "char_start": 249722,
    "char_end": 251100,
    "char_count": 1378,
    "text": "(a) The Concessionaire shall maintain books of accounts recording all its receipts (including all Tariff\ncollected and other revenues derived/collected by it from or on account of the Project and/or its\nuse), income, expenditure, payments (including payments from the Escrow Account), assets and\nliabilities, in accordance with this Agreement, Good Industry Practice, Applicable Laws and\nApplicable Permits. The Concessionaire shall provide 2 (two) copies of its balance sheet, cash\nflow Statement and profit and loss account, along with a report thereon by its Statutory Auditors,\nwithin 90 (ninety) days of the close of the Accounting Year to which they pertain and such audited\naccounts, save and except where expressly provided to the contrary, shall form the basis of\npayments by either Party under this Agreement. The Concessioning Authority shall have the right\neither through itself or through any of its authorised representatives, to inspect the records of the\nConcessionaire during office hours and require copies of relevant extracts of books of accounts,\nduly certified by the Statutory Auditors, to be provided to the Concessioning Authority for\nverification of basis of payments, and in the event of any discrepancy or error being found, the\nsame shall be rectified and such rectified account shall form the basis of payments by either Party\nunder this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0572",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 572,
    "page_start": 109,
    "page_end": 109,
    "char_start": 251101,
    "char_end": 251604,
    "char_count": 503,
    "text": "(b) The Concessionaire shall, within 30 (thirty) days of the close of each quarter of an Accounting\nYear, furnish to the Concessioning Authority its unaudited financial results in respect of the\npreceding quarter, giving summarised information on  the cargo types handled and liable for\npayment of Tariff therefore, and any other information, in the manner and form prescribed by the\nSecurities and Exchange Board of India for publication of quarterly result by the Companies listed\non a stock exchange.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0573",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 573,
    "page_start": 109,
    "page_end": 109,
    "char_start": 251605,
    "char_end": 251885,
    "char_count": 280,
    "text": "(c) On or before the 30th day of June each year, the Concessionaire shall provide to the\nConcessioning Authority, for the preceding Accounting Year, a statement duly audited by its\nStatutory Auditors giving summarised information on (a) the cargo traffic and liable for payment of",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
