    "page_end": 110,
    "char_start": 252880,
    "char_end": 253344,
    "char_count": 464,
    "text": "(c) Notwithstanding anything to the contrary contained in this Agreement, the Concessioning\nAuthority shall have the right, but not the obligation, to appoint at its cost from time to time and at\nany time, another firm (the “Additional Auditors”) from the Panel of Chartered Accountants to audit\nand verify all those matters, expenses, costs, realisations and things which the Statutory Auditors\nare required to do, undertake or certify pursuant to this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0579",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 579,
    "page_start": 110,
    "page_end": 110,
    "char_start": 253345,
    "char_end": 254447,
    "char_count": 1102,
    "text": "(d) The Concessioning Authority shall have the right, but not the obligation, to appoint at its cost, for\nthe duration of the Construction Period, another firm (the “Concurrent Auditors”) from the Panel of\nChartered Accountants to undertake concurrent audit of the Concessionaire’s accounts.\n21.2.3 Certification of Claims by Statutory Auditors\nAny claim or document provided by the Concessionaire to the Concessioning Authority in\nconnection with or relating to receipts, income, payments, costs, expenses, accounts or audit,\nand any matter incidental thereto shall be valid and effective only if certified by its Statutory\nAuditors. For the avoidance of doubt, such certification shall not be required for exchange of\ninformation in the normal course of business including the submission of License Fee as per\nClause 9.1.\n21.2.4 Set-off\nIn the event any amount is due and payable by the Concessioning Authority to the\nConcessionaire, it may set-off any sums payable to it by the Concessionaire and pay the\nbalance remaining. Any exercise by the Concessioning Authority of its rights under this Clause",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0580",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 580,
    "page_start": 111,
    "page_end": 111,
    "char_start": 254449,
    "char_end": 254452,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "107",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0581",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 581,
    "page_start": 111,
    "page_end": 111,
    "char_start": 254454,
    "char_end": 256167,
    "char_count": 1713,
    "text": "21.2.4 shall be without prejudice to any other rights or remedies available to it under this\nAgreement or otherwise.\n21.2.5 Dispute Resolution\nIn the event of there being any difference between the findings of the Additional Auditors or the\nConcurrent Auditors, as the case may be, and the certification provided by the Statutory\nAuditors, such Auditors hall meet to resolve the differences and if they are unable to resolve the\nsame, such dispute shall be resolved by the Concessioning Authority by recourse to the dispute\nresolution procedure as described in Article 19.\n21.3 Compensation for Breach of Agreement\n21.3.1  Compensation for Default by the Concessionaire\nSubject to the provisions of Clause 21.3.5, in the event of the Concessionaire being in material\nbreach or default of this Agreement, it shall pay to the Concessioning Authority by way of\ncompensation, all direct costs suffered or incurred by the Concessioning Authority as a consequence\nof such material breach or default, within 30 (thirty) days of receipt of the demand supported by\nnecessary documentation thereof; provided that no compensation shall be payable under this Clause\n21.3.1 for any material breach or default in respect of which damages are expressly specified and\npayable under this Agreement or for any consequential losses incurred by the Concessioning\nAuthority.\n21.3.2 Compensation for Default by the Concessioning Authority\nSubject to the provisions of Clause 21.3.5, in the event of the Concessioning Authority being in\nmaterial breach or default of this Agreement at any time after the Date of Award of Concession, it\nshall pay to the Concessionaire by way of compensation, all direct costs suffered or incurred by the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0582",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 582,
    "page_start": 111,
    "page_end": 111,
    "char_start": 256168,
    "char_end": 256863,
    "char_count": 695,
    "text": "Concessionaire as a consequence of such material breach or default within 30 (thirty) days of receipt\nof the demand supported by necessary documentation thereof; provided that no such compensation\nshall be payable for any material breach or default in respect of which damages have been expressly\nspecified in this Agreement. For the avoidance of doubt, compensation payable may include interest\npayments on debt, O&M Expenses, any increase in capital costs on account of inflation and all other\ncosts directly attributable to such material breach or default but shall not include loss of revenues\nfrom Tariff or debt repayment obligations or other consequential losses, and for determining such",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
