    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0636",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 636,
    "page_start": 129,
    "page_end": 129,
    "char_start": 286069,
    "char_end": 286344,
    "char_count": 275,
    "text": "Annexure\nCONSTRUCTION STANDARDS, OPERATIONS AND MAINTENANCE\nSTANDARDS AND SAFETY STANDARDS\n[Indicative and minimum standards and norms for various kinds of projects are prescribed\nherein. Concessioning Authority may modify these and customize them to suit the Scope of\nWork.]",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0637",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 637,
    "page_start": 129,
    "page_end": 129,
    "char_start": 286345,
    "char_end": 287612,
    "char_count": 1267,
    "text": "A. General\nThe Concessionaire shall execute the project by completing civil works as per the Scope of\nWork and provide appropriate equipment for cargo handling and other support facilities for\nproper and efficient functioning.\nThe Concessionaire shall carry out Construction Works, etc. duly complying with the\nprovisions of all relevant latest Indian Standards and in case certain item of works not covered\nby the Indian Standards, provisions of ISO/IEC/OISD standards, etc. shall be complied.\nThe construction of civil works, facilities, erection & commissioning of lifting appliances,\nequipment and machinery and their layout shall ensure that during cargo operations these\nfacilities meet the required provisions of the Dock Workers Safety Health & Welfare Act, 1986\nand the relevant Regulations 1990.\nThe Concessionaire shall meet the requirements of Management Quality System (IS/ISO –\n9001: 2000) and shall also obtain accreditation for operations at the terminal. In addition, the\nConcessionaire shall comply with all relevant statutory regulations, codes, practices and\nguidelines.\nIt is not intended to specify herein all the relevant standards required to complete the Project.\nSuch of those standards considered more pertinent are listed in this Annexure.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0638",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 638,
    "page_start": 129,
    "page_end": 129,
    "char_start": 287613,
    "char_end": 288420,
    "char_count": 807,
    "text": "B. Civil Construction Work\nB. 1. Dry Bulk, Break Bulk & Container Terminals\nThe civil construction work may comprise variety of works such as dredging, reclamation,\nconstruction of breakwaters, berths, development of back-up area for storage of\ncargo/containers, approach roads, railways sidings, operational buildings/offices, maintenance\nworkshop, drainage, water supply, environmental protection works and other amenities. The\nConcessionaire is required to undertake all tests required as per IS/ ISO/IEC standards to\nensure that the construction work carried out by him meets not only the functional requirements\nof the project but also conforms to the required quality as per the standards. In addition, the\nConcessionaire shall also comply with the provisions of specifications published by the Indian",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0639",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 639,
    "page_start": 130,
    "page_end": 130,
    "char_start": 288422,
    "char_end": 288425,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "126",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0640",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 640,
    "page_start": 130,
    "page_end": 130,
    "char_start": 288427,
    "char_end": 290197,
    "char_count": 1770,
    "text": "Road Congress, RDSO of Ministry of Railways and provisions of Shore Protection Manual\n(CERC) of US Army Corps of Engineers, as may be pertinent to the Project. In respect of\nimplementing the Project, the Concessionaire shall refer to and as relevant comply with the\ndesign and construction standards specified in the following paragraphs.\nIndian Standards for Construction of Ports and Harbours\nIS 4651 – Part – 1 – 1974 Code of practice for planning and design of ports and harbours: Part\n1 Site investigation\nIS 4651–Part 2–1989 Code of practice for planning and design of ports and harbours Part 2\nEarth pressure\nIS 4651-Part III-1974 Code of practice for planning and design of ports and harbours: Part III:\nLoading\nIS 4651- Part 4 -1989 Code of practice for planning and design of ports and harbours: Part 4:\nGeneral Design consideration.\nIS 4651-Part 5-1980:\nIS7314: 1974\nIS 9527: Part 1: 1981\nIS 9527: Part 3: 1983\nIS 9527: Part 4: 1980\nIS 9527: Part 6: 1989\nIS 10020: Part 4: 1981\nIS 9556: 1980\nCode of practice for planning and design of ports and harbour Part:5 Layout and functional\nrequirements\nGlossary of terms relating to port and harbour engineering\nCode of practice for design and construction of port and harbour structures: Part 1 Concrete\nmonoliths Code of practice for design and construction of port and harbour structure: Part 3\nSheet pile walls\nCode of practice for design and construction of port and harbour structure: Part 4 Cellular\nSheet pile structures\nCode of practice for design and construction of port and harbour structures: Part 6 Block work\nRecommendations for design and construction of port and harbour components Part 4\nSlipways. Code of Practice for design and construction of diaphragm walls\nIndian Standards for Foundation Work",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
