  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0676",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 676,
    "page_start": 144,
    "page_end": 144,
    "char_start": 308876,
    "char_end": 309733,
    "char_count": 857,
    "text": "APPENDIX 7\nTERMS OF REFERENCE FOR INDEPENDENT ENGINEER\n[This Appendix shall stipulate the terms of reference for the Independent Engineer which shall\ninclude the scope of work (review of design and drawings, notification of objection thereto,\ninspection of Construction Works and Tests to be carried out, notification of shortfalls if any,\nissue of completion certificate, seeking of approval from collector of\ncustoms for the purpose of operationalising the facilities and services) which shall include the\nmanner and timeliness of the reports of the Independent Engineer to be submitted while\nperforming the services within the scope of work. Following is an indicative scope of work of the\nIndependent Engineer. The scope would be revised to include such other functions as are\nrequired to be undertaken pursuant to specific provisions of the Agreement.]",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0677",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 677,
    "page_start": 144,
    "page_end": 144,
    "char_start": 309734,
    "char_end": 310236,
    "char_count": 502,
    "text": "1. Scope\n1.1.These Terms of Reference for the Independent Engineer (the “TOR”) are being specified\npursuant to the Concession Agreement dated\n (the “Agreement”),which has been entered\ninto between the Authority and\n. (the “Concessionaire”) for the Project at ………. on\ndesign, build, finance, operate and transfer (the “DBFOT”) basis, and a copy of which is\nannexed hereto and marked as Annex-A to form part of this TOR.\n1.2 This TOR shall apply to construction, operation and maintenance of the Project.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0678",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 678,
    "page_start": 144,
    "page_end": 144,
    "char_start": 310237,
    "char_end": 310923,
    "char_count": 686,
    "text": "2. Definitions and interpretation\n2.1 The words and expressions beginning with or in capital letters used in this TOR and not\ndefined herein but defined in the Agreement shall have, unless repugnant to the context, the\nmeaning respectively assigned to them in the Agreement\n2.2 References to Articles, Clauses and Appendix in this TOR shall, except where the context\notherwise requires, be deemed to be references to the Articles, Clauses and Appendix of the\nAgreement, and references to Paragraphs shall be deemed to be references to Paragraphs of\nthis TOR.\n2.3 The rules of interpretation stated in Clauses 1.3, 1.4 and 1.5 of the Agreement shall apply,\nmutatis mutandis, to this TOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0679",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 679,
    "page_start": 144,
    "page_end": 144,
    "char_start": 310924,
    "char_end": 311553,
    "char_count": 629,
    "text": "3. Role and functions of the Independent Engineer\n3.1 The role and functions of the Independent Engineer shall include the following:\na. review of the Drawings and Documents as set forth in Paragraph 4;\nb. review,\ninspection\nand\nmonitoring\nof\nConstruction Works\nas set forth\nin\nParagraph 5;\nc. conducting Tests on completion of construction and issuing Completion/ Provisional\nCertificate as set forth in Paragraph 5;\nd. review, inspection and monitoring of operation and maintenance as set forth in\nParagraph 6;\ne. review, inspection and monitoring of Concessionaire’s obligations in Clause 18.2 and as\nset forth in Paragraph 7;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0680",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 680,
    "page_start": 145,
    "page_end": 145,
    "char_start": 311555,
    "char_end": 311558,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "141",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0681",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 681,
    "page_start": 145,
    "page_end": 145,
    "char_start": 311560,
    "char_end": 312152,
    "char_count": 592,
    "text": "f.\ndetermining, as required under the Agreement, the costs of any works or services and/or\ntheir reasonableness;\ng. determining, as required under the Agreement, the period or any extension thereof, for\nperforming any duty or obligation;\nh. assisting the Parties in resolution of Disputes as set forth in Paragraph 9; and\ni.\nUndertaking all other duties and functions in accordance with the Agreement.\n3.2 The Independent Engineer shall discharge its duties in a fair, impartial and efficient manner,\nconsistent with the highest standards of professional integrity and Good Industry Practice.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0682",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 682,
    "page_start": 145,
    "page_end": 145,
    "char_start": 312153,
    "char_end": 313897,
    "char_count": 1744,
    "text": "4. Development Period\n4.1 During the Development Period, the Independent Engineer shall undertake a detailed review\nof the Drawings to be furnished by the Concessionaire along with supporting data, including the\ngeo-technical and hydrological investigations, characteristics of materials from borrow areas\nand quarry sites, topographical surveys and traffic surveys. The Independent Engineer shall\ncomplete such review and send its comments/observations to the Concessioning Authority and\nthe Concessionaire within 15 (fifteen) days of receipt of such Drawings. In particular, such\ncomments shall specify the conformity or otherwise of such Drawings with the Scope of the\nProject and specifications and standards.\n4.2 The Independent Engineer shall review any modified Drawings or supporting documents\nsent to it by the Concessionaire and furnish its comments within 7 (seven) days of receiving\nsuch Drawings or Documents.\n4.3 The Independent Engineer shall review the Drawings in accordance with Appendix-6 and\nfurnish its comments thereon to the Concessioning Authority and the Concessionaire within 7\n(seven) days of receiving such Drawings.\n4.4 The Independent Engineer shall review the detailed design, construction methodology,\nquality assurance procedures and the procurement, engineering and construction time schedule\nsent to it by the Concessionaire and furnish its comments within 15 (fifteen) days of receipt\nthereof.\n4.5 Upon reference by the Concessioning Authority, the Independent Engineer shall review and\ncomment on the EPC Contract or any other contract for construction, operation and\nmaintenance of the Project, and furnish its comments within 7 (seven) days from receipt of such\nreference from the Concessioning Authority.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0683",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 683,
    "page_start": 145,
    "page_end": 145,
    "char_start": 313898,
    "char_end": 314909,
    "char_count": 1011,
    "text": "5. Construction Period\n5.1 In respect of the Drawings, Documents received by the Independent Engineer for its review\nand comments during the Construction Period, the provisions of Paragraph 4 shall apply,\nmutatis mutandis.\n5.2 The Independent Engineer shall review the monthly progress report furnished by the\nConcessionaire and send its comments thereon to the Concessioning Authority and the\nConcessionaire within 7 (seven) days of receipt of such report.\n5.3 The Independent Engineer shall inspect the Construction Works once every month,\npreferably after receipt of the monthly progress report from the Concessionaire, but before the\n20th (twentieth) day of each month in any case, and make out a report of such inspection (the\n“Inspection Report”) setting forth an overview of the status, progress, quality and safety of\nconstruction, including the work methodology adopted, the materials used and their sources,\nand conformity of Construction Works with the Scope of the Project and the specifications and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0684",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 684,
    "page_start": 146,
    "page_end": 146,
    "char_start": 314911,
    "char_end": 314914,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "142",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0685",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 685,
    "page_start": 146,
    "page_end": 146,
    "char_start": 314916,
    "char_end": 316694,
    "char_count": 1778,
    "text": "standards. In a separate section of the Inspection Report, the Independent Engineer shall\ndescribe in reasonable detail the lapses, defects or deficiencies observed by it in the\nconstruction of the Project. The Independent Engineer shall send a copy of its Inspection Report\nto the Concessioning Authority and the Concessionaire within 7 (seven) days of the inspection.\n5.4 The Independent Engineer may inspect the project more than once in a month if any lapses,\ndefects or deficiencies require such inspections.\n5.5 For determining that the Construction Works conform to specifications and standards, the\nIndependent Engineer shall require the Concessionaire to carry out, or cause to be carried out,\ntests on a sample basis, to be specified by the Independent Engineer in accordance with Good\nIndustry Practice for quality assurance. For purposes of this Paragraph 5.5, the tests specified\nin the relevant Manuals specified by the Concessioning Authority in relation to structures,\nbuildings and equipment (the “Quality Control Manuals”) or any modification/substitution thereof\nshall be deemed to be tests conforming to Good Industry Practice for quality assurance. The\nIndependent Engineer shall issue necessary directions to the Concessionaire for ensuring that\nthe tests are conducted in a fair and efficient manner, and shall monitor and review the results\nthereof.\n5.6 The sample size of the tests, to be specified by the Independent Engineer under paragraph\n5.5, shall comprise 10%  of the quantity or number of tests prescribed for each category or type\nof tests in the Quality Control Manuals; provided that the Independent Engineer may, for\nreasons to be recorded in writing, increase the aforesaid sample size by up to 10% for certain\ncategories or types of tests.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0686",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 686,
    "page_start": 146,
    "page_end": 146,
    "char_start": 316695,
    "char_end": 318460,
    "char_count": 1765,
    "text": "5.7 The timing of tests referred to in Paragraph 5.5, and the criteria for acceptance/ rejection of\ntheir results shall be determined by the Independent Engineer in accordance with the Quality\nControl Manuals. The tests shall be undertaken on a random sample basis and shall be in\naddition to, and independent of, the tests that may be carried out by the Concessionaire for its\nown quality assurance in accordance with Good Industry Practice.\n5.8 In the event that the Concessionaire carries out any remedial works for removal or\nrectification of any defects or deficiencies, the Independent Engineer shall require the\nConcessionaire to carry out, or cause to be carried out, tests to determine that such remedial\nworks have brought the Construction Works into conformity with the specifications and\nstandards, and the provisions of this Paragraph 5 shall apply to such tests.\n5.9 In the event that the Concessionaire fails to achieve any of the Project Milestones, the\nIndependent Engineer shall undertake a review of the progress of construction and identify\npotential delays, if any. If the Independent Engineer shall determine that completion of the\nProject is not feasible within the time specified in the Agreement, it shall require the\nConcessionaire to indicate within 15 (fifteen) days the steps proposed to be taken to expedite\nprogress, and the period within which COD shall be achieved. Upon receipt of a report from the\nConcessionaire, the Independent Engineer shall review the same and send its comments to the\nConcessioning Authority and the Concessionaire forthwith.\n5.10 If at any time during the Construction Period, the Independent Engineer determines that\nthe Concessionaire has not made adequate arrangements for the safety of workers and Users",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0687",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 687,
    "page_start": 146,
    "page_end": 146,
    "char_start": 318461,
    "char_end": 318969,
    "char_count": 508,
    "text": "in the zone of construction or that any work is being carried out in a manner that threatens the\nsafety of the workers and the Users, it shall make a recommendation to the Concessioning\nAuthority forthwith, identifying the whole or part of the Construction Works that should be\nsuspended for ensuring safety in respect thereof.\n5.11 In the event that the Concessionaire carries out any remedial measures to secure the\nsafety of suspended works and Users, it may, by notice in writing, require the Independent",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0688",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 688,
    "page_start": 147,
    "page_end": 147,
    "char_start": 318971,
    "char_end": 318974,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "143",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0689",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 689,
    "page_start": 147,
    "page_end": 147,
    "char_start": 318976,
    "char_end": 320442,
    "char_count": 1466,
    "text": "Engineer to inspect such works, and within 3 (three) days of receiving such notice, the\nIndependent Engineer shall inspect the suspended works and make a report to the\nConcessioning Authority forthwith, recommending whether or not such suspension may be\nrevoked by the Concessioning Authority.\n5.12 If suspension of Construction Works is for reasons not attributable to the Concessionaire,\nthe Independent Engineer shall determine the extension of dates set forth in the Project\nCompletion Schedule, to which the Concessionaire is reasonably entitled, and shall notify the\nConcessioning Authority and the Concessionaire of the same.\n5.13 The Independent Engineer shall carry out, or cause to be carried out, all the Tests\nspecified in this Appendix-7 and issue a Completion Certificate or Provisional Certificate, as the\ncase may be. For carrying out its functions under this Paragraph 5.13 and all matters incidental\nthereto, the Independent Engineer shall act under and in accordance with the provisions of\nClause 6.7 and this Appendix-7.\n5.14 Upon reference from the Concessioning Authority, the Independent Engineer shall make a\nfair and reasonable assessment of the costs of providing information, works and services as set\nforth in Clause 6.8 and certify the reasonableness of such costs for payment by the\nConcessioning Authority to the Concessionaire.\n5.15 The Independent Engineer shall aid and advise the Concessionaire in preparing the\nmaintenance manual.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0690",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 690,
    "page_start": 147,
    "page_end": 147,
    "char_start": 320443,
    "char_end": 322205,
    "char_count": 1762,
    "text": "6. Operation Period\n6.1 In respect of the Drawings, Documents and Safety Standards received by the Independent\nEngineer for its review and comments during the Operation Period, the provisions of Paragraph\n4 shall apply, mutatis mutandis.\n6.2 The Independent Engineer shall review the monthly report on cargo traffic, unit gross\noutput/ discharge rates at berth, daily output rated per vessel, Tariff earned and collected in\nrespect of Project Facilities and Services furnished by the Concessionaire and send its\ncomments thereon to the Concessioning Authority and the Concessionaire within 7 (seven)\ndays of receipt of such report.\n6.3 The Independent Engineer shall inspect the Project, once every year, before the 20th\n(twentieth) day of any month, and make out an operation and maintenance inspection report\nsetting forth an overview of the status, quality and safety of operation and maintenance\nincluding its conformity with the key performance indicators, maintenance requirements and\nSafety Standards. In a separate section of the operation and maintenance inspection report, the\nIndependent Engineer shall describe in reasonable detail the lapses, defects or deficiencies\nobserved by it in operation and maintenance of the Project. The Independent Engineer shall\nsend a copy of its operation and maintenance inspection report to the Concessioning Authority\nand the Concessionaire within 7 (seven) days of the inspection.\n6.4 The Independent Engineer may inspect the Project more than once in a year, if any lapses,\ndefects or deficiencies require such inspections.\n6.5 The Independent Engineer shall in its operation and maintenance inspection report specify\nthe tests, if any, that the Concessionaire shall carry out, or cause to be carried out, for the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0691",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 691,
    "page_start": 147,
    "page_end": 147,
    "char_start": 322206,
    "char_end": 322430,
    "char_count": 224,
    "text": "purpose of determining that the Project is in conformity with the maintenance requirements. It\nshall monitor and review the results of such tests and the remedial measures, if any, taken by\nthe Concessionaire in this behalf.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0692",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 692,
    "page_start": 148,
    "page_end": 148,
    "char_start": 322432,
    "char_end": 322435,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "144",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0693",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 693,
    "page_start": 148,
    "page_end": 148,
    "char_start": 322437,
    "char_end": 322706,
    "char_count": 269,
    "text": "6.6 The Independent Engineer shall determine if any delay has occurred in completion of repair\nor remedial works in accordance with the Agreement, and shall also determine the damages, if\nany, payable by the Concessionaire to the Concessioning Authority for such delay.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0694",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 694,
    "page_start": 148,
    "page_end": 148,
    "char_start": 322707,
    "char_end": 323174,
    "char_count": 467,
    "text": "7. Termination\n7.1 At any time, not earlier than 90 (ninety) days prior to termination but not later than 15\n(fifteen) days prior to such termination, the Independent Engineer shall, in the presence of a\nrepresentative of the Concessionaire, inspect the Project for determining compliance by the\nConcessionaire with the requirements set forth in Clause 18.2 and, if required, cause tests to be\ncarried out at the Concessionaire’s cost for determining such compliance.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0695",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 695,
    "page_start": 148,
    "page_end": 148,
    "char_start": 323175,
    "char_end": 323500,
    "char_count": 325,
    "text": "8. Determination of costs and time\n8.1 The Independent Engineer shall determine the costs, and/or their reasonableness, that are\nrequired to be determined by it under the Agreement.\n8.2 The Independent Engineer shall determine the period, or any extension thereof, that is\nrequired to be determined by it under the Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0696",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 696,
    "page_start": 148,
    "page_end": 148,
    "char_start": 323501,
    "char_end": 324046,
    "char_count": 545,
    "text": "9. Assistance in Dispute resolution\n9.1. When called upon by either Party in the event of any Dispute, the Independent Engineer\nshall mediate and assist the Parties in arriving at an amicable settlement.\n9.2 In the event of any disagreement between the Parties regarding the meaning, scope and\nnature of Good Industry Practice, as set forth in any provision of the Agreement, the\nIndependent Engineer shall specify such meaning, scope and nature by issuing a reasoned\nwritten statement relying on good industry practice and authentic literature.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0697",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 697,
    "page_start": 148,
    "page_end": 148,
    "char_start": 324047,
    "char_end": 324175,
    "char_count": 128,
    "text": "10. Other duties and functions\nThe Independent Engineer shall perform all other duties and functions specified in the\nAgreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0698",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 698,
    "page_start": 148,
    "page_end": 148,
    "char_start": 324176,
    "char_end": 325676,
    "char_count": 1500,
    "text": "11. Miscellaneous\nThe Independent Engineer shall notify its programme of inspection to the Concessioning\nAuthority and to the Concessionaire, who may, in their discretion, depute their respective\nrepresentatives to be present during the inspection.\n11.2 A copy of all communications, comments, instructions, Drawings or Documents sent by the\nIndependent Engineer to the Concessionaire pursuant to this TOR, and a copy of all the test\nresults with comments of the Independent Engineer thereon shall be furnished by the\nIndependent Engineer to the Concessioning Authority forthwith.\n11.3 The Independent Engineer shall obtain, and the Concessionaire shall furnish in 2 (two)\ncopies thereof, all communications and reports required to be submitted, under this Agreement,\nby the Concessionaire to the Independent Engineer, whereupon the Independent Engineer shall\nsend 1 (one) of the copies to the Concessioning Authority along with its comments thereon.\n11.4 The Independent Engineer shall retain at least one copy each of all Drawings and\nDocuments received by it, including ‘as-built’ Drawings, and keep them in its safe custody.\n11.5 Upon completion of its assignment hereunder, the Independent Engineer shall duly classify\nand list all Drawings, Documents, results of tests and other relevant records, and hand them\nover to the Concessioning Authority or such other person as the Concessioning Authority may\nspecify, and obtain written receipt thereof. Two copies of the said documents shall also be",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
