  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0743",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 743,
    "page_start": 160,
    "page_end": 160,
    "char_start": 338747,
    "char_end": 340055,
    "char_count": 1308,
    "text": "APPENDIX 14\nPERFORMANCE STANDARDS\n[This Appendix will prescribe project-specific minimum Performance Standards. The\nPerformance Standards prescribed in this Appendix will assess productivity of the terminal/berth\netc. as also the manner in which the assessment of compliance/shortfall in compliance will be\nmade. The Performance Standards given below are indicative. Ports will have to develop\nPerformance Standards for each specific project. These Performance Standards can be drawn\nfrom the specific design parameters as prescribed in the feasibility report and circulated to the\nselected bidders as well as the operational requirements and will be firmed up at the RFP stage\nfor each project. Further, the dynamics in handling of export and import cargoes being different,\ndistinction in the Performance Standards between import and export cargoes should be made.\nThe guidelines for formulating the Performance Standards along with the indicative standards\nand norms are given below which may be customized as per the requirements of the Project.\nWeightages in case of shortfall in meeting the prescribed minimum standards in respect of each\nof the performance standards shall be assigned by the Concessioning Authority keeping in view\nthe project-specific operational requirements.]\nPerformance Standards",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0744",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 744,
    "page_start": 160,
    "page_end": 160,
    "char_start": 340056,
    "char_end": 340811,
    "char_count": 755,
    "text": "1. Gross Berth Output\nThe parameter deals with the productivity of the terminal (Gross Berth Output) for different types\nof cargo. In case of dry and break-bulk cargo, the capability of the terminal (mechanization,\nmethod of handling) and parcel size will determine the Gross Berth Output. Higher terminal\ncapability and greater parcel size will lead to high productivity.\nThe Gross Berth Output shall be calculated as the total cargo handled (either loaded/unloaded)\nfrom the ship during a month divided by the time spent by the ship at the terminal number of\nworking days of ships in that month at that terminal. While determining the number of working\ndays from the ship hours, the berth allowance of [●] hours shall be subtracted from the total\nhours.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0745",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 745,
    "page_start": 161,
    "page_end": 161,
    "char_start": 340813,
    "char_end": 340816,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "157",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0746",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 746,
    "page_start": 161,
    "page_end": 161,
    "char_start": 340818,
    "char_end": 341463,
    "char_count": 645,
    "text": "In the case of containers, the crane rate shall be measured by dividing total number of TEUs\nlifted on/off from ships by the elapsed crane time. The elapsed crane time is the total allocated\ncrane hours less operational and non-operational delays.\nThe indicative norms for Gross Berth Output for different categories of cargo are as follows:\nCargo Category\nIndicative Norms\nContainer\n(Main line vessel)\n[25 moves per hour]\n(Feeder vessel)\n[17 moves per hour]\nIron Ore - Import / Export (Mechanized)\nFor terminals capable of handling more than\n100,000MT parcel size\n[60,000T/day]\nFor terminals capable of handling less than\n100,000MT parcel size.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0747",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 747,
    "page_start": 161,
    "page_end": 161,
    "char_start": 341465,
    "char_end": 342049,
    "char_count": 584,
    "text": "a) 65,000-100,000\n[30,000T/day]\nb) 30,000- 65,000\n[20,000T/day]\nc)< 30,000\n[10,000T/day]\nCoking Coal - Import (Mechanized)\nFor terminals capable of handling more than\n100,000 MT parcel size\n[50,000T/day]\nFor terminals capable of handling between\n65,000 MT-100,000MT parcel size.\n[40,000T/day]\nFor terminals capable of handling between\n30,000MT-65,000MT parcel size.\n[30,000T/day]\nFor terminals capable of handling less than\n30,000MT parcel size\n[15,000T/day]\nThermal coal – Import / Export (Mechanized)\nFor terminals capable of handling more than\n100,000 MT parcel size.\n[50,000T/day]",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0748",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 748,
    "page_start": 162,
    "page_end": 162,
    "char_start": 342051,
    "char_end": 342054,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "158",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0749",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 749,
    "page_start": 162,
    "page_end": 162,
    "char_start": 342056,
    "char_end": 343190,
    "char_count": 1134,
    "text": "For terminals capable of handling more than\n65,000 MT parcel size.\n[45,000 T/day]\nFor terminals capable of handling between\n30,000-65,000 MT parcel size\n[30,000T/day]\nFor terminals capable of handling less than\n30,000MT parcel size.\n[10,000T/day]\nNon-coking coal - Import (Mechanized)\nFor terminals capable of handling more than\n100,000 MT parcel size\n[40,000T/day]\nFor terminals capable of handling more than\n65,000 T parcel size.\n[30,000T/day]\nFor terminals capable of handling between\n30,000MT-65,000MT parcel size.\n[25,000T/day]\nFor terminals capable of handling less than\n30,000MT parcel size\n[10,000T/day]\nCoke – Import\nFor terminals capable of handling more than\n30,000 MT parcel size.\n[10,000T/day]\nFor terminals capable of handling less than\n30,000MT parcel size\n[7,000T/day]\nMixed Dry bulk cargo (Fertilizer and Food grains)\nFor terminals capable of handling more than\n30,000 MT parcel size.\n[12,500 T/day]\nFor terminals capable of handling up to 30,000\nMT parcel size.\n[7,500 T/day]\nMixed dry bulk cargo terminal handling B.F\nslag, Field spar, Limonite sand etc.\n[7,500 T/day]\nBreak Bulk\nSteel and bagged cargo\n[4000 T/day]",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0750",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 750,
    "page_start": 163,
    "page_end": 163,
    "char_start": 343192,
    "char_end": 343195,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "159",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0751",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 751,
    "page_start": 163,
    "page_end": 163,
    "char_start": 343197,
    "char_end": 343259,
    "char_count": 62,
    "text": "Others\n[2500 T/day]\nLiquid Bulk\nCrude\n[5000 T/H]\nPOL Products:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0752",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 752,
    "page_start": 163,
    "page_end": 163,
    "char_start": 343261,
    "char_end": 344866,
    "char_count": 1605,
    "text": "White\n[1000T/H]\nBlack\n[700T/H]\nLPG/LNG\n[400 T/H]\nOther Liquids\n[250T/H]\nWeightage in case of a shortfall in meeting the prescribed performance standard - [●]\n2. Transit Storage Dwell Time:\n(a) Containers:\nThe Transit Storage Dwell Time for a container shall mean the total time for which the container\nremains in the terminal. The Transit Storage Dwell Time for containers shall be calculated as an\naverage and shall be the sum of the transit storage of each container handled during the month\nat that terminal divided by the number of containers. To further clarify, the date and time a\ncontainer is discharged from the vessel till the said container leaves the out - gate of the\nTerminal, is the total transit storage time for import box. In case of export the time and date from\nwhich the container enters the terminal till the time and date it is loaded on to a vessel will be\nthe storage time. The details of time of discharge, gate-in, gate-out and loading need to be\nmaintained in respect of each container including ICD containers.\nUnclaimed cargo or any cargo that has been detained by the customs or any Government\nAuthority may be excluded.\n(b) Bulk Cargo:\nThe Transit Storage Dwell Time for coal/coke/mixed dry bulk cargo/liquid cargo shall be\ncalculated, as half of average parcel size of above cargo vessels in a month divided by average\ndisposal of cargo from the port per day as per the following methodology:\nAverage disposal of Cargo per day (A) = OB+Received/Dispatched-CB No. of days\nOB = Opening Balance, CB = Closing Balance.\nAverage Parcel Sizes (B) = P1+P2+ ………+Pnn(no. of parcels)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0753",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 753,
    "page_start": 164,
    "page_end": 164,
    "char_start": 344868,
    "char_end": 344871,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "160",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0754",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 754,
    "page_start": 164,
    "page_end": 164,
    "char_start": 344873,
    "char_end": 346118,
    "char_count": 1245,
    "text": "P1, P2 ………Pn are parcel size of each vessel in a month.\nTransit Storage Time for Bulk Cargo = 0.5 (B/A)\n(c) Break-bulk cargo:\nThe Transit Storage Dwell Time of Break Bulk cargo shall be calculated in the same manner as\ncalculated for container in the terminal. The Transit Storage Dwell Time for Break Bulk Cargo is\nthe sum of time of each unit of cargo that remains in the Port in a month divided by the number\nof cargo units handled during that month in the terminal. To further clarify, the time the break\nbulk cargo remains in the port will commence from the date and time of landing till the date and\ntime of exit from the Port in case of import and for export from the date and time the cargo\nentered the Port area till the date and time of the shipment.\nTransit Storage Dwell Time- Import\na)\nContainer\n(at terminal)\n[5 days]\nb)\nCoal /Coke\nand other dry\nbulk cargo\n(at stack\nyard)\n[30 days after date of\ncompletion of vessel’s\ndischarging operation]\nc)\nBreak bulk\n(at stack\nyard)\n[10 days after date of\ncompletion of vessel’s\ndischarging operation]\nTransit Storage Dwell Time- Export\na)\nContainer\n(at terminal)\n[3 days]\nb)\nIron Ore &\nother dry bulk\ncargo\n(at stack\nyard)\n[20 days up to\ncommencement of ship\nloading operation]\nc)\nBreak bulk",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0755",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 755,
    "page_start": 164,
    "page_end": 164,
    "char_start": 346120,
    "char_end": 346585,
    "char_count": 465,
    "text": "[10 days up to\ncommencement of ship\nloading operation]\nWeightage in case of a shortfall in meeting the prescribed performance standard - [●]\n3. Turnaround Time for receipt/delivery operation:\nThe Turnaround Time for receipt/delivery operation shall be the sum of time taken for\nloading/unloading of cargo divided by the number of trucks/trailers/rakes deployed, as the case\nmay be, in a month. Further, in case the truck/trailer/rake does both unloading and loading",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0756",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 756,
    "page_start": 165,
    "page_end": 165,
    "char_start": 346587,
    "char_end": 346590,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "161",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0757",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 757,
    "page_start": 165,
    "page_end": 165,
    "char_start": 346592,
    "char_end": 346773,
    "char_count": 181,
    "text": "operations on a single entry into the terminal, the time allocated shall be doubled for those\ntrucks/trailers/rakes.\na. (i) Truck for conventional cargo (Single operation)\n[4 hours]",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0758",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 758,
    "page_start": 165,
    "page_end": 165,
    "char_start": 346774,
    "char_end": 347008,
    "char_count": 234,
    "text": "(ii) Truck for conventional cargo (Double operation)\n[8 hours]\nb. (i) Trailer for container (single operation)\n[2 hours]\n(ii)Trailer for container (double operation)\n[4 hours]\nc. (i) Rake for ICD container (Single operation)\n[6 hours]",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0759",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 759,
    "page_start": 165,
    "page_end": 165,
    "char_start": 347009,
    "char_end": 347127,
    "char_count": 118,
    "text": "(ii) Rake for ICD container (Double operation)\n[12 hours]\nd. (i) Rake for dry bulk cargo (Single operation)\n[10 hours]",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0760",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 760,
    "page_start": 165,
    "page_end": 165,
    "char_start": 347128,
    "char_end": 348654,
    "char_count": 1526,
    "text": "(ii) Rake for dry bulk cargo (Double operation)\n[18 hours]\nWeightage in case of a shortfall in meeting the prescribed performance standard - [●]\nPerformance Evaluation and calculation of liquidated damages:\nPerformance evaluation shall be made on a quarterly review of the reports furnished by the\nConcessionaire and/or the records of the Concessionaire and/or by an enquiry by the\nConcessioning\nAuthority.\nThe\nConcessionaire\nshall\nbe\nliable\nto\npay\nliquidated\ndamagesdetermined at the rate of [1% of the Tariff collected and other revenues derived from\nthe project in the respective quarter for every shortfall of 10% ] in the average performance\nwhich shall be assessed in the following manner.\nEach Performance Standard is calculated as an average in the manner indicated above. The\nactual average performance vis-à-vis a standard will be evaluated against the prescribed\nstandard. The shortfall will be computed as a percentage of the prescribed standard. The\nshortfall in respect of each performance standard will have a weightage assigned to it. The\noverall shortfall in average performance shall be assessed as the aggregate of the weighted\nshortfalls in respect of each of the performance standards. For example, if there is a shortfall in\nGross Berth Output by x%, Transit Storage Dwell Time by y% and Turn round time for\nreceipt/delivery operations by z% and the weightage assigned to such shortfalls is 0.7, 0.2 and\n0.1 respectively, then the overall shortfall in average performance will be (0.7x + 0.2 y + 0.1\nz)%.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0761",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 761,
    "page_start": 166,
    "page_end": 166,
    "char_start": 348656,
    "char_end": 348659,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "162",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
