    "char_end": 365379,
    "char_count": 269,
    "text": "(c) shall, within 5 (five) business Days after receipt, deliver a copy to the Senior Lenders'\nRepresentative of any notice or document received by it in its capacity as the Escrow Bank\nfrom the Concessionaire or any other person hereunder or in connection herewith; and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0810",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 810,
    "page_start": 173,
    "page_end": 173,
    "char_start": 365380,
    "char_end": 366542,
    "char_count": 1162,
    "text": "(d) shall, within 5 (five) business Days after receipt, deliver a copy to the Concessionaire of any\nnotice or document received by it from the Senior Lenders' Representative in connection\nherewith.\n5.4\nNo set off\nThe Escrow Bank agrees not to claim or exercise any right of set off, banker's lien or other right\nor remedy with respect to amounts standing to the credit of the Escrow Account. For the\navoidance of doubt, it is hereby acknowledged and agreed by the Escrow Bank that the monies\nand properties held by the Escrow Bank in the Escrow Account shall not be considered as part\nof the assets of the Escrow Bank and being trust property, shall in the case of bankruptcy or\nliquidation of the Escrow Bank, be wholly excluded from the assets of the Escrow Bank in such\nbankruptcy or liquidation.\n5.5\nRegulatory approvals\nThe Escrow Bank shall use its best efforts to procure, and thereafter maintain and comply with,\nall regulatory approvals required for it to establish and operate the Escrow Account. The Escrow\nBank represents and warrants that it is not aware of any reason why such regulatory approvals\nwill not ordinarily be granted to the Escrow Bank.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0811",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 811,
    "page_start": 173,
    "page_end": 173,
    "char_start": 366543,
    "char_end": 366847,
    "char_count": 304,
    "text": "6. ESCROW DEFAULT\n6.1\nEscrow Default\n6.1.1 Following events shall constitute an event of default by the Concessionaire (an “Escrow\nDefault”) unless such event of default has occurred as a result of Force Majeure or any act or\nomission of the Concessioning Authority or the Senior Lenders' Representative:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0812",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 812,
    "page_start": 173,
    "page_end": 173,
    "char_start": 366848,
    "char_end": 366985,
    "char_count": 137,
    "text": "(a) the Concessionaire commits breach of this Agreement by failing to deposit /cause the\ndeposit of any receipts into the Escrow Account;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0813",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 813,
    "page_start": 174,
    "page_end": 174,
    "char_start": 366987,
    "char_end": 366990,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "170",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0814",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 814,
    "page_start": 174,
    "page_end": 174,
    "char_start": 366992,
    "char_end": 367077,
    "char_count": 85,
    "text": "(b) the Concessionaire causes the Escrow Bank to transfer funds to any account of the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0815",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 815,
    "page_start": 174,
    "page_end": 174,
    "char_start": 367078,
    "char_end": 367394,
    "char_count": 316,
    "text": "(c) Concessionaire in breach of the terms of this Agreement; or the Concessionaire commits or\ncauses any other breach of the provisions of this Agreement.\n6.1.2 Upon occurrence of an Escrow Default, the consequences thereof shall be dealt with\nunder and in accordance with the provisions of the Concession Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0816",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 816,
    "page_start": 174,
    "page_end": 174,
    "char_start": 367395,
    "char_end": 369145,
    "char_count": 1750,
    "text": "7. TERMINATION OF ESCROW AGREEMENT\n7.1\nDuration of the Escrow Agreement\nThis Agreement shall remain in full force and effect so long as any sum remains to be advanced\nor is outstanding from the Concessionaire in respect of the debt, guarantee or financial\nassistance received by it from the Senior Lenders, or any of its obligations to the Concessioning\nAuthority remain to be discharged, unless terminated earlier by consent of all the Parties or\notherwise in accordance with the provisions of this Agreement.\n7.2\nSubstitution of Escrow Bank\nThe Concessionaire may, by not less than 45 (forty five) Days prior notice to the Escrow Bank,\nthe Concessioning Authority and the Senior Lenders' Representative, terminate this Agreement\nand appoint a new Escrow Bank, provided that the new Escrow Bank is acceptable to the\nSenior Lenders' Representative and arrangements are made satisfactory to the Senior Lenders'\nRepresentative for transfer of amounts deposited in the Escrow Account to a new Escrow\nAccount established with the successor Escrow Bank. The termination of this Agreement shall\ntake effect only upon coming into force of an Escrow Agreement with the substitute Escrow\nBank.\n7.3\nClosure of Escrow Account\nThe Escrow Bank shall, at the request of the Concessionaire and the Senior Lenders'\nRepresentative made on or after the payment by the Concessionaire of all outstanding amounts\nunder the Concession Agreement and the Financing Documents including the payments\nspecified in Article 4.2, and upon confirmation' of receipt of such payments, close the Escrow\nAccount and pay any amount standing to the credit thereof to the Concessionaire. Upon closure\nof the Escrow Account hereunder, the Escrow Agreement shall be deemed to be terminated.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0817",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 817,
    "page_start": 174,
    "page_end": 174,
    "char_start": 369146,
    "char_end": 370036,
    "char_count": 890,
    "text": "8. SUPPLEMENTARY ESCROW AGREEMENT\n8.1\nSupplementary Escrow Agreement\nThe Senior Lenders' Representative and the Concessionaire shall be entitled to enter into a\nsupplementary escrow agreement with the Escrow Bank providing, inter alia, for detailed\nprocedures and documentation for withdrawals from Escrow Account, creation of sub-accounts\npursuant to Clause 4.1.1 and for matters not covered under this Agreement such as the rights\nand obligations of Senior Lenders, investment of surplus funds, restrictions on withdrawals by\nthe Concessionaire in the event of breach of Financing Documents, procedures relating to\noperation of the Escrow Account and withdrawal therefrom, reporting requirements and any\nmatters incidental thereto; provided that such supplementary escrow agreement shall not\ncontain any provision which is inconsistent with this Agreement and in the event of any conflict",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0818",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 818,
    "page_start": 175,
    "page_end": 175,
    "char_start": 370038,
    "char_end": 370041,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "171",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0819",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 819,
    "page_start": 175,
    "page_end": 175,
    "char_start": 370043,
    "char_end": 370185,
    "char_count": 142,
    "text": "or inconsistency between provisions of this Agreement and such supplementary escrow\nagreement, the provisions of this Agreement shall prevail.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0820",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 820,
    "page_start": 175,
    "page_end": 175,
    "char_start": 370186,
    "char_end": 371915,
    "char_count": 1729,
    "text": "9. INDEMNITY\n9.1\nGeneral indemnity\n9.1.1 The Concessionaire will indemnify, defend and hold the Concessioning Authority, Escrow\nBank and the Senior Lenders, acting through the Senior Lenders' Representative, harmless\nagainst any and all proceedings, actions and third party claims for any loss, damage, cost and\nexpense arising out of any breach by the Concessionaire of any of its obligations under this\nAgreement or on account of failure of the Concessionaire to comply with Applicable Laws and\nApplicable Permits.\n9.1.2  The Concessioning Authority will indemnify, defend and hold the, Concessionaire\nharmless against any and all proceedings, actions and third party claims for any loss, damage,\ncost and expense arising out of failure of the Concessioning Authority to fulfill any of its\nobligations under this Agreement materially and adversely affecting the performance of the\nConcessionaire's obligations under the Concession Agreement or this Agreement other than\nany loss, damage, cost and expense arising out of acts done in discharge of their lawful\nfunctions by the Concessioning Authority, its officers, servants and agents.\n9.1.3 The Escrow Bank will indemnify, defend and hold the Concessionaire harmless against\nany and all proceedings, actions and third party claims for any loss, damage, cost and expense\narising out of failure of the Escrow Bank to fulfill its obligations under this Agreement materially\nand adversely affecting the performance of the Concessionaire's obligations under the\nConcession Agreement other than any loss, damage, cost and expense, arising out of acts\ndone in discharge of their lawful functions by the Escrow Bank, its officers, servants and agents.\n9.2\nNotice and contest of claims",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0821",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 821,
    "page_start": 175,
    "page_end": 175,
    "char_start": 371916,
    "char_end": 372858,
    "char_count": 942,
    "text": "In the event that any Party hereto receives a claim from a third party in respect of which it is\nentitled to the benefit of an indemnity under Clause 9.1 or in respect of which it is entitled to\nreimbursement (the “Indemnified Party”), it shall notify the other Party responsible for\nindemnifying such claim hereunder (the “Indemnifying Party”) within 15 (fifteen) Days of\nreceipt of the claim and shall not settle or pay the claim without the prior approval of the\nIndemnifying Party, which approval shall not be unreasonably withheld or delayed. In the event\nthat the Indemnifying Party wishes to contest or dispute the claim, it may conduct the\nproceedings in the name of the Indemnified Party and shall bear all costs involved in contesting\nthe same. The Indemnified Party shall provide all cooperation and assistance in contesting any\nclaim and shall sign all such writings and documents as the Indemnifying Party may reasonably\nrequire.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0822",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 822,
    "page_start": 175,
    "page_end": 175,
    "char_start": 372859,
    "char_end": 373136,
    "char_count": 277,
    "text": "10. MISCELLANEOUS PROVISIONS\n10.1 Governing law and jurisdiction\nThis Agreement shall be construed and interpreted in accordance with and governed by the\nlaws of India, and the Courts at [●] shall have jurisdiction over all matters arising out of or\nrelating to this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0823",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 823,
    "page_start": 176,
    "page_end": 176,
    "char_start": 373138,
    "char_end": 373141,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "172",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0824",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 824,
    "page_start": 176,
    "page_end": 176,
    "char_start": 373143,
    "char_end": 373237,
    "char_count": 94,
    "text": "10.2 Waiver of sovereign immunity\nThe Concessioning Authority unconditionally and irrevocably:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0825",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 825,
    "page_start": 176,
    "page_end": 176,
    "char_start": 373238,
    "char_end": 373387,
    "char_count": 149,
    "text": "(a) agrees that the execution, delivery and performance by it of this Agreement constitute\ncommercial acts done and performed for commercial purpose;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0826",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 826,
    "page_start": 176,
    "page_end": 176,
    "char_start": 373388,
    "char_end": 373760,
    "char_count": 372,
    "text": "(b) agrees that, should any proceedings be brought against it or its assets, property or revenues\nin any jurisdiction in relation to this Agreement or any transaction contemplated by this\nAgreement, no immunity (whether by reason of sovereignty or otherwise) from such\nproceedings shall be claimed by or on behalf of the Concessioning Authority with respect to\nits assets;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0827",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 827,
    "page_start": 176,
    "page_end": 176,
    "char_start": 373761,
    "char_end": 373931,
    "char_count": 170,
    "text": "(c) waives any right of immunity which it or its assets, property or revenues now has, may\nacquire in the future or which may be attributed to it in any jurisdiction; and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0828",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 828,
    "page_start": 176,
    "page_end": 176,
    "char_start": 373932,
    "char_end": 374970,
    "char_count": 1038,
    "text": "(d) consents generally in respect of the enforcement of any judgement or award against it in\nany such proceedings to the giving of any relief or the issue of any process in any\njurisdiction in connection with such proceedings (including the making, enforcement or\nexecution against it or in respect of any assets, property or revenues whatsoever\nirrespective of their use or intended use of any order or judgement that may be made or\ngiven in connection therewith).\n10.3 Priority of agreements\nIn the event of any conflict between the Concession Agreement and this Agreement, the\nprovisions contained in the Concession Agreement shall prevail over this Agreement.\n10.4 Alteration of terms\nAll additions, amendments, modifications and variations to this Agreement shall be effectual and\nbinding only if in writing and signed by the duly authorised representatives of the Parties.\n10.5 Waiver\n10.5.1 Waiver by any Party of a default by another Party in the observance and performance of\nany provision of or obligations under this Agreement:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0829",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 829,
    "page_start": 176,
    "page_end": 176,
    "char_start": 374971,
    "char_end": 375238,
    "char_count": 267,
    "text": "(a) shall not operate or be construed as a waiver of any other or subsequent default hereof or of\nother provisions of or obligations under this Agreement shall not be effective unless it is in\nwriting and executed by a duly authorised representative of the Party; and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0830",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 830,
    "page_start": 176,
    "page_end": 176,
    "char_start": 375239,
    "char_end": 375851,
    "char_count": 612,
    "text": "(b) shall not affect the validity or enforceability of this Agreement in any manner.\n10.5.2 Neither the failure by any Party to insist on any occasion upon the performance of the\nterms, conditions and provisions of this Agreement or any obligation thereunder nor time or\nother indulgence granted by any Party to another Party shall be treated or deemed as waiver of\nsuch breach or acceptance of any variation or the relinquishment of any such right hereunder.\n10.6 No third-party beneficiaries\nThis Agreement is solely for the benefit of the Parties and no other person or entity shall have\nany rights hereunder.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0831",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 831,
