  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0969",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 969,
    "page_start": 196,
    "page_end": 196,
    "char_start": 397522,
    "char_end": 398146,
    "char_count": 624,
    "text": "Performance Evaluation and calculation of liquidated damages:\nAny shortfall in performance as per above KPIs shall be documented by the Concessionaire\nwith adequate supporting documentations and presented to the Concessioning Authority along\nwith the quarterly performance reports submitted as per provisions set out in Appendix-14.\nSubject to any waivers as per Clause 7.3 (b), the Concessioning Authority shall be liable to pay\nliquidated damage determined at the rate of [0.5% of the Royalty of the respective quarter for\nevery shortfall of 10%] in the average performance which shall be assessed in the following\nmanner.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0970",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 970,
    "page_start": 197,
    "page_end": 197,
    "char_start": 398148,
    "char_end": 398151,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "193",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0971",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 971,
    "page_start": 197,
    "page_end": 197,
    "char_start": 398153,
    "char_end": 398988,
    "char_count": 835,
    "text": "Each Performance Standard is calculated as an average in the manner indicated above. The\nactual average performance vis-à-vis a standard will be evaluated against the prescribed\nstandard. The shortfall will be computed as a percentage of the prescribed standard. The\nshortfall in respect of each performance standard will have a weightage assigned to it. The\noverall shortfall in average performance shall be assessed as the aggregate of the weighted\nshortfalls in respect of each of the performance standards. For example, if there is a shortfall in\nPilotage services by x%, Rail turnaround time by y% and vessel berthing time for\ninward/outward movement of vessel by z% and the weightage assigned to such shortfalls is 0.7,\n0.2 and 0.1 respectively, then the overall shortfall in average performance will be (0.7x + 0.2 y +\n0.1 z) %.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0972",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 972,
    "page_start": 198,
    "page_end": 198,
    "char_start": 398990,
    "char_end": 398993,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "194",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0973",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 973,
    "page_start": 198,
    "page_end": 198,
    "char_start": 398995,
    "char_end": 399689,
    "char_count": 694,
    "text": "APPENDIX 19\nSupporting Project Infrastructure\nBelow is the list of supporting infrastructure to be provided by Concessioning\nAuthority and the timelines for completing the supporting infrastructure.\nS. No.\nSupporting infrastructure\nTimeline of\ncompletion\n1\nAccess Channels - Dredging of entrance channel to\n[m] and draft alongside berth to [ m]\n[COD +] [x] years\n2\n4 lane/6 lane connectivity to Highway outside port\n[COD +] [x] years\n3\nRailway connectivity to common rail facility\n[COD +] [x] years\n4\nProtective works including breakwaters, shore\nprotection;\n[COD +] [x] years\n5\n[Any other]\n[COD +] [x] years\nx- To be mentioned by authority for specific project\nCOD - Commercial Operations Date",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-0974",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 974,
    "page_start": 198,
    "page_end": 198,
    "char_start": 399691,
    "char_end": 399963,
    "char_count": 272,
    "text": "The mentioned infrastructure would need to be specified depending on the commitments made\nby the Concessioning Authority at the time of bidding of the specific Project. The supporting\nInfrastructure to be part of obligations of Authority during construction and O&M phase.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
