    "paragraph_index": 1034,
    "page_start": 221,
    "page_end": 221,
    "char_start": 430876,
    "char_end": 430999,
    "char_count": 123,
    "text": "(a) Allow any party, upon such terms of as to costs and otherwise) as it shall determine, to\namend claims or counterclaims;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-1035",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 1035,
    "page_start": 221,
    "page_end": 221,
    "char_start": 431000,
    "char_end": 431151,
    "char_count": 151,
    "text": "(b) Extend or abbreviate any time limits provided by these Rules;\n(c) Conduct such enquires as may appear to the Tribunal to be necessary or expedient;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-1036",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 1036,
    "page_start": 221,
    "page_end": 221,
    "char_start": 431152,
    "char_end": 431460,
    "char_count": 308,
    "text": "(d) Order the parties to make any property or thing available for inspection\n(e) Order any parties to produce to the tribunal, and to other parties for inspection, and to\nsupply copies of any documents, or classes of documents in their possession, custody, or\npower which the Tribunal determines to relevant.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-1037",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 1037,
    "page_start": 221,
    "page_end": 221,
    "char_start": 431461,
    "char_end": 431633,
    "char_count": 172,
    "text": "(f) Make orders or give directions to any party for interrogatories;\n(g) Make orders or give directions to any party for an interim injunction or any other interim\nmeasure;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-1038",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 1038,
    "page_start": 221,
    "page_end": 221,
    "char_start": 431634,
    "char_end": 433077,
    "char_count": 1443,
    "text": "(h) Make such orders or give such directions as it deems fit in so far as they are not inconsistent\nwith the Act or any statutory re-enactment thereof or such law which is applicable or these\nRules.\n34.2 If the parties so agree, the Tribunal shall also have the power to add other parties (with\ntheir consent) to be joined in the arbitration and make a single Final Award determining all\ndisputes between them.\nRule 35- Deposits to Costs and Expenses\n35.1 The Tribunal's fees and SAROD-PORTS administration fees shall be ascertained in\naccordance with the Schedule of Fees in Force at the time of commencement of the arbitration.\n35.2 The Claimant shall deposit with the SAROD-PORTS half of the fees payable at the time of\nfiling of the Statement of Case. The Respondent shall deposit with the SAROD-PORTS one-half\nof the fees payable at the time of filing the Statement of Respondent's Defense and\nCounterclaim (if any). The balance of fees payable shall be paid 60 days before the date of the\nfinal hearing or on such other date that the Secretary may direct.\n35.3 Where the amount of the claim or the counterclaim is not quantifiable at the time payment\nis due, the Secretary will make a provisional estimate. The fees will be adjusted in the light of\nsuch information as may subsequently become available. If the arbitration is settled or disposed\nof without a hearing, the amount of the Tribunal's fees and SAROD-PORTS administration fees",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-1039",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 1039,
    "page_start": 222,
    "page_end": 222,
    "char_start": 433079,
    "char_end": 433082,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "218",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC076-1040",
    "doc_id": "DOC-076",
    "paragraph_index": 1040,
    "page_start": 222,
    "page_end": 222,
    "char_start": 433084,
    "char_end": 434867,
    "char_count": 1783,
    "text": "shall be finally determined by the Secretary who will have regard to all the circumstances of the\ncase, including the stage of proceedings at which the arbitration is settled or otherwise disposed\nof\n35.4 The Secretary may from time to time direct parties to make one or more deposit(s) towards\nany further expenses incurred or to be incurred on behalf of or for the benefit of the parties.\n35.5 All deposit(s) shall be made to and held by the SAROD-PORTS. Any interest which may\naccrue on such deposit(s) shall be retained by the SAROD-PORTS.\n35.6 If a party fails to make the payments or deposits required or directed, the Tribunal may\nrefuse to hear the claims or counterclaims, whichever is applicable, by the non• complying party,\nalthough it may proceed to determine claims or counterclaims by any party who has complied\nwith orders\n35.7 The parties shall remain jointly and severally liable to the SAROD-PORTS for payment of\nall such fees and expenses until they have been paid in full even if the arbitration is abandoned,\nsuspended or concluded, by agreement or otherwise, before the final Award is made.\nRule 36 - Decision Making by the Tribunal\n36.1 Where a Tribunal has been appointed, any direction, order, decision or award of the\nTribunal must be made by the whole Tribunal or a majority. If an arbitrator refuses or fails to\nsign the Award, the signatures of the majority shall be sufficient, provided that the reason for the\nomitted signature is stated.\n36.2 If there is no unanimity, the same shall be made by the majority arbitrators as well as by\nthe dissenting arbitrator alone as if acting as a sole arbitrator.\n36.3 However, in case of a three-member Tribunal the presiding arbitrators may after consulting\nthe other arbitrators, make procedural rulings alone.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
