    "char_end": 72474,
    "char_count": 101,
    "text": "Draft for discussion purposes only\n34\n\nARTICLE 9\nUTILITIES AND TREES\n9.1\nExisting utilities and roads",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0222",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 222,
    "page_start": 45,
    "page_end": 45,
    "char_start": 72476,
    "char_end": 72942,
    "char_count": 466,
    "text": "Notwithstanding anything to the contrary contained herein, the Contractor shall ensure\nthat the respective entities owning the existing roads, right of way, level crossings,\nstructures, or utilities on, under or above the Site are enabled by it to keep them in\ncontinuous satisfactory use, if necessary, by providing suitable temporary diversions\nwith the authority of the controlling body of that road, right of way or utility.\n9.2\nShifting of obstructing utilities",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0223",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 223,
    "page_start": 45,
    "page_end": 45,
    "char_start": 72944,
    "char_end": 74729,
    "char_count": 1785,
    "text": "The Contractor shall, in accordance with Applicable Laws and with assistance of the\nAuthority, cause shifting of any utility (including electric lines, water pipes and\ntelephone cables) to an appropriate location or alignment, if such utility or obstruction\nadversely affects the execution of Works in accordance with this Agreement. The actual\ncost of such shifting, as approved and communicated by the entity owning the utility,\nshall be paid by the Contractor and reimbursed by the Authority to the Contractor. In\nthe event of any delay in such shifting by the entity owning the utility beyond a period\nof 180 (one hundred and eighty) days from the date of notice by the Contractor to the\nentity owning the utility and to the Authority, the Contractor shall be entitled to\nDamages in a sum calculated in accordance with the formula specified in Clause 8.3.1\nfor the period of delay, and to Time Extension in accordance with Clause 10.4 for and\nin respect of the part(s) of the Works affected by such delay; provided that if the delays\ninvolve any time overlaps, the overlaps shall not be additive.\n9.3\nNew utilities\n9.3.1 The Contractor shall allow, subject to such conditions as the Authority may specify,\naccess to, and use of the Site for laying telephone lines, water pipes, electric cables or\nother public utilities. Where such access or use causes any financial loss to the\nContractor, it may require the user of the Site to pay compensation or damages as per\nApplicable Laws. For the avoidance of doubt, it is agreed that use of the Site under this\nClause 9.3 shall not in any manner relieve the Contractor of its obligation to construct\nthe Project in accordance with this Agreement and any damage caused by such use shall\nbe restored forthwith at the cost of the Authority.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0224",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 224,
    "page_start": 45,
    "page_end": 45,
    "char_start": 74730,
    "char_end": 75546,
    "char_count": 816,
