    "char_start": 246375,
    "char_end": 246672,
    "char_count": 297,
    "text": "shall have the authority to bind the Contractor and each member of the Consortium; and shall\nbe deemed to be the Contractor for the purposes of this Agreement;}$\n“Major Bridge” means a bridge having a linear waterway of 18 metres or more or which has\na clear opening of 12 metres or more in spans;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0425",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 425,
    "page_start": 121,
    "page_end": 121,
    "char_start": 246674,
    "char_end": 247407,
    "char_count": 733,
    "text": "“Manuals” shall mean the manuals as specified in Schedule D\n“Material Adverse Effect” means a material adverse effect of any act or event on the ability\nof either Party to perform any of its obligations under and in accordance with the provisions of\nthis Agreement and which act or event causes a material financial burden or loss to either Party;\n“Materials” are all the supplies used by the Contractor for incorporation in the Works of the\nProject;\n“Non-Political Event” shall have the meaning as set forth in Clause 19.2;\n“Parties” means the parties to this Agreement collectively and “Party” shall mean any of the\nparties to this Agreement individually;\n“Performance Security” shall have the meaning as set forth in Clause 7.1.1;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0426",
