    "page_end": 135,
    "char_start": 258913,
    "char_end": 259027,
    "char_count": 114,
    "text": "10 May be omitted or substituted to reflect project-specific requirements.\n\nDraft for discussion purposes only\n124",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0459",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 459,
    "page_start": 135,
    "page_end": 135,
    "char_start": 259029,
    "char_end": 259198,
    "char_count": 169,
    "text": "Annex - IV\n(Schedule-A)\nEnvironmental Clearances\nThe following environment clearances have been obtained:\n[***]\nThe following environment clearances are awaited:\n[***]\n_",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0460",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 460,
    "page_start": 136,
    "page_end": 136,
    "char_start": 259200,
    "char_end": 259493,
    "char_count": 293,
    "text": "Draft for discussion purposes only\n125\n\nSCHEDULE - B\n(See Clause 2.1)\nDEVELOPMENT OF THE PROJECT\n1\nDevelopment of the Project\nDevelopment of the Project shall include design and construction of the Project as\ndescribed in this Schedule-B and in Schedule-C.\n[2\nRehabilitation and augmentation11",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0461",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 461,
    "page_start": 136,
    "page_end": 136,
    "char_start": 259495,
    "char_end": 259812,
    "char_count": 317,
    "text": "Rehabilitation and augmentation shall include Two-Laning and strengthening of the\nProject as described in Annex-I of this Schedule-B and in Schedule-C.]\n3\nSpecifications and Standards\nThe Project shall be designed and constructed in conformity with the Specifications and\nStandards specified in Annex-I of Schedule-D.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0462",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 462,
    "page_start": 136,
    "page_end": 137,
    "char_start": 259814,
    "char_end": 259928,
    "char_count": 114,
    "text": "11 May be omitted or substituted to reflect project-specific requirements.\n\nDraft for discussion purposes only\n126",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0463",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 463,
    "page_start": 137,
    "page_end": 137,
    "char_start": 259930,
    "char_end": 261379,
    "char_count": 1449,
    "text": "Annex - I\n(Schedule-B)\nDescription of the Project12\n[Note: Description of the Project shall be given by the Authority in detail together with\nexplanatory drawings (where necessary) to explain the Authority’s requirements precisely in\norder to avoid subsequent changes in the Scope of the Project. The particulars that must be\nspecified in this Schedule-B are listed below as per the requirements of the Manual of\nStandards and Specifications for Two Laning of Highways (IRC:SP:73-2007), referred to as\nthe Manual. If any standards, specifications or details are not given in the Manual, the\nminimum design/construction requirements shall be specified in this Schedule. In addition to\nthese particulars, all other essential project-specific details, as required, should be provided\nin order to define the Scope of the Project clearly and precisely.]\n1\nWIDENING OF THE EXISTING HIGHWAY\n1.1\nThe Highway shall follow the existing alignment unless otherwise specified by the\nAuthority and shown in the alignment plans specified in Annex III of Schedule-A.\nGeometric deficiencies, if any, in the existing horizontal and vertical profiles shall be\ncorrected as per the prescribed standards for plain and rolling terrain to the extent land\nis available.\n1.2\nWIDTH OF CARRIAGEWAY\n1.2.1 Two-Laning without paved shoulders shall be undertaken. The paved carriageway shall\nbe 7 (seven) m wide in accordance with the typical cross section drawings in the\nManual.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0464",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 464,
    "page_start": 137,
    "page_end": 137,
    "char_start": 261381,
    "char_end": 261675,
    "char_count": 294,
    "text": "Provided that in the built-up areas (refer to paragraphs 2.1 (ii) (a) of the Manual and\nprovide necessary details): the width of the carriageway shall be as specified in the\nfollowing table:\nS. No.\nBuilt-up\nsection\n(Township)\nLocation\n(km to km)\nWidth\n(m)\nTypical cross\nsection (Ref. to\nManual)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0465",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 465,
    "page_start": 137,
    "page_end": 137,
    "char_start": 261677,
    "char_end": 261884,
    "char_count": 207,
    "text": "1.2.2 Except as otherwise provided in this Agreement, the width of the paved carriageway\nand cross-sectional features shall conform to paragraph 1.1 above.\n2\nGEOMETRIC DESIGN AND GENERAL FEATURES\n2.1\nGeneral",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0466",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 466,
    "page_start": 137,
    "page_end": 137,
    "char_start": 261886,
    "char_end": 261992,
    "char_count": 106,
    "text": "12 This template is applicable to highway projects. It may be suitably modified in case of other projects.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0467",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 467,
    "page_start": 138,
    "page_end": 138,
    "char_start": 261994,
    "char_end": 262156,
    "char_count": 162,
    "text": "Draft for discussion purposes only\n127\n\nGeometric design and general features of the Highway shall be in accordance with\nSection 2 of the Manual.\n2.2\nDesign speed",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0468",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 468,
    "page_start": 138,
    "page_end": 138,
    "char_start": 262158,
    "char_end": 262354,
    "char_count": 196,
    "text": "The design speed shall be the minimum design speed of 80 km per hr for plain terrain.\n2.3\nImprovement of the existing road geometrics\n[Refer to paragraph 2.1 (v) of the Manual and provide details]",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0469",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 469,
    "page_start": 138,
    "page_end": 138,
    "char_start": 262356,
    "char_end": 262696,
    "char_count": 340,
    "text": "In the following sections, where improvement of the existing road geometrics to the\nprescribed standards is not possible, the existing road geometrics shall be improved to\nthe extent possible within the given right of way and proper road signs and safety\nmeasures shall be provided:\nS. No.\nSection\n(from km to\nkm)\nType of\ndeficiency\nRemarks",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0470",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 470,
    "page_start": 138,
    "page_end": 138,
    "char_start": 262698,
    "char_end": 263088,
    "char_count": 390,
    "text": "2.4\nRight of Way\n[Refer to paragraph 2.3 of the Manual]. Details of the Right of Way are given in Annex\nII of Schedule-A.\n2.5\nType of shoulders\n[Refer to paragraph 2.5.2 of the Manual and specify]\n(a)\nIn built-up sections, footpaths/fully paved shoulders shall be provided in the following\nsections:\nS. No.\nSection\n(from km to km)\nFully paved\nshoulders/\nfootpaths\nReference to cross\nsection",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0471",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 471,
    "page_start": 138,
    "page_end": 138,
    "char_start": 263090,
    "char_end": 263612,
    "char_count": 522,
    "text": "(b)\nIn open country, [paved shoulders of 1.5 m width shall be provided and balance 1.0 m\nwidth shall be covered with 150 mm thick compacted layer of granular material].\n(c)\nDesign and specifications of paved shoulders and granular material shall conform to\nthe requirements specified in paragraphs 5.9.9 and 5.9.10 of the Manual.\n2.6\nLateral and vertical clearances at underpasses\n2.6.1 Lateral and vertical clearances at underpasses and provision of guardrails/crash barriers\nshall be as per paragraph 2.11 of the Manual.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0472",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 472,
    "page_start": 139,
    "page_end": 139,
    "char_start": 263614,
    "char_end": 263811,
    "char_count": 197,
    "text": "Draft for discussion purposes only\n128\n\n2.6.2 Lateral clearance: The width of the opening at the underpasses shall be as follows:\nS. No.\nLocation\n(chainage)\n(from km to\nkm)\nSpan/opening (m)\nRemarks",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0473",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 473,
    "page_start": 139,
    "page_end": 139,
    "char_start": 263813,
    "char_end": 264118,
    "char_count": 305,
    "text": "2.7\nLateral and vertical clearances at overpasses\n2.7.1 Lateral and vertical clearances at overpasses shall be as per paragraph 2.12 of the\nManual.\n2.7.2 Lateral clearance: The width of the opening at the overpasses shall be as follows:\nSl. No.\nLocation\n(chainage)\n(from km to\nkm)\nSpan/opening\n(m)\nRemarks",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0474",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 474,
    "page_start": 139,
    "page_end": 139,
    "char_start": 264120,
    "char_end": 264421,
    "char_count": 301,
    "text": "2.8\nService roads\n\nService roads shall be constructed at the locations and for the lengths indicated below:\n[Refer to paragraph 2.13 of the Manual and provide details]\nS.No.\nLocation of service\nroad\n(from km to km)\nRight hand side\n(RHS)/Left hand side\n(LHS)/ or Both sides\nLength  of\nservice road\n(km)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0475",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 475,
    "page_start": 139,
    "page_end": 139,
    "char_start": 264423,
    "char_end": 264752,
    "char_count": 329,
    "text": "2.9\nGrade separated structures\n2.9.1 Grade separated structures shall be provided as per paragraph 2.14 of the Manual. The\nrequisite particulars are given below:\n[Refer to paragraphs 2.14.1 of the Manual and provide details]\nS. No.\nLocation of\nstructure\nLength (m)\nNumber\nand\nlength of\nspans (m)\nApproach\ngradient\nRemarks,\nif any",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0476",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 476,
    "page_start": 140,
    "page_end": 140,
    "char_start": 264754,
    "char_end": 265249,
    "char_count": 495,
    "text": "Draft for discussion purposes only\n129\n\n2.9.2 In the case of grade separated structures, the type of structure and the level of the\nHighway and the cross roads shall be as follows: [Refer to paragraphs 2.14.2 of the\nManual and specify the type of vehicular under pass/ overpass structure and whether\nthe cross road is to be carried at the existing level, raised or lowered]\nS.No. No.\nLocation\nType of\nstructure\n&\nLength\n(m)\nCross road at\nRemarks,\nif\nany\nExisting\nLevel\nRaised\nLevel\nLowered\nLevel",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0477",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 477,
    "page_start": 140,
    "page_end": 140,
    "char_start": 265251,
    "char_end": 265521,
    "char_count": 270,
    "text": "2.10\nCattle and pedestrian underpass /overpass\nCattle and pedestrian underpass/ overpass shall be constructed as follows: [Refer to\nparagraph 2.14.3 of the Manual and specify the requirements of cattle and pedestrian\nunderpass/ overpass]\nS. No.\nLocation\nType of crossing",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0478",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 478,
    "page_start": 140,
    "page_end": 140,
    "char_start": 265523,
    "char_end": 265675,
    "char_count": 152,
    "text": "2.11\nTypical cross-sections of the Highway\n\n[Give typical cross-sections of the Highway by reference to the Manual]\n3\nINTERSECTIONS AND GRADE SEPARATORS",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0479",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 479,
    "page_start": 140,
    "page_end": 140,
    "char_start": 265677,
    "char_end": 265846,
    "char_count": 169,
    "text": "All intersections and grade separators shall be as per section 3 of the Manual. Existing\nintersections which are deficient shall be improved to the prescribed standards.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0480",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 480,
    "page_start": 140,
    "page_end": 140,
    "char_start": 265848,
    "char_end": 266220,
    "char_count": 372,
    "text": "[Refer to paragraphs 3.1.1, 3.1.2 and 3.3 of the Manual and specify the requirements.\nExplain where necessary with drawings/sketches/general arrangement]\nProperly designed intersections shall be provided at the locations and of the types and\nfeatures given in the tables below:\n(a)\nAt-grade intersections\nS. No.\nLocation of\nintersection\nType of\nintersection\nOther features",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0481",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 481,
    "page_start": 141,
    "page_end": 141,
    "char_start": 266222,
    "char_end": 266436,
    "char_count": 214,
    "text": "Draft for discussion purposes only\n130\n\n(b)\nGrade separated intersection with/without ramps\nS. No.\nLocation\nSalient\nfeatures\nMinimum\nlength of\nviaduct to be\nprovided (m)\nRoad to be\ncarried\nover/under the\nstructures",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0482",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 482,
    "page_start": 141,
    "page_end": 141,
    "char_start": 266438,
    "char_end": 267058,
    "char_count": 620,
    "text": "4\nROAD EMBANKMENT AND CUT SECTION\n4.1\nWidening and improvement of the existing road embankment/cuttings and construction\nof new road embankment/ cuttings shall conform to the Specifications and Standards\ngiven in section 4 of the Manual and the specified cross sectional details. Deficiencies\nin the plan and profile of the existing road shall be corrected.\n4.2\nRaising of the existing road [Refer to paragraph 4.2.2 of the Manual and specify the\nsections to be raised]\nThe existing road shall be raised in the following sections:\nS. No.\nSection\n(from km to km)\nLength (km)\nExtent of raising\n[Top of finished road\nlevel]",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0483",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 483,
    "page_start": 141,
    "page_end": 141,
    "char_start": 267060,
    "char_end": 267663,
    "char_count": 603,
    "text": "5\nPAVEMENT DESIGN\n5.1\nPavement design shall be carried out in accordance with section 5 of the Manual.\n5.2\nType of pavement\n[Refer to paragraph 5.1 of the Manual and state specific requirement, if any, of\nproviding cement concrete pavement.]\n5.3\nDesign requirements\n[Refer to paragraphs 5.4, 5.9 and 5.10 of the Manual and specify design requirements\nand strategy]\n5.3.1 Design Period and strategy\nFlexible pavement for new pavement or for widening and strengthening of the existing\npavement shall be designed for a minimum design period of 15 (fifteen) years. Stage\nconstruction shall not be permitted.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0484",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 484,
    "page_start": 142,
    "page_end": 142,
    "char_start": 267665,
    "char_end": 267934,
    "char_count": 269,
    "text": "Draft for discussion purposes only\n131\n\n5.3.2 Design Traffic\n\nNotwithstanding anything to the contrary contained in this Agreement or the Manual,\nthe Contractor shall design the pavement for a design traffic of *** million standard\naxles.\n5.4\nReconstruction of sections",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC079-0485",
    "doc_id": "DOC-079",
    "paragraph_index": 485,
