  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0873",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 873,
    "page_start": 319,
    "page_end": 319,
    "char_start": 495108,
    "char_end": 495124,
    "char_count": 16,
    "text": "287\nSCHEDULE - S",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0874",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 874,
    "page_start": 319,
    "page_end": 319,
    "char_start": 495126,
    "char_end": 495164,
    "char_count": 38,
    "text": "Procedure for Dispute Resolution Board",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0875",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 875,
    "page_start": 319,
    "page_end": 319,
    "char_start": 495166,
    "char_end": 496205,
    "char_count": 1039,
    "text": "The parties to the Contract Agreement mutually agree as follows:\n\n1.\nThe Board shall comprise of three Members having experience in the field of\nconstruction or have been involved in the Works related to construction and with\nthe interpretation of contractual documents. One Member shall be selected by each\nof the Authority and the Contractor from the list maintained by NHAI hosted on its\nwebsite (www.nhai.gov.in). In the event the parties fail to select the member within\n28 days of the date of the signing of Contract agreement, in that eventuality, upon\nthe request of either or both parties such Member shall be selected by SAROD\nwithin 14 days. The third Member shall be selected by the other two members from\nthe same list. If the two Members selected by or on behalf of the parties fail to\nselect the third Member within 14 days after the later of their selections, then upon\nthe request of either or both parties such third Member shall be selected by SAROD\nwithin 14 days. The third Member shall serve as Chairman of the Board.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0876",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 876,
    "page_start": 319,
    "page_end": 319,
    "char_start": 496208,
    "char_end": 496469,
    "char_count": 261,
    "text": "2.\nThe Board shall be constituted when each of the three Board Members has signed a\nBoard Member's declaration of Acceptance as required by the DRB's rules and\nprocedures (which, along with the declaration of acceptance form, are attached as\nAnnexure herewith).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0877",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 877,
    "page_start": 319,
    "page_end": 319,
    "char_start": 496471,
    "char_end": 497586,
    "char_count": 1115,
    "text": "3.\nIn the event of death, disability, or resignation of any Member, such Member\nshall be replaced in the same manner as the Member being replaced was selected. If\nfor any other reason, a Member fails or is unable to serve, the Chairman (or failing\nthe action of the Chairman then either of the other Members) shall inform the\nParties and such non-serving Member shall be replaced in the same manner as the\nMember being replaced was selected. Any replacement made by the parties shall be\ncompleted within 28 days after the event giving rise to the vacancy on the Board,\nfailing which the replacement shall be made by SAROD in the same manner as\ndescribed above. Replacement shall be considered complete when the new Member\nsigns the Board Member's Declaration of Acceptance. Throughout any replacement\nprocess, the Members not being replaced shall continue to serve and the Board shall\ncontinue to function and its activities shall have the same force and effect as if the\nvacancy had not occurred, provided, however that the Board shall not conduct a\nhearing nor issue a decision until the replacement is completed.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0878",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 878,
    "page_start": 319,
    "page_end": 319,
    "char_start": 497588,
    "char_end": 498439,
    "char_count": 851,
    "text": "4.\nIf either the Authority or the Contractor is dissatisfied with any decision of the\nBoard, and/or if the Board fails to issue its decision within 56 days after receipt of\nall the pleadings (along with the supporting documents) of the parties by the\nChairman of the Board or any extension mutually agreed upon by the Authority and\nthe Contractor, in such a case, either the Authority or the Contractor may, within 28\ndays after his receipt of the decision, or within 28 days after the expiry of the said\nperiod, as the case may be, give notice to the other party, with a copy for\ninformation to the Authority’s Engineer, of his intention to refer the matter to the\nConciliation Committee of Independent Experts (CCIE) of the Authority for\nConciliation/amicable settlement.\nDraft No. DFA/54028\nAttachment:Annexure C- Revised Standard EPC Agreement.pdf",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0879",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 879,
    "page_start": 320,
    "page_end": 320,
    "char_start": 498441,
    "char_end": 498444,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "288",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0880",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 880,
    "page_start": 320,
    "page_end": 320,
    "char_start": 498446,
    "char_end": 498661,
    "char_count": 215,
    "text": "5.\nIt is mandatory to refer all the disputes to DRB before issuance of completion\ncertificate and satisfactory completion of punch list items. No dispute shall be\nentertained after completion of aforementioned date.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0881",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 881,
    "page_start": 320,
    "page_end": 320,
    "char_start": 498663,
    "char_end": 499227,
    "char_count": 564,
    "text": "6.\nIf the Board has issued a decision to the Authority and the Contractor within the\nsaid 56 days or any extension mutually agreed upon by the Authority and the\nContractor and no notice of intention to commence Conciliation by the Conciliation\nCommittee\nof\nIndependent\nExperts\n(CCIE)\nof\nthe\nAuthority\nfor\nConciliation/amicable settlement as to such dispute has been given by either the\nAuthority or the Contractor within 28 days after the parties received such decision\nfrom the Board, the decision shall become final and binding upon the Authority and\nContractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0882",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 882,
    "page_start": 320,
    "page_end": 320,
    "char_start": 499229,
    "char_end": 499514,
    "char_count": 285,
    "text": "7.\nWhether or not it has become final and binding upon the Authority and the\nContractor, a decision shall be admissible as evidence in any subsequent dispute\nresolution procedure, including any arbitration or litigation having any relation to\nthe dispute to which the decision relates.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0883",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 883,
    "page_start": 320,
    "page_end": 320,
    "char_start": 499516,
    "char_end": 499788,
    "char_count": 272,
    "text": "8.\nAll decision of DRB which have become final and binding or till they have been\nreversed in subsequent conciliation/Arbitration process shall be implemented by the\nparties forthwith. Such implementation shall also include any relevant action of the\nAuthority’s Engineer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0884",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 884,
    "page_start": 320,
    "page_end": 320,
    "char_start": 499790,
    "char_end": 500932,
    "char_count": 1142,
    "text": "9.\nIf during the Contract Period, the Authority and the Contractor are of the opinion\nthat the Disputes Resolution Board is not performing its functions properly, the\nAuthority and the Contractor may together disband the Disputes Resolution Board\nand reconstitute it. In that case, a new board shall be selected in accordance with\nthe provisions applying to the selection of the original Board as specified above,\nexcept that words \"within 28 days after the signing of this Contract agreement\"\nshall be replaced by the words \"within 28 days after the date on which the notice\ndisbanding the original Board became effective\".\n10.\nThe Authority and the Contractor shall jointly signed a notice specifying that the\nBoard shall stand disbanded with effect from the date specified in the notice. The\nnotice shall be posted by the email to each member of the Board. A Member shall\nbe deemed to have received the email even if he refuses to have received the same.\n11.\nAll other terms and conditions of the original Contract Agreement shall remain\nunaltered/unaffected and the parties shall remain bound by terms and conditions as\ncontained therein.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0885",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 885,
    "page_start": 320,
    "page_end": 320,
    "char_start": 500934,
    "char_end": 501011,
    "char_count": 77,
    "text": "Draft No. DFA/54028\nAttachment:Annexure C- Revised Standard EPC Agreement.pdf",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0886",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 886,
    "page_start": 321,
    "page_end": 321,
    "char_start": 501013,
    "char_end": 501293,
    "char_count": 280,
    "text": "289\nAnnexure to Schedule [S]\n\nDisputes Resolution Board's Rules and Procedures\n\n1.  Except for providing the services required hereunder, the Board Members shall not\ngive any advice to either party or to the Authority’s Engineer concerning conduct of the\nWorks. The Board Members:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0887",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 887,
    "page_start": 321,
    "page_end": 321,
    "char_start": 501295,
    "char_end": 501476,
    "char_count": 181,
    "text": "a.\nShall have no financial interest in any party to the Contract, or the Authority’s\nEngineer, or a financial interest in the contract, except for payment for services on\nthe Board.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0888",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 888,
    "page_start": 321,
    "page_end": 321,
    "char_start": 501478,
    "char_end": 501862,
    "char_count": 384,
    "text": "b.\n Shall have had no previous employment by, or financial ties to, any party to the\nContract Agreement, or the Authority’s Engineer, except for fee based consulting\nservices/advisers on other projects, and/or be Retired Government Officers (not\nconnected in whole or part with the project), all of which must be disclosed in\nwriting to both parties prior to appointment to the Board.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0889",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 889,
    "page_start": 321,
    "page_end": 321,
    "char_start": 501864,
    "char_end": 502195,
    "char_count": 331,
    "text": "c.\n Shall have disclosed in writing to both parties prior to appointment to the Board\nany and all recent or close professional or personal relationships with any director,\nofficer, or employee of any party to the Contract, or the Authority’s Engineer, and\nany and all prior involvement in the project to which the Contract relates:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0890",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 890,
    "page_start": 321,
    "page_end": 321,
    "char_start": 502197,
    "char_end": 502448,
    "char_count": 251,
    "text": "d.\nShall not, while Board member, be employed whether as a consultant or adviser\nor otherwise by either party to the Contract, or the Authority’s Engineer, except as\na Board Member, without the prior consent of the parties and the other Board\nMembers;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0891",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 891,
    "page_start": 321,
    "page_end": 321,
    "char_start": 502450,
    "char_end": 502742,
    "char_count": 292,
    "text": "e.\n Shall not, while a Board Member, engage in discussion or make any agreement\nwith any party to the Contract, or with the Authority’s Engineer, regarding\nemployment whether as a consultant or otherwise whether after the Contract is\ncompleted or after service as a Board Member is completed.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0892",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 892,
    "page_start": 321,
    "page_end": 321,
    "char_start": 502744,
    "char_end": 503086,
    "char_count": 342,
    "text": "f.\nShall remain and be impartial and independent of the parties and shall disclose in\nwriting to the Authority, the Contractor and one another any fact or circumstance\nwhich might be such as to cause either the Authority or the Contractor to question\nthe continued existence of the impartiality and independence required of Board\nMembers, and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0893",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 893,
    "page_start": 321,
    "page_end": 321,
    "char_start": 503088,
    "char_end": 503454,
    "char_count": 366,
    "text": "g.\n Shall be fluent in the language of the Contract.\n\n2. Except for its participation in the Board's activities as provided in the Contract\nAgreement and in this Agreement none of the Authority, the Contractor, and or the\nAuthority’s  Engineer shall solicit advice or consultation from the Board or the Board\nMembers on matters dealing with the conduct of the Works.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0894",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 894,
    "page_start": 321,
    "page_end": 321,
    "char_start": 503456,
    "char_end": 503480,
    "char_count": 24,
    "text": "3. The Contractor shall:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0895",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 895,
    "page_start": 321,
    "page_end": 321,
    "char_start": 503482,
    "char_end": 503559,
    "char_count": 77,
    "text": "Draft No. DFA/54028\nAttachment:Annexure C- Revised Standard EPC Agreement.pdf",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0896",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 896,
    "page_start": 322,
    "page_end": 322,
    "char_start": 503561,
    "char_end": 503773,
    "char_count": 212,
    "text": "290\na.\nFurnish to each Board member one copy of all documents which the Board may\nrequest including Contract Agreement, progress reports and other documents\npertinent to the performance of the Contract Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0897",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 897,
    "page_start": 322,
    "page_end": 322,
    "char_start": 503775,
    "char_end": 503923,
    "char_count": 148,
    "text": "b.\nIn cooperation with the Authority, coordinate the site visits of the Board, including\nconference facilities, and secretarial and copying service.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0898",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 898,
    "page_start": 322,
    "page_end": 322,
    "char_start": 503925,
    "char_end": 504120,
    "char_count": 195,
    "text": "4. The Board shall begin its activities following the signing of a Board Member's\nDeclaration of Acceptance by all three Board Members, and it shall terminate these\nactivities as set forth below:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0899",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 899,
    "page_start": 322,
    "page_end": 322,
    "char_start": 504122,
    "char_end": 504461,
    "char_count": 339,
    "text": "a.\nThe Board shall terminate its regular activities when either (i) issuance of\ncompletion certificate and completion of punch list items or (ii) the parties have\nterminated the contract and when, in either case, the Board has communicated to\nthe parties and the Authority’s Engineer its decision on all disputes previously\nreferred to it.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0900",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 900,
    "page_start": 322,
    "page_end": 322,
    "char_start": 504463,
    "char_end": 504763,
    "char_count": 300,
    "text": "b.\nOnce the Board has terminated its regular activities as provided by the previous\nparagraph, the Board shall remain available to process any dispute referred to it by\neither party. In case of such a referral, Board Members shall receive payments as\nprovided in paragraphs 7(a) (ii), (iii) and (iv).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0901",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 901,
    "page_start": 322,
    "page_end": 322,
    "char_start": 504765,
    "char_end": 504865,
    "char_count": 100,
    "text": "5. Board Members shall not assign or subcontract any of their work under these Rules and\nProcedures.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0902",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 902,
    "page_start": 322,
    "page_end": 322,
    "char_start": 504867,
    "char_end": 504975,
    "char_count": 108,
    "text": "6.  The Board Members are Independent and not employees or agents of either the\nAuthority or the Contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0903",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 903,
    "page_start": 322,
    "page_end": 322,
    "char_start": 504977,
    "char_end": 505075,
    "char_count": 98,
    "text": "7. Payments to the Board Members for their services shall be governed by the following\nprovisions.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0904",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 904,
    "page_start": 322,
    "page_end": 322,
    "char_start": 505077,
    "char_end": 505331,
    "char_count": 254,
    "text": "a.\n Each Board Member will receive payments as follows:\n\ni. A retainer fee per calendar month as specified in the schedule of fee made part of\nthis Schedule and its revision from time to time. This retainer fee shall be\nconsidered as payment in full for:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0905",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 905,
    "page_start": 322,
    "page_end": 322,
    "char_start": 505333,
    "char_end": 505436,
    "char_count": 103,
    "text": "A.\n Being available, on 7 days' notice, for all hearings, Site Visits, and other\nmeetings of the Board.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0906",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 906,
    "page_start": 322,
    "page_end": 322,
    "char_start": 505438,
    "char_end": 505519,
    "char_count": 81,
    "text": "B.\nBeing conversant with all project developments and maintaining relevant files.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0907",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 907,
    "page_start": 322,
    "page_end": 322,
    "char_start": 505521,
    "char_end": 505731,
    "char_count": 210,
    "text": "C.\nAll offices and overhead expenses such as secretarial services, photocopying and\noffice supplies (but not include telephone calls, faxes and telexes) incurred in\nconnection with the duties as a Board Member.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0908",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 908,
    "page_start": 322,
    "page_end": 322,
    "char_start": 505733,
    "char_end": 505972,
    "char_count": 239,
    "text": "ii.\nA daily fee as specified in the schedule of fee in respect of fee for site visit &\nmeeting, fee for meeting/ hearing not at site and extra charges for days max. of 02\ndays for travel on each occasion) other than hearing / meeting days.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0909",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 909,
    "page_start": 322,
    "page_end": 322,
    "char_start": 505974,
    "char_end": 506051,
    "char_count": 77,
    "text": "Draft No. DFA/54028\nAttachment:Annexure C- Revised Standard EPC Agreement.pdf",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0910",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 910,
    "page_start": 323,
    "page_end": 323,
    "char_start": 506053,
    "char_end": 506321,
    "char_count": 268,
    "text": "291\niii.\nExpenses, in addition to the above, all reasonable and necessary travel expenses\n(including economy class air fare, subsistence, and other direct travel expenses).\nReceipts for all expenses in excess of Rs. 2000/- (Rupees Two Thousand only) shall\nbe provided.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0911",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 911,
    "page_start": 323,
    "page_end": 323,
    "char_start": 506323,
    "char_end": 506439,
    "char_count": 116,
    "text": "iv.\nReimbursement of any taxes that may be levied on payments made to the Board\nMember pursuant to this paragraph 7.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0912",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 912,
    "page_start": 323,
    "page_end": 323,
    "char_start": 506441,
    "char_end": 506560,
    "char_count": 119,
    "text": "b.\nThe retainer fee and other fees shall remain fixed for the period of each Board\nMember's term until revised by NHAI.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0913",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 913,
    "page_start": 323,
    "page_end": 323,
    "char_start": 506562,
    "char_end": 507016,
    "char_count": 454,
    "text": "c.\nPhasing out of monthly retainer fee. Beginning with the next month after the\ncompletion certificate (or, if there are more than one, the one issued last) has been\nissued, the Board members shall receive only one-third of the monthly retainer fee\ntill next one year. Beginning with the next month after the Board has terminated its\nregular activities pursuant to paragraph 4(a) above, the Board members shall no\nlonger receive any monthly retainer fee.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0914",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 914,
    "page_start": 323,
    "page_end": 323,
    "char_start": 507018,
    "char_end": 507433,
    "char_count": 415,
    "text": "d.\nPayments to the Board Members shall be shared equally by the Authority and the\nContractor. The concerned Project Implementation Unit (PIU) of Authority shall\npay members' invoices within 30 calendar days after receipt of such invoices and\nshall invoice the Contractor for one-half of the amounts of such invoices. The\nContractor shall pay such invoices within 30 days' time period after receipt of such\ninvoices.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0915",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 915,
    "page_start": 323,
    "page_end": 323,
    "char_start": 507435,
    "char_end": 507900,
    "char_count": 465,
    "text": "8.\nBoard Site Visits:\n\na.\n The Board shall visit the Site and meet the representatives of the Authority, the\nContractor and the Authority’s Engineer at regular intervals, at times of critical\nconstruction events, at the written request of either party, and in any case not less\nthan 6 times in any period or 12 months. The timing of Site visits shall be as agreed\namong the Authority, the Contractor and the Board, but failing agreement shall be\nfixed by the Board.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0916",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 916,
    "page_start": 323,
    "page_end": 323,
    "char_start": 507902,
    "char_end": 508109,
    "char_count": 207,
    "text": "b.\nSite visits shall include an informal discussion of the status of the construction of\nthe Works. Site visits shall be attended by personnel from the Authority, the\nContractor and the Authority’s Engineer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0917",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 917,
    "page_start": 323,
    "page_end": 323,
    "char_start": 508111,
    "char_end": 508295,
    "char_count": 184,
    "text": "c.\nAt the conclusion of each Site visit, the Board shall prepare a report covering its\nactivities during the visit and shall send copies to the parties and to the Authority’s\nEngineer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0918",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 918,
    "page_start": 323,
    "page_end": 323,
    "char_start": 508297,
    "char_end": 508672,
    "char_count": 375,
    "text": "9.\nProcedure for Dispute Referral to the Board\n\na.\n lf either party objects to any action or inaction of the other party or the\nAuthority’s Engineer, the objecting party may file a written Notice of Dispute to\nthe other party with a copy to the Authority’s Engineer stating that it is given\npursuant to the Agreement and state clearly and in details the basis of the dispute.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0919",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 919,
    "page_start": 323,
    "page_end": 323,
    "char_start": 508674,
    "char_end": 508751,
    "char_count": 77,
    "text": "Draft No. DFA/54028\nAttachment:Annexure C- Revised Standard EPC Agreement.pdf",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0920",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 920,
    "page_start": 324,
    "page_end": 324,
    "char_start": 508753,
    "char_end": 508878,
    "char_count": 125,
    "text": "292\nb.\n The party receiving the Notice of Dispute will consider it and respond to it in\nwriting within 14 days after receipt.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0921",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 921,
    "page_start": 324,
    "page_end": 324,
    "char_start": 508880,
    "char_end": 509266,
    "char_count": 386,
    "text": "c.\n This response shall be final and conclusive on the subject, unless a written\nappeal to the response is filed with the responding party within 10 days after\nreceiving the response and call upon Authority’s Engineer to mediate and assist the\nparties in arriving an amicable settlement thereof. Both parties are encouraged to\npursue the matter further to attempt to settle the dispute.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0922",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 922,
    "page_start": 324,
    "page_end": 324,
    "char_start": 509268,
    "char_end": 509935,
    "char_count": 667,
    "text": "d.\n If the Authority’s Engineer receiving the Notice of Dispute fails to provide a\nwritten response within 14 days after receipt of such Notice or failing mediation by\nAuthority’s Engineer, either party may require such dispute to be referred to the\nBoard, either party may refer the dispute to the Board by written Request to the\nBoard. The Request for decision shall state clearly and in full detail the specific\nissues of the dispute (s) to be considered by Board and shall be addressed to the\nChairman of the Board, with copies to the other Board Members, the other party,\nand the Authority Engineer, and it shall state that it is made pursuant to this\nAgreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0923",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 923,
    "page_start": 324,
    "page_end": 324,
    "char_start": 509937,
    "char_end": 510344,
    "char_count": 407,
    "text": "e.\nWhen a dispute is referred to the Board, and the Board is satisfied that the dispute\nrequires the Board's assistance, the Board decide when to conduct a hearing on the\ndispute. The Board may request that written documentation and arguments from\nboth parties be submitted to each Board Member before the hearing begins. The\nparties shall submit insofar as possible agreed statements of the relevant facts.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0924",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 924,
    "page_start": 324,
    "page_end": 324,
    "char_start": 510346,
    "char_end": 510981,
    "char_count": 635,
    "text": "f.\nDuring the hearing, the Contractor, the Authority, and the Authority’s Engineer\nshall each have ample opportunity to be heard and to offer evidence. The Board's\ndecision for resolution of the dispute will be given in writing to the Authority, the\nContractor and the Authority’s Engineer as soon as possible, and in any event not\nmore than 56 days or any  mutually extended period between the Authority and the\nContractor. The time period of 56 days of issuance of DRB decision will\nreckon/start from the day of first hearing that begins after submission of complete\npleadings (including supporting documents, if any) by the parties.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0925",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 925,
    "page_start": 324,
    "page_end": 324,
    "char_start": 510983,
    "char_end": 511374,
    "char_count": 391,
    "text": "10.\nConduct of Hearings:\n\na.\n Normally hearings will be conducted at the Site, but any location that would be\nmore convenient and still provide all required facilities and access to necessary\ndocumentation may be utilized by the Board. Private session of the Board may be\nheld at any cost effective location convenient to the Board. Video recordings of all\nhearings shall invariably be made.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0926",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 926,
    "page_start": 324,
    "page_end": 324,
    "char_start": 511376,
    "char_end": 511582,
    "char_count": 206,
    "text": "b.\n The Authority, the Authority’s Engineer and the Contractor shall be given\nopportunity to have representatives at all hearings. Parties should restrain to bring\nany Advocate/Law Firm during DRB hearings.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0927",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 927,
    "page_start": 324,
    "page_end": 324,
    "char_start": 511584,
    "char_end": 511714,
    "char_count": 130,
    "text": "c.\nDuring the hearings, no Board Member shall express any opinion concerning the\nmerit of the respective arguments of the parties.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0928",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 928,
    "page_start": 324,
    "page_end": 324,
    "char_start": 511716,
    "char_end": 511793,
    "char_count": 77,
    "text": "Draft No. DFA/54028\nAttachment:Annexure C- Revised Standard EPC Agreement.pdf",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0929",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 929,
    "page_start": 325,
    "page_end": 325,
    "char_start": 511795,
    "char_end": 512381,
    "char_count": 586,
    "text": "293\nd.\n After the hearings are concluded, the Board shall meet privately to formulate its\ndecision. The private meeting (s) of the Board shall not exceed 3 sittings. All Board\ndeliberations shall be conducted in private, with all Members' individual views kept\nstrictly confidential. The Board's decisions, together with an explanation of its\nreasoning shall be submitted in writing to both parties and to the Authority’s\nEngineer. The decision shall be based on the pertinent contract provisions,\napplicable laws and regulations and the facts and circumstances involved in the\ndispute.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0930",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 930,
    "page_start": 325,
    "page_end": 325,
    "char_start": 512383,
    "char_end": 512675,
    "char_count": 292,
    "text": "e.\nThe Board shall make every effort to reach a unanimous decision. If this proves\nimpossible the majority shall decide and the dissenting Member may prepare a\nwritten minority report together with an explanation of its reasoning for submission\nto both parties and to the Authority’s Engineer",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0931",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 931,
    "page_start": 325,
    "page_end": 325,
    "char_start": 512677,
    "char_end": 513247,
    "char_count": 570,
    "text": "11.\nIn all procedural matters, including the furnishing of written documents and\narguments relating to disputes, site visits and conduct of hearings, the Board shall\nhave full and the final authority. If a unanimous decision on any such matter proves\nimpossible, the majority shall prevail.\n12.\nAfter having been selected and where necessary approved each Board Member\nshall sign two copies of the following declaration and make one copy available\neach to the Authority and to the Contractor.\nDraft No. DFA/54028\nAttachment:Annexure C- Revised Standard EPC Agreement.pdf",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC080-0932",
    "doc_id": "DOC-080",
    "paragraph_index": 932,
