    "char_count": 113,
    "text": "1.16 Field of Use shall mean < DEFINE FIELD(S) OF USE >.\n\n2.  License Grant and disclosure of Process Information",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC083-0028",
    "doc_id": "DOC-083",
    "paragraph_index": 28,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 4851,
    "char_end": 5390,
    "char_count": 539,
    "text": "2.1. Subject to the terms and conditions of this Agreement, IITK hereby grants to\nLicensee, and Licensee hereby accepts, an Exclusive [world-wide or Territory]/Non-\nExclusive [world-wide or Territory] license and licensing rights under Licensed\nProcess/Technology and improvements, if any, including, without limitation, the right\nto develop, have developed, to use, have used, to make, and have made Application\nin connection with the operations of Licensee and Dispose of Licensed Products and\nto create Derivatives for the Field of Use.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC083-0029",
    "doc_id": "DOC-083",
    "paragraph_index": 29,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 5392,
    "char_end": 6226,
    "char_count": 834,
    "text": "2.2. No right to sublicense the Process/Technology is hereby granted to Licensee\nexcept\n(1)\nthat\nLicensee\nmay\nsublicense\nto\nits\ncustomers\nLicensed\nProcess/Technology in the ordinary course of business and to the extent necessary\nfor use and practice of the Licensed Product Disposed of by Licensee to said\ncustomers or (2) with the prior written agreement by IITK.  Licensee understands\nthat any sublicenses granted by Licensee to entities, other than customers other\nthan in the ordinary course of business, (even though the prior written agreement\nby IITK to such a sublicense has been obtained) must provide for obligations to IITK\nunder this Agreement, including but not limited to, Indemnification, Insurance, and\nprocedures for Dispute Resolution, shall be binding upon such sub-licensee as if it\nwere a party to this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC083-0030",
    "doc_id": "DOC-083",
    "paragraph_index": 30,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 6228,
    "char_end": 6463,
    "char_count": 235,
    "text": "2.3. IITK shall have the right to use, free of charge, any product or process,\ndeveloped by Licensee which contains or is based on any of Licensed\nProcess/Technology for IITK research, educational, academic, or administrative\npurposes.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC083-0031",
    "doc_id": "DOC-083",
    "paragraph_index": 31,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 6465,
    "char_end": 6633,
    "char_count": 168,
    "text": "2.4. No provision of this Agreement shall restrict IITK's ability to conduct further\nresearch and development in the area of Licensed Process/Technology or other\nareas.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC083-0032",
    "doc_id": "DOC-083",
    "paragraph_index": 32,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 6635,
    "char_end": 7019,
    "char_count": 384,
    "text": "2.5. All Licensed Products shall be Disposed of and performed by Licensee in\ncompliance with all applicable governmental laws, rules and regulations. Licensee\nshall keep IITK fully informed of, and shall move expeditiously to resolve, any\ncomplaint by a governmental body relevant to the Licensed Products, except for\ncomplaints subject to Section 21 (Infringement) of this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC083-0033",
    "doc_id": "DOC-083",
    "paragraph_index": 33,
    "page_start": 4,
    "page_end": 4,
    "char_start": 7021,
    "char_end": 7762,
    "char_count": 741,
    "text": "2.6. IITK retains the right, exercisable in the sole discretion of IITK and upon\nadvance notice to Licensee, to grant non exclusive/exclusive licenses under the\nLicensed Process/Technology in the Field of Use to third parties as a means to\nresolve disputes or settle claims, suits or proceedings arising out of allegation that\nthe Licensed Process/Technology infringes upon the intellectual property rights of\nthe third party.  Each party shall promptly notify the other parties hereto of its\nreceipt of any such allegations.  Nothing in this Section 2.6 shall be construed as\nobligating IITK to resolve any dispute or to settle or defend any claim, suit or\nproceeding arising out of Licensee's Disposition of Licensed Products. IITK retains",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC083-0034",
    "doc_id": "DOC-083",
    "paragraph_index": 34,
