    "paragraph_index": 83,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 26878,
    "char_end": 26999,
    "char_count": 121,
    "text": "19.  Interpretation\n\nThis Agreement shall be governed by, and construed and enforced in accordance\nwith, the Indian laws.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC083-0084",
    "doc_id": "DOC-083",
    "paragraph_index": 84,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 27001,
    "char_end": 27784,
    "char_count": 783,
    "text": "20.  Dispute Resolution\n\nThe parties hereto shall endeavor to settle in an amicable way, all disputes or\ndifferences which may arise out of the present agreement or in connection\ntherewith. Any controversy or dispute arising under this Agreement not resolved\nshall be referred to and finally settled by arbitration in accordance with the Rules of\nConciliation and Arbitration of the International Chamber of Commerce by one or\nmore arbitrators appointed in accordance with the said rules. Arbitration shall be\nconducted in Delhi. Any award of the arbitrators shall be final and conclusive on the\nparties to this Agreement and judgment upon such award may be entered in any\ncourt having jurisdiction thereof. The jurisdiction of this agreement will be the courts\nat New Delhi (India).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC083-0085",
    "doc_id": "DOC-083",
    "paragraph_index": 85,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 27786,
    "char_end": 29133,
    "char_count": 1347,
    "text": "21.  Infringement\n\n21.1. Licensee shall have the right during the term of this Agreement to commence\nan action for infringement of the Patents against any third party for any infringement\noccurring within the Field of Use, provided that Licensee shall provide IITK ____\ndays' prior written notice of such infringement and of Licensee's intent to file such\naction.  IITK shall have the right at its own expense to appear in such action by\ncounsel of its own selection.  If required by the jurisdictional laws of the forum that\nany such action be prosecuted in the name of the owner of the Patent, IITK shall\nvoluntarily appear at Licensee's expense; provided that if such appearance subjects\nIITK to any unrelated action or claim of a third party or Licensee in such jurisdiction,\nthen IITK shall have the right to decline such appearance.  Settlement of any action\nbrought by Licensee shall require the consent of IITK and Licensee, which neither\nshall unreasonably withhold from the other, and any settlement amount or recovery\nfor damages shall be applied as follows:  (i) first, to reimburse the parties for their\nexpenses in connection with the litigation; and (ii) second, IITK shall receive\ncompensation for the time of any IITK personnel involved in the action and (iii)\nthird, IITK shall receive   x   percent (x%) of any monies remaining.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC083-0086",
    "doc_id": "DOC-083",
    "paragraph_index": 86,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 29135,
    "char_end": 30043,
    "char_count": 908,
    "text": "21.2. IITK shall have the right in its absolute discretion during the term of this\nAgreement to commence an action for infringement of the Patents against any third\nparty for any infringement occurring anywhere in the world, provided that, before\ncommencing any such action concerning the Field of Use, IITK shall provide Licensee\nnot less than ____ days' prior written notice of such infringement and of IITK's\nintent to file such action.  Licensee shall have the right at its own expense to appear\nin such action by counsel of its own selection.  If IITK provides Licensee with such\nnotice before instituting an action concerning the Field of Use and Licensee fails to\ninitiate an action against such third party prior to the commencement of an action by\nIITK, then any settlement amount or recovery for damages shall belong entirely to\nIITK and IITK may settle said action without the consent of Licensee.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC083-0087",
