    "char_start": 74017,
    "char_end": 74325,
    "char_count": 308,
    "text": "Page 32 of 50\n1.16. Adherence to the Empanelment Terms & Conditions\nThe Managed Service Provider shall ensure that the underlying Cloud Managed Service\nProvider is adhering to all the terms and conditions specified in the MeitY’s CSP Empanelment\nRFP at all times during the tenure of the Purchaser’s project.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0129",
    "doc_id": "DOC-085",
    "paragraph_index": 129,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 74326,
    "char_end": 74607,
    "char_count": 281,
    "text": "1.17. Information Security\nOne of the most critical issues that need to be addressed in the Cloud Contract / Agreement\nis the security of the data and application. The level of sensitivity of data requires different\ncontrols to be put in place in the Cloud to prevent a compromise.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0130",
    "doc_id": "DOC-085",
    "paragraph_index": 130,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 74608,
    "char_end": 76381,
    "char_count": 1773,
    "text": "1.17.1. Compliances and Certifications\n(i)\nAs part of the empanelment process, MeitY has mandated CSPs to have following\ncertifications.\na. ISO 27001:2013 – Information security management systems requirements\n(Data Center and the Cloud Services should be certified for the ISO 27001\nstandard)\nb. ISO 20000:1 - Service management system requirements (NOC and SOC offered\nfor the Data Center and the managed services quality should be certified for\nISO 20000:1)\nc. ISO 27017 - Code of practice for information security controls based on ISO/IEC\n27002 for Cloud Services\nd. ISO 27018 - Code of practice for protection of Personally Identifiable\nInformation (PII) in Public Clouds acting as PII processors\ne. TIA-942-B / UPTIME (Tier III or higher) – Data centre standard covering site\nspace and layout, cabling infrastructure, tiered reliability and environmental\nconsiderations\nThe Managed Service Provider shall ensure the sustenance of the above certificates\nand compliances applicable to the underlying CSPs during the entire duration of the\nproject. The Managed Service Provider is required to possess and sustain following\ncertifications in addition to ensuring the sustenance of the above certificates and\ncompliances applicable to the underlying CSP during the entire duration of the project.\na. ISO 27001:2013 – Information security management systems requirements\nb. ISO 20000:1 - Service management system requirements\n(ii)\nIf the Purchaser has financial and payment related data that is proposed to be hosted\non the Cloud, the Managed Service Provider shall provide Payment Card Industry Data\nSecurity Standard (PCI DSS) compliant technology infrastructure of underlying CSP for\nstoring, processing, and transmitting payment related information in the Cloud. This",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0131",
    "doc_id": "DOC-085",
    "paragraph_index": 131,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 76382,
    "char_end": 76452,
    "char_count": 70,
    "text": "standard is required if the transactions involve credit card payments.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0132",
    "doc_id": "DOC-085",
    "paragraph_index": 132,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 76454,
