    "char_start": 100014,
    "char_end": 100182,
    "char_count": 168,
    "text": "Page 41 of 50\nor other) that would adversely impact the ability of the Managed Service Provider to\ncomplete the requirements as given in the application document / RFP.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0169",
    "doc_id": "DOC-085",
    "paragraph_index": 169,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 100183,
    "char_end": 101144,
    "char_count": 961,
    "text": "1.27. Relationship\nThe Managed Service Provider is fully responsible for the services performed by it or on its\nbehalf.\n(i)\nNothing mentioned herein shall be construed as relationship of master and servant or\nof principal and agent as between the Purchaser and the Managed Service Provider.\nNo partnership shall be constituted between the Purchaser and the Managed Service\nProvider by virtue of this Agreement nor shall either party have powers to make, vary\nor release their obligations on behalf of the other party or represent that by virtue of\nthis or any other Agreement a partnership has been constituted, or that it has any such\npower. The Managed Service Provider shall be fully responsible for the services\nperformed by it or on its behalf.\n(ii)\nThe Managed Service Provider shall not use the Purchaser’s name or any service or\nproprietary name, mark or logo for promotional purpose without first having obtained\nthe Purchaser’s prior written approval.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0170",
    "doc_id": "DOC-085",
    "paragraph_index": 170,
    "page_start": 41,
    "page_end": 41,
    "char_start": 101145,
    "char_end": 102614,
    "char_count": 1469,
    "text": "1.28. Fraud & Corruption\nThe Managed Service Provider shall observe the highest standards of ethics during the\nperformance and execution of the Project.\n(i)\nThe Purchaser shall terminate the Agreement if the Managed Service Provider has been\ndetermined by the Purchaser to having been engaged in corrupt, fraudulent, unfair\ntrade practices, coercive or collusive.\n(ii)\nThe following terms apply in this context.\na. \"Corrupt practice\" means offering, giving, receiving or soliciting of anything of\nvalue to influence the action of the Purchaser during the tenure of the Project.\nb. \"Fraudulent practice\" means a misrepresentation of facts, in order to influence\na procurement process or the execution of a contract, to the Purchaser, and\nincludes collusive practices designed to establish proposal prices at artificially\nhigh or non-competitive levels and to deprive the Purchaser of the benefits of\nfree and open competition.\nc. “Unfair trade practices” means supply of services different from what is ordered\non, or change in the Scope of Work which was agreed to.\nd. “Coercive practices” means harming or threatening to harm, directly or\nindirectly, persons or their property to influence their participation during the\nperiod of Project.\ne. “Collusive practices” means a scheme or arrangement between two or more\nprospective Managed Service Providers with or without the knowledge of the\nPurchaser, designed to establish prices at artificial, non-competitive levels;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0171",
    "doc_id": "DOC-085",
    "paragraph_index": 171,
    "page_start": 42,
    "page_end": 42,
    "char_start": 102616,
    "char_end": 102723,
    "char_count": 107,
    "text": "Master Service Agreement - Procurement of Cloud Services\nMinistry of Electronics and Information Technology",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0172",
