    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0184",
    "doc_id": "DOC-085",
    "paragraph_index": 184,
    "page_start": 45,
    "page_end": 45,
    "char_start": 108394,
    "char_end": 108501,
    "char_count": 107,
    "text": "Master Service Agreement - Procurement of Cloud Services\nMinistry of Electronics and Information Technology",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0185",
    "doc_id": "DOC-085",
    "paragraph_index": 185,
    "page_start": 45,
    "page_end": 45,
    "char_start": 108503,
    "char_end": 110276,
    "char_count": 1773,
    "text": "Page 45 of 50\nSchedule I – Governance Schedule\nPurpose\nThe purpose of this Governance Schedule is to:\na) establish and maintain the formal and informal processes for managing the\nrelationship between the Purchaser and the Managed Service Provider\nb) define the principles that both Parties wish to follow to ensure the delivery of\nthe Services;\nc) ensure the continued alignment of the interests of the Parties;\nd) ensure that the relationship is maintained at the correct level within each Party;\ne) create the flexibility to revise and maintain the relationship and this Agreement\nduring the Term;\nf) set out the procedure for escalating disagreements; and\ng) enable contract administration and performance management.\nGovernance Structure\na) Project Managers: The relationship under this Agreement will be managed by the\nProject Managers appointed by each Party, who will provide the interface between the\nexecutive management of the respective Parties.\nb) Project Governance Team (PGT) - Within 7 days following the Effective Date,\nPurchaser or its nominated agencies and the Managed Service Provider shall each\nappoint a Project Manager. In the event that either Party wishes to substitute its\nProject Manager it will do so in manner in which the original appointment is made\nand notify the other Party of such substitution as soon as reasonably practicable but\nat the latest within 7 days of the substitution.\nc) The Project Managers shall have responsibility for maintaining the interface and\ncommunication between the Parties.\nd) The PGT shall meet formally on a fortnightly / monthly / quarterly, as required,\nbasis at a time and location to be agreed between them. These meetings will cover,\nas a minimum, the following agenda items: (i) consideration of periodic",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0186",
    "doc_id": "DOC-085",
    "paragraph_index": 186,
    "page_start": 45,
    "page_end": 45,
    "char_start": 110277,
    "char_end": 110911,
    "char_count": 634,
    "text": "performance reports; (ii) consideration of matters arising out of the change\ncontrol; (iii) escalated issues; (iv) matters to be brought before the PGT in accordance\nwith this Agreement; (v) any matter brought before the PGT by the Managed\nService Provider under this Agreement; and (vi) any other issue which either Party\nwishes to add to the agenda.\nGovernance Procedures\na) The Managed Service Provider shall document the agreed structures in a procedures\nmanual.\nb) The agenda for each meeting of the PGT shall be set to reflect the discussion items\nreferred to above and extraordinary items may be added either with the agreement",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0187",
    "doc_id": "DOC-085",
    "paragraph_index": 187,
    "page_start": 46,
    "page_end": 46,
    "char_start": 110913,
    "char_end": 111020,
    "char_count": 107,
    "text": "Master Service Agreement - Procurement of Cloud Services\nMinistry of Electronics and Information Technology",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0188",
    "doc_id": "DOC-085",
    "paragraph_index": 188,
    "page_start": 46,
    "page_end": 46,
    "char_start": 111022,
    "char_end": 112741,
    "char_count": 1719,
    "text": "Page 46 of 50\nof the Parties or at the request of either Party. Copies of the agenda for meetings of\nthe PGT, along with relevant pre-reading material, shall be distributed at least one\nweek in advance of the relevant meeting.\nc) All meetings and proceedings will be documented. Such documents shall be\ndistributed to the Parties and copies shall be kept as a record. All actions,\nresponsibilities and accountabilities arising out of any meeting shall be tracked and\nmanaged.\nd) The Parties shall ensure as far as reasonably practicable that the PGT shall resolve\nthe issues and resolve the objectives placed before them and that members\nrepresenting that Party are empowered to make relevant decisions or have easy\naccess to empowered individuals for decisions to be made to achieve this.\ne) In order to formally submit a Disputed Matter to the aforesaid for a resolution, one\nParty (\"Claimant\") shall give a written notice (\"Dispute Notice\") to the other Party.\nThe Dispute Notice shall be accompanied by (a) a statement by the Claimant\ndescribing the Disputed Matter in reasonable detail and (b) documentation, if any,\nsupporting the Claimant's position on the Disputed Matter.\nf) The other Party (\"Respondent\") shall have the right to respond to the Dispute Notice\nwithin 7 days after receipt of the Dispute Notice. In the event that the parties are unable\nto resolve the Disputed Matter within a further period of 7 days, it shall refer the\nDisputed Matter to next level of the dispute resolution for action as per the process\nmentioned in Clause 1.26.\ng) All negotiations, statements and / or documentation pursuant to these Articles shall\nbe without prejudice and confidential (unless mutually agreed otherwise).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0189",
    "doc_id": "DOC-085",
    "paragraph_index": 189,
    "page_start": 46,
    "page_end": 46,
    "char_start": 112742,
    "char_end": 112998,
    "char_count": 256,
    "text": "If the Disputed Matter is having a material effect on the operation of the Services (or any\nof them or part of them), the Parties will use all their respective reasonable endeavors to\nreduce the elapsed time in reaching a resolution of the Disputed Matter.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0190",
    "doc_id": "DOC-085",
    "paragraph_index": 190,
    "page_start": 47,
    "page_end": 47,
    "char_start": 113000,
    "char_end": 113107,
    "char_count": 107,
    "text": "Master Service Agreement - Procurement of Cloud Services\nMinistry of Electronics and Information Technology",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0191",
    "doc_id": "DOC-085",
    "paragraph_index": 191,
    "page_start": 47,
    "page_end": 47,
    "char_start": 113109,
    "char_end": 114209,
    "char_count": 1100,
    "text": "Page 47 of 50\n1.34. Schedule II – Change Control Schedule\nThis Schedule describes the procedure to be followed in the event of any proposed change\nto the Master Service Agreement (“MSA”), Project Execution Phase, SLA and Scope of\nWork. Such change shall include, but shall not be limited to, changes in the scope of\nservices provided by the Managed Service Provider and changes to the terms of\npayment.\nThe Purchaser and Managed Service Provider recognize that change is an inevitable part\nof delivering services and that a significant element of this change can be\naccomplished by re-organizing processes and responsibilities without a material\neffect on the cost. The Managed Service Provider will endeavor, wherever reasonably\npracticable, to effect change without an increase in the terms of payment and Purchaser\nor its nominated agencies will work with the Managed Service Provider to ensure that\nall changes are discussed and managed in a constructive manner. This Change Control\nSchedule sets out the provisions which will apply to all the changes to this agreement.\nChange Management Process",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0192",
    "doc_id": "DOC-085",
    "paragraph_index": 192,
    "page_start": 47,
    "page_end": 47,
    "char_start": 114210,
    "char_end": 115809,
    "char_count": 1599,
    "text": "A. Change Control Note (\"CCN\")\n(i)\nChange requests in respect of the MSA, the Project Execution, the\noperation, the SLA or Scope of work will emanate from the Parties'\nrespective Project Manager who will be responsible for obtaining\napproval for the change and who will act as its sponsor throughout the\nChange Control Process and will complete Part A of the CCN attached as\nAnnexure A hereto. CCNs will be presented to the other Party's Project\nManager who will acknowledge receipt by signature of the CCN.\n(ii)\nThe Managed Service Provider and the Purchaser or its nominated\nagencies, during the Project Execution Phase and the Purchaser or its\nnominated agencies during the Operations and Management Phase and\nwhile preparing the CCN, shall consider the change in the context of the\nfollowing parameter, namely whether the change is beyond the scope of\nServices including ancillary and concomitant services required and is\nsuggested and applicable.\n(iii)\nIt is hereby also clarified here that any change of control suggested\nbeyond 25 % of the value of this Project will be beyond the scope of the\nchange control process and will be considered as the subject matter for a\nseparate bid process and a separate contract. It is hereby clarified that\nthe 25% of the value of the Project as stated in herein above is\ncalculated on the basis of bid value submitted by the Managed Service\nProvider and accepted by the Purchaser or its nominated agencies or as\ndecided and approved by Purchaser or it Nominated Agencies. For arriving\nat the cost / rate for change up to 25% of the project value, the rates",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0193",
    "doc_id": "DOC-085",
    "paragraph_index": 193,
    "page_start": 48,
    "page_end": 48,
    "char_start": 115811,
    "char_end": 115918,
    "char_count": 107,
    "text": "Master Service Agreement - Procurement of Cloud Services\nMinistry of Electronics and Information Technology",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0194",
    "doc_id": "DOC-085",
    "paragraph_index": 194,
    "page_start": 48,
    "page_end": 48,
    "char_start": 115920,
    "char_end": 117041,
    "char_count": 1121,
    "text": "Page 48 of 50\nsubmitted in the Financial Proposal shall be considered.\nB. Quotation\n(i)\nThe Managed Service Provider shall assess the CCN and complete Part B of\nthe CC. In completing the Part B of the CCN, the Managed Service Provider\nshall provide as a minimum:\na) a description of the change\nb) a list of deliverables required for executing the change;\nc) a time table for execution;\nd) an estimate of any proposed change\ne) any relevant acceptance criteria\nf) an assessment of the value of the proposed change;\ng) material evidence to prove that the proposed change is not already\ncovered within the Agreement and the scope of work\n(ii)\nPrior to submission of the completed CCN to the Purchaser, or its nominated\nagencies, the Managed Service Provider will undertake its own internal review\nof the proposal and obtain all necessary internal approvals. As a part of this\ninternal review process, the Managed Service Provider shall consider the\nmateriality of the proposed change in the context of the MSA and the Project\nExecution affected by the change and the total effect that may arise from\nexecution of the change.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0195",
    "doc_id": "DOC-085",
    "paragraph_index": 195,
    "page_start": 48,
    "page_end": 48,
    "char_start": 117042,
    "char_end": 117486,
    "char_count": 444,
    "text": "C. Costs\nEach Party shall be responsible for its own costs incurred in the quotation, preparation of\nCCNs and in the completion of its obligations described in this process provided the\nManaged Service Provider meets the obligations as set in the CCN. In the event the\nManaged Service Provider is unable to meet the obligations as defined in the CCN then\nthe cost of getting it done by third party will be borne by the Managed Service Provider.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0196",
    "doc_id": "DOC-085",
    "paragraph_index": 196,
    "page_start": 48,
    "page_end": 48,
    "char_start": 117487,
    "char_end": 118019,
    "char_count": 532,
    "text": "D. Obligations\nThe Managed Service Provider shall be obliged to execute any proposed changes once\napproval in accordance with above provisions has been given, with effect from the date\nagreed for execution and within an agreed timeframe. The Managed Service Provider will\nnot be obligated to work on a change until the parties agree in writing upon its scope, price\nand/or schedule impact. The cost associated with any service/software/hardware/licenses\nshould not exceed the price quoted in the Managed Service Provider’s proposal.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
