  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0248",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 248,
    "page_start": 63,
    "page_end": 63,
    "char_start": 145256,
    "char_end": 146990,
    "char_count": 1734,
    "text": "14.4\nCompletion of Punch List items\n14.4.1 All items in the Punch List shall be completed by the Concessionaire within 90 (ninety) days\nof the date of issue of the Provisional Certificate and for any delay thereafter, other than for\nreasons solely attributable to the Authority or due to Force Majeure, the Authority shall be\nentitled to recover Damages from the Concessionaire to be calculated and paid for each day of\ndelay until all items are completed, at the lower of (a) 0.1% (zero point one per cent) of the\nPerformance Security, and (b) 0.2% (zero point two per cent) of the cost of completing such\nitems as estimated by the Independent Engineer. Subject to payment of such Damages, the\nConcessionaire shall be entitled to a further period not exceeding 120 (one hundred and twenty)\ndays for completion of the Punch List items. For the avoidance of doubt, it is agreed that if\ncompletion of any item is delayed for reasons solely attributable to the Authority or due to\nForce Majeure, the completion date thereof shall be determined by the Independent Engineer\nin accordance with Good Industry Practice, and such completion date shall be deemed to be the\ndate of issue of the Provisional Certificate for the purposes of Damages, if any, payable for\nsuch item under this Clause 14.4.1.\n14.4.2 Upon completion of all Punch List items, the Independent Engineer shall issue the Completion\nCertificate. Failure of the Concessionaire to complete all the Punch List items within the time\nset forth in Clause 14.4.1 for any reason, other than conditions constituting Force Majeure or\nfor reasons solely attributable to the Authority, shall entitle the Authority to terminate this\nAgreement.\n14.5\nWithholding of Provisional Certificate",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0249",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 249,
    "page_start": 63,
    "page_end": 63,
    "char_start": 146991,
    "char_end": 147917,
    "char_count": 926,
    "text": "14.5.1 If the Independent Engineer determines that the XXX Ropeway or any part thereof does not\nconform to the provisions of this Agreement and cannot be safely and reliably placed in\ncommercial operation, it shall forthwith make a report in this behalf and send copies thereof to\nthe Authority and the Concessionaire. Upon receipt of such a report from the Independent\nEngineer and after conducting its own inspection, if the Authority is of the opinion that the\nXXX Ropeway is not fit and safe for commercial service, it shall, within 7 (seven) days of\nreceiving the aforesaid report, notify the Concessionaire of the defects and deficiencies in the\nXXX Ropeway and direct the Independent Engineer to withhold issuance of the Provisional\nCertificate. Upon receipt of such notice, the Concessionaire shall remedy and rectify such\ndefects or deficiencies and thereupon Tests shall be undertaken in accordance with this Article",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0250",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 250,
    "page_start": 63,
    "page_end": 63,
    "char_start": 147918,
    "char_end": 148016,
    "char_count": 98,
    "text": "14. Such procedure shall be repeated as necessary until the defects or deficiencies are rectified.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0251",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 251,
    "page_start": 63,
    "page_end": 63,
    "char_start": 148018,
    "char_end": 148761,
    "char_count": 743,
    "text": "14.5.2 Notwithstanding anything to the contrary contained in Clause 14.5.1, the Authority may, at any\ntime after receiving a report from the Independent Engineer under that Clause, direct the\nIndependent Engineer to issue a Provisional Certificate under Clause 14.3, and such direction\nshall be complied forthwith.\n14.6\nRescheduling of Tests\nIf the Independent Engineer certifies to the Authority and the Concessionaire that it is unable\nto issue the Completion Certificate or Provisional Certificate, as the case may be, because of\nevents or circumstances on account of which the Tests could not be held or had to be suspended,\nthe Concessionaire shall be entitled to re-schedule the Tests and hold the same as soon as\nreasonably practicable.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0252",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 252,
    "page_start": 64,
