    "char_end": 195495,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "85",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0340",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 340,
    "page_start": 86,
    "page_end": 86,
    "char_start": 195497,
    "char_end": 195499,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "86",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0341",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 341,
    "page_start": 86,
    "page_end": 86,
    "char_start": 195501,
    "char_end": 196158,
    "char_count": 657,
    "text": "ARTICLE 22: EMERGENCY MEDICAL AID\n22.1\nMedical Aid Posts\nThe Concessionaire shall have requisite first aid kits at each Station as well as the basic\nfirst aid training to the ropeway operators (similar to first aid kits and training of air\nhostesses in airlines).\nFor providing emergency medical aid during the Operation Period, as set forth in this\nAgreement, the Concessionaire shall assist the State Government [or a substitute thereof\nto be designated by the Authority] in setting up and operating a medical aid post (the\n“Medical Aid Post”) at [each of the terminals with round-the-clock ambulance services\nfor victims of accidents on the XXX Ropeway.]",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0342",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 342,
    "page_start": 87,
    "page_end": 87,
    "char_start": 196160,
    "char_end": 196162,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "87",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0343",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 343,
    "page_start": 88,
    "page_end": 88,
    "char_start": 196164,
    "char_end": 196166,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "88",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0344",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 344,
    "page_start": 88,
    "page_end": 88,
    "char_start": 196168,
    "char_end": 197938,
    "char_count": 1770,
    "text": "ARTICLE 23: TRAFFIC CENSUS AND SAMPLING\n23.1\nTraffic census and Train operations\nThe Concessionaire shall install, maintain and operate an electronic/computerised fee\ncollection system and a train control system, the number of Users, distance travelled,\nfrequency and capacity of the XXX Ropeway, travel time and Fee collected. A statement\nof such data shall be compiled and furnished forthwith by the Concessionaire to the\nAuthority substantially in the forms specified in Schedule-M.\n23.2\nTraffic survey\nThe Authority may require the Concessionaire to conduct, during each year of the\nConcession Period, a detailed traffic survey at such frequency and on such days as the\nAuthority may specify, provided that the cumulative period of such survey shall not exceed\n7 (seven) days in a year. The Concessionaire shall, at its own cost, carry out or cause to be\ncarried out, the survey in the form and manner reasonably specified by the Authority and\nfurnish a detailed report thereof within 15 (fifteen) days of the completion of each survey.\nFor the avoidance of doubt, the Authority may also conduct traffic surveys, in such manner\nas it deems fit and at its own cost, through any agency designated by it for this purpose.\n23.3\nTraffic sampling\n23.3.1 For determining the actual traffic on the XXX Ropeway, the Authority shall be entitled to\ninspect the relevant records of the Concessionaire, and may, at its own cost, undertake\ntraffic sampling substantially in the manner set forth in Schedule-P or in such manner as\nthe Parties may agree upon. The Concessionaire shall provide such assistance as the\nAuthorities may reasonably require for such User traffic sampling.\n23.3.2 If the traffic sampling pursuant to this Clause 23.3 demonstrates that the actual traffic is",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0345",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 345,
    "page_start": 88,
    "page_end": 88,
    "char_start": 197939,
    "char_end": 198989,
    "char_count": 1050,
    "text": "more than the traffic reported by the Concessionaire, the traffic determined by the traffic\nsampling shall be deemed to be the traffic for purposes of this Agreement and in the event\nof any Dispute relating to the traffic sampling, the Dispute Resolution Procedure shall\napply. For the avoidance of doubt, Realisable Fee for any comparable period shall be\ncalculated with reference to the traffic determined hereunder.\n23.4\nComputer systems and network\nThe Concessionaire shall install, operate and maintain a computer system with round-the-\nclock connections to the networks of the Authority and other related entities for exchange\nof data and information useful or necessary for efficient and transparent regulation and\nmanagement of traffic. For this purpose, it shall follow such protocol for Electronic Data\nInterchange (the “EDI”) as the Authority may specify. For the avoidance of doubt, it is\nagreed that the form specified in Schedule-M may be modified by the Authority from time\nto time for conforming to the requirements and output of EDI.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0346",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 346,
    "page_start": 89,
    "page_end": 89,
    "char_start": 198991,
