    "char_end": 203309,
    "char_count": 28,
    "text": "PART IV: FINANCIAL COVENANTS",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0354",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 354,
    "page_start": 93,
    "page_end": 93,
    "char_start": 203311,
    "char_end": 203313,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "93",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0355",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 355,
    "page_start": 94,
    "page_end": 94,
    "char_start": 203315,
    "char_end": 203317,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "94",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0356",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 356,
    "page_start": 94,
    "page_end": 94,
    "char_start": 203319,
    "char_end": 204585,
    "char_count": 1266,
    "text": "ARTICLE 25:  FINANCIAL CLOSE\n25.1\nFinancial Close\n\n25.1.1 The Concessionaire hereby agrees and undertakes that it shall achieve Financial Close\nwithin 180 (one hundred and eighty) days from the date of this Agreement and in the event\nof delay, it shall be entitled to a further period not exceeding [120 (one hundred and\ntwenty)] days, subject to payment of Damages to the Authority in a sum calculated at the\nrate of 0.1% (zero point one per cent) of the Performance Security for each day of delay,\nand for a further period not exceeding [80 (eighty)] days, subject to payment of Damages\nat the rate specified in Clause 4.3; provided that the Damages specified herein shall be\npayable every week in advance and the period beyond the said 180 (one hundred and\neighty) days shall be granted only to the extent of Damages so paid; provided further that\nno Damages shall be payable if such delay in Financial Close has occurred solely as a result\nof any default or delay by the Authority in procuring satisfaction of the Conditions\nPrecedent specified in Clause 4.1.2 or due to Force Majeure. For the avoidance of doubt,\nthe Damages payable hereunder by the Concessionaire shall be in addition to the Damages,\nif any, due and payable under the provisions of Clause 4.3.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0357",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 357,
    "page_start": 94,
    "page_end": 94,
    "char_start": 204587,
    "char_end": 205105,
    "char_count": 518,
    "text": "25.1.2 The Concessionaire shall, upon occurrence of Financial Close, notify the Authority\nforthwith, and shall have provided to the Authority, at least 2 (two) days prior to Financial\nClose, 3 (three) true copies of the Financial Package and the Financial Model, duly attested\nby a Director of the Concessionaire, along with 3 (three) soft copies of the Financial Model\nin MS Excel version or any substitute thereof, which is acceptable to the Senior Lenders.\n25.2\nTermination due to failure to achieve Financial Close",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0358",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 358,
    "page_start": 94,
    "page_end": 94,
    "char_start": 205107,
    "char_end": 205918,
    "char_count": 811,
    "text": "25.2.1  Notwithstanding anything to the contrary contained in this Agreement, but subject to\nClause 35.6.1 , in the event that Financial Close does not occur, for any reason whatsoever,\nwithin the period set forth in Clause 25.1.1  or the extended period provided thereunder,\nall rights, privileges, claims and entitlements of the Concessionaire under or arising out of\nthis Agreement shall be deemed to have been waived by, and to have ceased with the\nconcurrence of the Concessionaire, and the Concession Agreement shall be deemed to have\nbeen terminated by mutual agreement of the Parties. For the avoidance of doubt, it is agreed\nthat in the event the Parties hereto have, by mutual consent, determined the Appointed Date\nto precede the Financial Close, the provisions of this Clause 25.2.1 shall not apply.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0359",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 359,
    "page_start": 94,
    "page_end": 94,
    "char_start": 205920,
    "char_end": 206565,
    "char_count": 645,
    "text": "25.2.2  Upon Termination under Clause 25.2.1 1, the Authority shall be entitled to encash the Bid\nSecurity and appropriate the proceeds thereof as Damages; provided, however, that if\nFinancial Close has not occurred solely as a result of the Authority being in default of any\nof its obligations under Clause 4.2, it shall, upon Termination, return the Bid Security\nforthwith along with the Damages due and payable under Clause 4.2. For the avoidance of\ndoubt, it is expressly agreed that if the Bid Security shall have been substituted by\nPerformance Security, the Authority shall be entitled to encash therefrom an amount equal\nto Bid Security.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0360",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 360,
    "page_start": 95,
    "page_end": 95,
    "char_start": 206567,
    "char_end": 206569,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "95",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0361",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 361,
    "page_start": 96,
    "page_end": 96,
    "char_start": 206571,
    "char_end": 206573,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "96",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0362",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 362,
    "page_start": 96,
    "page_end": 96,
    "char_start": 206575,
    "char_end": 206857,
    "char_count": 282,
    "text": "ARTICLE 26: GRANT\n26.1\nGrant\n\n26.1.1 The Authority agrees to provide to the Concessionaire cash support by way of an outright\ngrant equal to the sum set forth in the Bid, namely, Rs. ………… (Rupees in\nwords……………………), in accordance with the provisions of this Article 26 (the\n“Grant”).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0363",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 363,
    "page_start": 96,
    "page_end": 96,
    "char_start": 206859,
    "char_end": 207010,
    "char_count": 151,
    "text": "26.1.2 The Grant shall be disbursed to the Concessionaire by way of Equity Support in accordance\nwith the provisions of Clause 26.2\n26.2\nEquity Support",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0364",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 364,
    "page_start": 96,
    "page_end": 96,
    "char_start": 207012,
    "char_end": 207227,
    "char_count": 215,
    "text": "26.2.1 Subject to the conditions specified in this Clause 26.2, the Grant shall be credited to the\nEscrow Account and shall be applied by the Concessionaire for meeting the Total Project\nCost (the “Equity Support”).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0365",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 365,
    "page_start": 96,
    "page_end": 96,
    "char_start": 207229,
    "char_end": 207973,
    "char_count": 744,
    "text": "26.2.2 The Equity Support shall not exceed the sum specified in the Bid and as accepted by the\nAuthority but shall in no case be greater than twice the Equity and shall be further restricted\nto a sum not exceeding 40% (forty per cent) of the Total Project Cost. Provided, however\nthat in the event Equity Support shall exceed 20% (twenty per cent) of the Total Project\nCost, the amount in excess of such 20% (twenty per cent) shall be released against an\nirrevocable bank guarantee for 2 (two) years which may be invoked if the Concessionaire\ncommits any breach of the obligations specified in this Agreement. For the avoidance of\ndoubt, the Total Project Cost to be reckoned for the purposes of this Clause 26.2.2 shall\ninclude Equity Support.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0366",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 366,
    "page_start": 96,
    "page_end": 96,
    "char_start": 207975,
    "char_end": 208430,
    "char_count": 455,
    "text": "26.2.3 Equity Support shall be due and payable to the Concessionaire after it has expended the\nEquity and shall be disbursed proportionately along with the loan funds thereafter\nremaining to be disbursed by the Senior Lenders under the Financing Agreements. The\nAuthority shall disburse each tranche of the Equity Support as and when due, but no later\nthan 15 (fifteen) days of receiving a request from the Concessionaire along with necessary\nparticulars.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0367",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 367,
    "page_start": 96,
    "page_end": 96,
    "char_start": 208432,
    "char_end": 208629,
    "char_count": 197,
    "text": "26.2.4 In the event of occurrence of a Concessionaire Default, disbursement of Equity Support\nshall be suspended till such Concessionaire Default has been cured by the Concessionaire.\n26.3\nPremium$",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0368",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 368,
    "page_start": 96,
    "page_end": 96,
    "char_start": 208631,
    "char_end": 209004,
    "char_count": 373,
    "text": "The Concessionaire acknowledges and agrees that as set forth in the Bid, it shall pay to the\nAuthority for each year of the Concession Period, but commencing from the day falling\nafter ......... (........) days from the COD, a premium (the “Premium”) in the form of an\nadditional Concession Fee, as set forth in Clause 27.2.1 , and in the manner set forth in\nClause 27.3 .}",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0369",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 369,
    "page_start": 96,
    "page_end": 96,
    "char_start": 209006,
    "char_end": 209297,
    "char_count": 291,
    "text": "$ In the event that the Concessionaire does not seek any Grant from the Authority and offers to pay a\nPremium instead, the provisions of Clauses 27.1, 27.2 and 27.3 relating to Grant shall be substituted by the\nprovisions of Clause 27.4 relating to Premium, which Clause shall be renumbered.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0370",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 370,
    "page_start": 97,
    "page_end": 97,
    "char_start": 209299,
    "char_end": 209301,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "97",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0371",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 371,
    "page_start": 98,
    "page_end": 98,
    "char_start": 209303,
    "char_end": 209305,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "98",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0372",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 372,
    "page_start": 98,
    "page_end": 98,
    "char_start": 209307,
    "char_end": 209353,
    "char_count": 46,
    "text": "ARTICLE 27: CONCESSION FEE\n27.1\nConcession Fee",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0373",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 373,
    "page_start": 98,
    "page_end": 98,
    "char_start": 209355,
    "char_end": 211140,
    "char_count": 1785,
    "text": "In consideration of the grant of Concession, the Concessionaire shall pay to the Authority\nby way of concession fee (the “Concession Fee”) a sum of Re. 1 (Rupee one) per annum\n{and the Premium specified in Clause 27.2}.\n27.2\nAdditional Concession Fee\n27.2.1 Without prejudice to the provisions of Clause 25.1., the Concessionaire agrees to pay to\nthe Authority for the {20th (twentieth) year of the Concession Period}£, a premium (the\n“Premium”) in the form of an additional Concession Fee equal to {1% (one per cent)}$ of\nthe total Realisable Fee during that year, net of any taxes on Fee; and for each subsequent\nyear of the Concession Period, the Premium shall be determined by increasing the\nproportion of Premium to the total Realisable Fee in the respective year by an additional\n1% (one per cent) as compared to the immediately preceding year; provided that the\nPremium payable under this Article 27 shall be subject to a ceiling of 20% (twenty per\ncent) of the total Realisable Fee in the respective year. For the avoidance of doubt and by\nway of illustration, the Premium for the {21st (twenty-first) and 22nd (twenty-second)}\nyears shall be equal to {2% (two per cent) and 3% (three per cent)} respectively of the total\nRealisable Fee for the respective years.\n27.2.2 The Premium payable under Clause 27.2.1 shall be deemed to be part of the Concession\nFee for the purposes of this Agreement.\n27.3\nPayment of Concession Fee\nThe Concession Fee payable under the provisions of this Article 27 shall be due and\npayable in half yearly instalments within 7 (seven) days of the close of each month, the\nConcessionaire shall pay to the Authority against the Concession Fee, a provisional amount\ncalculated on the basis of total Realisable Fee of the immediately preceding month, and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0374",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 374,
    "page_start": 98,
    "page_end": 98,
    "char_start": 211141,
    "char_end": 211355,
    "char_count": 214,
    "text": "final settlement thereof, based on audited accounts of the Concessionaire, shall be made\nwithin 120 (one hundred and twenty) days of completion of the respective Accounting\nYear.\n27.4\nVerification of Realisable Fee",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0375",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 375,
    "page_start": 98,
    "page_end": 98,
    "char_start": 211357,
    "char_end": 211742,
    "char_count": 385,
    "text": "27.4.1 The Authority may, in order to satisfy itself that the Concessionaire is reporting its\nRealisable Fee honestly and faithfully, depute its representatives to the Stations, centralised\ncontrols of automatic Fee collection system and its offices of the concessionaire , and\nundertake such other measures and actions it may deem necessary, to ascertain the actual\nrevenues from Fee.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0376",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 376,
    "page_start": 98,
    "page_end": 98,
    "char_start": 211744,
    "char_end": 212809,
    "char_count": 1065,
    "text": "£ Where the successful bidder has sought a Grant or has not offered any Premium, payment of additional\nConcession Fee shall commence from the 20th (twentieth) year of the Concession Period and the Premium in\nthat year shall be 1% of the total Realisable Fee. Annual increase thereafter shall be in accordance with the\nprovisions of Clause 30.2.1.\n$ In case no Grant is sought by the bidder, it may offer a Premium and specify the reference date for\ncomputation and commencement of its payment, subject always to a ceiling of 20% (twenty per cent) of the\nTotal Realisable Fee. For the avoidance of doubt, the rate of Premium payable by the successful bidder and\nthe date of commencement thereof shall be determined by inviting bids with reference to the number of days\nbefore/after the COD. In the event of the bidder specifying a date prior to COD for giving effect to a Premium\ngreater than 1% (as specified in the curly parenthesis), such higher Premium shall be payable from COD and\nshall be increased annually in accordance with the provisions of Clause 30.2.1.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0377",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 377,
    "page_start": 99,
    "page_end": 99,
    "char_start": 212811,
    "char_end": 212813,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "99",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0378",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 378,
    "page_start": 99,
    "page_end": 99,
    "char_start": 212815,
    "char_end": 214017,
    "char_count": 1202,
    "text": "27.2.2 If the verification of Fee revenues pursuant to this Clause 27.4 demonstrates that the\nRealisable Fee is more than the amount reported by the Concessionaire, the Authority shall,\nfor the purpose of determining the Fee revenues, be entitled to undertake traffic sampling\nfor a continuous period of 7 (seven) days in accordance with Clause 23.3. The Parties\nhereto agree that if the Average Daily Fee revenue determined under this Clause 28.4.2\nexceeds the average daily Realisable Fee reported by the Concessionaire during the\npreceding month by 1% (one percent) thereof, the difference between such Fee revenue\nand Realisable Fee shall be multiplied by 180 (one hundred and eighty) and the product\nthereof shall be paid as Damages by the Concessionaire to the Authority, and in the event\nof any Dispute relating to the traffic sampling, the Dispute Resolution Procedure shall\napply. For the avoidance of doubt, it is agreed that seasonal variations in traffic volume\nshall be determined by the Independent Engineer on the basis of past trends and other\nrelevant information, and due weightage shall be assigned to such variations in computing\nthe Realisable Fee payable under this Clause 28.4.2.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0379",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 379,
    "page_start": 100,
    "page_end": 100,
    "char_start": 214019,
    "char_end": 214022,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "100",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0380",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 380,
    "page_start": 100,
    "page_end": 100,
    "char_start": 214024,
    "char_end": 214333,
    "char_count": 309,
    "text": "ARTICLE 28: USER FEE\n28.1\nCollection and appropriation of Fee\n\n28.1.1 On and from the COD till the Transfer Date, the Concessionaire shall have the sole and\nexclusive right to demand, collect and appropriate Fee from the Users subject to and in\naccordance with the Fee Notification as issued by the Authority.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0381",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 381,
    "page_start": 100,
    "page_end": 100,
    "char_start": 214335,
    "char_end": 214682,
    "char_count": 347,
    "text": "28.1.2 The Concessionaire acknowledges and agrees that upon payment of Fee, any User shall be\nentitled to use the XXX Ropeway and the Concessionaire shall not place, or cause to be\nplaced, any restriction on such use, except to the extent specified in any Applicable Law,\nApplicable Permit or the provisions of this Agreement.\n28.2\nRevision of Fee",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0382",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 382,
    "page_start": 100,
    "page_end": 100,
    "char_start": 214684,
    "char_end": 216467,
    "char_count": 1783,
    "text": "28.2.1  The Parties hereto acknowledge and agree that the Fee shall be revised annually on April\n1 subject to and in accordance with the provisions of the Fee Notification.\n28.3\nDiscounted Fee for frequent Users\n28.3.1   The Concessionaire shall, upon request from any person, issue a return pass on payment of\na sum equal to 180% (one hundred and eighty per cent) of the Fee payable if it were to\nundertake a single one-way trip on the XXX Ropeway. Such return pass shall entitle the\nUser to undertake a return journey on the same day as the outward journey.\n28.3.1   The Concessionaire shall, upon request from any person for issue of a daily pass, issue\nsuch pass on payment of a sum equal to twice the Fee payable if it were to undertake a\nsingle one-way trip on the longest route of the XXX Ropeway. Such daily pass shall entitle\nthe User to unlimited travel on the XXX Ropeway for the date of issue.\n28.3.3 The Concessionaire shall, upon request from any person for issue of a weekly pass, issue\nsuch pass on payment of a sum equal to ten times the Fee payable if it were to undertake a\nsingle one-way trip on the selected section of the XXX Ropeway. Such weekly pass shall\nentitle the User to unlimited travel on such section of the XXX Ropeway for one week\nfrom the date of issue.\n28.3.4 The Concessionaire shall, upon request from any person for issue of a monthly pass, issue\nsuch pass on payment of a sum equal to forty times the Fee payable if it were to undertake\na single one-way trip on the selected section of the XXX Ropeway. Such monthly pass\nshall entitle the User to unlimited travel on such section of the XXX Ropeway for one\nmonth from the date of issue.\n28.4\nFee Contractor\nThe Concessionaire may appoint a Fee Contractor or any other person to collect the Fee",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0383",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 383,
    "page_start": 100,
    "page_end": 100,
    "char_start": 216468,
    "char_end": 216900,
    "char_count": 432,
    "text": "for and on behalf of the Concessionaire, provided that notwithstanding such appointment,\nthe Concessionaire shall be and remain solely liable and responsible for the collection of\nFee in accordance with this Agreement and its deposit into the Escrow Account and for\ncompliance with the provisions of this Agreement.\n28.5\nFee collection points\nThe Concessionaire shall be entitled to set up at its own risk and cost, its temporary or",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0384",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 384,
    "page_start": 101,
    "page_end": 101,
    "char_start": 216902,
    "char_end": 216905,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "101",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0385",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 385,
    "page_start": 101,
    "page_end": 101,
    "char_start": 216907,
    "char_end": 218703,
    "char_count": 1796,
    "text": "permanent Fee collection counters and gates, or impose such other restrictions on entry to\nthe XXX Ropeway, as may reasonably be necessary for preventing evasion of Fee. For the\navoidance of doubt, the Concessionaire hereby acknowledges and agrees that it shall\nestablish and operate a system of Fee collection in conformity with Good Industry Practice.\n28.6\nAdditional charge for evasion of Fee\nIn the event that any person uses the XXX Ropeway without payment of Fee due, the\nConcessionaire shall, subject to Applicable Law and Applicable Permits, be entitled to\ndetermine and collect from such person the Fee due and  thrice the amount thereof towards\npredetermined liquidated damages for attempt to make unauthorised use of the XXX\nRopeway; provided that the determination and collection of such Fee and liquidated\ndamages shall be at the risk and cost of the Concessionaire and the Authority shall not in\nany manner be liable on account thereof.\n28.7\nDifferential Fee\n28.7.1\nThe Concessionaire may, after obtaining prior written approval of the Authority which\napproval the Authority may in its discretion deny, determine and collect a higher and\ndiscounted  Fee (the “Differential Fee”) for use of the XXX Ropeway during peak and\noff-peak hours respectively in accordance with this Clause 28.7 For the avoidance of\ndoubt, the provisions of this Clause 28.7 shall not apply to passes or tickets, as the case\nmay be, issued under Clause 28.3.\n28.7.2\nThe Concessionaire may designate not more than 4 (four) hours in a day as peak hours\nand a period equal to twice the peak hours as off-peak hours. The Concessionaire may\ndetermine and collect a premium of up to 25% (twenty-five per cent) of the Fee during\npeak hours or such higher premium as the Authority may by order permit. Simultaneously",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0386",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 386,
    "page_start": 101,
    "page_end": 101,
    "char_start": 218704,
    "char_end": 218988,
    "char_count": 284,
    "text": "with such premium on peak hour Fee, the Concessionaire shall offer a discount during\noff-peak hours at a rate equal to the said premium. For the avoidance of doubt, the\ndetermination of Differential Fee shall be with reference to the time of entry of a User.\n28.8\nDisplay of Fee Rates",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0387",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 387,
    "page_start": 101,
    "page_end": 101,
    "char_start": 218990,
    "char_end": 219156,
    "char_count": 166,
    "text": "28.8.1 The Concessionaire shall conspicuously display the Fee structure at each of the terminal\nStations of the Project at least in English, Hindi and local language.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0388",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 388,
    "page_start": 101,
    "page_end": 101,
    "char_start": 219158,
    "char_end": 219385,
    "char_count": 227,
    "text": "28.8.2 The Concessionaire shall, from time to time, inform the Authority of the applicable Fee.\nSuch information shall be communicated at least **** days prior to the revision of Fee\nunder and in accordance with this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0389",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 389,
    "page_start": 101,
    "page_end": 101,
    "char_start": 219387,
    "char_end": 219768,
    "char_count": 381,
    "text": "28.8.3 The Concessionaire shall not revise, display or collect any amounts in excess of the rates\nof Fee payable under this Agreement. In the event any excess amounts are collected by or\non behalf of the Concessionaire, it shall, upon receiving a notice to this effect from the\nAuthority, refund such excess amounts to the Authority along with Damages equal to\n****percent thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0390",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
