    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0391",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 391,
    "page_start": 102,
    "page_end": 102,
    "char_start": 219775,
    "char_end": 220427,
    "char_count": 652,
    "text": "ARTICLE 29: REVENUE SHORTFALL LOAN\n29.1\nRevenue Shortfall Loan\n29.1.1 If the Realisable Fee in any Accounting Year shall fall short of the Subsistence Revenue\nas a result of an Indirect Political Event, a Political Event or a Authority Default, as the\ncase may be, the Authority shall, upon request of the Concessionaire, provide a loan for\nmeeting such shortfall (the “Revenue Shortfall Loan”) at an interest rate equal to 2% (two\nper cent) above the Bank Rate.\n29.1.2 If the half-yearly results of the Concessionaire indicate that the shortfall referred to in\nClause 29.1.1 and contemplated for an Accounting Year has arisen in respect of the first 6",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0392",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 392,
    "page_start": 102,
    "page_end": 102,
    "char_start": 220428,
    "char_end": 222065,
    "char_count": 1637,
    "text": "(six) months thereof, the Concessionaire shall be entitled to a provisional Revenue\nShortfall Loan; provided that, no later than 60 (sixty) days after the close of such\nAccounting Year, the Concessionaire shall either repay the provisional loan with interest\nor adjust it against the Revenue Shortfall Loan, if any, as may be due to it under this Clause\n29.1.\n29.1.3 The Authority shall disburse the Revenue Shortfall Loan or the provisional Revenue\nShortfall Loan, as the case may be, within 30 (thirty) days of receiving a valid request from\nthe Concessionaire along with the particulars thereof including a detailed account of the\nIndirect Political Event, Political Event or the Authority Default, as the case may be, and\nits impact on the collection of Fee.\n29.2\nRepayment of Revenue Shortfall Loan\nA sum equal to 50% (fifty per cent) of the ‘profit before tax’ of the Concessionaire, as and\nwhen made, shall be earmarked for repayment of the Revenue Shortfall Loan and interest\nthereon, and paid by the Concessionaire to the Authority within 90 (ninety) days of the\nclose of the Accounting Year in which such profits have been made; provided that the\nConcessionaire shall repay the entire Revenue Shortfall Loan and interest thereon no later\nthan one year prior to the expiry of the Concession Period and in the event that any sum\nremains due or outstanding at any time during such period of one year, the Authority shall\nbe entitled to terminate this Agreement forthwith. For the avoidance of doubt, it is agreed\nthat the repayment of Revenue Shortfall Loan shall be in accordance with and subject to\nthe provisions of Article 32.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0393",
