    "page_end": 222,
    "char_start": 410938,
    "char_end": 411353,
    "char_count": 415,
    "text": "SCHEDULE – I\nSELECTION OF INDEPENDENT ENGINEER\n(See Clauses 24.1 and 24.2\n1.\nSelection of Independent Engineer\n1.1\nThe provisions of Part II of the Standard Bidding Documents for Consulting Assignments.\nTime Based (Volume V) issued by the Ministry of Finance, GOI in July, 1997 or any\nsubstitute thereof shall apply, mutatis mutandis, for invitation of bids and evaluation\nthereof save as otherwise provided herein.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0725",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 725,
    "page_start": 222,
    "page_end": 222,
    "char_start": 411355,
    "char_end": 412283,
    "char_count": 928,
    "text": "1.2\nThe Authority shall invite expressions of interest from consulting engineering firms or\nbodies corporate to undertake and perform the duties and functions set forth in Schedule -\nR and thereupon shortlist 6 (six) qualified firms in accordance with pre-determined criteria.\nThe Authority shall convey the aforesaid list of firms to the Concessionaire for scrutiny\nand comments, if any. The Concessionaire shall be entitled to scrutinise the relevant\nrecords of the Authority to ascertain whether the selection of firms has been undertaken in\naccordance with the prescribed procedure and it shall send its comments, if any, to the\nAuthority within 15 (fifteen) days of receiving the aforesaid list of firms. Upon receipt of\nsuch comments, if any, the Authority shall, after considering all relevant factors, finalise\nand constitute a panel of 6 (six) firms (the “Panel of Firms”) and convey its decision to\nthe Concessionaire.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0726",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 726,
    "page_start": 222,
    "page_end": 222,
    "char_start": 412285,
    "char_end": 414029,
    "char_count": 1744,
    "text": "1.3\nThe Authority shall invite the aforesaid firms in the Panel of Firms to submit their\nrespective technical and financial offers, each in a separate sealed cover. All the technical\nbids so received shall be opened and pursuant to the evaluation thereof, the Authority shall\nshortlist 3 (three) eligible firms on the basis of their technical scores. The financial bids in\nrespect of such 3 (three) firms shall be opened and the order of priority as among these\nfirms shall be determined on the basis of a weighted evaluation where technical and\nfinancial scores shall be assigned respective weights of 80:20.\n1.4\nIn the event that the Authority shall follow the selection process specified in the Model\nRFP for selection of Technical Consultant, as published by the Ministry of Finance, the\nselection process specified in this Schedule – I shall be deemed to be substituted by the\nprovisions of the said Model RFP and the Concessionaire shall be entitled to scrutinize the\nrelevant records forming part of such selection process.\n2.\nFee and expenses\n2.1        In determining the nature and quantum of duties and services to be performed by the\nIndependent Engineer during the Development Period and Construction Period, the\nAuthority shall endeavour that payments to the Independent Engineer on account of fee\nand expenses do not exceed [1% (one per cent)] of the Total Project Cost, including Equity\nSupport, if any. Payments not exceeding such [1% (one per cent)] shall be borne equally\nby the Authority and the Concessionaire in accordance with the provisions of this\nAgreement and any payments in excess thereof shall be borne entirely by the Authority.\n2.2\nThe nature and quantum of duties and services to be performed by the Independent",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0727",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 727,
    "page_start": 222,
    "page_end": 222,
    "char_start": 414030,
    "char_end": 414291,
    "char_count": 261,
    "text": "Engineer during the Operation Period shall be determined by the Authority in conformity\nwith the provisions of this Agreement and with due regard for economy in expenditure. All\npayments made to the Independent Engineer on account of fee and expenses during the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0728",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 728,
    "page_start": 223,
    "page_end": 223,
    "char_start": 414293,
    "char_end": 414296,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "223",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0729",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 729,
    "page_start": 223,
    "page_end": 223,
    "char_start": 414298,
    "char_end": 415306,
    "char_count": 1008,
    "text": "Operation Period, including the construction of system augmentation, shall be borne\nequally by the Authority and the Concessionaire.\n3.\nSelection every three years\n3.1\nNo later than 3 (three) years from the date of appointment of the Independent Engineer, in\naccordance with the provisions of Paragraph 1 of this Schedule-I, the Authority shall\nengage another firm in accordance with the criteria set forth in this Schedule-I.\n4.\nAppointment of government entity as Independent Engineer\n4.1\n[Notwithstanding anything to the contrary contained in this Schedule - I, the Authority may\nin its discretion appoint a government-owned entity as the Independent Engineer; provided\nthat such entity shall be a  body  corporate  having as one of its primary function the\nprovision of consulting, advisory and supervisory services for engineering projects;\nprovided further that a government- owned entity which is owned or controlled by the\nAuthority shall not  be eligible for appointment as an Independent Engineer.]",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0730",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 730,
    "page_start": 224,
    "page_end": 224,
    "char_start": 415308,
    "char_end": 415311,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "224",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0731",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 731,
    "page_start": 224,
    "page_end": 224,
    "char_start": 415313,
    "char_end": 415837,
    "char_count": 524,
    "text": "(Annex-1)\n\nI.\nTERMS OF REFERENCE FOR INDEPENDENT ENGINEER\n\n1.\nScope\n1.1\nThese Terms of Reference for the Independent Engineer (the “TOR”) are being specified\nin accordance with the Concession Agreement dated.………. (the “Agreement”), which\nhas been entered into between the Authority and………………... (the “Concessionaire”)\nfor XXX Ropeway at ...………. corridor in city of.………. on design, build, finance,\noperate and transfer (the “DBFOT”) basis, and a copy of which is annexed hereto and\nmarked as Annex-A to form part of this TOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0732",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 732,
    "page_start": 224,
    "page_end": 224,
    "char_start": 415839,
    "char_end": 415993,
    "char_count": 154,
    "text": "1.2\nThis TOR shall apply to construction, operation and maintenance of the XXX Ropeway,\nand shall apply, mutatis mutandis, to system augmentation thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0733",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 733,
    "page_start": 224,
    "page_end": 224,
    "char_start": 415995,
    "char_end": 416353,
    "char_count": 358,
    "text": "The TOR for the appointment of the Independent Engineer will be as follows:\n\n2.\nDefinitions and Interpretation\n2.1        The words and expressions beginning with or in capital letters used in this TOR and not\ndefined herein but defined in the Agreement shall have, unless repugnant to the context,\nthe meaning respectively assigned to them in the Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0734",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 734,
    "page_start": 224,
    "page_end": 224,
    "char_start": 416355,
    "char_end": 416647,
    "char_count": 292,
    "text": "2.2       References to Articles, Clauses and Schedules in this TOR shall, except where the context\notherwise requires, be deemed to be references to the Articles, Clauses and Schedules of\nthe Agreement, and references to Paragraphs shall be deemed to be references to\nParagraphs of this TOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0735",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 735,
    "page_start": 224,
    "page_end": 224,
    "char_start": 416649,
    "char_end": 416772,
    "char_count": 123,
    "text": "The rules of interpretation stated in Clauses 1.2, 1.3 and 1.4 of the Agreement shall apply, mutatis\nmutandis, to this TOR.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0736",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 736,
    "page_start": 224,
    "page_end": 224,
    "char_start": 416774,
    "char_end": 417693,
    "char_count": 919,
    "text": "3.\nRole and functions of the Independent Engineer\n3.1\nThe role and functions of the Independent Engineer shall include the following:\n(i)\nreview of the Drawings and Documents as set forth in Paragraph 4;\n(ii)\nreview, inspection and monitoring of Construction Works as set forth in Paragraph\n5;\n(iii)\nreview, inspection and testing of rolling stock as set forth in Paragraph 5;\n(iv)\nconducting Tests on completion of construction and issuing Completion/\nProvisional Certificate as set forth in Paragraph 5;\n(v)\nreview, inspection and monitoring of O&M as set forth in Paragraph 6;\n(vi)\nreview, inspection and monitoring of Divestment Requirements as set forth in\nParagraph 7;\n(vii)\ndetermining, as required under the Agreement, the costs of any works or services\nand/or their reasonableness;\n(viii)\ndetermining, as required under the Agreement, the period or any extension thereof,\nfor performing any duty or obligation;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0737",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 737,
    "page_start": 225,
    "page_end": 225,
    "char_start": 417695,
    "char_end": 417698,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "225",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0738",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 738,
    "page_start": 225,
    "page_end": 225,
    "char_start": 417700,
    "char_end": 418022,
    "char_count": 322,
    "text": "(ix)       assisting the Parties in resolution of disputes as set forth in Paragraph 9; and\n(x)\nundertaking   all   other   duties   and   functions   in   accordance   with   the\nAgreement.\n3.2\nThe role and functions of the Independent Engineer shall not include construction works\ncomprising the Real Estate Development.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0739",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 739,
    "page_start": 225,
    "page_end": 225,
    "char_start": 418024,
    "char_end": 418214,
    "char_count": 190,
    "text": "3.3\nThe Independent Engineer shall discharge its duties in a fair, impartial and efficient\nmanner, consistent with the highest standards of professional integrity and Good Industry\nPractice.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0740",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 740,
    "page_start": 225,
    "page_end": 225,
    "char_start": 418216,
    "char_end": 418881,
    "char_count": 665,
    "text": "4\nDevelopment Period\n\n4.1\n During the Development Period, the Independent Engineer shall undertake a detailed\nreview of the Drawings to be furnished by the Concessionaire along with supporting data,\nincluding the geo-technical and hydrological investigations, characteristics of materials,\ntopographical surveys and traffic surveys. The Independent Engineer shall complete such\nreview and send its comments/observations to the Authority and the Concessionaire within\n15 (fifteen) days of receipt of such Drawings. In particular, such comments shall specify\nthe conformity or otherwise of such Drawings with the Scope of the Project and\nSpecifications and Standards.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0741",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 741,
    "page_start": 225,
    "page_end": 225,
    "char_start": 418883,
    "char_end": 419091,
    "char_count": 208,
    "text": "4.2\nThe Independent Engineer shall review any modified Drawings or supporting Documents\nsent to it by the Concessionaire and furnish its comments within 7 (seven) days of receiving\nsuch Drawings or Documents.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0742",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 742,
    "page_start": 225,
    "page_end": 225,
    "char_start": 419093,
    "char_end": 419502,
    "char_count": 409,
    "text": "4.3     The Independent Engineer shall review the Drawings sent to it by the Safety Consultant in\naccordance with Schedule-M and furnish its comments thereon to the Authority and the\nConcessionaire within 7 (seven) days of receiving such Drawings. The Independent\nEngineer shall also review the Safety Report and furnish its comments thereon to the\nAuthority within 15 (fifteen) days of receiving such report.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0743",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 743,
    "page_start": 225,
    "page_end": 225,
    "char_start": 419504,
    "char_end": 419792,
    "char_count": 288,
    "text": "4.4     The Independent Engineer shall review the detailed design, construction methodology,\nquality assurance procedures and the procurement, engineering and construction time\nschedule sent to it by the Concessionaire and furnish its comments within 15 (fifteen) days\nof receipt thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0744",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 744,
    "page_start": 225,
    "page_end": 225,
    "char_start": 419794,
    "char_end": 420040,
    "char_count": 246,
    "text": "4.5\nThe Independent Engineer shall review the detailed design, manufacturing, installation,\ntesting and commissioning plans for the XXX Ropeway sent to it by the Concessionaire\nand furnish its comments within 15 (fifteen) days of receipt thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0745",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 745,
    "page_start": 225,
    "page_end": 225,
    "char_start": 420042,
    "char_end": 420332,
    "char_count": 290,
    "text": "4.6\n Upon reference by the Authority, the Independent Engineer shall review and comment on\nthe EPC contract or any other contract for construction, operation and maintenance of the\nXXX Ropeway and furnish its comments within 7 (seven) days from receipt of such\nreference from the Authority.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0746",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 746,
    "page_start": 225,
    "page_end": 225,
    "char_start": 420334,
    "char_end": 420575,
    "char_count": 241,
    "text": "5.\nConstruction Period\n\n5.1\nIn respect of the Drawings, Documents and Safety Report received by the Independent\nEngineer for its review and comments during the Construction Period, the provisions of\nParagraph 4 shall apply, mutatis mutandis.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0747",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 747,
    "page_start": 225,
    "page_end": 225,
    "char_start": 420577,
    "char_end": 420748,
    "char_count": 171,
    "text": "5.2\nThe Independent Engineer shall review the monthly progress report furnished by the\nConcessionaire and send its comments thereon to the Authority and the Concessionaire",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0748",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 748,
    "page_start": 226,
    "page_end": 226,
    "char_start": 420750,
    "char_end": 420753,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "226",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0749",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 749,
    "page_start": 226,
    "page_end": 226,
    "char_start": 420755,
    "char_end": 421834,
    "char_count": 1079,
    "text": "within 7 (seven) days of receipt of such report.\n\n5.3\nThe Independent Engineer shall inspect the Construction Works and electromechanical\nequipment (if any) once every month, preferably after receipt of the monthly progress\nreport from the Concessionaire, but before the 20th(twentieth)day of each month in any\ncase, and make out a report of such inspection (the “Inspection Report”) setting forth an\noverview of the status, progress, quality and safety of construction, including the work\nmethodology adopted, the materials used and their sources, and conformity of Construction\nWorks and electromechanical with the Scope of the Project and the Specifications and\nStandards. In a separate section of the Inspection Report, the Independent Engineer shall\ndescribe in reasonable detail the lapses, defects or deficiencies observed by it in the\nconstruction of the XXX Ropeway or the deficiencies in the electromechanical equipment.\nThe Independent Engineer shall send a copy of its Inspection Report to the Authority and\nthe Concessionaire within 7 (seven) days of the inspection.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0750",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 750,
    "page_start": 226,
    "page_end": 226,
    "char_start": 421836,
    "char_end": 421983,
    "char_count": 147,
    "text": "5.4\nThe Independent Engineer may inspect the XXX Ropeway more than once in a month if\nany lapses, defects or deficiencies require such inspections.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0751",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 751,
    "page_start": 226,
    "page_end": 226,
    "char_start": 421985,
    "char_end": 423783,
    "char_count": 1798,
    "text": "5.5\nFor determining that the Construction Works conform to Specifications and Standards, the\nIndependent Engineer shall require the Concessionaire to carry out, or cause to be carried\nout, tests on a sample basis, to be specified by the Independent Engineer in accordance\nwith Good Industry Practice for quality assurance. For purposes of this Paragraph 5.5, the\ntests specified in the IRC Special Publication-47 {Guidelines on Quality systems for Road\nBridge (Plain, Reinforced, Pre-stressed and Composite Concrete)} and other relevant\nManuals specified by the Authority in relation to structures, buildings, track, equipment\nand rolling stock (the “Quality Control Manuals”) or any modification/substitution\nthereof shall be deemed to be tests conforming to Good Industry Practice for quality\nassurance. The Independent Engineer shall issue necessary directions to the Concessionaire\nfor ensuring that the tests are conducted in a fair and efficient manner, and shall monitor\nand review the results thereof.\n5.6\nThe sample size of the tests, to be specified by the Independent Engineer under Paragraph\n5.5, shall comprise 10% (ten per cent) of the quantity or number of tests prescribed for\neach category or type of tests in the Quality Control Manuals; provided that the\nIndependent Engineer may, for reasons to be recorded in writing, increase the aforesaid\nsample size by up to 10% (ten per cent) for certain categories or types of tests.\n5.7\nThe timing of tests referred to in Paragraph 5.5, and the criteria for acceptance/ rejection\nof their results shall be determined by the Independent Engineer in accordance with the\nQuality Control Manuals. The tests shall be undertaken on a random sample basis and shall\nbe in addition to, and independent of, the tests that may be carried out by the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0752",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 752,
    "page_start": 226,
    "page_end": 226,
    "char_start": 423784,
    "char_end": 423870,
    "char_count": 86,
    "text": "Concessionaire for its own quality assurance in accordance with Good Industry Practice",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0753",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 753,
    "page_start": 226,
    "page_end": 226,
    "char_start": 423872,
    "char_end": 424567,
    "char_count": 695,
    "text": "5.5\nIn the event that the Concessionaire fails to achieve any of the Project Milestones, the\nIndependent Engineer shall undertake a review of the progress of construction and identify\npotential delays, if any. If the Independent Engineer shall determine that completion of the\nXXX Ropeway is not feasible within the time specified in the Agreement, it shall require\nthe Concessionaire to indicate within 15 (fifteen) days the steps proposed to be taken to\nexpedite progress, and the period within which COD shall be achieved. Upon receipt of a\nreport from the Concessionaire, the Independent Engineer shall review the same and send\nits comments to the Authority and the Concessionaire forthwith.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0754",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 754,
    "page_start": 226,
    "page_end": 226,
    "char_start": 424569,
    "char_end": 424744,
    "char_count": 175,
    "text": "5.6\nIf at any time during the Construction Period, the Independent Engineer determines that\nthe Concessionaire has not made adequate arrangements for the safety of workers and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0755",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 755,
    "page_start": 227,
    "page_end": 227,
    "char_start": 424746,
    "char_end": 425070,
    "char_count": 324,
    "text": "227\n\nUsers in the zone of construction or that any work is being carried out in a manner that\nthreatens the safety of the workers and the Users, it shall make a recommendation to the\nAuthority forthwith, identifying the whole or part of the Construction Works that should\nbe suspended for ensuring safety in respect thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0756",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 756,
    "page_start": 227,
    "page_end": 227,
    "char_start": 425072,
    "char_end": 425517,
    "char_count": 445,
    "text": "5.7\nIn the event that the Concessionaire carries out any remedial measures to secure the safety\nof suspended works and Users, it may, by notice in writing, require the Independent\nEngineer to inspect such works, and within 3 (three) days of receiving such notice, the\nIndependent Engineer shall inspect the suspended works and make a report to the Authority\nforthwith, recommending whether or not such suspension may be revoked by the\nAuthority.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0757",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 757,
    "page_start": 227,
    "page_end": 227,
    "char_start": 425519,
    "char_end": 425842,
    "char_count": 323,
    "text": "5.8\nIf Suspension of Construction Works is for reasons not attributable to the Concessionaire,\nthe Independent Engineer shall determine the extension of dates set forth in the Project\nCompletion Schedule, to which the Concessionaire is reasonably entitled, and shall notify\nthe Authority and the Concessionaire of the same.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0758",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 758,
    "page_start": 227,
    "page_end": 227,
    "char_start": 425844,
    "char_end": 425995,
    "char_count": 151,
    "text": "5.9     The Independent Engineer shall carry out, or cause to be carried out, all the Tests specified\nin Schedule-I and issue a Completion Certificate.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0759",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 759,
    "page_start": 227,
    "page_end": 227,
    "char_start": 425997,
    "char_end": 426203,
    "char_count": 206,
    "text": "5.10\nFor carrying out its functions under this Paragraph 5.10 and all matters incidental thereto,\nthe Independent Engineer shall act under and in accordance with the provisions of Article\n14 and Schedule-I.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0760",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 760,
    "page_start": 227,
    "page_end": 227,
    "char_start": 426205,
    "char_end": 426597,
    "char_count": 392,
    "text": "5.11\nUpon reference from the Authority, the Independent Engineer shall make a fair and\nreasonable assessment of the costs of providing information, works and services as set forth\nin Article 16 and certify the reasonableness of such costs for payment by the Authority to\nthe Concessionaire. The Independent Engineer shall aid and advise the Concessionaire in\npreparing the Maintenance Manual.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0761",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 761,
    "page_start": 227,
    "page_end": 227,
    "char_start": 426599,
    "char_end": 426833,
    "char_count": 234,
    "text": "6\nOperation Period\n\n6.1\nIn respect of the Drawings, Documents and Safety Report received by the Independent\nEngineer for its review and comments during the Operation Period, the provisions of\nParagraph 4 shall apply, mutatis mutandis.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0762",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 762,
    "page_start": 227,
    "page_end": 227,
    "char_start": 426835,
    "char_end": 427082,
    "char_count": 247,
    "text": "6.2      The Independent Engineer shall review the annual Maintenance Programme furnished by\nthe Concessionaire and send its comments thereon to the Authority and the Concessionaire\nwithin 15 (fifteen) days of receipt of the Maintenance Programme.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0763",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 763,
    "page_start": 227,
    "page_end": 227,
    "char_start": 427084,
    "char_end": 427302,
    "char_count": 218,
    "text": "6.3\nThe Independent Engineer shall review the monthly status report furnished by the\nConcessionaire and send its comments thereon to the Authority and the Concessionaire\nwithin 7 (seven) days of receipt of such report.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0764",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 764,
    "page_start": 227,
    "page_end": 227,
    "char_start": 427304,
    "char_end": 428127,
    "char_count": 823,
    "text": "6.4       The Independent Engineer shall inspect the XXX Ropeway, including carriers and\nStations, once every month, preferably after receipt of the monthly status report from the\nConcessionaire, but before the 20th (twentieth)  day  of  each  month in any case, and make\nout an O&M Inspection Report setting forth an overview of the status, quality and safety\nof O&M including its conformity with the Key Performance Indicators, Maintenance\nRequirements and Safety Requirements. In a separate section of the O&M Inspection\nReport, the Independent Engineer shall describe in reasonable detail the lapses, defects or\ndeficiencies observed by it in O&M of the XXX Ropeway. The Independent Engineer shall\nsend a copy of its O&M Inspection Report to the Authority and the Concessionaire within\n7 (seven) days of the inspection.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0765",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 765,
    "page_start": 228,
    "page_end": 228,
    "char_start": 428129,
    "char_end": 428287,
    "char_count": 158,
    "text": "228\n\n6.5      The Independent Engineer may inspect the XXX Ropeway more than once in a month, if\nany lapses, defects or deficiencies require such inspections.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0766",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 766,
    "page_start": 228,
    "page_end": 228,
    "char_start": 428289,
    "char_end": 429084,
    "char_count": 795,
    "text": "6.6\nThe Independent Engineer shall in its O&M Inspection Report specify the tests, if any, that\nthe Concessionaire shall carry out, or cause to be carried out, for the purpose of determining\nthat the XXX Ropeway is in conformity with the Maintenance Requirements. It shall\nmonitor and review the results of such tests and the remedial measures, if any, taken by the\nConcessionaire in this behalf. In respect of any defect or deficiency referred to in Paragraph\n3 of Schedule - L, the Independent Engineer shall, in conformity with Good Industry\nPractice, specify the permissible limit of deviation or deterioration with reference to the\nSpecifications and Standards and shall also specify the time limit for repair or rectification\nof any deviation or deterioration beyond the permissible limit.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0767",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 767,
    "page_start": 228,
    "page_end": 228,
    "char_start": 429087,
    "char_end": 429346,
    "char_count": 259,
    "text": "6.7     The Independent Engineer shall determine if any delay has occurred in completion of repair\nor remedial works in accordance with the Agreement, and shall also determine the\nDamages, if any, payable by the Concessionaire to the Authority for such delay.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0768",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 768,
    "page_start": 228,
    "page_end": 228,
    "char_start": 429348,
    "char_end": 430038,
    "char_count": 690,
    "text": "6.8\nThe Independent Engineer shall examine the request of the Concessionaire for closure of\nthe XXX Ropeway for undertaking maintenance/repair thereof, keeping in view the need\nto minimize disruption in traffic and the time required for completing such\nmaintenance/repair in accordance with Good Industry Practice. It shall grant permission\nwith such modifications, as it may deem necessary, within 3 (three) days of receiving a\nrequest from the Concessionaire. Upon expiry of the permitted period of closure, the\nIndependent Engineer shall monitor the re-opening of such rope(s), and in case of delay,\ndetermine the Damages payable by the Concessionaire to the Authority under Clause 17.7.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0769",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 769,
    "page_start": 228,
    "page_end": 228,
    "char_start": 430040,
    "char_end": 430183,
    "char_count": 143,
    "text": "6.9\nThe Independent Engineer shall monitor and review the curing of defects and deficiencies\nby the Concessionaire as set forth in Clause 19.4.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0770",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 770,
    "page_start": 228,
    "page_end": 228,
    "char_start": 430185,
    "char_end": 430489,
    "char_count": 304,
    "text": "6.10   In the event that the Concessionaire notifies the Independent Engineer of any modifications\nthat it proposes to make to the XXX Ropeway, the Independent Engineer shall review the\nsame and send its comments to the Authority and the Concessionaire within 15 (fifteen)\ndays of receiving the proposal.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0771",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 771,
    "page_start": 228,
    "page_end": 228,
    "char_start": 430491,
    "char_end": 430653,
    "char_count": 162,
    "text": "6.11    In Independent Engineer shall undertake traffic sampling, as and when required by the\nAuthority, under and in accordance with Article 23 and Schedule – O.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0772",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 772,
    "page_start": 228,
    "page_end": 228,
    "char_start": 430655,
    "char_end": 430945,
    "char_count": 290,
    "text": "7.\nAudit of Fee collection system\n\n7.1\nThe Independent Engineer shall, at least once every month, conduct an audit of the working\nof the automatic fee collection system installed by the Concessionaire, to check its accuracy\nin recording the entry and exit of Users and in recording the fee.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0773",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 773,
    "page_start": 228,
    "page_end": 228,
    "char_start": 430947,
    "char_end": 431728,
    "char_count": 781,
    "text": "8.\nTermination\n\n8.1\nAt any time, not earlier than 90 (ninety) days prior to Termination but not later than 15\n(fifteen) days prior to such Termination, the Independent Engineer shall, in the presence of\na representative of the Concessionaire, inspect the XXX Ropeway for determining\ncompliance by the Concessionaire with the Divestment Requirements set forth in Clause\n39.1  and, if required, cause tests to be carried  out at the Concessionaire’s cost for\ndetermining such compliance. If the Independent Engineer determines that the status of the\nXXX Ropeway is such that its repair and rectification would require a larger amount than\nthe sum set forth in Clause 40.2, it shall recommend retention of the required amount in\nthe Escrow Account and the period of retention thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0774",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 774,
    "page_start": 229,
    "page_end": 229,
    "char_start": 431730,
    "char_end": 432187,
    "char_count": 457,
    "text": "229\n\n8.2\nThe Independent Engineer shall inspect the XXX Ropeway once in every 15(fifteen) days\nduring a period of 90 (ninety) days after Termination for determining the liability of the\nConcessionaire under Article 43, in respect of the defects or deficiencies specified therein.\nIf any such defect or deficiency is found by the Independent Engineer, it shall make a report\nin reasonable detail and send it forthwith to the Authority and the Concessionaire.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0775",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 775,
    "page_start": 229,
    "page_end": 229,
    "char_start": 432189,
    "char_end": 432511,
    "char_count": 322,
    "text": "9.\nDetermination of costs and time\n\n9.1\nThe Independent Engineer shall determine the costs, and/or their reasonableness, that are\nrequired to be determined by it under the Agreement. The Independent Engineer shall\ndetermine the period, or any extension thereof, that is required to be determined by it under\nthe Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0776",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 776,
    "page_start": 229,
    "page_end": 229,
    "char_start": 432513,
    "char_end": 433056,
    "char_count": 543,
    "text": "10.\nAssistance in Dispute resolution\n\n10.1\nWhen called upon by either Party in the event of any Dispute, the Independent Engineer\nshall mediate and assist the Parties in arriving at an amicable settlement. In the event of\nany disagreement between the Parties regarding the meaning, scope and nature of Good\nIndustry Practice, as set forth in any provision of the Agreement, the Independent Engineer\nshall specify such meaning, scope and nature by issuing a reasoned written statement\nrelying on Good Industry Practice and authentic literature.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0777",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 777,
    "page_start": 229,
    "page_end": 229,
    "char_start": 433058,
    "char_end": 433210,
    "char_count": 152,
    "text": "11.\nOther duties and functions\n\n11.1\nThe Independent Engineer shall perform all other duties and functions specified in the\nAgreement.\n12.\nMiscellaneous",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0778",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 778,
    "page_start": 229,
    "page_end": 229,
    "char_start": 433212,
    "char_end": 433433,
    "char_count": 221,
    "text": "12.1\nThe Independent Engineer shall notify its programme of inspection to the Authority and to\nthe Concessionaire, who may, in their discretion, depute their respective representatives to\nbe present during the inspection.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0779",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 779,
    "page_start": 229,
    "page_end": 229,
    "char_start": 433435,
    "char_end": 433752,
    "char_count": 317,
    "text": "12.2\nA copy of all communications, comments, instructions, Drawings or Documents sent by\nthe Independent Engineer to the Concessionaire pursuant to this TOR, and a copy of all the\ntest results with comments of the Independent Engineer thereon shall be furnished by the\nIndependent Engineer to the Authority forthwith.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0780",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 780,
    "page_start": 229,
    "page_end": 229,
    "char_start": 433754,
    "char_end": 434108,
    "char_count": 354,
    "text": "12.3\nThe Independent Engineer shall obtain and the Concessionaire shall furnish in 2 (two)\ncopies thereof, all communications and reports required to be submitted, under this\nAgreement, by the Concessionaire to the Independent Engineer, whereupon the\nIndependent Engineer shall send 1 (one) of the copies to the Authority along with its\ncomments thereon.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0781",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 781,
    "page_start": 229,
    "page_end": 229,
    "char_start": 434110,
    "char_end": 434287,
    "char_count": 177,
    "text": "12.4\nThe Independent Engineer shall retain at least one copy each of all Drawings and\nDocuments received by it, including ‘as-built’ Drawings, and keep them in its safe custody.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0782",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 782,
    "page_start": 229,
    "page_end": 229,
    "char_start": 434289,
    "char_end": 434741,
    "char_count": 452,
    "text": "12.5\nUpon completion of its assignment hereunder, the Independent Engineer shall duly classify\nand list all Drawings, Documents, results of tests and other relevant records, and hand them\nover to the Authority or such other person as the Authority may specify and obtain written\nreceipt thereof. Two copies of the said documents shall also be furnished in editable digital\nformat or in such other medium or manner as may be acceptable to the Authority.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0783",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 783,
    "page_start": 230,
    "page_end": 230,
    "char_start": 434743,
    "char_end": 435817,
    "char_count": 1074,
    "text": "230\n\nSCHEDULE – J\n(See Clause 14.1.2)\nTEST\n\n1\nSchedule for Tests\n\n1.1\nThe Concessionaire shall, no later than 60 (sixty) days prior to the likely completion of the\nXXX Ropeway, notify the Independent Engineer and the Authority of its intent to subject\nthe XXX Ropeway to Tests, and no later than 7 (seven) days prior to the actual date of\nTests, furnish to the Independent Engineer and the Authority detailed inventory and\nparticulars of all works and equipment forming part of the XXX Ropeway.\n1.2\nThe Concessionaire shall notify the Independent Engineer of its readiness to subject the\nXXX Ropeway to Tests at any time after 7 (seven) days from the date of such notice, and\nupon receipt of such notice, the Independent Engineer shall, in consultation with the\nConcessionaire, determine the date and time for each Test and notify the same to the\nAuthority who may designate its representative to witness the Tests. The Independent\nEngineer shall thereupon conduct the Tests itself or cause any of the Tests to be conducted\nin accordance with Article 14 and this Schedule-J.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0784",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 784,
    "page_start": 230,
    "page_end": 230,
    "char_start": 435819,
    "char_end": 435999,
    "char_count": 180,
    "text": "2\nTests\n\n2.1\nThe Independent Engineer shall conduct, or cause to be conducted, the Tests in accordance\nwith Applicable Law, Good Industry Practice and Specifications and Standards.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0785",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 785,
    "page_start": 231,
    "page_end": 232,
    "char_start": 436001,
    "char_end": 436785,
    "char_count": 784,
    "text": "231\n\n232\n\nSCHEDULE – K\n(See Clause 14.2 & 14.3)\nCOMPLETION CERTIFICATE\n1. I/We, ……………… (Name of the Independent Engineer), under and in accordance with the\nConcession Agreement dated …………. (the “Agreement”), for development and operation\nof the XXX Ropeways for ............ corridor in city of ............ on design, build, finance, operate\nand transfer (the “DBFOT”) basis, through …………………… (Name of Concessionaire),\nhereby certify that the Tests specified in Article 14 and Schedule-J of the Agreement have been\nsuccessfully undertaken to determine compliance of the XXX Ropeway with Specifications\nand  Standards and with the provisions of the Agreement, and I/We am/are satisfied that the\nXXX Ropeway can be safely and reliably placed in commercial service of the Users thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0786",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 786,
    "page_start": 232,
    "page_end": 232,
    "char_start": 436787,
    "char_end": 437005,
    "char_count": 218,
    "text": "2. It is certified that, in terms of the aforesaid Agreement, all works forming part of XXX\nRopeway have been completed, and the XXX Ropeway is ready for entry into commercial\noperation on this the ………… day of ……… 20……",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0787",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 787,
    "page_start": 232,
    "page_end": 232,
    "char_start": 437007,
    "char_end": 437081,
    "char_count": 74,
    "text": "SIGNED, SEALED AND DELIVERED\nFor and on behalf of INDEPENDENT ENGINEER by:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0788",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 788,
    "page_start": 232,
    "page_end": 232,
    "char_start": 437083,
    "char_end": 437094,
    "char_count": 11,
    "text": "(Signature)",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0789",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 789,
    "page_start": 232,
    "page_end": 234,
    "char_start": 437096,
    "char_end": 437136,
    "char_count": 40,
    "text": "(Name)\n(Designation)\n(Address)\n\n233\n\n234",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0790",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 790,
    "page_start": 234,
    "page_end": 234,
    "char_start": 437138,
    "char_end": 438932,
    "char_count": 1794,
    "text": "PROVISIONAL CERTIFICATE\n1\nI, …………………… (Name of the Independent Engineer), under and in accordance with\nthe Concession Agreement dated ……………. (the “Agreement”), for ***ropeway (the\n“XXX Ropeway”) on design, build, finance, operate and transfer (the “DBFOT”) basis\nthrough …………………… (Name of Concessionaire), hereby certify that the Tests\nspecified in Article 14 and Schedule-J of the Agreement have been undertaken to determine\ncompliance of the XXX Ropeway with the provisions of the Agreement.\n2\nConstruction Works that were found to be incomplete and/or deficient have been specified\nin the Punch List appended hereto, and the Concessionaire has agreed and accepted that it\nshall complete and/or rectify all such works in the time and manner set forth in the\nAgreement. (Some of the incomplete works have been delayed as a result of reasons\nattributable to the Authority or due to Force Majeure and the Provisional Certificate cannot\nbe withheld on this account. Though the remaining incomplete works have been delayed\nas a result of reasons attributable to the Concessionaire,)@ I am satisfied that having regard\nto the nature and extent of such incomplete works, it would not be prudent to withhold\ncommercial operation of the XXX Ropeway, pending completion thereof.\n3\nIn view of the foregoing, I am satisfied that the XXX Ropeway can be safely and reliably\nplaced in commercial service of the Users thereof, and in terms of the Agreement, the XXX\nRopeway is hereby provisionally declared fit for entry into commercial operation on this\nthe ………… day of ……….. 20…...\nACCEPTED, SIGNED, SEALED\nSIGNED, SEALED AND\nAND DELIVERED\nDELIVERED\nFor and on behalf of\nFor and on behalf of\nCONCESSIONAIRE by:\nINDEPENDENT ENGINEER  by:\n(Signature)(Signature)\n(Name and Designation) (Name and (Designation)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0791",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 791,
    "page_start": 234,
    "page_end": 234,
    "char_start": 438933,
    "char_end": 438951,
    "char_count": 18,
    "text": "(Address)(Address)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0792",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 792,
    "page_start": 235,
    "page_end": 236,
    "char_start": 438953,
    "char_end": 439062,
    "char_count": 109,
    "text": "235\n\n236\n\nSCHEDULE – L\n(See Clause 17.2)\nPERFORMANCE AND MAINTENANCE REQUIREMENTS\n1.\nMaintenance Requirements",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0793",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 793,
    "page_start": 236,
    "page_end": 236,
    "char_start": 439064,
    "char_end": 439422,
    "char_count": 358,
    "text": "1.1\nThe Concessionaire shall, at all times, operate and maintain the XXX Ropeway in\naccordance with the provisions of the Agreement, Applicable Laws and Applicable\nPermits. In particular, the Concessionaire shall, at all times during the Operation Period,\nconform to the maintenance requirements set forth in this Schedule-L (the “Maintenance\nRequirements”).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0794",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 794,
    "page_start": 236,
    "page_end": 236,
    "char_start": 439424,
    "char_end": 439861,
    "char_count": 437,
    "text": "Performance and Maintenance Requirements\nThe list of performance and maintenance requirements of key ropeway components to\noptimize ropeway efficiency during its operational lifetime. Each equipment supplier will\nprovide service schedule which the Concessionaire will follow for trouble free and safe\nperformance of the ropeway. Checks are recommended for daily, weekly, monthly,\nquarterly, half yearly, yearly, 3-year, 6-year basis etc.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0795",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 795,
    "page_start": 236,
    "page_end": 236,
    "char_start": 439863,
    "char_end": 441197,
    "char_count": 1334,
    "text": "1.\nCheck the loading and unloading points as well as the access and exit areas and fix\nthem if need be;\n2.\nTowers: Check the platforms, handrails, catwalks, anemometers, ladders and rope\nlifting frames for cracks, rust, deformation, correct position or any deviation from\nthe standard\n;\n3.\nOverhead Cables - Signal Cables: Check for any visual deviation in terms of\nphysical damage such as breakage, color deformation, cuts, correct position,\noverhead cable for oscillations;\n4.\nLighting Protection Cable inspection as Overhead Cables at Serial No.3;\n5.\nMain Gear Box: Follow gear box manufacturers recommendation for maintenance\nschedule;\n6.\nUniversal Shaft: Check for any unusual noise (technician should be trained to\ndifferentiate between a normal and abnormal noise during shaft operation);\n7.\nMain Motor: refer to manufacturer’s manual schedule of activities;\n8.\nGear Rim: General check for any physical damage or aberration;\n9.\nHydraulic Unit for emergency drive / brakes;\n10.\nService Brake: check for correct functioning by actuating the switch\n'EMERGENCY STOP' check stopping distance. Check the brake and hydraulic\nlines for any leaks;\n11.\nEmergency Brake:\nCheck for correct functioning by actuating the switch\n'EMERGENCY STOP' check stopping distance. Check the brake release cylinder\nand the hydraulic lines for any leaks;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0796",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 796,
    "page_start": 236,
    "page_end": 236,
    "char_start": 441199,
    "char_end": 441496,
    "char_count": 297,
    "text": "12.\nRope Tensioner Hydraulic Unit: check tension on display and visual check for\nleaks;\n13.\nDrive and Return Bull wheels: Check for any unusual noise, wobble or eccentricity\nin the motion of the bull wheel, etc.;\n14.\nBull wheel coupling, positioning monitoring unit, axle position monitoring unit,",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0797",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 797,
    "page_start": 237,
    "page_end": 237,
    "char_start": 441498,
    "char_end": 442795,
    "char_count": 1297,
    "text": "237\n\nbearing;\n15.\nTension Carriage: Check tension carriage position;\n16.\nGrip Opening/Closing Equipment: Check for Normal Operation as per approved\nmanufacturer’s process; other components associated with functioning of the grips\nsuch as grip fault before launch limit switch, not open limit switch, grip gauge,\ngrip operating lever fault, electronic grip force testing device;\n17.\nOuter Guide Rail: Functional check of the dampened outer guide rail;\n18.\nTyre Conveyors: General inspection as per schedule of maintenance;\n19.\nHydraulic Lifting Unit: Check for leaks and loose pipe connections;\n20.\nClutch/Brake\nCombination/Safety\nClutch:\nCheck\nthe\nclutch/brake\ncombination/safety clutch for correct functioning;\n21.\nLine components such as rope, sheave assemblies, hangar, grip mechanism, tacho\ndrive, counting sheave, haul rope grounding, towers, overhead cables, signal\ncables, lightning protection rope, gear rim, rope tensioner hydraulic unit, power\ntake off (PTO) drive, break fork switch etc. including all safety features listed in\nSchedule M to be checked and technical specifications of the equipment suppliers;\n22.\nDoor opening closing of gondolas, access control barriers and passenger control\nsystems; and\n23.\nMagnetic Particle Testing of components to ensure safety of the operations.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0798",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 798,
    "page_start": 237,
    "page_end": 237,
    "char_start": 442797,
    "char_end": 443318,
    "char_count": 521,
    "text": "1.2\nThe Concessionaire shall repair or rectify any defect or deficiency set forth in Paragraph 2\nof this Schedule-L within the time limit specified therein and any failure in this behalf shall\nconstitute a breach of the Agreement. Upon occurrence of any breach hereunder, the\nAuthority shall be entitled to recover Damages as set forth in Clause 17.7 of the Agreement,\nwithout prejudice to the rights of the Authority under the Agreement, including\nTermination thereof.\n2.\nRepair/rectification of defects and deficiencies",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0799",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 799,
    "page_start": 237,
    "page_end": 237,
    "char_start": 443320,
    "char_end": 443719,
    "char_count": 399,
    "text": "The obligations of the Concessionaire in respect of Maintenance Requirements shall\ninclude repair and rectification of the defects and deficiencies specified in Annex - I of this\nSchedule - L within the time limit set forth therein. The Concessionaire shall at all times\nmaintain an adequate inventory of spares and consumables to meet the Maintenance\nRequirements.\n3.\nOther defects and deficiencies",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0800",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 800,
    "page_start": 237,
    "page_end": 237,
    "char_start": 443721,
    "char_end": 444429,
    "char_count": 708,
    "text": "3.1\nIn respect of any defect or deficiency not specified in Annex - I of this Schedule-L, the\nConcessionaire shall undertake repair or rectification in accordance with Good Industry\nPractice and within the time limit specified by the Independent Engineer.\n3.2\nIn respect of any defect or deficiency not specified in Annex - I of this Schedule-L, the\nIndependent Engineer may, in conformity with Good Industry Practice, specify the\npermissible limit of deviation or deterioration with reference to the Specifications and\nStandards, and any deviation or deterioration beyond the permissible limit shall be repaired\nor rectified by the Concessionaire within the time limit specified by the Independent\nEngineer.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0801",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 801,
    "page_start": 238,
    "page_end": 238,
    "char_start": 444431,
    "char_end": 444988,
    "char_count": 557,
    "text": "238\n\n4.          Extension of time limit\n\nNotwithstanding anything to the contrary specified in this Schedule-L, if the nature and\nextent of any defect or deficiency justifies more time for its repair or rectification than the\ntime specified herein, the Concessionaire shall be entitled to additional time in conformity\nwith Good Industry Practice and Specification and Standards. Such additional time shall\nbe determined by the Independent Engineer and conveyed to the Concessionaire and the\nAuthority with reasons thereof.\n5.\nEmergency repairs/restoration",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0802",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 802,
    "page_start": 238,
    "page_end": 238,
    "char_start": 444990,
    "char_end": 445326,
    "char_count": 336,
    "text": "Notwithstanding anything to the contrary contained in this Schedule-L, if any defect,\ndeficiency or deterioration in the XXX Ropeway poses a hazard to safety or risk of damage\nto property, the Concessionaire shall promptly take all reasonable measures for eliminating\nor minimizing such danger.\n6.\nDaily Inspection by the Concessionaire",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0803",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 803,
    "page_start": 238,
    "page_end": 238,
    "char_start": 445328,
    "char_end": 445752,
    "char_count": 424,
    "text": "The Concessionaire shall, through its engineer, undertake a daily visual inspection of the\nXXX Ropeway and maintain a record thereof in a register to be kept in such form and\nmanner as the Independent Engineer may specify. Such record shall be kept in safe custody\nof the Concessionaire and shall be open to inspection by the Authority and the Independent\nEngineer at any time during office hours.\n7.\nDivestment Requirements",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0804",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 804,
    "page_start": 238,
    "page_end": 238,
    "char_start": 445754,
    "char_end": 445979,
    "char_count": 225,
    "text": "All defects and deficiencies specified in this Schedule-L shall be repaired and rectified by\nthe Concessionaire so that the XXX Ropeway conforms to the Maintenance Requirements\non the Transfer Date.\n8.\nDisplay of Schedule – L",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0805",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 805,
    "page_start": 238,
    "page_end": 238,
    "char_start": 445981,
    "char_end": 446116,
    "char_count": 135,
    "text": "The Concessionaire shall display a copy of this Schedule-L at every station along with the\nComplaint Register stipulated in Article 47.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0806",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 806,
    "page_start": 239,
    "page_end": 240,
    "char_start": 446118,
    "char_end": 446200,
    "char_count": 82,
    "text": "239\n\n240\n\nAnnex - I\n(Schedule-L)\n\nRepair/Rectification of Defects and Deficiencies",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0807",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 807,
    "page_start": 240,
    "page_end": 240,
    "char_start": 446202,
    "char_end": 446363,
    "char_count": 161,
    "text": "Any deficiency leading to stoppage of XXX Ropeway shall be rectified in accordance with\nApplicable Laws, Good Industry Practice and Specifications and Standards.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0808",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 808,
    "page_start": 241,
    "page_end": 242,
    "char_start": 446365,
    "char_end": 446446,
    "char_count": 81,
    "text": "241\n\n242\n\nSCHEDULE-M\n(See Clause 18.1)\n\nSAFETY REQUIREMENTS\n\n1\nGuiding principles",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0809",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 809,
    "page_start": 242,
    "page_end": 242,
    "char_start": 446448,
    "char_end": 447226,
    "char_count": 778,
    "text": "1.1\nSafety Requirements aim at reduction in injuries, loss of life and damage to property\nresulting from accidents on the XXX Ropeway, irrespective of the person(s) at fault.\n1.2\nUsers of the XXX Ropeway include staff of the Concessionaire and its contractors working\non the XXX Ropeway.\n1.3\nSafety Requirements apply to all phases of construction, operation and maintenance with\nemphasis on identification of factors associated with accidents, consideration of the same,\nand implementation of appropriate remedial measures.\n1.4\nSafety Requirements include measures associated with safe movement, safety\nmanagement, safety equipment, fire safety, enforcement and emergency response, with\nparticular reference to the safety guidelines specified in Annex - I of this Schedule - M.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0810",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 810,
    "page_start": 242,
    "page_end": 242,
    "char_start": 447228,
    "char_end": 448940,
    "char_count": 1712,
    "text": "1.5\nThe XXX Ropeway shall be especially designed, operated and serviced in such a way so\nas to:\n(a)\neliminate and reduce risks by means of design and construction features;\n(b)\nimplement necessary measures to protect against risks that cannot be completely\neliminated; and\n(c)\nlay down precautions to be taken to avoid any risks.\n2\nObligations of the Concessionaire\nThe Concessionaire shall abide by the following insofar as they relate to safety of the Users:\n(a)\nApplicable Laws and Applicable Permits;\n(b)\nManual for safety;\n(c)\nprovisions of this Agreement; and\n(d)\nrelevant standards/Guidelines addressing highest human safety parameters; and\n (e)\nGood Industry Practice.\n3\nSafety measures during Development Period\n3.1\nNo later than 90 (ninety) days fr om the date of this Agreement, the Authority shall appoint\na Safety Consultant for carrying out safety audit at the design stage of the Project.\n3.2\nThe Concessionaire shall provide to the Safety Consultant, in four copies, the relevant\ndrawings containing the design details that have a bearing on safety of Users (the “Safety\nDrawings”). Such design details shall include ropeway alignments; horizontal and vertical\nforces, layouts of ropeway profile, foundation drawings, inertia forces, bending moments\nin global coordinates, tower loads, sheave loads, effects of forces caused by winds, snow,\nice or any other external factors, Station forces and design, people movement and safety\nprocedures at Stations along with other incidental or consequential information.  The\nSafety Consultant shall review the design details and forward 3 (three) copies of the Safety\nDrawings with its recommendations, if any, to the Independent Engineer who shall record",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0811",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 811,
    "page_start": 243,
    "page_end": 243,
    "char_start": 448942,
    "char_end": 449035,
    "char_count": 93,
    "text": "243\n\nits comments, if any, and forward one copy each to the Authority and the Concessionaire.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0812",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 812,
    "page_start": 243,
    "page_end": 243,
    "char_start": 449037,
    "char_end": 449539,
    "char_count": 502,
    "text": "3.3\nThe design and equipment details shall be compiled, analysed and used by the Safety\nConsultant for evolving a package of recommendations consisting of safety related\nmeasures for the XXX Ropeways.  The safety audit shall be completed in a period of 3\n(three) months and a report thereof (the “Safety Report”) shall be submitted to the\nAuthority, in 5 (five) copies. One copy each of the Safety Report shall be forwarded by the\nAuthority to the Concessionaire and the Independent Engineer forthwith.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0813",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 813,
    "page_start": 243,
    "page_end": 243,
    "char_start": 449541,
    "char_end": 450325,
    "char_count": 784,
    "text": "3.4\nThe Concessionaire shall endeavour to incorporate the recommendations of the Safety\nReport in the design of the XXX Ropeways, as may reasonably be required in accordance\nwith Applicable Laws, Applicable Permits, Manuals and Guidelines of the Authority,\nSpecifications and Standards, and Good Industry Practice. If the Concessionaire does not\nagree with any or all of such recommendations, it shall state the reasons thereof and convey\nthem to the Authority forthwith. In the event that any or all of the works and services\nrecommended in the Safety Report fall beyond the scope of Schedule-C, Schedule-D or\nSchedule-E, the Concessionaire shall make a report thereon and seek the instructions of the\nAuthority for funding such works in accordance with the provisions of Article 18.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0814",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 814,
    "page_start": 243,
    "page_end": 243,
    "char_start": 450327,
    "char_end": 452122,
    "char_count": 1795,
    "text": "3.5\nWithout prejudice to the provisions of Paragraph 4, the Concessionaire and the\nIndependent Engineer shall, within 15 (fifteen) days of receiving the Safety Report, send\ntheir respective comments thereon to the Authority, and no later than 15 (fifteen) days of\nreceiving such comments, the Authority shall review the same along with the Safety Report\nand by notice direct the Concessionaire to carry out any or all of the recommendations\ncontained therein with such modifications as the Authority may specify; provided that any\nworks or  services required to be undertaken hereunder shall be governed by the provisions\nof Article 18.\n4\nSafety measures during Construction Period\n4.1\nA Safety Consultant shall be appointed by the Authority, no later than 6 (six) months prior\nto the expected Project Completion Date, for carrying out a safety audit of the completed\nConstruction Works.\n4.2\nThe Safety Consultant shall study the Safety Report for the Development Period and\ninspect the XXX Ropeway to assess the adequacy of safety measures. The Safety\nConsultant shall complete the safety audit within a period of 4 (four) months and submit a\nSafety Report recommending a package of additional safety measures, if any, that are\nconsidered essential for reducing accident hazards on the XXX Ropeway. Such\nrecommendations shall be processed, mutatis mutandis, and acted upon in the manner set\nforth in Paragraphs 4.3, 4.4 and 4.5 of this Schedule-M.\n4.3\nThe Concessionaire shall make adequate arrangements during the Construction Period for\nthe safety of workers and road users in accordance with Applicable Laws and Good\nIndustry Practice for safety in construction zones and notify the Authority and the\nIndependent Engineer about such arrangements.\n4.4\nLayout, speed, distance between vehicles",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0815",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 815,
    "page_start": 243,
    "page_end": 243,
    "char_start": 452123,
    "char_end": 452570,
    "char_count": 447,
    "text": "4.4.1\nThe XXX Ropeways shall be designed taking into account the characteristics of the terrain\nand its surroundings i.e., atmospheric and meteorological conditions.\n4.4.2\nSufficient distance shall be maintained laterally and vertically between vehicles, towing\ndevices, tracks, cables, etc., and possible structures and obstacles located in the vicinity\neither on the ground or in the air, taking account of the vertical, longitudinal and lateral",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0816",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 816,
    "page_start": 244,
    "page_end": 244,
    "char_start": 452572,
    "char_end": 453374,
    "char_count": 802,
    "text": "244\n\nmovement of the cables and vehicles or of the towing devices under the most adverse\nforeseeable operating conditions.\n4.4.3\nThe maximum distance between vehicles and ground shall take account of the nature of\nthe XXX Ropeway, the type of vehicles and the rescue procedures. In the case of open\ncars, it shall also take account of the risk of fall as well as the psychological aspects\nassociated with the distance between vehicles and ground.\n4.4.4\nThe maximum speed of the vehicles or towing devices, the minimum distance between the\ntwo and their acceleration and braking performance shall be decided in a way to ensure the\nsafety of Users and safe operation of the XXX ropeways.\n4.5\nCables and their supports\n4.5.1. All measures shall be taken in line with the latest technological developments:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0817",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 817,
    "page_start": 244,
    "page_end": 244,
    "char_start": 453376,
    "char_end": 453858,
    "char_count": 482,
    "text": "(a)\nto avoid cables or their attachments breaking;\n(b)\nto cover their minimum and maximum stress values;\n(c)\nto ensure that they are safely mounted on their supports and prevent derailment;\nand\n(d)\nto enable them to be monitored.\n4.5.2. Measures to be taken to ensure that cables can be retrieved in case of any cable derailement\nand that the XXX Ropeways can be shut down without any risks to any persons in the event\nof such derailment.\n4.6.\nMechanical installations\n4.6.1. Drives",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0818",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 818,
    "page_start": 244,
    "page_end": 244,
    "char_start": 453860,
    "char_end": 453999,
    "char_count": 139,
    "text": "The drive system of the XXX Ropeways shall be of a suitable performance and capability,\nadapted to the various operating systems and modes.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0819",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 819,
    "page_start": 244,
    "page_end": 244,
    "char_start": 454001,
    "char_end": 454143,
    "char_count": 142,
    "text": "4.6.2. Standby drive\n\nThe XXX Ropeways shall have a standby drive with an energy supply which is\nindependent of that of the main drive system.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0820",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 820,
    "page_start": 244,
    "page_end": 244,
    "char_start": 454145,
    "char_end": 454462,
    "char_count": 317,
    "text": "4.6.3. Braking\n\n4.6.3.1. In an Emergency it shall be possible to shut down the XXX Ropeways and/or the vehicles\nat any moment, under the most unfavourable conditions in terms of authorised load and\npulley adhesion during operation. The stopping distance shall be as short as the security of\nthe XXX Ropeways dictates.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0821",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 821,
    "page_start": 244,
    "page_end": 244,
    "char_start": 454464,
    "char_end": 454680,
    "char_count": 216,
    "text": "4.6.3.2. Deceleration values shall be within adequate limits fixed in such a way as to ensure both\nthe safety of the Users and the satisfactory functioning of the vehicles, cables and other\nparts of the XXX Ropeways.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0822",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 822,
    "page_start": 244,
    "page_end": 244,
    "char_start": 454682,
    "char_end": 455013,
    "char_count": 331,
    "text": "4.6.3.3. In all XXX Ropeways there shall be 2 (two) or more braking systems, each capable of\nbringing the it to a halt, and coordinated in such a way that they automatically replace the\nactive system when its efficiency becomes inadequate. The XXX Ropeways’ last braking\nsystem shall act as close as possible to the traction cable.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0823",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 823,
    "page_start": 245,
    "page_end": 245,
    "char_start": 455015,
    "char_end": 455903,
    "char_count": 888,
    "text": "245\n\n4.6.3.4. The XXX Ropeways shall be fitted with an effective clamp and locking mechanism to\nguard against premature restarts.\n4.7\nControl devices\nThe control devices shall be designed and constructed in a way that they are safe and\nreliable, and able to withstand normal operating stresses and external factors such as\nhumidity, extreme temperatures or electromagnetic interference.\n4.8\nCommunication devices\nThe Concessionaire to ensure that the operational staff is provided with equipment to\ncommunicate with one another and the Users in case of an Emergency\n4.9\nVehicles and Towing devices\n4.9.1\nThe fittings of vehicles and towing devices shall be dimensioned and constructed so as not\nto:\na)\ndamage the cable, or\nb)\nslip, except where slippage does not significantly affect the safety of the vehicle,\nthe towing device or the installation, under the most unfavorable conditions.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0824",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 824,
    "page_start": 245,
    "page_end": 245,
    "char_start": 455905,
    "char_end": 456201,
    "char_count": 296,
    "text": "4.9.2\nVehicle doors (on cars, carriers) shall be designed and constructed in such a way as to make\nit possible to close and lock them. The vehicle floor and walls shall be designed and\nconstructed so as to withstand pressure and loads exerted by Users and operating staff\nunder any circumstances.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0825",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 825,
    "page_start": 245,
    "page_end": 245,
    "char_start": 456203,
    "char_end": 456337,
    "char_count": 134,
    "text": "4.9.3\nThe vehicle shall be fitted with the suitable equipment if, for reasons of operational safety,\nan operator is required on board.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0826",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 826,
    "page_start": 245,
    "page_end": 245,
    "char_start": 456339,
    "char_end": 456562,
    "char_count": 223,
    "text": "4.9.4\nVehicles and/or towing devices and, in particular, their suspension mechanisms shall be\ndesigned and fitted so as to ensure the safety of personnel servicing them in accordance\nwith appropriate rules and instructions.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0827",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 827,
    "page_start": 245,
    "page_end": 245,
    "char_start": 456564,
    "char_end": 456945,
    "char_count": 381,
    "text": "4.9.5\nIn the case of vehicles equipped with disconnectable fittings, all measures shall be taken\nto bring to a halt, without risk to Users or operating staff, at the moment of departure, any\nvehicle whose fitting has been incorrectly connected to the cable and, at the moment of\narrival, any vehicle whose fitting has not been disconnected, and to prevent the vehicle\nfrom falling.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0828",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 828,
    "page_start": 245,
    "page_end": 245,
    "char_start": 456947,
    "char_end": 457030,
    "char_count": 83,
    "text": "4.9.6\nAll ropeway installations shall be equipped with an automatic braking device.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0829",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 829,
    "page_start": 245,
    "page_end": 245,
    "char_start": 457032,
    "char_end": 457255,
    "char_count": 223,
    "text": "4.9.7\nWhere all risk of derailment of the vehicle cannot be eliminated by other measures, the\nvehicle shall be fitted with an anti-derailment device which enables the vehicle to be\nbrought to a halt without risk to persons.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0830",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 830,
    "page_start": 245,
    "page_end": 245,
    "char_start": 457257,
    "char_end": 457805,
    "char_count": 548,
    "text": "4.9.8\nVehicles and/or towing devices shall be designed and fitted out in such a way that under\nforeseeable operating conditions no passenger or operation personnel can fall out or\nencounter any other risks i.e., getting stuck in doors, etc.\n5\nSafety measures during Operation Period\n5.1\nThe Concessionaire shall develop, implement and administer a surveillance and safety\nprogramme for Users, including correction of safety violations and deficiencies and all\nother actions necessary to provide a safe environment in accordance with this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0831",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 831,
    "page_start": 246,
    "page_end": 246,
    "char_start": 457807,
    "char_end": 457810,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "246",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0832",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 832,
    "page_start": 246,
    "page_end": 246,
    "char_start": 457812,
    "char_end": 459593,
    "char_count": 1781,
    "text": "This shall be approved by the Safety Consultant after an inspection and shall form part of\nthe Safety Manual.\n5.2\nThe Safety Consultant shall establish a Ropeway Safety Management Unit (the “RSMU”)\nto be functional on and after COD and designate one of its officers to be in-charge of the\nRSMU. Such officer shall have specialist knowledge and training in ropeway system safety\nby having attended a course conducted by a reputed organisation on the subject.\n5.3\nThe Safety Consultant shall keep a copy of every FIR recorded by the Police with respect\nto any accident occurring on the XXX Ropeway. In addition, the Safety Consultant shall\nalso collect data for all cases of accidents not recorded by the Police. The information so\ncollected shall be summarised in the form prescribed by the Authority for this purpose. The\nSafety Consultant shall also record the exact location of each accident on a route map. The\naforesaid data shall be submitted to the Authority at the conclusion of every quarter.\n5.4\nThe Safety Consultant shall submit to the Authority before the 31st (thirty first) May of\neach year, an annual report (in ten copies) containing, without limitation, a detailed listing\nand analysis of all accidents of the preceding Accounting Year and the measures taken by\nthe Safety Consultant  pursuant to the provisions of Paragraph 6.1 of this Schedule-M for\naverting or minimising such accidents in future.\n5.5\nOnce in every Accounting Year, a safety audit shall be carried out by the Safety Consultant\nto be appointed by the Authority. It shall review and analyse the annual report and accident\ndata of the preceding year and undertake an inspection of the XXX Ropeway. The Safety\nConsultant shall complete the safety audit within a period of 1 (one) month and submit a",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0833",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 833,
    "page_start": 246,
    "page_end": 246,
    "char_start": 459594,
    "char_end": 461375,
    "char_count": 1781,
    "text": "Safety Report recommending specific improvements, if any, required to be made in the\nXXX Ropeway. Such recommendations shall be processed, mutatis mutandis, and acted\nupon in the manner set forth in Paragraphs 4.3, 4.4 and 4.5 of this Schedule-M.\n5.6\nThe Safety Manual and the corresponding notes shall be drawn up in a vernacular language\nof a Member State or any language which can be easily understood by Users, as determined\nby the Member State in the territory of which the XXX Ropeway is constructed and\ninstalled.\n5.7\nThe workspace for the construction and operation of the XXX Ropeways shall be designed\nin such a way so as to prevent trained personnel from any accidents by way of falling. The\nSafety Consultant shall provide its appointed personnel with adequate protective gear to\nprevent workplace accidents.\n5.8\nSafety in the event of immobilization of the ropeway installation: all technical provisions\nand measures shall be adopted to ensure that passengers and operating personnel can be\nbrought to safety within a set time appropriate to the type of ropeway installation and its\nsurrounding is immobilized and cannot be restarted quickly.\n5.9\nOperators’ stands and workplaces: Movable part which are normally accessible in the\nStations shall be designed, constructed and installed in such a way as to preclude any risks\nor, where such risks exist, be fitted with protective devices so as to prevent any contact\nwith parts of the ropeway installation which may cause accidents. Those devices shall be\nof a type that cannot easily be removed or rendered inoperative.\n6\nCosts and expenses\nCosts and expenses incurred in connection with the Safety Requirements set forth herein,\nincluding the provisions of Paragraph 2 of this Schedule, shall be met in accordance with",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0834",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 834,
    "page_start": 246,
    "page_end": 246,
    "char_start": 461376,
    "char_end": 461467,
    "char_count": 91,
    "text": "Article 18, and in particular, the remuneration of the Safety Consultant, safety audit, and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0835",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 835,
    "page_start": 247,
    "page_end": 247,
    "char_start": 461469,
    "char_end": 462815,
    "char_count": 1346,
    "text": "247\n\ncosts incidental thereto, shall be met by the Concessionaire.\n7\nDimensions\nThe ropeway installation, the subsystems and all its safety components shall be\ndimensioned, designed and constructed to withstand, with a sufficient degree of safety, all\nstresses encountered under all foreseeable conditions, including those which occur when\nnot in operation, and taking account in particular of outside influences, dynamic effects\nand fatigue phenomena, while complying with the acknowledged rules of design, in\nparticular with regard to the choice of materials.\n8\nAssembly\n8.1\nThe ropeway installation, the subsystems and all the safety components shall be designed\nand constructed in such a way as to ensure that they can be safely assembled and put into\nplace.\n8.2\nThe safety components shall be designed as to make assembly mistakes impossible either\nas a result of construction or by means of appropriate markings on the components\nthemselves.\n9\nIntegrity of the Ropeway Installation\n9.1\nThe safety components shall be designed and constructed and be useable in such a way as\nto ensure that, in every case, their own operational integrity and/or the safety of the\nropeway installation is ensured, so that their failure is avoidable and with an acceptable\nsafety margin.\n9.2\nSafety analysis and Safety Report for Planned Ropeway Installations.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0836",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 836,
    "page_start": 247,
    "page_end": 247,
    "char_start": 462817,
    "char_end": 462989,
    "char_count": 172,
    "text": "9.2.1\nThe bidder responsible for the ropeway installation, shall carry out a safety analysis of the\nplanned ropeway installation or have such a safety analysis carried out.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0837",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 837,
    "page_start": 247,
    "page_end": 247,
    "char_start": 462991,
    "char_end": 463928,
    "char_count": 937,
    "text": "9.2.2\nThe safety analysis required for each ropeway installation shall:\n\n(a)\ntake into account all modes of operation envisaged;\n(b)\nfollow a recognized or established method;\n(c)\ntake into account the design parameters and the complexity if the ropeway\ninstallation in question;\n(d)\nensure that the design and configuration of the ropeway installation takes account\nof the local surroundings and the most adverse situations in order to ensure\nsatisfactory safety conditions;\n(e)\ncover all safety aspects of the ropeway installation and its external factor sin the\ncontext of the design, construction and entry into service;\n(f)\nmake it possible to identify from past experience risks liable to occur during the\noperation of the ropeway installation.\n9.2.3\nThe safety analysis shall also cover the safety devices and their effects on the ropeway\ninstallation and related subsystems that they bring into action so that the safety devices:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0838",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 838,
    "page_start": 248,
    "page_end": 248,
    "char_start": 463930,
    "char_end": 463933,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "248",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0839",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 839,
    "page_start": 248,
    "page_end": 248,
    "char_start": 463935,
    "char_end": 464631,
    "char_count": 696,
    "text": "(a)\nare capable of reacting to an initial breakdown or failure detected so as to remain\neither in a state that guarantees safety, in a lower operation mode or in a fail-safe\nstate;\n(b)\nare redundant and are monitored; or\n(c)\nare such that the probability of their failure can be evaluated, and their effects are\nof a standard equivalent to that achieved by safety devices that meet the criteria set\nout in points (a) and (b).\n9.2.4\nThe safety analysis shall be used to draw up the inventory of risks and dangerous situations,\nto recommend the measure envisaged to deal with such risks and to determine the list of\nsubsystems and safety components to be incorporated into the ropeway installation.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0840",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 840,
    "page_start": 248,
    "page_end": 248,
    "char_start": 464633,
    "char_end": 464980,
    "char_count": 347,
    "text": "9.2.5\nThe result of the safety analysis shall be included in a safety report.\n\n9.3\nThe safeguards referred to in Clause 10.2 2. Shall apply throughout the period between two\nscheduled inspections of the competent concerned. The time period for the scheduled\ninspection of the safety components shall be clearly indicated in the instruction manual.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0841",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 841,
    "page_start": 248,
    "page_end": 248,
    "char_start": 464982,
    "char_end": 465194,
    "char_count": 212,
    "text": "9.4\nSafety components which are incorporated as spare parts shall satisfy the essential safety\nrequirements and the conditions relating to the smooth interaction with the other parts of\nthe ropeway installations.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0842",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 842,
    "page_start": 248,
    "page_end": 248,
    "char_start": 465196,
    "char_end": 465327,
    "char_count": 131,
    "text": "9.5\nMeasures shall be taken to ensure that the effects of a fire in the ropeway installation do\nnot endanger the safety of persons.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0843",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 843,
    "page_start": 248,
    "page_end": 248,
    "char_start": 465329,
    "char_end": 465810,
    "char_count": 481,
    "text": "9.6\nSpecial measures shall be taken to protects ropeway installations and persons from the\neffects of lightning.\n10\nSafety Devices\n10.1\nAny defect in the ropeway installation which could result in a failure endangering safety\nshall, where practicable, be detected, reported and processed by a safety device. The same\napplies to any normally foreseeable external event which may endanger safety.\n10.2\nIt shall be possible at all times to shut down the ropeway installation manually.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0844",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 844,
    "page_start": 248,
    "page_end": 248,
    "char_start": 465812,
    "char_end": 466735,
    "char_count": 923,
    "text": "10.3\nAfter the ropeway installation has been shut down by a safety device, it shall not be possible\nto restart it unless appropriate action has been taken.\n11\nMaintainability\nThe ropeway installation shall be designed and constructed for routine or special\nmaintenance and repair operations and procedures to be carried out safely.\n12\nEquipment for passengers and operating personnel\n12.1\nThe access to embarkation areas and exit and disembarkation areas and the embarkation\nand disembarkation of passengers and operating personnel shall be organized with regard\nto the movement and stopping of vehicles in such a way as to ensure the safety of\npassengers and operating personnel, in particular in areas where there is a risk of falling.\n12.2\nIt must be possible for children and persons with reduced mobility to use the ropeway\ninstallation safely if the ropeway installation is designed for the transport of such persons.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0845",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 845,
    "page_start": 249,
    "page_end": 249,
    "char_start": 466737,
    "char_end": 466740,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "249",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0846",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 846,
    "page_start": 250,
    "page_end": 250,
    "char_start": 466742,
    "char_end": 467210,
    "char_count": 468,
    "text": "250\n\nAnnex - I\n(Schedule-M)\n\nSafety Guidelines\n\n1.\nSafe movement\n\n1.1.\nIn the design, construction and operation of Stations and ropeway system, particular care\nshall be taken to ensure safety of Users in entry and exit; while waiting, boarding or\nalighting; and in moving systems in case of any immobilization. This shall include facilities\nfor safe and efficient evacuation in case of Emergency In particular, ropeways shall be\ndesigned and tested for safe movement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0847",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 847,
    "page_start": 250,
    "page_end": 250,
    "char_start": 467212,
    "char_end": 468097,
    "char_count": 885,
    "text": "2.\nSystem integrity\n\n2.1\nIn the design of power supply, ropeway, circuits and equipments, particular care shall be\ntaken to minimise the likely incidence of failure.\n2.2\nAll noxious gases, noise emissions and vibrations fall within the prescribed limit set by the\nMember State in whose territory the ropeway system is installed and should be in\naccordance with Applicable Law.\n3.\nSafety management\n3.1\nA safety statement shall be prepared by the Concessionaire once every quarter to bring out\nclearly the system of management of checks and maintenance tolerances for various assets\nincluding carriers, and compliance thereof. The statement shall also bring out the nature\nand extent of, staff training and awareness in dealing with such checks and tolerances. Two\ncopies of the statement shall be sent to the Independent Engineer within 15 (fifteen) days\nof the close of every quarter.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0848",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 848,
    "page_start": 250,
    "page_end": 250,
    "char_start": 468099,
    "char_end": 468634,
    "char_count": 535,
    "text": "4.\nSafety equipment\n4.1\nThe following equipment shall be provided at every Station:\na.\nFire extinguishers and fire alarms at the appropriate locations on the platforms;\nb.\nTwo fire extinguishers in the station office;\nc.\nTwo stretchers and two standard first aid boxes; and\nd.\nSuch other equipment as may be required in conformity with Good Industry\nPractice.\n4.2\nAny defect in the ropeway installation which could result in a failure endangering safety\nshall, where practicable, be detected, reported and processed by a safety device.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0849",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 849,
    "page_start": 250,
    "page_end": 250,
    "char_start": 468636,
    "char_end": 468735,
    "char_count": 99,
    "text": "4.3\nThe ropeway installation shall be designed in a way to ensure that it can be shut down\nmanually",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0850",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 850,
    "page_start": 250,
    "page_end": 250,
    "char_start": 468737,
    "char_end": 468922,
    "char_count": 185,
    "text": "5.\nEmergency\n\n5.1\nA set of emergency procedures shall be formulated to deal with different Emergency\nsituations and the operations staff shall be trained to respond appropriately during",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0851",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 851,
    "page_start": 251,
    "page_end": 251,
    "char_start": 468924,
    "char_end": 469374,
    "char_count": 450,
    "text": "251\n\nemergency through periodic simulated exercises as laid down in a manual for management\nof disasters (the “Disaster Management Manual”) to be prepared and published by the\nConcessionaire prior to COD. The Disaster Management Manual shall form part of the\nSafety Manual. The Concessionaire shall provide 5 (five) copies each of the Disaster\nManagement Manual to the Authority and the independent expert no later than 30 (thirty)\ndays prior to COD.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0852",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 852,
    "page_start": 251,
    "page_end": 251,
    "char_start": 469376,
    "char_end": 469579,
    "char_count": 203,
    "text": "6.\nFire safety\n\n6.1\nThe Concessionaire shall adopt provisions in a combination of the National Fire Protection\nAssociation (NFPA) 130 standard & Fire Safety Recommendations for Passenger\nRopeway Systems.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0853",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 853,
    "page_start": 251,
    "page_end": 251,
    "char_start": 469581,
    "char_end": 469827,
    "char_count": 246,
    "text": "6.2\nTo prevent fire in the passenger areas, the Concessionaire shall use fire resistant materials\nin the construction thereof and shall avoid use of materials which are to some extent\nflammable, or which emit smoke and harmful gases when burning.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0854",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 854,
    "page_start": 251,
    "page_end": 251,
    "char_start": 469829,
    "char_end": 470041,
    "char_count": 212,
    "text": "6.3\nEmergency exit should be accessible without any obstructions and the exit doors should be\nkept locked in the ordinary course. The exit doors shall be easy to open from inside the\nStation in case of Emergency.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0855",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 855,
    "page_start": 251,
    "page_end": 251,
    "char_start": 470043,
    "char_end": 470352,
    "char_count": 309,
    "text": "6.4\nEscape routes shall be clearly marked by arrows in the correct direction and no cryptic\nsymbols shall be used. In complying with the provisions of this Clause 6.4, the possibility\nof poor visibility due to smoke shall be duly taken into account. All notices and signages\nshall be uniform and standardized.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0856",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 856,
    "page_start": 251,
    "page_end": 251,
    "char_start": 470354,
    "char_end": 470458,
    "char_count": 104,
    "text": "6.5\nProvisions regarding fire safety as laid down in this Clause 6 shall form part of the Safety\nManual.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0857",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 857,
    "page_start": 251,
    "page_end": 251,
    "char_start": 470460,
    "char_end": 471011,
    "char_count": 551,
    "text": "7\nUser safety and information system:\n\n7.1\nThe Independent Engineer / Safety Consultant shall provide the RSMU with the facilities\nrequired for supervising passenger areas and carriers, and shall provide visual information\nto Users, both onboard and on the Stations. The Independent Engineer / Safety Consultant\nshall also provide one way communication to Users at the Stations through a Public\nAnnouncement (PA) system. The User call points should be located on all platforms at\nconvenient locations to allow Users to contact the RSMU in emergencies.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0858",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 858,
    "page_start": 251,
    "page_end": 251,
    "char_start": 471013,
    "char_end": 471101,
    "char_count": 88,
    "text": "7.2\nThe User information system shall comprise dynamic visual displays and loudspeakers.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0859",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 859,
    "page_start": 252,
    "page_end": 252,
    "char_start": 471103,
    "char_end": 471468,
    "char_count": 365,
    "text": "252\n\nSCHEDULE – N\n(See Clause 39.4)\nVESTING CERTIFICATE\n\nThe Chairman, Department of Tourism, XXX State (the “Authority”) refers to the Concession\nAgreement dated ………………. (the “Agreement”) entered into between the Authority and\n……………………. (the “Concessionaire”) for *** ropeway (the “XXX Ropeway”) on design,\nbuild, finance, operate and transfer (the “DBFOT”) basis.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0860",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 860,
    "page_start": 252,
    "page_end": 252,
    "char_start": 471470,
    "char_end": 471917,
    "char_count": 447,
    "text": "The Authority hereby acknowledges compliance and fulfilment by the Concessionaire of the\nDivestment Requirements set forth in Clause 39.1  of the Agreement on the basis that upon issue\nof this Vesting Certificate, the Authority shall be deemed to have acquired, and all title and interest\nof the Concessionaire in or about the XXX Ropeway shall be deemed to have vested unto the\nAuthority, free from any Encumbrances, charges and liens whatsoever.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0861",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 861,
    "page_start": 252,
    "page_end": 252,
    "char_start": 471919,
    "char_end": 472294,
    "char_count": 375,
    "text": "Notwithstanding anything to the contrary contained hereinabove, it shall be a condition of this\nVesting Certificate that nothing contained herein shall be construed or interpreted as waiving the\nobligation of the Concessionaire to rectify and remedy any defect or deficiency in any of the\nDivestment Requirements and/or relieving the Concessionaire in any manner of the same.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0862",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 862,
    "page_start": 252,
    "page_end": 252,
    "char_start": 472296,
    "char_end": 472424,
    "char_count": 128,
    "text": "Signed this ……………. day of …………., 20………. at Delhi.\n\nAGREED, ACCEPTED AND SIGNED\nSIGNED, SEALED AND DELIVERED\nFor and on behalf of",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
