    "char_end": 501122,
    "char_count": 85,
    "text": "$ To be affixed in accordance with the articles of association of the Concessionaire.",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0943",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 943,
    "page_start": 265,
    "page_end": 266,
    "char_start": 501124,
    "char_end": 501389,
    "char_count": 265,
    "text": "265\n\n266\n\nSCHEDULE – Q\n(See Clause 28.1.1)\n\nFEE NOTIFICATION\n\n[The Fee Rules/Notification issued by the State Government shall constitute Schedule- Q of the\nAgreement and shall be in accordance with the local legislation governing ropeways in the\napplicable state.]",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0944",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 944,
    "page_start": 266,
    "page_end": 266,
    "char_start": 501391,
    "char_end": 501565,
    "char_count": 174,
    "text": "[Note 1: Fee Rules/ Notification shall be included in the draft concession agreement to be provided\nto the bidders before inviting Bids and would broadly cover the following:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0945",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 945,
    "page_start": 266,
    "page_end": 266,
    "char_start": 501567,
    "char_end": 501807,
    "char_count": 240,
    "text": "The notification shall specify the fee payable for each category of Users using the XXX Ropeway.\nThe fee shall be based on the rates approved by Government/Authority and escalated to reflect the\nincrease in price index as specified therein.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0946",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 946,
    "page_start": 266,
    "page_end": 266,
    "char_start": 501809,
    "char_end": 502032,
    "char_count": 223,
    "text": "The notification shall specify that the fee structure shall be modified to reflect the variation in price\nindex as specified in Clause 28.2 and the  Fee Notification shall be issued and gazetted by the\nconcerned department.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0947",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 947,
    "page_start": 266,
    "page_end": 266,
    "char_start": 502034,
    "char_end": 502188,
    "char_count": 154,
    "text": "The notification shall provide for rounding off of the fee to the nearest one rupee, and for escalation\nof fee, in line with the provisions of Article 30.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0948",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 948,
    "page_start": 266,
    "page_end": 266,
    "char_start": 502190,
    "char_end": 502368,
    "char_count": 178,
    "text": "Discounted fee rates for frequent Users, additional charge for evasion of fee and differential fee\nstructure for peak and off- peak hours should be provided in the notification.]",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0949",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 949,
    "page_start": 266,
    "page_end": 266,
    "char_start": 502370,
    "char_end": 502536,
    "char_count": 166,
    "text": "[Note 2: For assistance in drafting the fee rules for the project, a model notification is provided at\nAnnex-I for consideration of the respective State Governments.]",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0950",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 950,
    "page_start": 267,
    "page_end": 267,
    "char_start": 502538,
    "char_end": 502541,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "267",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0951",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 951,
    "page_start": 268,
    "page_end": 268,
    "char_start": 502543,
    "char_end": 502546,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "268",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0952",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 952,
    "page_start": 268,
    "page_end": 268,
    "char_start": 502548,
    "char_end": 502641,
    "char_count": 93,
    "text": "Annex  - I\n\n(Schedule-Q)\n\n[Model Rules/Notification]27\n\nGOVERNMENT  OF ***\n\n****** DEPARTMENT",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0953",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 953,
    "page_start": 268,
    "page_end": 268,
    "char_start": 502643,
    "char_end": 502715,
    "char_count": 72,
    "text": "The Passenger Ropeway (Collection of Fee by Concessionaires) Rules, 20**",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0954",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 954,
    "page_start": 268,
    "page_end": 268,
    "char_start": 502717,
    "char_end": 504486,
    "char_count": 1769,
    "text": "In exercise of the powers conferred by [section ** of the ***** Act, 20**] (hereinafter referred to\nas the “Act”), and all other powers enabling him in this behalf, the Governor of *** makes the\nfollowing rules (hereinafter referred to as the “Rules”) for collection of fee for use of passenger\nropeway system, namely: -\n1.\nShort title, commencement and application:\nThese Rules may be called the Passenger Ropeway (Collection of Fee by Concessionaires)\nRules, 20**.\nThese Rules shall come into force on the date of their publication in the Official Gazette\nand shall apply to all concessions granted by the State Government after such date.\n2.\nDefinitions\n2.1\nIn these Rules, unless the context otherwise requires,\n(a)\n“Act” means the ***** Act, 20**\n(b)\n“Appellate Authority” means any officer not below the rank of superintending\nengineer or equivalent designated as such by the Government;\n(c)\n“Authority” means an agency appointed by the Government under the provisions\nof the Act, which will enter into an agreement with the Concessionaire for\nconstruction, operation or maintenance of a Ropeway system for transportation;\n(d)\n“CPI (IW)” means the Consumer Price Index for Industrial Workers as published\nby the Labour Bureau, Government of India or any Index published in substitution\nthereof by the Government of India;\n(e)\n“Concession Agreement” means an agreement entered into between the Authority\nand any person or persons for construction, operation or maintenance of a\nRopeway system for transportation;\n(f)\n“Concessionaire” means a person who has entered into a Concession Agreement\nwith the Authority under the provisions of the Act;\n(g)\n“Government” means the Government of ***;\n(h)\n“Price Index” shall comprise:\n[(a) 70% (seventy per cent) of WPI; and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0955",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 955,
    "page_start": 269,
    "page_end": 269,
    "char_start": 504488,
    "char_end": 505428,
    "char_count": 940,
    "text": "269\n\n(b) 30% (thirty per cent) of CPI (IW)],\nwhich constituents may be substituted by such alternative index or indices as\nthe Parties may by mutual consent determine;\n(i)\n“Ropeway system” means the Ropeway system that is constructed, operated or\nmaintained under a Concession Agreement for transporting commuters;\n(j)\n“Unauthorised Collection” means the collection of any amount not provided for\nin these Rules, by the concessionaire;\n(k)\n“User” means a person who uses the Ropeway system or any part thereof on\npayment of fee; and\n(l)\n“WPI” means the Wholesale Price Index as published by the Ministry of Industry,\nGovernment of India or any Index published in substitution thereof by the\nGovernment of India.\n(m)\n“Year” means a period from 1st April of a year and ending on 31st March of the\nfollowing year.\nWords and expressions used herein but not defined in these Rules shall have the meaning\nrespectively assigned to them in the Act.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0956",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 956,
    "page_start": 269,
    "page_end": 269,
    "char_start": 505430,
    "char_end": 505594,
    "char_count": 164,
    "text": "3.\nLevy and Collection of Fee\n3.1\nIt shall be levied and paid to the Concessionaire by every User, a fee under and in\naccordance with the provisions of these Rules.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0957",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 957,
    "page_start": 269,
    "page_end": 269,
    "char_start": 505596,
    "char_end": 505704,
    "char_count": 108,
    "text": "3.2\nEvery User, upon payment of the fee shall be issued a ticket / token / smart card by the\nConcessionaire.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0958",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 958,
    "page_start": 269,
    "page_end": 269,
    "char_start": 505706,
    "char_end": 505987,
    "char_count": 281,
    "text": "4.\nBasic Fee\n4.1\nThe Concessionaire will communicate the fee for Ropeway system in the Concession\nAgreement. Basic fee for parking at any designated parking area within a Station of the\nRopeway system shall be as specified in column (4) below and will be revised from time\nto time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0959",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 959,
    "page_start": 269,
    "page_end": 269,
    "char_start": 505989,
    "char_end": 506177,
    "char_count": 188,
    "text": "Serial No.\n(1)\nVehicle\n(2)\nTime period of parking\n(3)\nBasic fee (in Rs.) (4)\n1.\nCar\nUpto 2 hours\nFor every hour in excess of the\nfirst 2 hours 105\n10\n5\n2.\nMotorised 2-\nwheeler\nUpto 2 hours",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0960",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 960,
    "page_start": 269,
    "page_end": 269,
    "char_start": 506179,
    "char_end": 506226,
    "char_count": 47,
    "text": "For every hour in excess of the\nfirst 2 hours\n4",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0961",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 961,
    "page_start": 269,
    "page_end": 269,
    "char_start": 506228,
    "char_end": 506229,
    "char_count": 1,
    "text": "2",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0962",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 962,
    "page_start": 269,
    "page_end": 269,
    "char_start": 506231,
    "char_end": 506414,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "The basic fee for parking specified in sub-rule (2) above shall be increased by 50% (fifty\nper cent) thereof for parking provided in the basement or on a floor above the ground floor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0963",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 963,
    "page_start": 270,
    "page_end": 270,
    "char_start": 506416,
    "char_end": 506419,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "270",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0964",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 964,
    "page_start": 270,
    "page_end": 270,
    "char_start": 506421,
    "char_end": 506903,
    "char_count": 482,
    "text": "5.\nAnnual revision of basic fee\n5.1\nThe basic fee referred to in Rule 4 shall be increased annually, without compounding, by\n5% (five per cent) thereof for a period of 15 (fifteen) successive years commencing from\nApril 1, 2019. The first increase of 5% (five per cent) hereunder shall take effect on April\n1, 2020, and the last and fifteenth such increase shall be affected on April 1, 2034. Such\nincreased rates shall be deemed to be the base rates for the purpose of these rules.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0965",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 965,
    "page_start": 270,
    "page_end": 270,
    "char_start": 506905,
    "char_end": 507250,
    "char_count": 345,
    "text": "6.\nPeak and off-peak fee\n6.1\nEvery Concessionaire may, after obtaining prior written approval of the Authority, which\napproval the Authority may in its discretion deny, levy and collect a higher and discounted\nfee (the “Differential Fee”) for use of the Ropeway system, during peak and off-peak hours\nrespectively in accordance with this Rule 6:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0966",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 966,
    "page_start": 270,
    "page_end": 270,
    "char_start": 507252,
    "char_end": 507360,
    "char_count": 108,
    "text": "Provided, however, that such Differential Fee shall not apply to Users availing of a lower\nfee under Rule 9.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0967",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 967,
    "page_start": 270,
    "page_end": 270,
    "char_start": 507362,
    "char_end": 508052,
    "char_count": 690,
    "text": "6.2\nThe Concessionaire shall, for the purposes of these Rules, designate not more than 4 (four)\nhours in a day as peak hours and a period equal to twice the peak hours as off-peak hours.\nDuring peak hours, the Concessionaire may levy and collect a premium of upto 25%\n(twenty-five per cent) on the applicable fee or such higher premium as the Authority may\nby order permit. Simultaneously, with levy of such premium for peak hours, the\nConcessionaire shall offer a discount during off-peak hours for an amount equal to the\npremium for peak hours. For the avoidance of doubt, the determination of Differential Fee\nshall be with reference to the time of entry of a User in the Ropeway system.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0968",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 968,
    "page_start": 270,
    "page_end": 270,
    "char_start": 508054,
    "char_end": 508765,
    "char_count": 711,
    "text": "6.3\nIf the determination and collection of Differential Fee results in an increase in the fee\nrevenues of the Concessionaire, then 80% (eighty per cent) of the additional revenue in\neach year resulting from the Differential Fee shall be deposited in the Safety Fund and used\nin accordance with provisions of the respective concession agreement. For the purposes of\nthis Rule 6.3, additional revenue from Differential Fee shall mean the gross amount\ncollected at differential fee pursuant to this Rule 6, less gross revenues which would have\nbeen collected at the applicable fee on footing that the option to levy and collect\nDifferential Fee pursuant to this Rule 6 has not been exercised by the Concessionaire.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0969",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 969,
    "page_start": 270,
    "page_end": 270,
    "char_start": 508767,
    "char_end": 509071,
    "char_count": 304,
    "text": "7.\nFee collection points\n7.1\nFor collection of fee under these Rules, the Concessionaire shall establish and operate\nticket counters and ticket vending machines in accordance with the provisions of its\nConcession Agreement. The Concessionaire may install fee collection gates for checking\nevasion of fee.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0970",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 970,
    "page_start": 270,
    "page_end": 270,
    "char_start": 509073,
    "char_end": 509310,
    "char_count": 237,
    "text": "8.\nRemittance and Utilisation of fee\n8.1\nThe fee collected shall be appropriated by the Concessionaire in accordance with and for\nthe performance of its obligations under and in accordance with the provisions of the\nConcession Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0971",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 971,
    "page_start": 270,
    "page_end": 270,
    "char_start": 509312,
    "char_end": 509697,
    "char_count": 385,
    "text": "9.\nDiscounted rates for frequent Users\n9.1\nUpon request from any person, the Concessionaire shall issue a return ticket on payment\nof a sum equal to 180% (one hundred and eighty per cent) of the fee payable if it were to\nundertake a single one-way trip on the Ropeway system. Such return pass shall entitle the\nUser to undertake a return journey on the same day as the outward journey.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0972",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 972,
    "page_start": 271,
    "page_end": 271,
    "char_start": 509699,
    "char_end": 510026,
    "char_count": 327,
    "text": "271\n\n9.2\nUpon request from any person, the Concessionaire shall issue a daily pass on payment of\na sum equal to twice the fee payable if it were to undertake a single one-way trip on the\nlongest route of the Ropeway system. Such daily pass shall entitle the user to unlimited\ntravel on the Ropeway system for the date of issue.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0973",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 973,
    "page_start": 271,
    "page_end": 271,
    "char_start": 510028,
    "char_end": 510801,
    "char_count": 773,
    "text": "9.3\nThe Concessionaire shall, upon request from any person for issue of a weekly  pass, issue\nsuch pass on payment of a sum equal to ten times the fee payable if it were to undertake a\nsingle one-way trip on the selected section of the Ropeway system. Such weekly pass shall\nentitle the user to unlimited travel on such section of the Ropeway system for one week\nfrom the date of issue. The Concessionaire shall, upon request from any person for issue\nof a monthly pass, issue such pass on payment of a sum equal to forty times the fee payable\nif it were to undertake a single one-way trip on the selected section of the Ropeway system.\nSuch monthly pass shall entitle the user to unlimited travel on such section of the Ropeway\nsystem for one month from the date of issue.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0974",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 974,
    "page_start": 271,
    "page_end": 271,
    "char_start": 510803,
    "char_end": 510912,
    "char_count": 109,
    "text": "[In addition to the above, the Authority may prescribe any other scheme of discounted fee\nunder these Rules.]",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0975",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 975,
    "page_start": 271,
    "page_end": 271,
    "char_start": 510914,
    "char_end": 511953,
    "char_count": 1039,
    "text": "10.\nLuggage\n10.1\nA User may carry upto 7 (seven) kg of hand luggage without any payment for such luggage.\nA User can carry 50 (fifty) kg of luggage on a payment of an amount equal to the cost of\none ticket. The carriers are designed to carry a fixed number of riders. The assumption for\nluggage is that the weight of 50 (fifty) kg luggage will occupy one seat equivalent of weight\nin the carriers. Therefore, one person carrying 50 (fifty) kg luggage will deemed to buy\ntickets for 2 (two) travelling riders. The Concessionaire can levy a per kilogram charge\nequal to or more than the cost of ticket for a single rider. e.g.users may, at any time other\nthan peak hours, carry luggage in excess of 7 (seven) kilograms, but not exceeding 50\n(fifty) kg, upon payment of basic fee calculated at the rate of Rs. 2 (two) per kilogram,\nwhich rate may be revised by the Concessionaire in accordance with Rule 5; provided that\nany luggage which is hazardous, unhygienic or in any manner offensive to other users shall\nnot be permitted on the train.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0976",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 976,
    "page_start": 271,
    "page_end": 271,
    "char_start": 511955,
    "char_end": 512393,
    "char_count": 438,
    "text": "11.\nIncrease in fee due to increase in insurance premium\n11.1\nIn the event of a significant rise in the risk premium for insurance on account of a change\nin the security environment, the Concessionaire shall be entitled to recover 80% (eighty\npercent) of such increase in premium from the Users by means of a corresponding increase\nin fee with the prior written approval of the Authority which approval shall not be\nunreasonably withheld.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0977",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 977,
    "page_start": 271,
    "page_end": 271,
    "char_start": 512395,
    "char_end": 513101,
    "char_count": 706,
    "text": "12.\nAdditional charge for evasion of fee\n\n12.1\nThe Concessionaire shall be entitled to levy and collect an additional sum equal to the\ngreater of three times the applicable fee [or Rs. 200] from a person found to be evading\npayment of fee due. Such additional sum shall be deemed to be fee due and payable under\nthese Rules and may be used for defraying the expenses on prevention of such evasion.\nProvided that the Concessionaire shall not be entitled to any reduction in its liability on\naccount of any amount payable by it to the Authority or to any other relief from or any\nclaim against the Authority for its failure to stop evasion of fee; and its failure to collect\nfee prescribed under these Rules.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0978",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 978,
    "page_start": 272,
    "page_end": 272,
    "char_start": 513103,
    "char_end": 513106,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "272",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0979",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 979,
    "page_start": 272,
    "page_end": 272,
    "char_start": 513108,
    "char_end": 513221,
    "char_count": 113,
    "text": "13.\nRounding off of the fee\n13.1\nFee to be collected under these Rules shall be rounded off to the nearest Rupee.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0980",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 980,
    "page_start": 272,
    "page_end": 272,
    "char_start": 513223,
    "char_end": 513480,
    "char_count": 257,
    "text": "14.\nCommencement of fee collection\n14.1\nLevy and collection of fee shall commence upon completion/ provisional completion of\nconstruction of the Ropeway system for entry into commercial service, in accordance with\nthe provisions of the Concession Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0981",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 981,
    "page_start": 272,
    "page_end": 272,
    "char_start": 513482,
    "char_end": 513969,
    "char_count": 487,
    "text": "15.\nDisplay of Fee\n15.1\nThe Concessionaire shall, near the entry point of each Station, prominently display the\napplicable fee for information of Users approaching from either side of the Station. The\nConcessionaire shall from time to time, by written notice, inform the Authority of the\napplicable fee and the detailed calculation thereof. Such information shall be\ncommunicated at least 30 (thirty) days prior to the date of initial levy of fee or revision\nthereof, as the case may be.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0982",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 982,
    "page_start": 272,
    "page_end": 272,
    "char_start": 513971,
    "char_end": 514307,
    "char_count": 336,
    "text": "15.2\nThe Concessionaire shall, at least 15 (fifteen) days prior to the commencement of collection\nof fee or revised fee, as the case may be, publish a notice specifying the actual amount of\nfee to be charged from Users, in at least one newspaper each in English and local language\nof the area and having a wide circulation in such area.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0983",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 983,
    "page_start": 272,
    "page_end": 272,
    "char_start": 514309,
    "char_end": 514975,
    "char_count": 666,
    "text": "16.\nUnauthorised collection\n16.1\nIn the event that a Concessionaire collects from any person a sum of money not due and\npayable hereunder, the Concessionaire shall be liable to refund to such person forthwith\nthe amount so collected along with a sum computed @ 0.5 % (zero point five per cent) of\nthe amount so collected, for each day from the date of collection till the date of refund, by\nway of damages. In the event that such amount together with damages computed in the\nmanner as aforesaid is not paid to such person for any reason whatsoever, the same shall\nbe deposited with the Authority within a period of 15 (fifteen) days from the date of such\ncollection.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0984",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 984,
    "page_start": 272,
    "page_end": 272,
    "char_start": 514977,
    "char_end": 515786,
    "char_count": 809,
    "text": "16.2\nAny User aggrieved with the collection of unauthorised fee, may lodge a complaint with\nthe authorised representative of the Concessionaire  who  shall, after hearing the Parties\npass an order on such complaint within 30 (thirty) days of receiving the complaint and\nappeal, if any, against such order may be made to the Appellate Authority designated as\nsuch by the Authority within 45 (forty five) days of the date on which the order of the\nauthorised representative was received by such User. In passing an order under this Rule,\nthe authorised representative or the Appellate Authority may, after giving an opportunity\nof hearing to the complainant and the Concessionaire, direct the Concessionaire to refund\nthe excess payment and may also award damages for the inconvenience suffered by an\napplicant.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0985",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 985,
    "page_start": 272,
    "page_end": 272,
    "char_start": 515788,
    "char_end": 516014,
    "char_count": 226,
    "text": "16.3   The Concessionaire shall keep a record of all complaints received and action taken thereon\nwith respect to the fee collection, and forward a copy on a fortnightly basis to the authorised\nrepresentative of the Authority.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0986",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 986,
    "page_start": 272,
    "page_end": 272,
    "char_start": 516016,
    "char_end": 516416,
    "char_count": 400,
    "text": "16.4   The Authority may assess the excess fee collection, if any, made by a Concessionaire and\ntake appropriate action for recovering the same from such Concessionaire along with an\nadditional sum equal to the 25% (twenty five per cent) of the excess fee collection. Such\nadditional sum shall be deemed to be predetermined liquidated damages for assessment\nand recovery of the excess fee collection.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0987",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 987,
    "page_start": 273,
    "page_end": 273,
    "char_start": 516418,
    "char_end": 516421,
    "char_count": 3,
    "text": "273",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0988",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 988,
    "page_start": 273,
    "page_end": 273,
    "char_start": 516423,
    "char_end": 516685,
    "char_count": 262,
    "text": "17.\nPower of Authority to verify records\n17.1     The Authority shall have the power to verify, through any of its designated officers, the\ncollection of fee and for this purpose, inspect any document, records, other information or\nreports of the Concessionaire.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0989",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 989,
    "page_start": 273,
    "page_end": 273,
    "char_start": 516687,
    "char_end": 516787,
    "char_count": 100,
    "text": "18.\nExempted Users\n18.1     The following categories of Users shall be exempted from payment of fee:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0990",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 990,
    "page_start": 273,
    "page_end": 273,
    "char_start": 516789,
    "char_end": 516873,
    "char_count": 84,
    "text": "•\nEmployees of the concessionaire on duty; and\n•\nSecurity personnel on Station duty.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-0991",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 991,
    "page_start": 274,
    "page_end": 274,
    "char_start": 516875,
    "char_end": 516960,
    "char_count": 85,
    "text": "274\n\nSCHEDULE – R\n(See Clause 19.5)\n\nMONTHLY FEE STATEMENT22\n\nRopeway System:\n\nMonth:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
