    "char_start": 602006,
    "char_end": 602446,
    "char_count": 440,
    "text": "310\n\ncommission, arbitrator or governmental authority, and there are no outstanding\njudgments, decrees or orders of any such courts, commissions, arbitrators or\ngovernmental authorities, which materially and adversely affects its ability to\nperform its obligations under this Agreement.\n7.2\nEach of the Private Participants and the Concessionaire hereby irrevocably undertake,\nwarrant and represent to and for the benefit of Authority that:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-1176",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 1176,
    "page_start": 310,
    "page_end": 310,
    "char_start": 602448,
    "char_end": 602697,
    "char_count": 249,
    "text": "(a)\nthe rights vested in the Authority under this Agreement and the Concession\nAgreement shall not be abridged, abrogated or in any manner affected by any act\ndone or purported to be done by any of the Private Participants or the\nConcessionaire; and",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-1177",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 1177,
    "page_start": 310,
    "page_end": 310,
    "char_start": 602699,
    "char_end": 603212,
    "char_count": 513,
    "text": "(b)\nany divestment of equity in the Concessionaire shall not in any manner affect the\nrights of the Authority herein and that the successors, assigns and substitutes of the\nConcessionaire shall be bound by such undertaking.\n7.3\nThe Authority hereby warrants and represents to and for the benefit of the Concessionaire\nand the Private Participants that it has all requisite legal power and authority to execute this\nAgreement and carry out the terms, conditions and provisions hereof.\n8\nTERMINATION\n8.1\nTermination",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-1178",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 1178,
    "page_start": 310,
    "page_end": 310,
    "char_start": 603214,
    "char_end": 604975,
    "char_count": 1761,
    "text": "The Parties agree that in the event any of the Shareholders cease to hold, directly or\nindirectly, any Equity Shares of the Concessionaire, this Agreement shall stand terminated\nautomatically vis-à-vis such Shareholder. Provided however, the obligations of such\nShareholder under this Agreement relating to confidentiality (Clause 9) and dispute\nresolution (Clause 10) and such other provisions of this Agreement that by their nature are\nintended to survive, shall survive any termination of this Agreement.\n8.2\nRight to Terminate for Cause\n8.2.1\nIn the event of occurrence of a material breach of any of the terms and conditions of this\nAgreement or any covenant, representation, warranty or agreement set forth herein\n(\"Material Breach\") on the part of a Shareholder (the \"Defaulting Party\"), any other\nShareholders (\"Non-Defaulting Party\") may give written notice of the alleged breach\n(\"Breach Notice\") to the Defaulting Party.\n8.2.2\nA termination event (\"Termination Event\") shall be deemed to have occurred if such\nMaterial Breach, if reasonably capable of being cured, is not cured by the Defaulting Party\nwithin 30 (thirty) days of receipt of the Breach Notice (\"Cure Period\"), or if such Material\nBreach is not reasonably capable of being cured, forthwith upon issue of the Breach Notice.\n8.2.3\nOn the occurrence of a Termination Event on the part of any of the Private Participants,\nthe Authority may, in its discretion, require such Private Participant to transfer all, but not\nless than all, of the Equity Shares held by it to the Authority at the lower of the market\nvalue of Equity Shares or 25% (twenty five per cent) of the par value thereof; and the\ntransfer of such shares shall take place at the registered office of the Concessionaire within",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-1179",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 1179,
    "page_start": 310,
    "page_end": 310,
    "char_start": 604976,
    "char_end": 605049,
    "char_count": 73,
    "text": "30 (thirty) days from the date of notice by the Authority in this behalf.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-1180",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 1180,
    "page_start": 311,
    "page_end": 311,
    "char_start": 605051,
    "char_end": 606843,
    "char_count": 1792,
    "text": "311\n\n9\nCONFIDENTIALITY\n9.1\nThe Parties hereby acknowledge and agree that each of them possess and will continue to\npossess information that has been created, discovered, developed, or otherwise known and\nowned by them, which information has commercial value in the business in which they are\nor may become engaged (the aforementioned information is hereinafter called\n\"Proprietary Information\"). The Parties, on behalf of themselves, agree that during the\nterms of this Agreement and after the termination or expiration hereof, each of them will\nkeep in confidence and trust all Proprietary Information received from the other Party, and\nthey will not use or disclose any such Proprietary Information or anything directly relating\nto it without the written consent of the other Party(s).\n9.2\nIn the event of the expiration or termination of this Agreement for any reason, the Parties\nshall promptly, at the direction of the owner of such Proprietary Information, cease to use,\ndestroy or return to the owner all documents and data of any nature pertaining to the\nProprietary Information owned by such Party, and will not keep or deliver to anyone else\nany documents or data of any description or any reproduction of any description containing\nor pertaining to any Proprietary Information.\n9.3\nThis Clause shall not, however, apply to information which:\n(a)\nis or becomes publicly available without the fault of any Party;\n(b)\nwas known to any Party on a non-confidential basis prior to disclosure;\n(c)\nis independently developed by any Party without use of the Proprietary\nInformation;\n(d)\nis disclosed by the owner of such information to a Third Party without restrictions\nsimilar to those contained herein;\n(e)\nis disclosed in order to enable the sell-down/ draw-down of debt or to proposed",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-1181",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 1181,
    "page_start": 311,
    "page_end": 311,
    "char_start": 606844,
    "char_end": 608036,
    "char_count": 1192,
    "text": "Third Party transferees, provided that the recipient executes a confidentiality\nundertaking to use the information solely for that purpose;\n(f)\nis disclosed in order to comply with the requirements of Applicable Laws including\nany requirements for the stock exchange listing of the Concessionaire or any entity,\nwhich directly or indirectly, holds Equity Shares;\n(g)\nis disclosed to any of the consultants (legal, financial, technical or otherwise) of\nthe Parties, provided that the recipient executes a confidentiality undertaking to\nuse the information solely for the purpose disclosed.\n9.4\nThe Shareholders agree with each other and the Concessionaire to use their, and to cause\nthe Concessionaire to use its, best efforts to assure that all information disclosed in\nconnection with the business of the Concessionaire and not otherwise generally available\nshall be kept confidential and shall not be revealed.\n10\nGOVERNING LAW AND CONSENT TO JURISDICTION; ARBITRATION\n10.1\nThis Agreement and all questions of its interpretation shall be construed in accordance with\nthe laws of India. Subject to Clause 10.3, the courts at [New Delhi] shall have exclusive\njurisdiction over this Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-1182",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 1182,
    "page_start": 312,
    "page_end": 312,
    "char_start": 608038,
    "char_end": 609712,
    "char_count": 1674,
    "text": "312\n\n10.2\nThe Parties agree that they shall attempt to resolve through good faith consultation, all and\nany issue, dispute, difference or controversy of whatever nature howsoever arising under\nor out of or in relation to this Agreement (including its interpretation) between the Parties,\nand so notified in writing by either Party to the other Party (\"Disputes\"), and such\nconsultation shall begin promptly after a Party has delivered to the other Party a written\nrequest for such consultation: Provided that if such good faith consultations have not\nresulted in a resolution of the dispute within 60 (sixty) days of such consultations having\ncommenced, the provisions of Clause 10.3 shall apply.\n10.3\nArbitration\n10.3.1 Any dispute, difference or claim arising out of or in connection with this Agreement, which\nis not resolved amicably, shall be decided finally by reference to a sole arbitrator to be\nappointed by the Chief Justice of the [Delhi] High Court. Such arbitration shall be held in\naccordance with the Rules of Arbitration of the International Centre for Alternative Dispute\nResolution, New Delhi (the \"Rules\") or such other rules as may be mutually agreed by the\nParties, and shall be subject to the provisions of the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996.\n10.3.2 The arbitrator shall issue a reasoned award and such award shall be final and binding on\nthe Parties. The venue of arbitration shall be [New Delhi] and the language of arbitration\nshall be English.\n10.3.3 This Agreement and the rights and obligations of the Parties shall remain in full force and\neffect, pending the award in any arbitration proceedings hereunder.\n11\nMISCELLANEOUS\n11.1\nNotices",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-1183",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 1183,
    "page_start": 312,
    "page_end": 312,
    "char_start": 609714,
    "char_end": 611476,
    "char_count": 1762,
    "text": "All notices or other communications to be given or made under this Agreement shall be in\nwriting, shall either be delivered personally or sent by courier or registered post with an\nadditional copy to be sent by facsimile or e-mail. The address for service of each Party, its\nfacsimile number and e-mail address are set out under its name on the signing pages hereto.\nA notice shall be effective upon actual receipt thereof, save that where it is received after\n5.30 (five thirty) p.m. on any day, or on a day that is a public holiday, the notice shall be\ndeemed to be received on the first working day following the date of actual receipt. Without\nprejudice to the foregoing, a Party giving or making a notice or communication by\nfacsimile or e-mail shall promptly deliver a copy thereof personally, or send it by courier\nor registered post to the addressee of such notice or communication. It is hereby agreed\nand acknowledged that any Party may by notice change the address to which such notices\nand communications to it are to be delivered or mailed. Such change shall be effective\nwhen all the Parties have notice of it.\n11.2\nForce Majeure\nNotwithstanding anything to the contrary contained in this Agreement, it is hereby\nexpressly agreed between the Parties that no relief shall be granted to any Party under this\nAgreement for, or on account of, Force Majeure.\n11.3\nSpecific performance of obligations\nThe Parties to this Agreement agree that, to the extent permitted under Applicable Laws,\nthe rights and obligations of the Parties under this Agreement shall be subject to the right\nof specific performance and may be specifically enforced against a defaulting Party. The\nParties acknowledge that any breach of the provisions of this Agreement will cause",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-1184",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 1184,
    "page_start": 313,
    "page_end": 313,
    "char_start": 611478,
    "char_end": 612774,
    "char_count": 1296,
    "text": "313\n\nimmediate irreparable harm to the adversely affected Party (\"Affected Party\") for which\nany compensation payable in damages shall not be an adequate remedy. Accordingly, the\nParties agree that the Affected Party shall be entitled to immediate and permanent\ninjunctive relief, specific performance or any other equitable relief from a court of\ncompetent jurisdiction in the event of any such breach or threatened breach by any other\nParty. The Parties agree and stipulate that the Affected Party shall be entitled to such\ninjunctive relief, specific performance or other equitable relief without (i) the necessity of\nproving actual damages; or (ii) posting a bond or other security. Nothing contained herein\nshall limit the Affected Party's right to any remedies at law or in equity, including without\nlimitation the recovery of damages from the defaulting Party.\n11.4\nEntire Agreement\n11.4.1 Subject to the provisions of the Clause 11.4.2, this Agreement, together with all Annexures,\nSchedules, Exhibits and attachments hereto, represents the entire agreement and\nunderstanding between the Parties with respect to the subject matter of this Agreement and\nsupersedes any prior agreement or understanding, written or oral, that the Parties may have\nhad.\n11.4.2 Nothing contained herein shall:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-1185",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 1185,
    "page_start": 313,
    "page_end": 313,
    "char_start": 612776,
    "char_end": 613327,
    "char_count": 551,
    "text": "(a)\naffect the provisions of the Concession Agreement;\n(b)\nprevent the Private Participants from having any other inter-se arrangements\nregarding their shareholding in the Concessionaire, provided that no such\narrangements shall in any way affect the rights of the Authority under this\nAgreement or under the Concession Agreement.\nFor the avoidance of doubt, it is clarified that in the event of a conflict between the\nprovisions of the Concession Agreement and this Agreement, the provisions of the\nConcession Agreement shall prevail.\n11.5\nAmendments",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-1186",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 1186,
    "page_start": 313,
    "page_end": 313,
    "char_start": 613329,
    "char_end": 613538,
    "char_count": 209,
    "text": "Any modification, amendment, or waiver of any provision of this Agreement shall be\neffective if, but only if, in writing and signed in person or by an authorised representative\nof each Party.\n11.6\nSeverability",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-1187",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 1187,
    "page_start": 313,
    "page_end": 313,
    "char_start": 613540,
    "char_end": 614286,
    "char_count": 746,
    "text": "If any article, clause, section or paragraph, or part thereof, of this Agreement or any\nagreement or document appended hereto or made a part hereof is invalid, ruled illegal by\nany court of competent jurisdiction, or unenforceable under present or future Applicable\nLaws, then it is the intention of the Parties that the remainder of the Agreement, or any\nagreement or document appended hereto or made a part hereof, shall not be affected\nthereby unless the deletion of such provision shall cause this Agreement to become\nmaterially adverse to any Party in which case the Parties shall negotiate in good faith such\nchanges to the Agreement as will best preserve for the Parties the benefits and obligations\nunder such provision.\n11.7\nCounterparts",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-1188",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 1188,
    "page_start": 313,
    "page_end": 313,
    "char_start": 614288,
    "char_end": 614488,
    "char_count": 200,
    "text": "This Agreement may be executed in two or more counterparts, and by each Party on the\nsame or different counterparts, but all of such counterparts shall together constitute one\nand the same instrument.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-1189",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 1189,
    "page_start": 314,
    "page_end": 314,
    "char_start": 614490,
    "char_end": 615114,
    "char_count": 624,
    "text": "314\n\n11.8\nWaivers\n\nNo failure by a Party to take any action with respect to a breach of this Agreement or a\ndefault by any other Party shall constitute a waiver of the former Party's right to enforce\nany provision of this Agreement or to take action with respect to such breach or default or\nany subsequent breach or default. Waiver by any Party of any breach or failure to comply\nwith any provision of this Agreement by a Party shall not be construed as, or constitute, a\ncontinuing waiver of such provision, or a waiver of any other breach of or failure to comply\nwith any other provision of this Agreement.\n11.9\nNo agency",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-1190",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 1190,
    "page_start": 314,
    "page_end": 314,
    "char_start": 615116,
    "char_end": 615434,
    "char_count": 318,
    "text": "This Agreement shall not constitute any Party as the legal representative or agent of another\nParty, nor shall any Party have the right or authority, to assume, create or incur any liability\nor obligation, express or implied, against, in the name of, or on behalf of another Party.\n11.10   No Third Party beneficiaries",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-1191",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 1191,
    "page_start": 314,
    "page_end": 314,
    "char_start": 615436,
    "char_end": 615830,
    "char_count": 394,
    "text": "Nothing expressed or mentioned in this Agreement is intended or shall be construed to give\nany entity other than the Parties hereto (and their respective successors and permitted\nassigns) any legal or equitable right, remedy or claim under or in respect of this Agreement\nor any provision herein contained.\n11.11  Independence of the Parties with respect of each other and of the Concessionaire",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-1192",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 1192,
    "page_start": 314,
    "page_end": 314,
    "char_start": 615832,
    "char_end": 616125,
    "char_count": 293,
    "text": "The Parties are and shall remain independent. None of the Parties shall be considered an\nagent of the other, nor shall they have authority to enter into any contract or any obligation\nfor, or make any warranty or representation on behalf of the other, or the Concessionaire.\n11.12  Arms length",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-1193",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 1193,
    "page_start": 314,
    "page_end": 314,
    "char_start": 616127,
    "char_end": 616581,
    "char_count": 454,
    "text": "All relationships between each Party of the one part, and the Concessionaire of the other\npart, shall be conducted at arms length and on competitive terms.\n11.13  Encumbrance\nThe Parties agree that the Private Participants shall not be entitled to Encumber their\nshareholding in the Concessionaire other than in favour of or for the benefit of the Senior\nLenders under the Financing Agreements and/or for working capital\narrangements for the XXX Ropeway.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC086-1194",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "paragraph_index": 1194,
    "page_start": 314,
    "page_end": 314,
    "char_start": 616583,
    "char_end": 617772,
    "char_count": 1189,
    "text": "11.14  Consequential Loss\n\nNotwithstanding anything to the contrary contained in this Agreement, in no event shall\nany Party, its officers, employees or agents be liable to any other Party (on the basis of\ncontract, indemnity, warranty or tort including negligence and strict or absolute liability or\nbreach of statutory duty or otherwise) for any matter arising out of, or in connection with,\nthis Agreement in respect of any Consequential Loss suffered by such other Party. For the\npurposes of this provision, “Consequential Loss” means any indirect or consequential loss\n(including loss of profit, loss of revenue, loss of contract, loss of goodwill, liability under\nother agreements, or liability to third parties) resulting from such breach and whether or\nnot the Party committing the breach ought to have known, that such indirect or\nconsequential loss would be likely to be suffered as a result of such breach and includes\nthe payment or repayment of any amounts (or any acceleration thereof) to lenders or\ncreditors of the aggrieved Party from time to time, but excludes death or personal injury\nresulting from the negligence of the Party liable, its officers, employees or agents.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
