    "paragraph_index": 173,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 47605,
    "char_end": 48117,
    "char_count": 512,
    "text": "11.5  If in any case, the Contractor fails to make payments to outsourced personnel in the stipulated\ntime, due to some genuine reason submitted in writing, this office, at the discretion of the\ncompetent authorities, reserves the right to make the payments of minimum wages directly\ninto the accounts of outsourced personnel. The Contractor, hereby, binds himself to deposit\nstatutory deductions (EPF, ESIC and others, if any) for the default month and no claim for the\nservice charge of that month may be paid.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0174",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 174,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 48119,
    "char_end": 48538,
    "char_count": 419,
    "text": "11.6  Further, if the contractor fails to deposit statutory deductions (EPF, ESIC and others, if any)\nfor the default month, he is liable to share the Establishment ID with this office for the\npayment of the above by this office. In this effect, he shall provide the consent to use the\ncredentials to make above statutory payments. Application of this clause attracts a penalty of\nhalf of the service charge of a month.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0175",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 175,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 48540,
    "char_end": 48691,
    "char_count": 151,
    "text": "11.7 The above Clause 10.5 and 10.6 may be operated only two times in the entire contractual\nperiod not exceeding two months, combinedly or separately.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0176",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 176,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 48693,
    "char_end": 48881,
    "char_count": 188,
    "text": "11.8 The initial cost of the Contract shall be valid for a period of one year. No price escalation,\nother than minimum wages revision, shall be entertained by the Client during the period.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0177",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 177,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 48883,
    "char_end": 49144,
    "char_count": 261,
    "text": "11.9 After expiry of the initial period of the Contract of one year and if the Contract is renewed by\nthe Client, the Contractor shall claim increase in the Contract cost only on account of increase\nin the minimum wages, as and when increased by the Government.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0178",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 178,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 49146,
    "char_end": 49332,
    "char_count": 186,
    "text": "11.10 If the contract is extended for a further period of one year, the cost of materials will increase\nby 10%. The Contractor is hereby agreed to accept such rates in case of extension.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0179",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 179,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 49334,
    "char_end": 49495,
    "char_count": 161,
    "text": "11.11 In addition to the Contract payments, the Client shall pay for any additional services required\nby the Client, which are not specified in the bid document.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0180",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 180,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 49497,
    "char_end": 49636,
    "char_count": 139,
    "text": "11.12 All payments shall be made by NEFT only, after deducting TDS, as per the rules of the\nGovernment and as applicable from time to time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0181",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 181,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 49638,
    "char_end": 49979,
    "char_count": 341,
    "text": "11.13 Client shall be entitled to deduct in accordance with Applicable Law, Income Tax or\nwithholding tax or other deductions (as the case may be), from any payments made to the\nContractor, and the amount so deducted shall be deemed to be a payment made to the\nContractor. Client shall provide a certificate certifying the deduction so made.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0182",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 182,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 49981,
    "char_end": 50130,
    "char_count": 149,
    "text": "11.14 No payment shall be made in advance nor any loan from any bank or financial institution\nrecommended on the basis of the order of award of work.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0183",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 183,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 50132,
    "char_end": 50319,
    "char_count": 187,
    "text": "11.15 Client shall not be liable for any payment of any administrative charges incurred by the\ncontractor on account of disbursal of insurance claim/ EPF/ ESIC etc. towards its employees.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0184",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 184,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 50321,
    "char_end": 50555,
    "char_count": 234,
    "text": "12. FORCE MAJEURE - OBLIGATIONS OF THE PARTIES\n\n12.1 “Force Majeure” shall mean any event beyond the control of Client or of the Contractor, as\nthe case may be, and which is unavoidable notwithstanding the reasonable care of the party",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0185",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 185,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 50557,
    "char_end": 50694,
    "char_count": 137,
    "text": "Office of the Accountant General (Audit-II),\nMadhya Pradesh, Bhopal\nBid Document No. Admin-III/outsourcing/2024-25/\nDated 2 6 . 0 1 . 2 4",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0186",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 186,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 50696,
    "char_end": 50868,
    "char_count": 172,
    "text": "affected, and which could not have been prevented by exercise of reasonable skill and care\nand good industry practices and shall include, without limitation, the following:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0187",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 187,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 50870,
    "char_end": 51042,
    "char_count": 172,
    "text": "(i) War, hostilities, invasion, act of foreign enemy and civil war;\n\n(ii) Rebellion, revolution, insurrection, mutiny, conspiracy, riot, civil commotion and terrorist acts;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0188",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 188,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 51044,
    "char_end": 51188,
    "char_count": 144,
    "text": "(iii) Strike, sabotage, unlawful lockout, epidemics, quarantine and plague;\n\n(iv) Earthquake, fire, flood or cyclone, or other natural disaster.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0189",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 189,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 51190,
    "char_end": 51468,
    "char_count": 278,
    "text": "As soon as reasonably practicable but not more than 48 (forty-eight) hours following the date of\ncommencement of any event of Force Majeure, an Affected Party shall notify the other Party of\nthe event of Force Majeure setting out, inter alia, the following in reasonable detail:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0190",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 190,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 51470,
    "char_end": 51591,
    "char_count": 121,
    "text": "12.2  the date of commencement of the event of Force Majeure;\n\n12.3  the nature and extent of the event of Force Majeure;",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0191",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 191,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 51593,
    "char_end": 51886,
    "char_count": 293,
    "text": "12.4 the estimated Force Majeure Period,\n\n12.5 reasonable proof of the nature of such delay or failure and its anticipated effect upon the time\nfor performance and the nature of and the extent to which, performance of any of its obligations\nunder the Contract is affected by the Force Majeure.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0192",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 192,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 51888,
    "char_end": 52085,
    "char_count": 197,
    "text": "12.6 the measures which the Affected Party has taken or proposes to take to alleviate/mitigate the\nimpact of the Force Majeure and to resume performance of such of its obligations affected\nthereby.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0193",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 193,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 52087,
    "char_end": 52221,
    "char_count": 134,
    "text": "12.7 any other relevant information concerning the Force Majeure and /or the rights and obligations\nof the Parties under the Contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0194",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 194,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 52223,
    "char_end": 52367,
    "char_count": 144,
    "text": "13. TERMINATION\n\nThis Contract may be terminated forthwith by either party by giving written notice to the other at\nleast 30 days in advance if:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0195",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 195,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 52369,
    "char_end": 52603,
    "char_count": 234,
    "text": "13.1 The other party is in material breach of its obligations under this Agreement and / or, in the\ncase of such breaches capable of being remedied, fails to remedy that breach within thirty\ndays of receiving notice of such breach; or",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0196",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 196,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 52605,
    "char_end": 52708,
    "char_count": 103,
    "text": "13.2 The Contract may be terminated forthwith by the Client by giving written notice to the\nContractor:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0197",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 197,
    "page_start": 22,
    "page_end": 22,
    "char_start": 52710,
    "char_end": 52890,
    "char_count": 180,
    "text": "13.2.1 In case of breach of any of terms and conditions of the Contract by the Contractor, the\nCompetent Authority of the Client shall have the right to cancel the Contract without",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0198",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 198,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 52892,
    "char_end": 53029,
    "char_count": 137,
    "text": "Office of the Accountant General (Audit-II),\nMadhya Pradesh, Bhopal\nBid Document No. Admin-III/outsourcing/2024-25/\nDated 2 6 . 0 1 . 2 4",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0199",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 199,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 53031,
    "char_end": 53212,
    "char_count": 181,
    "text": "assigning any reason thereof, and nothing will be payable by the Client and in that event\nand the performance security deposit in the form of DD/FDR shall be forfeited and\nencashed.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0200",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 200,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 53214,
    "char_end": 53784,
    "char_count": 570,
    "text": "13.2.2 If the Contractor goes bankrupt and becomes insolvent.\n\n13.3 In case of failure to comply with the provisions of the terms and conditions of the contract by\nthe agency (ies) that has/have been awarded the contract, the competent authority of the Office\nof the Accountant General (Audit-II) Madhya Pradesh, Bhopal reserves the right to award the\ncontract to the next higher bidder or any other outside agency and the difference of price shall\nbe recovered from the defaulter agency who has been awarded the initial contract and this\nwill be binding on the bidders.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0201",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 201,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 53786,
    "char_end": 54085,
    "char_count": 299,
    "text": "13.4 The Office of the Accountant General (Audit-II) Madhya Pradesh, Bhopal may terminate the\nContract if it is found that the Contractor is blacklisted/debarred on previous occasions by any\nof the Government Departments / Institutions / Local Bodies / Municipalities/ Public Sector\nUndertaking etc.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0202",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 202,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 54087,
    "char_end": 54314,
    "char_count": 227,
    "text": "13.5 If the Contractor fails continuously to clean the premises satisfactorily due to low\nquality/quantity of the materials, the employer shall at its discretion, may terminate the\nContract without assigning any reason thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0203",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 203,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 54316,
    "char_end": 54637,
    "char_count": 321,
    "text": "13.6 Further, in case of termination of contract, the contractor is liable to share the Establishment\nID with this office for the payment of the statutory deductions by this office. In this effect, he\nshall provide the consent to use the credentials for deposition of statutory deductions till\nfinalization of new tender.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0204",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 204,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 54639,
    "char_end": 54811,
    "char_count": 172,
    "text": "14. DISCLAIMER\n\nThe relatives / near relatives of employees of the Client are prohibited from participation in this\nbid. The near relatives for this purpose are defined as:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0205",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 205,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 54813,
    "char_end": 55112,
    "char_count": 299,
    "text": "(a) Members of a Hindu Undivided Family.\n(b) Their husband or wife.\n(c) The one is related to the other in the manner as father, mother, son(s), son’s wife (daughter-in-\nlaw), daughter(s) & daughter’s husband (son-in-law), brother(s) & brother’s wife, sister(s) and\nsister’s husband (brother-in-law)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0206",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 206,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 55114,
    "char_end": 55391,
    "char_count": 277,
    "text": "15. INSOLVENCY\n\n15.1 The competent authority of the Office of the Accountant General (Audit-II) Madhya  Pradesh,\nBhopal may at any time by notice in writing summarily terminate the contract without\ncompensation to the contractor in any of the following events, that is to say:-",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0207",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 207,
    "page_start": 23,
    "page_end": 23,
    "char_start": 55393,
    "char_end": 55780,
    "char_count": 387,
    "text": "i) If the contractor being an individual or if firm, any partner in the contractor’s firm, shall at any\ntime be adjudged insolvent or shall have a receiving order or orders for administration of his\nestate made against him or shall take any proceedings for liquidation or composition under any\ninsolvency not for the time being in force or shall make any convenience or assignment of his",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0208",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 208,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 55782,
    "char_end": 55919,
    "char_count": 137,
    "text": "Office of the Accountant General (Audit-II),\nMadhya Pradesh, Bhopal\nBid Document No. Admin-III/outsourcing/2024-25/\nDated 2 6 . 0 1 . 2 4",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0209",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 209,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 55921,
    "char_end": 56071,
    "char_count": 150,
    "text": "efforts or enter into any arrangements or composition with his creditors or suspend payment\nthereof if the firm be dissolved under partnership act, or",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0210",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 210,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 56073,
    "char_end": 56395,
    "char_count": 322,
    "text": "ii) If the contractor being a company shall pass a resolution or the court shall make an order for\nthe liquidation of the affairs or a receiver of Manager on behalf of the debenture holder shall be\nappointed or circumstances shall have arisen which entitled the court or debenture holders to\nappoint a receiver or Manager.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0211",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 211,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 56397,
    "char_end": 56826,
    "char_count": 429,
    "text": "iii) If the contractor commits any breach of this contract not herein specifically proved for: Provided\nalways that such determination shall not prejudice any right of action or remedy which shall\nhave accrued or shall accrue thereafter to the purchaser and provided also that the contractor\nshall be liable to pay the purchaser for any extra expenditure, he is thereby put to but shall not\nbe entitled to any gain on repurchase.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0212",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 212,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 56828,
    "char_end": 56987,
    "char_count": 159,
    "text": "16. CURRENCIES OF BID AND PAYMENTS\n\n16.1 The Bidder shall submit his price bid in Indian Rupees and payments under this contract will\nbe made in Indian Rupees.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0213",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 213,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 56989,
    "char_end": 57870,
    "char_count": 881,
    "text": "17. GOVERNING LAWS AND SETTLEMENT OF DISPUTE\n\n17.1 Any claims, disputes and or differences (including a dispute regarding the existence, validity\nor termination of this Contract) arising out of or relating to this contract including\ninterpretation of its terms shall be resolved through joint discussion of the Authorised\nRepresentatives of the concerned parties. However, if the disputes are not resolved by the\ndiscussions as aforesaid within a period 30 days, then the matter will be referred for\nadjudication to the arbitration of a sole arbitrator to be appointed by the Client in accordance\nwith the provisions of the Arbitration and Conciliation Act 1996 and rules made thereunder\nincluding any modifications, amendments and future enactments thereto. The venue for the\nArbitration will be Bhopal and the decision of the arbitrator shall be final and binding on the\nparties.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0214",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 214,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 57872,
    "char_end": 58034,
    "char_count": 162,
    "text": "17.2 Jurisdiction of Court: This Contract is governed by the laws of Republic of India and shall\nbe subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts in Bhopal.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0215",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 215,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 58036,
    "char_end": 58172,
    "char_count": 136,
    "text": "18. CORRUPT OR FRAUDULENT PRACTICES\n18.1 The Contractors shall observe the highest standard of ethics during the period of the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0216",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 216,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 58174,
    "char_end": 58334,
    "char_count": 160,
    "text": "18.2 The Client shall reject the Bid, if it determines that the Bidder has engaged in corrupt or\nfraudulent practices in competing for the contract in question.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0217",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 217,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 58336,
    "char_end": 58594,
    "char_count": 258,
    "text": "18.3 The Client will declare a firm ineligible / blacklist, either indefinitely or for a stated period of\ntime, if it at any time determines that the firm has engaged in corrupt or fraudulent practices\nin competing for this bid, or in executing the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0218",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 218,
    "page_start": 24,
    "page_end": 24,
    "char_start": 58596,
    "char_end": 58783,
    "char_count": 187,
    "text": "18.4 The Client shall also terminate the contract and blacklist the contractor in case it is found that\nthe contractor was blacklisted /debarred by any other organization on any occasion.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0219",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 219,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 58785,
    "char_end": 58922,
    "char_count": 137,
    "text": "Office of the Accountant General (Audit-II),\nMadhya Pradesh, Bhopal\nBid Document No. Admin-III/outsourcing/2024-25/\nDated 2 6 . 0 1 . 2 4",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0220",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 220,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 58924,
    "char_end": 59107,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "ANNEXURE-4\nSPECIAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT\n(SCC)\n1.  The special conditions of Contract shall supplement the “Instructions to the Bidders” and\nGeneral Conditions of the Contract (GCC).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0221",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 221,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 59109,
    "char_end": 59878,
    "char_count": 769,
    "text": "2. INDEMNIFICATION:\n\nThe successful bidder is solely liable to fully indemnify and keep Client indemnified against all\nlosses/penalties/awards/decrees arising out of litigation/claims/application initiated against the\nClient on account of acts of omission/commission attributable to the Contractor and which are\npunishable under the provisions of various Central Labour and Employment Acts including the\nfollowing Acts as amended from time to time. Client shall be vested with sole discretion to\ndetermine damages/ loss suffered on account of above from the dues payable from security deposit\nor from either the personal property of bidder or property owned by his firm/company by way of\ninitiating suitable legal litigation against the Contractor at any point of time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0222",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 222,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 59880,
    "char_end": 60308,
    "char_count": 428,
    "text": "3. LABOUR LAW COMPLIANCES\n\n3.1 The engagement and employment of labourers and payment of wages to them as per existing\nprovisions of various labour laws and regulations is the sole responsibility of the Contractor\nand any breach of such laws or regulations shall be deemed to be breach of this contract. Client\nmay ask the contractor to produce documents to verify that these provisions/laws are complied\nwith by the contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0223",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 223,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 60310,
    "char_end": 60523,
    "char_count": 213,
    "text": "(a) All wages and allied benefits such as leave, ESI, PF, Gratuity, Bonus etc., shall be paid by the\ncontractor and Client shall not incur any liability or additional expenditure whatsoever for\npersonnel deployed.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0224",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 224,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 60525,
    "char_end": 60605,
    "char_count": 80,
    "text": "(b) It is mandatory that the employees must be paid through online banking only.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0225",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 225,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 60607,
    "char_end": 61296,
    "char_count": 689,
    "text": "3.2 The Contractor shall abide by all labour laws, laws related to EPF Organization, ESI\nCorporation, Workmen Compensation Act. The details of EPF, ESIC in respect of their\ndeployed staff shall be submitted by the Contractor to Client every month along with the bill.\nThe Contractor shall abide including but not limited to, matters relating to timely payment of\nwages and allowances, payment of minimum wages, payment of overtime, grant of leave,\npayment of workmen's compensation, working hours, safety, maternity benefits, holidays,\nframing of standing orders, disciplinary action against employees, payment of provident fund\ncontributions, payment of gratuities and payment of bonuses.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0226",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 226,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 61298,
    "char_end": 61483,
    "char_count": 185,
    "text": "3.3 The contractor shall be liable for any legal dispute / case / claims that arises or may arise during\ncurrency of the contract due to non-compliances of labour or other related laws.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0227",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 227,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 61485,
    "char_end": 61622,
    "char_count": 137,
    "text": "Office of the Accountant General (Audit-II),\nMadhya Pradesh, Bhopal\nBid Document No. Admin-III/outsourcing/2024-25/\nDated 2 6 . 0 1 . 2 4",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0228",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 228,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 61624,
    "char_end": 61997,
    "char_count": 373,
    "text": "3.4 The contractor shall be responsible for compliance of all the laws rules/regulations and Govt.\ninstructions that are/will be applicable to and aimed to protect the interest of the\nemployees/worker engaged by it and shall ensure payment of all the statutory dues/liabilities\nas may have arisen during the past ‘or’ may arise during the course of performance of contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0229",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 229,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 61999,
    "char_end": 62088,
    "char_count": 89,
    "text": "3.5 The Contractor shall submit periodical returns as may be specified from time to time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0230",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 230,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 62090,
    "char_end": 62506,
    "char_count": 416,
    "text": "4. OFFICIAL RECORDS:\n\n4.1 The Contractor shall maintain complete official records of disbursement of wages / salary,\nshowing specifically details of all deductions such as ESI, PF etc. in respect of all the staff\ndeployed in Client’s office.\n4.2 The Contractor shall maintain complete official records of all the cleaning materials provided\nin the office every month or as an when required, right from the beginning.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0231",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 231,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 62508,
    "char_end": 62843,
    "char_count": 335,
    "text": "4.3 The Contractor shall maintain a personal file in respect of all the staff who is deployed in\nClient’s office. The personal file shall invariably consist of personal details such as name,\naddress, date of birth, gender, residential address (Temporary / Permanent) and all grievances\nrecorded by the staff vis-à-vis action taken etc.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0232",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 232,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 62845,
    "char_end": 63129,
    "char_count": 284,
    "text": "4.4 The Contractor shall furnish an undertaking that within seven days of the close of every month\nthey will submit to Client a statement showing the recoveries of contributions in respect of\nemployees with Certificate that the same have been deposited with ESIC / EPFO\nCommissioners.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0233",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 233,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 63131,
    "char_end": 63231,
    "char_count": 100,
    "text": "4.5 The Contractor shall not make any unauthorized deductions from the wages of the contract\nlabour.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0234",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 234,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 63233,
    "char_end": 63942,
    "char_count": 709,
    "text": "4.6 Each monthly bill must accompany the:\n(a) List of employees with their date of engagement\n(b) The amount of wages (The Contractor shall ensure that minimum wages are paid to\nall the employees with all the benefits (such as ESIC/ EPF/ Bonus etc.)\n(c) Copies of authenticated documents of payments of such contributions to EPFO/ESIC\n(d) Declaration of the Contractor regarding compliance of Amount of EPF / ESIC\n(e) The monthly bill shall also include the total cost on cleaning materials which has been\nalready fixed by the Client as per bid document along with the list of items and quantities\nused during the month. (The Contractor shall be required to submit segregated bills, if\nrequired by the client)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0235",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 235,
    "page_start": 26,
    "page_end": 26,
    "char_start": 63944,
    "char_end": 64056,
    "char_count": 112,
    "text": "4.7 The Contractor shall also prepare a register indicating all payments / dues in respect of all the\nemployees.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0236",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 236,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 64058,
    "char_end": 64195,
    "char_count": 137,
    "text": "Office of the Accountant General (Audit-II),\nMadhya Pradesh, Bhopal\nBid Document No. Admin-III/outsourcing/2024-25/\nDated 2 6 . 0 1 . 2 4",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0237",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 237,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 64197,
    "char_end": 64599,
    "char_count": 402,
    "text": "ANNEXURE-5\nSCHEDULE OF WORKS/ SERVICES\nTO BE PROVIDED\nIn this Schedule of Requirements, the details of Manpower (Sanitation/ Housekeeping) Service\nalong with Cleaning material to be provided by the Contractor and also other information,\ninstructions of the Client and instructions to the Contractor’s employees posted at the Clients’ site\nand all such other aspect of the Contracts are to be mentioned.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0238",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 238,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 64601,
    "char_end": 64785,
    "char_count": 184,
    "text": "1. GENERAL INSTRUCTIONS\n\n1.1 The Contractor shall deploy all Manpower (Sanitation/ Housekeeping Service) at the Client\nfacility in the manner and as per the instructions of the Client.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0239",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 239,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 64787,
    "char_end": 64992,
    "char_count": 205,
    "text": "1.2 The Contractor shall ensure that all personnel are fully conversant with the premises and with\nthe client’s business activities and its related Manpower (Sanitation/ Housekeeping Service)\nrequirements.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0240",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 240,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 64994,
    "char_end": 65237,
    "char_count": 243,
    "text": "1.3 The Client shall have the right to have any person removed who is considered to be undesirable\nor otherwise and similarly the Contractor reserves the right to remove the personnel with prior\npermission of the Client, emergencies, exempted.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0241",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 241,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 65239,
    "char_end": 65347,
    "char_count": 108,
    "text": "1.4 The Contractor shall cover its personnel for personal accident and/ or death whilst performing\nthe duty.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0242",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 242,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 65349,
    "char_end": 65545,
    "char_count": 196,
    "text": "1.5 The Contractor shall exercise adequate supervision to ensure proper performance of Manpower\n(Sanitation/ Housekeeping Service) and supply of cleaning items in accordance with the\nrequirements.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0243",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 243,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 65547,
    "char_end": 65909,
    "char_count": 362,
    "text": "1.6 The Contractor shall issue identity cards / identification documents to all its employees who\nwill be instructed by the Contractor to display the same at all times. The personnel of the\nContractor shall be subject to detailed direction and control of the Contractor and in relation\nto manner and model of performance of duties, as agreed vide this agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0244",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 244,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 65911,
    "char_end": 66239,
    "char_count": 328,
    "text": "1.7 The personnel of the Contractor shall not be the employees of the Client and they shall not\nclaim any salary or allowances, compensation, damages, or anything arising out of their\nemployment/duty under this Contract. The Contractor shall make them known about this\nposition in writing before deployment under this agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0245",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 245,
    "page_start": 27,
    "page_end": 27,
    "char_start": 66241,
    "char_end": 66419,
    "char_count": 178,
    "text": "1.8 The Contractor shall also provide at its own cost all benefits statutory or otherwise to its\nemployees and the Client shall not have any liability whatsoever on this account.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0246",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 246,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 66421,
    "char_end": 66558,
    "char_count": 137,
    "text": "Office of the Accountant General (Audit-II),\nMadhya Pradesh, Bhopal\nBid Document No. Admin-III/outsourcing/2024-25/\nDated 2 6 . 0 1 . 2 4",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0247",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 247,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 66560,
    "char_end": 66740,
    "char_count": 180,
    "text": "1.9 The list of materials as mentioned in this bid document are for indicative purpose only. The\nsuccessful bidder may provide better available options too in the cleaning service.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0248",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 248,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 66742,
    "char_end": 66920,
    "char_count": 178,
    "text": "1.10 The quantities of housekeeping materials for a month as per given list of items mentioned at\n2.6 shall be procured by the successful bidder one week in advance of the month.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0249",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 249,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 66922,
    "char_end": 67067,
    "char_count": 145,
    "text": "1.11 Stock of material shall be purchased and stored in office only. The materials shall be used in\ncleaning service at the office premises only.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0250",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 250,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 67069,
    "char_end": 68834,
    "char_count": 1765,
    "text": "1.12 The bidders may visit the office premises to assess the cleaning requirements and storage\nof materials for cleaning service. The successful bidder shall agree to store the materials\nat a designated place provided by this office and shall submit a consent letter in this\nregard to office before commencement of the contract.\n1.13 The successful bidder shall purchase the materials and hand over the materials to his\nrepresentative. The representative shall submit the report annexing the list of items and\nindicating their quantities brought by him to the office Caretaker/ any other representative\nappointed by the employer each time. The agency shall ensure supervision of the entire\ncleaning in the office premises and storage of material.\n1.14 The Contractor shall store the material in the office one week before the anticipated full\nconsumption of the stock in order to maintain continuity in supply of cleaning materials in the\noffice.\n1.15 The materials shall be of the same/similar specification as mentioned in the bid document.\n1.16 If the materials used in cleaning work by the successful bidder will not be of satisfactory\nquality, the bidder is liable to change the material as desired by the office within 3 days from\nthe date of materials provided in the office by the bidder.\n1.17 The responsibility of storing the materials shall lie upon the successful bidder only. He shall\nnot lay any claim on the employer on account of any loss or degradation of any material, in\nany case.\n1.18 As the expenditure to be incurred in yearly procurement of materials is Rs 1,79,300/-.\nThe total material cost including freight charges, loading/unloading charges,\ntransportation charges or any other charges must not exceed Rs. 14,950/- per month in\nany case.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0251",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 251,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 68835,
    "char_end": 69295,
    "char_count": 460,
    "text": "1.19 If the contract is extended for a further period of one year, the cost of materials will increase\nby 10%. The Contractor is hereby agreed to accept such rates in case of extension.\n1.20 In case of any dispute arising between the office and the successful bidder, the decision of Sr.\nDeputy Accountant General (Administration) of Office of the Accountant General (Audit- II)\nM.P., 53, Arera Hills, Hoshangabad Road, Bhopal, M.P. shall be final and binding.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0252",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 252,
    "page_start": 28,
    "page_end": 28,
    "char_start": 69297,
    "char_end": 69509,
    "char_count": 212,
    "text": "2. DEPLOYMENT AND TENTATIVE REQUIREMENTS OF MANPOWER AND MATERIAL\n\n2.1 The Client intends to outsource Manpower (Sanitation/ Housekeeping Service) along with\nCleaning materials as per the norms of the Government.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0253",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 253,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 69511,
    "char_end": 69648,
    "char_count": 137,
    "text": "Office of the Accountant General (Audit-II),\nMadhya Pradesh, Bhopal\nBid Document No. Admin-III/outsourcing/2024-25/\nDated 2 6 . 0 1 . 2 4",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0254",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 254,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 69650,
    "char_end": 69896,
    "char_count": 246,
    "text": "2.2 The Manpower (Sanitation/ Housekeeping Service) appointed shall be deployed by the Client\nfor the work of Sanitation/ Cleaning of Urinals, Toilets and Mopping of floors etc. as deemed\nfit by the Client as per the provisions of para 3.1 above.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0255",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 255,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 69898,
    "char_end": 70209,
    "char_count": 311,
    "text": "2.3 The Contractor is not required to quote prices for Unskilled staff.\n\n2.4 The Contractor shall ensure that except that of the Service Margin all other levies (Wages,\nUniform, ESIC, EPF, Bonus etc.), which are charged to Client are passed on to the deployed\nemployees as their monthly wages by the Contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0256",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 256,
    "page_start": 29,
    "page_end": 29,
    "char_start": 70211,
    "char_end": 70331,
    "char_count": 120,
    "text": "2.5 The tentative requirements of Manpower (Sanitation/ Housekeeping Service) in each of\nthe category shall be as under:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
