    "paragraph_index": 264,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 73432,
    "char_end": 74171,
    "char_count": 739,
    "text": "* 1. For monthly average estimated quantity, the yearly estimated total quantity of any item/\nall item can be brought out by dividing by 12.\n* 2. The items and their quantity is indicative only. The actual quantity may vary as per actual\nrequirement of the Client.\n* 3. if there shall be requirement of any other item apart from the above list to be used in\ncleaning, the Contractor shall provide the additional item without any additional cost i.e. the\nadditional item shall be provided within the given fixed value of cost of materials.\n*  4 . It is also instructed that if 20% variation (increase or decrease) in consumption/ usage of\nany item in a month, the bidder shall bring into the notice of the office administration\nimmediately.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0265",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 265,
    "page_start": 31,
    "page_end": 31,
    "char_start": 74173,
    "char_end": 74778,
    "char_count": 605,
    "text": "3. PENALTIES\n\n3.1 The Contractor shall disburse salary to its deployed Manpower (Sanitation/ Housekeeping\nService) inclusive of DA, if any, latest by 5th of every month, failing which penalty of Rs.\n5000/- per day will be imposed upto 15th of the month and the contract shall liable to be\nterminated.\n3.2 In case the Contractor fails to make the payments by the stipulated date and time, the Contract\nis liable to be terminated and the Contractor is liable to be blacklisted and Performance\nSecurity Deposit submitted by the Contractor shall be forfeited and deposited in Clients’ bank\naccount thereafter.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0266",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 266,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 74780,
    "char_end": 74917,
    "char_count": 137,
    "text": "Office of the Accountant General (Audit-II),\nMadhya Pradesh, Bhopal\nBid Document No. Admin-III/outsourcing/2024-25/\nDated 2 6 . 0 1 . 2 4",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0267",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 267,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 74919,
    "char_end": 75421,
    "char_count": 502,
    "text": "3.3 If in any case, the Contractor fails to make payments to outsourced personnel in the stipulated\ntime, due to some genuine reason submitted in writing, this office, at the discretion of the\ncompetent authorities, reserves the right to make the payments of minimum wages directly\ninto the accounts of outsourced personnel. The Contractor, hereby, binds to deposit statutory\ndeductions (EPF, ESIC and others, if any) for the default month and no claim for the service\ncharge of that month may be paid.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0268",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 268,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 75423,
    "char_end": 75840,
    "char_count": 417,
    "text": "3.4 Further, if the contractor fails to deposit statutory deductions (EPF, ESIC and others, if any)\nfor the default month, he is liable to share the Establishment ID with this office for the\npayment of the above by this office. In this effect, he shall provide the consent to use the\ncredentials to make above statutory payments. Application of this clause attracts a penalty of\nhalf of the service charge of a month.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0269",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 269,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 75842,
    "char_end": 75990,
    "char_count": 148,
    "text": "3.5 The above Clause 3.3 and 3.4 may be operated only two times in the entire contractual period\nnot exceeding two months, combinedly or separately.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0270",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 270,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 75992,
    "char_end": 76367,
    "char_count": 375,
    "text": "3.6 The Contractor has to maintain adequate number of Manpower (Sanitation/ Housekeeping\nService) as per this contract and also arrange a pool of standby manpower. If the required\nnumber of Manpower (Sanitation/ Housekeeping Service)  are less than specified number\nas mentioned in the contract, a penalty of Rs. 500/- per absentee per day shall be deducted\nfrom the bill(s).",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0271",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 271,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 76369,
    "char_end": 76735,
    "char_count": 366,
    "text": "3.7 In case the Contractor fails to fulfill the minimum statutory requirements (ESIC/EPF) as per\nthe conditions of the bid document and fails to produce the concerned documents, it shall be\ntreated as breach of the Contract and the Contractor is liable to be blacklisted by the Client,\nin addition to forfeiting of the monthly bills and Performance Security Deposit.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0272",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 272,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 76737,
    "char_end": 77357,
    "char_count": 620,
    "text": "3.8 In case of breach of any conditions of the contract and for all types of losses caused including\nexcess cost due to hiring Manpower (Sanitation/ Housekeeping Service) along with Cleaning\nitems in the event of Contractor failing to provide requisitioned number of Manpower\n(Sanitation/ Housekeeping Service), the Client shall make deductions at double the rate of\nhiring rate on pro-rata basis from the bills preferred by the Vendor or that may become due\nto the Vendor under this or any other contract or from the security deposit or may be\ndemanded from him to be paid within seven days to the credit of the Client.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0273",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 273,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 77359,
    "char_end": 78036,
    "char_count": 677,
    "text": "3.9 Whenever and wherever it is found that the assigned work is not performed up to the entire\nsatisfaction of the Client, it will be brought to the notice of Contractor by the Client and if no\naction is taken immediately, penalty of Rs. 5000/- per day per complaint will be imposed\nby invoking penalty clause.\n3.10 If in any case, the successful bidder fails to provide/ store any item or all the items to be used\nin cleaning service, the employer would procure the same from the market and adjust this\namount from the bill of the successful bidder. Apart from this, a penalty @ 50 % of the value\nof procured materials by this office shall be imposed on the successful bidder.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0274",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 274,
    "page_start": 32,
    "page_end": 32,
    "char_start": 78038,
    "char_end": 78229,
    "char_count": 191,
    "text": "3.11 If, the reason of non-supply of cleaning materials to office being submitted in writing to the\nCompetent authorities, is not found genuine, the office, at the discretion of the Competent",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0275",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 275,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 78231,
    "char_end": 78368,
    "char_count": 137,
    "text": "Office of the Accountant General (Audit-II),\nMadhya Pradesh, Bhopal\nBid Document No. Admin-III/outsourcing/2024-25/\nDated 2 6 . 0 1 . 2 4",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0276",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 276,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 78370,
    "char_end": 78465,
    "char_count": 95,
    "text": "authorities, reserves the right to terminate the contract without assigning any reason thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0277",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 277,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 78467,
    "char_end": 78762,
    "char_count": 295,
    "text": "4. SCOPE OF WORK-CONTRACTOR\n\n4.1 The Contractor must provide standard and clean liveries to its employees / supervisors with\ntheir photo identity cards properly displayed during duty time. No extra payments shall be\nclaimed by the Contractor or its deployed staff from the Client for such items.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0278",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 278,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 78764,
    "char_end": 79266,
    "char_count": 502,
    "text": "4.2 The Contractor must provide salary slips, EPF numbers and ESI Cards, duly activated, to all\nthe deployed Manpower (Sanitation/ Housekeeping Service) at Client’s office. The Contractor\nshould also ensure that EPF statements to the deployed Manpower (Sanitation/ Housekeeping\nService) are provided immediately after the financial year closing. Any delay in submission\nof these records will force Client to deduct a proportionate amount from the bills, as decided\nby the competent authority of Client.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0279",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 279,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 79268,
    "char_end": 79983,
    "char_count": 715,
    "text": "4.3 Contractor must employ adult and skilled personnel only. Employment of child labour shall\nlead to the termination of the contract at the risk and cost of the Contractor. Contractor shall\ndeploy/engage reliable persons at Client’s office after proper character and police verification\nand impose any conditions as per prevailing contractual labour laws for such engagements,\ntake disciplinary action or reward any person at work etc., at its sole costs, risks and\nresponsibilities. Contractor shall intimate the details like name, age, parentage, address\n(residential as well as permanent) of all staff to the Client’s Office and shall also intimate\nchanges in addresses of the staff as and when they take place.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0280",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 280,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 79985,
    "char_end": 80187,
    "char_count": 202,
    "text": "4.4 Contractor shall deal with and settle the matters related with unions and shall make sure that\nno labour disputes / problems are referred to Client. It shall totally indemnify Client in this\nregard.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0281",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 281,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 80189,
    "char_end": 80650,
    "char_count": 461,
    "text": "4.5 Contractor should at all times indemnify Client against all claims, damages or compensation\nunder the provisions of Payment of Wages Act, 1936; Minimum Wages Act, 1948; Employer’s\nLiability Act, 1938; the Workmen Compensation Act, 1923; Industrial Disputes Act, 1947;\nMaternity Benefit Act, 1961; or any modification thereof or any other law relating thereto and\nrules made hereunder from time to time. Client will not own any responsibility in this regard.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0282",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 282,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 80652,
    "char_end": 81224,
    "char_count": 572,
    "text": "4.6 Contractor staff shall always be disciplined, properly dressed and be presentable all the time\nduring duty. The Manpower (Sanitation/ Housekeeping Service) deployed by Contractor shall\nbe properly trained, have requisite experience and skills for carrying out a wide variety of\nwork. The Contractor shall be solely responsible to tackle the matters in case any of its staff\ndeployed under this contract falls sick or is injured or goes on strike/ unfair activities etc. during\nperformance of his/her duty. It shall indemnify Client in all respects under this contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0283",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 283,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 81226,
    "char_end": 81430,
    "char_count": 204,
    "text": "4.7 Be it private or public areas, the Contractor’s employees shall be liable to be frisked/ checked\nby the security personnel at Client premises or on duty at any time during performance of their\nduties.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0284",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 284,
    "page_start": 33,
    "page_end": 33,
    "char_start": 81432,
    "char_end": 81608,
    "char_count": 176,
    "text": "4.8 Contractor’s employees shall perform their duties at the premises with due diligence and take\nall precautions to avoid any loss or damage to the government property/person.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0285",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 285,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 81610,
    "char_end": 81747,
    "char_count": 137,
    "text": "Office of the Accountant General (Audit-II),\nMadhya Pradesh, Bhopal\nBid Document No. Admin-III/outsourcing/2024-25/\nDated 2 6 . 0 1 . 2 4",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0286",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 286,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 81749,
    "char_end": 81963,
    "char_count": 214,
    "text": "4.9 Contractor shall be solely responsible for any indiscipline, theft, loss or damage to any person\nor persons / property at the premises on account of acts of omission and commission by the\nstaff deployed by him.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0287",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 287,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 81965,
    "char_end": 82216,
    "char_count": 251,
    "text": "4.10 The payments to its employees shall be disbursed by the Contractor through Bank Account\nremittance. The Contractor shall be required to produce details of bank transfer along with the\nmonthly invoice to the Client.\n5. SCOPE OF WORK – FOR SERVICES",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0288",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 288,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 82218,
    "char_end": 82803,
    "char_count": 585,
    "text": "5.1 The Manpower (Sanitation/ Housekeeping Service) shall be deployed at Building/Premises of\nOffice of the Accountant General (Audit-II) Madhya Pradesh, Bhopal.\n5.2 The Unskilled staff provided by of Contractor are liable to be deployed as Safaiwalas\n(Sanitation/ Housekeeping) in the Client’s premises. While working as Safaiwalas (Sanitation/\nHousekeeping), the  Contractor’s personnel are liable to perform duties which are related to\ncleaning in Client’s premises, open areas, cleaning of urinals, toilets, mopping of floors etc. or any\nother job as may be assigned by the Client.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0289",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 289,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 82805,
    "char_end": 83023,
    "char_count": 218,
    "text": "5.3 While providing all the Services, Contractor shall ensure that all duties are performed\ninvariably as per the desired standards of the Client, failing which it shall invoke penalty clauses\nof this Bidding Document.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0290",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 290,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 83025,
    "char_end": 83317,
    "char_count": 292,
    "text": "5.4 The Contractor shall also ensure that only Safaiwalas (Sanitation/ Housekeeping) with good\nhealth and experience are deployed in Client’s premises who can  cater to the requirements of\nClient’s standards, failing which it shall be liable for Contractor to provide replacement\nimmediately.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0291",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 291,
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 34,
    "char_start": 83319,
    "char_end": 84147,
    "char_count": 828,
    "text": "6. CODE OF CONDUCT:\n\nThe Contractor shall strictly observe that its personnel:\n\n Are free from any communicable disease.\n Are always smartly turned out and vigilant.\n Are punctual and arrive at least 15 minutes before start of their duty time.\n Take charges of their duties properly and thoroughly.\n Perform their duties with honesty and sincerity.\n Read and understand their post and site instructions and follow the same.\n Extend respect to all Officers and staff of the office of the Client.\n Shall not drink on duty, or come drunk and report for duty.\n Will not gossip or chit chat while on duty.\n Will never sleep while on duty post.\n Will not read newspaper or magazine while on duty.\n Will immediately report if any untoward incident / misconduct or misbehavior occurs, to\nContractor’s Control and the Client.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0292",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 292,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 84149,
    "char_end": 84286,
    "char_count": 137,
    "text": "Office of the Accountant General (Audit-II),\nMadhya Pradesh, Bhopal\nBid Document No. Admin-III/outsourcing/2024-25/\nDated 2 6 . 0 1 . 2 4",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0293",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 293,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 84288,
    "char_end": 84483,
    "char_count": 195,
    "text": " When in doubt, approach concerned person immediately.\n Get themselves checked by security personnel whenever they go out.\n Do not entertain visitors.\n Shall not smoke in the office premises.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0294",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 294,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 84485,
    "char_end": 84659,
    "char_count": 174,
    "text": "CONFIDENTIALITY\n\n The phone number and movement plans of the client shall not be given to anyone.\n The following information about the client shall not be given to anyone:-",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0295",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 295,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 84661,
    "char_end": 84923,
    "char_count": 262,
    "text": "o Car make, color and number of any officer(s)/official(s).\no Telephone no./ any other information.\no Location and movement plans.\no Meetings and conference schedules.\no Site plan of the premises.\no Travel details of the clients.\no Assets of the Client’s office.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0296",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "paragraph_index": 296,
    "page_start": 35,
    "page_end": 35,
    "char_start": 84925,
    "char_end": 85078,
    "char_count": 153,
    "text": "TELEPHONE HANDLING\n\nThe Contractor’s employees shall be instructed by the Contractor strictly not to misuse the\ntelephones in the facility of the Client.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
