    "char_start": 9226,
    "char_end": 10714,
    "char_count": 1488,
    "text": "Sign of Tenderer with seal\n12. Technical Bids will be scrutinized, by the evaluation committee as constituted by the\nMedical Superintendent to check all requisite and relevant documents and their\nauthenticity. The Tenderers, whose Technical Bids are accepted will be informed\nabout the date and time of opening of Financial Bids.\n13. In case the successful Tenderer declines the offer of Contract, for whatsoever reason(s),\nhis EMD will be forfeited.\n14. A formal contract shall be entered into with the successful tenderer. In this contract,\nthe successful tenderer shall be defined as Contractor.\n15. The successful tenderer will have to deposit the Performance Security Deposit of\nRs. 2,75,000/-(Rs. Two Lac Seventy Five Thousand Only)in the form of Demand\nDraft/Banker’s cheque of any scheduled bank, drawn in favour of “ESIC Fund A/c No. 1”\npayable at Ahmedabad and commence the work within 15 days of acceptance of tender\notherwise the contract may be cancelled and EMD will be forfeited.\n16. An agreement between Successful Bidder & Medical Superintendent will be entered\ninto on Rs. 100/- Non Judicial Stamp Paper. Stamp value will be paid by the bidder.\n17. Medical Superintendent reserves the right to withdraw/relax/modify any of the terms\nand conditions mentioned in the tender document if it is felt necessary in the benefit of\nthe hospital.\n18. Medical Superintendent reserves the right to reject all or any tender in whole, or in\npart, without assigning any reason thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0036",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 36,
    "page_start": 7,
    "page_end": 7,
    "char_start": 10716,
    "char_end": 12239,
    "char_count": 1523,
    "text": "III. GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT (GCC)\n1. The Contract shall initially be valid for a period of One year and may be extended for\nfurther period based on satisfactory performance and with mutual consent, as per the\nsame rates, terms and conditions.\n2. ESIC reserves the right to terminate the contract by serving one month’s notice, in\nwriting if the services of the contractor are not found satisfactory. The Contractor may\nalso ask for the same by giving one month’s notice but he has to provide the house\nkeeping facility till the next agency is engaged.\n3. The persons to be deployed by the Contractor should be properly trained, have\nrequisite experience and skills for carrying out a wide variety of housekeeping work\nusing appropriate materials and tools/equipments.\n4. The Contractor will have to provide standard liveries as approved by ESIC\nadministration at his own cost to its housekeeping staff. The staff shall be in proper\nuniform all the time with their identity card properly displayed. Samples of liveries will\nhave to be submitted by the Contractor for the approval of competent authority within\nseven days from the date of entering into the agreement.\n5. The contractor will arrange all items needed for his staff viz., time keeping machine,\ncomputerized inventory of stores, computerized daily duty roster chart etc. The house\nkeeping staff will first report to the control room and subsequently deployed for duty\nafter having been checked for liveries, upkeep, issue of material and equipments, etc.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0037",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 37,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 12241,
    "char_end": 12253,
    "char_count": 12,
    "text": "Page 8 of 35",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0038",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 38,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 12255,
    "char_end": 12289,
    "char_count": 34,
    "text": "Initial of ESIC authorised officer",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0039",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 39,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 12291,
    "char_end": 12599,
    "char_count": 308,
    "text": "Sign of Tenderer with seal\n6. ESIC Model Hospital Bapunagar, Ahmedabad will provide the space for setting up a\ncontrol room for the Contractor in the premises of the hospital from where the\ncontractor and his own supervisory or office staff can control the house keeping labour\nforce working in the hospital.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0040",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 40,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 12600,
    "char_end": 12952,
    "char_count": 352,
    "text": "7. ESIC Model Hospital Bapunagar will provide space for a store room to the Contractor in\nthe premise of the hospital. The store keeper deployed by the contractor will store all\ntheir liveries, materials, equipments in the store room and maintain a computerized\nrecord of the stores which shall be opened to inspection by ESIC Model Hospital\nBapunagar.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0041",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 41,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 12953,
    "char_end": 13115,
    "char_count": 162,
    "text": "8. The Contractor should ensure the Health and safety measures of the employees. ESIC\nmay also conduct health check up of the staff deployed at regular intervals.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0042",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 42,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 13116,
    "char_end": 13332,
    "char_count": 216,
    "text": "9. The Contractor will be responsible for supply / installation / refilling / maintenance of\nall consumables, items and equipments used in all areas of the hospital for\nhousekeeping purpose, as given in “Annexure-II”",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0043",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 43,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 13333,
    "char_end": 13517,
    "char_count": 184,
    "text": "10. The Contractor must employ adult and skilled labour only. Employment of child labour\nwill lead to the termination of the contract and necessary action under Indian Penal\nCode also.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0044",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 44,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 13518,
    "char_end": 13756,
    "char_count": 238,
    "text": "11. The Contractor shall engage only such workers, whose antecedents have been\nthoroughly verified, including character and police verification and other formalities.\nThe Contractor shall be fully responsible for the conduct of his staff.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0045",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 45,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 13757,
    "char_end": 14214,
    "char_count": 457,
    "text": "12. The Contractor at all times should indemnify ESIC against all claims, damages or\ncompensation under the provisions of Payment of Wages Act, 1936, Minimum Wages\nAct 1948, Employer’s Liability Act 1938, the Workmen Compensation Act 1923,\nIndustrial Disputes Act 1947, Maternity Benefit Act 1961, Payment of Bonus Act, 1965\nor any other law relating thereto and rules made there under from time to time. ESIC\nwill not own any responsibility in this regard.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0046",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 46,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 14215,
    "char_end": 14452,
    "char_count": 237,
    "text": "13. The tenderer should quote manpower charges in Financial Bid strictly in accordance\nwith the minimum wages as decided by the Central Govt. for Ahmedabad City. If the\nrates quoted found below the minimum wages, tender will be rejected.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0047",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 47,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 14453,
    "char_end": 14583,
    "char_count": 130,
    "text": "14. Under any circumstances whatsoever, the manpower deployed shall be paid wages\nnot below the Minimum wages set by Central Govt.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0048",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 48,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 14584,
    "char_end": 14962,
    "char_count": 378,
    "text": "15. All the rates quoted by the bidder shall remain unchanged during the period of contract\nexcept Manpower charges, which may be revised in case of revision of Minimum Wages\nby Central Govt.  This revision will, however, be restricted to revised Minimum Wages\nonly. If the revised Monthly Minimum wages remain less than the Quoted Manpower\ncharges, no revision will be allowed.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0049",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 49,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 14963,
    "char_end": 15163,
    "char_count": 200,
    "text": "16. In case of breach of any terms and conditions attached to the contract, the\nPerformance Security Deposit of the Contractor will be liable to be forfeited by ESIC\nbesides annulment of the contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0050",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 50,
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 8,
    "char_start": 15164,
    "char_end": 15337,
    "char_count": 173,
    "text": "17. Once the house keeping staff is allotted an area of work he or she will be under\nsupervision of the HoD/Staff/Sister I/c of that area i.e. wards/OPD /stores/offices etc.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0051",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 51,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 15339,
    "char_end": 15351,
    "char_count": 12,
    "text": "Page 9 of 35",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0052",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 52,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 15353,
    "char_end": 15387,
    "char_count": 34,
    "text": "Initial of ESIC authorised officer",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0053",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 53,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 15389,
    "char_end": 15626,
    "char_count": 237,
    "text": "Sign of Tenderer with seal\nand in addition to the instructions issued by the contractor side they have to follow all\ninstructions and orders given by the HoD/Staff/Sister I/C. These instructions should be\nconsidered as the scope of work.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0054",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 54,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 15627,
    "char_end": 16861,
    "char_count": 1234,
    "text": "18. The Contractor shall:-\na) Ensure Pest/Animal and Rodent free environment in the premises of ESIC Model\nHospital Bapunagar,\nb) Provide all items and consumables to his housekeeping staff as per Annexure-II.\nc) Ensure that their managers / supervisors are equipped with mobile phones, and are\navailable round the clock.\nd) Only deploy the workforce that is on his payroll.\ne) Provide Hospital Waste (Non-Biomedical) management Services including all\nequipment, containers, trolleys etc.\nf) Arrange for a garbage disposal vehicle and other equipments required for\nsegregation and disposal of waste in a professional manner,\ng) Plan, manage, collect, mechanically screen and segregate dry and wet garbage in the\nearmarked area, efficiently transport and dispose the garbage in the disposal area.\nThe work should be carried out in an eco friendly manner. The Contractor will\narrange for required resources, including manpower, machinery, disposables etc\nwhich is used by the house keeping staff.\nh) Ensure that the garbage collection / disposal work does not adversely affect the\nsurroundings or personnel deputed for the work. Protective gear including boots,\ngloves etc. shall be provided by the Contractor to the housekeeping staff.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0055",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 55,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 16862,
    "char_end": 17415,
    "char_count": 553,
    "text": "19.  Scope of work and services for each of the premises:\na) Details of the scope of work are enclosed at “Annexure-I”.\nb) Details of Equipments to be used, number of manpower to be deployed,\nconsumables and items to be used at hospital are given at Annexure ‘II’ under\nresource management.\nc) The number of equipments, consumable except manpower mentioned in Annexure\n‘II’ is minimum. The contractor, however, shall provide all the resources, to meet\nthe contractual obligations and under no circumstances whatsoever the contractor\nwill claim anything.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0056",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 56,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 17416,
    "char_end": 17554,
    "char_count": 138,
    "text": "20. Variations\nThe ESIC Model Hospital Bapunagar may order variations in the scope through a written\nvariation order based on requirement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0057",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 57,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 17555,
    "char_end": 17896,
    "char_count": 341,
    "text": "21. Payment Procedure:\nPayment will be made in the first week of the succeeding month upon submission of the\nbill in triplicate. Payment of the bill will be based on computerized print outs in\nstandardized Performa approved by ESIC Model Hospital, Bapunagar, along with\ncomputer generated attendance sheet in respect of the persons deployed.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0058",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 58,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 17898,
    "char_end": 17911,
    "char_count": 13,
    "text": "Page 10 of 35",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0059",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 59,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 17913,
    "char_end": 17947,
    "char_count": 34,
    "text": "Initial of ESIC authorised officer",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0060",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 60,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 17949,
    "char_end": 19533,
    "char_count": 1584,
    "text": "Sign of Tenderer with seal\nWhile submitting the bill for the next month, the services provider must file a\ncertificate certifying the following along with ESI contribution sheet downloaded from\nESIC Insurance Portal:-\na) Wages of workers were credited to their bank accounts on _______\n(Acknowledgment by bank enclosed).\nb) ESI Contribution relating to workers amounting to Rs.______________ was\ndeposited on _________ (Copy of Challan enclosed with contribution sheet)\nc) EPF Contribution relating to workers amounting to Rs.______________ was\ndeposited on ______ (copy of the Challan enclosed with contribution sheet)\nd) We are complying with all statutory Labour Laws including Minimum Wage Act.\nThe payment would be made on monthly basis on verification of attendance sheets, wage\nregister,\nmonthly\nESIC/EPF/Service\nTax\nchallan/Deployment\nsheets/\nDuty\nRoster/Satisfaction Report duly signed by HoD of the concerned areas, documents in\nsupport of salary disbursement through ECS. Workers of contractors should get the wages\non the seventh day of each month. The payment of wages shall not be linked to the\npayment of bill by ESIC. If the contractor fails to provide proof of payment of statutory\ndues, his contract shall be terminated after serving one month’s notice. The\nHousekeeping Agency shall make payment of monthly wages (as quoted in the Financial\nBid) to the deployed staffs by ECS only. Cash payment receipt will not be entertained and\npayment in cash will be deemed as no payment at all. If the agency does not make\npayment through ECS, the contract will be terminated.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0061",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 61,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 19534,
    "char_end": 19967,
    "char_count": 433,
    "text": "22. Liquidated Damages:\nWhenever and wherever it is found that the cleanliness is not up to the mark, it will be\nbrought to the notice of the supervisory staff of the Contractor by sister I/C or any other\nstaff of the hospital and if no action is taken within ONE hour, liquidated damages @ Rs.\n1000/- per complaint shall be imposed. The decision of Medical Superintendent ESIC Model\nHospital Bapunagar shall be final in this regard.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0062",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 62,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 19968,
    "char_end": 20886,
    "char_count": 918,
    "text": "23. Manpower\na. Any misconduct / misbehaviour on the part of the manpower deployed by the Contractor\nwill not be tolerated and such person will have to be replaced by the Contractor at his\nown costs, risks and responsibilities immediately, with written intimation to Medical\nSuperintendent of ESIC Model Hospital Bapunagar.\nb. The Contractor should ensure to maintain adequate no. of manpower as per Annexure\n‘II’ and also arrange a pool of stand-by housekeeping staff In case any housekeeping staff\nabsences from the duty, the reliever of equal status shall be provided by the Contractor\nfrom an existing pool of housekeeping staff. If the deputed workers found are less than\nthe\nminimum\nrequired\nas\nper\nAnnexure\n‘II’\non\nany\nday,\npenalty\n@\nRs. 1000/- per worker per day will be deducted from the bill. Payment will be done only\nfor the staff who was on duty and will be restricted to the salary paid to him/her by the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0063",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 63,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 20888,
    "char_end": 20901,
    "char_count": 13,
    "text": "Page 11 of 35",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
