    "text": "Sign of Tenderer with seal\nANNEXURE–I",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0076",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 76,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 24660,
    "char_end": 24673,
    "char_count": 13,
    "text": "SCOPE OF WORK",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0077",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 77,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 24675,
    "char_end": 24863,
    "char_count": 188,
    "text": "Area of work:\nAll open and covered area within the boundary of the ESIC Model Hospital, Bapunagar,\nAhmedabad will be in the scope of housekeeping services to be provided by the contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0078",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 78,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 24865,
    "char_end": 24951,
    "char_count": 86,
    "text": "Total Plot Area\n\n:\nApprox. 35043 Sq. Mtr\n\nTotal Built-up Area\n\n:\nApprox. 26420 Sq. Mtr",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0079",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 79,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 24953,
    "char_end": 26745,
    "char_count": 1792,
    "text": "Total Landscape & Horticulture Area\n:\nApprox. 12665 Sq. Mtr\nCleaning Services:\nThe aim and objective is to provide a high level of a clean, hygienic and presentable look to\nthe entire area. The contractor and his management team will supervise the awarded work.\nThe Contractor has to ensure that the staff deployed is dressed in neat and clean uniform\napproved by the ESIC Model Hospital Bapunagar Ahmedabad. Officials of ESIC will also\nmonitor the entire work and staff.\nGeneral Instructions:\n1. All collection, storage, transportation and disposal of hospital waste shall be in\naccordance with Bio-Medical Waste Management and Handling Rules of India, 1998\namended in 2000 and any other amendments or other regulations, in this regard.\n2. A detailed Hospital Waste Management Plan shall be prepared and got approved from\nESIC before starting the work.\n3. All infected, chemical, Radiation, Cytotoxic Health care Waste shall be segregated,\ncollected, stored, transported and disposed in accordance with set guidelines in safety,\nensuring that at no stage it gets mixed with general waste. Unscientific burning shall not\nbe permitted. Different coloured bags/containers namely green, red, yellow and\npuncture proof or stainless steel, lead containers shall be used depending on the\ncategory of waste.\n4. Waste shall not be transferred from one bag to another. Bags should be tied when three\nfourths full.\n5. Covered Trolleys should be used for transportation. Before final disposal/treatment,\nwaste should be kept in specified location and in specific liners and containers.\n6. The scope includes segregation, collection, storage, transportation within and outside\nthe hospital until final disposal. All statutory rules and regulations and legal\nrequirements are to be followed at each stage.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0080",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 80,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 26747,
    "char_end": 26760,
    "char_count": 13,
    "text": "Page 14 of 35",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0081",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 81,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 26762,
    "char_end": 26796,
    "char_count": 34,
    "text": "Initial of ESIC authorised officer",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0082",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 82,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 26798,
    "char_end": 28385,
    "char_count": 1587,
    "text": "Sign of Tenderer with seal\nGeneral Requirements and Documentation\n• Organisational structure and line of authority\n• Housekeeping manual and all SOP ( Standard Operating Procedures)\n• List of equipments used\n• Colour coding\n• On job training and documentation\n• Description for each category of housekeeping\n• Empathetic and polite behaviour with patients, visitors and hospital staff.\n• Personal Protective Equipments for the Housekeeping staff\n• HBV vaccination of all Housekeeping staff\n• Maintaining records / details of\na) Needle stick injuries or any other injury\nb) Amount of waste going out to outsourced agency\nc) Complaint Book\nd) Duty Roster / Deployment Sheet of Housekeeping Staff\ne) Inventory of Stores\nf) Accident / theft Register\ng) Logs and checklists\n• Female patients should be attended by female staff only\n(A)\nDaily Services\nHousekeeping/  cleaning  services  should  be  provided  round  the  clock  on  all  days\nincluding holidays, so that all areas are spic and span all the time. Working hours should be\nadjusted in such a manner that cleaning work in the morning should be completed well\nbefore 8.30 AM in rooms where work starts at 9:00 AM. Contractor will arrange manpower\nfor special VIP visits at no extra cost and provide full support and cooperation during\nHospital accreditation process.\nHousekeeping staff has to do following activities for all hospital rooms / blocks of all the\ndepartments, stores, canteen, kitchen, consultants chambers, wards, ICUs, operation\ntheatres, CSSD, laundry, labs, blood bank, all corridors and all covered and open areas.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0083",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 83,
    "page_start": 14,
    "page_end": 14,
    "char_start": 28387,
    "char_end": 29019,
    "char_count": 632,
    "text": "1) Cleaning, scrubbing and disinfecting bathrooms, toilets, wash basins, sanitary fittings,\nfloors etc. of all the areas including wards, ICUs, OT and all other departments at hourly\nbasis.\n2) The Contractor will provide, maintain, refill Hand Wash / sanitizer in all the Toilets /\nRest Rooms.\n3) Cleaning, sweeping, mopping with disinfectant stair cases, cabins, lobbies, reception,\npantries, kitchen, canteen, CSSD, Laundry, corridors, ceilings, office rooms, training\nrooms every two hours or as per requirement/direction.\n4) Vacuum cleaning of all carpets and upholstered furniture once in a day or as per\nrequirement/direction.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0084",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 84,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 29021,
    "char_end": 29034,
    "char_count": 13,
    "text": "Page 15 of 35",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0085",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 85,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 29036,
    "char_end": 29070,
    "char_count": 34,
    "text": "Initial of ESIC authorised officer",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0086",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 86,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 29072,
    "char_end": 29255,
    "char_count": 183,
    "text": "Sign of Tenderer with seal\n5) Cleaning and disinfecting kidney trays, urinals, bed pans, sputum mugs, humidifiers,\nsuction bottles and emptying urine and drain bags whenever required.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0087",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 87,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 29256,
    "char_end": 29370,
    "char_count": 114,
    "text": "6) Cleaning blood and others spills such as human excrement, urine, vomits, sterile body\nfluids whenever required.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0088",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 88,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 29371,
    "char_end": 29603,
    "char_count": 232,
    "text": "7) Cleaning, dusting electrical switch boards, light fixtures, fans, air conditioner vents,\nname plates, door mats, fire fighting equipments, computer systems, phones, doors,\nwindows, furniture, window glasses, grills, curtains etc.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0089",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 89,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 29604,
    "char_end": 29784,
    "char_count": 180,
    "text": "8) Cleaning of dust bins, waste paper baskets, cobwebs etc. and disposing off all collected\nrefuse on daily basis at regular intervals i.e. 3 times or as per requirement/direction.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0090",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 90,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 29785,
    "char_end": 29920,
    "char_count": 135,
    "text": "9) The dust bins shall be washed and garbage bags need to be placed in all garbage bins to\navoid stains and clear them when it is full.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0091",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 91,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 29921,
    "char_end": 30098,
    "char_count": 177,
    "text": "10) Collect garbage in specified colour coded bags from all dust bins and garbage bins\nexisting inside the premises and shall dispose at the designated area within the hospital.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0092",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 92,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 30099,
    "char_end": 30369,
    "char_count": 270,
    "text": "11) Refilling, replacing and emptying of containers at all stations.\n12) Offering and assisting the patient with kidney tray, urinals, bed pans, sputum cups\nwhenever required and disposing the contents in the sluice room, clean, disinfect and\nkeep it ready for next use.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0093",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 93,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 30370,
    "char_end": 30535,
    "char_count": 165,
    "text": "13) Cleaning the patients who have soiled themselves with stool, urine, vomits with\nassistance of Patient attendant / Nursing orderly / Staff nurse / Nursing sister.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0094",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 94,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 30536,
    "char_end": 30637,
    "char_count": 101,
    "text": "14) Washing linen which are soiled by urine, vomits, faeces and others with 1% hypochlorite\nsolution.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0095",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 95,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 30638,
    "char_end": 30733,
    "char_count": 95,
    "text": "15) Spraying room fresheners in all rooms on twice a day basis or as per\nrequirement/direction.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0096",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 96,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 30734,
    "char_end": 30871,
    "char_count": 137,
    "text": "16) Assist in transporting dead bodies to mortuary and dispose off dead fetus and\namputated limbs or other parts to BMW collection point.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0097",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 97,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 30872,
    "char_end": 31104,
    "char_count": 232,
    "text": "17) Carry out fumigation of ICUs / OTs as perrequirement/direction.\n18) Cleaning, mopping, disinfecting OT floors, walls, ceilings/OT lights morning before\nstarting case, in between cases and terminal cleaning at the end of the day.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0098",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 98,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 31105,
    "char_end": 31253,
    "char_count": 148,
    "text": "19) Clean the patient’s bed, lockers, trolleys, wheel chairs and surrounding areas twice a day\nor when patient is discharged or when soiling occurs.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0099",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 99,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 31254,
    "char_end": 31379,
    "char_count": 125,
    "text": "20) Cleaning and carbolization of ICU beds, OT beds between cases.\n21) Washing of slippers in ICU’s, OT, dialysis centre etc.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0100",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 100,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 31380,
    "char_end": 31527,
    "char_count": 147,
    "text": "22) Scrubbing / cleaning of toilets, wash basins, sanitary fittings, glasses, toilets, floors, etc\non hourly basis or as per requirement/direction.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0101",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 101,
    "page_start": 15,
    "page_end": 15,
    "char_start": 31528,
    "char_end": 31974,
    "char_count": 446,
    "text": "23) Cleaning and disinfecting all vitreous fixtures including toilet bowls, urinals, sinks, toilet\nseats, containers etc. Brush thoroughly to include below water level and under rims\nincluding areas at hinges and cistern handles. Re-stock toiletries, which include liquid\nhand soap, toilet rolls, air fresheners, sanitary cubes, naphthalene balls in toilets, etc.\nafter daily check-ups in the morning, afternoons and on call basis during daytime.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0102",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 102,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 31976,
    "char_end": 31989,
    "char_count": 13,
    "text": "Page 16 of 35",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0103",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 103,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 31991,
    "char_end": 32025,
    "char_count": 34,
    "text": "Initial of ESIC authorised officer",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0104",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 104,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 32027,
    "char_end": 32219,
    "char_count": 192,
    "text": "Sign of Tenderer with seal\n24) Cleaning of all open areas between the building and boundary including sweeping of\nroads, lawns, paths, cleaning open drains etc or as per requirement/direction.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0105",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 105,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 32220,
    "char_end": 32576,
    "char_count": 356,
    "text": "25) Any additional work assigned by the sister I/C of the area where the house keeping staff\nhas been placed on duty. Once assigned an area the house keeping staff will be under\nthe control and supervision of the sister I/C on duty of that area.\n(B)\nWeekly Services\nThe deep cleaning of the entire area will be done by the Contractor once a week as under:-",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0106",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 106,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 32577,
    "char_end": 32674,
    "char_count": 97,
    "text": "1) Dusting of entire area including windows / windowpanes/ doors / ledges / elevation\nframes etc.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0107",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 107,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 32675,
    "char_end": 32786,
    "char_count": 111,
    "text": "2) Cleaning of ceilings and high walls, removal of wash / spit stains on walls, cleaning of\nroofs, porches etc.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0108",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 108,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 32787,
    "char_end": 32892,
    "char_count": 105,
    "text": "3) Cleaning of sanitary fittings, toilet drain pipes etc. in the toilets with standard cleaning\nmaterial.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0109",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 109,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 32893,
    "char_end": 33075,
    "char_count": 182,
    "text": "4) Cleaning of all windows glasses and grills with detergent/ cleaning agents.\n5) Washing of roads, lawns, paths etc with High Pressure Jet machine or as per\nrequirement/direction...",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0110",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 110,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 33076,
    "char_end": 33156,
    "char_count": 80,
    "text": "6) Clean all chrome fittings, glass frames, soap holders etc. to a shiny finish.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0111",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 111,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 33157,
    "char_end": 33408,
    "char_count": 251,
    "text": "7) The Tenderer will make a cleaning program and submit to ESIC for weekly cleaning so\nthat ESIC’s concerned official / In charge for the particular area can be deputed on the\nday of cleaning to make the area available and supervise the cleaning work.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0112",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 112,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 33409,
    "char_end": 33548,
    "char_count": 139,
    "text": "8) The Contractor will cover all the specified area of scope of work.\n9) The Contractor will provide the duty register to ESIC as required.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0113",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 113,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 33549,
    "char_end": 33694,
    "char_count": 145,
    "text": "10) The Contractor will maintain a Checklist record of all weekly services and submit.\n(C)\nWaste Disposal Management Other than Bio-Medical Waste",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0114",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 114,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 33695,
    "char_end": 33789,
    "char_count": 94,
    "text": "1) The contractor will prepare a flowchart indicating the method of collection / disposal\netc.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0115",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 115,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 33790,
    "char_end": 33934,
    "char_count": 144,
    "text": "2) The contractor will teach and train his staff for collection / disposal work. The garbage\nwill have to be disposed off at least thrice a day.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0116",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 116,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 33935,
    "char_end": 34162,
    "char_count": 227,
    "text": "3) The contractor will make arrangement to collect garbage in specified colour coded bags\nfrom all dustbins and garbage bins existing inside the premises and shall dispose the\ngarbage at the designated area within the hospital.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0117",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 117,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 34163,
    "char_end": 34244,
    "char_count": 81,
    "text": "4) Ensure that the AMC bin is cleared daily.\n(D)\nPest and Rodent Control Services",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0118",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 118,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 34245,
    "char_end": 34380,
    "char_count": 135,
    "text": "1) The Contractor shall take effective measures for Rodent and Disinfection Services\nincluding fogging etc. in the area under contract.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0119",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 119,
    "page_start": 16,
    "page_end": 16,
    "char_start": 34381,
    "char_end": 34548,
    "char_count": 167,
    "text": "2) The Contractor shall use chemicals that are harmless to humans and machines and\ntreated area. Material Safety Data Sheet(MSDS) report of these chemicals should also",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0120",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 120,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 34550,
    "char_end": 34563,
    "char_count": 13,
    "text": "Page 17 of 35",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0121",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 121,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 34565,
    "char_end": 34599,
    "char_count": 34,
    "text": "Initial of ESIC authorised officer",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0122",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 122,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 34601,
    "char_end": 34767,
    "char_count": 166,
    "text": "Sign of Tenderer with seal\nbe attached. These chemicals, tools required for pest and rodent control and man\npower needed has to be arranged by the contractor himself.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0123",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 123,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 34768,
    "char_end": 35020,
    "char_count": 252,
    "text": "3) The Contractor will be responsible for any damage to human/machinery by any\nchemicals used by him. Any damage caused to machinery/books due to rodent and\ndisinfection services in the areas covered under contract shall be made good by the\nContractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0124",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 124,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 35021,
    "char_end": 35279,
    "char_count": 258,
    "text": "4) The Contractor will submit a detailed plan for carrying out the Pest and Rodent Control\nServices for the approval of ESIC Model Hospital Bapunagar.  Frequency of the services\nas decided by the Medical Superintendent will be final.\n(E)\nHorticulture Service",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0125",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 125,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 35280,
    "char_end": 35432,
    "char_count": 152,
    "text": "1) The Contractor shall maintain, secure and develop outdoor and indoor plants including\ngrass in lawns by cutting hedges, watering & grass cutting etc.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0126",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 126,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 35433,
    "char_end": 35535,
    "char_count": 102,
    "text": "2) The contractor has to procure manpower, equipment etc. The hospital will only pay for\nthe services.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0127",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 127,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 35536,
    "char_end": 35828,
    "char_count": 292,
    "text": "3) The Contractor shall be responsible for any loss to the landscaping of this Hospital due\nto negligence of his staff or lack of service.\n(F)\nHousekeeping Monitoring and Control\nFor better management and smooth services, the following monitoring mechanism will\nbe adopted by the Contractor:-",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0128",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 128,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 35829,
    "char_end": 35981,
    "char_count": 152,
    "text": "1. Toilets Checklist\nThis is to be attached on the back of the toilet door. It is to be filled up by the supervisor\n/Housekeeping staff on hourly daily.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0129",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 129,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 35982,
    "char_end": 36521,
    "char_count": 539,
    "text": "2. Management / Housekeeping Service Requirements/ Complaints Report\nThis is to be filled up by the management and administrative staff of the Contractor who\nreceive/observe the complaints/requirements for any of the services. All suggestions,\ncomplaints related to services or staff deployed by the Contractor will be registered at site\non a computer and should be reported to Caretaker, ESIC or any other designated official.\nThe Contractor will take immediate action to resolve the same failing which the Penalty\nClause will be invoked.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0130",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 130,
    "page_start": 17,
    "page_end": 17,
    "char_start": 36522,
    "char_end": 37289,
    "char_count": 767,
    "text": "3. Housekeeping Services Complaint Register\nThis register is to be completed on the basis of information received by the Housekeeping\nManager from ESIC officials through the inspection of the site, material on site, attendance\nsheet of the staff, weekly report, client letter/fax/e-mail, verbal complaints from ESIC, etc.\nand necessary action is to be taken.\nADDITIONAL SCOPE AND PARTICULAR CONDITIONS FOR HOSPITAL:\nHousekeeping in the hospital conditions is different than the house keeping services in\nother commercial organisations. Housekeeping staff has to work between the infected\npatients and has to handle dangerous infected materials and waste. Along with the routine\nhousekeeping activities the house keeping staff has to show his /her humanitarian concern",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0131",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 131,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 37291,
    "char_end": 37304,
    "char_count": 13,
    "text": "Page 18 of 35",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0132",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 132,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 37306,
    "char_end": 37340,
    "char_count": 34,
    "text": "Initial of ESIC authorised officer",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0133",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 133,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 37342,
    "char_end": 38508,
    "char_count": 1166,
    "text": "Sign of Tenderer with seal\ntowards the patient and provide him all types of required help and services. Such services\nmay be need based and might not have been included in the general scope of work but they\nhave to be provided by the house keeping staff if needed.\nIn view of the above any work assigned by the sister I/C for the patients’ benefit like\ncleaning of vomits, urine, stool, blood or any undesired material produced by the ill patient\nor helping him in changing of soiled cloths / linen or any type of need in emergency and\nhelping the ill patient in any type of need is included in the scope of work.\nIn case of any differences, these particular conditions of Contract shall supersede the\nGeneral Conditions of Contract. The services shall be provided round the clock on all days\nincluding holidays. The services include:\n(i) Cleaning of the whole premises including toilets and open areas.\n(ii) Wet moping of covered areas.\n(iii) Cleaning of window panes and door panels.\n(iv) Cleaning and dusting of furniture and fittings.\n(v) Vacuum Cleaning of all Carpets and upholstered furniture.\n(vi) Any other work within the scope of the specialized services.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0134",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 134,
    "page_start": 18,
    "page_end": 18,
    "char_start": 38510,
    "char_end": 39966,
    "char_count": 1456,
    "text": "1. PATIENTS ROOM:\nThe Contractor shall be responsible for routine cleaning of the patient room / ward\neveryday in the morning and evening. The Contractor shall also maintain cleanliness in the\npatient rooms/ward throughout the day and shall clean the room thoroughly on patient’s\ndischarge and keep it ready for the next arrival.  The routine cleaning will include dusting of\nthe furniture in the room including bed, chair, table, TV, freeze etc sweeping and mopping\nof the entire room with a disinfectant solution, cleaning of toilet and bathroom with a\nbathroom cleaning solution.\n2.  PATIENT COMMON AREAS:\n• Dusting the walls, furniture and fixtures in the corridor and lobby.\n• Sweeping and mopping the floor with a disinfectant.\n• Cleaning public toilets with soap solution and keeping them odour free using\ndeodorizer cubes/odonil.\n• Cleaning doors and windows with soap solutions.\n• Cleaning consulting room, dressing room, laboratory and other similar areas. The\nCleaning pattern will be same as cleaning of patient room.\n3. OPERATION THEATERS:\nOperation theatres are the most important place in the hospital which needs maximum care\nand cleanliness by the house keeping staff.\nRepeated cleaning and disinfection of the operation theatres after every operation, removal\nof the biomedical waste including human body parts and soiled waste, cleaning the used /\nsoiled linen as per SOPs of the Operation theatres and any other type of work assigned by",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0135",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 135,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 39968,
    "char_end": 39981,
    "char_count": 13,
    "text": "Page 19 of 35",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0136",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 136,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 39983,
    "char_end": 40017,
    "char_count": 34,
    "text": "Initial of ESIC authorised officer",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0137",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 137,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 40019,
    "char_end": 40976,
    "char_count": 957,
    "text": "Sign of Tenderer with seal\nthe sister I/C of operation theatre to the house keeping staff has to be performed\nefficiently.\n• All the dustbins washed and lined with colour-coded bags in the morning. The trash\nbag shall be changed as per schedule or as directed by Sister I/C.\n• Operation theatre walls shall be thoroughly cleaned using a specialized\nsoap/disinfectant solution before and after every operation.\n• Floor shall be washed and thoroughly mopped with a specialized soap/disinfectant\nsolution. The entire operation theatre floor area shall be scrubbed once a day.\n• Toilets/bathrooms will be cleaned with soap solution and kept odour free using\ndeodorizer cubes.\n• The common areas, doctor’s lounge, nurses lounge, Change rooms, waiting lounge and\ninside operation theatre shall be swept and mopped in the morning and at regular\nintervals to keep them clean.\n• The floor scrubbing will be done in the night or as and when asked for according to the",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0138",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 138,
    "page_start": 19,
    "page_end": 19,
    "char_start": 40978,
    "char_end": 42383,
    "char_count": 1405,
    "text": "scheduled operations and movements in that area.\n4. CLEANING OF OFFICES/CONSULTANT ROOMS\n The Contractor shall remove trash from office dustbins and change the trash liner\nevery evening before closing hours.\n The offices shall be dry dusted and swept after the closing hours.\n Vacuum cleaning shall be done on carpets and upholstery.\n The worktables shall be cleaned with soap solution in the morning.\n The office shall be mopped with soap solution in the morning.\n Office staff rest rooms/toilets shall be cleaned using soap solution and kept odour free\nusing deodorizer.\n The Contractor will provide, maintain, refill Hand Wash / sanitizer in all the Toilets /\nRest Rooms.\n Cleaning of Computers’ peripherals, telephones, LCD panels etc with appropriate\nbrushes.\n5. CLEANING OF LABORATORY AND OTHER CRITICAL AREAS\n All the dustbins shall be washed and lined with colour coded bags in the morning. The\ntrash bag shall be changed when it is full.\n Walls shall be thoroughly cleaned using a specialized soap/disinfectant solution in the\nmorning.\n The floor shall be thoroughly mopped with a specialized soap solution.\n The entire laboratory area shall be scrubbed at least twice in a week.\n Toilets/bathrooms shall be cleaned with soap solution and kept odour free using\ndeodorizer cubes.\n The common areas shall be swept and mopped in the morning and at regular intervals\nto keep them clean.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0139",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 139,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 42385,
    "char_end": 42398,
    "char_count": 13,
    "text": "Page 20 of 35",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0140",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 140,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 42400,
    "char_end": 42434,
    "char_count": 34,
    "text": "Initial of ESIC authorised officer",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0141",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 141,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 42436,
    "char_end": 43713,
    "char_count": 1277,
    "text": "Sign of Tenderer with seal\nRotation of staff in critical areas like OT, Laboratory, ICU & Wards may be kept at\nminimum.\n6. GLASS WINDOWS, DOORS & ALUMINIUM PARTITIONS:\nAll glass windows, doors and aluminium partitions should be cleaned with appropriate soap\nsolution on daily basis. Glasses shall be wiped with dry cloth to remove fingerprints at\nregular intervals.\n7. GARBAGE DISPOSAL\nThe Contractor shall collect garbage in specified colour coded bags from all dustbins and\ngarbage bins existing inside the premises and shall dispose the garbage at the designated\narea as directed by the Hospital Administration. The Contractor’s quoted rates should be\ninclusive of this item. No extra payment what so ever will be made on this account.\n8. UNDERGROUND & OVERHEAD WATER TANKS\nThe Contractor shall clean & disinfect the Under Ground & Overhead Tank periodically after\nemptying the water from the tanks as per instruction of ESIC. The Contractor’s quoted rates\nshould be inclusive of this item. No extra payment what so ever will be made on this\naccount.\n9. TERRACE CLEANING\nThe Contractor shall clean the terrace periodically as per instruction of ESIC. The\nContractor’s quoted rates should be inclusive of this item. No extra payment what so ever\nwill be made on this account.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0142",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 142,
    "page_start": 20,
    "page_end": 20,
    "char_start": 43715,
    "char_end": 44013,
    "char_count": 298,
    "text": "IMPORTANT: Every care has been taken to cover all important scopes, aspects, areas\nrequiring Housekeeping services, these are ,however, not exhaustive and if deemed fit,\nMedical Superintendent may add additional scope of work, for which no additional\npayment whatsoever on any account will be made.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0143",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 143,
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "char_start": 44015,
    "char_end": 44028,
    "char_count": 13,
