    "paragraph_index": 160,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 49527,
    "char_end": 49618,
    "char_count": 91,
    "text": "Sign of Tenderer with seal\nANNEXURE–I\nRESOURCES REQUIREMENT\n\nA. TO BE PROVIDED BY HOSPITAL:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0161",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 161,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 49620,
    "char_end": 49701,
    "char_count": 81,
    "text": "ALL DUST BINS AND COLOURED WASTE DISPOSABLE BAGSWILL BE PROVIDED BY THE\nHOSPITAL.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0162",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 162,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 49703,
    "char_end": 49751,
    "char_count": 48,
    "text": "B. THE CONTRACTOR HAS TO PROVIDE THE FOLLOWINGS:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0163",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 163,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 49753,
    "char_end": 51322,
    "char_count": 1569,
    "text": "1. ALL THE CLEANING MATERIAL, SOAP SOLUTIONS, ROOM FRESHENERS, NAPHTHALINE\nBALLS, DISINFECTANTS, DEODORANTS, ANY OTHER ARTICLES/SOLUTION/CHECMICAL\nAS MENTIONED IN THIS TENDER DOCUMENT WILL BE PROVIDED BY THE CONTRACTOR.\n2. All the manpower, equipments, tools and tackles, their accessories /refills pertaining to\nhousekeeping services will have to be provided by the contractor.\n3. The contractor has to provide supervisory and management support by his own staff to\nget the maximum output from the house keeping force deployed at the hospital.\nTeaching and training to the Housekeeping staff has to be done by the contractor. The\nman and all materials needed for the management of the house keeping staff will be\nthe responsibility of the contractor. The hospital will only pay the management fee or\nservice charges.\n4. For Pest and rodent control the contractor has to procure manpower, equipment and\nchemicals. The hospital will only pay for the services.\n5. For Horticulture Services, the contractor has to procure manpower, equipment etc. The\nhospital will only pay for the services.\n6. Following equipments, tools and tackles are minimum and mandatory to be provided to\nthe housekeeping staff by the contractor. These numbers, however, can be increased as\nper requirement but payment will only be done as per financial bid. Minimum No. of\nEquipments, tools, tackles etc have to be maintained in the hospital at all times.  A record\nof all these items should be kept by the Supervisor. All these equipments may be\ninspected by designated ESIC official at any time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC088-0164",
    "doc_id": "DOC-088",
    "paragraph_index": 164,
    "page_start": 25,
    "page_end": 25,
    "char_start": 51324,
    "char_end": 51505,
    "char_count": 181,
    "text": "LIST OF EQUIPMENTS, TOOLS & TACKLES\n\nS. No.\nDescription\nNumber  required\n(Mandatory)\n1.\nSCRUBBING MACHINE\n6\n2.\nWET/ DRY VACCUM CLEANER\n3\n3.\nHIGH PRESSURE JET\n3\n4.\nWRINGER TROLLEY\n15",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
