  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0064",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 64,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 12825,
    "char_end": 12826,
    "char_count": 1,
    "text": "9",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0065",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 65,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 12828,
    "char_end": 13161,
    "char_count": 333,
    "text": "(To be made on Rs 500.00 Non Judicial Stamp Paper)\nDRAFT AGREEMENT\n\nThis Agreement is made on ______________ day of ______ Two thousand eighteen between\nNational Academy of Customs, Indirect taxes & Narcotics, Faridabad, as one part, hereinafter\ncalled NACIN and M/s _________________ Agency for providing Manpower on the other part.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0066",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 66,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 13163,
    "char_end": 13350,
    "char_count": 187,
    "text": "Whereas NACIN is desirous to engage the Agency for providing Manpower for the National\nAcademy of Customs, Indirect taxes & Narcotics, Faridabad, on the terms and conditions stated\nbelow:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0067",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 67,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 13352,
    "char_end": 13686,
    "char_count": 334,
    "text": "1. The agency shall be solely responsible for compliance to provisions of various labour,\nIndustrial and any other laws applicable and all statutory obligations, such as, wages,\nallowances, compensations, EPF, Bonus, Gratuity, ESI etc relating to contract personnel\ndeployed in NACIN. The NACIN shall have no liability in this regard.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0068",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 68,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 13688,
    "char_end": 13885,
    "char_count": 197,
    "text": "2. The Agency shall be solely responsible for any accident/medical/health related\nliability/compensation for the personnel deployed by it at NACIN. The NACIN shall have no\nliability in this regard.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0069",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 69,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 13887,
    "char_end": 14234,
    "char_count": 347,
    "text": "3. Any violation of instruction/agreement or suppression of facts will attract cancellation of\nagreement without any reference or any notice period.\n4. The contract can be terminated by giving one months’ notice on either side.\n5. In case of non-compliance with the contract, the NACIN reserves its right to:\na) Cancel/revoke the contract, and /or",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0070",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 70,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 14236,
    "char_end": 14689,
    "char_count": 453,
    "text": "b) Impose penalty up to 10% of the total annual value of contract.\n\n6. The Agency shall submit a Performance Security deposit equal to 10% of the Annual\nContract Value (refundable without interest after two months of termination of contract) in\nthe form of pay order/demand draft/FDR/or bank guarantee from a Nationalized /\nScheduled bank only, at the time of signing of the Agreement. In case of FDR, it should be\nvalid for minimum period of 24 months.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0071",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 71,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 14691,
    "char_end": 14822,
    "char_count": 131,
    "text": "7. The Agency shall be fully responsible for timely monthly payment of wages and any other\ndues to the personnel deployed in NACIN.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0072",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 72,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 14824,
    "char_end": 15036,
    "char_count": 212,
    "text": "8. The personnel provided by the Agency will not claim to become the employees of NACIN\nand there will be no Employee and Employer relationship between the personnel engaged\nby the Agency for deployment in NACIN.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0073",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 73,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 15038,
    "char_end": 15190,
    "char_count": 152,
    "text": "9. There would be no increase in rates payable to the Agency during the contract period\nexcept reimbursement of the statutory wages revised by the Govt.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0074",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 74,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 15192,
    "char_end": 15304,
    "char_count": 112,
    "text": "10. The agency also agrees to comply with annexed Terms and Conditions and amendments\nthereto from time to time.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0075",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 75,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 15306,
    "char_end": 15443,
    "char_count": 137,
    "text": "11. Decision of NACIN in regard to interpretation of the terms and conditions and the\nAgreement shall be final and binding on the Agency.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0076",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 76,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 15445,
    "char_end": 15634,
    "char_count": 189,
    "text": "12. In case of any dispute between the Agency and NACIN, NACIN shall have the right to decide.\nHowever, all matters of jurisdiction shall be at the local courts located at Distt. Faridabad.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0077",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 77,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 15636,
    "char_end": 15779,
    "char_count": 143,
    "text": "IN WITNESS WHEREOF both the parties have set and subscribed their respective hands with\ntheir Seal in Faridabad in the presence of the witness:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0078",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 78,
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 9,
    "char_start": 15781,
    "char_end": 15882,
    "char_count": 101,
    "text": "National Academy of Customs, Indirect taxes & Narcotics, Faridabad\n\nWitness:\n1.\n2.\nAGENCY\nWitness:\n1.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0079",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 79,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 15884,
    "char_end": 15886,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "10",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0080",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 80,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 15888,
    "char_end": 16094,
    "char_count": 206,
    "text": "Annexure-III\n\nA. SCOPE OF WORK: SUPPLY OF MANPOWER ON CONTRACT BASIS at The National Academy\nof Customs, Indirect taxes & Narcotics, Sector-29, Faridabad, by deploying required number\nof contract personnel.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0081",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 81,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 16096,
    "char_end": 16297,
    "char_count": 201,
    "text": "B.  TERMS & CONDITIONS:\n\n1.\nThe Director General, NACIN, reserves the right to postpone and/or extend the date of\nreceipt / opening of bids or to withdraw the same without assigning any reason thereof.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0082",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 82,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 16299,
    "char_end": 16502,
    "char_count": 203,
    "text": "2.\nThe Financial bids of those bidders only would be opened who are found to be eligible\nbased on the Technical bids opened on the stipulated dates by the Tender Committee in\nthe presence of the bidders.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0083",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 83,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 16504,
    "char_end": 16750,
    "char_count": 246,
    "text": "3.\nThe said contract will be initially for a period of one year commencing from the date of\nsigning the contract. However, in normal circumstances the Agreement is terminable by\ngiving one month notice in writing by either party to the agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0084",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 84,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 16752,
    "char_end": 17072,
    "char_count": 320,
    "text": "4.\nNACIN reserves the right to reject any bid (including the lowest one) which in its\nopinion is not responsive or violating any of the conditions/specifications or which is\nfound to be adopting unethical business practices, without bearing any liability or any\nloss whatsoever it may cause to the bidder in the process.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0085",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 85,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 17074,
    "char_end": 17206,
    "char_count": 132,
    "text": "5.\nPreference may be given to the contractor(s) having valid Quality System Certificate as\nper ISO 9001:2000, in case of same rates.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0086",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 86,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 17208,
    "char_end": 17617,
    "char_count": 409,
    "text": "6.\nSelection of the bidder would be made after taking all the relevant factors like past\nperformance, credentials, responsible business practices, competency to execute such\ncontracts, credentials of fulfillment of provisions of labour laws with past contracts and\nabove conditions into account together. Mere Lowest rates are not the sole criteria of\nselection. NACIN is not bound to accept the lowest rates.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0087",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 87,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 17619,
    "char_end": 17722,
    "char_count": 103,
    "text": "7.\nWages payable shall not be less than the minimum wages payment as declared by the\nCentre Government.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0088",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 88,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 17724,
    "char_end": 17920,
    "char_count": 196,
    "text": "If the Financial bids are having rates quoted less than the statutory rates the same\nshall be out rightly rejected irrespective of the fact that the said bidder has qualified in\nthe Technical bid.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0089",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 89,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 17922,
    "char_end": 18155,
    "char_count": 233,
    "text": "8.\nWithout affecting the sanctity of the above criterion NACIN has power to relax any\ncondition of eligibility criteria qualifying the bid(s) based on merit of each case and the\nsituation so warrants in the interest of work of NACIN.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0090",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 90,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 18157,
    "char_end": 18376,
    "char_count": 219,
    "text": "The Contracting Agency shall render the following services to NACIN:\n\n(i)\nTo PROVIDE MANPOWER ON CONTRACT BASIS in NACIN, Faridabad. The supplied\nmanpower should be competent enough to execute the work assigned to them.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0091",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 91,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 18378,
    "char_end": 18634,
    "char_count": 256,
    "text": "(ii)\nThe contract workers, as specified in Annx.-I (subject to vary/change as per the\nrequirement) would be engaged for six days in a week in shift duty in the NACIN hostels\n/ Officers Mess / Cafeteria and as designated by the competent authority of NACIN.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0092",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 92,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 18636,
    "char_end": 18764,
    "char_count": 128,
    "text": "(iii)\nThe contract workers shall attend to all work assigned to them by the concerned\nsectional in charge / competent authority.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0093",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 93,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 18766,
    "char_end": 18918,
    "char_count": 152,
    "text": "(iv)\nThe personnel deployed shall be healthy, active and not less than 18 yrs or more than 45\nyears of age. Nobody shall have any communicable diseases.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0094",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 94,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 18920,
    "char_end": 19005,
    "char_count": 85,
    "text": "(v)\nThe personnel deployed shall be smartly dressed in proper uniform and always with",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0095",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 95,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 19007,
    "char_end": 19397,
    "char_count": 390,
    "text": "Identity Card. The agency shall provide fully trained and disciplined personnel who Page\nshould be well behaved and well mannered.\n(vi)\nThe contractor shall bear all expenses regarding uniforms, preparation of their Identity\ncard, compensations, wages and allowances (DA), PF, ESI, Bonus and Gratuity as\napplicable relating to personnel engaged by him and abide by the provisions of various",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0096",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 96,
    "page_start": 10,
    "page_end": 10,
    "char_start": 19399,
    "char_end": 19575,
    "char_count": 176,
    "text": "labour legislations including weekly off and working hours. The Contractor shall pay the\nwages to the personnel on or before the 7th day of every succeeding month, irrespective",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0097",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 97,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 19577,
    "char_end": 19579,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "11",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0098",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 98,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 19581,
    "char_end": 20146,
    "char_count": 565,
    "text": "of delay in payment of Bill by the NACIN for whatever reason. Wages payable shall not\nbe less than the minimum wages payment as declared by the Centre Govt.\n(vii)\nThe Contractor shall submit workers EPF number and proof of submission of EPF, ESI etc\nas applicable every month for the previous month along with the monthly bill with\nrespect to all employees deployed by him at NACIN. The manpower agency shall\nspecifically ensure compliance of various Labour Laws/Acts including but not limited to\nwith the following and their re-enactments/amendments/modifications:",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0099",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 99,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 20148,
    "char_end": 20239,
    "char_count": 91,
    "text": "The payment of wages Act 1936\n\nThe Employees Provident Fund Act,\n1952 The Factory Act, 1948",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0100",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 100,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 20241,
    "char_end": 20348,
    "char_count": 107,
    "text": "The Contract Labour (Regulation) Act,\n1970 The Payment of Bonus Act, 1965\nThe Payment of Grautity Act, 1972",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0101",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 101,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 20350,
    "char_end": 20454,
    "char_count": 104,
    "text": "The Employees State Insurance Act,\n1948 The Employment of Children Act,\n1938 The Motor Vehicle Act, 1988",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0102",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 102,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 20456,
    "char_end": 21256,
    "char_count": 800,
    "text": "The Minimum Wages Act, 1948\n(viii)\nIf the Contractor wishes to replace any of the personnel, the same shall be done after\nprior consultation with the NACIN. The full particulars of the personnel to be deployed\nby the contractor including the names and address shall be furnished to the NACIN\nalong with testimonials before they are actually deployed for the job.\n(ix)\nIn case of any loss that might be caused to the NACIN due to lapse on the part of the\npersonnel deployed by the manpower agency discharging their responsibilities, the such\nloss shall be compensated by the contracting Agency and in this connection, the NACIN\nshall have the right to deduct appropriate amount from the bill etc. to make good of\nsuch loss to the NACIN besides imposition of penalty. In case of any deficiencies/lapses",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0103",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 103,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 21258,
    "char_end": 21452,
    "char_count": 194,
    "text": "on the part of the personnel deployed by the contractor, the NACIN shall be within its\nright to terminate the contract forthwith or take any other action without assigning any\nreason whatsoever.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0104",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 104,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 21454,
    "char_end": 21589,
    "char_count": 135,
    "text": "(x)\nIf case of a death or mishap occurred during discharging the duty, the compensation\nliability will solely rest with the Contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0105",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 105,
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 11,
    "char_start": 21591,
    "char_end": 23206,
    "char_count": 1615,
    "text": "(xi)\nThat Contractor’s authorized representative( Owner/Director/Partner/Manager) shall\npersonally contact Head of the NACIN or the office in charge of Administration at NACIN\nat least once a month to get a feedback on the services rendered by the contractor viz-\na-viz corrective action required to make the services more efficient\n(xii)\nIn the event of contract personnel being on leave/absent, the contractor shall ensure\nsuitable alternative arrangement to make up for such absence. To meet such\neventualities, the contractor shall make provision for leave reserve; Failure on this\naccount shall attract penalty of Rs.500/- per day per person who is found missing /\nabsent from duty payable by the Contractor for such absence.\n(xiii)\nThe successful bidder would have to deposit an amount of 10% (Ten percent) of Annual\ncontract of value towards performance security deposit through pay order/demand\ndraft /FDR/or bank guarantee from a Nationalized / Scheduled bank only in favour of\nthe PAO, CBEC payable at New Delhi which would remain with NACIN during the\ncontract period and no interest shall be payable on the performance Security Deposit\namount. In case of FDR, it should be valid for minimum period of 24 months.\n(xiv)\nThe contractor shall arrange to maintain the daily shift-wise attendance record of the\ncontract personnel deployed by him. This attendance record is to be submitted every\nweek to NACIN with an attested photo- copy of the attendance record of the personnel\nto which it pertains. The attendance record shall be produced for verification on\ndemand\nby\nthe\nNACIN\nat\nany\nother\npoint\nof\ntime.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0106",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 106,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 23208,
    "char_end": 23210,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "12",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0107",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 107,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 23212,
    "char_end": 24933,
    "char_count": 1721,
    "text": "(xv)\nThe contractor shall be solely liable for all payment/dues of the workers employed and\ndeployed by him with reliable evidence provided to the NACIN. In the event, NACIN\nmakes any payment or incurs any liability, the contractor shall indemnify the NACIN\ncompletely;\n(xvi)\nIn case of any dispute arising out of this agreement then DG, NACIN shall nominate any\nofficer of the NACIN a sole arbitrator to adjudicate upon the issue involved in the\ndispute and the provisions of the Arbitration Act shall be applicable. In case of any\ndispute with regard to providing services and interpretation of any clause of the\nAgreement, Faridabad Court will have the jurisdiction to settle and decide all the\ndisputes.\n(xvii)\nIncome Tax TDS as per rules shall be deducted from the bills of the contractor as per\napplicable laws.\n(xviii)\nAs and when the NACIN requires additional contract personnel on temporary or\nemergency basis, the contractor will depute such personnel in accordance with pro-rata\nrates. For the same, a notice of two days will be given by the NACIN.\n(xix)\nAny violation of instructions/agreement or suppression of facts will attract cancellation\nof agreement without any reference.\n(xxi)\nIn case the NACIN suspects or finds any work is entrusted to any sub-contractor on\npiecemeal basis or on regular terms, the NACIN reserves the right to terminate the\ncontract without assigning any reasons.\n(xxii)\nPersonnel engaged on day-to-day works should not be utilized for carrying out the\noccasional work for which contractor has to engage extra personnel.\n(xxiii)\nThe contractor will be held wholly responsible for any action taken by statutory bodies\nfor violation/non-compilation of any such provision/rule.\n(xxiv)",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0108",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 108,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 24934,
    "char_end": 25554,
    "char_count": 620,
    "text": "The contractor shall, at all times, maintain all the statutory records and documents, in\nproper format, as prescribed under the various Acts / Rules / Laws applicable to contract\nlabours/personnel and shall ensure filing of all prescribed return in proper format to the\nconcerned authorities well within the time limit specified under the respective Acts /\nRules / Laws.\n(xxv)\nThe contractor shall, on demand by NACIN, produce all such records / documents /\nreturns for inspection as NACIN deems fit for ensuring proper compliance towards the\nprovisions of applicable Acts / Rules / Laws is being done by the contractor.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0109",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 109,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 25556,
    "char_end": 27341,
    "char_count": 1785,
    "text": "(xxvi) The contractor should obtain a Licence from the Jurisdictional Labour Commissioner to\nengage the Contract labour/personnel as per Contract Labour Act within a period of one\nmonth from the date of award of contract by the NACIN.\n(xxvii) The contractor shall ensure that the payment of wages to his workmen deployed for\ncarrying out his contractual obligations shall not be less than the minimum wages\nprescribed by Centre /State/Govt. of NCT of Delhi, and such minimum wages shall be\nthe higher between the Centre/ State/Govt. of NCT of Delhi notified minimum wages,\nfrom time to time, as applicable during the contract period.\n(xxviii) The contractor should ensure payment of wages to his workmen on or before 7th of\nevery succeeding month. The payment of wages will be made in the presence of an\nauthorized representative of NACIN at a place and time notified for the purpose.\n(xxix)\nThe wages shall be paid to workmen without any deduction except those under the\npayment of Wages Act and Minimum wages Act.\n(xxx)\nThe Contractor should ensure that his workmen are granted Holidays/Leave with wages\nas per applicable Act/Rules.\n(xxxi)\nThe NACIN reserves its rights to withhold bills, if the contractor fails to produce proof\nfor having remitted the ESI/PF dues.\n(xxxii) The contractor must get police verification of all his personnel employed at NACIN and\nsubmit the report to this office along with voter IDs, and other valid proof of residence\nand qualifications. The Contractor has to submit the attested photocopies of his voter\nID, PAN, residential address, educational qualifications etc.\n(xxxiii) If any of the personnel of the contractor indulges in theft or any illegal/irregular\nactivities, misconduct, the contractor will take appropriate action as per law and rules",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0110",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 110,
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 12,
    "char_start": 27342,
    "char_end": 27582,
    "char_count": 240,
    "text": "against its erring personnel in consultation with this office and intimate the action taken\nto this office. Such personnel, who indulge in such type of activities, should not be\nfurther employed in this office by the contractor in any case.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0111",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 111,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 27584,
    "char_end": 27586,
    "char_count": 2,
    "text": "13",
    "is_boilerplate": true,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0112",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 112,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 27588,
    "char_end": 28305,
    "char_count": 717,
    "text": "(xxxiv) Whenever there is a duplication of clause either in the terms and conditions or in the\nagreement, the clause which is beneficial to the NACIN will be considered applicable at\nthe time of any dispute/following any statutory rules.\n(xxxv) The contractor shall appoint at least one Supervisor on his behalf to coordinate with\nNACIN and supervise the work done by the personnel deployed to the satisfaction of\nNACIN. The details of the Supervisor shall be provided separately to NACIN before\ncommencement of the work and any change shall also be duly intimated.\n(xxxvi) The contractor shall ensure that there is no scope for any grievance from the personnel\ndeployed by him on account of delayed payment of wages.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0113",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 113,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 28307,
    "char_end": 28438,
    "char_count": 131,
    "text": "C. Terms of Payment:\n\nNo advance payment will be made. Payment will be made on monthly basis after satisfactory\ncompletion of work.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0114",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 114,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 28440,
    "char_end": 28953,
    "char_count": 513,
    "text": "i)\nThe contractor shall submit the pre-receipted bill (three copies) for every month\nby the first day of next month duly certified by the Caretaker. No interim bills will\nbe entertained. All attempts would be made to pay the bills through ECS only\nwithin 20 days from the date of submission of bill provided there is no dispute in\nrespect of rates, quantity and quality of work and on the basis of endorsement\nmade by the respective Caretaker. The payment is subject to TDS applicable as\nper Income Tax Act, 1961.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0115",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 115,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 28955,
    "char_end": 29166,
    "char_count": 211,
    "text": "ii)\nIn case of any complaint of non-fulfillment of any obligation under the contract,\nthe Director General NACIN Faridabad reserves the right to deduct the\npayments due from the contractor from monthly bill (s),",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0116",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 116,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 29168,
    "char_end": 29555,
    "char_count": 387,
    "text": "iii)\nProof of challan / receipt for the payment made towards wages to each\nemployee should be furnished to this office along with the monthly charges bill\nto be submitted for reimbursement. In case this office receives any complaint\nregarding non-payment of wages to any personnel the amount payable to these\npersonnel will be recovered from contractor’s bill and paid to such personnel.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0117",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 117,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 29557,
    "char_end": 29712,
    "char_count": 155,
    "text": "iv)\nThe contractor shall strictly comply with the provisions of the Employee\nProvident Fund Act, 1952 and the provisions of Employees’ State Insurance Act,",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0118",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 118,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 29714,
    "char_end": 30087,
    "char_count": 373,
    "text": "1952. The contractor shall deposit Employees and Employer Contributions in the\ndesignated account with the designated authority every month. The contractor\nshall furnish along with each running bill, the challan / receipt for the payment of\nProvident Fund and ESI made on account of the workers for the preceding\nmonth together with their ESIC Ins. No. / EPF subscriber No.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0119",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 119,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 30089,
    "char_end": 30365,
    "char_count": 276,
    "text": "v)\nNACIN shall pay to the contractor only the minimum wages, as per the contract,\non monthly basis and any other payments such as PF/ESI/Service Tax etc. would\nbe made only after submission of proof of payment by the contractor to the\nconcerned statutory authorities/accounts.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
  {
    "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC089-0120",
    "doc_id": "DOC-089",
    "paragraph_index": 120,
    "page_start": 13,
    "page_end": 13,
    "char_start": 30367,
    "char_end": 30569,
    "char_count": 202,
    "text": "Note: These terms and conditions are part of the Contract/Agreement as indicated in the\nAgreement between NACIN and the Agency and any non-compliance shall be deemed as\nbreach of the Contract/Agreement.",
    "is_boilerplate": false,
    "is_superseded": false
  },
